ments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T15:07:30-07:00","id":878141,"title":"","content":"It may be still too early to speculate on this, but.. based on the spoilers, could a Matter mage craft a spell that repells breathable air from a given target, either with Lodestone, or a Ruling spell? It wouldn't even need to be a long duration. Five minutes would be plenty harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  Because my autocorrect and this website have a weird relationship. 04-29-2016, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:02:10-07:00","id":878372,"title":"","content":"Yes, though I don't think Lodestone would work since moving gases like that would, I think, create an unnatural pressure differential. Ruling though could do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:45:30-07:00","id":878537,"title":"","content":"Glad to see you Ophid.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T23:46:47-07:00","id":878539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=878372#post878372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, though I don't think Lodestone would work since moving gases like that would, I think, create an unnatural pressure differential. Ruling though could do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might work depending on location though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:00:03-07:00","id":882134,"title":"","content":"Stickied with the release of 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:56:09-07:00","id":882259,"title":"","content":"Oh great I will make tons of these. I could probably write a full supplement (*wink* *wink*) myself...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lying Clocks (Time 2)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Larceny, Science<br /> <br /> This spell twists the subject's sense of time. For the duration, the subject is unable to notice the passage of time except as intended by the mage and even looking at clocks or other methods to know the time is uneffective. When casting this spell the mage can decide if the subject thinks they have &quot;a lot of free time&quot;, &quot;really late&quot; or &quot;just in time&quot; for an event or just as a general feeling. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hiding Ban and Bane (Spirit 2)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Rank<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Subterfuge, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Another tool that a Mage can use when negotiating with Spirits is to offer protecting their secrets from their enemies. The mage hides the mystical ban, banes, influences or Numina of the subject amongst other information. The spell obscures up to one piece of information per Potency. This doesn't actually do anything to remove or mitigate their effects. Any attempt to discern those qualities either through mundane research is reduced to a chance die. Supernatural powers that may uncover the information cause a clash of wills. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can provide false results for each piece of information hidden by the spell. If the mage wins the clash of wills or the mundane research rolls fail, the false information is provided instead of the truth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:31:49-07:00","id":883173,"title":"","content":"Here's one I just thought up. I'll probably come up with more over time.<br /> <br /> <b>Peripheral Enhancement (Prime 1)<br /> Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Subterfuge, Investigation<br /> Peripheral Mage Sight can help tell a Mage that something nearby might be a Mystery worth studying, but often times utilizing Active Mage Sight or Unveiling Magic can be a bit distracting. When this spell is cast on a Mage, however, it provides a bit more information to the subject. Whenever their Peripheral Sight is activated, they may immediately use an instant action, representing a few seconds 'attuning' to the sensation, to get a flash of insight that reveals the anything to them that a turn of watching the offending supernal power or phenomenon with Active Mage Sight might provide, as if only the character's Ruling Arcana were used.<br /> For instance, if a ghost in twilight utilized a Numina, a Moros benefiting from this spell would get a flash of insight telling them a Numina was used and approximately where (though without the Death 2 attainment, they wouldn't get a sense of the ghost responsible if not already visible). A Thyrsus might get a flash of insight if a Werewolf nearby spent Essence to speed their regeneration, showing them the individual and letting them know spiritual energy was used to reduce their injuries.<br /> Note that by default, this does not allow a Mage to use their 1 dot Counterspell attainment, as the information is still only learned when Peripheral Sight is triggered.<br /> When used on an unAwakened character, the target benefits from typical Peripheral Mage Sight for the duration, but gains no further benefit.<br /> <b>Add Any Arcanum \u2022: </b>By spending 1 Mana and utilizing another Arcana, information can be provided from that Arcanum in addition to the target's Ruling Arcana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The information provided by the spell is reflexive and can provide an Awakened character with enough notice of a spell to use Counterspell even without Active Mage Sight active. They gain knowledge of the Arcana used and a sort of sixth sense of the character's Nimbus, rather than seeing it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 05-06-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:33:25-07:00","id":883175,"title":"","content":"Pretty much just Command spirit -&gt; Command ghost, not the most creative but I feel it should at least be mentioned.<br /> <br /> Command Ghost (Death 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Rank<br /> Suggested rote skills: Persuasion, Occult, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The text of the spell would remain relatively unchanged from the command spirit spell except for the changes of spirit to ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:24:16-07:00","id":883398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883173#post883173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I just thought up. I'll probably come up with more over time.<br /> <br /> <b>Peripheral Enhancement (Prime 1)<br /> Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Subterfuge, Investigation<br /> Peripheral Mage Sight can help tell a Mage that something nearby might be a Mystery worth studying, but often times utilizing Active Mage Sight or Unveiling Magic can be a bit distracting. When this spell is cast on a Mage, however, it provides a bit more information to the subject. Whenever their Peripheral Sight is activated, they get a flash of insight that reveals the anything to them that a turn of watching the offending supernal power or phenomenon with Active Mage Sight might provide, as if only the character's Ruling Arcana were used.<br /> For instance, if a ghost in twilight utilized a Numina, a Moros benefiting from this spell would get a flash of insight telling them a Numina was used and approximately where (though without the Death 2 attainment, they wouldn't get a sense of the ghost responsible if not already visible). A Thyrsus might get a flash of insight if a Werewolf nearby spent Essence to speed their regeneration, showing them the individual and letting them know spiritual energy was used to reduce their injuries.<br /> Note that by default, this does not allow a Mage to use their 1 dot Counterspell attainment, as the information is still only learned when Peripheral Sight is triggered.<br /> When used on an unAwakened character, the target benefits from typical Peripheral Mage Sight for the duration, but gains no further benefit.<br /> <b>Add Any Arcanum \u2022: </b>By spending 1 Mana and utilizing another Arcana, information can be provided from that Arcanum in addition to the target's Ruling Arcana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The information provided by the spell can provide an Awakened character with enough notice of a spell to use Counterspell even without Active Mage Sight active. They gain knowledge of the Arcana used and a sort of sixth sense of the character's Nimbus, rather than seeing it directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm ... I'm not sure I like the feel of this. I mean it's definitely useful, but it seems to give all the benefits of Active Mage Sight without any of the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> This actually seems about as useful as a utility Attainment, come to think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:46:19-07:00","id":883415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883398#post883398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm ... I'm not sure I like the feel of this. I mean it's definitely useful, but it seems to give all the benefits of Active Mage Sight without any of the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> This actually seems about as useful as a utility Attainment, come to think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. There's plenty of things that Active Sight sees that wouldn't trigger PS first. Though, would it help if I made it so you need to specifically take an instant action when your PS first triggers to gain the benefit as the default, and then make it so the Reach effect makes it automatic (which is what lets you counterspell)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:51:19-07:00","id":883444,"title":"","content":"Okay, what do you guys think of this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reversal of Fortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Larceny, Subterfuge</span></span><br /> <br /> Many cultures revere the Sacred Fool, a clownish figure that perverts many of society's mores and yet, in their contrary behavior, are able to access a sort of crazy wisdom that allows them to know things beyond their ken and perform miraculous feats. This archetype rings true in Supernal Arcadia, and the Fate Arcanum allows a mage to tap into this same wisdom, turning hindrances into blessings. The subject of this spell reverses the dice effects of any Conditions and Tilts which they are under, penalties becoming bonuses and vice versa.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The reversal only applies one way. Penalties become bonuses, but bonuses do not become penalties, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:04:23-07:00","id":883455,"title":"","content":"I'd give it some mechanics for reversing dice tricks provided by conditions; 9 again becomes lack of 10 again and visa versa, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T00:26:51-07:00","id":883538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883444#post883444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, what do you guys think of this?<br /> <br /> [SIZE=16px]Reversal of Fortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can reverse all buffs the targets have, it can be a great spell to humble lesser mages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. In any way, I wouldn't add the need of reach to just affect penalties or bonuses, it's a Patterning spell. If you don't reach, you're turning an advanced practise in a spell good for lolz but not much field utility. In fact, I would require reach to affect both bonuses and penalties. Good idea in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:47:46-07:00","id":883583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883444#post883444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, what do you guys think of this?<br /> <br /> [SIZE=16px]Reversal of fortune (fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably add a clause of it pertaining to mundane penalties or bonuses as other spells do or else one could convert a ridiculously difficult spell into a simple one.<br /> <br /> Edit: my appoligies, I didn't see that it was only from conditions or tilts. Looks good as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:15:58-07:00","id":883623,"title":"","content":"One more spell:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Discover the Reaper (Death \u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Survival, Empathy<br /> <br /> Contact with the death marks you, and the more you mess with the reaper the more you wear it's scent. Assassins, gravediggers, emergency workers, war veterans, coroners... all of them wear their share. For the spell's duration, the caster can focus his sight on a subject and measure the amount of contact with the death the target has. Most people have only a very minor death aura, but a veteran coroner's aura could be startling.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You know if the death cloud is caused because the target is a killer. Also gives you a measure of how many people he has killed, one, a few, docens, hundreds.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if someone who don't kill by himself but orders an assassination, bombing or military operation should have a death aura, what do you think?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","user":"Masa","date":". 05-06-2016, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:18:50-07:00","id":883739,"title":"","content":"New to making complex spells.<br /> Feel free to slap my hand and say &quot;No&quot; if I'm doing this wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Boneitis (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> By causing muscles to tug and tense as hard as they can in all sorts of directions, you can get the human body to crush its own bones in a twisted dance of snapping and popping. This applies the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Conditions to your subject at intervals determined by your Gnosis-based casting time. Additionally it causes one point of Lethal damage each time a Condition should be applied.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The bones get in on the action and start to tear at other body tissues with their own volition. This spell does an additional point of Lethal each time a Condition should be applied.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, you make the effects of this spell supernaturally contagious. Others within the vicinity of the subject when a Condition should be applied resist infection with Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance vs the spell's Potency(?). An Exceptional Success on a roll to resist grants immunity for the remaining duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B3uk5bJcyM8\" data-code=\"B3uk5bJcyM8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/B3uk5bJcyM8/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:38:02-07:00","id":883756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883455#post883455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd give it some mechanics for reversing dice tricks provided by conditions; 9 again becomes lack of 10 again and visa versa, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yes, I was thinking about that, but how to word it so it's both balanced and not too unwieldy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883623#post883623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more spell:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Discover the Reaper (Death \u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Survival, Empathy<br /> <br /> Contact with the death marks you, and the more you mess with the reaper the more you wear it's scent. Assassins, gravediggers, emergency workers, war veterans, coroners... all of them wear their share. For the spell's duration, the caster can focus his sight on a subject and measure the amount of contact with the death the target has. Most people have only a very minor death aura, but a veteran coroner's aura could be startling.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You know if the death cloud is caused because the target is a killer. Also gives you a measure of how many people he has killed, one, a few, docens, hundreds.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if someone who don't kill by himself but orders an assassination, bombing or military operation should have a death aura, what do you think?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a logical thematic spell for Death. Could be beefed up with perhaps a minor mechanical benefit? Not bad, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883739#post883739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New to making complex spells.<br /> Feel free to slap my hand and say &quot;No&quot; if I'm doing this wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, not how we're going to do things in this thread. It's all about helping each other with constructive criticism. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883739#post883739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Boneitis (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> By causing muscles to tug and tense as hard as they can in all sorts of directions, you can get the human body to crush its own bones in a twisted dance of snapping and popping. This applies the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Conditions to your subject at intervals determined by your Gnosis-based casting time. Additionally it causes one point of Lethal damage each time a Condition should be applied.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The bones get in on the action and start to tear at other body tissues with their own volition. This spell does an additional point of Lethal each time a Condition should be applied.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, you make the effects of this spell supernaturally contagious. Others within the vicinity of the subject when a Condition should be applied resist infection with Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance vs the spell's Potency(?). An Exceptional Success on a roll to resist grants immunity for the remaining duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple comments:<br /> <br /> I like more spells that apply Conditions and Tilts. I'm not sure what your wording about &quot;each time a Condition should be applied.&quot; Should be? Like, it only damages if it tries to apply a Condition and can't? I don't think making the spell contagious makes sense for this spell. Also, maaaaybe we could come up with a better name? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I personally like &quot;Wrack.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:58:22-07:00","id":883786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883756#post883756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple comments:<br /> <br /> I like more spells that apply Conditions and Tilts. I'm not sure what your wording about &quot;each time a Condition should be applied.&quot; Should be? Like, it only damages if it tries to apply a Condition and can't? I don't think making the spell contagious makes sense for this spell. Also, maaaaybe we could come up with a better name? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I personally like &quot;Wrack.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't too sure how to word it. More that it does a tilt and a point of damage each interval. Oh. Now I know how to word it.<br /> Yeah, I guess the contagiousness does feel out of place.<br /> True that the name does seem a bit too novelty.<br /> Lesseeeee.....<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wrack (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> By causing muscles to tug and tense as hard as they can in all sorts of directions, you can get the human body to crush its own bones in a twisted dance of snapping and popping. This applies the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilts to your subject at intervals determined by your Gnosis-based casting time. Additionally it causes one point of Lethal damage each interval.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The bones get in on the action and start to tear at other body tissues with their own volition. This spell does an extra point of Lethal each interval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 05-06-2016, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:27:47-07:00","id":883802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883786#post883786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wrack (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> By causing muscles to tug and tense as hard as they can in all sorts of directions, you can get the human body to crush its own bones in a twisted dance of snapping and popping. This applies the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack Tilts to your subject at intervals determined by your Gnosis-based casting time. Additionally it causes one point of Lethal damage each interval.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The bones get in on the action and start to tear at other body tissues with their own volition. This spell does an extra point of Lethal each interval.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I like that much better. Ooh, here's another idea:<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Treat the casting mage's Gnosis as 2 higher for the purposes of ritual interval for this spell.<br /> <br /> Because a Gnosis 1 or 2 mage is only causing an Arm Wrack every 3 hours, and then you also have to spend successes to get the duration to last that long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:41:40-07:00","id":883815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883802#post883802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I like that much better. Ooh, here's another idea:<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Treat the casting mage's Gnosis as 2 higher for the purposes of ritual interval for this spell.<br /> <br /> Because a Gnosis 1 or 2 mage is only causing an Arm Wrack every 3 hours, and then you also have to spend successes to get the duration to last that long.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hee~ I like that idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Perfect fit for the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:51:04-07:00","id":883859,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vicious Gauntlet (Spirit 4)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Survival, Stealth, Brawl<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> This spell alters the nature of the gauntlet, adding bitting fangs, snarling thorns and vicious claws to its &quot;surface&quot;. The subject of this spell is the gauntlet itself as it covers the area affected by the spell. While the alteration lasts, whenever an entity attempts to cross it, roll Gauntlet Strength x 2, resisted by the entity's Stamina (or Resistance if a Spirit or similar entity). Each success causes a point of lethal damage to the crossing entity. Once the gauntlet has performed a number of attacks equal to the spell's Potency, the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet deals aggravated damage instead of lethal. Costs 1 Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet may be altered by the spell in one direction only.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You may designate a Key that prevents the gauntlet from attacking it's holder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","user":"arthexis","date":". 05-06-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:54:11-07:00","id":883862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883859#post883859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vicious Gauntlet (Spirit 4)</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Survival, Stealth, Brawl<br /> <br /> This spell alters the nature of the gauntlet, adding bitting fangs, snarling thorns and vicious claws to its &quot;surface&quot;. The subject of this spell is the gauntlet itself as it covers the area affected by the spell. While the alteration lasts, whenever an entity attempts to cross it, roll Gauntlet Strength x 2, resisted by the entity's Stamina (or Resistance if a Spirit or similar entity). Each success causes a point of lethal damage to the crossing entity. Once the gauntlet has performed a number of attacks equal to the spell's Potency, the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet deals aggravated damage instead of lethal. Costs 1 Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The gauntlet may be altered by the spell in one direction only.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You may designate a Key that prevents the gauntlet from attacking it's holder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Just seems to be more of a Patterning spell than an Unraveling one :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:02:22-07:00","id":883869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883862#post883862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this. Just seems to be more of a Patterning spell than an Unraveling one :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct, I will change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:46:47-07:00","id":883897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=883756#post883756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, yes, I was thinking about that, but how to word it so it's both balanced and not too unwieldy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do a simple table. 9 again becomes no 10 again, 8 again becomes no 10 again and 1s subtract, rote becomes roll twice and take worst (unless you can think of a better way to opposite rote), exceptional at 3 becomes dramatic failure instead of failure.<br /> And visa versa for each, of course.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:08:52-07:00","id":884058,"title":"","content":"I'm still working on the full write up, but as my first 2e mage is autistic, I spoke to my ST about filtering sensory inputs to make crowds more bearable and we came down to Mind and Forces both being options, and it being a Shielding effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:30:54-07:00","id":884077,"title":"","content":"Life would also do it pretty directly, and you could probably make a case for most other arcana as usual. For instance Fate could do it for you by just making sure you're never in the same place as unwanted stimuli. Practice would vary depending on arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:01:45-07:00","id":884162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884077#post884077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life would also do it pretty directly, and you could probably make a case for most other arcana as usual. For instance Fate could do it for you by just making sure you're never in the same place as unwanted stimuli. Practice would vary depending on arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate's not always going to be the best option. If she has to go anywhere like an airport...there's going to be crowds and noise and such. Mind was actually my first pick, but realizing Forces would be easier for my Obrimos was a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:44:22-07:00","id":884183,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just a note: the following spells treat a sympathetic link as their targets, rather than the two people holding one. If a Condition is &quot;placed&quot; on a Sympathetic link, either character may choose to accept one Willpower as a Reflexive action to transfer that Condition to themselves, removing it from the link.</span><br /> <br /> Broken Heartstrings (Space 3)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood:</b> Sympathy (Connection)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Empathy, Politics<br /> This nasty little spell was designed by a Mastigos Banisher - it's designed to hurt, not kill. Broken Heartstrings reduces the Sympathetic Strength of the link by one step for each dot of Potency; reducing it to 0 suppresses the link for the duration of the spell. This spell cannot affect Connected links.<br /> <br /> <i>Just a nasty little spell that deals relationship damage.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Twist Link (Space 3)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood:</b> Sympathy (Connection)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> Relationships are fragile, weak things - easily twisted and turned and placed on their head. Twist Link allows the mage to redefine the <i>context</i> of a sympathetic link; they could redefine a business rivalry as a childhood friendship, or a pair of lovers as a pair of enemies. The mage only defines the new relationship in general terms - much like creating or destroying a link, this spell doesn't guarantee outcomes or force reactions. This effect is Lasting, but normal interactions can restore the original link context over time. Much like other weaker sympathy-changing magic, Twist Link cannot affect Connected links.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Place the Embarassing Secret condition regarding the original context of the relationship on the link.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Place the Swooning condition on the link.<br /> <br /> <i>This really is more of a distraction than anything else. Or a really UnWise way to get out of the friendzone.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">Abyssal Lure (Prime 2)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Larceny, Occult.<br /> Whoever first thought of this spell was a <i>dick</i>. It doesn't <i>do</i> anything on its own - instead, its designed to sit on the soul of a Banisher or Sleeper, aggravating their personal shard of the Abyss. This spell gives the subject 9-again on any Dissonance or Paradox rolls they make. This spell only affects targets with the Integrity advantage.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The lump of magic metastasises like a really good cancer - the Sleeper gets 8-again on the Dissonance or Paradox rolls instead.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Sleeper also gains the Lie merit.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage managed to cage a sliver of the Abyss in the imago of this spell (or some managed to slip in) - whenever the subject of the spell makes a Dissonance roll, they also roll a chance die as a Paradox Backlash on this spell, modified as normal. The subject of the spell is considered to be of Understanding Wisdom for the purposes of the duration of Paradox effects.<br /> <b>Invite Paradox into the Spell:</b> If the mage has already spent Reach to provoke Paradox Backlashes, they may funnel any Reach they take control of into those dice pools, increasing the number of dice the subject rolls by one for each Reach funneled into it.<br /> <br /> <i>This one is messy, probably not within the boundaries of the spellcasting system, and opens up the </i>interesting <i>design space of spells that get straight-up better if you invite the Abyss into them. Abyssal Lure is the equivalent of strapping a time bomb onto someone and setting the timer to random. Well, if that time bomb could hop between people. </i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:45:32-07:00","id":884187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884162#post884162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fate's not always going to be the best option. If she has to go anywhere like an airport...there's going to be crowds and noise and such. Mind was actually my first pick, but realizing Forces would be easier for my Obrimos was a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space! A tweak of Isolation would disperse crowds from your perspective and could stop people from <i>touching</i> you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:50:10-07:00","id":884193,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering, shouldn't Abyssal Lure shouldn't be Fraying or Weaving instead, considering how it relates to Prime's purview?<br /> <br /> Edit: Hrm, maybe not since the logic is that it's commanding the abyssal shard to behave in a certain way? Which probably dooooes break the restrictions of the spellcasting rules.<br /> <br /> Twist Link and Broken Heartstrings are interesting and nice to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-06-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:06:29-07:00","id":884211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884193#post884193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering, shouldn't Abyssal Lure shouldn't be Fraying or Weaving instead, considering how it relates to Prime's purview?<br /> <br /> Edit: Hrm, maybe not since the logic is that it's commanding the abyssal shard to behave in a certain way? Which probably does break the restrictions of the spellcasting rules yeah.<br /> <br /> Twist Link and Broken Heartstrings are interesting and nice to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was justifying it as basically commanding a layer of Symbols to essentially poke the abyssal shard with a stick. It could be Fraying, though, where it'd be justified as widening the &quot;gap&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only regret I have about Twist Link and Broken Heartstrings is that there isn't an obvious way to &quot;map&quot; spacial and temporal sympathy to each-other. Mmm, a Time spell that damages memories by damaging your connection to having been there might be... interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:34:53-07:00","id":884229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884162#post884162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fate's not always going to be the best option. If she has to go anywhere like an airport...there's going to be crowds and noise and such. Mind was actually my first pick, but realizing Forces would be easier for my Obrimos was a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate: Less crowds on the route you pick. Not saying Forces can't do it, but a Shield effect like that is going to dull all your perception abilities in an attempt to block out extraneous stimuli. Also? My main point is simply that you shouldn't limit yourself to the idea that only two arcana are able to achieve the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:39:59-07:00","id":884265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884058#post884058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still working on the full write up, but as my first 2e mage is autistic, I spoke to my ST about filtering sensory inputs to make crowds more bearable and we came down to Mind and Forces both being options, and it being a Shielding effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, to expand on some options:<br /> <b>Fate-Knowing:</b> Go <i>around</i> the crowds (Serendipity is a good model here.)<br /> <b>Fate-Patterning:</b> Strings of Fate pretty much means you'll never have to actually interact with crowds.<br /> <b>Life-Ruling:</b> &quot;Oh, hey, brain. Hi. <i>Work the way you're supposed to, god damn it</i>.*&quot; This is pretty much one of the reasons that I'd &quot;dip&quot; Life if I were a Mage (Dip because I'd be a Mastigos so hard. Space 3/Mind 2/Life 2/Prime 1, most probably).<br /> <b>Mind-Shielding:</b> If the sensory processing problems that come with autism are anything like my own, the problems are entirely in the tender brain-meats.<br /> <b>Space-Ruling:</b> There. You've got your breathing room.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you were planning on using Forces - if you're using it to block light and sound... it's awfully overkill (and a big, obvious target for your enemies) in comparison to using prescription sunglasses and earplugs.**<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Meant in the least offensive way possible - I'm not entirely good at the whole &quot;being sensitive&quot; thing, so I hope you'll forgive me if this <i>is</i> offensive.<br /> ** That's what I use - I wear sunglasses when in public unless there is no chance I'm going to be in a bright place (so basically all day and sometimes at night), and I literally never leave the house without my earplugs.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:35:30-07:00","id":884305,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea (and I have a feeling I will have many a post that starts with that): Claimed incubator.<br /> <br /> So you have this hypothetical mage, and he's determined to make assembly line-style Claimed. He might owe some big nasty in the Shadow a favor, he might need a powerful army, he might be crazy, who knows. Point is, the part where he binds a spirit to a person to make them claimed is straightforward Spirit 4. The Claiming process happens over a period of time, and that might be a complication that's unacceptable. So, besides the obvious solution (Time magic, stick them in a bubble, go get a cup of coffee, come back to a fully formed Claimed) I'm wondering if it's possible to use Spirit/Life to accelerate the process?<br /> <br /> This is kind of rambly and I don't have the coherence to do a full spell writeup right now, but to workshop it: my main thoughts are based on Life 4's Accelerate Growth; if one accepts that Patterning can accelerate natural processes and that the merging process is a &quot;natural&quot; part of the Claming phenomenon, then maybe Spirit/Life can speed up the merging process? My gut feeling puts it at Spirit 4/Life 4, and needing both Spirit and Life because that's what it takes to mess with Claimed and also you're messing with this weird hybrid process that effects both ephemera and flesh. What are your thoughts?<br /> <br /> Bonus challenge: If you can create this incubator style effect, how would you apply this to an area? Say, create a consecrated area where Claimed naturally merge much, much faster than normal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:42:11-07:00","id":884313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884265#post884265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, to expand on some options:<br /> <b>Fate-Knowing:</b> Go <i>around</i> the crowds (Serendipity is a good model here.)<br /> <b>Fate-Patterning:</b> Strings of Fate pretty much means you'll never have to actually interact with crowds.<br /> <b>Life-Ruling:</b> &quot;Oh, hey, brain. Hi. <i>Work the way you're supposed to, god damn it</i>.*&quot; This is pretty much one of the reasons that I'd &quot;dip&quot; Life if I were a Mage (Dip because I'd be a Mastigos so hard. Space 3/Mind 2/Life 2/Prime 1, most probably).<br /> <b>Mind-Shielding:</b> If the sensory processing problems that come with autism are anything like my own, the problems are entirely in the tender brain-meats.<br /> <b>Space-Ruling:</b> There. You've got your breathing room.<br /> <br /> Not sure how you were planning on using Forces - if you're using it to block light and sound... it's awfully overkill (and a big, obvious target for your enemies) in comparison to using prescription sunglasses and earplugs.**<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">* Meant in the least offensive way possible - I'm not entirely good at the whole &quot;being sensitive&quot; thing, so I hope you'll forgive me if this <i>is</i> offensive.<br /> ** That's what I use - I wear sunglasses when in public unless there is no chance I'm going to be in a bright place (so basically all day and sometimes at night), and I literally never leave the house without my earplugs.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So, my current Arcanum spread for Lamb is Prime/Mind/Forces/Matter (for reasons unrelated to this one spell), so most of those options weren't on my personal radar. Thank you. Though you have no idea how much I want the Space version you thought of, especially for my daily commute. That said, I'm not sure the Life variant is something I'd allow, if I were the ST. It's a little to fiddly-into-the-mind for Life, imho; especially with Mind as Thyrsus inferior. Letting them fix brain patterns is iffy by me. But personal bias there is a thing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Note: I the player have never been diagnosed with autism. I do have ADHD and anxiety, which offer me some perspective wrt issues that magic could resolve, but it is not exactly the same.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:42:21-07:00","id":884314,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it be easier to just force a Claiming?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:44:20-07:00","id":884316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884314#post884314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be easier to just force a Claiming?</div> </div> </div> </div>By <i>what</i>, praytell?<br /> <br /> I'm legitimately curious.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oops, I skipped a post. Sorry.<br /> <br /> You could probably get away with just Spirit 4 to speed it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 05-07-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:52:16-07:00","id":884328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884314#post884314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be easier to just force a Claiming?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might legitimately be easier to force a spirit to use Claiming by it's own natural abilities than to use Spirit 4 to Supernally force the merging, but as far as I know either method still takes time to fully develop, and that time is what I'm focusing on right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:09:21-07:00","id":884406,"title":"","content":"So, I've been pushing for how to figure this one out in other threads too, but I figured I might as well come here for it too.<br /> <br /> I want to figure out how to make morpheans, ghost-mages, and spirit-mages. Which Practices for which Arcana should be necessary to become them? What exactly does a mage who becomes one look like, mechanically?<br /> <br /> I figure, obviously Mind/Death/Spirit is involved as appropriate to the kind of entity you're becoming, but do you only need that one Arcanum to do it? What Practices are involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:14:03-07:00","id":884428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884406#post884406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been pushing for how to figure this one out in other threads too, but I figured I might as well come here for it too.<br /> <br /> I want to figure out how to make morpheans, ghost-mages, and spirit-mages. Which Practices for which Arcana should be necessary to become them? What exactly does a mage who becomes one look like, mechanically?<br /> <br /> I figure, obviously Mind/Death/Spirit is involved as appropriate to the kind of entity you're becoming, but do you only need that one Arcanum to do it? What Practices are involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>It simple - Making Practice - as you reMAKE yourself or other in to that being, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T05:15:01-07:00","id":884557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884406#post884406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been pushing for how to figure this one out in other threads too, but I figured I might as well come here for it too.<br /> <br /> I want to figure out how to make morpheans, ghost-mages, and spirit-mages. Which Practices for which Arcana should be necessary to become them? What exactly does a mage who becomes one look like, mechanically?<br /> <br /> I figure, obviously Mind/Death/Spirit is involved as appropriate to the kind of entity you're becoming, but do you only need that one Arcanum to do it? What Practices are involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the beginings, you need Life though.<br /> Changing a Living thing, a human, directly into a spirit would require Spirit. So, Life and Spirit, both at adept level.<br /> Replace Spirit with any other Arcanum to turn a human into any other thing. You're gold as long as both are at adept level.<br /> These are Patterning spells.<br /> <br /> As for the mechanics, I dunno.<br /> You could probably work the spell to build your own ephemeral body how you like, customizing according to the Rank you achieve through success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884428#post884428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It simple - Making Practice - as you reMAKE yourself or other in to that being, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This works in that you make a body and move the subject's consciousness over to the empty shell.<br /> There's lots of ways to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 05-07-2016, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:43:58-07:00","id":884651,"title":"","content":"Here goes my first spell, let me know what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Ward (Prime <i>\u25cf\u25cf</i>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve (unwlling subjects only)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Manipulation, Empathy, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell wards the subject from creatures of the Abyss, meaning they gain general armor dots equal to their Prime dots against Abyssal Creature attacks and Numina as the truth shields the subject from the Lie. Each successful use of a Numina or attack by an abyssal creature reduces the potency of this spell by 1 point.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Removed Space component as it was not needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 05-07-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:09:41-07:00","id":884675,"title":"","content":"The Space part doesn't make sense, you can already create a protected area by increasing the Scale factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:52:11-07:00","id":884702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884557#post884557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've got the beginings, you need Life though.<br /> Changing a Living thing, a human, directly into a spirit would require Spirit. So, Life and Spirit, both at adept level.<br /> Replace Spirit with any other Arcanum to turn a human into any other thing. You're gold as long as both are at adept level.<br /> These are Patterning spells.<br /> <br /> As for the mechanics, I dunno.<br /> You could probably work the spell to build your own ephemeral body how you like, customizing according to the Rank you achieve through success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This works in that you make a body and move the subject's consciousness over to the empty shell.<br /> There's lots of ways to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if I didn't want to bother with Life - say, I wanted to just abandon the body altogether and have my character's soul and consciousness do its thing. What do you think would work there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:42:20-07:00","id":884959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884702#post884702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if I didn't want to bother with Life - say, I wanted to just abandon the body altogether and have my character's soul and consciousness do its thing. What do you think would work there?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds similar to Soul Jar, so Death 2 should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:02:26-07:00","id":884975,"title":"","content":"Popping a soul out is Death 3, popping a consciousness out is Mind 4. So it would be a Mind 4 Death 4 spell since arcana levels usually need to match. Follow the rules for Astral Projection and Soulessness, unless you add in Space 4 to maintain the Sympathy between yourself and your removed soul to a degree necessary to trick all the different parts of you into thinking they're still together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:07:59-07:00","id":884976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=884975#post884975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Popping a soul out is Death 3, popping a consciousness out is Mind 4. So it would be a Mind 4 Death 4 spell since arcana levels usually need to match. Follow the rules for Astral Projection and Soulessness, unless you add in Space 4 to maintain the Sympathy between yourself and your removed soul to a degree necessary to trick all the different parts of you into thinking they're still together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to become one of the emphemeral entities listed under Left-Handed Liches. This seems a little... off, with regards to that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:16:01-07:00","id":884981,"title":"","content":"Death 5, make a ghost-mage of yourself. You can probably also place a spell on yourself whose purpose is to create a ghost of a person when they die, making the ghost-mage-ness a permanent side effect because the spell is &quot;Create a ghost&quot; and what the actual ghost is, is not part of the spell's purview. Similar to how a healing spell lasts because the magic is just &quot;Heal this&quot; not &quot;Keep this wound closed&quot;.<br /> <br /> For going Morphean I'd say you have to get inside your Oneiros and then basically go to any realm that could possibly connect to the Temenos or other Oneiroi and either destroy them with Mind or sever their Sympathetic ties to humanity.<br /> <br /> Becoming a spirit probably requires joining a legacy like the Scions of God because I can't think of a way to make it permanent otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:21:09-07:00","id":885025,"title":"","content":"What Practice would you use to &quot;freeze&quot; a Condition in place to prevent it from resolving? Like, if you wanted to make a Reaper who used magic to &quot;lock in&quot; their victims at the first stage of Soul Loss, keeping them from resolving it and acquiring the next Condition, what level of Death would you use? Don't have the book yet, so sorry if it's a stupid question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:57:48-07:00","id":885043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Practice would you use to &quot;freeze&quot; a Condition in place to prevent it from resolving? Like, if you wanted to make a Reaper who used magic to &quot;lock in&quot; their victims at the first stage of Soul Loss, keeping them from resolving it and acquiring the next Condition, what level of Death would you use? Don't have the book yet, so sorry if it's a stupid question. </div> </div> </div>I would say a Shielding spell regarding Time would do this. They don't progress toward the next stage, but they also don't heal or age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T03:43:55-07:00","id":885279,"title":"","content":"How would people recreate the Prime 4 &quot;Siphon Integrity&quot; spell from 1e?<br /> <br /> It's still rank 4, unraveling but the original form strips Structure from an object and converts it into Mana. Nowadays it seems that should use Prime+Matter and be Patterning?<br /> <br /> Going from Prime 4 to Prime+Matter 4 is a fairly major shift though. Have the Practices of Unraveling changed that much between editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:14:15-07:00","id":885328,"title":"","content":"It would still be Unraveling, but yeah probably Prime+Matter.<br /> <br /> One thing that isn't clear with this edition is, if the spell isn't in the new book should it be considered defunct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:47:49-07:00","id":885340,"title":"","content":"Good question Mrmdubois. I personally am under the impression that should a spell not exist in the 2E core book but exist from previous books (including 1E Core) that they are probably still viable, because a lot of the spells from 1E crossed over into 2E with minor alterations with perhaps spell functionality and sometimes lowering of dot level because of the new strict Practices guideline. You also have to think, they had a huge word count limitation, so why waste this on spells that are already published with pretty much the same mechanics and just require a little bit of thinking on part of the ST or player to duplicate in 2E.<br /> <br /> On the note of Siphon Integrity, I think this spell should still be a Prime 4 spell, because it is unraveling the &quot;Truth&quot; from the object, so it would not require Matter, but that IMO. I would also think that the &quot;Platonic&quot; form of an item would grant more Mana as well since these objects are much closer to the &quot;Truth&quot; than other items.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:19:31-07:00","id":885359,"title":"","content":"<b>Define Unity (Space <i>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</i>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting/Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Craft, Science, Socialize<br /> Which is two can be made one. This spell take two or more targets (determined by Scale) in contact, and tie them magically together with a Strength equal to the spell's Potency, for the spell Duration. If the bond is broken, the mage must recast Define Unity to create a new bond.<br /> In the reverse, the spell can loose a bond between two targets (which may be by ropes, electromagnets, glue, screws...), reducing the Strength of the bond by the spell's Potency. Once the bond is broken, new bonds are treated normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the bond created by this spell is broken, it reassert itself when the targets are in contact again during the spell Duration. <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Once the frayed bond is broken, if another bond, whatever its nature, is put in place between the targets during the spell Duration, it's also reduced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":". 05-10-2016, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:03:57-07:00","id":886145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=885359#post885359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Define Unity (Space <i>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</i>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting/Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina or Durability<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Craft, Science, Socialize<br /> Which is two can be made one. This spell take two or more targets (determined by Scale) in contact, and tie them magically together with a Strength equal to the spell's Potency, for the spell Duration. If the bond is broken, the mage must recast Define Unity to create a new bond.<br /> In the reverse, the spell can loose a bond between two targets (which may be by ropes, electromagnets, glue, screws...), reducing the Strength of the bond by the spell's Potency. Once the bond is broken, new bonds are treated normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the bond created by this spell is broken, it reassert itself when the targets are in contact again during the spell Duration. This effect cannot be made Lasting.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Once the frayed bond is broken, if another bond, whatever its nature, is put in place between the targets during the spell Duration, it's also reduced. This effect cannot be made Lasting.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> By spending 1 Mana, the effect is Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean a sympathetic bond or a literal bond, like physically fusing two things together?<br /> <br /> Edit, oh you mean physical. Okay interesting. It's like a specific form of ban or that spell the traps someone in place. I like it, but I don't think it should be able to go to lasting. It doesn't fit Space, to me. Matter, yes, but not Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":1018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","user":"Ophidimancer","date":". 05-09-2016, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:25:13-07:00","id":886335,"title":"","content":"A few from me<br /> <br /> <b>Lethal weapon (Death ***)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Medicine, Crafts, Intimidation<br /> The mage can improve a objects abillity to harm others. This bestows the 8-again quality on a weapon<br /> <b> +1 Reach</b>: Instead the weapon gains the rote quality<br /> <b> +1 Reach</b>: The mage improves the lethal qualities of a non-weapon object. This can increase a poisons Toxicity or increase the amount of dmg inflicted by for instance a fire or a electric circuit<br /> <b> +2 Reach</b>: Used with the above effect, changes bashing dmg done by the source to lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Executioners sight (Death *)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Unveilling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Crafts, Medicine, Empathy<br /> The subject is able to see the inner flaws of any object or person. By studying something the subject can substract one point of Durabillity from something he studied during the spells duration for each turn he was observing the object. The maximum reduction is equal to the spells potency. When studying a person, each turn of observation allows the mage to reduce the targets Defense by one point in the first turn of combat<br /> <b> +1 Reach</b>: The subject gains also 9-again on the first roll<br /> <br /> <b>Spark (Forces **)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Rulling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Larcery, Science, Firearms<br /> The mage can concentrate heat on a subject to create an instanteous spark that might light a particulary flammable object, like gasoline fumes or a match (anything that could be lit on fire by a single spark) on fire. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bag of holding(Space ***)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Crafts, Survival, Larcery<br /> The mage can increase the capacity of a container, doubling it for each point of potency. This only increases capacity for objects or substances that there intended to be stored in that kind of container. A bottle can store more liquid, while a magazine can store an additional bullets.<br /> <br /> <b>Alter flammability (Matter ***)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> [b]Primary Factor[b]: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Survival, Larcery, Firearms<br /> The subject can be made flamable or non-flamable. A subject made flamable will be as easy to light on fire as dry wood.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> The subject can be made extremely flamable or even explosive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T02:38:27-07:00","id":887054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=886145#post886145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean a sympathetic bond or a literal bond, like physically fusing two things together?<br /> <br /> Edit, oh you mean physical. Okay interesting. It's like a specific form of ban or that spell the traps someone in place. I like it, but I don't think it should be able to go to lasting. It doesn't fit Space, to me. Matter, yes, but not Space.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry if the wording is confusing. Yes, it creates physical bond, but not by fusing things together, more by enforcing contact. It works on the Separation purview of Space. I don't see why not Lasting: the bond can still be broken with brute force, so it doesn't seems overpowered. See the Rope equipment for rules on bond strength.<br /> <br /> While I'm here:<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Chains (Space <i>\u25cf\u25cf</i>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Socialize, Politics, Empathy<br /> This spell target a sympathetic connection. As long as the spell endures, this link cannot be altered in strength or quality by mundane events: he'll remain in the friendzone, she'll never manage to get a divorce, this kid will never get bored of his favorite toy.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The spell can take two targets not connected by a sympathetic link. It prevents any meaningful relationship to develop, maintaining their sympathy null.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Even the supernatural can't break the Iron Chain. Any attempt to alter the sympathetic connection provoke a Clash of Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":". 07-28-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T03:22:42-07:00","id":887061,"title":"","content":"I beliebe the Rote effect of Lethal Weapon also needs a Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T11:50:38-07:00","id":887353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887054#post887054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not Lasting: the bond can still be broken with brute force, so it doesn't seems overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about it being over powered, it's that using Space to force two things together seems pretty unnatural. Lasting effects are generally things that become natural after the spell is cast. This does not seem like a state that the Fallen World would naturally maintain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:12:29-07:00","id":887373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887353#post887353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about it being over powered, it's that using Space to force two things together seems pretty unnatural. Lasting effects are generally things that become natural after the spell is cast. This does not seem like a state that the Fallen World would naturally maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't understand Lasting effects like this, but it looks like you're right. Spell edited, thanks for the insight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:26:43-07:00","id":887449,"title":"","content":"What rank of Mind would I need to convince someone that a bit of magic I just performed doesn't trigger the Lie?<br /> <br /> For example, I want to use Life transformation to make a video of an 'authentic bigfoot/cryptid/little green man' but all I have on hand is a sleeper friend. Couldn't I put the whammy on him to make him think he's putting on a costume or some makeup?<br /> <br /> Quiescence shouldn't trigger if a person doesn't realize the impossibility of something, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:19:38-07:00","id":887487,"title":"","content":"It's not about belief, but you can probably do it with a Veiling spell to cloud their ability to perceive it with Mind or Prime and there are probably methods other arcana can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:07:42-07:00","id":887644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887449#post887449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rank of Mind would I need to convince someone that a bit of magic I just performed doesn't trigger the Lie?<br /> <br /> For example, I want to use Life transformation to make a video of an 'authentic bigfoot/cryptid/little green man' but all I have on hand is a sleeper friend. Couldn't I put the whammy on him to make him think he's putting on a costume or some makeup?<br /> <br /> Quiescence shouldn't trigger if a person doesn't realize the impossibility of something, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it's not about belief. It cannot be. Even if it was, it wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> Or, explained another way: it cannot be about belief because Sleepers cannot believe in Supernal magic to begin with. The Quiessence is precisely that. Any attempt to reveal Supernal Truth to them makes them go bonkers.<br /> <br /> If you throw a fireball in a shopping mall, all Sleepers there are affected by Quiessence. After the incident they will forget or misremember. Some might thing an helicopter fell out of the sky, or that there was some terrorist bomber and now it is being covered up, or that a gas pipe burst, or they just don't remember what happened leaving a gap in their memories that they do not dare question too much. But it is perfectly reasonable that some could actually have a supernatural explanation! Perhaps the devil appeared, or a dragon came over, or Voldemort showed up and had a fight with Harry Potter. Regardless, even if they give it a supernatural explanation, they are still unaware of the Truth.<br /> <br /> As Mrmdubois said, you could remove their senses with mind so they don't witness it (or you might as well put a paperbag over their head) but once witnessed, their capability to rationalize it or believe it is irrelevant, the Abyss has been stirred by the unveiling of Magic.<br /> <br /> Edit: Buy the way, cutting off their senses is obviously magical too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:12:36-07:00","id":887652,"title":"","content":"I wasn't suggesting you cut off all their senses, just their ability to sense anything out of the ordinary.<br /> <br /> It could actually be similar to what the Bearers of the Eternal Voice and Blank Badges can achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:08:51-07:00","id":887702,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a Veiling spell that puts people into a waking dream, so that they can still interact with the world, but aren't really seeing it as it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:10:17-07:00","id":887703,"title":"","content":"Or heck, just devise a spell that temporarily grants that Merit, the one that makes it so people ignore the obviously supernatural things around them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:35:46-07:00","id":887722,"title":"","content":"What dot and Practice of Space would best cover allowing melee attacks to strike at range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:56:57-07:00","id":887743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887722#post887722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What dot and Practice of Space would best cover allowing melee attacks to strike at range?</div> </div> </div> </div>3 dot and Weaving maybe? Ranged Blow was that in 1e IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:49:49-07:00","id":887874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887743#post887743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 dot and Weaving maybe? Ranged Blow was that in 1e IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on exactly how you're trying to accomplish this. I mean, I could see Forces simply extending your kinetic attacks, or Space doing funny things to the intervening space. At a minimum, Forces would need Ruling to do it, basically just pushing the kinetic force of your strikes out further than normal. For Disciple Practices, I'd think Perfecting over Weaving, since you're not really transforming or changing the nature of the force, just extending it further than it would normally go. That's with Forces. For something like Space, Weaving might be more appropriate, but I'll have to think on how I'd do that.<br /> <br /> Edit: After thinking about it, a Weaving Space spell to &quot;pinch&quot; space between the subject and something she wants to strike in melee seems like it could work. Your punches are basically traveling further than they ought because you're temporarily compressing space between you and your target, but only for a moment, and not to a degree that would require Patterning or even Unraveling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 05-11-2016, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:25:12-07:00","id":887981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887054#post887054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry if the wording is confusing. Yes, it creates physical bond, but not by fusing things together, more by enforcing contact. It works on the Separation purview of Space. I don't see why not Lasting: the bond can still be broken with brute force, so it doesn't seems overpowered. See the Rope equipment for rules on bond strength.<br /> <br /> While I'm here:<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Chains (Space <i>\u25cf\u25cf</i>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Socialize, Politics, Empathy<br /> This spell target a sympathetic connection. As long as the spell endures, this link cannot be altered in strength or quality by mundane events: he'll remain in the friendzone, she'll never manage to get a divorce, this kid will never get bored of his favorite toy.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The spell can take two targets or more not connected by a sympathetic link. It prevents any meaningful relationship to develop, maintaining their sympathy null.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Even the supernatural can't change the Iron Chain. Any attempt to alter the sympathetic connection provoke a Clash of Will.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>Instead of targeting a single sympathetic connection, the spell targets all the links of a single target, including non existent ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first reach option of this spell is equivalent to the master level unmaking spell Forge No Bonds. That probably isn't a good idea.<br /> <br /> On a completely separate note, would it be possible to use life magic to relieve some of the tension in a sleeper's body while giving them a massage? I mean, so long as it isn't so powerful as to leave them completely healed, it might not provoke dissonence and quiescence, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:41:58-07:00","id":887986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887981#post887981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a completely separate note, would it be possible to use life magic to relieve some of the tension in a sleeper's body while giving them a massage? I mean, so long as it isn't so powerful as to leave them completely healed, it might not provoke dissonence and quiescence, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. This is both a generous and very simple use of Life magic. A simple Compelling Life spell would do the trick of relieving tension, and there's nothing about it that should trigger Dissonance or risk Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:49:18-07:00","id":887990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887986#post887986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. This is both a generous and very simple use of Life magic. A simple Compelling Life spell would do the trick of relieving tension, and there's nothing about it that should trigger Dissonance or risk Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude01 My next mage officially has a career.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T03:04:05-07:00","id":888011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=887990#post887990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\ud83d\ude01 My next mage officially has a career.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would literally have to go out of your way to demonstrate that you're using magic in order for there to be any problem. Otherwise, you're Compelling something the body is wont to do naturally, anyway, especially at the hands of a skilled masseuse. Your biggest worry? The crazy word of mouth that will get around about how damned good you are, with hands like magic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T03:40:37-07:00","id":888023,"title":"","content":"<b>The World</b> <b>(Time \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Unmaking<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Science, Occult, Drive<br /> This spell creates a time bubble centered on the caster (measured by Scale) where all time ceases to exist. Only she can act and move around, while the rest of the world inside the bubble (which doesn't move with her) stands completely frozen in place. She can move objects and people around as per her usual capabilities and these offer no resistance at all. The only limitation is that she can't alter the patterns in a way that would imply a variation of Structure, Health or Willpower in anyone but herself (So she cannot attack or heal other targets). She could even cross from one building to another as if walking in mid air, as she won't fall unless she wills herself to, and then she would just move downwards at her usual Speed per Turn.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>By adding a Reach and paying a Mana the caster can actually attack or heal others inside the bubble once per dot of Potency. Once all the Potency has been used, even if some Duration remains, the spell ends.<br /> <br /> Ok, this is a bit of a joke, but I tried to make it legit. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:22:09-07:00","id":888042,"title":"","content":"I'd make the base option to simply freeze everything except herself, +1 Reach to move things around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:59:51-07:00","id":888068,"title":"","content":"Now I want to make a super-pumped-up &quot;Ora Ora Ora&quot; spell, Forces 5 Unmaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:57:05-07:00","id":888140,"title":"","content":"What Mrmdubois said. Also the Reach option there is bit too powerful if you wanna make it &quot;serious&quot;, perhaps if you take that option Withstand should apply to the attacked target, otherwise you get like 5 free attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T12:41:14-07:00","id":888454,"title":"","content":"Also, you have to cross out the &quot;With&quot; part of &quot;Withstand.&quot; It's just &quot;Stand.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:50:07-07:00","id":888575,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, I don't see the Reach option that extreme. Note that you are going to need to pump both Scale and Potency to be able to do something actually nasty with it. I'll give it more thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T16:02:24-07:00","id":888636,"title":"","content":"<b>Foreshadow (Fate </b><b>\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Expression, Subterfuge<br /> When a mage casts this spell, he chooses a destiny (or Destiny) of which he is aware. The spell causes the strings of fate to manifest one symbol per dot of Potency of that destiny between the time of casting and when the fated event occurs. For instance, if a Sleeper is destined to get into a car crash, the spell might cause her to see a commercial about auto insurance, or she might drive by the site of a car crash the day before. The effects of this spell are normally minor and subtle, but they can be useful for getting someone to believe in the power of fate and symbolism. Alternatively, the mage might wish to cause foreshadowing to manifest for particularly obscure destinies in order to analyze a mystery from a different point of view.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage chooses how the foreshadowing manifests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:47:12-07:00","id":888831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=888636#post888636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Foreshadow (Fate </b><b>\u25cf)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this spell, though I would make it Fate 2 Ruling... Or if you wanna keep it at Fate 1, make it Unveiling on the subject that you want to see the signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:36:15-07:00","id":888976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=888831#post888831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this spell, though I would make it Fate 2 Ruling... Or if you wanna keep it at Fate 1, make it Unveiling on the subject that you want to see the signs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fits better as an Unveiling spell, seeing as it's about uncovering more about one's Destiny. That said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>, you mind if I use this for my 2E conversion of the Awakening Gambit Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T06:56:25-07:00","id":889073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=888976#post888976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it fits better as an Unveiling spell, seeing as it's about uncovering more about one's Destiny. That said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>, you mind if I use this for my 2E conversion of the Awakening Gambit Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:44:20-07:00","id":889199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=888023#post888023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ZA WARUDO</b> <b>(Time \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Unmaking<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Science, Occult, Drive<br /> This spell creates a time bubble centered on the caster (measured by Scale) where all time ceases to exist. Only she can act and move around, while the rest of the world inside the bubble (which doesn't move with her) stands completely frozen in place. She can move objects and people around as per her usual capabilities and these offer no resistance at all. The only limitation is that she can't alter the patterns in a way that would imply a variation of Structure, Health or Willpower in anyone but herself (So she cannot attack or heal other targets). She could even cross from one building to another as if walking in mid air, as she won't fall unless she wills herself to, and then she would just move downwards at her usual Speed per Turn.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>By adding a Reach and paying a Mana the caster can actually attack or heal others inside the bubble once per dot of Potency. Once all the Potency has been used, even if some Duration remains, the spell ends.<br /> <br /> Ok, this is a bit of a joke, but I tried to make it legit. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a small typo, but I caught it for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:35:45-07:00","id":889633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=889073#post889073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889631-the-awakening-gambit-2e-conversion-discussion\">Got a discussion thread for my Awakening Gambit conversion, if you're interested.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:49:16-07:00","id":890152,"title":"","content":"A first stab at a remix of a Virtual Adepts rote from the olden days. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> (This could be achieved in a more straightforward fashion using Conditional Duration as a lever, of course. What Practice would you place the &quot;malevolent Serendipity&quot; thing at if it were its own spell?)<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Adrasteia (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve (if desired)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Athletics, Streetwise</span></span><br /> <br /> Fate often strikes ironically, dooming people in venues where they imagine themselves at their best. This spell gathers a cluster of misfortune around one Skill that the mage names during casting, causing the subject to suffer unexpected setbacks when they attempt to exercise it. The subject gains the Ordeal of [Trait] Persistent Condition keyed to the named Skill. While this can foil a skilled rival in a moment of crisis, mages also levy the curse on those that seek to improve a Skill, as the hardships will provide a more strenuous and rapid course of enrichment.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> During the spell's Duration, minor perturbations of Fate steer the subject into situations where they are obligated to use the marked Trait. This works as a malevolent version of Serendipity, <i>forcing</i> use of the Trait during one important roll of a different Trait from the same type (Skill, Attribute, etc.) and category (Mental, Social, Physical) in a given scene.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above, but the marked Trait will substitute in for any Trait of the same type. A diplomat with Ordeal of [Firearms] would find their Socialize effort now hinges on small talk about military hardware, for instance.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may instead name an Attribute; the Condition will apply to this Trait.<br /> (<i>Comedy option</i>: <b>+2 Reach:</b> The mage may instead name an Arcanum, which the subject must possess; the Condition will apply to this Trait.)<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The spell becomes Lasting; the Condition will persist until Resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ordeal of [Trait] (Persistent)</span><br /> Fate conspires to foil your efforts regarding a Skill or other Trait. The first time each scene that you roll a dice pool containing the Trait, circumstances turn against you, levying an equipment penalty equal to your dots in the Trait. A character with Medicine 3 discovers that some of their tools have been misplaced and the lighting has become unreliable, imposing a -3 penalty; if they had been less capable fate would have been less cruel, while a master surgeon might find themselves more deeply disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Increase your rating in the marked Trait or gain a Specialty or Merit that displays growth in that field.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> Suffer the penalty on a roll where the consequences of failure would represent a genuine setback or real hardship for you or those around you.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Here's an alternate version that assumes that Ordeal isn't Persistent (but is supernatural, thus Weaving) and instead uses the spell to recur the Condition. The last Reach effect isn't really kosher but re-establishes the notion of using the spell to facilitate growth.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> As above, except:<br /> Adrasteia (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Condition recurs at each of the mage's ritual intervals until the Duration elapses.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> The spell becomes Lasting. The Condition recurs at each of the mage's ritual intervals until the subject gains a dot or new Specialty tied to the named Trait or has the effect excised by Atonement or a similar restorative measures.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ordeal of [Trait]</span><br /> ...<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Suffer the penalty on a roll where the consequences of failure would represent a genuine setback or real hardship for you or those around you.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:05:31-07:00","id":891216,"title":"","content":"This spell is incredibly easy to make with Mind, so I thought I'd try my hand at making it in an entirely new way. I made it Lasting because the idea is that you are removing something entirely, though if it's thought to be better with a duration then the Primary Factor would be duration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Tabula Rasa</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Arcana: Time<br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Temporal Sympathy<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Intimidation, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> A person is the sum of his whole collective experiences and memories. This spell does not change the past, but removes a targets connection to their own past by unmaking the their unchanged temporal connection. The individual loses touch with who they are - their memories cut off from their mind, they become a blank slate, experiencing full and total amnesia. The effect is Lasting.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: In addition to removing a target's memories, they may also remove a persons connections to their skills, making all skills the target had prior to the casting &quot;untrained&quot;.<br /> <br /> Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 : By adding space and spending a Reach, the caster of Tabula Rasa can make it so that not only does the target not remember the world, but the world does not remember the target - leaving them a shell of the individual they were with no connections.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:17:55-07:00","id":891841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=891216#post891216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell is incredibly easy to make with Mind, so I thought I'd try my hand at making it in an entirely new way. I made it Lasting because the idea is that you are removing something entirely, though if it's thought to be better with a duration then the Primary Factor would be duration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\">Tabula Rasa</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I disagree with how this spell would work. If you destroy their temporal sympathy that doesn't change their memories, it just makes them disconnected from the &quot;proof&quot; of those occurrences and experiences. I think what this spell would really do is make someone lose touch with their past to the point they would suddenly have sensations of &quot;was that really me?&quot; or &quot;are these memories my own?&quot; they'd still remember who they are but they'd have no reason to BELIEVE that's who they are, they'd suffer from a severe dissociation (and tilt). Unmaking Time can definitely swing the effect you described, but I don't think simply removing the time sympathy is enough. I think you'd need a combined spell to pull this.<br /> <br /> As an ongoing condition, though, I bet a person suffering from this dissociation WOULD start forgetting their past and maybe even their Skills, but I think this would be a gradual progression like Soul Loss.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:43:40-07:00","id":891856,"title":"","content":"Body Control doesn't quite do what I want to do, so here's the adjustment (probably needs a better name):<br /> <br /> Metabolic Overdrive (Life 2)<br /> <br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> <br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athlethics, Expression, Medicine, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage overcharges the target's metabolism, giving all of the following benefict and drawbacks, stacking with itself per Potency:<ul><li>The healing rate of bashing damage is doubled</li> <li>Add +1 to the target's initiative</li> <li>Double the amount of oxygen consumed</li> <li>Halve the interval in which toxins and illnesses do damage</li> <li>Halve the amount of time between checks for deprivation and fatigue</li> </ul><br /> +1 Reach each: Each reach removes one drawback from the spell<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The rate of healing lethal damage is also doubled<br /> <br /> +3 Reach: As above, but at the cost of 1 Mana, the rate of healing aggravated damage is also doubled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":6508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","user":"Tambov","date":". 05-22-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:41:04-07:00","id":891891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=891841#post891841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I disagree with how this spell would work. If you destroy their temporal sympathy that doesn't change their memories, it just makes them disconnected from the &quot;proof&quot; of those occurrences and experiences. I think what this spell would really do is make someone lose touch with their past to the point they would suddenly have sensations of &quot;was that really me?&quot; or &quot;are these memories my own?&quot; they'd still remember who they are but they'd have no reason to BELIEVE that's who they are, they'd suffer from a severe dissociation (and tilt). Unmaking Time can definitely swing the effect you described, but I don't think simply removing the time sympathy is enough. I think you'd need a combined spell to pull this.<br /> <br /> As an ongoing condition, though, I bet a person suffering from this dissociation WOULD start forgetting their past and maybe even their Skills, but I think this would be a gradual progression like Soul Loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that both effects could could be pulled off, however I think what your describing would actually be more of a patterning effect lowering or distancing a person from Strong connections to medium or weak connections. I'm not sure I see that same result for disconnecting someone from their past of 1 second ago. Your example feels like it would be something that was still actually connected -weakly, sure but the connection is still there. In this, your removing it entirely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mind you, this effect was thought up from the statement that you destroy an objects past and people will forget it's history so I thought it'd be a cool trick <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":".  added more 05-16-2016, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T19:59:12-07:00","id":892215,"title":"","content":"Ghostly projection (Death **** Patterning)<br /> Primary: Duration<br /> Effect<br /> After creating ectoplasm (pg 129 Ectoplasm Death **) a mage can try to project themselves through this ectoplasm and temporally act as a ghost. While acting as a ghost this projected form uses the highest of the mage's traits to establish the power, finesse and resistance of this ephemeral form. They still retain their ability of gnosis and arcana but it is often taxing to use magic while in this form (Maintaining both ectoplasm and this spell so reach adds up).<br /> A mage can only move away from their body as far as the scale factor of this spell when cast. <hr /><br /> Far from perfect but the idea is that the mage shapes present ectoplasm into a form that they can project their soul through. I am unsure what the reach effects should be so any feedback or suggestions are appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T03:06:22-07:00","id":892404,"title":"","content":"There's a safer way to do that, move to Twilight, thus becoming ephemera, then use Patterning to give yourself a Manifestation. No body left behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T08:55:03-07:00","id":892555,"title":"","content":"I don't think ghostly projection needs to be limited by Scale factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:12:56-07:00","id":892856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=892215#post892215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghostly projection (Death **** Patterning)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems more restrictive than Twilit Body or Psychic Projection, for not much more utility. Perhaps something like this? May be a bit far in the other direction.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Morbid Projection (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Stealth</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage slackens the connection between the subject's self and their mortal form, causing them to become a deathlike projection - a living ghost. Their ephemeral form uses the rules for Dream Forms (Chapter six) and is present in (and tangible to) ghostly Twilight, leaving the body in a comatose state with no signs of life (as Suppress Life.) Anything carried on the body may be echoed in deathly ephemera if desired, but this morbid reflection dooms mortal objects - their material forms will be destroyed, leaving only ghostly echoes, at some point before the end of the story.<br /> If the ephemeral projection is destroyed, the subject returns to their body with the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The projection may be passed through an Avernian gate within range during its creation, causing the subject's consciousness to undergo a sojourn to the Underworld as a half-ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As an instant action, the subject may sculpt and reshape their ephemeral body, as per Shape Ephemera. One shaping may be maintained at a time for each Potency of the spell; any shapings in excess of this replace old ones.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage creates an ectoplasmic shell anchored to the projection. For the duration of the spell the subject's ghostly form is effectively mirrored by this medium, allowing it to be perceived by non-ephemeral beings. It remains intangible, barring the use of other magic.<br /> <b>+2 Reach and +1 Mana cost:</b> As above, save that the projection is effectively Manifested through the ectoplasmic medium and may interact normally with material beings and objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T16:16:56-07:00","id":892861,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a>, I was debating how to make it stronger without going too far. I do like the write up you have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:40:56-07:00","id":893492,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Invisible Fence (Life \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Survival, Intimidation<br /> <br /> You can make an area or perimeter feel unwelcome on a primal level. The instincts flare and the need to flee overcomes the desire to progress. If a living creature were to attempt to enter an area, or cross a boundary, affected by this spell; that creature must succeed on a Composure+Supernatural Tolerance roll penalized by the spell's Potency in order to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> A failed check imposes the Spooked Condition on the creature.<br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022:</b> The mage can select a number of subjects, based on scale, that may pass unhindered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:04:26-07:00","id":893646,"title":"","content":"So Ban can create a pocket space, and co-location can bend spaces together. What about a spell that can shut down a door or similar portal structure? Or is this too similar to Secrete Door which merely masks the door?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lock Portal (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Crafts, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Where a mundane or magic portal, isis, is already established, this spell makes passage through it impossible for the duration. Doors lock, passcodes fail, trails end. Archways and otherwise open portals &quot;brick up&quot; the space / material around the space fills in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>+1Reach</b> The sympathy connects of the portal are likewise suppressed. People Conveniently forget the passageway in favor of other means, or know the area beyond but can't remember how to get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:14:10-07:00","id":893794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=893492#post893492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Invisible Fence (Life \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Survival, Intimidation<br /> <br /> You can make an area or perimeter feel unwelcome on a primal level. The instincts flare and the need to flee overcomes the desire to progress. If a living creature were to attempt to enter an area, or cross a boundary, affected by this spell; that creature must succeed on a Composure+Supernatural Tolerance roll penalized by the spell's Potency in order to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> A failed check imposes the Spooked Condition on the creature.<br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022:</b> The mage can select a number of subjects, based on scale, that may pass unhindered.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Use the Withstand rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:15:21-07:00","id":893797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=893646#post893646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ban can create a pocket space, and co-location can bend spaces together. What about a spell that can shut down a door or similar portal structure? Or is this too similar to Secrete Door which merely masks the door?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lock Portal (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Crafts, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Where a mundane or magic portal, isis, is already established, this spell makes passage through it impossible for the duration. Doors lock, passcodes fail, trails end. Archways and otherwise open portals &quot;brick up&quot; the space / material around the space fills in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>+1Reach</b> The sympathy connects of the portal are likewise suppressed. People Conveniently forget the passageway in favor of other means, or know the area beyond but can't remember how to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, read this at first thinking Keys already cover this, but it actually seems pretty badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:56:09-07:00","id":893855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=893794#post893794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Use the Withstand rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Right.<br /> I'm still too accustomed to rolling a check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T23:11:04-07:00","id":893869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=893646#post893646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lock Portal (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Crafts, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Where a mundane or magic portal, isis, is already established, this spell makes passage through it impossible for the duration. Doors lock, passcodes fail, trails end. Archways and otherwise open portals &quot;brick up&quot; the space / material around the space fills in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>+1Reach</b> The sympathy connects of the portal are likewise suppressed. People Conveniently forget the passageway in favor of other means, or know the area beyond but can't remember how to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>IRIS, not Isis - first is magical portal in <b>Mage</b>. Second it terrorist organization ( also, Queen Goddess of Ancient Egypt ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:37:49-07:00","id":893957,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Great Equalizer (Death 3)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> <i>Perfecting</i><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> <i>Duration</i><br /> <b>Cost:</b> <i>1 Mana</i><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b><i> Weaponry, Medicine, Intimidation</i><br /> <br /> <i>Grim Reaper has always reminded humanity that no matter who you are, people are all equal in the face of Death. This spell embraces this quality - weapon targeted by it always deals at least Lethal Damage, ignoring Potence points of Armor, and ignoring qualities - supernatural or not - that would degrade the type of Damage. This means that this weapon will deal Lethal Damage to Vampires, for example.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: For each point of Potency assigned to the spell, you may increase Weapon Rating by one. This may not go beyond 5.<br /> +2 Reach: As above, but you may go beyond 5 if you also spend a point of Mana.<br /> +2 Reach: If you pay a Mana, trying to heal damage dealt by this Weapon using Supernatural means provokes a Clash of Will. </i><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if Reach option should increase the Weapon Rating by 1-per-1 basis, or should it be more something 2 potency for 1 Weapon Rating. Weapon Rating is pretty powerful, much more than equipment bonuses - one WR is like 3 bonus rolled dice at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-19-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:57:03-07:00","id":894168,"title":"","content":"If it turned out to be a problem you could do something like &quot;+1 Reach: The weapon's rating is increased by one or set to the Potency of the spell - whichever is higher.&quot;<br /> <br /> Riffing on your theme:<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mortal Frailty (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Weaponry, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <br /> This spell reasserts Death's claim on a subject, overcoming supernatural resilience. For the duration of the spell, the subject suffers lethal damage from any source that would cause lethal damage to a normal human; a manifested spirit or ambulatory corpse finds that blades and guns are just as fearsome to them as to a flesh-and-blood mortal. This affects a number of injuries equal to the spell's Potency during the course of its Duration.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> All injuries during the spell's Duration are affected.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and +1 Mana cost (</b>maybe<b>):</b> The subject will suffer aggravated damage from sources that deal aggravated harm to normal humans.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Attacks against the subject gain the armor-piercing quality, rated at the spell's Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Any reflexive or instant action taken to heal the subject by supernatural means provokes a Clash of Wills*.<br /> <br /> * This wording exempts most of werewolf regen, which isn't an action, but would technically interfere with spending essence to speed lethal healing up, if that's not considered an innate feature of the template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 05-19-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:31:30-07:00","id":894196,"title":"","content":"+1 Reach for aggravated damage should also charge a mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:01:27-07:00","id":894255,"title":"","content":"Maybe? I see the reasoning, but the spell doesn't cause agg damage (like the unraveling spells do) or even create a source of aggravated damage (as Prime 3 can). I was thinking that made it more akin to Fate 3's Grave Misfortune, which can cause additional aggravated damage but cannot inflict it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:18:27-07:00","id":894273,"title":"","content":"Hmm, good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T15:00:10-07:00","id":894343,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thank you, I was thinking the same thing but I wanted to really touch upon mundane portals Windows Trails and Archways, and really look at the Meta application of Space. And Ban and Co-location gave me good idea of seperation and overlapping. I was looking at Break the Bonds, Lying Map and thought, why can't we do this reverse? But I needed the higher level to Solidify what I wanted the spell to do. The Bricking up of an archway into a solid wall part really amuses me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Seeing as how you understood the intent, and its repeated in the same line before hand. I think we understood each other Mate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A simple spelling error is all.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a><br /> I like the idea of ignoring armor; It goes well with destroying an prevention of death. but I believe adding the two effects with one spell is a little much. and it sounds like you want to combine two different spells effects, which is possible at gnosis three. Five Eyes has the right idea.<br /> <br /> If you scaled back down to bashing, you could easily justify dropping the cost down to zero. And include that the armor penetration also ignores supernatural armor. While at the same time including a Reach component that gives the item (Potency) Lethal Rating. Splitting the themes allows you to scale the one effect you want better. Image taking on a Roit Squad with a Pencil. THE PEN IS MIGHTIER THAN THE SWORD -stab- -bleeding out-<br /> <br /> Now how about this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bgXH3sJ2Q\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bgXH3sJ2Q\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bgXH3sJ2Q\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4bgXH3sJ2Q </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kill Box (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Firearms, Intimidation<br /> <br /> On this battlefield noone wins. An area determined by scale is afflicted with the Environment Tilt, -Kill Box-. Any damage afflicted in the area gains a number of bashing damage equal to potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1Reach</b> Characters entering or already in the area gain the Shaken Tilt; as less than obvious cues, raven's call, snapped twiggs, frayed wires, a putrid smell, ect alert her of the danger of the area without revealing the source.<br /> <br /> <b>+1Reach</b> Additional Damage is Lethal instead of bashing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T10:34:52-07:00","id":895553,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Offering Table (Death </span></b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Practice: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Crafts, Socialize<br /> <br /> The Master of Death conjures up a feast for the departed. This spell creates a number of ephemeral goods equal to the spell's Scale; these objects usually take on the forms of things offered to the dead in various cultures: candy, bread, money, liquor, and so forth. The area of the offering gains the Resonant Condition for all ghosts, and any ghost who partakes of the offerings gains Essence equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The offering area gains the Open Condition for ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Mortals who partake of the feast become infused with the power of the Underworld, gaining the ability to see unmanifested ghosts for the spell's Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As above, but instead, a feasting mortal gains the Open Condition for the spell's Duration.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T11:39:32-07:00","id":895599,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11641_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11641\" data-vbnamecard=\"11641\">Yelesom</a> . Lure and Repel (p. 149), basically does the same as your Rote, Lure and Repel just has some more flexibility to it. But with the Tilt aspect of it, I think it could have its own uses. But I regrettably have no real suggestions -.-' .. Maybe give the Shaken Tilt to the targets as a &quot;weakened&quot; version of the Reach?<br /> =========================<br /> Here is my own attempt at making a custom Rote<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">False Health (Life \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>suggested rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Brawl, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The subjects health seem to be fine even if it is actually suffering from wounds, diseases or toxins. If it is already suffering from wounds, these seem to cover up and bruises fade. If the subjects is bleeding out (Health full of lethal), this power does not prevent the bleeding. \u200bYou may also instead seem hurt, even though you are not.<br /> <br /> If the subject contains any toxins and is tested with mundane means or with Matter; the toxins can be detected (unless Matter 2 is also used in casting of this Rote), but the subject's body will still seem fine. Supernatural senses that can scan the subjects health triggers a Clash of Will as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject can seem much healthier than it looks. Add the spells potency as fake bonus Stamina. No bonus is gained from this extra Stamina.<br /> <br /> To wordy? To weak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":".  Messed up the Arcana 05-21-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T11:43:19-07:00","id":895602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=895599#post895599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11641_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11641\" data-vbnamecard=\"11641\">Yelesom</a> . Lure and Repel (p. 149), basically does the same as your Rote, Lure and Repel just has some more flexibility to it. But with the Tilt aspect of it, I think it could have its own uses. But I regrettably have no real suggestions -.-' .. Maybe give the Shaken Tilt to the targets as a &quot;weakened&quot; version of the Reach?<br /> =========================<br /> Here is my own attempt at making a custom Rote<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">False Health</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>suggested rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Brawl, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The subjects health seem to be fine even if it is actually suffering from wounds, diseases or toxins. If it is already suffering from wounds, these seem to cover up and bruises fade. If the subjects is bleeding out (Health full of lethal), this power does not prevent the bleeding. \u200bYou may also instead seem hurt, even though you are not.<br /> <br /> If the subject contains any toxins and is tested with mundane means or with Matter; the toxins can be detected (unless Matter 2 is also used in casting of this Rote), but the subject's body will still seem fine. Supernatural senses that can scan the subjects health triggers a Clash of Will as normal.<br /> <b><br /> +1 Reach:</b> The subject can seem much healthier than it looks. Add the spells potency as fake bonus Stamina. No bonus is gained from this extra Stamina.<br /> <br /> To wordy? To weak?</div> </div> </div> </div>WHat's the arcane? Death/Life? But yeah that seems like neat spell, and it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T11:58:21-07:00","id":895613,"title":"","content":"Dough!! Off course I forget the most important thing.. It was Life \u2022\u2022 and I have corrected it :P<br /> But I guess it could be Death to, since you aren't hiding Life (except maybe in the case of diseases), but the wounds there is. Aka, the &quot;Death&quot;. But just hiding diseases seems like a rather underwhelming Rote :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 05-22-2016, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:35:18-07:00","id":895710,"title":"","content":"Oh, one other.<br /> <br /> <b>Nihilism (Death </b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b><b>: </b>Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <br /> As below, so above. The mage infuses the subject with the Underworld's tableuaux of abject self-abuse. The subject of the spell gains the Wonton Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject's Virtue and Vice are switched, as if they were in the Autochthonous Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T01:35:56-07:00","id":895988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=895710#post895710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The subject of the spell gains the Wonton Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the Wonton Condition? Can't find it in the CoD or MtA book.Otherwise, it sounds interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:05:51-07:00","id":896042,"title":"","content":"There is a Wanton Condition in Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T07:20:16-07:00","id":896070,"title":"","content":"That's the one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:22:41-07:00","id":899814,"title":"","content":"Stabilize (Life <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Practice: compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency</span></span><br /> Suggested Rote skills: Medicine, Athletics, Survival<br /> <br /> If a character is gravely wounded they might undergo surgery under sleeper care to stabilize (If bleeding out) Or simply help them recover. The roll is an extended Medicine + Intelligence roll once per hour with successes equal to boxes of damage (See WoD Pg96) Potency of this spell counts as successes already gained on this roll greatly increasing the chances of such an action succeeding within the time limit.<br /> It's subtle enough to not be noticed even under direct scrutiny of sleepers, Rates of bleeding from major arteries slow but don't heal, organs continue to function with diminished blood where they might otherwise shut-down.<br /> <br /> A weird one but a character I play did actually use this one time when an ally was begin operated on by a sleeper doctor. The doctor didn't notice the &quot;Extra&quot; nurse who silently slinked in sat in the corner of the theater. Not stealing his thunder, just giving him a helping hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:34:21-07:00","id":899821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pebbles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=899814#post899814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stabilize (Life <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Practice: compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency</span></span><br /> Suggested Rote skills: Medicine, Athletics, Survival</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not have Reach option to use on another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:37:30-07:00","id":899825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=899821#post899821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should not have Reach option to use on another?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't inherently need Reach to cast on someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T00:53:47-07:00","id":899837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=899825#post899825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't inherently need Reach to cast on someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any spell? All powers in corebook stated works on both you or other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avat