_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T01:06:30-07:00","id":899844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=899837#post899837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any spell? All powers in corebook stated works on both you or other?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\">This is not new information</a> and has literally been known for almost two years now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2e Dev Blog &quot;Paradoxical&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, spells are cast in ritual time (as defined by Gnosis), on the caster or something the caster is touching, using the basic versions of all spell factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:04:48-07:00","id":901043,"title":"","content":"The following is born out of one of my player's frustration caused by not being able to alchemically transform one substance into another before Matter 4:<br /> <br /> <b>Close Enough</b> (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Occult, Science<br /> <br /> This spell transforms one substance into another, as long as both are conceptually related. A glass of water can be turned into wine, lead can be turned into gold, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:16:22-07:00","id":901058,"title":"","content":"So again a few ideas:<br /> <br /> Never lost (Space*)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Key factor: Duration<br /> A mage with basic understanding of Space is never lost. This spell allows the subject to instinctively locate known places. He can determine the direction in which he'll find any one place per dot of Potency he has visited. Alternatively for one dot of Potency he can know which way is north.<br /> +1 Reach: The subject can determine his general location ( &quot;Jakarta&quot;, &quot;Saharan desert&quot;, &quot;the Amazonian Jungle&quot;)<br /> +2 Reach: The subject knows his specific locations (&quot;apartment 5, baker street 29, Misteryville&quot;)<br /> <br /> Surestep (Forces **)<br /> Practice: Rulling<br /> Keyfactor: Duration<br /> The mage manipulates gravity and friction is such way that allows the subject to walk on any surface able to support his weight be it slippery ice or a rope stretched between two buildings. Ignore any relevant tilts or conditions<br /> +2 Reach: The subject can also freely walk on vertical surfaces.<br /> <br /> Illusion (Forces ****) [could be Forces ****** and making]<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Keyfactor: Duration<br /> The mage manipulates light to create an mirage. The spells Scale factor determines the size of the mirage, while the mage can create one illusion per dot of potency. It is fully sight dependant and static unless the actively spends a turn concentrating and controlling it,<br /> +1 Reach: The illusion also has audible effects<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can program the illusion to change and move in a predermined way.<br /> +2 Reach, Mind ***&quot; Not only is the illusion mobile but it is capable of reacting to what's happening around it in a basic way the same way something it represents would react For instance an illusion of a person might bleed when shot or an illusion of a cat might flee is someone aproaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T06:55:17-07:00","id":902013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=901043#post901043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The following is born out of one of my player's frustration caused by not being able to alchemically transform one substance into another before Matter 4:<br /> <br /> <b>Close Enough</b> (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Occult, Science<br /> <br /> This spell transforms one substance into another, as long as both are conceptually related. A glass of water can be turned into wine, lead can be turned into gold, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this is a perfectly valid application of Weaving. You see, with Weaving you can reconfigure a feature of a pattern to be the same feature from a different pattern that naturally exists. So, taste and color of one beverage could be given to another one, etc. I have a version of this spell on my own lists, though I called it Transubstantiation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T01:16:49-07:00","id":902554,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Warden of Life (Life \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Brawl, Expression<br /> <br /> The body isn\u2019t just meat and bones; It is a vessel for the soul. With this spell a mage can protect the subject\u2019s living pattern, or the pattern of living beings in the area, from being tampered with by the Life Arcana. Any attempt to alter the subject\u2019s living pattern must succeed at a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Magic and powers from other supernatural beings that would alter the living pattern of the subject are likewise affected.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a Key that allows the subjects pattern to be altered.<br /> <b>+2 Reach (Edited):</b> The protection afforded by this spell extends to physical attacks from living beings, where the attacker suffers the potency of the spell as a penalty. This protection doesn't work if inanimate objects are used, like swords, clubs, ect.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> Not sure about the Suggested Rote Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":".  It was abit to powerful and I added some more text to explain some things 05-31-2016, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:26:06-07:00","id":902703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=902554#post902554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Warden of Life (Life \u2022\u2022)</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Almost total physical immunity for two dots? Not sure if I like it...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:04:19-07:00","id":902750,"title":"","content":"Boost it to 3 and make it optimized towards specific thing. use Sworn Oath as a spell to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:17:46-07:00","id":902790,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Phasing (Space \u2022\u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Brawl, Stealth<br /> <br /> You are here; but at the same time, you aren't. By carefully manipulating space your body occupies, you are protected against all physical attacks - they just pass through your body. People are still able to see, hear and smell you; mental and magical attacks work as normal. Liquids and gases don't affect you, but you are still able to be blinded, deafened and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By passing the light through the body to the other side, you are invisible as well.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can manipulate objects, carry items and physically attack your enemies.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Aimed spells won't work on you - enemy needs to attack your Pattern directly to harm you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:54:29-07:00","id":902810,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Death Perception (Death \u2022, Life \u2022</b></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Medicine, Brawl<br /> <br /> Destruction is easy, if you know the structure of a target - attack it's weak point for a massive damage. You combine your knowledge of life and death to find the most weak point of a target - the pillar upon which it's existence stands. If you successfully physically damage enemy in hit locations (arms, legs, head, heart, hands or foots) while this spell works, reduce Stamina of enemy by Potency for counting infliction of Tilt (for example, in you successfully strike your enemy with Stamina 4 in arm while this spell with Potency 2, he gets Arm Wrack Tilt on 3 or more damage).<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Apply Potency of a spell to damage. You only get additional damage if you target and successfully strike enemy in hit location with at least 1 point of damage. Type of damage does not change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:49:00-07:00","id":902989,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>In Two Places at Once (Space \u2022\u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Crafts, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Many people are aware of Banach-Tarski paradox: you can decompose ball in certain way into unmeasureable parts and reconstruct two balls from these parts, which are in all ways identical to the original one. This idea inspired you to do the same; however, in your spell these parts are still connected with each other, and every change in one part is causing identical change in another one (any attempts to get rid of this caused Paradox whenever spell duration ended and two different conditions clashed in one object).<br /> Your spell create an identical copy of subject (or object) in the place you want. Those copies are, in a way, one object - destruction of one will correspond with destruction of another, and so on. Because of that, copy is absolute for all means and purposes. When Duration of spell ends, created copy disappears. You can create a copy of living being, but because you aren't creating two different minds to control two bodies, this leads only to confusion of this being (unless it can multitask naturally or with Mind spell). As with inanimate objects, any change in one &quot;copy&quot; leads to similar change in another one. With addition of Time you can delay these changes in another copy until end of spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 05-29-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T18:01:52-07:00","id":903144,"title":"","content":"Seems more like Co-Location on a single target instead of an area, much the way it worked in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:46:03-07:00","id":903360,"title":"","content":"I was a little unsure about how balanced it was myself, which was also the reason I posted it. But I based the spell mostly on Ephemeral Shield (which can protect against attacks as well) and partly on the Ward spell. However, I am not sure how Clash of Wills work when dealing with normal attacks since its not a supernatural thing being done. So the attacker rolls xxxx + Power Stat first and then their attack dice pool? Wouldn't it be easier and simpler to just say that Potency gave a penalty to the attack roll?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=902703#post902703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost total physical immunity for two dots? Not sure if I like it...</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was the subject was Shielded from life, meaning; the subject is only affected by the attacks of living beings. It wouldn't protect against inanimate things like a sword or club. This aspect of the Reach, I completely forgot to put in there though :P<br /> But I do think I should make it more than +1 now though. +3 might to high since it is still easily gotten around, and if cast as an AoE spell, everything would be affected by this rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=902750#post902750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boost it to 3 and make it optimized towards specific thing. use Sworn Oath as a spell to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like specific living beings? Or specific types of attacks?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T03:02:03-07:00","id":903363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=902554#post902554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Warden of Life (Life \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Brawl, Expression<br /> <br /> The body isn\u2019t just meat and bones; It is a vessel for the soul. With this spell a mage can protect the subject\u2019s living pattern, or the pattern of living beings in the area, from being tampered with by the Life Arcana. Any attempt to alter the subject\u2019s living pattern must succeed at a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Magic and powers from other supernatural beings that would alter the living pattern of the subject are likewise affected.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The protection afforded by this spell extends to physical attacks from living beings.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a Key that allows the subjects pattern to be altered.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> Not sure about the Suggested Rote Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is almost as the fourth dot attainmente...as function and level of power.<br /> And with the second reach, is better too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:34:40-07:00","id":903748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=903363#post903363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is almost as the fourth dot attainmente...as function and level of power.<br /> And with the second reach, is better too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that means a spell can't exist. I wouldn't allow the reach to allow a clash of wills for simply being physically attacked, though. That's not how Clash of Wills works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:36:34-07:00","id":904012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=903363#post903363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is almost as the fourth dot attainmente...as function and level of power.<br /> And with the second reach, is better too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a> said, a spell to protect life should be exist since shielding yourself against the Arcanas aspect is a thing. With spirit, you can shield yourself from a spirit's supernatural AND physical attacks after all. And as fare as I know, a spirit Attainment that does the same as the fourth Life Attainment can exist, since the Attainments in the book are just samples.<br /> <br /> But I agree with you to some extend <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, that it might be to good compared to the Attainment. The Attainment however, has its own strengths, like not being a spell counts against your spell control and it can be used reflexively, which no spells can't. They are either Instant, or Ritual Casted. So you don't have to cast it before hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:25:45-07:00","id":904052,"title":"","content":"Which practice would it be for a shaman to be able to speak and understand First Tongue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:43:02-07:00","id":904069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904052#post904052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which practice would it be for a shaman to be able to speak and understand First Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Unveiling or Knowing to understand it at least, I believe there's already a spell in the book that does just that however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:04:44-07:00","id":904076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904052#post904052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which practice would it be for a shaman to be able to speak and understand First Tongue?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Spirit Arcanum. The entities of the Shadow use that language, so as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said, there is already a spell that lets you speak and understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:24:31-07:00","id":904134,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dead Mind (Mind \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Your thoughts freeze; your mind is still. You can act, but you don't think about it; you just act. This spell makes it much harder to read your thoughts, intentions or mental presence. Apply the spell\u2019s Potency as a penalty to relevant Skill rolls (such as Empathy or Subterfuge) between the subjects. You may not reduce Skill rolls below their default - your penalty can only cancel bonuses from telepathy, ability to read emotions and so on.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You may also apply the spell\u2019s Potency as a bonus to Withstand any attempts to locate you with Mind magic.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You may also apply the spell\u2019s Potency as a bonus to Withstand any attempts to inflict Mental Condition or Tilt on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 05-31-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:34:41-07:00","id":904139,"title":"","content":"Isn't Veiling a two dot Practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:01:25-07:00","id":904155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904139#post904139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Veiling a two dot Practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:25:52-07:00","id":904172,"title":"","content":"I would make the addition to Withstand a Reach clause, unless I'm misreading it and that's the actual benefit of the spell instead of eleminating the bonuses from telepathy, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T08:48:27-07:00","id":904199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904069#post904069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's Unveiling or Knowing to understand it at least, I believe there's already a spell in the book that does just that however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Exorcist's Eye, maybe? I thought that it, like the 2 dot attainment, only made it possible to speak to spirits that you otherwise can't because of Twilight, slumber, etc. I'll ask in the other thread. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T11:51:33-07:00","id":904329,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Transparency (Matter \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> One of the best ways to hide something is to make it invisible. One possible way to do this is to manipulate Forces, forcing light to go though object; the other possible way is to make everybody unsee it with Mind. This spell uses Matter for that effect - it simply makes the matter of object completely transparent. This does not change mass, density or other properties of object, though if it have functions which depend on ability to block light (solar panels, for example), then it can't function anymore. You can wear armor and weapons in this way, and nobody will notice unless you go though scanner or be searched physically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Grease (Matter \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>) </b>and <b>Glue (Matter \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Scale: Area<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Brawl, Survival<br /> <br /> The easy way to turn the tide of physical combat and make those damn wheels spin, those spells changes the properties of matter it cast upon, causing the following Environmental Tilts:<br /> <b>Grease </b>create <b>Ice</b> Tilt in area it cast upon.<br /> <b>Glue </b>create <b>Glue</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tilt</span> in area it cast upon: -4 to Speed, Dramatic Failure causes <b>Immobilized </b>Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 05-31-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:23:21-07:00","id":904445,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mass Distortion (Forces \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Firearms<br /> <br /> Cube-square law is a Lie. Yet Force mage can use this lie to his own advantage by making mass of his enemy so huge that his own muscles and bones crush under titanic weight of his body. This spell deals bashing damage equal to its Potency. This damage ignores all kinds of armor, including most Mage armor, with exception of Prime Armor. The damage also depends on a Size of an subject: -1 per unit of Size below 5, +1 per unit of Size above 5. This spell won't work on enemy who does not have any weight, including spirits, ghosts, immaterial Abyssal intruders, etc.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Mage increases the mass even further, literally collapsing target with it's own weight. The spell deals lethal damage. Cost: 1 Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:34:27-07:00","id":904454,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Myopia (Forces \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Firearms, Crafts<br /> <br /> Many people suffer from myopia, and with his spell mage can his enemies to this list by disrupting light patterns near enemy. This spell places a <b>Myopic </b>Condition on enemy: -1 to all vision-related rolls per dot of Potency. Note that while his Defence suffers from this penalty, he still can use his full Defence for Dodge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 06-01-2016, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T21:37:35-07:00","id":904709,"title":"","content":"Inspired by another thread...<br /> <br /> <b>Terminator (Matter 4)<br /> Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Science, Computer, Medicine<br /> <b>Requirement: </b>Temporal Sympathy (Time 2)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>+1 Reach and 1 Mana (for Temporal Sympathy)<br /> <br /> The mage builds a servant (see the Golem spell) using the materials at a location or subject substance or object in the past. Use the rules of Temporal Sympathy to determine how far back in Time the Golem can be created. The servant can perform changes to the past while the spell is active. When the spell's duration elapses, the servant crumbles and any changes it has performed become Lasting. The servant can only perform simple tasks related to its chosen field.<br /> <b>Add Mind 5:</b> The mage can provide the servant with a full mind (see Psychic Genesis) to help it with its tasks and allow it to better improvise. This can be a a copy of the mage's own mind.<br /> <b>Add Life 2:</b> The servant can be disguised as a living being. <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The servant can be made of liquid metal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:15:58-07:00","id":904799,"title":"","content":"uhmm Time 2 is too low: with Time 2 you cannot bring yourself back; at least Time 3 for some turn, or scene....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:44:47-07:00","id":904810,"title":"","content":"I miss old Prime phantasms; at the same time, I really don't see why we can't bring them back. So I did:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Phantasm (Prime \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Crafts, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> This spell creates an inanimate phantasm, a construct woven of Mana threads. Such a creation possesses a degree of substance and appears to be a normal object of its type to Sleeping eyes, but is in reality a solidified illusion. The mage can create books, knives, chairs, stones or any other lifeless, inanimate objects she can think of. These objects do not and cannot possess qualities such as conductivity, magnetism or the like, because they aren't matter in the magical sense of this word.<br /> The spell creates an object of Size 5 or less. The phantasm has one point of Durability. It is fragile and breaks easily. The mage cannot create functional tools, weapons or armor at this level. To create a convincing illusion, a reflexive Intelligence + appropriate Skill roll is required, and excess successes on the casting add one die each to this roll. To simulate an animal, use Animal Ken. For an object, use Crafts. For a person, use Medicine or perhaps Empathy.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage creates a more sturdy phantasm, which can be functional tool, weapon or armor. Weapons created in this way deal lethal damage, and armor works as normal armor.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Created object has simultaneously Ephemeral Enchantment casted on it.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The mage imbues phantasm with celestial power, creating a short-timed magical item. Weapon, created in this way, deals aggravated damage, and armor works as Prime Armor in addition to being normal armor at the same time. Cost: 1 Mana.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 06-01-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T04:15:15-07:00","id":904846,"title":"","content":"Isn't this pretty much covered by Platonic Form already? Granted, that spell has a mana cost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T10:22:05-07:00","id":905039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904846#post904846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this pretty much covered by Platonic Form already? Granted, that spell has a mana cost</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Platonic Form is more about storing Tass. You also can't really use it as tool effectively, because &quot;profane matter of the Fallen World corrupts the purity of the Form&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:09:20-07:00","id":905059,"title":"","content":"I know, but it's basically how it works in 2e.<br /> <br /> Y'know, it'd probably be easier to just develop a Shielding spell that prevents a Platonic Form from hemorrhaging mana by protecting it from that corruption of the Fallen World. You could also make such protection a Reach option of Platonic Form. I feel that either of those options would be better than creating a spell which is functionally identical with the one thing that makes the original undesirable removed.<br /> <br /> I'd also put complex items as a Platonic Form that can be made via Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-01-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:09:28-07:00","id":905095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904799#post904799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">uhmm Time 2 is too low: with Time 2 you cannot bring yourself back; at least Time 3 for some turn, or scene....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Read the text of Temporal Sympathy again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:15:24-07:00","id":905169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904709#post904709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by another thread...<br /> <br /> The servant can perform changes to the past while the spell is active. When the spell's duration elapses, the servant crumbles and any changes it has performed become Lasting. The servant can only perform simple tasks related to its chosen field.</div> </div> </div> </div>I re read, but for &quot;come back&quot; yourself, you need time 3.<br /> I doubt that you can create a golem &quot;on the past&quot; that can change the past, at Time 2.<br /> Can you give me more input about your point?<br /> Edit: If you can come back at Time 2, why Shifting Sands need Time 3?","signature":"","edited"