ess/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T03:35:37-07:00","id":906302,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lightning Javelin (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Streetwise, Crafts, Firearms<br /> <br /> Grasp firmly the spear of lightning, and let it sunder your foes just a surely. With this spell you can pull a charge of electricity out of a source and hold onto it. You can make a thrown attack while holding this charge. A success allows you to release any amount of that charge as damage. Any remainder stays in your grasp for another attack, unless you let go of it or the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Half Potency rounded up is added as bonus dice for the throwing attack.<br /> <br /> Example: I pull a charge out of a wall socket, giving me 4B to work with. Succeeding on an attack, I choose to use 2B as damage. I have 2B remaining in my hand, ready for another attack next turn.<br /> <br /> Anything I need to tweak with this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 06-03-2016, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T03:40:36-07:00","id":906305,"title":"","content":"I would just remind the caster that he'd better shield himself before grabbing a bolt of electricity or he's going to get electrocuted. Pretty cool idea though, and of course now I'm thinking of how to do that with other types of energy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:19:40-07:00","id":906519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906302#post906302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lightning Javelin (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Streetwise, Crafts, Firearms<br /> <br /> Grasp firmly the spear of lightning, and let it sunder your foes just a surely. With this spell you can pull a charge of electricity out of a source and hold onto it. You can make a thrown attack while holding this charge. A success allows you to release any amount of that charge as damage. Any remainder stays in your grasp for another attack, unless you let go of it or the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Half Potency rounded up is added as bonus dice for the throwing attack.<br /> <br /> Example: I pull a charge out of a wall socket, giving me 4B to work with. Succeeding on an attack, I choose to use 2B as damage. I have 2B remaining in my hand, ready for another attack next turn.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anything I need to tweak with this one?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906305#post906305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just remind the caster that he'd better shield himself before grabbing a bolt of electricity or he's going to get electrocuted. Pretty cool idea though, and of course now I'm thinking of how to do that with other types of energy as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Through Ruling you are controlling exactly what the electricity is doing, which as defined by this Imago is holding a shape of a javelin which you can throw at people and not a charge running down your arm to ground itself out which is what would be electrocuting you. If it holds the javelin shape while held then by definition it isn't killing the mage using it.<br /> <br /> Though it could be argued that it may take Weaving to make the electricity to take such a shape instead of Ruling to give the electricity the properties needed to be held without grounding out. I can see it both ways, with Ruling taking much more intense concentration every round the power is held, and Weaving being cast and forget.<br /> <br /> I'd add that if the duration elapses while the charge is held, the charge grounds out on the caster.<br /> <br /> I think where this spell would be better than just arcing the power straight from the source is that it creates a weapon which can be brandished, used when needed, and carried to areas where there wasn't an electricity source to start with. When you need Electricity as something's Bane and the thing you are fighting has the power to extinguish or hide from mundane power sources, this spell would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:25:03-07:00","id":906524,"title":"","content":"And yet Mages are advised to take proper precautions when working with Forces because it's inherently dangerous. Electricity is specifically called out and the 4th dot attainment is specifically reduce the chances of a Mage frying himself by accident.<br /> <br /> You're free to rule it that way though I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:33:30-07:00","id":906789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906302#post906302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lightning Javelin (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Streetwise, Crafts, Firearms<br /> <br /> Grasp firmly the spear of lightning, and let it sunder your foes just a surely. With this spell you can pull a charge of electricity out of a source and hold onto it. You can make a thrown attack while holding this charge. A success allows you to release any amount of that charge as damage. Any remainder stays in your grasp for another attack, unless you let go of it or the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Half Potency rounded up is added as bonus dice for the throwing attack.<br /> <br /> Example: I pull a charge out of a wall socket, giving me 4B to work with. Succeeding on an attack, I choose to use 2B as damage. I have 2B remaining in my hand, ready for another attack next turn.<br /> <br /> Anything I need to tweak with this one?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Book<br /> Ruling spells grant fuller control over phenomena than a<br /> mere Compelling spell. Water can be made to flow uphill<br /> or into unnatural shapes (Matter), animals (or even human<br /> beings) can be commanded (Life or Mind), or time can be<br /> momentarily made to accelerate or slow down (Time). A<br /> Ruling spell can\u2019t fundamentally alter its target\u2019s abilities:<br /> Water can be directed, but not turned solid or gaseous.<br /> Time can be altered, but not overwritten. An animal can<br /> be commanded, but not made stronger or fiercer.<br /> <br /> Using the water as an example You can direct the flow of the lightening, but holding it without shocking yourself adds more complexity. An additional sheilding spell would do it. Mundane electrical protection would do it. but you just couldn't hold it in the way you want.<br /> <br /> But making it a weaving spell gets around the problem. You're not making/unmaking, you're not perfecting/transforming/breaking the lightening. You containing it and alterting its behavior/property to dicharge / swipe in an area.<br /> <br /> Weaving spells can alter nearly any property of a target<br /> without transforming it into something completely different.<br /> Solid steel can be transmuted to liquid (Matter),<br /> a sword can be enchanted to damage beings in Twilight<br /> (Death or Spirit), or a few seconds of time can be rewritten<br /> (Time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:34:28-07:00","id":906873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11731_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11731\" data-vbnamecard=\"11731\">MercSet</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> Hmm. I suppose making it Weaving is the way to go.<br /> Adding in melee attack option.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lightning Javelin (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Streetwise, Crafts, Firearms<br /> <br /> Grasp firmly the spear of lightning, and let it sunder your foes just a surely. With this spell you can pull a charge of electricity out of a source and hold onto it. You can make a melee or thrown attack while holding this charge. A success allows you to release any amount of that charge as damage. Any remainder stays in your grasp for another attack, unless you let go of it or the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Half Potency rounded up is added as bonus dice for the attack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:00:39-07:00","id":906964,"title":"","content":"I was looking for ways to make Prime more useful at dealing with mundane stuff, so I came up with this spell for manipulating your Nimbus Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Empower Nimbus (Prime 3)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Persuasion, Occult<br /> The mage can strengthen the subject\u2019s Nimbus, making their Nimbus Tilt more powerful. Choose an Attribute or Skill which the subject\u2019s Nimbus Tilt affects. If the Nimbus tilt applies a bonus to that trait, the bonus increases by the spell\u2019s potency. If a penalty, the penalty worsens by the spell\u2019s potency.<br /> If the mage targets himself with this spell, this spell affects its own Nimbus Flare as well.<br /> This spell also improves the Nimbus\u2019s ability to contest the auras of other supernatural creatures. Add the spell\u2019s Potency to any contested roll between the subject\u2019s aura and another creature\u2019s aura.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell affects an additional Attribute or Skill covered by the subject\u2019s Nimbus tilt. Divide the spell\u2019s Potency between both. This effect may be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Nimbus (Prime 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Persuasion, Occult<br /> The mage manipulates the subject\u2019s Nimbus. For the spell\u2019s duration, the mage can cause the Nimbus to flare when it would not, or to fail to flare when it otherwise would. The spell may also cause it to continuously flare, applying its Nimbus Tilt to those who see it for as long as they continue to see it flare. <br /> If the Nimbus has been detached from its owner, such as with the Sever Nimbus spell, this spell also allows the mage to move the Nimbus around within sensory range.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage may cause the subject's Nimbus to flare towards specific targets, applying the Nimbus tilt to them if they can see it, but not to others.<br /> <b>1 Mana:</b> The mage may reveal the subject\u2019s Nimbus to the Fallen World, affecting even those not using Mage Sight. Sleepers suffer Quiescence after the Tilt ends.<br /> <b>1 Mana:</b> The mage imprints the target's Signature Nimbus on a single object, place, or person. (See Signature Nimbus p.90)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-06-2016, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T22:48:35-07:00","id":906979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906873#post906873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Lightning Javelin (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks reasonable to me; do you envision the throws as respecting Defense?<br /> <br /> Does Potency limit the size of the electricity source used? You might have the attack deal damage as per the source and &quot;ablate&quot; one level of charge/Potency per use; this leads to more overall damage (instead of divvying up 6B into up to three hits, it hits thrice with less oomph each time) but can simplify book-keeping.<br /> <br /> Here's a riff on the theme - a translation of an old Wu Long rote, Thunder Bridge. This is a tricky one to translate, as its primary effects - short-range flight and a defensive aura - were secondary to its medium, a conjured bolt of lightning.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lei Gong's Raiment (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Athletics, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage harnesses a nearby source of electricity to wrap a subject in a crackling corona of lightning. While the spell anchors the aura and prevents an immediate discharge into the surroundings, anyone that moves or interacts with the subject after the aura is set suffers harm as if they'd come into contact with the power source. Unless they are shielded, this threatens the subject as well, who must remain still to avoid harm. The Potency of the effect determines how much charge can be settled into the aura (as per the chart under Transform Energy), and each discharge reduces the remaining Potency of the effect by one, making future strikes less vicious or negating the aura altogether.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Strikes do not reduce the Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b><b>:</b> The subject and aura's innate forces are harmonized to one another; the subject may move without harm. As a beneficial side effect, the subject is shielded from <i>other </i>sources of electricity, reducing their effective intensity by the Potency of the spell.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b><b>:</b> As above, and the aura exerts a modest &quot;lift&quot; on the subject. As long as the spell's Potency (treated as Strength) is sufficient to lift the subject's weight, they may, as an instant action, jump-float at a Speed of (Gnosis + Potency).<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject may &quot;throw&quot; the aura; it has range bands of (Potency x 10/Potency x 20/Potency x 40) and is aimed with Dexterity + Athletics - the target's Defense. A successful throw inflicts damage as a strike. If the subject is not protected in some way, they will be injured upon moving as usual. If the subject is being lifted by the aura (as in the +2 Reach option above), they may opt to &quot;ride&quot; a throw to its destination, the lightning carrying them to a new position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:07:54-07:00","id":907817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906979#post906979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks reasonable to me; do you envision the throws as respecting Defense?<br /> <br /> Does Potency limit the size of the electricity source used? You might have the attack deal damage as per the source and &quot;ablate&quot; one level of charge/Potency per use; this leads to more overall damage (instead of divvying up 6B into up to three hits, it hits thrice with less oomph each time) but can simplify book-keeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was figuring that the attacks would respect defense, yees.<br /> That potency idea solves the problem I was having with damage output.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906979#post906979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a riff on the theme - a translation of an old Wu Long rote, Thunder Bridge. This is a tricky one to translate, as its primary effects - short-range flight and a defensive aura - were secondary to its medium, a conjured bolt of lightning.</div> </div> </div> </div>This spell is awesome! trumps the one I was trying to craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:43:12-07:00","id":908148,"title":"","content":"Say. Has anyone tried writing up a spell that allows you to assume control over a relinquished spell by anchoring it to your spell limit? I can see it requiring Prime 5 to cast, and it could also be used to essentially 'hijack' a spell from an enemy Mage with a successful Clash of Wills. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T22:45:26-07:00","id":908150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=906964#post906964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking for ways to make Prime more useful at dealing with mundane stuff, so I came up with this spell for manipulating your Nimbus Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Empower Nimbus (Prime 3)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Persuasion, Occult<br /> The mage can strengthen the subject\u2019s Nimbus, making their Nimbus Tilt more powerful. Choose an Attribute or Skill which the subject\u2019s Nimbus Tilt affects. If the Nimbus tilt applies a bonus to that trait, the bonus increases by the spell\u2019s potency. If a penalty, the penalty worsens by the spell\u2019s potency.<br /> If the mage targets himself with this spell, this spell affects its own Nimbus Flare as well.<br /> This spell also improves the Nimbus\u2019s ability to contest the auras of other supernatural creatures. Add the spell\u2019s Potency to any contested roll between the subject\u2019s aura and another creature\u2019s aura.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell affects an additional Attribute or Skill covered by the subject\u2019s Nimbus tilt. Divide the spell\u2019s Potency between both. This effect may be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> <b>Control Nimbus (Prime 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Persuasion, Occult<br /> The mage manipulates the subject\u2019s Nimbus. For the spell\u2019s duration, the mage can cause the Nimbus to flare when it would not, or to fail to flare when it otherwise would. The spell may also cause it to continuously flare, applying its Nimbus Tilt to those who see it for as long as they continue to see it flare.<br /> If the Nimbus has been detached from its owner, such as with the Sever Nimbus spell, this spell also allows the mage to move the Nimbus around within sensory range.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage may cause the subject's Nimbus to flare towards specific targets, applying the Nimbus tilt to them if they can see it, but not to others.<br /> <b>1 Mana:</b> The mage may reveal the subject\u2019s Nimbus to the Fallen World, affecting even those not using Mage Sight. Sleepers suffer Quiescence after the Tilt ends.<br /> <b>1 Mana:</b> The mage imprints the target's Signature Nimbus on a single object, place, or person. (See Signature Nimbus p.90)</div> </div> </div> </div>These are some interesting spells, Strill. It definitely offers more applications for one's Nimbus with sufficient mastery in Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T11:44:41-07:00","id":908471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=908148#post908148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say. Has anyone tried writing up a spell that allows you to assume control over a relinquished spell by anchoring it to your spell limit? I can see it requiring Prime 5 to cast, and it could also be used to essentially 'hijack' a spell from an enemy Mage with a successful Clash of Wills. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to read up on the setting metaphysics to see if it was kosher, but I could imagine this as being a Prime 4 Patterning to match the original caster's Nimbus and then an Aura clash to &quot;convince&quot; the relinquished spell that you're the genuine article and draw it into your control.<br /> <br /> But does being able to re-integrate a relinquished spell mess with any setting assumptions? It seems like it trivializes the issue of whether leaving magic out in the world is irresponsible by giving an option that lets a mage &quot;clean up&quot; the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=907817#post907817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell is awesome! trumps the one I was trying to craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all - to my mind they serve different purposes. I was thinking a bit more about the idea of using Forces to make weapons (because how can I Obrimos without a flaming sword?) - what about the possibility of making your spell's template more broad, akin to the higher-dot wide-applicability Forces spells?<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Form Blazing Sword (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Weaponry, Expression</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage shapes and contains a source of energy into a melee weapon of elemental force; a campfire becomes a blade of flame, a concert provides a literal hammer of sound, or the mage enters a vampire's den armed with a spear of sunlight. The spell maintains the weapon's form and partially contains its energies, though the bearer suffers the full effects of continuous exposure. If the weapon is used to strike, it releases its stored energy into the target, as if they had spent a turn exposed to the source. The Potency of the effect determines how much energy may be contained in the weapon (as per the chart under Transform Energy), and each discharge reduces the remaining Potency of the effect by one, making future strikes less vicious or negating the spell altogether. The user's passive exposure does not reduce the spell's efficacy, however.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b><b>:</b> The containment of the weapon is improved, and the user is no longer subject to its effects while bearing it.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Strikes do not reduce the Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b><b>:</b> The weapon acquires a &quot;core&quot; of kinetic energy that gains heft when swung. If the weapon is used in a Weaponry attack and strikes the target, this buffeting force inflicts bashing damage equal to the attack successes, in addition to the effects of exposure to the stored energy. Armor can reduce this impact damage, but generally does not help against the energy.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b><b>:</b> As above, and the core is more refined in shape; the weapon acquires the traits (equipment/initiative modifiers, Size, Strength requirement, etc.) of a weapon with a maximum equipment modifier of [Half Potency, round up.] While it still inflicts only bashing damage (including the weapon's modifier), it is in all other ways treated as the form copied - a flaming chain has the Grapple property, a flaming spear improves Defense and requires two hands to wield, and so on. As an instant action the mage may, if in range of the weapon, reconfigure it into another form within these limits.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The weapon may be thrown; it has range bands of (Potency x 10/Potency x 20/Potency x 40) and is aimed with Dexterity + Athletics - the target's Defense. A successful throw inflicts damage as a strike. If the weapon has a kinetic element (as above), a throw inflicts additional bashing damage on a successful hit. The &quot;thrown&quot; energy splits off from the original weapon and dissipates upon impact, leaving the weapon itself still in the user's grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:34:49-07:00","id":911441,"title":"","content":"These two spells are in response to the fact that arch-mastery is required to create a soul whole cloth. Their point is what if one does not try to create a soul from nothing but rather to create more with what one has. It is still a rough concept and a WIP but I felt I could share my progress.<br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sunder Soul (Death****)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Composure<br /> Suggested rote skills: Occult, weaponry or larceny<br /> <br /> For many souls are an important concept but to a mage that concept has worth and value. That is why this spell sickens many mages often even those regularly using it but not always, some are so lost that this violation does not cause them to even pause (Wisdom understanding sin). The reason why this is such a violation is that it literally sunders a soul in two but not a true destruction of the whole. This is represented by the Imperfect soul condition and this condition will remain unless both fragments are within the individual when the spell's duration ends and the soul has a week to heal, for the soul can only heal itself naturally if all parts are present.<br /> <br /> Condition: Imperfect soul (persistant)<ul><li>-1 penalty to resisting possession.</li> <li>No willpower regained from surrender or rest.</li> <li>Does not have the decent of soul loss but can not heal the damage either, at most it stabilizes one without a true soul.</li> <li>Resolution: For the soul to heal naturally as above or to receive a whole soul.</li> </ul><br /> [I am not quite happy with this but I feel it is so close to being right] <hr /><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mend Soul (Death ***)</span><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary factor: </b>duration<br /> <b>Suggested rote skills:</b> Occult, craft or medicine<br /> <br /> The soul can be damaged and harmed but as it can be harmed so can it be healed. This spell was designed for that very purpose, to heal what wounds or marks a soul. Often that is a persistent condition the person in question is suffering from and that can seen when a mage investigates the soul with the spell soul marks. One such aliment may be healed per potency but the soul only remains in this new found state of health for the spells duration. <br /> <br /> A notable use of this spell is to heal an imperfect soul temporarily, to make a fragment of a soul equal to a whole soul and capable of it's functions. However this is not an accomplishment that one can use to claim that they have truly created a soul because this mended soul can still be dispelled and if this mended soul were to be sundered again the result would not be half of a soul but a quarter and require two instances of this spell to be maintained for it to act as a whole soul.<br /> <br /> +2 reach and a mana the spell's duration is lasting.<br /> <br /> [Even if these could not be consumed by a Tremere the ability to give these stand in souls for the original at least would allow one to continue extending their life with less weighing on their conscious]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:33:20-07:00","id":911820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=911441#post911441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mend Soul (Death ***)</span><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary factor: </b>duration<br /> <b>Suggested rote skills:</b> Occult, craft or medicine<br /> <br /> The soul can be damaged and harmed but as it can be harmed so can it be healed. This spell was designed for that very purpose, to heal what wounds or marks a soul. Often that is a persistent condition the person in question is suffering from and that can seen when a mage investigates the soul with the spell soul marks. One such aliment may be healed per potency but the soul only remains in this new found state of health for the spells duration.<br /> <br /> A notable use of this spell is to heal an imperfect soul temporarily, to make a fragment of a soul equal to a whole soul and capable of it's functions. However this is not an accomplishment that one can use to claim that they have truly created a soul because this mended soul can still be dispelled and if this mended soul were to be sundered again the result would not be half of a soul but a quarter and require two instances of this spell to be maintained for it to act as a whole soul.<br /> <br /> +2 reach and a mana the spell's duration is lasting.<br /> <br /> [Even if these could not be consumed by a Tremere the ability to give these stand in souls for the original at least would allow one to continue extending their life with less weighing on their conscious]</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this particular spell could be rather handy. I see no reason why this one wouldn't apply to temporarily boosting Integrity/Wisdom/Humanity/Clarity, and making it Lasting means you could actually heal someone's soul, which is extremely thematic and could be really useful. A Beast has a Moros friend and is being pursued by a Hero? No problem, the Moros boosts their Integrity by Potency, makes it Lasting, and the Hero loses their crippling Beast-hunting obsession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:42:09-07:00","id":911904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=911820#post911820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, this particular spell could be rather handy. I see no reason why this one wouldn't apply to temporarily boosting Integrity/Wisdom/Humanity/Clarity, and making it Lasting means you could actually heal someone's soul, which is extremely thematic and could be really useful. A Beast has a Moros friend and is being pursued by a Hero? No problem, the Moros boosts their Integrity by Potency, makes it Lasting, and the Hero loses their crippling Beast-hunting obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to heal someone's integrity and make it lasting is probably too much but to be able to effect it at all I'd a good idea I hadn't concidered!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:52:55-07:00","id":914636,"title":"","content":"I wrote up this spell based on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912519-can-the-death-arcanum-kill-magic?p=913089#post913089\">Aspel's idea</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cassandra's Curse (Prime **)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Politics, Subterfuge, Occult<br /> <br /> Just like the prophet who always spoke the truth but was cursed so that no one believed her, the mage conceals all truth the subject speaks. Everyone who listens to her words is left with the impression that she's either lying, ignorant, or confused. If the spell adds a tinge of falsehood to statements that Sleeper witnesses are absolutely certain is true, those Sleepers may suffer Quiescence if they think about the contradiction too much.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Listeners perceive the subject to not just be confused or mistaken, but outright lying.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell affects all forms of communication the subject engages in.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can restrict the curse to apply only to particular facts or categories. (e.g. &quot;My company's illegal financial dealings&quot;, &quot;The secret tunnels underneath my house&quot;, &quot;Statements made while performing as a fortune teller&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-17-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:39:06-07:00","id":914769,"title":"","content":"I'd make it subtler, instead of making it appear the person is lying it's that they're speaking the truth but it's not important. No one thought Cassandra was lying, they just ignored her.<br /> <br /> In mechanical terms it could penalize Social rolls to spread a message by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:43:36-07:00","id":914822,"title":"","content":"Lower First impressions in Social Manuevering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:33:26-07:00","id":914941,"title":"","content":"Hello, long time lurker, first time poster here, I need a bit of help refining some spells for my NPCs:<br /> <br /> for the first one, for my Acanthus adamantine arrow i was thinking something like:<br /> <i><br /> <b>Just a flesh wound (Mind **)</b><br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested rote skills: Expression, stealth, subterfuge<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> The target of this ability believes that his attacks have the opposite outcomes. Attacks that strike the target seem like they missed, attacks that missed seem like they hit. Enveloping all the senses, someone swinging, and hitting with a sword p.e., wouldn't feel the impact of the blow nor hear the cry of his target, but instead would &quot;see&quot; the defender dodging out of the way. Similary, someone throwing a fireball, and missing, would instead see, and smell, his opponent being chared to &quot;really wounded, but not quite dead&quot; state. The actual attack is resolved normaly despite the perception of it (so you swing a sword and hit, you think you missed, opponent seems healthy, but in reality he does take, and note the damage and/or assosiated penalties)<br /> <br /> This spell doesn't fool the one actually getting attacked (the target of the attack still knows, and feels, the full burn of the attack)<br /> This spell is not limited to &quot;attack roll&quot; actions, but instead is applied to everything the &quot;attacker&quot; thinks is an attack (so even social slander and etc, or sensory spells)<br /> <br /> +1 reach: The caster can now reflexivly decide if an attack looks like a miss or a hit.<br /> +1 reach: This spell fools even the one getting attacked (The ST should keep his life total a secret)<br /> </i><br /> I'm not certain if ruling is strong enough for this, would also love to be able to simplify the writing of the spell (english not my native language) but have a bit of a problem doing so. Lastly, opinions on the actual spell (power level, flavor, utility, etc are always welcome. <br /> <br /> In my mind, this is a spell best utilized by a high defence/resist character so as to appear to keep taking damage and keep the enemies attention (<i>&quot;we almost have him!&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;he hits like a truck!&quot;</i>) while keeping the focus away from his weaker allies (<i>&quot; those weaklings keep dodging but at least they don't do any damage!&quot;</i>)<br /> with the reach option that even the one taking the damage is fooled, it becomes quite deadly, since one doesn't know when to retreat, defend, and overcommits to a fight till he falls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:15:22-07:00","id":914970,"title":"","content":"I actually came up with a similar effects to the &quot;target seems like lying&quot; spells in the previous Crea.Thaum. thread. I think I called it Cassandra's Toungue. Yours seem a bit tidier.<br /> As of the mechanical effect of the spell it could add a Door in social manouvering - you need an additional step aka. convincing the interlocutor you're not lying.<br /> <br /> Something fun:<br /> <br /> Goetic insertion (Mind ***)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure/Rank<br /> Suggested rote skills: Expression, Persuassion, Larcery<br /> The casting mage can insert a free floating Goetic into the subjects mind. Unless the mage targets himself with the spell this requires taking aditional spell factors. The goetic becomes an inherent part of the subjects psyche. This might cause the subject to gain an additional Virtue, Vice or Aspiration. However as a person's psyche can only hold so much the Goetia in her fight for domination so after a time the new element of his psyche fades or replaces some other one of the same type.<br /> +1 Reach: The goetic can coexist indefinetily with other parts of the targets personality<br /> +2 Reach: The effect is lasting (but see above, also the effect ends if the goetic is removed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:44:58-07:00","id":915254,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11977\" data-vbnamecard=\"11977\">Shroudb</a> It'd be Veiling, not Ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:13:29-07:00","id":915457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=915254#post915254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> It'd be Veiling, not Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too thought that it might be veiling in the beginning, but <br /> A)veiling, imo, would target you and not the opponent<br /> And more importantly<br /> B)veiling seems like it should just mask things, while this spell modifies your perception from one thing to another<br /> <br /> That's why in the end I chose ruling, since changing stuff seems closer to what happens (as opposed to just hiding them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:19:13-07:00","id":915459,"title":"","content":"Veiling, like any Practice can be used on any valid target. Also, if a mask doesn't alter perceptions then what good is it? Your spell is masking damage, but not actually changing the damage. That's why it's Veiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:33:49-07:00","id":915559,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Safety Between (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Larceny, Empathy<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> The subject becomes wrapped into the very fabric of the Gauntlet, existing neither in the material world nor the Shadow. When inside the Gauntlet, the subject is kept in stasis until the spell ends. This means the subject cannot take any actions or be further affected by Conditions or Tilts it is currently suffering from.<br /> <br /> When the spell ends or the mage wishes to dispel it as usual, the subject reappears where they entered the Gauntlet. If a large object is in the way when they reappear, the subject will end up Knocked Down at the objects closest edge from the exit point.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> the mage can choose that the subject doesn\u2019t have to reappear on the side it entered.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> the subject can take mental actions like thinking and casting spells. These spells however will first take effect when the subject leaves the Gauntlet, but Paradoxes can still occur. For 1 Mana, the subject may take physical actions at a -2 penalty and move around at a speed equal to their Gnosis within the Gauntlet. If the subject move, it will reappear where it has walked to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 02-11-2017, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:15:09-07:00","id":915835,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shroudb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=914941#post914941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ====Original Idea===</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i><b>Apparent Juggernaut(Life **)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested rote skills:</b> Athletics, Brawl, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> The target of this spell appears to be immune to damage. Attacks that strike the target seem like they leave no injury. Enveloping all the senses, someone swinging, and hitting with a sword would feel the impact of the blow and hear the cry of his target, but wouldn't perceive the defender being wounded or impaired by the strike. The actual attack is resolved normally despite the perception of it. Likewise blood splatter from injuries is veiled until either the spell ends or end of scene, which ever happens first. If the blood pools cause Environmental Tilts due to slipperiness, attempts to resist those tilts must be rolled twice, taking the lower of the two rolls. Note perception of clothing and armor is unaffected by this spell.<br /> <br /> This spell doesn't fool the one actually getting attacked (the target of the attack still knows, and feels, the full damage of the attack)<br /> <br /> <b>+1 reach:</b> The caster can now reflexive decide if an attack looks like a miss or a hit.<br /> <b>+1 reach:</b> This spell fools even the one getting attacked and they don't suffer Wound Penalties(The ST should keep his Health Boxes a secret)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-16-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:51:37-07:00","id":915921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=915835#post915835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>nvm, missread, it's a take on it with life. nice.<br /> <br /> btw, really liking the new name<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:01:30-07:00","id":915926,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><b>Apparent Perfection(Death **)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested rote skills:</b> Crafts, Medicine, Science<br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> The target of this spell appears to be immune to damage and appears completely free of damage, injury, erosion, or wear. Attacks that strike the target seem like they leave no injury. Enveloping all the senses, someone swinging, and hitting with a sword would feel the impact of the blow and hear the cry of his target, but wouldn't perceive the defender being wounded or impaired by the strike. The actual attack is resolved normally despite the perception of it. Blood splatter from injuries is not veiled.note perception of clothing and armor is affected by this spell if the target has them. If cast on a target which is worn, injured or otherwise damaged it appears in perfect health/pristine condition.<br /> <br /> This spell doesn't fool the one actually damaged, the target of an attack still knows, and feels, the full damage of the attack.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 reach:</b> This spell fools even the one getting attacked and they don't suffer Wound Penalties(The ST should keep his Health Boxes a secret)</i></div>Reworked it so it essentially a way to conceal death's influence on a subject or object. Not intended to be a &quot;switch perception if struck&quot; affect.<br /> <br /> Falsely curing cancer, psuedo-healing, or fake making old object look new, it's pretty versatile actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T02:28:37-07:00","id":918516,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Constantinople (Fate** Space**)</b><br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> Cost: 1 mana<br /> <br /> Named after the legend of the founding of Constantinople, this spell allows one to find the perfect location for the task at hand. The caster sets the <b>general</b> parameters (nothing TOO specific) and fate takes care of the rest. Mages still argue if the spell slightly changes fate to accommodate the caster, or if it simply finds the perfect thread of fate to guide him.<br /> <br /> For the duration of the spell, as long as the targets of the spell are within the area of effect, they gain +Potency to non-magical skills pertaining to the requested task.</i><br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> &quot;What is the best hiding place in this building&quot; with an personal area of effect, might point out that one closet in the next hallway that the guard won't bother to check (+stealth rolls)<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is the best place In the city to defend ourselves from our pursuers? &quot; with an area of effect equal to a room, might point out to a specific room in an abandoned factory, where, if the targets fight in there, they will have +potency on their non-magical rolls for the combat<br /> <br /> &quot;Where can I find the seer headquarters? &quot; is too specific, but &quot;Where can I find some seers in the city&quot; might point out to a park where some seers will be present at some time, granting +potency to perception and/or investigation rolls.<br /> <br /> And etc<br /> <br /> (Effectively, instead of a normal, unconditional skill boost, you pigeonhole yourself to a specific task and location, that, furthermore is NOT chosen by you, but on the flipside, you get a boost to ALL relevant skill checks, AND you might gain some relevant clues from the actual location you are sent)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 06-21-2016, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:12:45-07:00","id":919385,"title":"","content":"Spirit Marriage (Spirit 0000)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstood: Rank<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Politics, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <br /> This spell invites a spirit to possess a mage for a while, lending the mage its powers and capabilities. The mage essentially becomes a living fetish for the spirit in question. This has a few benefits and a few drawbacks for the duration.<br /> First, the spirit's attributes boost those of the mage. For each Potency of the spell the mage may&quot; borrow&quot; an attribute dot from the spirit's Power, Finesse or Resistance to his own attributes in this category. For example, a point drawn from Resistance may boost Resolve, Stamina or Composure.<br /> Secondly, the mage gains access to the numina of the spirit and may use these as if he were a living fetish, using the spirit's attributes (which are diminished if the mage had elected to borrow its attributes).<br /> Third, the mage gains access to the Influences of the spirit, and may fuel them with Essence and/or Mana.<br /> <br /> This spell may not be applied to any familiar since these are already bound in a special way to the mage.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The spirit possessing the mage is neither slave nor servant no matter what the mage thinks. It will be an opportunistic parasite at best and a dangerous lunatic or troublemaker at worst. Any time the spirit sees an opportunity to strengthen its resonance it will try to wrest control from the mage. For example, a fire spirit wants to ignite flamable materials while a greed spirit wants to gain wealth and power no matter if it's legal or moral. The mage may try to appease the spirit with a social roll. If this fails, the mage will have to win a Clash of Wills versus the spirit which will cause the spirit to immediately eject from the body of the mage. If the spirit wins it gains control of the mage for the duration of the spell.<br /> Also, the mage will have a slight change of appearance depending on what type of spirit he marries with. If it is a fire spirit he may gain uncanny glowing eyes and / or may smell of phosphorous or exhude ash with every breath. If he is possessed by a spirit of greed he might gain a strange green hue to his eyes or lick his lips a little too often (or maybe don a top hat). This effect will be noticeable after a while to sleepers, and nearly obvious to other shamans, werewolves and characters with high Occult ratings.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: the spirit is effectively enslaved for the duration of the spell, nullifying all of its potential of possessing the mage. The spirit is still not willing and will surely not appreciate this treatment.<br /> +1 Reach: the mage can optionally change his appearance radically, taking the form of the spirit materialized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:23:10-07:00","id":919860,"title":"","content":"Shadow Golem (Death ****)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> <br /> The mage constructs a moving construct out of shadows, mimicking the capacity of Matter Adepts to create golems. The Potency of this spell is divided between the Durability and Retainer rating of the Golem. The golem is size 5 or lower, as the mage sees fit. The Shadow Golem is incapable of combat and has no Defense rating. It\u00b4s Structure will determine its Health.<br /> The shadow golem is in no way capable of decisi\u00f3n-making and can only obey short and simple commands given by the mage.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The mage may install a ghost to act as a guiding intelligence for the golem, which also grants it the ability to use Numina. This will also offer the Golem a basic Defence rating equal to the Potency of the spell.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage may make the golem capable of defence, granting a Defence rating equal to the Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> Add Spirit ****: The mage installs a Spirit as a guiding intelligence, granting the Golem the capacity to use Numina.<br /> Add Mind *****: The mage installs a synthetic mind as a crude guiding intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:47:31-07:00","id":920952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shroudb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=918516#post918516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Constantinople (Fate** Space**)</b><br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> Cost: 1 mana<br /> <br /> Named after the legend of the founding of Constantinople, this spell allows one to find the perfect location for the task at hand. The caster sets the <b>general</b> parameters (nothing TOO specific) and fate takes care of the rest. Mages still argue if the spell slightly changes fate to accommodate the caster, or if it simply finds the perfect thread of fate to guide him.<br /> <br /> For the duration of the spell, as long as the targets of the spell are within the area of effect, they gain +Potency to non-magical skills pertaining to the requested task.</i><br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> &quot;What is the best hiding place in this building&quot; with an personal area of effect, might point out that one closet in the next hallway that the guard won't bother to check (+stealth rolls)<br /> <br /> &quot;Where is the best place In the city to defend ourselves from our pursuers? &quot; with an area of effect equal to a room, might point out to a specific room in an abandoned factory, where, if the targets fight in there, they will have +potency on their non-magical rolls for the combat<br /> <br /> &quot;Where can I find the seer headquarters? &quot; is too specific, but &quot;Where can I find some seers in the city&quot; might point out to a park where some seers will be present at some time, granting +potency to perception and/or investigation rolls.<br /> <br /> And etc<br /> <br /> (Effectively, instead of a normal, unconditional skill boost, you pigeonhole yourself to a specific task and location, that, furthermore is NOT chosen by you, but on the flipside, you get a boost to ALL relevant skill checks, AND you might gain some relevant clues from the actual location you are sent)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Space is needed for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:40:28-07:00","id":921062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=920952#post920952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Space is needed for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>i put space 2 because it kinda works like scrying:<br /> where will X be best? is what you ask with the spell, and you get a specific location as an answer<br /> hence the mana cost as well, it works &quot;kinda&quot; like you cast a spell at sympathetic range (the answer you get isn't always within sensory range) but it also can't be sympathetic because you don't need to know anything about where the &quot;divination&quot; will sent you.<br /> So, the best way, for me, to emulate that pseudo-sympathetic range was to give it a space 2 requirement as well as 1 mana cost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:52:34-07:00","id":921069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shroudb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=921062#post921062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i put space 2 because it kinda works like scrying:<br /> where will X be best? is what you ask with the spell, and you get a specific location as an answer<br /> hence the mana cost as well, it works &quot;kinda&quot; like you cast a spell at sympathetic range (the answer you get isn't always within sensory range) but it also can't be sympathetic because you don't need to know anything about where the &quot;divination&quot; will sent you.<br /> So, the best way, for me, to emulate that pseudo-sympathetic range was to give it a space 2 requirement as well as 1 mana cost</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that Fate can already guide you to places/people/things/goals using the spells in the book. If you're not actually getting a remote vision of the location it wouldn't require space (that would be a cool distinguishing effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T02:27:45-07:00","id":921411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=921069#post921069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that Fate can already guide you to places/people/things/goals using the spells in the book. If you're not actually getting a remote vision of the location it wouldn't require space (that would be a cool distinguishing effect)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate actually CAN give remote visions under certain circumstances. Look at Oath's Fulfilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:12:14-07:00","id":921572,"title":"","content":"Oaths Fulfilled works for a different reason: remember that no spell can break the range rules, so you need to have the subject within range to cast the spell. However, once the spell is on the subject, it continues to work regardless of distance. This can be applied to any spell, Oath's Fulfilled is just an example of that mechanic. <br /> <br /> You could for example create a Life Knowing spell to track a subject's health with a long Duration that will notify you if the subject becomes hurt or sick, for example. (Even after the subject has moved away from your range).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T18:11:25-07:00","id":922329,"title":"","content":"Hope I'm doing this right. This is my first time homebrewing a spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Spacial Map (Space \u25cf)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Firearms, Investigation, Occult<br /> <b>Intent:</b> Allows Space Mage to use Space Arcana to \u201csee\u201d surroundings and negate penalties due to range as well as darkness and similar poor visibility. Only works in \u201cSensory\u201d range, and, unlike Outward and Inward Eye, cannot be used to perceive things from all directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T13:17:14-07:00","id":922810,"title":"","content":"Is the intent that it completely negates them, or offsets them based on Potency (like Outward/Inward Eye does)?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's something I've been considering. Not quite sure I got it to work how I'd like it to.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense? Any suggestions?<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Principle of Contagion (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Connection<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Politics, Socialize</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage spins a web of occult connections around themselves or another mage, which incorporates itself into a spell they release. As that magic unfolds, it leaps from target to target, following along the threads of sympathy. The subject must be a mage, who may adopt the web's symbolism into their Imago and expend one Mana during casting to make one spell &quot;contagious.&quot; A contagious spell affects the original target as usual, but may also spread beyond them. When the target meaningfully interacts with a sympathetic link, the contagious spell will attempt to affect that individual. The contagious spell continues to affect new targets until it ends, it reaches the limit of its Scale factor, or until the Duration of the web elapses, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> The Potency of this spell determines how remote a sympathetic connection the contagion may use to affect other targets. Secondary targets are not themselves contagious. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Up to one spell per level of Potency cast by the subject may be rendered contagious.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Targets beyond the first are contagious. The chain of contagion can be up to (Potency) steps beyond the initial target (so a Potency 3 contagious spell might affect the target, their spouse, their spouse's co-worker, and the co-worker's dogs.) This does not change the Scale limit on total targets.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a general category of sympathetic connections, such as &quot;family members&quot; or &quot;co-conspirators&quot;. Contagious spells will only be transferred across that variety of connection.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022, </span><b>+1 Reach</b><b>:</b> The mage may specify something that must occur during interaction to cause contagion, such as discussing a forbidden subject, or which will prevent it, such as performing a warding gesture or wearing a certain color.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022\u2022</span><b>:</b> The original target is exempted from the effects of the contagious spell; they are merely a carrier for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T14:30:44-07:00","id":922850,"title":"","content":"I like it very much. Its a nifty little spell in a theme of mysteries. But to make affect targets gradually over time you would need to hang a spell with time attainment. Otherwise it would go all at once, throu the strongest sympathies.<br /> It could work without time and fate but it'd be a Dynymics spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:28:08-07:00","id":922907,"title":"","content":"It's not Dynamic though, it's not changing the spell just the targets until all valid targets are affected. I think it works fine, but I don't see why it can only be cast on a Mage. Like, you ought to be able to cast it on a Sleeper and then cast a spell into the line of contagion and have it affect the Sleeper and any secondary targets, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:38:17-07:00","id":923355,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback, folks. I suspect that Awakening's metaphysical rules might require that the secondary targets be in range, which may defeat the purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=922850#post922850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it very much. Its a nifty little spell in a theme of mysteries. But to make affect targets gradually over time you would need to hang a spell with time attainment. Otherwise it would go all at once, throu the strongest sympathies.<br /> It could work without time and fate but it'd be a Dynymics spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. You're probably right that this would require Time and maybe Fate for the delayed firing... but at that point it'd probably be simpler to just Borrow Threads the primary target and cast Conditional Hung Spells along the sympathetic connections to fire when they meet with the primary target.<br /> <br /> Do we think that any spell that doesn't take immediate effect requires Time 2 and any contingent spell requires Time and Fate 2?<br /> <br /> Is any spell that responds to conditions Dynamic? I thought the key element of Dynamics was that it would revise itself to continue to achieve an outcome? Not really that familiar with the arch-level Practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=922907#post922907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not Dynamic though, it's not changing the spell just the targets until all valid targets are affected. I think it works fine, but I don't see why it can only be cast on a Mage. Like, you ought to be able to cast it on a Sleeper and then cast a spell into the line of contagion and have it affect the Sleeper and any secondary targets, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that as a &quot;Patient Zero&quot; effect - though it would be harder to justify a &quot;secondary targets are also contagious&quot; Reach option in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:55:55-07:00","id":923363,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:33:27-07:00","id":923612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=922810#post922810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the intent that it completely negates them, or offsets them based on Potency (like Outward/Inward Eye does)?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's something I've been considering. Not quite sure I got it to work how I'd like it to.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense? Any suggestions?<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Principle of Contagion (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Connection<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Politics, Socialize</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage spins a web of occult connections around themselves or another mage, which incorporates itself into a spell they release. As that magic unfolds, it leaps from target to target, following along the threads of sympathy. The subject must be a mage, who may adopt the web's symbolism into their Imago and expend one Mana during casting to make one spell &amp;quot;contagious.&amp;quot; A contagious spell affects the original target as usual, but may also spread beyond them. When the target meaningfully interacts with a sympathetic link, the contagious spell will attempt to affect that individual. The contagious spell continues to affect new targets until it ends, it reaches the limit of its Scale factor, or until the Duration of the web elapses, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> The Potency of this spell determines how remote a sympathetic connection the contagion may use to affect other targets. Secondary targets are not themselves contagious. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Up to one spell per level of Potency cast by the subject may be rendered contagious.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Targets beyond the first are contagious. The chain of contagion can be up to (Potency) steps beyond the initial target (so a Potency 3 contagious spell might affect the target, their spouse, their spouse's co-worker, and the co-worker's dogs.) This does not change the Scale limit on total targets.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify a general category of sympathetic connections, such as &amp;quot;family members&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;co-conspirators&amp;quot;. Contagious spells will only be transferred across that variety of connection.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022, </span><b>+1 Reach</b><b>:</b> The mage may specify something that must occur during interaction to cause contagion, such as discussing a forbidden subject, or which will prevent it, such as performing a warding gesture or wearing a certain color.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022\u2022</span><b>:</b> The original target is exempted from the effects of the contagious spell; they are merely a carrier for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally rule that such a spell would be a sin against falling wisdom given the fact that it could affect people without interaction or even knowledge of their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:21:53-07:00","id":923768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=923355#post923355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see that as a &quot;Patient Zero&quot; effect - though it would be harder to justify a &quot;secondary targets are also contagious&quot; Reach option in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why it would be harder to justify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T07:28:04-07:00","id":923844,"title":"","content":"How might one create a spell that would take someone dressed in a costume and turn them into what they are dressed as for the duration? I know you could use Mind to make them think and act they are what they are dressed as, but what I'm looking for is a way to actually turn them into what they are portraying. If they are dressed as a horse, boom, they're a horse. Dressed as a ghost, boom, you're a ghost. Dressed as Superman ... you get the idea. I'm thinking of being able to use it on a number of subjects in an area (a costume party for example) and not have to specify what each target is to become aside from &quot;that which the costume imitates&quot; or something like that<br /> <br /> Would this fall under Life for the transformation quality? Or do you think this kind of thing somehow eludes the abilities of the Awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T07:54:17-07:00","id":923854,"title":"","content":"I could see that as a Life/Prime Weaving effect (plus Death 2 if it's meant to transform the target into an actual ghost).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:12:24-07:00","id":923860,"title":"","content":"So basically toss in some of Death, Spirit, Matter and Forces just to cover bases of what all people might be dressed as?<br /> <br /> That sounds exceptionally complicated to cast (granted it's an exceptionally complicated effect given the breadth of the human imagination where costumes are concerned)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:35:59-07:00","id":923869,"title":"","content":"You'd probably want Matter as well. And yes, it's complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:07:26-07:00","id":923971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jmkoontz1980</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=923844#post923844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How might one create a spell that would take someone dressed in a costume and turn them into what they are dressed as for the duration? I know you could use Mind to make them think and act they are what they are dressed as, but what I'm looking for is a way to actually turn them into what they are portraying. If they are dressed as a horse, boom, they're a horse. Dressed as a ghost, boom, you're a ghost. Dressed as Superman ... you get the idea. I'm thinking of being able to use it on a number of subjects in an area (a costume party for example) and not have to specify what each target is to become aside from &quot;that which the costume imitates&quot; or something like that<br /> <br /> Would this fall under Life for the transformation quality? Or do you think this kind of thing somehow eludes the abilities of the Awakened?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a &quot;short cut&quot; I'd take is Life 4, Spirit 4, Fate 1 to turn people into materialized spiritual representations of what they were dressed as, also leaves room for abstract or role based costumes. Neat side affect is you could then make the masquerade party now a spirit court. Fate 1 is for the spell for the 'knowing' practice to sort through the meaning of each costume, as I am assuming you will be casting this on a crowd. So Thyrsus hosted Masked Balls can be fairly interesting,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T03:13:06-07:00","id":928036,"title":"","content":"From the Tamers of Fire legacy conversion thread, with all due credit to Deionscribe:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Will Of Fire</u> (Mind 3)<br /> Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Expression, Persuasion<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Fiery rhetoric can bolster human spirits. And with the right words, a Mage can give a group of friends and followers the will to succeed above and beyond their own capacity. The spell grants one Willpower point to the subject equal to its Potency. These Willpower points can only be used for actions related to the purpose of the spell, and cannot be regained once used.<br /> <br /> <b>+ 2 Reach:</b> The Willpower gained from this spell may now be spent without any restriction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Stoke the Flames</u> (Mind 2)<br /> Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> The Mage can urge a given subject towards accomplishing a particular goal of his choosing, This grants him the Inspired Condition for the duration of the spell, or until he chooses to resolve it earlier.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> By spending a point of Mana, the Mage allows a subject to avail of the Condition a number of times equal to the spell's Potency before it's resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Burning Bright</u> (Mind 3)<br /> Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> The Mage can bless a subject so that a given action he exerts great effort on has a higher chance of success. When he spends Willpower to bolster an action, he may add the spell's Potency as the bonus, instead of the usual +3.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject may apply the benefits of the spell an additional number of times equal to Reach spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:34:46-07:00","id":930356,"title":"","content":"<b><u>The Road Less Traveled</u> (Prime 3)<br /> Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> The Mage can impose his personal symbolism on a Tool Yantra, making it resonate with his Path.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can impose the symbolism of a different Tool. For example, he can cause a simple stick to have the symbolism of a Coin.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Clarification</u> (Prime 3)<br /> Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> When Focusing his Mage Sight and attempting Revelation, the subject can ignore the penalty caused by Opacity, up to this spell's Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T06:37:48-07:00","id":933840,"title":"","content":"A simple way to make basic potion brewing work.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Brew Potion</u> (Matter ***)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Magical potions and unguents are widely recognized as part of the wizard\u2019s trade. This spell prepares a material compound to hold a supernal charge. A mage may then cast another spell into the potion, specifically shaping their Imago and spending a point of Mana. The potion may contain up to its Potency in spells, but using the compound triggers all of them. While within the potion, a spell counts against the caster\u2019s spell control, but its Duration is held.<br /> <br /> Potions come with certain limitations. Whomever imbibes the potion becomes the subject of its spells, although a cream or oil might be spread or splattered. If <i>Brew Potion</i>\u2019s Duration runs out while it still contains spells, the held spells are lost and the potion visibly spoils.<br /> <br /> Usually this spell is cast on a liquid that resonates with the spell effect, but it could also be cast on a piece of fruit to be eaten, a powder to be inhaled, a breakable object to be tossed like a grenade, etc. \u201cIngredients\u201d act as Sacrament Yantras.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may add a Key to the activation of the potion. Perhaps it will only work once a certain reagent is mixed in, or it only has an effect on a certain person.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The potion\u2019s ingredients lose any effect they may have had on an imbiber; so an Acceleration potion of quicksilver won\u2019t inflict mercury poisoning.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The potion may contain multiple doses. If the same spell is cast into it multiple times, each adds an additional use to the potion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:51:36-07:00","id":933879,"title":"","content":"Since there's no requirement for ingredients of a potion there's no point for the Reach clause that negates deleterious effects of the ingredients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T08:26:06-07:00","id":933903,"title":"","content":"You can use an ingredient as a Sacrament. Yeah, using ingredients with adverse effects isn't required, but the Reach effect opens up the option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:52:15-07:00","id":934370,"title":"","content":"<br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Battle Body (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The subject\u2019s body becomes better at withstanding attempts to hamper or harm its functionality. Attempts to inflict most physical Tilts must overcome the usual resistance (usually Stamina) + the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Edited: </b><b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject becomes more resistant to cruder attempts to harm it. Add the spell's Potency to its health.<br /> <b>Edited: +2 Reach:</b> The subject\u2019s senses and reflexes becomes enhanced to such a degree that it allows them to land precise blows and react to opportunities. It gains a dice bonus to Brawl rolls equal to the spells Potency. This is not a weapon bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> The Health Reach could maybe be tweaked and the Brawl bonus Reach I am unsure off if it is to strong. But I found it fitting for the spells theme.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>The Translucent Barrier (Spirit \u2022)</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Survival, Streetwise<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> Looking across the Gauntlet is a key ability in every Shaman\u2019s life. This spell allows the subject to perceive what is on the other side of the Gauntlet without having to cross it. All of the subject's senses, except for touch, is cast to the other side so the subject will be unaware of things around it's body. The subject cannot interact with the spirit world with spell, only observe.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject's senses are split and it can perceive both the Shadow and the material realm at the same time with no ill effect..<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> Me and my player was tired of having to spend extra Reach just to see through the Gauntlet and we figured she should be able to do so without the need to be able to speak with spirits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Safety Between (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Larceny, Empathy<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Gauntlet Strength<br /> <br /> The subject becomes wrapped into the very fabric of the Gauntlet, existing neither in the material world nor the Shadow. When inside the Gauntlet, the subject is kept in stasis until the spell ends. This means the subject cannot take any actions or be further affected by Conditions or Tilts it may currently be suffering from.<br /> When the spell ends the subject reappears where they entered the Gauntlet. If a large object is in the way when they reappear, the subject will end up with the Knocked Down Tilt at the objects closest edge from the exit point.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> the mage can choose that the subject doesn\u2019t have to reappear on the side it entered from when casting the spell.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> the subject can take mental actions like thinking and casting spells. These spells however will first take effect when the subject leaves the Gauntlet, but Paradoxes can still occur inside the Gauntlet. For 1 Mana, the subject may take physical actions at a -2 penalty and move around at a speed equal to their Gnosis within the Gauntlet. If the subject moves, it will reappear where it has walked to.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I figured with spirit that a mage also would be able to manipulate the Gauntlet itself. I just hope that it isn't to powerful, but I really liked the idea of wrapping one-self in the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 07-30-2016, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:08:02-07:00","id":934374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=934370#post934370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Battle Body (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The subject\u2019s body becomes better at withstanding attempts to hamper or harm its functionality. Attempts to inflict most physical Tilts must overcome the usual resistance (usually Stamina) + the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I wanted to have more Reach options, but I am not sure what these should be. I was thinking a bonus to Brawl attacks, but that seemed it would &quot;override&quot; spells that gave claws and such.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage becomes more resistant to cruder attempts to harm him. Add the spell's Potency to his health.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:04:00-07:00","id":934953,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a> That sounds like it could be a fitting Reach for something that would improve the body.<br /> <br /> But after looking at it, I am not sure if it is a viable spell since Honing the Form does the same thing, except it actually increases Stamina. But since Battle Body doesn't actually increase the subject's Stamina, would it then be affected by the Attribute limit like Honing the Form's is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T02:52:02-07:00","id":934971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=934953#post934953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a> That sounds like it could be a fitting Reach for something that would improve the body.<br /> <br /> But after looking at it, I am not sure if it is a viable spell since Honing the Form does the same thing, except it actually increases Stamina. But since Battle Body doesn't actually increase the subject's Stamina, would it then be affected by the Attribute limit like Honing the Form's is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing Stamina does have some other benefits <sup>[<span style=\"color:#008080\">citation needed</span>]</sup>, which you wouldn't get with Battle Body, so I'm guessing not having the attribute limit would be fine. Alternatively, limit it to half the target's size, with an additional +1 reach to ignore said limit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T19:28:29-07:00","id":935895,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if this is okay or if it is broken:<br /> <br /> <b>Veil Truth (Prime \u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By disguising the Truth of something, the Mage may make it seem to be something else.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The subject appears to be something else similar; a person appears to be a different person, an animated statue of Cerberus appears to be an ordinary dog, a ratty old outfit appears to be an expensive outfit, etc. This deception need not make something look more normal or nicer; any of those examples could go the other direction. It is almost always possible to conceal the supernatural nature of a subject even if doing so would necessitate making it appear to be very different; for example: a humanoid creature of living fire could be disguised as a human with a burning flameproof suit. Supernatural senses allow a Clash of Wills against the effect. Additionally, when casting the Spell, the Mage may choose to make the veil so weak that it only deceives sleepers.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Mage may veil the subject as something completely different.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>The Mage may veil the subject as nothing at all, concealing it, or veil nothing as something creating an illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 07-23-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T03:28:17-07:00","id":936008,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a> Since it already does less than Honing the Form, I don't think there should be a limit to, or at least, not that big a limit as half the targets size. But using the Size could be a good limit if needed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11888\" data-vbnamecard=\"11888\">Custos Tenebrarum</a> There is already kinda a spell that hides the truth in this thread called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=914636#post914636\">Casandra's Curse</a>. However it doesn't physically change the apperance. Also, yours can be used on any subject. So a universal Shapechange spell. I think that would be to strong... Not sure about it though when it at higher dots since you are in essence at that point, actually changing the Truth. Also, it seems like you can do allot with this spell.<br /> <br /> But the idea of changing the truth is rather coool. Maybe, as an example, more like making a cat be a dog or a burger is cyanide. They still see a cat and a burger and these things will act and work as such. But they believe what they are seeing to be these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:04:46-07:00","id":936650,"title":"","content":"Waterway [Space 2 + Matter 2] - open a small portal from some liquid rich environment and into enemies mouth. They drown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T13:19:04-07:00","id":936688,"title":"","content":"Not a valid spell. Wouldn't need Matter if it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:30:18-07:00","id":936721,"title":"","content":"I kinda wonder how Tilts for Drowning and Air-Starving would look like. After all, in combat you are supposed to represent such threats using Tilts; this makes all of the &quot;instant kill&quot; spells like this much less game breaking (because they kinda stop being instant kills)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T15:03:56-07:00","id":936738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=936721#post936721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda wonder how Tilts for Drowning and Air-Starving would look like. After all, in combat you are supposed to represent such threats using Tilts; this makes all of the &quot;instant kill&quot; spells like this much less game breaking (because they kinda stop being instant kills)</div> </div> </div> </div>We have those in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=145773#post145773\">Fan Made Conditions</a> thread.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Some Prime or Space spells that mess with the Nimbus and soul stones would be neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:45:41-07:00","id":937444,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Control Cold</u> (Death 2)<br /> Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> By commanding powers of cold and absence, Mage invites winter into the area. Each level of Potency allows a change of of 1 level of Extreme Environment to produce cold, counting a temperate room temperature as &quot;zero&quot;. For example, with Potency 3, a mage could transform a Level 1 Extreme Environment based on heat into a Level 2 Environment based on cold.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T17:43:15-07:00","id":938452,"title":"","content":"So, here comes my first attempt at a new spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Forgetfulness</b></u> (Mind 3)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand </b>: Resolve<br /> This spell allows the mage to alter the subjects thoughts that it possesses in the moment, hiding them from the subjects consciousness. Making every action harder to focus on because the subject need to force its will to remember her own thoughts. This spell gives the subject a penalty equal to potency on her next action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":".  Should probably have a withstand trait as well 07-27-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T18:21:52-07:00","id":938475,"title":"","content":"The Reach is probably too powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:39:53-07:00","id":939046,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Shatter Symbolism</u></b> (Prime 5)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unmaking<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> This Spell weakens supernal symbolism in the area. Within the area, Yantras rated less than Potency are nullified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T02:25:08-07:00","id":939410,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"523\" data-vbnamecard=\"523\">Poseur</a> I like it, however with the way it is described it sounds more like a Veiling. I think to make it fit better with Fraying, you should probably reword so it more &quot;destroys&quot; the targets train of thought instead of hiding it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11888\" data-vbnamecard=\"11888\">Custos Tenebrarum</a> I like this one. Seems fitting for an Unmaking spell for Prime. Maybe a Reach where a penalty is gained when using Yantra's, further destroying the symbolism? Or should that be a whole different spell. Also, what about two Reach and some mana to make it lasting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:53:39-07:00","id":940635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=904329#post904329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Grease (Matter \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>) </b>and <b>Glue (Matter \u2022</b></span><b>\u2022</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Scale: Area<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Brawl, Survival<br /> <br /> The easy way to turn the tide of physical combat and make those damn wheels spin, those spells changes the properties of matter it cast upon, causing the following Environmental Tilts:<br /> <b>Grease </b>create <b>Ice</b> Tilt in area it cast upon.<br /> <b>Glue </b>create <b>Glue</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tilt</span> in area it cast upon: -4 to Speed, Dramatic Failure causes <b>Immobilized </b>Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually made a spell similar to your Grease, but bumped it up to Perfecting since Tilts are typically caused by 3 or 4 dot spells. Also, Duration and Potency are, as far as I know, the only spell factors that can be primary spell factors. For that reason I would use Duration as the primary spell factor, although I agree with you that Scale is a very logical thing to want to boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T10:07:29-07:00","id":941241,"title":"","content":"Spell Request:<br /> Write me a 1 or 2nd Dot Death Spell that allows the user to function in the darkness comfortably enough to ignore blindness and &quot;sight&quot; penalties. Doesn't have to be actual &quot;sight&quot;, something like &quot;shadows and darkness extend your touch&quot; or &quot;they whisper what lays within them&quot; would be cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:35:33-07:00","id":941294,"title":"","content":"Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Athletics, Larceny<br /> <br /> The Mage switches off their visual sight in favor of sensing all shadows in the vicinity. They can determine the location and shape of all shadows within Sensory Range. Within complete darkness the effect is much more pronounced. The Mage can sense the distribution of all darkness, with living and inanimate objects visible as solid white outlines. For many purposes, the spell negates the effects of Blinded Tilt when within full darkness. The Mage can still suffer the effects of Poor Light Tilt because of residual amounts of light. Within strongly illuminated areas the Mage suffers from the Blinded Tilt<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The Mage receives both the usual and magical sensory input. The do not suffer the effects of either Poor Light or Blinded Tilts within bright areas.<br /> +1 Reach: All dark areas also carry tactile sensations, should the Mage pay attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:39:23-07:00","id":941299,"title":"","content":"Edited: Dang it... To slow..<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Revealing Shadows (Death \u2022)</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Athletics, Streetwise<br /> <br /> Darkness and shadows are the places where strange and dangerous beings hide and hunt. But to a Moros, that very darkness can become the very thing that can turn the hunt around. Any shadow the subject looks upon reveals what it is hiding within.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> When staging a surprise attack from the shadows against the subject it gains a bonus equal to the spells potency to its roll to notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:46:57-07:00","id":941306,"title":"","content":"Oooh, I like the idea that without Reach, Mage literally blinds themselves to get this effect. Now it clicks together enough to feel like it's own spell, not just a recolour of Nightivision.<br /> I think I could actually use both spells, with one dedicated solely to &quot;perceiving&quot; in Darkness, and second one (Revealing Shadows) to get some kind of Perception bonus when hunting in darkness.<br /> Yes, I'm making a Shadow Mage :P. Moros definitely has a very interesting playstyle.<br /> EDIT<br /> Are there any cool Shadow-Based powers and abilities in other gamelines I could poach for spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-01-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T12:23:06-07:00","id":941337,"title":"","content":"You have Shadowdancers in DnD, they have some pretty nifty abilites that you could adapt to spells. Or look through the Pathfinder srd for shadow spells. unless this is not the kind of gameline you mean.<br /> <br /> What about creating a shadow clone of someone that has their exact physical skills and will try to hunt them down? That would be at least Death 4 since it comes pretty close to the Golem spell.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:05:31-07:00","id":941355,"title":"","content":"Oh! Use Shadow Crafting (Death 3) to give them sharp cutting edges. Make your enemies afraid to move a muscle.<br /> <br /> If you're really mean, carry ordinary flash-bangs for when their eyes adapt to the dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:16:32-07:00","id":941363,"title":"","content":"Current &quot;combo&quot; for dealing with Bad Things is to cast Deepen Shadows targeting the whole room and plunging it into darkness, followed by Shadow Crafting targeting the whole-room Darkness, yes :P. Mages really excel at turning the scene into the most fucked up, unlivable and unfair setting ever that will first immobilize you in some way (or just make your range of actions very limited), and then kill you slowly while you slither in frustration. <br /> The good thing about this kind of mage warfare is that players can usually use the &quot;slowly killing you&quot; time to figure up a way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:25:42-07:00","id":941365,"title":"","content":"It's... It's beautiful. I feel happier for having read that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:29:59-07:00","id":941368,"title":"","content":"Request for some time and fate spells, just want a small list of things that can be made","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:48:01-07:00","id":941386,"title":"","content":"You win a no-prize if you know where this is from:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Golden Years, Tarnished Black (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Intimidate, Occult<br /> Memories are fickle and changeable - exploiting this, the subject has one of their happy memories stripped of all of its positive aspects. They suffer the False Memories (VtR: B&amp;S) condition with regards to that memory.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You are no longer restricted to only affecting happy memories. When this spell is used to worsen unhappy memories, the subject suffers the Fugue condition with regards to that memory instead.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can use this spell to make a memory happier, rather than worsening it. When the False Memories condition caused by this spell is resolved, the subject takes a Condition as if this spell was used to worsen that memory instead.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject gains the Addicted condition in relation to an element of that memory instead of the False Memories condition. Nostalgia can be a <i>bitch</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Yes, the second Reach effect can normally only be used on happy memories - you <i>need</i> the first Reach effect to have it affect bad memories. Why? Because that's the right bastard thing to do.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit Edit:</b> Oops. forgot a Reach effect. Now you can make people crave drugs because they had a crazy bad drug trip once that put them in the hospital! Woot! You're <i>such</i> a nice person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 08-01-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:45:27-07:00","id":941507,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> My group's Moros is developing a Light/Darkness Legacy, based on the founding principles of the Celestial Masters and study of his Stryx Familiar. If you have more Darkness-based spells (which can't be replicated easily by Forces), please share them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> That's deliciously awful. I'm not exactly sure if it's a Weaving, as having &quot;memories stripped of all of its positive aspects&quot; feels more like Fraying to me, but this is just a nit-pick.<br /> <br /> Time to contribute:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Blazing Light (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Science, [one more]<br /> The light in the target area becomes blinding. Affected characters take a penalty to all rolls dependent on vision equal to the spell's Potency, and a -1 to all other actions due to pain and distraction.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can't dodge what you can't see. Subjects inside the affected area lose half their Defense.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">See the Cracks (Death \u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Investigation, Subterfuge<br /> The caster intuits the target\u2019s Vice, Integrity level, and the presence of any Integrity-related Conditions. Against mages, it reads Wisdom, any Wisdom related Conditions, and which (if any) are the target's inured spells.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Knowledge of the target's psyche makes him easier to manipulate. The caster gains a bonus to appropriate Social rolls against the target equal to the spell's Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T17:03:56-07:00","id":941515,"title":"","content":"I would make the See The Cracks work by reading the Soul. I don't have any extra Darkness spells, sadly. I'm still exploring! As for Light/Shadow, I always wanted to make a Shadow/Phantasmal Legacy for Death/Prime, focused on weaving Platonic Ideals and Darkness together to create...<i>something.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:18:59-07:00","id":941606,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4854\" data-vbnamecard=\"4854\">Justin Sane</a> Eh, the memories are still inherently the <i>same</i>, you're just messing with the connotations.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Aphasia (Prime \u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Socialize, Subterfuge<br /> Language is rooted in the mind's ability to decipher symbols - and this spell renders a specific set of symbols indecipherable. Within this spell's area, a particular language becomes gibberish - it can't be spoken, read, or written, and anyone inside the area finds that they cannot understand it if they somehow hear a sample.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Rather than targeting a particular language, the spell can instead suppress the symbols of a particular subculture. In that case, any meaningful communication regarding that subculture is doomed to failure; and, as a side effect, any Yantra rooted in that subculture is unusable within the area.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ideolect</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Socialize, Streetwise<br /> Culture is just a collection of symbols, combined <i>this</i> way. While under the effects of this spell, the subject becomes capable of intuitively &quot;sensing&quot; the appropriate symbols of a specific local subculture - reduce any penalties to social rolls they suffer due to being an outsider by this spell's Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 08-02-2016, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:31:08-07:00","id":941616,"title":"","content":"I don't think you need the sentence about Withstand in Aphasia since it's a given that's how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:13:39-07:00","id":941668,"title":"","content":"You would be correct - I was distracted when I wrote that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:14:21-07:00","id":941722,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any Time Arcanum or Fate Arcanum spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11595-chaos965","name":"Chaos965","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11595_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:54:19-07:00","id":941915,"title":"","content":"Well I do have a particularly nasty curse for you: Curse the target to be unable to use paper for anything. Now while this may not seem like such a terrible curse in the first place during the electronic age where a lot of information is digital, but I have two words for you: toilet paper.<br /> <br /> As for Time, its just an idea but what about a spell that continually shifts a target a few seconds forward in time? That way you would only be able to find it by also shifting yourself forward the same amount or dispelling the effect. And yes I stole this idea from Raymond E. Feist's Midkemia books.<br /> At the moment I am not sure under which practice this should be placed, but I have full confidence in your ability to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:03:52-07:00","id":943508,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">I've noticed that I am not that good at coming up with Reach despite the fact that I love them and how they add more to a spell :P</span><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Black Light (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Science, Brawl, Empathy<br /> <br /> The targeted shadow gains the properties of an energy selected upon casting. The strength of the energy is determined by the Potency of the spell on the energy chart on p. 146. The shadow could shine like a flashlight, burn like a torch or emit sound as loud as a gun.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I know there are better ways of harming someone with Death or Forces, but I like the idea of giving shadows traits from other Arcanums.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Burning Corpse </b></u></span><u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Weaponry, Intimidation<br /> <br /> This spell turns something dead into scorching flames. Usually used to form dangerous zombies, they will function as normal except they will be burning with a strength equal to the spells Potency. The type of energy the subject is turned into does not have to be fire though.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> When the zombie dies it explodes. The size of the explosion is equal to the spells Potency in yards x2 and the damage is the same as the damage of the energy.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I thought about making it a Reach for Quicken Corpse, but you are turning matter into energy, so Patterning is required.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Soul Fire (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested rote skills:</b> Science, Stealth, Empathy<br /> <br /> The energy targeted by this spell no longer affects the physical world but instead harms the soul. Fire wont sear flesh, light won\u2019t illuminate objects, ect. Mechanically, most effects are affected on how high peoples Integrity is. Like the higher light illuminates better when it is high, damaging energy harms better the lower it is (crispy sins).<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> I really like the idea of the spell, but I am not sure how damage should be affected. Also unsure if it should be a Patterning effect since it is losing its ability to affect the physical realm, which seems like it adds another &quot;layer&quot; of transformation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T17:41:15-07:00","id":945177,"title":"","content":"Here's an attempt to recreate one of my favorite first edition spells:<br /> <br /> Suspension (Space oooo)<br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstood: Resolve<br /> Suggested rote skills: Occult, Science, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The caster alters the fabric of space around his subject such that it is static. This prevents the subject from moving, though internal systems caught within the spell are not affected (blood and electricity still flow, engines still run, light still shines, air still moves so a living subject isn't asphyxiated). While this spell does not prevent spellcasting, it does prevent the motion necessary to make the mudras for rote spells.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Create a key that bypassses the effect.<br /> <br /> Add oo in Mind, Death, or Spirit to affect the appropriate twilight phase.<br /> <br /> Add oo Forces or Matter to prevent motion of subjects under their purview (light stops, air doesn't move, electricity doesn't flow, etc).<br /> <br /> A few questions about the spell:<br /> 1: Is there anything stopping Life from being a possible addition to the added arcanum with the likely effect of such a spell being death of the subject (not necessarily the intention, just what I think would be the most likely thing to happen)?<br /> 2: For the Forces and Matter options, should it be higher than 2 dots?<br /> 3: Can anyone think of additional reach effects?<br /> <br /> <br /> Comments and criticisms are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:24:20-07:00","id":946215,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit of a noob, but I hope you guys can help me figure out how the spells work. And the best way for it is to do magic! Or write about it, at least ^^<br /> <br /> Weaving allows to &quot;give something a property of something else without changing what that first thing is&quot;. Could a Matter mage give somebody's clothes the Ph of sulfuric acid? How would that work with the rules? What about changing the density of a bullet in-flight. Or its size, like with the &quot;grow&quot; spell. Would that affect its kinetic energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:42:36-07:00","id":946232,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you could do that. It'd likely do the same damage as whatever strong acid does.<br /> <br /> Changing a bullet in flight would require a Hung spell with the trigger being the bullet being fired. It's unlikely you'd be able to change it fast enough after its fired without preparing ahead of time. I'd assume that yes, it'd affect its kinetic energy, namely slowing it down since the energy it already has isn't enough to propel the increased mass or density.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:30:14-07:00","id":946268,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't changing its speed be under the mantle of Forces? The way I figured, increasing the bullet's mass would make it hit harder since its velocity wouldn't be changed. Could such a spell be set up in such a way that it affected &quot;all bullets that travel through this space&quot;? Finding &quot;combat&quot; applications does seem a bit boring, but I'm just trying to work through the process ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:56:07-07:00","id":946284,"title":"","content":"Making bullets heavier or lighter while not changing their velocity would indeed be a way to amplify or mitigate the damage. However, I would go with reshaping the bullets while they are in flight. As for the clothes to acid: remember that you probably will still have to touch their clothes so that might not be a very bright idea. Plus I would think that it would be difficult to change the pH of clothing and that it would make more sense to simply transmute the clothes into sulfuric acid. And then I would have you roll a Wisdom check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:03:58-07:00","id":946292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=946268#post946268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't changing its speed be under the mantle of Forces? The way I figured, increasing the bullet's mass would make it hit harder since its velocity wouldn't be changed. Could such a spell be set up in such a way that it affected &amp;quot;all bullets that travel through this space&amp;quot;? Finding &amp;quot;combat&amp;quot; applications does seem a bit boring, but I'm just trying to work through the process ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural physics kick in after the change, in size or density, Forces magic would allow you to maintain the bullet's velocity after you change it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12164\" data-vbnamecard=\"12164\">Zaephyrus</a> that seems unnecessarily arbitrary, what makes changing a shirt's Ph any harder than changing the shirt itself? Also there's nothing requiring you to touch it to make the change because Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:37:50-07:00","id":946322,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> going with a physical explanation: You would be increasing the amount of hydrogen ions present in/around the shirt which for me would mean that you are either creating them from nothing (Making) or changing something into them (Patterning). That way they would no longer fall under the practice of Weaving. And in that case you might as well change the entire shirt into acid. Then again this might just be my personal preference concerning the interpretation of the spell's effect.<br /> As for the touching, I assume that you will want to do magic safely and as soon as possible. This means allowing for the minimum Reach required. Plus I would rather spend my Reach on something else if I can manage it. I am not saying you would not be able to do it, or that it would not be a Reach well spent (the opposite actually), but a spell that would do something harmfull without endangering yourself without extra Reach seems like a better idea to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:52:34-07:00","id":946332,"title":"","content":"Making the specification that the shirt's Ph value is changed might have been the cause of this, if the poster had just said, &quot;I want to make the shirt burn like acid.&quot; That's clearly just a property change which falls under Weaving. Trying to be too scientific is frequently counterintuitive to using magic.<br /> <br /> I also don't think it's a great idea to assume that the way that you would prefer to spend Reach is a great way to give advice to someone else without a qualifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:04:17-07:00","id":946345,"title":"","content":"Remember that magic operates on symbols. You aren't &quot;changing PH of a shirt&quot; necessarily; you might be attaching Symbol of &quot;It's Acidic&quot; to subject of &quot;Shirt&quot;, which will then be reinterpreted by fallen reality to be &quot;A Shirt that's Acidic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T12:20:07-07:00","id":946362,"title":"","content":"Wording it like that would indeed make it fall under Weaving and circumvent any issues I had with it.<br /> Then again, the added advantage of my approach would be that you do not need to have acid in the vicinity to swap the property with. I base this argument on the Wonderful Machine spell (which I am referring to a lot lately) which transposes a property from one machine onto another and you need to have both at hand. I would assume that this spell would follow the same setup.<br /> <br /> I also think that giving advice based on an unmodified spell (except for the 1 Reach for Instant casting) is the best way to give advice. Unless the question involves a certain use of Reach. This is my personal preference.<br /> Yes I am new to this forum, so none of you could have known that, but now I have come clean about it: I prefer to cast spells with the minimum amount of Reach required to do so safely and will base my suggestions on that. I might even add that to my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T13:21:37-07:00","id":946406,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the reason why I was going with weaving is that that allows to &quot;alter nearly any property of a target without transforming it into something completely different&quot;. If size (grow), durability (nigredo), and conductivity - why is that rulling and not weaving? - can be changed, I don't see why mass or acidity are any different. Also, I know I've seen posts about needing the things you're going to frankenstein together on hand, but I can't find anything on the book. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:48:40-07:00","id":946584,"title":"","content":"My attempt at making changing Fate Magic to make my experience as a Acanthus little more interesting:<br /> <br /> Alternate Quantum Flux<br /> <br /> This spell attunes Mage with the existence-spanning web of probability, chance, iron-clad destiny and chain-breaking force of free will. For the duration of the spell, Subject is bestowed a Condition with following benefits: they can perceive Fortune regarding their object of focus or chosen context. Practically, this means they can see and judge Bonuses and Penalties to rolls, identify their sources, spot Luck and Destiny related Conditions and Tilts, and so on.<br /> <br /> 1 Reach - For the Duration of the Spell, Subject gains a number of charges equal to spell's Potency; they may spend one charge to gain particularly deep insight into a particular Fortune - this, among other things, allow them to deduce what kind of action could manipulate the Fortune and change it's modifier by up to Mage's Fate. Sometimes it's as easy as trying to push the object from different angle or mention cute kittens to your date; sometimes it's far more esoteric, like trying again in exactly 3 minutes without your glasses on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T02:12:38-07:00","id":946816,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a><br /> Not excactly sure what the spell is suppose to do. Does it put the target in stasis by making less space around it?<br /> <br /> 1. Not sure about the question. Are you asking if you can kill with this spell by adding the Life arcanum?<br /> <br /> 2. As explained, I don't think you would need extra arcanums since they are affected by space.<br /> <br /> 3. Im not that good at making Reach myself :P<br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12017_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12017\" data-vbnamecard=\"12017\">Ehkesoyo</a><br /> You are correct. The clothing doesn't become acid but just gains the properties of it. You could also use Forces with matter and make the clothing burn or shine. But as pointed out, unless you use Sensory range, you will need to touch the clothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:19:46-07:00","id":946837,"title":"","content":"@Neros<br /> <br /> Suspension is designed to cause things to stop. It does this by transforming space to be static instead of dynamic, thus patterning, though I could see an argument for either weaving or dynamics (archmage practice)being the practice used. The first edition had the spell creating a net that could catch subjects, but they could escape either by using Space or a successful dex check if I remember correctly. I'm using withstand to represent that possibility.<br /> <br /> 1: not really, it's just that that seemed like the most likely outcome. I could totally also see something like xavier's mind stasis ability being an outcome of adding Life.<br /> <br /> 2: Reeeally? Interesting. Huh, I'll have to look more closely at twilight's mechanics.<br /> <br /> 3: Aye, 'tis perhaps the hardest thing about creative thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:27:10-07:00","id":946856,"title":"","content":"Suspension basically seems like an attempt at an advanced Ban, is that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:55:16-07:00","id":946867,"title":"","content":"Yeah, reaches for quick casting and sensory reach are almost a given, me thinks. Although, now that I think about it... Alchemist's touch to make yourself impervious to it and advanced scale so *everything* in a room is deadly acidic/radioactive/whatever sounds like a great way to turn an ambush around. Also, I love how the gsme isn't concerned by that being overpowered. Its answer is more along the lines of &quot;of course you can make that horrible, horrible thing! Now, enjoy your trip to madness<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:42:46-07:00","id":946935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=946856#post946856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suspension basically seems like an attempt at an advanced Ban, is that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but not really. Ban and Suspension could both be classified as spells that &quot;stop stuff,&quot; but they do it differently. Both ban and Suspension can trap something, but Suspension actually stops the motion of the subject. Ban is better for hiding (obviously), but Suspension can create a wall. While ban loses some of it's protective value the larger it gets, Suspension doesn't. Ban prevents an enemy mage from physically reaching you (presuming you are not both on the same side of the ban), Suspension goes further and prevents a mage from implementing yantras that include physical motion (grasping a magical tool, forming mudras, using brawl/athletics/weaponry, looking in a mirror (presuming they aren't already), etc). Suspension can trap an individual without risking them from dieing of asphyxiation (unless you ruled that air wouldn't move, in which case this spell is instantly evil). Ban inverts space while Suspension transforms it from being dynamic to being static. <br /> <br /> The more you think about, the more different applications you'll find. And one of the beautiful things about that is that Suspension doesn't make Ban obsolete (not even the wierd, +1reach advantage obsolete).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:50:13-07:00","id":946940,"title":"","content":"That's assuming you place Ban on an area though, right? What happens if you just place Ban on a single target like another Mage? Wouldn't that effectively immobilize them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:40:56-07:00","id":947272,"title":"","content":"That may be possible, but once again, you can't interact with the subject under a Ban. Suspension with the reach for the key works. Also, Suspension can stop bullets mid air, while Ban would let the bullets hit whatever was behind the ban (though not within it). Alternatively, if you were to throw a Ban on someone as they were firing a gun the bullet might hit them (possible uses there) while a Suspension would stop the bullets mid air, preserving the subject (useful if it's a friend that you don't want to hurt).<br /> <br /> You can definitely find similar uses, which means that a mage with Space doesn't have to wait until they are an adept to do those things. However, Suspension provides utility that Ban doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T16:34:59-07:00","id":947323,"title":"","content":"My take on it:<br /> <br /> Suspension (Space ooo)<br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstood: Stamina<br /> Suggested rote skills: Occult, Science, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The caster strengthens the fabric of space around his subject, solidifying his position. This prevents the subject from moving, though internal systems caught within the spell are not affected (blood and electricity still flow, engines still run, light still shines, air still moves so a living subject isn't asphyxiated). While this spell does not prevent spellcasting, it does prevent the motion necessary to make the mudras for rote spells. The subject is affected by the Immobilized Tilt, with the Durability to break free equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Create a key that bypasses the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T18:13:58-07:00","id":947371,"title":"","content":"What about a space spell to create or strengthen boundaries? Line in the sand kind of deal maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:53:51-07:00","id":948172,"title":"","content":"I had a silly idea earlier. Based on Shifting the odds and both enhancing spells of mind 3. Lemme know what you think about it. <br /> <br /> I know Kung Fu (Mind ooo)<br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> Movie nights at the Lorehouse can, sometimes, lead to some interesting developments. Its is said the first Rote version included a &quot;come hither&quot; gesture among its Mudras. This spell allows the mage to access a fighting merit with dots equal to potency for the duration. The subject must fulfil the requirements as usual since the spell only provides the knowledge and muscle memory for the merit, but doesn't do anything to improve the capabilities of the mage <br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Mental or social attributes or skills can be enhanced in order to fulfil the requirements for a merit. Each point of potency spent this way nets one point. Add Life 3 to allow the same with physical attributes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:15:01-07:00","id":948371,"title":"","content":"I'd rather make spells dealing with muscle memory, Life. The Reach effect is a bit unclear, do you really increase those traits or only to regards to the Merit's prerequisites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:41:03-07:00","id":948462,"title":"","content":"Keep in Mind that Mind 3 can only enhance skills that are allready present, I would assume the same goes for Style Merits. So in order to master Kung Fu with a Perfecting Spell, a character would need to have at least one dot in the Martial Arts skill allready. If the target has no knowledge of the Ability/Style Merit whatsoever a Pattering effect would be required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:54:09-07:00","id":948468,"title":"","content":"Something, something, something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-11-2016, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:08:07-07:00","id":948474,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> My idea was to actually increase those traits. It might be interesting to get them only for requisite filling purposes. Dunno. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> That's why I pointed to Shifting the Odds. That's a 2 dot spell that grants merits. Admittedly, it does so in a different manner, but I still feel this should work. As for the &quot;Mind can only enhance skills already present&quot;, I purposefully kept the need to meet the requirements for that same reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:37:46-07:00","id":948481,"title":"","content":"The Reach effect then seems more like a Combined Spell, honestly. There are precise spells for that very thing. If it is only &quot;virtual&quot; dots to qualify , you are better just making so the Reach eliminates the need to fulfill the requirements alltogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T01:41:19-07:00","id":949191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=947323#post947323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on it:<br /> <br /> Suspension (Space ooo)<br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstood: Stamina<br /> Suggested rote skills: Occult, Science, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The caster strengthens the fabric of space around his subject, solidifying his position. This prevents the subject from moving, though internal systems caught within the spell are not affected (blood and electricity still flow, engines still run, light still shines, air still moves so a living subject isn't asphyxiated). While this spell does not prevent spellcasting, it does prevent the motion necessary to make the mudras for rote spells. The subject is affected by the Immobilized Tilt, with the Durability to break free equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Create a key that bypasses the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this doesn't encompass what I'm looking for. First off, there's no breaking free through physical force. You can do one of four things to escape: resist the spell, counter it, dispel it, or teleport away. Otherwise you're stuck.<br /> <br /> Secondly I want the spell to be able to not only catch things mid-air, but also keep them there. I'm not so sure the immobilized tilt would do that.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, I'm looking to alter space itself. Time does a similar thing at master level where you can freeze time (in an area if you change it to an aoe spell). I'm looking to do something similar. Sure, you CAN cast Suspension as a direct target spell, but there's something satisfying about freezing an area of space. Anything mid-air would stay mid-air. Anything in the process of sinking or rising within a liquid or otherwise would be stuck at its position until the spell wore off. That's what you could do with it in 1e. Immobilized seems like it would cause a man that was running to fall, where what I'm looking for would cause him to immediately stop in whatever pose he was in as the spell hit.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T02:56:57-07:00","id":949211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=949191#post949191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, this doesn't encompass what I'm looking for. First off, there's no breaking free through physical force. You can do one of four things to escape: resist the spell, counter it, dispel it, or teleport away. Otherwise you're stuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my take is a Perfecting spell, not Patterning. Maybe add a Reach option so affected targets can't roll to escape?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly I want the spell to be able to not only catch things mid-air, but also keep them there. I'm not so sure the immobilized tilt would do that. </div> </div> </div>I don't see why it wouldn't. The Tilt is more of a shorthand mechanical ruling than an actual &quot;this is exactly what happens&quot;. It's going to need reinterpretation based on the subject (a person, a bullet, etc).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thirdly, I'm looking to alter space itself. Time does a similar thing at master level where you can freeze time (in an area if you change it to an aoe spell). I'm looking to do something similar. Sure, you CAN cast Suspension as a direct target spell, but there's something satisfying about freezing an area of space. Anything mid-air would stay mid-air. Anything in the process of sinking or rising within a liquid or otherwise would be stuck at its position until the spell wore off. That's what you could do with it in 1e. </div> </div> </div>I see that as targeting an area instead of a specific subject.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Immobilized seems like it would cause a man that was running to fall, where what I'm looking for would cause him to immediately stop in whatever pose he was in as the spell hit. </div> </div> </div>Again, depends on how you interpret the Tilt. I think it should work as you're describing.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does that make sense? </div> </div> </div>Absolutely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T05:14:13-07:00","id":949247,"title":"","content":"I see. I do suppose it would come down to ST interpretation of the immobilized tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:06:42-07:00","id":949263,"title":"","content":"I guess it would help if I came up with a new Tilt that does exactly what this spell should, but Immobilized is close enough, and I'm lazy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:25:46-07:00","id":950223,"title":"","content":"Inspired (one could say copied from) Devouring the Slain, I had this notion of a Moros Legacy that can gain Mana or other benefits through various Frayings or other destructive spells. Most notably this one:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Devouring the Fallen (Matter 3)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Durability<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Craft, Expression, Science<br /> The mage may pull energy from his target's decay into himself. The target must have at least one less point of Structure than it would when perfectly preserved or properly repaired. For each level of Potency, he may Scour the target's Pattern for one point of Mana, decreasing Structure by one in the process, causing damage through decay. Using this spell counts towards the limit of times per day a mage can gain Mana through Scouring.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may affect a target that is fully preserved and/or in perfect shape instead of one that is damaged.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell does not count toward the limit of times per day a mage can gain Mana through Scouring.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does this work thematically or am I, ahem, reaching?<br /> Is there something else to be ripped from a structure akin to Slain's Willpower?<br /> Is there a convenient alternative target to an item/structure like Slain does with ghosts?<br /> As this feeds off of decay, would it maybe also be Death 3 instead of Matter 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:30:45-07:00","id":951693,"title":"","content":"Wonder what Perfected Ice would be like...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:41:08-07:00","id":952676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=951693#post951693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder what Perfected Ice would be like...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cold.<br /> <br /> (I am so sorry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:54:42-07:00","id":953050,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> I would definitely say that this spell works thematically for Death. Allot of the spells can be &quot;copy-pasted&quot; into another arcanum, and I think this is intentional to save space. Like I've made a Life spell that works exactly like Invisibility, but it only affects life. Not light.<br /> <br /> Not sure what else you could reap from an object, though.. Minerals maybe? Uh, maybe if you added Matter, you could &quot;convert&quot; it and gain Willpower as well?<br /> <br /> And I would say it is Death you would need, not Matter. Remember, Devour the Slain don't require Life, so a spell for objects shouldn't require Matter. Especially since it is Death that draws upon the aspect of decay.<br /> <br /> Not sure what you are asking about items and ghosts..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:07:17-07:00","id":953053,"title":"","content":"Devouring the Slain has a Reach option to consume ghosts. They are asking for a similar Reach option for the consume matter spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:17:20-07:00","id":953055,"title":"","content":"Need a spell to make instant copy of Grimoire, like m<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">itosis</span></span></span> of cells - Puff, and Grimoire is into, identical books. I suspect Prime 1 will be needed to copy Rotes, but what about book itself? Is it Matter's Weaving or Perfecting? I still thinks that Making would be not needed her, as it's only copy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:28:02-07:00","id":953061,"title":"","content":"Identical books? Quite possibly Patterning. Books with the same informational content would just be Weaving since I assume you're turning one book into a replica of the other either completely or just in terms of what's in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:01:09-07:00","id":953087,"title":"","content":"If you had the paper and a whole bunch of ink, I'd say a rulling practice of matter should do it for copying the text, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:29:00-07:00","id":953093,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the book wouldn't be identical. Then again maybe I'm placing too much importance on that distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:38:06-07:00","id":953095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953087#post953087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you had the paper and a whole bunch of ink, I'd say a rulling practice of matter should do it for copying the text, basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>But without paper and ink? Just like splitting of original book in two? ( Probably like 'commanding' book to make copy of each page and then to split in to whole books. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4govZdjEBrs\" data-code=\"4govZdjEBrs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4govZdjEBrs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:56:19-07:00","id":953099,"title":"","content":"That'd be Patterning at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T05:46:35-07:00","id":953113,"title":"","content":"Creating the book from nothing would be Making. Creating the book from a plate of metal you happen to be carrying around would be Patterning (since you would be transmuting the materials into paper and maybe leather).<br /> The copying of the Rote aspect would then require Prime 3, but I am not sure of the practice. The version of the spell that does that from the 1E Mysterium book uses Perfecting, but personally is would shelve it under Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:35:34-07:00","id":953130,"title":"","content":"Copying a Rote is only Prime 1. Wyrdhamster is talking about splitting a book into two identical copies, that's Patterning Matter and some level of Prime. I'd be inclined to just rule it should be a combined spell.<br /> <br /> I don't see why you're referencing 1e when we're talking 2e and have relevant spells to address the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:38:30-07:00","id":953131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zaephyrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953113#post953113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating the book from nothing would be Making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the Mage is in a vacuum, he can probably Pattern the air around him into a new book. Making Matter is one of those really situational abilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:00:27-07:00","id":953142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953095#post953095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But without paper and ink? Just like splitting of original book in two? ( Probably like 'commanding' book to make copy of each page and then to split in to whole books. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4govZdjEBrs\" data-code=\"4govZdjEBrs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4govZdjEBrs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Making, Patterning if the mage remembers they are surrounded by air they can use. <br /> <br /> I think I would summarise the whole thing by saying that it would be Ruling if the mage had access to some suitable materials (paper&amp;ink, but also just paper and ambient water vapor or whatever), Weaving if they have access to *any* kind of material (you could technically copy the whole book into the casing of your mobile phone with the smallest font ever), Patterning if they want a book out of thin air (literally), Making if they're a bit of a show off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:33:11-07:00","id":953159,"title":"","content":"Still requires some Prime though since we're talking about a Grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:06:55-07:00","id":953222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ehkesoyo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953142#post953142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would summarise the whole thing by saying that it would be Ruling if the mage had access to some suitable materials (paper&amp;ink, but also just paper and ambient water vapor or whatever), Weaving if they have access to *any* kind of material (you could technically copy the whole book into the casing of your mobile phone with the smallest font ever), Patterning if they want a book out of thin air (literally), Making if they're a bit of a show off.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the chain of spells? I envisioned they are <i>really</i> usefull for Mysterium mages. I may try them below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953159#post953159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still requires some Prime though since we're talking about a Grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>it can easily be &quot;Prime 1 Option&quot; in spell chains - if Prime 1 is enough for <i>Scribe Grimoire</i> spell, it's enough for copying of them from existing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:19:34-07:00","id":953230,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I didn't say it wouldn't be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:19:55-07:00","id":953231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953222#post953222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the chain of spells? I envisioned they are <i>really</i> usefull for Mysterium mages. I may try them below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> it can easily be &quot;Prime 1 Option&quot; in spell chains - if Prime 1 is enough for <i>Scribe Grimoire</i> spell, it's enough for copying of them from existing one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not too sure what you mean by &quot;chain of spells&quot;. Also, <i>Scribe Grimoire </i>allows is the actual spell for copying a rote, so if that's what you want, it's already there ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:20:16-07:00","id":953232,"title":"","content":"<b>Copying (Matter \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> By means of this spell, the mage can copy the item he is seeing with materials that are suitable to it\u2019s composition. Many Mysterium apprentices makes copies of precious books from just stashes of ink and paper by this spell.<br /> When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, the original items return to their original form.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the spell\u2019s Duration is Lasting.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>For copying complex mechanisms.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022:</b> Mage can copy also any Rote found in the original Grimoire, like with \u2018Scribe Grimoire\u2019 Prime \u2022 spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Printing (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> Like in \u2018Copying\u2019 spell, only any solid material will be good for copy. Reach and Prime option are the same.<br /> <br /> <b>Duplicate (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Pattering<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability of original item<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> Like in \u2018Copying\u2019 spell, only mage can conjure copy out of thin air. In reality he IS making it out of air. To witness, item just come in two exactly the same things, like cell is dividing itself. Reach and Prime option are the same like in \u2018Copying\u2019 spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:24:28-07:00","id":953235,"title":"","content":"Copying the Lasting option should be +2 Reach.<br /> <br /> Printing should be Patterning it does literally nothing different than Duplicate as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:53:53-07:00","id":953253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953235#post953235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Copying the Lasting option should be +2 Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's based on 'Scribe Grimoire' spell - and there Lasting option is just +1 Reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=953235#post953235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Printing should be Patterning it does literally nothing different than Duplicate as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duplicate - book from air<br /> <br /> Printing - book from wood, stone or other solid material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:57:25-07:00","id":953256,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> So it really does do literally the same thing. 2e doesn't differentiate between states of matter. It should be Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:02:21-07:00","id":953258,"title":"","content":"So why 'I have ink and paper' is okay on Ruling only? It can be said to be doing exactly the same as Pattering version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-18-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:08:59-07:00","id":953296,"title":"","content":"No, it can't, because books are made of ink and paper, all you're doing with magic is cutting out the physical labor of actually making the book from the materials books are made out of. It isn't the same thing as turning a stone or air into ink and paper at all! Ideally, to make a book via Ruling you would be required to have ink, paper, binding material, and cover material, saying that Ruling can do it with just ink and paper is just convenient short hand.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> I don't understand how you can see them as equivalent at all. It makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-18-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T12:26:38-07:00","id":957106,"title":"","content":"Because I am a Moros at heart:<br /> <br /> <b>Mend Soul (Death 3)<br /> Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>None<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Empathy<br /> The willworker turns his ability to manipulate souls towards a good end. For each point of Potency, the caster may either remove one Condition that the target is suffering from as a result of reaching a breaking point or reduce one Persistent Condition to its non-Persistent form. Resolving Conditions this way does not award a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Fracture Soul (Death 3)<br /> Practice: </b>Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Empathy<br /> The caster attacks a Sleeping soul without severing it, causing it to bend unnaturally. The target suffers the Soul Shocked condition for the spell's Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirror Mirror (Death 2)<br /> Practice: </b>Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> By wrapping a person's soul with a reflective coating, the Mage causes others to see a bit of themselves, potentially fooling them into thinking the subject is one of them. For the spell's Duration, any passive attempt to discern the nature of the target of this spell reveals him to be of the same type of being as the discerner. A Vampire would, for example, see his own Beast reflected in the target in passing and assume him to be another of the Damned. A Changeling would see his tatterdemalion soul reflected there, and perceive the subject with a facsimile of his own Mien. However, this spell does not grant the subject knowledge of what <i>someone else</i> is. If unprepared, he will be quite confused by the Changeling who has decided he is kin and wants to know all about his time in Arcadia. This spell only works on passive attempts to discern the subject's nature. Active attempts (such as through the use of Auspex) provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Hasten End </b><b> (Death 3)<br /> Practice: </b>Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Brawl, Medicine, Survival<br /> A subtle tweaking of the willworker's entropic shield, made possible by greater understanding, allows him to focus and direct the decay with his intent. For the spell's Duration, whenever he succeeds in causing damage to a target using the Brawl skill he converts a number of points of damage equal to the spell's Potency from bashing to lethal, as the focused decay causes bones to crack and skin to weaken. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:03:23-07:00","id":957329,"title":"","content":"Mirror MIrror, so, from what I understand when a vampire meets another vampire for the first time their Beasts try to make them go at each other, so what happens when a Beast sees its reflection and if the vampire perceives the target as a vampire but has never seen them before and yet his Beast doesn't react how weird would that be?<br /> <br /> The rest of those are pretty cool though.I would make the ability of Mend Soul to step a Persistent Condition down to a regular Condition a Reach Option. Probably +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:17:48-07:00","id":957390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=957329#post957329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirror MIrror, so, from what I understand when a vampire meets another vampire for the first time their Beasts try to make them go at each other</div> </div> </div> </div>That's First Edition. 2e's Predatory Aura is more broadly &quot;vampires recognize each other by occult sensory cues that they can turn in on themselves to hide their nature from other vampires as part of the basics of psychic stealth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T03:02:09-07:00","id":957489,"title":"","content":"And make downgrading of Conditions non lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:44:43-07:00","id":957519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=957489#post957489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And make downgrading of Conditions non lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the reason I made &quot;Potency&quot; the Primary Factor was because at Death 3 you get an automatic Potency of 3, which is enough to cure three Conditions or one Condition and one Persistent Condition, by stepping down the Persistent Condition and then removing it using two dots of Potency.<br /> <br /> Though I can easily see how that ought to be a Reach Effect, and it's not hard to specify that it's only for the Duration of the Spell. It may make more sense to require two successive castings of the spell to remove a Persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=957390#post957390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's First Edition. 2e's Predatory Aura is more broadly &quot;vampires recognize each other by occult sensory cues that they can turn in on themselves to hide their nature from other vampires as part of the basics of psychic stealth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I must have my 1st and 2nd edition wires crossed, then. My understanding was that the Beast recognizes its own. <br /> <br /> Okay, so how do we get &quot;Mirror Mirror&quot; to function as intended? It doesn't have to be a Death spell; I just thought that the fluff made it fall best under Death's purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:03:15-07:00","id":957526,"title":"","content":"I assume it does work as intended, but if a vampire is hiding his own vampirism via whatever means Satchel is talking about then he won't detect the enchanted person as a vampire either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:05:06-07:00","id":957527,"title":"","content":"Remember that a lot of terrible diseases and problems are reflected by Persistent Conditions. So for example, someone being permanently blinded is going to have a Condition for that, and a Life 4 spell will only supress that (by regenerating eyes) for the duration of the spell. With your soul shaeningans, you could permanently fix things that are supposed to require indefinite spells. <br /> So my suggestion is - removing non-permanent Conditions is ok, Persistent Conditions should come back when duration ru.ns out. <br /> What creative thaumaturgy says about it, by the way? I'm away from my personal computer, so I can't check","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:58:56-07:00","id":957548,"title":"","content":"Just checked it and it would appear you're correct. Removing a Persistent Condition should probably be Unraveling or Patterning according to those guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:04:49-07:00","id":957549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=957527#post957527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that a lot of terrible diseases and problems are reflected by Persistent Conditions. So for example, someone being permanently blinded is going to have a Condition for that, and a Life 4 spell will only supress that (by regenerating eyes) for the duration of the spell. With your soul shaeningans, you could permanently fix things that are supposed to require indefinite spells.<br /> So my suggestion is - removing non-permanent Conditions is ok, Persistent Conditions should come back when duration ru.ns out.<br /> What creative thaumaturgy says about it, by the way? I'm away from my personal computer, so I can't check</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. But the spell specifically can't cure something like Blindness. It can only cure Conditions that come as a result of the character reaching a breaking point, so specifically Spooked, Shaken, Guilty, Fugue (Persistent), Madness (Persistent), or Broken (Persistent). That said, I see your point as to how they ought to be comparable.<br /> <br /> Creative Thaumaturgy allows a Ruling spell to create most non-Persistent, mundane Conditions, with Supernatural Conditions requiring a Weaving spell. Creating a Persistent Condition is a Patterning or Unraveling, meaning that removing a Persistent Condition ought to also be a Patterning or Unraveling. Okay, then, let's work it out:<br /> <br /> <b>Mend Soul (Death 3)<br /> Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>None<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Empathy<br /> The willworker turns his ability to manipulate souls towards a good end. For each point of Potency, the caster may either remove the Spooked, Shaken, or Guilty conditions from a target.<br /> <br /> <b>Restore the Foundation (Death 4)<br /> Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>None<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Empathy<br /> The Mage uses his Supernal knowledge and a bit of his own power to fill in the cracks in the soul of another. For the spell's Duration, the Mage may suppress one instance of the following Conditions: Madness, Broken, or Fugue. <br /> <br /> And re-reading the Creative Thaumaturgy rules gave me the inspiration for this one:<br /> <b>Bolster Soul (Death 2)<br /> Practice: </b>Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>None<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Empathy<br /> The caster wards a target's soul against iniquity, allowing him to better weather the slings and arrows of this world. For the spell's Duration, the target gains the 9-again quality on any degeneration roll he makes as a result of reaching a breaking point.<br /> +1 Reach: The target instead gains the 8-again quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":"from Conditions list, because that's too much. 08-25-2016, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:27:36-07:00","id":957610,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea that *all* persistent Conditions leave their mark on the Soul. Note that Soul Marks don't specify what kind of Persistent Conditions can be divined from them - both Persistent Madness and Persistend Blindness and Persistent Lovestruck should be highlighted by the spell, as written now. While it might be just a slip up, I really like the implications of such read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:36:56-07:00","id":957635,"title":"","content":"That does make sense from both a RAW and RAI standpoint, but they'd be beyond the ability of the Death Arcanum to fix as I understand it. Just as the Death Arcanum can't remove the Open Condition created by a spirit of the Shadow. Working the soul is within its purview, and those Conditions specifically are not the result of a chemical imbalance but of a scarred soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:44:47-07:00","id":957640,"title":"","content":"Which is why I personally made the Soul-Fixing magic go &quot;Ok, remove Persistent tag&quot;. So you might lift Persistence of Blindness, which allows Life Magic to cure it<br /> ...but the moment Soul-Fix runs out, Persistent Blindness comes back, and guy's new pair of eyes is suddenly rejected, and horror ensues. <br /> <br /> Like:<br /> DUDE is suffering from PERSISTENT BLINDNESS<br /> MAGE applies SOUL FIX to DUDE!<br /> SOUL FIX turns PERSISTENT BLINDNESS into BLINDNESS for SOUL FIX's duration!<br /> MAGE now applies a CONDITION-REMOVING SPELL to REMOVE BLINDNESS!<br /> DUDE is no longer BLIND!<br /> <br /> But then, SOUL FIX is dispelled! There is a paradox between subject's soul and their body! Violent reaction fixes the issue, and DUDE is PERSISTENTLY BLIND again! And probably traumatized like fuck. <br /> <br /> [This, kinda, allows you to simulate Regeneration with 2 spells instead of one and different suite of Arcanas. It also has great horror potential.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:56:53-07:00","id":957647,"title":"","content":"That is decidedly evil. How about a spell that reverses the ravages of old age for the spell's Duration? &quot;Congratulations, I've cured your Alzheimer's. Now that's only gonna last for about a day. If you'd like a more...<i>permanent</i> solution, I'm sure we can come to some kind of an agreement.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now imagine putting that and Regeneration together with a limited Duration...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:59:19-07:00","id":957649,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Dave somewhere said that something like this was the design goal when making spells like Regeneration dependant on Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T09:36:05-07:00","id":957665,"title":"","content":"Which is fantastic. On the one side of the morality spectrum, you get to play up the &quot;evil sorcerer&quot; archetype, keeping dependents in your thrall. On the other, you get to play up the &quot;questing martyr&quot; archetype, always seeking for a permanent solution to that which ails mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:39:57-07:00","id":958700,"title":"","content":"Did these mostly for a laugh.<br /> <br /> <b>Carry on my Wayward Son (Death 1)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Medicine, Crafts<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> The willworker slowly seeps the vitality from a target. Against an awake and aware target, this spell has no effect, but against someone who is already tired and distracted, it causes the Drugged Condition for the Spell\u2019s Duration.<br /> <br /> <b>There\u2019ll be Peace When You are Done (Death 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Medicine, Crafts<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> With greater understanding comes greater power, and now the Mage can affect even the awake and the aware. For the spell\u2019s Duration, the target becomes subjected to the Drugged Condition. This spell does not work on targets who are currently experiencing an adrenaline rush, such as those in combat or who are already on edge.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may apply this Spell to a target in combat or otherwise hyped up on adrenaline.<br /> <br /> <b>Lay Your Weary Head to Rest (Death 3)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Medicine, Crafts<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> The willworker can now take someone whose mind is already reeling from fatigue or narcotic and give them the final push they need to go to the land of dreams. Against a target with the Drugged Condition (whether inflicted by other spells or by conventional consumption of alcohol or narcotics), this spell causes the target to fall asleep for the Spell\u2019s Duration. This spell does not work on a target in combat.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may apply this spell to a target in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Don\u2019t You Cry No More (Death 4)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Medicine, Crafts<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> Draining vitality and energy from the target, the Mage forces the target to go straight from \u201cawake\u201d to \u201casleep\u201d without needing all those steps in between. The target sleeps for the spell\u2019s Duration. Against a target undergoing an adrenaline rush, such as from being in combat or otherwise on edge, this spell merely applies the Drugged Condition.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell now unleashes its full effect on a target experiencing a rush of adrenaline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:03:33-07:00","id":958707,"title":"","content":"No Rest for the Wicked (Death 3)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Suggested Rote skills: Medicine, occult, Intimidation<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> By weakening parts of the living soul in a subject it looses its self-repairing ability to replenish its energy in the form of Willpower when sleeping or resting for the duration of the spell. Any supernatural effect that gives back Willpower points as if the subject had rested is resisted by a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T06:12:44-07:00","id":958712,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12307_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12307\" data-vbnamecard=\"12307\">Frishman</a> They should probably be Life instead of Death. Not sure that applying the Drugged Condition works for some of those though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T07:47:22-07:00","id":958740,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I'd argue it could be either. I picked Death because it holds purview over enervation, which is fatigue and exhaustion. Life would be able to do it, too, but through different means (releasing sleep hormones instead of draining vital energy). Drugged was selected because fatigue affects the human body almost exactly as alcohol does. Deprived could also work, though that is, ironically, caused by <i>not</i> getting a fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:38:38-07:00","id":962130,"title":"","content":"I like to recreate \u2018cloning\u2019 spell from 1E Space Arcanum that my players loved. There is game design catch in here, but you will see in first draft of it. Behold!<br /> <br /> <b>Manifold Presence (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Subterfuge, Science<br /> By means of this spell, the mage is uncovering the truth about Sympathy \u2013 that you exist whenever someone thinks about you. In the effect, mage copy the subject in to perfect duplicate, up to one per Mind dot, with all traits and perks. However, all duplicates are in reality the same being, so they make exactly same actions.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage can add next duplicate of target.<br /> <b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022: </b>Mage can copy subject conciseness synchronizing with conciseness of his duplicates. Subject can makes command the copy will do, on next turn.<br /> <b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: </b>Mage is perfectly copy subjects own Mind in to duplicates. It\u2019s independent and so is making actions instantly, on it\u2019s own. However, the subjects players is making decisions on what copy will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-02-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T02:45:11-07:00","id":962169,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> that spell is unusable. Copies of yourself should be determined by Target factors not by Mind dots -especially- since this is a Space spell and not a Mind one. Thus the Reach clause is also meaningless.<br /> <br /> The original spell in 1e that you're trying to duplicate called for Life and there's a really good reason for this. Without it you're projecting your presence into multiple locations but all of those &quot;images&quot; are in fact one body. Since Space in 2e can't can't create physical bodies you still need Life in this spell. Definitely one of the rare conjunctional spells. Technically all you need is Life to create a clone of yourself of course, the Space component allows you to split a Connected Sympathy with your clones so they don't suffer Soul Loss.<br /> <br /> Micromanaging your clones via Mind should be a separate spell since its modifying the results of the first spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T02:44:53-07:00","id":962744,"title":"","content":"Not much Fate stuff lately, so here's some. If someone already posted some similar stuff than sorry.<br /> <br /> Against the Odds - Fate 3<br /> Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested rote skills: Athletics, Drive, Subtefuge<br /> One in a million chances happen in 9 cases out of 10 at least when you're an Adept of Fate. Under the effects of this spell the subject of this spell can change enviromental penalties to rolls into enviromental bonuses up to the potency of the spell. This affects rolls up to equal to the spells potency.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can do the opposite and change bonuses into penalties.<br /> <br /> Nobody - Fate 5<br /> Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested rote skills: Intimidation, Larcery, Computer<br /> Our lives are stories told by fate. We grow when we face the unexpected, either succeding or failing.. This spell breaks that and curses the target with an uneventfull life.. Unexpected things rarely happens to he subject,and he fails to confront those that do, his narrative destroyed by the magic. The subject of the spell can never gain Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T06:47:00-07:00","id":962801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=962744#post962744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against the Odds - Fate 3</div> </div> </div> </div>I am uncertain how this one would work. Would you mind giving an example of how it'd go in play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:43:20-07:00","id":962821,"title":"","content":"There is a terrible weather giving you -5 penalty to shooting and you are bleeding for -2 penalty. You have Against The Odds with Potency of 7. You turn weather penalty into +5 bonus, but you can't turn -2 wound penalty because it's not enviromental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:36:46-07:00","id":963193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=962821#post962821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a terrible weather giving you -5 penalty to shooting and you are bleeding for -2 penalty. You have Against The Odds with Potency of 7. You turn weather penalty into +5 bonus, but you can't turn -2 wound penalty because it's not enviromental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And that's a super neat spell!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:33:23-07:00","id":964160,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2636_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2636\" data-vbnamecard=\"2636\">Menace</a> <br /> I think there is a problem with the Reach for &quot;Against the Odds&quot;; there is no environmental bonuses... Except maybe for darkness when sneaking.. I would also like some examples for this..<br /> <br /> Also, Is the &quot;Nobody&quot; spell lasting?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12017_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12017\" data-vbnamecard=\"12017\">Ehkesoyo</a> <br /> I think it is something like in a snow storm and wanted to shoot someone at a range of 30 yards (that is a -3 penalty). So if the spell had a potency of 3, it would turn that penalty into a bonus. Fluff-wise, it could be translated into a sudden buff of wind bringing the targets movement almost to a halt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:09:35-07:00","id":964177,"title":"","content":"Although, thinking about it, that spell is extremely powerful. Each potency is giving a swing of 2 dice, double the usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12017-ehkesoyo","name":"Ehkesoyo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12017_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T03:25:17-07:00","id":964184,"title":"","content":"Yeah it should negate dice penalties, then for a Reach excess Potency that doesn't go to negating penalties create bonuses. So you have a -5 from the environment, cast the spell with the Reach and 7 Potency and receive a +2 to your roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:40:42-07:00","id":964340,"title":"","content":"You think a Patterning Space effect could weave together two objects sympathy enough to give them a Connected rating? I mean obviously you can do that with Spirit, so I figure it's kosher, but what effects would you get? An empathic form of communication because Sympathy is created by emotions? Maybe for a Reach they could share sensory input?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:41:14-07:00","id":964341,"title":"","content":"Negating penalties would be kind of pointless as you can just give yourself bonus dice at that point. But it might be too strong. Feel free to do modify as you please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Is the &quot;Nobody&quot; spell lasting </div> </div> </div>Spells aren't lasting unless noted otherwise. It should have Withstand: Composure though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:42:20-07:00","id":964928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=964340#post964340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think a Patterning Space effect could weave together two objects sympathy enough to give them a Connected rating? I mean obviously you can do that with Spirit, so I figure it's kosher, but what effects would you get? An empathic form of communication because Sympathy is created by emotions? Maybe for a Reach they could share sensory input?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a spell that already can give you a connected sympathetic rating with something. I would imagine that you would only need a reach to change the &quot;target&quot; to a different subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T06:53:24-07:00","id":964933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=964928#post964928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's a spell that already can give you a connected sympathetic rating with something. I would imagine that you would only need a reach to change the &amp;quot;target&amp;quot; to a different subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:59:24-07:00","id":965204,"title":"","content":"I had an idea while pondering something earlier: Could the Life 2 spell Lure and Repel be paired with Prime and maybe a Reach effect to allow it to repel Sleepers and/or attract Sleepwalkers and Awakened?<br /> <br /> If so, it feels like a spell that Guardians would get a ton of mileage out of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:07:14-07:00","id":965213,"title":"","content":"I would let it work on Sleepers like that as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T23:38:56-07:00","id":969046,"title":"","content":"What Death spell would remake you into Ghost Mage after your death? Death 5 or lower maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:15:00-07:00","id":969411,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> <br /> I think Prime might be able to do that without the need for life where its not the life itself it is Repelling or Luring, but the fact that they are Sleepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> <br /> Hmm.. I think you also might need Prime to keep a hold on the Awakened aspect of the desceased...... Though, I cannot remember how Ghost Mages work :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:30:15-07:00","id":969419,"title":"","content":"Hmm...could you accomplish the effect by removing your soul, binding it into a Dedicated Tool and then killing yourself with a Death Spell that anchors your ghost to that Tool? Cause that would be purely Death. If you could then rebind your soul to your ghost it might get around the whole &quot;phylactery&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T13:47:21-07:00","id":969431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=969411#post969411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Prime might be able to do that without the need for life where its not the life itself it is Repelling or Luring, but the fact that they are Sleepers</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you do that? How can you repel someone with Prime? You might be able to broadcast a feeling that the person is flawed in some way, but there's no Truth to use here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:31:38-07:00","id":970233,"title":"","content":"I could see a Prime 2 (veiling?) effect creating an, hm, aura of Supernality or Significance that the Quiescent subconsciously avoid? (Possibly based on integrity, so people with sounder minds are more likely to avoid it.)<br /> <br /> You could do an equivalent Death 2 effect creating an &quot;air of mystery/secrecy&quot; that draws in people with Obsessions.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Here's a riff on another Ascension rote. The original was Spirit 3/Forces 3/Prime 2, which would be &quot;create a fire and awaken its spirit&quot; in that system. That's a Mastery effect in Awakening, though, so this version is &quot;bolster a fire spirit and give it a specific Manifestation-like effect.&quot; The effect can be replicated-ish with Bolster Spirit +2 reach or Bind Spirit. I unscientifically decided that determining the exact manifestation gained from a Rank increase was trivial (comparable to picking a numen) and that involving a second sphere and limiting it to a specific scenario justified pulling down the Reach requirements a bit.<br /> <br /> It's not unlike Quicken Corpse, I suppose? What do you think? Does it need to go up to Spirit 4? I suspect as a raw Spirit 4 effect it wouldn't need Forces but I kind of like lower-dot conjunctional approaches.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hungry Flame (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Gauntlet Strength<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Survival, Animal Ken</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage renders the substance of a flame fluid and mobile and stokes the awareness and power of the slumbering mote within. This spell must be performed in an area Resonant to flames or burning; one sufficient for such a mote to have formed. Once enacted, it temporarily elevates the mote into a Rank 1 spirit and invests it into a body of flames for the duration of the spell. Divide the spell's Potency to provide the spirit with its Attribute dots (subject to the normal maximums.) Its fiery body effectively exhibits the Fire Elemental Dread Power (Werewolf the Forsaken, pg 210) but it has no other Influences, Manifestations, or Numina. It is not bound to obey the mage and will instead pursue its natural inclination - to create as large a fire as possible and feed on the resulting flow of essence.<br /> The Potency of this spell limits how large a fiery &quot;body&quot; the spirit may be invested into (as per Transform Energy), provided one is available. Flames outside of the spirit's control act normally.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can &quot;steer&quot; the spirit's path, providing a one-or-two-word suggestion for what the spirit might burn first - &quot;those men&quot; or &quot;that building&quot;. Once this mission has been accomplished or become impractical or impossible, the spirit carries on as it sees fit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can enhance the ferocity of the flames the spirit is invested into. Levels of Potency can be spent (at a one-to-one rate) increasing the heat or size of the fire instead of providing Attribute dots to the spirit. When the spell ends the fire returns to its normal form.<br /> <br /> <b>Death </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span><b> <i>Instead</i>:</b> By replacing Spirit with Death, a mage can invest a plasm associated with an arson or death by burning into the fire; it will generally seek to burn things or people linked to the event that created the deathly imprint in the first place, or to re-enact that moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:23:41-07:00","id":971772,"title":"","content":"How about some <i>unusual</i> Weaving Spells from the Subtle Arcana?<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Moral Dilemma (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Empathy. Politics<br /> <br /> This <i>bizarre</i> spell adds a touch of psychological cruelty to what would otherwise be a straight-forward curse. This spell must be cast with <i>exactly</i> two targets - any more or less, and it immediately fails. Once cast, each target chooses either <i>masochism</i> or <i>sadism</i> as a Reflexive action. If they picked masochism, the spell imposes one Hex on them - if they choose sadism, the spell imposes two Hexes on the other target instead. The targets have a rough understanding of what each choice entails - hurt yourself, or hurt the other person more.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Each target that chooses sadism also receives a Boon - they are aware of this fact.<br /> <b>Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> If there is a sympathetic tie between the two targets, each target that chose sadism reduces the strength of the tie by one step.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Yes, I decided to apply game theory to this biznitch. Yes, if both people choose sadism, both of them get saddled by two Hexes.</i><br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Power Through Slavery (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <br /> A <i>distressingly</i> popular spell amongst both the Adamantine Arrow and the Seers of the Throne (though for <i>very</i> different reasons). Upon casting this spell, choose another person to be your target's &quot;master&quot; - your target receives Obedience to [Master's Name] as a second Vice, and takes a Beat whenever they fulfil that Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target may take an Arcane Beat instead of a normal Beat whenever they would fulfil their secondary Vice. They may also treat &quot;following my master's orders&quot; as an Oblation.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The master you choose may be an organization rather a single person - the target's second Vice becomes Obedience to Members of [Organization Name].<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The master you choose gains the benefits of the Loved merit with regards to the Target.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022:</b> The target does not suffer Breaking Points due to their master's spells - they still suffer from all the other effects of the Sleeping Curse.<br /> <b>Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The target suffers from the Soulless condition for the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> <i>A little weirdness in terms of the third Reach effect - while the target's &quot;master&quot; is not </i>technically<i> the target of the spell, that merit represents someone feeling REALLY strongly about you. So I thought it'd be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrows tend to cast it on themselves, pop the third (and maybe the first) Reach effects, and pick whoever they happen to be bodyguarding as their master. Seers... well, you know Seers.<br /> <br /> =---=</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Suffer Not The Witch (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> An old &quot;favorite&quot; amongst Banishers, this spell <i>messily</i> purges mana from a Pattern. The target must immediately spend Mana equal to the spell's potency on absolutely nothing - if this would exceed their limit on mana spent each turn, they continue wasting mana until they have either spent a total amount of Mana equal to the spell's potency or the spell ends. As a side effect, any Mage targeted by this spell <i>immediately</i> flares a warped version of their Nimbus - it lasts for the full duration of the spell, though it doesn't impose their Nimbus Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The victim of the spell also suffers from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=223525#post223525\">Nausea</a> tilt - this is not considered part of the spell's effects, and therefore doesn't end when the spell does.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the victim was under the effects of Active Mage Sight or Mage Armor, they immediately end. For the duration of the spell, reactivating either effect costs an additional point of Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The victim must immediately scour their Pattern - doing so doesn't grant them additional Mana (or whatever other benefit they would receive from the scouring).<br /> <br /> <i>I think it goes without saying that spending to spend is a Reflexive action. More importantly, this is the kind of spell that gets you challenged to the Duel Arcane if you cast it in &quot;polite society&quot;. Banishers love it because it strips a Mage of defenses and can leave them literally vomiting magic. Plus, getting the lynch-mob to target the person emanating the howls of the damned is a damn sight easier than the alternative.</i><br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">End Debate (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <br /> Upon casting this spell, pick a topic - the spell &quot;kills&quot; it, setting the target's impression level towards anyone who attempts to change their opinion on the topic through Social Maneuvering to Hostile. In addition, any Social Maneuvering attempt that brings up the topic causes the subject to immediately close a Door before the other character makes their roll. If the subject has an Aspiration related to the topic, they can't take Beats from that Aspiration for the duration of the spell - if you spend one mana when casting the spell, this also applies to Oblations.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target also loses the drive to do anything about the &quot;killed&quot; topic - any Extended Action they attempt related to the topic is treated like they had suffered a Dramatic Failure (which counts towards the number of rolls they may make).<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target is immune to any attempt to change their stance on the topic - Supernatural powers instead trigger a Clash of Wills with this spell.<br /> <br /> <i>Death covers both endings and enervation - this fits. It's a reasonably dickish way to wipe out interest in a topic. </i><br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bind in Flesh (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Rank<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> This spell tears a spirit out of Twilight and into the material world. For the duration of the spell, the spirit is modified as follows:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The spirit is naturally material, and cannot enter Twilight or the Shadow.<br /> \u2022 The spirit can scour its Pattern as if it were a Mage with Gnosis equal to twice its Rank - it cannot naturally recover Essence through other means.<br /> \u2022 The spirit gains the benefit of Spirit Armor as if it had a number of dots in Spirit equal to its Rank.<br /> \u2022 The spirit loses Essence at twice the normal rate.<br /> <br /> If the spirit is forced to return to Twilight or the Shadow, this spell immediately ends. There is a related version of this spell under the Death Arcana, which targets ghosts instead of spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spirit generates appropriate Resonant conditions as if it were a natural denizen of the material. This is usually sufficient to prevent them from suffering the accelerated Essence bleed due to being outside of a Resonant area.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The spirit's body is reconfigured to work like a living creature - it no longer downgrades damage (due to having organs now, however strange they might happen to be). As some Mages have discovered, this also renders the spirit fertile - a spirit bound to flesh in this way can mate with any creature related to its Influences, creating strange half-spirit hybrids.<br /> <br /> <i>I cribbed this a bit from the Flesh-Bound Spirit rules from W:tF. This one has some... interesting consequences (I was</i> this<i> close to giving it a Reach option to make it Lasting.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:14:48-07:00","id":971900,"title":"","content":"There's no reason moral dilemma should be limited to two targets, and I'm not sure why targets who choose sadism are preferred (Via a possible Boon) but those who pick masochism aren't, haven't you ever heard of bdsm? <br /> <br /> I think the first Reach effect of Power through Slavery is too good.<br /> <br /> The second Reach of Suffer not the Witch shouldn't work, you're affecting additional targets that weren't included in the casting with a different effect than the original spell.<br /> <br /> Bind in Flesh should probably be Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:45:01-07:00","id":971925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=971900#post971900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason moral dilemma should be limited to two targets, and I'm not sure why targets who choose sadism are preferred (Via a possible Boon) but those who pick masochism aren't, haven't you ever heard of bdsm?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've never heard of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prisoner%27s_dilemma\" target=\"_blank\">Prisoner's Dilemma</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:01:41-07:00","id":971928,"title":"","content":"I have heard of it, but as far as I can see it has only a tangential bearing on the spell. First, there's still no reason to limit the spell to two targets, the prisoner's dilemma isn't limited to that except in its simplest variation. Second, there still isn't a reason for only the sadist option to receive a Boon. Third, the prisoner's dilemma isn't a choice between sadism and masochism but between selfishness and group loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:17:04-07:00","id":972119,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:41:43-07:00","id":972234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=971928#post971928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have heard of it, but as far as I can see it has only a tangential bearing on the spell. First, there's still no reason to limit the spell to two targets, the prisoner's dilemma isn't limited to that except in its simplest variation. Second, there still isn't a reason for only the sadist option to receive a Boon. Third, the prisoner's dilemma isn't a choice between sadism and masochism but between selfishness and group loyalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically:<br /> <br /> 1) If both people pick Masochism, the group is best off.<br /> 2) It is, however, <i>apparently</i> in the individual's best interests to pick Sadism (since you don't <i>necessarily</i> get cursed).<br /> 3) This is <i>literally</i> an inverse version of the simplest form of the Prisoner's Dilemma. Seriously. I pulled the numbers from it and everything.<br /> 4) The Sadist option gets the Boon because it encourages you dicking over the other person - the point of the spell is to destroy trust, after all.<br /> 5) I am <i>entirely</i> aware of what the Prisoner's Dilemma is about - I picked Sadism and Masochism because they're catchy words.<br /> <br /> Who knows, I might remake it so it works with the larger context. I might do my final exam for Advanced Linear Algebra, why not\u00b9<br /> <br /> As for the other ones...<br /> <br /> A) (Power through Slavery): I don't see what's so strong about it - is it the Oblation? I might swap it over to taking the Leveraged condition instead.<br /> <br /> B) (Suffer Not The Witch): That's... not what I meant. Huh. What it's <i>supposed</i> to do is knock the target out of Active Mage Sight and Mage Armor. So if they're scrutinising something, they lose the benefits of Active Mage Sight, and if they've got (say) Death Armor up, it ends that. Essentially, it's rewriting your Pattern to purge mana posthaste.<br /> <br /> I might swap it to &quot;the target cannot bolster their Pattern&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> C) (Bind in Flesh): In retrospect, I put too much in there. I'm thinking of swapping it to something less all-encompassing (Maybe they just Materialize and can't leave. I like the bit about Scouring their Pattern, though - maybe I'll make that a Reach option.)<br /> <br /> \u00b9 <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Our professor joked that the final would work as follows:<br /> 1) If you show up and take it, your grade on the final is whatever you scored on the test.<br /> 2) If no-one shows up, everyone gets a perfect score.<br /> He later reminded everyone he was joking after people took it <i>super</i>-seriously.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:28:20-07:00","id":973769,"title":"","content":"It's not really that creative but asking for some feedback. Is it any good?<br /> <br /> <b>Shield (Forces 2)<br /> Practice: </b>Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> Mage surrounds the target with a screen of anti-force that redirects all kinetic based attack. Target is safe from any mundane source of pressure, sound and velocity induced damage. The spell requires a Clash of Wills to work against magicaly induced kinetic attacks.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-21-2016, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:43:35-07:00","id":973821,"title":"","content":"What does the Potency do? If nothing then make the primary factor Duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:04:55-07:00","id":973832,"title":"","content":"Shielding and Veiling Practice is nuts. Love it. I edited the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T02:56:19-07:00","id":974310,"title":"","content":"Death 4 or 5 you can heal Inuring on a Mage's soul. Alternatively, you could increase Inuring past the normal limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:06:58-07:00","id":977923,"title":"","content":"Newish to mage, definitely new to the spellcasting angle. Second edition seems to have made figuring out the mechanics a lot easier but I'm trying to figure out the different Practices and their capabilities, as well as adding it into a spell.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking of a spell that would take a roll of coins and basically forge a sword out of them, with them stuck together in the general shape of a sword, the edges honed to sharpness and the whole thing made durable. Would this be doable with just Matter? And if so, how?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thank you but was looking for the long answer.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.oriental-arms.co.il/photos/items/83/002583/ph-0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>Sort of like this, except made for combat and not ritual.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Apologies if this should be asked elsewhere, just direct me there if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:46:08-07:00","id":977948,"title":"","content":"Short answer is yes. <br /> <br /> Edit: You could pull it off with just Shape Matter. Maybe State Change to make them malleable and cohesive enough to bond when they're pressed together, but personally I think I'd skip that step. Sharpness could probably just default to 0L, but be enhanced via something like Crucible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-28-2016, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:01:52-07:00","id":977987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=977948#post977948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer is yes.<br /> <br /> Edit: You could pull it off with just Shape Matter. Maybe State Change to make them malleable and cohesive enough to bond when they're pressed together, but personally I think I'd skip that step. Sharpness could probably just default to 0L, but be enhanced via something like Crucible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I guess the problem I'm having is what to do about spells that would use multiple practices. I <i>think </i>it doesn't have to be done with separate spells, but I can't see anything about that in the book. And would it even count, if it's just combining Matter 3 + Matter 3 + Matter 3 effects?<br /> <br /> Okay I just found that, p118. It looks like the number of effects you can put in a spell are limited by Gnosis. Could it be done with Ruling, to have them stick together, then Weaving, to sharpen? The practices part is mixing me up too.<br /> <br /> When combining, are you combining Practices? Or spells, like the rote examples offered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:12:33-07:00","id":977993,"title":"","content":"Shape Matter is Ruling, that's only two dots and I'd let it work as long as the coins are of the same composition. It's not really that different than using Shape Matter to turn a tire iron into a crowbar. I did recall the name of the spell wrong though, it's properly called Shaping. Find the Balance is also a Ruling effect that can grant 9-again, and a Reach would grant 8-again. Perfecting would just let you increase the L damage a sword of its type should be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-28-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:23:02-07:00","id":978026,"title":"","content":"Just a simple one I'm tinkering with for a Mastigos PC with Time. I wanted to make a 2-dot spell that imposes a Condition, although as I think about it, this might be better suited to a Reach effect for Temporal Summoning or a hypothetical Time 3 version of Web-Weaver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your Worst Day (Time \u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Empathy, Investigation<br /> <br /> Good days and bad days are more than just memories, they're inscribed in Time. By pulling tight on the strings of Temporal Sympathy, the mage can conjure the low points and happy moments of the past into the present. The mage can apply a single non-persistent mental Condition that the subject has previously experienced, such as Guilty, Shaken, Swooned, or Inspired. This spell is not powerful enough to apply persistent Conditions such as Broken or Madness, and it can only apply Conditions that the subject experienced within the same day. If the Temporal Sympathy Attainment is incorporated, the spell can apply an older non-persistent Condition, although the mage must have a specific idea of what moment in the subject's timeline they are drawing on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:45:46-07:00","id":980952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=977987#post977987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I guess the problem I'm having is what to do about spells that would use multiple practices. I <i>think </i>it doesn't have to be done with separate spells, but I can't see anything about that in the book. And would it even count, if it's just combining Matter 3 + Matter 3 + Matter 3 effects?<br /> <br /> Okay I just found that, p118. It looks like the number of effects you can put in a spell are limited by Gnosis. Could it be done with Ruling, to have them stick together, then Weaving, to sharpen? The practices part is mixing me up too.<br /> <br /> When combining, are you combining Practices? Or spells, like the rote examples offered?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is, &quot;Whatever your ST allows,&quot; but the long answer is &quot;it would be a combination of the Matter 3 Spell 'State Change' and the Matter 2 'Shaping' spells.&quot; The first spell would Weave the roll of coins into a &quot;liquid&quot; while the second spell would Rule the &quot;liquid&quot; coins into the shape of a sword. This would allow you to turn the roll of coins into a fused, sharp sword of your design. So yes it's a bit of an advanced spell, but it has a LOT of utility for something that costs 0 Mana and does not require Reach to use on something you're touching. For reference as to just what someone with that kind of power can do, I refer you to Magneto. And that's just with metal. Now add in stone, concrete, earth, wood, Kevlar, etc., and remember that all it takes is Gnosis 3 and Matter 3 to pull off. <br /> <br /> However, there's nothing saying you can't spend 4 Merit dots to grab an Artifact that accomplishes the same thing for that one limited effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T13:46:12-07:00","id":980997,"title":"","content":"I don't see a reason to need more than Shape Matter really, maybe with a Reach to have separate things of similar compositions fuse. Shape Matter could certainly be used to take one thing and take parts off it after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T06:34:47-07:00","id":981410,"title":"","content":"Here's Shaping, for everyone looking who doesn't feel like breaking out the book to see what we're referencing. <br /> <br /> Shaping (Matter \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Durability<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Expression, Persuasion<br /> Liquids, gases, and amorphous solids are the mage\u2019s playthings with this spell. She can shape them into any form she desires, manipulating them in defiance of gravity, for as long as the spell lasts. This spell cannot change the state of matter (e.g. from solid to liquid), but substances that have been temporarily transformed into shapeable states by magic may be affected. Particularly intricate shapes may require a reflexive Wits + Crafts<br /> roll, at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can alter the shape of solid substances as well. If used to warp a tool or weapon, each point of Potency reduces the subject\u2019s equipment bonus or damage by \u20131. If the equipment bonus or damage is reduced to 0, the object is useless.<br /> +1 Reach: If the mage is creating or repairing an object using this spell, reduce the number of successes required on the extended action by one per point of Potency. This can\u2019t reduce the number of required successes below one.<br /> +2 Reach: The mage can create an appropriate Environmental Tilt, such as Earthquake, Flooded, or Howling Winds.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach gives you the ability to shape solids, which technically <i>could</i> be used to fuse the coins together and sharpen them using the Standard Scale rules, but the other +1 Reach effect implies that attempting to craft an item such as a sword using this spell requires an Extended Action as per the Crafting rules. What we're looking for is an instantaneous effect which, to me, requires both State Change to turn the roll of coins into a liquid and Shaping to cast them into the form you want before State Change's effect ends. But, like I said, it's ultimately up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:25:29-07:00","id":981604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=981410#post981410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">+1 Reach gives you the ability to shape solids, which technically <i>could</i> be used to fuse the coins together and sharpen them using the Standard Scale rules, but the other +1 Reach effect implies that attempting to craft an item such as a sword using this spell requires an Extended Action as per the Crafting rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Crafting rules? The ones on the Chronicles of Darkness corebook state Crafting is an Instant Action (that might take some time to complete, but still).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:59:44-07:00","id":981676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=981604#post981604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Crafting rules? The ones on the Chronicles of Darkness corebook state Crafting is an Instant Action (that might take some time to complete, but still).</div> </div> </div> </div>The ones in the Mage book state that Creating Art or Repairing an Item is an extended action (p. 209), so presumably so is Creating an Item. When in doubt, I always default to the linebook I'm working in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:25:37-07:00","id":981776,"title":"","content":"If you decrease the number of successes needed on the Extended Action by pumping Potency you could probably bring it down to one success which you can probably get on one roll, or just add an additional +1 Reach to make it an Instant Action Crafts roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:21:11-07:00","id":981906,"title":"","content":"I could see the Reach effect working. Something akin to &quot;+1 Reach: When using this Spell to create an item, you reduce the interval for the extended action to one turn. In addition, you add this spell's Potency to your Intelligence + Crafts roll.&quot; If you manage to screw up the first time you'll have to cast the spell again, though, but someone specializing in this effect ought to be rocking between +8 and +11 for the Int + Crafts + Potency roll. That's roughly 2-4 successes. I have no idea how much is required to craft a sword, as I don't have the core book and the Mage book doesn't seem to cover it specifically, unless I've missed it somewhere.<br /> <br /> What say ye, sir?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:50:46-07:00","id":982016,"title":"","content":"Something I should have explained better is I was thinking of the Reach costs going like this: +1 Reach to lower the Crafts roll to an Instant action only if the Reach option for Potency to lower the number of necessary successes has been activated.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah that works. Normally crafting a sword is probably between ten and fifteen successes btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:21:29-07:00","id":982071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=982016#post982016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I should have explained better is I was thinking of the Reach costs going like this: +1 Reach to lower the Crafts roll to an Instant action only if the Reach option for Potency to lower the number of necessary successes has been activated.<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah that works. Normally crafting a sword is probably between ten and fifteen successes btw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so for the low cost of 4 Reach and a -20 penalty to the spellcasting roll you can use this 2-dot spell to accomplish this effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:46:05-07:00","id":982081,"title":"","content":"-20 in penalties for Potency is probably too high, I dunno. I feel like the cost should be more prohibitive because of Reach than dice penalties.<br /> <br /> Actually after thinking about it I'm okay with that. One thing you can do to reduce Potency cost is spend yet another Reach to make Potency the primary factor. Because of the fact that you cast the spell and then spend an Instant action to roll Craft you'll never be able to use this spell to get it all done in one turn either. Anyone with higher than Matter 2 will be able to come up with a more efficient method, especially after Matter 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-05-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:40:09-07:00","id":982234,"title":"","content":"To me the problem seems is that rearranging the coins <i>and</i> fusing them sounds like two different Effects, so I'm wondering if there's a way to accomplish the same outcome without the two distinct effects. To that end!<br /> <br /> <b>Form Follows Function (Matter 3)</b><br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Expression, Persuasion<br /> The Mage transcribes a Supernal blueprint onto a collection of discrete but homogenous pieces, forcing them to take that shape and its associated function for a time. The willworker could use this spell to draw a sword from the sand, a bottle from broken glass, a shield from smoke or any other simple item with no moving parts from disparate pieces of the same material. The only limitation is that he needs to have enough of the material to create the item within the Scale of the spell, and thus the Scale may need to be enhanced in order to create items out of air or smoke. If the item created is a weapon, it gains a weapon bonus of 2; if armor, an armor rating of 2; and if another type of item an equipment bonus of +2.<br /> +1 Reach: the Mage can use this spell to create complex items, ones with a number of moving parts equal to the spell's Potency. A revolver, for example, could be created using a spell of Potency 3 (though you would have to provide your own ammunition). <br /> <br /> I figured, &quot;Hey, it works for Shadow Sculpting!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:40:19-07:00","id":983143,"title":"","content":"I decided to create a spell in respect to the new Dishonored game coming out, by emulating one of the iconic powers available to you.<br /> <br /> Beneath Your Skin(Mind 4+Death 4)<br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning:<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Stealth, Occult, Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> The Mage possesses a target, as per the Mind 4 spell &quot;Possession&quot;, with the added twist of transforming their dormant body into a shadow, as per the Death 4 spell &quot;Shadow Flesh&quot;, and pinning the shadow unto the possessed target's own. In this form you gain the Physical Attributes of the subject, and retain your Mental Attributes, as well as your ability to cast spells. As a standard action, you may touch another subject and &quot;jump&quot; into them, also instantly pinning your own shadow-body without any conscious effort. However, this does cause the previously possessed to come out of it under a state of malaise, potentially drawing suspicion, if only for a moment.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The Mage can alternate between controlling the possessed body, or moving the shadow-body independently of it as a reflexive action, though you can only control one by default.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage can possess another subject via Sensory Range, not just Touch.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may, as a Standard action, take an item originally transformed on their person at the time of spellcasting, and bring it into normal form again for use.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8573,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","user":"Zombiecakes","date":". 10-07-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:29:58-07:00","id":989609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=928036#post928036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>Stoke the Flames</u> (Mind 2)<br /> Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> The Mage can urge a given subject towards accomplishing a particular goal of his choosing, This grants him the Inspired Condition for the duration of the spell, or until he chooses to resolve it earlier.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> By spending a point of Mana, the Mage allows a subject to avail of the Condition a number of times equal to the spell's Potency before it's resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ripped off the concept of this spell and applied the mechanics of the Fate spell Exceptional Luck:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tend the Flames (Mind \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Intimidation, Socialize<br /> The mage urges the subject towards accomplishing certain goals or douses their enthusiasm. This spell bestows a number of Conditions (such as Deprived, Inspired, Obsession, Shaken or Steadfast) or Tilts (such as Beaten Down, or Insane) on the subject equal to Potency for the Duration of the Spell. The subject may Withstand negative effects with Composure.<br /> Note that beneficial Conditions don't grant Beats when the subject resolves them unless the caster achieved an exceptional success in the casting.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The Conditions and Tilts can affect spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Obsession Condition (which we call Obsessed to distinguish from Mage Obsessions) is technically a Persistent Condition which the guidelines states should fall under Patterning or Unraveling, but since it's not Lasting I don't think it matters much. I also removed the Reach to cast this reflexively that Exceptional Luck has because I think this is a bit too complex to do reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:37:29-07:00","id":991690,"title":"","content":"So, is it okay to ask for help designing spells if we have a concept but aren't great on mechanics? I've been looking into how to handle using magic for large engineering projects: say, mass-producing objects or creating large, complex objects, like turning a huge pile of scrap into a supersonic VTOL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:18:19-07:00","id":992312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=991690#post991690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is it okay to ask for help designing spells if we have a concept but aren't great on mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, we might even get you different takes on the same effect.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been looking into how to handle using magic for large engineering projects: say, mass-producing objects or creating large, complex objects, like turning a huge pile of scrap into a supersonic VTOL. </div> </div> </div>The first example seems like a recurring Matter Making spell (but I think something nifty can be done with Spirit instead), while the second one seems Patterning of Matter. I'll write something when I get off work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:13:58-07:00","id":992489,"title":"","content":"How about if I wanted a personal pocket dimension I could carry around with me and pull things out of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:17:24-07:00","id":992490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=992489#post992489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about if I wanted a personal pocket dimension I could carry around with me and pull things out of?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in luck: Pocket Dimension already exists as a spell. Page 178.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:26:56-07:00","id":993424,"title":"","content":"I swear this must already exist somewhere but I can't find it. How can Death magic be used to suppress or destroy an Anchor?<br /> <br /> Create Anchor is a Death Making spell, but suppressing a ghost's ability to harvest Essence from an Anchor shouldn't need Unmaking, right? Could you use Shielding (Death 2), similar to Cap the Well? Or perhaps some kind of Fraying spell to weaken or limit their connection to an Anchor?<br /> <br /> Just wondering what other approach would work for a mage who wants to exorcise a ghost. How do people usually go about doing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:29:36-07:00","id":993466,"title":"","content":"Either you resolve the anchor, like in clasic ghost story or if you want to force the issue with magic either Fraying or Unraveling could work. That highly depends on what the anchor is, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:37:39-07:00","id":993538,"title":"","content":"The last time I played a Moros, the ST and I got a short but fun side-story out of an extended Investigation action over several days to learn what was anchoring a ghost and resolve it &quot;naturally.&quot; It was cool, the character only had Death 1 so most of the magic options weren't on the table, and we ended up resolving it by improvising a Death/Forces spell to let the ghost send a final text message via an automatic writing trance.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do things magically, Death 4 &quot;Exorcism&quot; can force a ghost to unManifest or stop possessing someone or what have you. What you're probably looking for is a Death 3 Fraying spell equivalent to Spirit 3 &quot;Erode Resonance,&quot; which removes the Open or Resonant condition as a Lasting effect. I tend to assume that most Spirit spells have a Death or Mind equivalent, even if that steps on Spirit's toes a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:44:47-07:00","id":993546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=993466#post993466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either you resolve the anchor, like in classic ghost story or if you want to force the issue with magic either Fraying or Unraveling could work. That highly depends on what the anchor is, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could probably be a little more straightforward than that, depending on the approach. Here's an example of what I might suggest, inspired very heavily by Cap the Well (Spirit 2). Does this seem appropriate?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Buried Anchor (Death \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Occult, Survival, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> When ghosts are formed, they develop intimate connections with people, places, or objects that held personal significance to them in their life. These Anchors protect ghosts from Essence bleed and provide sustenance. This spell wards one potential source of Essence, preventing the ghost from obtaining Essence from a specified Anchor for the duration of this spell unless they succeed on a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=993538#post993538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last time I played a Moros, the ST and I got a short but fun side-story out of an extended Investigation action over several days to learn what was anchoring a ghost and resolve it &quot;naturally.&quot; It was cool, the character only had Death 1 so most of the magic options weren't on the table, and we ended up resolving it by improvising a Death/Forces spell to let the ghost send a final text message via an automatic writing trance.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do things magically, Death 4 &quot;Exorcism&quot; can force a ghost to unManifest or stop possessing someone or what have you. What you're probably looking for is a Death 3 Fraying spell equivalent to Spirit 3 &quot;Erode Resonance,&quot; which removes the Open or Resonant condition as a Lasting effect. I tend to assume that most Spirit spells have a Death or Mind equivalent, even if that steps on Spirit's toes a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks for clarifying. I like those approaches, both the magical and non-magical. Forgot that Exorcism was already in here, but I think the Death 3 Fraying spell idea and exctended Investigation action are both really neat ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:07:16-07:00","id":993552,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a homebrew Legacy that uses this spell as a major Attainment, I'd love to get some feedback on it in spell form. It's inspired by Shadow Flesh, as well as the Dataform demonic form ability from Descent.<br /> <br /> <b>Inhabit Name (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Investigation, Computer<br /> <br /> The mage transforms the subject's body and all her personal possessions into an embodiment of her Sympathetic Name. The subject has no physical presence, even in Twilight. Instead she exists as a sentient form of her sympathetic connections. The subject's awareness is centered on one location or person at a time which she has a Strong or Connected sympathetic connection to, and can cast spells and use Mage Sight at that location as if viewing it through Scrying. The subject can reflexively move her awareness to a different sympathetic connection once per turn. When the spell ends, the subject physically reappears at the location she is currently viewing.<br /> <br /> The subject retains all her Attributes and Skills, but may not take any Physical actions, including oblations or using yantras that require touch or speech. She is immune to attacks or damage, but not magic that can perceive her, while inhabiting her Sympathetic Name. She can be targeted sympathetically as normal. She can also be targeted at her current location at sensory range using Space Sight or similar powers which detect spatial rifts.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The benefits of the spell extend to the subject's Medium sympathetic connections.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The subject has a Withstand rating for all spells as if she were the sympathetic connection (Strong, Medium, etc) she is currently inhabiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:31:22-07:00","id":993568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=993552#post993552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Inhabit Name (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the concept, but it's incredibly unbalanced. You already know Web-Weaver by that time so you can basically use this spell to get rid of the Mana cost of the sympathetic range attainment since all spells that would've been cast sympathetically now is cast remotely. And on top of that you can practically grant mages without Space a limited form of the sympathetic range attainment that they also don't need to pay Mana for.<br /> <br /> Just simply casting a spell sympathetically requires a Mana. This spell allows you to transfer your consciousness <b>through </b>your sympathetic connections without costing a Mana. That in itself makes it broken. And just adding a flat Mana cost to the casting doesn't help much since you can teleport virtually an unlimited amount of times for one Mana, and has Scrying active for free on all sympathetic connections you can manage to up to Connected or Strong (or Medium with that Reach) for the same Mana.<br /> <br /> Edit: And adding a Mana for every action taken with this spell removes most of the advantage with this spell. Except for the Scrying that you can't simply add a Mana cost to since it's automatic on all the relevant connections.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to make it somewhat balanced is limit the amount of connections you can use by Potency. And add a cost of one Mana per connection. Then use the same Reaches that Correspondence has to choose which connections are used in the spell. If no Reaches used it'll default to the strongest connections.<br /> I also think Withstand should be the sympathetic range Withstand for the weakest sympathetic connection the spell targets, as well as Resolve or Composure instead of Stamina for unwilling subjects. (Multiple Withstand ratings automatically uses the highest Withstand + 1.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-26-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:30:59-07:00","id":993705,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> :removed mana cost is unlikely to be of much benefit because of increased Reach cost for Remote casting. <br /> <br /> Scale would determine the number of possible Sympathetic connections that could be targeted. <br /> <br /> Technically, you're not teleporting you're co-locating until the spell ends at which point you pick a place you end at. To balance that I'd make flipping between connections cost a mana much in the same way that co-location already works.<br /> <br /> Withstand should be treated as normal, Potency over Withstand determines if a connection is actually established or not.<br /> <br /> Used to it's most impressive level possible is going to cost a butt load in dice penalties or Reach. Establishing it against one target still isn't better than simply Scrying or Sympathetic casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-26-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T21:29:12-07:00","id":993879,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thanks for the advice! I overlooked a lot of the basic spell rules when I was running on pure inspiration. The main point of the spell is to make the subject (usually the caster) untouchable, not to inherently recreate Scrying or Co-Location, so I hadn't really considered those implications. Here's a revised version that hews closer to my intent.<br /> <br /> <b>Inhabit Name (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Computer<br /> <br /> The mage transforms the subject's body and all her personal possessions into an embodiment of her Sympathetic Name. The subject has no physical presence, even in Twilight- she is actually not anywhere in particular. She exists only within her Name, and can only interact with the world by means of spells like Scrying. This is an incredibly disturbing experience for subjects who cannot use remote spellcasting, akin to absolute sensory deprivation. Prolonged exposure to this spell (more than an hour per dot of the subject\u2019s Composure) may provoke breaking points or adverse Conditions like Shaken or Spooked. This spell cannot be used on subjects that, for whatever reason, lack a Sympathetic Name. If the subject loses her Sympathetic Name while the spell is active, the spell's Duration ends immediately.<br /> <br /> The subject retains all her Attributes and Skills, but may not take any Physical actions, including oblations or using yantras that require touch or speech, though she can still cast spells. This usually means that without some means of remote viewing, she may only cast spells on herself, through her Familiar or a soul stone, or on a subject whose Sympathetic Name she concentrates on for one turn. She is immune to attacks or damage, but not supernatural powers that can perceive her, while inhabiting her Sympathetic Name. She can be targeted sympathetically as normal. Mages who wish to remain in their Name for an extended time often use spells like Possession to act in the physical world. When the spell's Duration ends, she returns at the point she disappeared from.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>By using the Sympathetic Range Attainment tied to a destination, the spell brings the subject back at that destination rather than at the point she left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T01:54:40-07:00","id":993939,"title":"","content":"This seems more like a torture spell you'd put on someone else to imprison and isolate them. For protected existence outside of normal space a Mage would use Pocket Dimension which has all the same &quot;benefits&quot; and still allows physical actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:41:09-07:00","id":994163,"title":"","content":"How would you do Flesh to Stone?<br /> <br /> Turning a living being into a stone statue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:26:28-07:00","id":994181,"title":"","content":"Life and Matter 4. It's a pretty straightforward Patterning spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:34:59-07:00","id":994187,"title":"","content":"Withstood by Stamina, I imagine?<br /> <br /> If spell is made Indefinite, does age as a statue correspond to 'life' age? If someone was petrified a hundred years ago, and you undid it, would they be their age plus a hundred? Or just their age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T13:39:40-07:00","id":994192,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> I would rule time as a statue doesn't count, so you will be just your age previous to the transmutation once the spell wears off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:04:01-07:00","id":994256,"title":"","content":"I think that makes the most sense. None of your biological processes are active while you're not biological, so your biological age should pause. Spells and effects that reveal age without looking at one's biological makeup would still show age including time spent as a statue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T01:38:46-07:00","id":995999,"title":"","content":"Flesh to Stone should be Withstood by Dexterity. Stamina is altogether too aligned to stone.<br /> <br /> I was playing around with this trying to hammer it into something worthy:<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightened Will:</b><br /> <b>Mind 3 (Perfecting)</b><br /> <br /> The mage calls on the Supernal Ideal of Will to empower their own. This transforms their personality to perfect and reinforce their will. The subject's Vice is transformed into a thing that merely reinforces success rather than something self-destructive.<br /> <br /> While this spell is in effect, the subject's Vice is replaced with &quot;Succeeding on invested actions&quot; which counts as their Vice for the duration. This means the first significant success towards an Aspiration or Obsession in a scene restores a point of willpower. Of course, these are not the only investments a mind makes; any roll on which the character spends Willpower counts, as well. <br /> <br /> Though potentially attractive, this is actually a side effect of the enhanced will.<br /> <br /> The effect empowers the mage's will, improving the benefit from spending willpower on actions. The benefits are the same as normal, with such rolls gaining the 8-Again quality. If the 10-Again quality is somehow currently revoked, this restores it and applies 9-Again instead of 8-Again.<br /> <br /> Any effect that prevents the expenditure of willpower provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Reach 2:</b><br /> The Enlightened Will simply overcomes any mundane mental or social challenges. When invested in the outcome of such a challenge, the effect provides *net* Successes equal to Potency. This, of course, triggers a Clash of Wills when contesting another bearing this effect or when opposed by supernatural effects. For example, if a mage bearing Enlightened Will attempts to persaude a crowd and another attempts to sway them in opposition, a Mental Shield applies on those being persuaded but not on the contesting person unless they also count as part of the crowd.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional Prime 2: </b>Spellcasting and Clash of Will rolls always count as invested, regardless of willpower investment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Reach 2: Reqs. Prime 3:</b> For a mana, the benefit from spending willpower can be improved, conditionally. When spent on a spellcasting roll, it improves by Prime. When spent during a Clash of Wills, it improves by Mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T02:46:18-07:00","id":996008,"title":"","content":"Dexterity can't be used as a Withstand rating. When it's an attribute Withstand is always a Resistance attribute. And as the change is physical it should be the physical attribute. It doesn't matter if Stamina is alligned with stone. Stamina is the attribute for resisting physical change forced upon you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:36:18-07:00","id":996236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=995999#post995999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Enlightened Will:</b><br /> <b>Mind 3 (Perfecting)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a perfectly good idea for a Mind spell, but IMO it's not really in line with the dot levels of written spells. Rewriting someone's Vice is done at Mind 4 Patterning with Psychic Reprogramming. From the creative thaumaturgy rules, a 2-dot Ruling spell can grant 9-again on a certain type of action (such as ones you spend Willpower on), or 8-again with a Reach. At 3 dots, Perfecting can grant rote action for 1 Mana. Provoking a Clash of Wills is good as it is.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect that gives auto-successes is a little confusing. If your intent is to automatically succeed on actions you spend Willpower on, I'd suggest spending 1 Mana for each action in line with &quot;Mana Costs&quot; on page 125, or maybe spending 1 Mana to cast the spell and have it work on a number of actions equal to Potency, and provoke a Clash of Wills as usual. Or, if you want to add net successes as in a contested action, maybe the spell instead adds Potency to your effective successes if you succeed at all? Mechanically the same thing as weapon damage.<br /> <br /> I would if anything suggest changing the Prime 2 requisite to &quot;this spell does not normally apply to spellcasting or a clash of wills, but for +2 Reach it affects them if willpower is spent on the action.&quot; I'd be wary of letting mages directly affect their own Clash of Wills rolls with magic though, since that's an abstract representation of raw magical ability above and beyond spellcasting itelf.<br /> <br /> Something like this:<br /> <br /> Honed Will (Mind \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> The mage grants the subject the 9-again quality on mundane dice rolls where the subject spends Willpower, up to a number of rolls equal to Potency during the spell's Duration.<br /> +1 Reach: The benefit becomes 8-again.<br /> +2 Reach: The benefit extends to spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Enlightened Will (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <br /> The mage grants the subject an additional Vice, as the Vice-Ridden Merit: &quot;Succeeding on invested actions.&quot;<br /> +1 Reach: For a point of Mana, mundane actions where the subject spends Willpower have the rote quality.<br /> +2 Reach: For a point of Mana, the subject automatically succeeds on uncontested mundane actions where they spend Willpower. On contested mundane actions, they add effective successes equal to Potency if they rolled at least one success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:48:09-07:00","id":996277,"title":"","content":"Interesting take. Thanks for the feedback, Cal; I'll roll it around my head a bit. Your language is certainly cleaner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:28:44-07:00","id":996899,"title":"","content":"What Arcana and Practice would identity theft fall under? I assume Space or Prime depending on how you do it, and Weaving or Patterning depending on the extent of the theft?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:08:49-07:00","id":996913,"title":"","content":"It depends wildly upon what you mean by identity theft. Mind allows you to trick people into thinking you're someone else. Space is useful for locating and stealing identity documents. Matter can forge identity documents. If you mean something more mystical Borrow Threads (Space 2, Ruling) allows you to temporarily take the sympathetic connections of another person. Prime Veiling should probably allow someone to temporarily change what their pattern looks like, possibly replicating a target's pattern.<br /> <br /> Edit: Prime Veiling should also be able to do the same with signature nimbuses, which is basically the ID of a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-01-2016, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:43:38-07:00","id":996982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=996913#post996913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends wildly upon what you mean by identity theft. Mind allows you to trick people into thinking you're someone else. Space is useful for locating and stealing identity documents. Matter can forge identity documents. If you mean something more mystical Borrow Threads (Space 2, Ruling) allows you to temporarily take the sympathetic connections of another person. Prime Veiling should probably allow someone to temporarily change what their pattern looks like, possibly replicating a target's pattern.<br /> <br /> Edit: Prime Veiling should also be able to do the same with signature nimbuses, which is basically the ID of a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Life Weaving can make you physically and biologically become another person, right down to expressing their fingerprints and DNA profile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:57:49-07:00","id":996988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=996913#post996913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Prime Veiling should also be able to do the same with signature nimbuses, which is basically the ID of a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure. Hiding your signature nimbus maybe, but altering it entirely is a benefit granted by the Masque merit, which makes me think it might not be intended to be easily replicated with a 2-dot spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:02:02-07:00","id":997073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=996988#post996988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not so sure. Hiding your signature nimbus maybe, but altering it entirely is a benefit granted by the Masque merit, which makes me think it might not be intended to be easily replicated with a 2-dot spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure that Fast Spells merit can be replicated with a 1 dot spell. And Masque merit only have changing signature nimbus as one of its effect. Prime won't allow for changing Vice, Aspiration, Skill Specialties or grant merit dots but those are effects that also can be achieved with spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T04:36:11-07:00","id":997080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=996988#post996988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not so sure. Hiding your signature nimbus maybe, but altering it entirely is a benefit granted by the Masque merit, which makes me think it might not be intended to be easily replicated with a 2-dot spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of that, but it only replicates one dot in a four dot merit. Other spells can actually grant merits (though at higher spell dot ratings if you don't simply increase the rating of a merit you already have).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:21:49-07:00","id":997102,"title":"","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996525-time-again\">this thread </a>and refined by kind answers to my post up above;<br /> <br /> <b>Stolen Face (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>WIthstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Subterfuge, Stealth, Occult<br /> The mage steals someone's place in the world by stealing his social connections to the world. For the spell's Duration, the mage's sympathetic connections become identical to that of the spell's subject, while her own ones are concealed and suppressed. Additionally, everyone who interacts with the mage find themselves placing her in the same emotional context as the subject. While people do realize that the mage and the subject are indeed differrent persons, they can't help but feel the same way towards both of them. If the Scale factor is increased, the mage can steal the social identities of multiple people. Connected sympathies cannot be stolen by this spell, and magically strengthened sympathies trigger a Clash of Wills. Supernatural methods of discerning true identities or observing sympathetic connections also trigger a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject's sympathetic connections are concealed and suppressed for the spell's Duration.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage can now 'benefit' another person, as long as that person is also included in the spell's Targets.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage can copy even Connected sympathies she is aware of by spending one point of Mana per each.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The mage's physical appearance is also transformed to become identitcal to the subject's.This includes any biological identifiers, such as blood type, fingerprints, genes, the corneas and such.<br /> <b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022</b>: While interacting with the mage, people 'remember' hazy memories that justify why they would feel what they feel now. These fake memories dissipate shortly after the mage, leaving only dream-like recollections that are forgotten later.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022</b>: If the spell's subject is another mage, the spell also copies his Nimbus.<br /> <b>Add Time \u2022\u2022</b>: The mage steals the past identity of the subject. While this is usually limited to the subject's Unchanged past, the Temporal Sympathy Attainment allows access to further pasts.<br /> <br /> Looking back, I may have went overboard with this. Oh well, it just gives more reason to fear Adepts and Masters of Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:29:27-08:00","id":1002898,"title":"","content":"Hello folks, I'm new to the game/forum. I've got a creative thaumaturgy question. Is it possible to make a spell that has a heal over time component e.g. heals over multiple turns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:40:39-08:00","id":1002903,"title":"","content":"Not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:54:25-08:00","id":1002911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1002903#post1002903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bummer. Thank you for the reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:21:35-08:00","id":1002922,"title":"","content":"Body Control (Life \u2022\u2022) halves the natural healing time per Potency during the spell's Duration. Bashing heals every 15 minutes, which is equal to 300 turns. At Potency 8 the spell would heal 1 Bashing every turn. Each Potency above would double the amount of Bashing healed each turn. Two Reach and Potency 15 would start healing one Lethal (and over 100 Bashing) per turn.<br /> The amount of Potency required to heal one point per turn is really not manageable for most Mages. Especially not Lethal damage. I crunched some numbers quickly and I don't think a Mage can get above 18 Potency on this spell (at Gnosis 10 and then only having a single die left for the casting) without teamwork or preparation spells that grants bonus dice on casting rolls.<br /> <br /> Your best bet is convincing your ST to allow a Reach on Knit or Mend that spreads out Potency over a number of turns (until all Potency is spent), but that effect requires the Fate 2 attainment to deactivate a combi-cast Dispellation (to suppress the effect of the spell until wanted) when damaged instead of immediately starting to heal the subject (assuming you want it as a preparation spell).<br /> <br /> So, technically yes, but not in a way that is particularly useful.<br /> <br /> Edit: I forgot about Primary Factors. 20 is the highest Potency I calculated, but I doubt anyone under Gnosis 6 will realistically be able to heal Lethal each turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-14-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T09:48:58-08:00","id":1002932,"title":"","content":"I have to say that as an ST, I can't think of a persuasive reason not to let a mage spend a Reach to divide the Potency of a healing spell over several turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:00:23-08:00","id":1003087,"title":"","content":"Or you can cast Hung Spell of an indefinite duration with Conditional Duration, setting it to release its spell whenever you get hurt. Then Hang a healing spell cast at Advanced Duration. Because healing spells like Knit and Mend have instantaneous effects, they'll repeat themselves in an interval equal to the mage's ritual casting time derived from Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T20:05:47-08:00","id":1005949,"title":"","content":"Added something I posted on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1002551-mind-vs-ghosts-and-spirits/page3\">here</a>:<br /> <br /> <b>Disperse Wounds (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Medicine, Survival, Empathy<br /> The necromancer calls forth entropy, but he may unwind it for those he favors. For each level of Potency, the mage may convert one point of lethal damage the subject suffers into two points of bashing damage. This spell does not work against lethal damage upgraded from accumulated bashing damage, including accumulation from this very spell. So, if a subject with 8 levels of Health had suffered 4 lethal damage, this spell may convert them into 1 lethal damage and 6 bashing damage at Potency 3, or 8 bashing damage at Potency 4. If that same subject had suffered 5 lethal damage instead, even at Potency 5 this spell would still leave him at 2 lethal damage and 6 bashing damage.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell instead converts one point of lethal damage into one point of bashing damage per level of Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: For one point of Mana, the spell instead converts one point of aggravated damage into two points of lethal damage instead. The limit concerning damage accumulation applies as normal.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022</b>: The spell also heals any Tilts connected to the Health box affected, even if the box is technically uncleared and thus the Tilt should remain.<br /> <b>Add Time \u2022\u2022</b>: The spell may also heal scars and physical Conditions related to the healed wounds. With the Temporal Sympathy Attainment, the spell may force persistent Conditions caused from past injuries into transient Conditions, so that they naturally heal over time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:10:41-08:00","id":1006294,"title":"","content":"Great spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>! Here is my silly take on some weird cross arcana effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Chicken Time (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Stamina<br /> The caster changes time experienced by the target into a chicken. As you can't really inhabit the CHICKEN* the target is helplessly pushed into the future just like with Temporal Stutter but instead of not remembering anything he remembers the CHICKEN*. Target gets Broken condition for what he experienced.<br /> <br /> *ROASTED","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-22-2016, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:27:05-08:00","id":1006494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1006294#post1006294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great spell <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>! Here is my silly take on some weird cross arcana effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Chicken Time (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Stamina<br /> The caster changes time experienced by the target into a chicken. As you can't really inhabit the CHICKEN the target is helplessly pushed into the future just like with Temporal Stutter but instead of not remembering anything he remembers the CHICKEN. Target gets Broken condition for what he experienced.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now Mage becomes a surreal horror game!<br /> <br /> Although, shouldn't it use Life and not Matter? And Duration seems better as the primary factor - lengthening the period time converted into a chicken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T00:55:59-08:00","id":1006625,"title":"","content":"I lost in a translation that it should be a Chicken Nuggets <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but basically yea. I always knew that you can do weird things with arcana but never came with something really weird. So I tried. And I'm sure there is more of it.<br /> Temporal Stutter has potency as primary so I took it from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T09:00:54-08:00","id":1006739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1002911#post1002911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bummer. Thank you for the reply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> <b>Kali's Caress (Life <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Cost: 1 Mana</b><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Medicine, Occult, Animal Ken<br /> <br /> With a gesture the mage grants the target the innate capacity to recover from wounds.<br /> The spell applies the Recovering tilt to the target<br /> <br /> <b>Spend 1 additional Mana and +2 Reach</b>: The spell applies the Regenerating tilt instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Recovering</b><br /> Your character's pain diminishes on its own at remarkable rates. Cuts close, and bruises vanish in moments.<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Every turn your character heals one bashing damage<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt</b>: This tilt is caused by spells or other supernatural effects<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt</b>: You heal all bashing damage<br /> <br /> <b>Regenerating</b><br /> Even significant wounds close rapidly and bones click into place and mend at miraculous speeds.<br /> <b>Effect</b>: Every turn your character downgrades one point of lethal damage to bashing. If you have no lethal damage, you heal one bashing damage<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt</b>: This Tilt is caused by spells or other supernatural effects<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt</b>: You all lethal and bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Go figure, Kali's domain is regeneration too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I wasn't sure whether to make those things Tilts or Conditions. So thar we go, healing over time. Figured if you can set someone on fire for damage over time, why not some healing over time too.<br /> <br /> Ending the tilts by being fully healed (to the extent they can heal) should neatly sidestep the &quot;I cast regeneration with duration of 1 year&quot; potential problem I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:22:03-08:00","id":1008032,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Atlas</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Prime \u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Rulling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes a willworker needs to go all out to accomplish his task or merelly survive. Atlas carries the spells for him in this hard times.<br /> Treat higher of Gnosis and Potency as the spell control slots. Target can use this only for his spells that Imagos were specifically build for Atlas - pay one mana to create a vessel for every spell beyond your unmodified spell control.<br /> <br /> I need some feedback. Is this too much for a Rulling?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:37:53-08:00","id":1008038,"title":"","content":"What is the subject of Atlas? Do you cast it on yourself to gain additional spell slots? Is it something or someone else who holds the spells for you like Sleepwalkers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:46:49-08:00","id":1008040,"title":"","content":"I didn't make that clear... Subject must be a mage and he is also a recipient of benefits.<br /> <br /> Edit: there's some place for Reach to affect sleepwalkers or even making amulets that when used as Yantra allow for this kind of effects","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:31:14-08:00","id":1008051,"title":"","content":"I think you might want to look at the Sanctum Merit for how to make it work. And Perfecting seems like a more fitting Practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:56:16-08:00","id":1008062,"title":"","content":"I've ported mechanics from Hung Spell which is Rulling but I was thinking about making it a Perfecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:57:52-08:00","id":1008065,"title":"","content":"I think the language needs to be cleared up, I'm still not exactly sure what this spell is doing. Is it increasing spell control slots, or bundling maintained spells into one slot or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T14:36:15-08:00","id":1009484,"title":"","content":"True Action<br /> Prime \u00b0\u00b0<br /> Practice of Ruling<br /> Primary Factor : Duration<br /> Cost: 1 Mana<br /> <br /> Effect: The Mage choose an action that want enchanted. The next round, this action will be inspired by the Supernal Archetype of itself. The pool dice gain the 8 again. Mundane action only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T15:07:51-08:00","id":1009501,"title":"","content":"In your text the action would have to be made the next turn. There's no purpose of having Duration as the Primary Factor since the spell resolves in the smallest Duration possible.<br /> I can recommend looking at the guidelines for creative thaumaturgy in the book. There's a small section about modifying dice pools that you could use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-28-2016, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T23:32:17-08:00","id":1009651,"title":"","content":"Potency had no use : with duration, the next action can be...next action that require a dice pool, over round etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:01:57-08:00","id":1009659,"title":"","content":"Generally such a spell affects a number of actions equal to Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T00:28:28-08:00","id":1009663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1009659#post1009659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally such a spell affects a number of actions equal to Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are examples of both in the books, actually. I wish that many of the spells in the books that only provide a bonus to the next action actually provided it for a number = Potency, but many don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:27:44-08:00","id":1009683,"title":"","content":"Actually, most spells that grant 9-Again or 8-Again are either one dot higher or grants the bonus to a tool instead of to actions. I point towards the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines (p126) and Boons from Fate spells that grant 9-Again (8-Again with a Reach) on a number of rolls equal to Potency with the Ruling practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T01:34:50-08:00","id":1009685,"title":"","content":"My issue is that: Prime have a many spell of variable effect. Enchant an item so that it can strike all type of ephemeral, create object from mana or &quot;thing&quot; as with Eidolon, etc.<br /> I fear that give &quot;more&quot; leeway to copy the best bless of Fate is too unbalanced for game economy. Too usefull Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T02:03:43-08:00","id":1009693,"title":"","content":"I have a rule (house rule obviously) that you need to have a target. Fate can target your destiny, Time can target your next action, but Prime? It can't target anything you will do in the future and because of that it needs to target tools. Shoes for running or boxing gloves for hitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:16:30-08:00","id":1009702,"title":"","content":"The Target is a Supernal Symbol , that bestow its power for manifest a &quot;mundane, pale, shadow&quot; of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:34:36-08:00","id":1009708,"title":"","content":"That is a good explanation. But why the mana cost and no reach options?<br /> <br /> From Core p.125<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depending on the intent of the spell, this<br /> might be obvious, or there might be several ways you could<br /> go about accomplishing your intent. Don\u2019t worry about<br /> whether the effect seems \u201ctoo powerful\u201d for its dot level or<br /> \u201cunbalanced\u201d compared to a similar effect under a different<br /> Arcanum; part of the fun of playing Mage is coming up with<br /> clever, unexpectedly-useful applications of magic. </div> </div> </div><b>True Action</b><br /> <b>Prime \u00b0\u00b0</b><br /> <b>Practice</b> of Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor </b>: Duration<br /> The Mage chooses an action that want Enchanted. Number of this actions equal to Potency will be inspired by the Supernal Archetype of itself. The dice pool gains the 9 again. Mundane action only.<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach:</b> Make it 8 again<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach: </b>The action can be magical in nature<br /> <b>+ 2 Reach:</b> Mage can choose when the dice trick applies and use this Enchantment for important deeds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T03:45:22-08:00","id":1009710,"title":"","content":"I'd have it cost two Reach to affect spell casting rolls, like Exceptiona Luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:08:44-08:00","id":1009715,"title":"","content":"The mana cost is present on Exceptional Luck, so as other spell very aboard: Incognito Presence is a veiling two dot spell, but with a mana cost.<br /> But your quote make my day! For spellcasting, there is too a spell: As Above, So Below.<br /> Thanks a lot at all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Remake:<br /> <br /> <b>True Action</b><br /> <b>Prime \u00b0\u00b0</b><br /> <b>Practice</b> of Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor </b>: Duration<br /> <b>Mana Cost : </b>1 Mana<br /> The Mage chooses an action that want Enchanted. Number of this actions equal to Potency will be inspired by the Supernal Archetype of itself. The dice pool gains the 9 again. Mundane action only.<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach:</b> Make it 8 again<br /> <b>+ 1 Reach:</b> Mage can choose when the dice trick applies and use this Enchantment for important deeds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T04:17:28-08:00","id":1009717,"title":"","content":"Cost in Exceptional Luck pertains a reach option that lets you cast it reflexivelly. As Above, As Below talks about spellcasting and yantras - its not the same as &quot;action magical in nature&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:25:23-08:00","id":1009966,"title":"","content":"A spell I created in homage to Molly Carpenter from Harry Dresden: <br /> <br /> Bright Moon(Mind 3)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Subterfuge, Empathy<br /> <br /> The mage weaves the target's mind into a state of unconsciousness, causing them to immediately fall asleep should they fail to resist. All subjects of the spell slowly stop what they're doing and instead begin to prepare themselves for the forced sleep. <br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may control what the sleeping subjects of the spell dream, inflicting temporary Conditions upon waking up.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may choose to instead make the targets fall asleep instantly, not slowly and while stopping their current actions. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T00:27:47-08:00","id":1010964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1009966#post1009966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell I created in homage to Molly Carpenter from Harry Dresden:<br /> <br /> Bright Moon(Mind 3)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Subterfuge, Empathy<br /> <br /> The mage weaves the target's mind into a state of unconsciousness, causing them to immediately fall asleep should they fail to resist. All subjects of the spell slowly stop what they're doing and instead begin to prepare themselves for the forced sleep.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may control what the sleeping subjects of the spell dream, inflicting temporary Conditions upon waking up.<br /> +1 Reach: The Mage may choose to instead make the targets fall asleep instantly, not slowly and while stopping their current actions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Psychic Domination can force someone to sleep at Mind 2. Why is weaving required for this spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:21:50-08:00","id":1011168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1010964#post1010964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Domination can force someone to sleep at Mind 2. Why is weaving required for this spell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Weaving changes something within an Arcanum's purview without transforming the entirety of its being. Weaving them into a state of magical slumber seems plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:59:21-08:00","id":1011175,"title":"","content":"Ruling lets you do everything to the target that is within the scope of its normal capabilities. Sleep is a normal mind function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:12:04-08:00","id":1011419,"title":"","content":"Can you force yourself to sleep right now, at demand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:27:14-08:00","id":1011424,"title":"","content":"Can the water flow uphill?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ruling spells grant fuller control over phenomena than a<br /> mere Compelling spell. Water can be made to flow uphill<br /> or into unnatural shapes (Matter), animals (or even human<br /> beings) can be commanded (Life or Mind), or time can be<br /> momentarily made to accelerate or slow down (Time). A<br /> Ruling spell can\u2019t fundamentally alter its target\u2019s abilities:<br /> Water can be directed, but not turned solid or gaseous.<br /> Time can be altered, but not overwritten. An animal can<br /> be commanded, but not made stronger or fiercer. </div> </div> </div>If you could force yourself to sleep or you are sleepy you would need just a Compelling spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:33:28-08:00","id":1011532,"title":"","content":"Psychic Domination can force a target to fall asleep. So making a spell that puts a target to sleep is Ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:17:53-08:00","id":1011586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1011532#post1011532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psychic Domination can force a target to fall asleep. So making a spell that puts a target to sleep is Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I should specify that this spell puts them in what is essentially, a coma? They can't be roused as easily just normal sleep, until the Duration elapses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:30:44-08:00","id":1011697,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about a lesser form of 'Turn Momentum' I could use until I have the experience dots to invest more into forces. Would a veiling spell be sufficient if the spell doesn't reflect attacks backwards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:45:22-08:00","id":1012113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1011419#post1011419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you force yourself to sleep right now, at demand?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a requirement for Compelling, not Ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:58:13-08:00","id":1012117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1011586#post1011586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I should specify that this spell puts them in what is essentially, a coma? They can't be roused as easily just normal sleep, until the Duration elapses?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would probably be more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:00:15-08:00","id":1012118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1011697#post1011697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about a lesser form of 'Turn Momentum' I could use until I have the experience dots to invest more into forces. Would a veiling spell be sufficient if the spell doesn't reflect attacks backwards?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Veiling works, you could use Shielding to block the momentum of incoming attacks. Think Neo when he stops all the bullets being fired at him in midair and they sit there for a moment before dropping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:15:07-08:00","id":1012390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1012118#post1012118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how Veiling works, you could use Shielding to block the momentum of incoming attacks. Think Neo when he stops all the bullets being fired at him in midair and they sit there for a moment before dropping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah right sorry. I always mixup veiling and shielding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T08:27:12-08:00","id":1018099,"title":"","content":"<b>Beast Master (Mind </b>\u2022\u2022<b>)</b> (working title)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Empathy, Survival<br /> Gain a number of dots in an animal training fighting style (such as Falconry or K-9) equal to Potency for the Duration of this spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Including an animal as a Subject of this spell circumvents the training period required to benefit from the Merit. If the Subjects do not share the Bonded Condition (or another fitting Condition such as Familiar) they both gain the Bonded Condition for the Duration of the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:14:03-08:00","id":1018677,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for Forces spells to manipulate electronics, cybernetics, and the internet in general? Wanted to do a version of the Virtual Adepts with Forces as the third Ruling and Space as optional, but the existing Forces spells are quite lacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T00:01:00-08:00","id":1018717,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Reveal Avernian key </u>(Death 1, knowing)<br /> Primary factor: ?<br /> Effect: Learn an Avernian gate's key.<br /> <br /> I want to put more to this but I'm unsure what further it can have.<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <hr /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> <br /> <u>Open Avernian gate (Death 2 ruling)</u>, Improvised creative thaumaturgy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Primary factor: Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Effect: Through the mastery of death you present a key to one of the many barred gates to the underworld. You apply the gateway condition(pg.260) to a location by forcing a present Avernian Gate to act as though its required key has been presented.<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'm unsure of any reach effects that'd fit this spell.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T04:22:01-08:00","id":1018765,"title":"","content":"Primary factor would be Potency in case it has a Withstand or multiple Keys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T06:45:07-08:00","id":1018790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1018677#post1018677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for Forces spells to manipulate electronics, cybernetics, and the internet in general? Wanted to do a version of the Virtual Adepts with Forces as the third Ruling and Space as optional, but the existing Forces spells are quite lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence electricity, Tune in, Transmission, transform energy. I would maybe suggest making Mind the optional Arcana. You could then project your mind into the internet. There isn't really a virtual realm in Awakening so Space would be limited in its ability to take you there unless you wanted to make that part of your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:04:57-08:00","id":1018809,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you do need Mind, Forces clearly can deliver sensory information to you on its own without Mind, and it can communicate binary to your brain without translation, plus it can manipulate the light, sounds and haptic feedback you're experiencing and you don't need to leave your body to take a trip on the Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:26:03-08:00","id":1018819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1018809#post1018809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you do need Mind, Forces clearly can deliver sensory information to you on its own without Mind, and it can communicate binary to your brain without translation, plus it can manipulate the light, sounds and haptic feedback you're experiencing and you don't need to leave your body to take a trip on the Internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true. I think I only suggested that to play off my experience of the Virtual Adepts. It wouldn't be hard for a Forces mage to interact with the internet at all. Maybe some sort of Verge could be made around the internet and technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:28:01-08:00","id":1019106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1018809#post1018809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you do need Mind, Forces clearly can deliver sensory information to you on its own without Mind, and it can communicate binary to your brain without translation, plus it can manipulate the light, sounds and haptic feedback you're experiencing and you don't need to leave your body to take a trip on the Internet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind might be required for matters like decryption or reading data in foreign languages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T18:12:42-08:00","id":1022159,"title":"","content":"I have been playing Mage the Awakening 2e for about 3 week (played 1e demo twice) and I thought that I would give the spell development a try. i am sure it needs some work but I could use some constructive criticism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Splice Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidate, Medicine, Occult.<br /> This spell can only be cast as a ritual and takes 1 additional casting interval per level of potency (gaining no additional dice from doing so). The mage splices a small sliver of his soul to the soul of a sleeper, creating something very similar to a Soul Stone (pg. 98) with all the benefits and penalties that accompany it, except they cannot be used to create a Demenes, including the fact that this is an Act of Hubris against the Enlightened and Understanding Wisdom. He is a hitchhiker in the others body and is just along for the ride. For the duration of the spell the subject is considered a very loyal sleepwalker. Also as long as they are in the same room all magic cast by the mage with a target of self also affects the sleepwalker at no extra cost. This also creates a strong Sympathetic Connection between the two.<br /> The sleepwalker is unaware they have this hitchhiker and the mage has no particular control over the sleepwalker. However since there is a sliver of awakened soul attached to the sleepwalker magic can be cast around him as with any other person that is aware on the truth. The individual does register as a sleepwalker to the various types of detection and if scrutinizes by Death or Spirit magic the sliver can be detected.<br /> The mage can temporarily transfer the rest of his soul to the sleepwalker, taking control. For 1 point of mana the mage\u2019s soul leaves his body and travels to the sleepwalker, this travel is not instantaneous unless the mage uses Space magic to make it so. His body gains the Thrall condition while he rides along with the host. The sleepwalker registers as fully awakened for as long as the mage\u2019s soul is in control. The mage is fully capable of casting magic as if this was his true body. This transfer lasts for 1 hour or a scene at best then the mage must travel back to his body.<br /> There is a danger in this as the mage\u2019s soul uses the twilight to travel to the host\u2019s body. While in the twilight he is just as susceptible to the hazards therein as any ghost would be, in fact he is the same as any other wandering soul in that realm. The two bodies act as anchors.<br /> Lastly if the mage dies while a sliver of his soul is in the sleepwalker he has a chance to make the journey to reunite the sliver with his soul. Unfortunately for the sleepwalker his soul is consumed in the process and this triggers another Act of Hubris. If the sleepwalker dies the sliver returns to the mage reuniting the two, however the soul of the sleepwalker becomes a very angry rank 2 ghost with the mage as an anchor.<br /> Even when this spell ends there is a lasting effects as the subject can never truly return to his former lie riddled life, the subject is a sleepwalker with a strong tie to the mage but has none of the benefits of this spell unless this spell is cast again.<br /> The Additional Arcana listed below have added benefits and extends the usefulness of this spell and you may incorporate one per potency of the spell. The adders share the casting statistics of the spell when added.<br /> <b> Add Life \u2022\u2022:</b> By adding life to the mix the mags may now use the sleepwalker\u2019s senses. He may enter a trance and pay 1 Mana at any time to take control of the sleepwalker\u2019s body. The mage also strengthens his host body as if the host was under the effects of a Body Control spell. This may be used in conjunction with the Mind adder below.<br /> <b> Add Mind \u2022\u2022:</b> By adding mind he can communicate with the sleepwalker making his thoughts be known. He may enter a trance and pay 1 Mana at any time to take control of the sleepwalker\u2019s mind. The mage also defends his host mind as if the host was under the effects of a Mental Shield spell. This may be used in conjunction with the Life adder above.<br /> <b> Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> By adding Space he can use the sleepwalker as a Sympathetic Connection. Also the mage and sleepwalker no longer have to be in the same room to share spells. This connection forms a conduit by which he can use his magic through.<br /> <b> +1 Reach:</b> The mage may mask his soul from detection by other mages. Any attempt to detect the sliver of the mages soul will cause a Clash of Will.<br /> <b> +1 Reach:</b> The mage may make the duration indefinite at the additional cost of 1 mana and a -10 to the dice pool.<br /> <b> +1 Reach:</b> If the duration is longer than a week the mage may renew this connection at the cost of one Mana each time that he renews the spell. Renewing the spell in this way resets the duration counter extending the spell.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum Leach (Death, Spirit, or Mind \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Science.<br /> The mage names an Arcanum and casts the spell at a target. If the target possesses the named Arcanum the leach will attach to their soul. Once attached it will leach a small amount of arcane energy every time a spell is cast of the type named. This does not hinder the casting in any way and the drain is so slight that the only effect felt by the mage is a slight nausea. Once 10 spells have been siphoned the leach is full and drops off. Detached it sprouts wings and enters twilight flying back to the caster. If the duration of the spell ends before it siphons enough energy then falls to the ground and dissipates. The caster is aware that the leach is dead.<br /> The caster can devour the leach and gain knowledge of the Arcanum siphoned. (In game terms the mage may spend experience in the named Arcanum without a tutor, the spell needs a potency equal to the level of knowledge learned.)<br /> <b> +1 Reach:</b> You can use the stolen energy to turn a turn an untutored legacy attainment into a tutored legacy attainment.<br /> <b> +1 Reach:</b> The leach can be set to siphon of skills in which case it takes 10 days to collect the information desired before returning to the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-25-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T19:29:34-08:00","id":1022170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022159#post1022159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Splice Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is, to be frank, a completely overdesigned mess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This spell can only be cast as a ritual and takes 1 additional casting interval per level of potency (gaining no additional dice from doing so). </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage splices a small sliver of his soul to the soul of a sleeper, creating something very similar to a Soul Stone (pg. 98) with all the benefits and penalties that accompany it, except they cannot be used to create a Demenes, including the fact that this is an Act of Hubris against the Enlightened and Understanding Wisdom. </div> </div> </div>Alright, this seems like a decent simple effect \u2014 &quot;invest your Gnosis in somebody through the same channels as making a soul stone&quot; is workable on its face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He is a hitchhiker in the others body and is just along for the ride. For the duration of the spell the subject is considered a very loyal sleepwalker. </div> </div> </div>Alright, now we've lumped in at least one extra effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also as long as they are in the same room all magic cast by the mage with a target of self also affects the sleepwalker at no extra cost. This also creates a strong Sympathetic Connection between the two. </div> </div> </div>Why is this a consequence of the spell and not a prerequisite for its use?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sleepwalker is unaware they have this hitchhiker and the mage has no particular control over the sleepwalker. However since there is a sliver of awakened soul attached to the sleepwalker magic can be cast around him as with any other person that is aware on the truth. The individual does register as a sleepwalker to the various types of detection and if scrutinizes by Death or Spirit magic the sliver can be detected. </div> </div> </div>Is there any meaningful reason that &quot;the target is a Sleepwalker for the duration&quot; is the outcome rather than &quot;this spell targets a Sleepwalker&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mage can temporarily transfer the rest of his soul to the sleepwalker, taking control. For 1 point of mana the mage\u2019s soul leaves his body and travels to the sleepwalker, this travel is not instantaneous unless the mage uses Space magic to make it so. His body gains the Thrall condition while he rides along with the host. The sleepwalker registers as fully awakened for as long as the mage\u2019s soul is in control. The mage is fully capable of casting magic as if this was his true body. This transfer lasts for 1 hour or a scene at best then the mage must travel back to his body. There is a danger in this as the mage\u2019s soul uses the twilight to travel to the host\u2019s body. While in the twilight he is just as susceptible to the hazards therein as any ghost would be, in fact he is the same as any other wandering soul in that realm. The two bodies act as anchors. </div> </div> </div>This is another effect entirely and also raises the question of what is actually stopping the mage from terminating their spell to return to their own body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly if the mage dies while a sliver of his soul is in the sleepwalker he has a chance to make the journey to reunite the sliver with his soul. Unfortunately for the sleepwalker his soul is consumed in the process and this triggers another Act of Hubris. If the sleepwalker dies the sliver returns to the mage reuniting the two, however the soul of the sleepwalker becomes a very angry rank 2 ghost with the mage as an anchor. </div> </div> </div>Understandable drawback, but this is yet another effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even when this spell ends there is a lasting effects as the subject can never truly return to his former lie riddled life, the subject is a sleepwalker with a strong tie to the mage but has none of the benefits of this spell unless this spell is cast again. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The subject is a Sleepwalker when the spell ends, but with none of the benefits of the spell, the only subject-facing one of which is 'the subject is a Sleepwalker for the duration.'&quot;<br /> <br /> You've made this thing a lower-dot Stealing Fire without any of the associated drawbacks along with tacking on about three more effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Additional Arcana listed below have added benefits and extends the usefulness of this spell and you may incorporate one per potency of the spell. </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> Add Life \u2022\u2022:</b> By adding life to the mix the mags may now use the sleepwalker\u2019s senses. He may enter a trance and pay 1 Mana at any time to take control of the sleepwalker\u2019s body. The mage also strengthens his host body as if the host was under the effects of a Body Control spell. This may be used in conjunction with the Mind adder below. </div> </div> </div>This is both two extra effects and a near-explicit combined spell effect without engaging with the Combined Spell rules \u2014 if it's the only extra Arcanum you've added, your Potency-based stipulation makes it more efficient than just combining Body Control (at what Potency?) with the base spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> Add Mind \u2022\u2022:</b> By adding mind he can communicate with the sleepwalker making his thoughts be known. He may enter a trance and pay 1 Mana at any time to take control of the sleepwalker\u2019s mind. The mage also defends his host mind as if the host was under the effects of a Mental Shield spell. This may be used in conjunction with the Life adder above. </div> </div> </div>As above, this is multiple effects that bypass the drawbacks of combining spells to use multiple effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> By adding Space he can use the sleepwalker as a Sympathetic Connection. Also the mage and sleepwalker no longer have to be in the same room to share spells. This connection forms a conduit by which he can use his magic through. </div> </div> </div>Having a Strong sympathetic connection means the target already has a sympathetic connection to the mage. This addition adds nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> +1 Reach:</b> The mage may mask his soul from detection by other mages. Any attempt to detect the sliver of the mages soul will cause a Clash of Will. </div> </div> </div>This is a separate effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> +1 Reach:</b> The mage may make the duration indefinite at the additional cost of 1 mana and a -10 to the dice pool. </div> </div> </div>This is a Common Reach Effect and does not need to be listed in an individual spell's set of Reach effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b> +1 Reach:</b> If the duration is longer than a week the mage may renew this connection at the cost of one Mana each time that he renews the spell. Renewing the spell in this way resets the duration counter extending the spell. </div> </div> </div>This appears to be referencing a rule that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> My first piece of advice is to split this spell up into the separate effects. By way of example:<br /> <br /> <b>Invest Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult<br /> The mage primes a living target to serve as a vessel of their Gnosis. The target, who must be a Sleepwalker with a Strong connection to a mage included in the Scale factor of this spell, may be made into a soul stone by any mage under the effects of the same spell (the caster does not require extra spell factors to be included).<br /> <br /> For the Duration factor of this spell, a number of mages up to the Potency of this spell may imprint their Signature Nimbus on the target and spend a Willpower dot, ignoring the normal Size 2 limitation for soul stones. While the spell lasts, the subject counts as a soul stone for all purposes and gains a number of dots in the Banner-Bearer Merit equal to the number of mages using them as a soul stone (this may take them above the Merit's normal maximum rating of three dots, though dots above the fifth &quot;fall off&quot; unless the caster spends a point of Mana at the time of casting).<br /> <br /> If the subject is used as the basis for a Demesne, the Demesne persists only as long as they are alive and within the bounds of the location the Demesne was made in (e.g. a Demesne forged from a Sleepwalker acting as a soul stone for three members of a cabal will be disrupted if they leave their church Sanctum).<br /> <br /> While serving as a soul stone for a mage, the target is subject to the Nimbus Tilt of that mage for the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target may be a Sleepwalker with a Medium connection to a mage included in the Scale factor of this spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target is not subject to the Nimbus Tilt of a mage whose soul has been invested in them.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target may treat the number of soul stones they serve as as a Supernatural Tolerance Trait, adding to relevant contested rolls and allowing them to store up to the spell's Potency in Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target and any mage whose soul stone they serve as may share their senses as a reflexive action, much like a mage's familiar.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above, but the target may serve as a relay for two or more mages to share their senses.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The target may remain a soul stone even after their death; as long as the spell's Duration persists, a portion of the dead subject up to Size 2 remains a soul stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-25-2016, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T03:52:01-08:00","id":1022263,"title":"","content":"#1) This is, to be frank, a completely overdesigned mess.<br /> <br /> This is why I posted it for comments and criticism, as I started I am new to this entire way of thinking about mages and magic. If I do not get a grasp of this system then I will not be able to convince my face to face group to try it. So I joined a game on a PBP site to try and learn the rules of this system, this is my next step in attempting to bring the system into focus.<br /> <br /> I have not submitted the two spells posted to the Storyteller on the PBP site because I do not think he is allowing Creative Thaumaturgy, I can see where it would slow the game down even more while they have a discussion about a new spell, stopping the game progression while it is going on.<br /> <br /> So on to answering your question as best as I can. I do appreciate your critiques, but I can tell in your writing style that you are somewhat frustrated with this bumbling mess so I will try to be more concise with my explanations so as to explain my way of thinking as an outsider to this system.<br /> <br /> #2) Why?<br /> <br /> In my mind this isn\u2019t something that you would do out in the open, slicing off a piece of your soul and splicing it to another person shouldn\u2019t be taken lightly and as a whim. I see instantaneous magic as impulsive and somewhat haphazard, and I do not see this spell as either. Therefore I feel that limiting it to being only \u201cBehind closed doors\u201d is just.<br /> <br /> As for the second part of that sentence, I was using the potency to limit the number of adders you could put on the spell because it is making the spell more potent. I see all these spells with adders and there is no associated cost for them. In my way of thinking each adder requires another casting interval. Additional casting intervals usually add dice to the spell, this is just stating that the benefit of the extra time is already being used to cast the additional spells.<br /> <br /> #3) Alright, this seems like a decent simple effect \u2014 &quot;invest your Gnosis in somebody through the same channels as making a soul stone&quot; is workable on its face.<br /> <br /> Ok, not much to comment on here.<br /> <br /> #4) Alright, now we've lumped in at least one extra effect.<br /> <br /> In my thinking this is a surreptitious and lasting way of turning a sleeper into a sleepwalker. The soul of an awakened being has been attached to the soul, no spliced to the soul, of a sleeper fundamentally changing the sleeper\u2019s soul, the core and center of who he is. Once again why it shouldn\u2019t be done on the fly. As for the loyal to you part well your soul attached to his soul should make him loyal.<br /> <br /> #5) Why is this a consequence of the spell and not a prerequisite for its use?<br /> <br /> May be it should have been worded a different way. The basic gist behind the statement is that with both pieces of the mages soul in close proximity to each other they receive the benefits of the spell cast by the mage. The sympathetic connection is there to be capitalized upon if you have Space. As for being a consequence of the spell and not a prerequisite, it is because of the spell that allows you to share this without paying for extra scale.<br /> <br /> #6) Is there any meaningful reason that &quot;the target is a Sleepwalker for the duration&quot; is the outcome rather than &quot;this spell targets a Sleepwalker&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because like Stealing Fire it is targeting a sleeper, but unlike Stealing Fire it is targeting a specific sleeper to transform him into a sleepwalker with the predilection for following you. This allows you to handpick a sleeper to groom as a sleepwalker instead of letting random events determine who is and isn\u2019t a sleepwalker. So even if this spell wasn\u2019t already an Act of Hubris, changing the fundamental beliefs of a sleeper would be.<br /> <br /> #7) This is another effect entirely and also raises the question of what is actually stopping the mage from terminating their spell to return to their own body.<br /> <br /> There is nothing that stops a mage from terminating the spell and returning to his own body. It is still not an instantaneous trip. Yes I know that a soul returning to his body after it left his body is supposed to be instantaneous. This spell makes it different, once again a limiting factor and adds a hint of danger. The mages body will remain in a thrall condition until the soul returns, so there is danger to both the soul and the body. Benefit: being able to take control of another, Price: danger to your soul and body. Every benefit should have a price, now if you are saying that the price isn\u2019t high enough then I am open to suggesting as to how to increase the price.<br /> <br /> #8) Understandable drawback, but this is yet another effect.<br /> <br /> This is just to state that if the mage dies he does not move on instead his soul seeks out the piece of his soul that is still in a living body. The travel through the twilight to get to his remaining soul is fraught with perils but he has a chance to live again if he makes it to the other piece of his soul, of course the destruction of the soul already inhabiting that body is an Act of Hubris. If the sleepwalker dies his ghost follows the sliver of soul back to the mage and haunts him for as long as he lives. The mage is his anchor. He is pissed and he is powerful once again a cost for messing with someone\u2019s soul. If I was the ST and this happened I would also find a way to make the ghost super resistant to the powers of the mage. But the ghost wouldn\u2019t kill the mage because then he would move on and his revenge wouldn\u2019t be complete.<br /> <br /> #9) &quot;The subject is a Sleepwalker when the spell ends, but with none of the benefits of the spell, the only subject-facing one of which is 'the subject is a Sleepwalker for the duration.'&quot;<br /> <br /> Poorly worded, all it is stating is that he is a sleepwalker with no connection between him and the mage. This is a way for the mage to say that this guy isn\u2019t who he thought he was so he will drop him. But just because he was dropped doesn\u2019t mean that he would return to the sleeping world as his soul has been changed.<br /> <br /> #10) You've made this thing a lower-dot Stealing Fire without any of the associated drawbacks along with tacking on about three more effects.<br /> <br /> First it is the same cost as Stealing Fire, three dots. Second it isn\u2019t meant to do the same thing as Stealing Fire it has a different purpose. And as it states in the side bar \u201cMany Roads\u201d on page 124 spells with the same effect can cost different prices depending on how they are used and or implemented. It has its own drawbacks, for one a continuous strong sympathetic connection between the two making the mage very vulnerable to anyone with Space magic, which I am finding out should be everyone and my character in the PBP game doesn\u2019t have but that is an entirely different can of worms.<br /> <br /> #11) Why?<br /> <br /> I explained my thought pattern in the above explanation as to the making it a ritual only spell.<br /> <br /> #12) This is both two extra effects and a near-explicit combined spell effect without engaging with the Combined Spell rules \u2014 if it's the only extra Arcanum you've added, your Potency-based stipulation makes it more efficient than just combining Body Control (at what Potency?) with the base spell.<br /> <br /> Maybe I wasn\u2019t clear about this. The body control happens when the mage takes control of the others body. As to the casting of a combined spell, I don\u2019t see it that way. He took the extra time to add this spell, and the spell has its own spell parameters, the effect doesn\u2019t even have a benefit until the mage takes control. This is a predetermined effect that happens since the mage has not capability of casting a spell once he takes control of the body. Remember he is back at the office in a trance and defenseless he is unable to cast other magic unless his soul travels to the sleepwalker and fully takes control.<br /> <br /> #13) As above, this is multiple effects that bypass the drawbacks of combining spells to use multiple effects.<br /> <br /> Same as above.<br /> <br /> #14) Having a Strong sympathetic connection means the target already has a sympathetic connection to the mage. This addition adds nothing.<br /> <br /> Ah but it does have an effect the connection is from soul to soul not a portal that opens that allows bi-directional viewing. But maybe it isn\u2019t needed.<br /> <br /> #15) This is a separate effect.<br /> <br /> And that is why it is a reach, reaches add effects and abilities making the spell harder to cast.<br /> <br /> #16) This is a Common Reach Effect and does not need to be listed in an individual spell's set of Reach effects.<br /> <br /> Ok \u2013 Then it can be removed.<br /> <br /> #17) This appears to be referencing a rule that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> I was treating this similar to the +1 reach effect in Crucible (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022) where they can \u201cRecharge\u201d the effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the spell that you presented, I like it and it is cool but it isn\u2019t the intent of the spell that I was aiming for. It sounds amazing for a cabal to share a sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-26-2016, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T04:12:45-08:00","id":1022270,"title":"","content":"Please excuse the double post but I wanted to address this separately. What are your thoughts on the second spell? Re-posted for convenience sake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arcanum Leach (Death, Spirit, or Mind \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Science.<br /> The mage names an Arcanum and casts the spell at a target. If the target possesses the named Arcanum the leach will attach to their soul. Once attached it will leach a small amount of arcane energy every time a spell is cast of the type named. This does not hinder the casting in any way and the drain is so slight that the only effect felt by the mage is a slight nausea. Once 10 spells have been siphoned the leach is full and drops off. Detached it sprouts wings and enters twilight flying back to the caster. If the duration of the spell ends before it siphons enough energy then falls to the ground and dissipates. The caster is aware that the leach is dead.<br /> The caster can devour the leach and gain knowledge of the Arcanum siphoned. (In game terms the mage may spend experience in the named Arcanum without a tutor, the spell needs a potency equal to the level of knowledge learned.)<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can use the stolen energy to turn a turn an untutored legacy attainment into a tutored legacy attainment.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The leach can be set to siphon of skills in which case it takes 10 days to collect the information desired before returning to the mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T04:30:16-08:00","id":1022271,"title":"","content":"This leech sounds like something that might be more appropriate as a Making spell, in my opinion, and thus require five dots in one of the three Arcana? Given its cerebral quality, though, it probably should be Mind or Spirit only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:00:36-08:00","id":1022277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022271#post1022271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This leech sounds like something that might be more appropriate as a Making spell, in my opinion, and thus require five dots in one of the three Arcana? Given its cerebral quality, though, it probably should be Mind or Spirit only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting, but as a level 5 effect I would expect more than just skipping the tutor portion of the learning process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:14:11-08:00","id":1022279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022277#post1022277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, but as a level 5 effect I would expect more than just skipping the tutor portion of the learning process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it could also allow you to learn rotes and/or praxes in the specified Arcanum, by default?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:24:37-08:00","id":1022281,"title":"","content":"Interesting take on the spell, I think I like that. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T06:47:54-08:00","id":1022305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022277#post1022277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting, but as a level 5 effect I would expect more than just skipping the tutor portion of the learning process.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcanum dots (and thus what Practice the spell falls under) is more about how the spell affects stuff, rather than the strength of its final effects. The spell creates a magical pseudo-life form whose function don't exactly map to any other Practices, so it looked more like Making.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see this as a Mind Making spell that creates a psychic leech that drains mundane Skill knowledge as its basic effect, and then drains Arcana and Rotes as its Reach option.<br /> <br /> And also chiming into Satchel's main criticism about the other spell - spells in this game don't have multiple, different effects, not even with Reach. Reach only gives you <i>augmented </i>effects, not <i>different </i>ones. The line is fuzzy, I admit, but it is still there.<br /> <br /> I use something like this: If I can describe a spell as &quot;A and B&quot;, it should've been two spells. If I can describe a spell as &quot;A and A+&quot;, then it's a single spell with the A+ a Reach effect. For what constitutes A and B in the first place, I usually look at the Arcanum's purview. Take the Death Arcanum, for example. A spell that conjures tendrils of darkness that rot everything it touches? &quot;Darkness&quot; and &quot;decay&quot; are different items under the Death purview, so I say this is actually two spells in one.<br /> <br /> Hope that helped! It's always nice seeing new users and new spells in this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  some clarification on the writing 12-26-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:34:53-08:00","id":1022325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022305#post1022305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Arcanum dots (and thus what Practice the spell falls under) is more about how the spell affects stuff, rather than the strength of its final effects. The spell creates a magical pseudo-life form whose function don't exactly map to any other Practices, so it looked more like Making.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see this as a Mind Making spell that creates a psychic leech that drains mundane Skill knowledge as its basic effect, and then drains Arcana and Rotes as its Reach option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I was looking at the leach part of it as just a description of what it looks like. not an actual creature. It can't be attacked, pulled off killed when it leaves or arrives. It isn't a creature. I went with the Practice: Knowing because you are learning something. The spell could have been just as easily described as you tapping into their castings to learn something. But I see your point if it was to actually create something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022305#post1022305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also chiming into Satchel's main criticism about the other spell - spells in this game don't have multiple, different effects, not even with Reach. Reach only gives you <i>augmented </i>effects, not <i>different </i>ones. The line is fuzzy, I admit, but it is still there.<br /> <br /> I use something like this: If I can describe a spell as &quot;A and B&quot;, it should've been two spells. If I can describe a spell as &quot;A and A+&quot;, then it's a single spell with the A+ a Reach effect. For what constitutes A and B in the first place, I usually look at the Arcanum's purview. Take the Death Arcanum, for example. A spell that conjures tendrils of darkness that rot everything it touches? &quot;Darkness&quot; and &quot;decay&quot; are different items under the Death purview, so I say this is actually two spells in one.<br /> <br /> Hope that helped! It's always nice seeing new users and new spells in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>And i do not see them as separate effects, I look at it logically what would happen if someone was to actually attach part of a soul to another soul. Being new to the game I am probably wrong but that is still my view point.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments. This is a frustrating and difficult system to learn but I must learn it if I am to try and introduce this to my face-to-face players. I have played in alot of different game systems, including cWoD all flavors, since the mid to late 70's and with the exception of Champions and stuff like SFB this is one of the most complex systems to try and pick up. The daunting and sometimes needless nuances of the system complicates and lengthens the learning curve. By needless nuances I am referring to stuff like Nimbus Tilts, Doors and keys, Chance dice, Yantras. When I saw the Yantras section the first thing I thought of was &quot;Shadowrun&quot; being referred to the bucket O'Dice game. Base Gnosis +Arcana +13 Yantra bonus dice -8 bonus dice to get other effects +willpower, teamworks, and whatever else the players can think of is more that just a little convoluted.<br /> <br /> Sorry this isn't the place to talk of other game mechanics just a little overwhelmed and frustrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-26-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:37:29-08:00","id":1022326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022325#post1022325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok I was looking at the leach part of it as just a description of what it looks like. not an actual creature. It can't be attacked, pulled off killed when it leaves or arrives. It isn't a creature. I went with the Practice: Knowing because you are learning something. The spell could have been just as easily described as you tapping into their castings to learn something. But I see your point if it was to actually create something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And i do not see them as separate effects, I look at it logically what would happen if someone was to actually attach part of a soul to another soul. Being new to the game I am probably wrong but that is still my view point.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments. This is a frustrating and difficult system to learn but I must learn it if I am to try and introduce this to my face-to-face players. I have played in alot of different game systems, including cWoD all flavors, since the mid to late 70's and with the exception of Champions and stuff like SFB this is one of the most complex systems to try and pick up. The daunting and sometimes needless nuances of the system complicates and lengthens the learning curve. By needless nuances I am referring to stuff like Nimbus Tilts, Doors and keys, Yantras. When I saw the Yantras section the first thing I thought of was &quot;Shadowrun&quot; being referred to the bucket O'Dice game. Base Gnosis +Arcana +13 bonus dice -8 bonus dice to get other effects +willpower, teamworks, and whatever else the players can think of is more that just a little convoluted.<br /> <br /> Sorry this isn't the place to talk of other game mechanics just a little overwhelmed and frustrated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're just talking about Creative Thaumaturgy, then this thread is exactly what that's for - so you're good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:42:50-08:00","id":1022329,"title":"","content":"Modified the above port to include Chance Dice to the needless nuances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:54:00-08:00","id":1022332,"title":"","content":"That first spell is definitely a mess of different effects. Spliced soul, loyalty (Really don't like that part doesn't make sense to me since souls don't work like that), making a sleepwalker (Which is erroneously Lasting), improved Sympathetic connections, and Possession at a lower dot level than you're supposed to have it at? Just no, I'd never allow one spell to do all that.<br /> <br /> Plus it forces you to cast it in ritual time, which is unnecessary. All spells are cast in ritual time by default, you pay a Reach to cast Instantly. There shouldn't be any spell that forces you to not be &quot;reckless.&quot; Heck, making a soul stone is an Instakt action, and not even a spell. It's a very easy &quot;reckless&quot; thing to be able to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:49:50-08:00","id":1022358,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, I understand what is being said and I am trying to heads or tails of it. You are pointing out that each one is a separate and stand alone effect. If that is correct then each should have a separate and stand alone benefit. So help me understand why they are separate and stand alone and not consequences of the base effect of having the souls spliced.<br /> <br /> Splice Soul: What solo effect would splicing two souls or splicing a piece of soul to another soul have in game terms? What benefit could a mage expect by splicing his soul to another that wouldn't be a separate effect. Is it only that I can share spells with him as I would a familiar?<br /> <br /> Loyalty: Is there no such thing as loyalty in Mage the Awakening? I was looking at it like Ghouls in Vampire. They are magically forced to be predisposed to their masters. BTW I have never played Vampire the Requiem either so not even sure if there is a Ghoul any more. However unlike Ghouls which giving the mortal power it just makes them loyal to you. Would this be a mind adder? or a reach?<br /> <br /> Making a Sleepwalker: Ok, just took a look at the sleepwalker section again and it states that there is no known means to force someone to become a sleepwalker that the brute force effect is the only way and that is temporary. So with a &quot;Recharge&quot; reach similar to the Crucible (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022) spell, it would be in effect as long as the spell was recharged. I can see this as a separate and stand alone spell and I am more that willing to remove that from the Splice Soul spell.<br /> <br /> Improved Sympathetic Connection: Don't really see this as Improved. I was looking to express the same connection as with a Soul Stone as part of your soul is in there.<br /> <br /> Limited Possession: I can see where this is a separate and distinct spell all and unto itself, but how would a Death Mage take control of another other than splicing a portion of his soul to another. It being a mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell. But since it is a separate effect it can be withdrawn from the spell as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-26-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:01:35-08:00","id":1022363,"title":"","content":"Maybe the spell would be best to build an entire Legacy around and make the different effects Legacy Attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:58:38-08:00","id":1022380,"title":"","content":"If a Death Mage can possess someone then Possession probably goes like this: Enter Twilight, use Death 4 to transform your ephemeral form into a Ghost Mage with the Possession Numina, find acceptable target, or just use Death to &quot;force&quot; your ghost self to possess a target. It's a multiple step process at least.<br /> <br /> As for the effects of a spliced soul Satchel's spell made the most sense to me. Alternatively, just say that the spell is simply lifting the restriction that soul stones be made of inanimate objects and grants all attached benefits of a soul stone. So the Mage and the target would share a Connected strength Sympathy and the Mage would be able to use them as a Dedicated Tool that could reduce the Paradox die pool by 2. I don't think I'd allow such a soul &quot;stone&quot; to be used to establish a demesne or anything though. Note though, the spell's effect is just &quot;Lift this restriction&quot; all these other effects come from actually creating the soul &quot;stone&quot; which isn't a spell. If the spell ends then the target would no longer be a suitable vessel for the shard of the Mage's soul and it would count as a destroyed soul stone. This wouldn't be a good spell to cast on a Sleeper because you'd potentially be exposing them to a lot of magic they couldn't handle, plus a Sleeper witness to your magic would reduce the effectiveness of making them a soul stone in the first place. On the other hand, it would be a pretty good way to keep track of someone, even Sleepers, because of the lack of Sympathetic Withstand. It wouldn't allow sense swapping though, that's specifically part of the familiar manifestation and not the Connected Sympathy.<br /> <br /> By the way, the Arcanum Leech, I'd change that from siphoning off a specific number of spells to it having to last through a story. After a story is usually when you get to spend XP anyway, and it removes the clunky bit about having to check if the person it's attached to has cast 10 spells of the appropriate arcana or not. You can just say: Well, this spell has been running without interference for the entire story, so that's my justification for spending XP on this arcana. I'm not sure the reach to effect mundane skills is appropriate since usually only Mind gives those, and even if it is appropriate then this spell should be flipped to benefit mundane skills first with a reach to benefit a designated arcana as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-26-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T10:51:06-08:00","id":1022390,"title":"","content":"That all sounds good to me and I do like Satchel's spell. and so I could make several spells out of the one.<br /> <br /> Splice Soul: Satchel's spell.<br /> <br /> Possession: Death 4 and as the way that you described it.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalker: Same effect as Steal Fire with +1 Reach to allow recharge.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Arcanum leach swapping the mundane and the arcane around does make more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now I can't stop thinking of these spells being the basis of a Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-26-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:28:23-08:00","id":1022478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022380#post1022380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Death Mage can possess someone then Possession probably goes like this: Enter Twilight, use Death 4 to transform your ephemeral form into a Ghost Mage with the Possession Numina, find acceptable target, or just use Death to &quot;force&quot; your ghost self to possess a target. It's a multiple step process at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple of questions:<br /> When a Death Mage enters twilight is he a ghost. I do not see a Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell that will transform a mages ephemeral into a ghost. I see a spell that will allow a mage to enter twilight and turn into ephemeral. I see a spell that will give a ghost manifested conditions, so once a ghost you can give yourself the possessed manifested condition. I see on page 238 it talks about a Ghost-Mage in the Lich section and then it directs you to page 253 for Supernal Being, but one again it doesn't talk about how one would go from being a mage to being a Ghost-Mage, except for a Legacy that can turn your mind, body, and soul into a Ghost-Mage. Just entering twilight doesn't make you a Supernal Being does it? I see where a Supernal Being has dots equal to their rank in two Arcana.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:56:57-08:00","id":1022497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022478#post1022478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Couple of questions:<br /> When a Death Mage enters twilight is he a ghost. I do not see a Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spell that will transform a mages ephemeral into a ghost. I see a spell that will allow a mage to enter twilight and turn into ephemeral. I see a spell that will give a ghost manifested conditions, so once a ghost you can give yourself the possessed manifested condition. I see on page 238 it talks about a Ghost-Mage in the Lich section and then it directs you to page 253 for Supernal Being, but one again it doesn't talk about how one would go from being a mage to being a Ghost-Mage, except for a Legacy that can turn your mind, body, and soul into a Ghost-Mage. Just entering twilight doesn't make you a Supernal Being does it? I see where a Supernal Being has dots equal to their rank in two Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even after a mage attunes himself into Death-Twilight, he is still not a ghost. He is an ephemeral entity that shares the same &quot;wavelength&quot; or &quot;frequency&quot; of Twilight as ghosts, which means that he can see, talk with, and punch out ghosts. But he is not a 'real' ghost, for a real ghost is the psychic residue of a consciousness.<br /> <br /> There are two types of beings that can be called &quot;ghost mages&quot;. One is simply the ghost of a mage. It might be more self-aware and powerful, and wield unique Numina that resemble the mage's Praxes, but it is ultimately a ghost. The other, the &quot;real&quot; Ghost Mage, is a type of lich, who was so consumed with overcoming his mortality that he abandoned his humanity in the way of attaining it. Unlike a ghost of a mage, which are nothing more than ephemera-made replicas of the person, a Ghost Mage retains his Awakened powers. Although, without clear 2E mechanics on them, to what extent I have no idea. Neither on how a mage transforms himself into a Ghost Mage - I suspect it would have someting to do with soul stones.<br /> <br /> I don't know why the Lich section would redirect the reader to the Supernal Entity section, though. (I can't remember everything!) Maybe calling upon an Entity to wrestle a Pact from it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:26:14-08:00","id":1022513,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> said. There isn't a Death 4 spell to transform a Mage's ephemeral form into a Mage, you would have to make that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:08:22-08:00","id":1022533,"title":"","content":"<b>Ghost Form (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Empathy, Survival.<br /> While in twilight the mage may turn his ephemeral substance into a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:15:03-08:00","id":1022537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022533#post1022533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ghost Form (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Empathy, Survival.<br /> While in twilight the mage may turn his ephemeral substance into a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would it be appropriate to add a +1 reach that like below.<br /> +1 Reach: spend 1 mana the mage may turn the ghost int twilight ephemera. The ghost would withstand with rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:17:04-08:00","id":1022597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022537#post1022537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be appropriate to add a +1 reach that like below.<br /> +1 Reach: spend 1 mana the mage may turn the ghost int twilight ephemera. The ghost would withstand with rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what this means. What's the Reach do?<br /> <br /> Anyway, for the spell in general you might want to give the effects of becoming a ghost, for instance acquiring Manifestations and Numina. I'd say your rank is pretty easily determined by your dots in Death similar to the way a Mage with Spirit 4 counts as a Rank 4 spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T20:36:04-08:00","id":1022603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022497#post1022497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why the Lich section would redirect the reader to the Supernal Entity section, though. (I can't remember everything!) Maybe calling upon an Entity to wrestle a Pact from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat as a ghost/spirit/goetia that uses Mana instead of Essence, has at least two Arcana at a rating of [Rank] and others at lower levels instead of using Influences, rolls their Paradox pools with rote quality and takes aggravated damage rather than generating anomalies, and has a casting pool of Power + Finesse and infinite free Reach.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral liches are goddamn terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T01:33:11-08:00","id":1022652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022603#post1022603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Treat as a ghost/spirit/goetia that uses Mana instead of Essence, has at least two Arcana at a rating of [Rank] and others at lower levels instead of using Influences, rolls their Paradox pools with rote quality and takes aggravated damage rather than generating anomalies, and has a casting pool of Power + Finesse and infinite free Reach.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral liches are goddamn terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What you quoted is for Supernal Entities, Ghost are not Supernal Entities they are Ephemeral Entities as stated in the top paragraph on page 253. As stated on page 254 first column, second paragraph from the bottom, a ghost is rank 1 or 2 outside of the Underworld unless summoned back from the underworld at which point they may be of any rank. On page 258 second paragraph it states that Ghosts have influence equal to their ranks and Supernal Entities has at least two Arcana at a rating of [Rank] and others at lower levels instead of using Influences.<br /> <br /> A Lich that has become a Ghost-Mage is still just a ghost and therefore an Ephemeral Being. He may still have Arcana but I do not feel that he should get to use the Arcana with the same impunity that a Supernal Being would and they should still follow the rules that govern all mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:32:08-08:00","id":1022662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022597#post1022597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know what this means. What's the Reach do?<br /> <br /> Anyway, for the spell in general you might want to give the effects of becoming a ghost, for instance acquiring Manifestations and Numina. I'd say your rank is pretty easily determined by your dots in Death similar to the way a Mage with Spirit 4 counts as a Rank 4 spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How is this.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Form (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Empathy, Survival.<br /> This spell allows the mage to transform a subject from twilight state into an Ephemeral Entity known as a ghost. For the duration of the spell the subject has the following traits determined by the mage at the time of casting. If the subject was a mage they use mana to power their abilities and they keep the Arcana ratings that they have, otherwise the newly formed ghost uses essence to power its abilities.<br /> <b><i>** Drawbacks:</i></b> This power comes with a price. For every hour that the subject remains in ghost form they must roll Power + Resolve + Gnosis - 1 per previous roll. If they fail they start to become disconnected to their former self gaining the Driven condition (see below). If they ever dramatically fail this roll they gain the Amnesia condition forgetting there previous existence believing that they truly are just a ghost.<br /> <br /> ** <b>Driven Condition: </b>(persistent)<br /> Your character loses interest in everything except one task. This could be brought on by a tragedy, a mental break, or a spell gone tragically wrong. Whatever the reason your character loses interest in everything not related to fulfilling their goal.<br /> <i>Game Effect:</i> Your character loses interest in the current task at hand in favor of a new task which they will single mindedly peruse. All rolls not related to their new task is at a -2 dice.<br /> <i>Resolution: </i>Accomplish the goal.<br /> <i>Beat:</i> Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her task.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Traits:</b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>* Power, Finesse, and Resistance:</b> Average the dots in each category to arrive at the new rating for each.<br /> <b>Influence:</b> The mage assigns what the ghost has influence over, this influence is at rank 2.<br /> <b>Twilight Form:</b> The ghost has the Twilight Form manifestation.<br /> <b>*** Manifestation:</b> The mage may assign 2 additional manifestation (page 258 \u2013 261 or Chronicles of Darkness page 133 - 136) of his choice on the ghost.<br /> <b>Numina:</b> The mage may assign 3 Numina (page 261 \u2013 263 or Chronicles of Darkness page 136 - 138) of his choice to the ghost.<br /> <b>Essence/Mana Max:</b> 15<br /> <b>Bans:</b> The mage assigns a ban to the ghost.<br /> <b>Banes:</b> The mage assigns one bane to the ghost.<br /> All other traits listed on page 256 are calculated accordingly.<br /> <br /> * Edited to follow the suggestion from the Chronicles of Darkness page 127, the states that the Ghosts usually use the average rating in each category from when they were alive.<br /> <br /> ** Edited added a drawback and a condition. It isn't needed but it could bring some interesting situations.<br /> <br /> *** Edited reducing the number of manifestation to that rank of the ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-27-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:43:39-08:00","id":1022683,"title":"","content":"I think you're only supposed to have a number of Manifestations equal to Rank, otherwise looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T04:19:09-08:00","id":1022688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1022683#post1022683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're only supposed to have a number of Manifestations equal to Rank, otherwise looks good.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct i will change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:26:41-08:00","id":1023203,"title":"","content":"<b>Ephemeral Vision (Death \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> The mage can gaze into the very Ephemeral of all that reside in the Death-attuned Twilight. The mage must have the ability to see into Twilight albeit by magical or by actually being there. By studying an Ephemeral patterns of an entity or object the mage can gather information as to its general abilities and condition. The mage must study the pattern for a minimum of one turn after which he can gather certain information about it. For each level of potency that mage can ask one of the following questions.<br /> \u2022 What is the Rank of the entity?<br /> \u2022 How many manifestation does it have?<br /> \u2022 What one of its manifestations? * This question may be asked more than once.<br /> \u2022 What is its General level of decay?<br /> \u2022 Is the pattern bleeding essence?<br /> \u2022 What is its Ban<br /> \u2022 What is its Bane<br /> The symbols of death and decay start to appear around the entity or object. The subject may continue to study the Ephemera and continue to get more answers as long as the spell lasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Splice Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidate, Medicine, Occult.<br /> For the duration of this spell the mage can splice a sliver of his soul onto that of a Living soul. The target must be a sleeper and for the duration of this spell he temporarily becomes a sleepwalker with all that entails. Any breaking points due to witnessing magic and Quiescence effects the subject would normally suffer are held in abeyance until the spell\u2019s Duration expires, only to come crashing down all at once when the spell ends.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As long as the spell\u2019s Duration lasts, its wielder may spend one point of Mana at any time to \u201crecharge\u201d this effect, and the sleeper remains a sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Form (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Empathy, Survival.<br /> This spell allows the mage to transform a subject from twilight state into an Ephemeral Entity known as a ghost. For the duration of the spell the subject has the following traits determined by the mage at the time of casting. If the subject was a mage they use mana to power their abilities and they keep the Arcana ratings that they have, otherwise the newly formed ghost uses essence to power its abilities.<br /> <b><i>Drawbacks:</i></b> This power comes with a price. For every hour that the subject remains in ghost form they must roll Power + Resolve + Gnosis - 1 per previous roll. If they fail they start to become disconnected to their former self gaining the Driven condition (see below). If they ever dramatically fail this roll they gain the Amnesia condition forgetting there previous existence believing that they truly are just a ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>Driven Condition:</b> (persistent)<br /> Your character loses interest in everything except one task. This could be brought on by a tragedy, a mental break, or a spell gone tragically wrong. Whatever the reason your character loses interest in everything not related to fulfilling their goal.<br /> <b><i>Game Effect:</i></b> Your character loses interest in the current task at hand in favor of a new task which they will single mindedly peruse. All rolls not related to their new task is at a -2 dice.<br /> <b><i>Resolution:</i></b> Accomplish the goal.<br /> <b><i>Beat:</i></b> Character fails to fulfill an obligation due to pursuing her task.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Traits:</b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Power, Finesse, and Resistance:</b> Average the dots in each category to arrive at the new rating for each.<br /> <b>Influence:</b> The mage assigns what the ghost has influence over, this influence is at rank 2.<br /> <b>Twilight Form:</b> The ghost has the Twilight Form manifestation.<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> The mage may assign 2 additional manifestation (page 258 \u2013 261 or Chronicles of Darkness page 133 - 136) of his choice on the ghost.<br /> <b>Numina:</b> The mage may assign 3 Numina (page 261 \u2013 263 or Chronicles of Darkness page 136 - 138) of his choice to the ghost.<br /> <b>Essence/Mane Max:</b> 15<br /> <b>Bans:</b> The mage assigns a ban to the ghost.<br /> <b>Banes:</b> The mage assigns one bane to the ghost.<br /> All other traits listed on page 256 are calculated accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:15:32-08:00","id":1023256,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering why Ghost Form isn't a Death 4/ Life 4 effect. Humans and Ghosts are only related like a cause and effect. I don't get the Shadow Form either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-28-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:27:40-08:00","id":1023261,"title":"","content":"I assume that since when you transition to Twilight you're made of ephemera and so Death as an arcana that deals with ephemera can warp it from one form to another Mage to Ghost.<br /> <br /> The Shadow spell makes no sense to me without Life either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:54:45-08:00","id":1023275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023256#post1023256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering why Ghost Form isn't a Death 4/ Life 4 effect. Humans and Ghosts are only related like a cause and effect. I don't get the Shadow Form either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Mrmdubois said once you cross over into twilight you are already ephemera.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023261#post1023261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow spell makes no sense to me without Life either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow form? What shadow form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:10:09-08:00","id":1023284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023275#post1023275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow form? What shadow form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check Death 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:16:49-08:00","id":1023286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023284#post1023284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check Death 4.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh you mean Shadow Flesh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:24:15-08:00","id":1023376,"title":"","content":"<b>Deaden Nerves (Life \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> Pain travels along the nervous system and into the brain. You can stop subject from feeling pain in several different ways. One of the most efficient ways is to deaden the nerves and thus stopping the pain at the source. This spell does just that. It deadens the nerve preventing the impulses from reaching the brain. Each level of potency stops the pain cause from two levels of bashing wounds. It does not stop the wound from bleeding and the subject will still notice that an impact was made.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Each level of potency will block the pain from a lethal wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 12-28-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T14:38:38-08:00","id":1023434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023376#post1023376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Deaden Nerves (Life \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> Pain travels along the nervous system and into the brain. You can stop subject from feeling pain in several different ways. One of the most efficient ways is to deaden the nerves and thus stopping the pain at the source. This spell does just that. It deadens the nerve preventing the impulses from reaching the brain. Each level of potency stops the pain cause from two levels of bashing wounds. It does not stop the wound from bleeding and the subject will still notice that an impact was made.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Each level of potency will block the pain from a lethal wound.</div> </div> </div> </div>If blocking the pain is what the spell does narratively, then shouldn't its mechanical effect be preventing wound penalties? Or is that what you were intending?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T14:52:15-08:00","id":1023441,"title":"","content":"Perhaps +1 Reach: The subject suffers no wound penalties from Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Wound penalties from lethal probably represents the body failing rather than pain just hindering your actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T15:04:15-08:00","id":1023447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1023441#post1023441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps +1 Reach: The subject suffers no wound penalties from Bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was leaning to the spell's base effects being that, and preventing bashing damage itself being the Reach option. Maybe another Reach to prevent Tilts caused by bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T15:17:26-08:00","id":1023451,"title":"","content":"I was intending for it to deal with abilities and conditions that cause excruciating pain, if that is possible. Or to deal with the injury penalties if pain isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T07:53:43-08:00","id":1023758,"title":"","content":"I would make it like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Deaden Nerves (Life \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b><i> Veiling</i><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b><i> Potency</i><br /> <b>Withstanding:</b><i> Stamina</i><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b><i> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.</i><br /> <i>Pain travels along the nervous system and into the brain. You can stop subject from feeling pain in several different ways. One of the most efficient ways is to deaden the nerves and thus stopping the pain at the source. This spell does just that. It deadens the nerve preventing the impulses from reaching the brain. The subject ignores a dice of wound penalties for each Potency. Also, he suffers a penalty equal to Potency for any physical action from reduced feedback.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Alternatively, the subject may ignore one physical Tilt for each Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can excert greater control over which nerve feedback it numbs, allowing him to either numb pain without losing tactile feedback, or vice versa.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:21:59-08:00","id":1023809,"title":"","content":"The gaming group and I was talking and the spell is poorly worded and the way it is no to should be practice: Flaying as it is getting rid of the pain. To keep it as a Practice: Veiling spell it should only mask the pain.<br /> <br /> As i was telling them in my mind the body of the text is the actual Imago and the Practice is how you go about bringing to pass the spell. As the wording of the spell gets rid of the pain and that needing to be a flaying spell it would not work and therefore the ST should say something like this &quot;The imago forms in your mind, unfortunately nothing happens as the energies used were not capable of bringing the spell forth&quot;. Basically the spell fails and the turn is wasted.<br /> <br /> With that being said, for the spell to remain a Practice: Veiling it would need to be something like this.<br /> <br /> <b>Deaden Nerves (Life \u2022\u2022) or (Mind \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult.<br /> An apprentice of life is able to hide or mask the pain that others would feel from injuries or condition. For the duration of this spell the injuries still produce the pain but the body just ignores it as it never registers. All other sensation is felt by the subject, the running blood as it flows over the skin, the pressure of the boulder and it crushes the foot, etc.... Each level of potency can mask the pain from 2 bashing wounds, or the pain of one condition, if this is equal to the amount of damage taken the subject may act as if nothing happened. A maimed foot is still maim, a broken arm is still broken.<br /> <b><i>Drawback:</i></b> This can actually do more harm to the subject. The pain is there to tell someone that what they are doing is harming them or to let them know that what they are doing is causing more damage. If the action taken would normally exacerbate the condition then the subject takes an additional point of the same type of damage. this may increase the pain enough that the subject once again feels it, albeit at a reduced level.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Each level of potency will block the pain from a lethal wound.<br /> <br /> <br /> The spell that you presented is good but I would actually change it to a level 3 as such.<br /> <br /> <b>Deaden Nerves (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> <i>Flaying</i><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> <i>Potency</i><br /> <b>Withstanding:</b> <i>Stamina</i><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> <i>Empathy, Medicine, Occult.</i><br /> <i>Pain travels along the nervous system and into the brain. You can stop subject from feeling pain in several different ways. One of the most efficient ways is to deaden the nerves and thus stopping the pain at the source. This spell does just that. It deadens the nerve preventing the impulses from reaching the brain. The subject ignores a dice of wound penalties for each Potency. Also, he suffers a penalty equal to Potency for any physical action from reduced feedback.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Alternatively, the subject may ignore one physical Tilt for each Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can excert greater control over which nerve feedback it numbs, allowing him to either numb pain without losing tactile feedback, or vice versa.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:36:27-08:00","id":1023820,"title":"","content":"The Practice is Fraying, not Flaying.<br /> <br /> Basically though, you're talking about using two different Practices for essentially the same effect.<br /> <br /> By the way, I don't think the Veiling version should have a drawback written into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:42:09-08:00","id":1023826,"title":"","content":"Yes fraying, not flaying. I was not paying attention to the word and much as the meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:30:41-08:00","id":1023845,"title":"","content":"Since the spell only affects sensory information, I don't see how it would be Fraying. It's not like it creates nerve damage, or has any effects in any bodily function. It just makes pain and tactile information &quot;invisible&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:19:16-08:00","id":1023861,"title":"","content":"I assumed the Fraying version would be actually damaging the nerves from the language of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:48:17-08:00","id":1023871,"title":"","content":"It could fry the nerves if you wanted it to permanently numbing the nerve, I would go so far as to say that it could be used as a weapon to paralyze someone if the spine was fried.<br /> <br /> It might be worth it to adjust the spell to heal or damage the nervous system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:55:18-08:00","id":1023875,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that's even necessary, you can inflict Tilts or remove them with 3 dots so it could be a Reach effect added to Bruise Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:47:35-08:00","id":1023899,"title":"","content":"That is true I never thought of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T11:33:04-08:00","id":1024855,"title":"","content":"My players on last session wanted to locate their kidnapped Promethean friend. One of players wanted to recreate this like effect from Constatine TV series on Space 3 - just look on this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://projectfandom.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/Con-pic1-3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I let him, as I thought it would be Reach option on simple Space 1 <i>Locate Object </i>spell. Did I do it right, or does this would need higher Space dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:16:13-08:00","id":1024947,"title":"","content":"If you have a Sympathetic Connection to a thing and they're not behind Wards then it would be just a Sympathetic use of Locate Object or some similar Creative Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:22:37-08:00","id":1024950,"title":"","content":"But if you can't target what you're looking for Fate would be a lot more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRt