a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a quick question: To change the size of a person, from size 5 to size 6 or from six 6 to size 5 would that be Weaving or Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per <i>Shrink and Grow</i>, it's Weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T13:40:55-08:00","id":1025146,"title":"","content":"Ok I was looking for Growth and Shrink in life not matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T15:17:24-08:00","id":1025178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1025146#post1025146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I was looking for Growth and Shrink in life not matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The spell is essentially usable in both circumstances, as most spells are. You only need change the Arcanum you're affecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T15:31:09-08:00","id":1025180,"title":"","content":"Yes I can see that, what I was referring to is that I was looking in the life spells and didn't she it in the matter spells. Now that i have read it I know that it can be used on both matter and life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:36:59-08:00","id":1026778,"title":"","content":"What Practice would you peg creating a corpse at? Death Making seems obvious enough, but it also seems like a kind of weak effect for a five-dot spell. Maybe Death Weaving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:39:36-08:00","id":1026780,"title":"","content":"It's at whatever Practice can get a person killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:51:20-08:00","id":1026786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026780#post1026780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's at whatever Practice can get a person killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I meant like, making a corpse out of nothing. For times when you need a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:32:36-08:00","id":1026800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026786#post1026786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I meant like, making a corpse out of nothing. For times when you need a corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about adding a Death 5 option to the Life spell &quot;Create Life&quot; so that the created organism is dead from the start?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T18:51:46-08:00","id":1026802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026800#post1026800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about adding a Death 5 option to the Life spell &amp;quot;Create Life&amp;quot; so that the created organism is dead from the start?</div> </div> </div> </div>Needlessly over complicated. Death 5 ought to be able to provide a corpse, Death 4 can turn one kind of Death related thing into a corpse as well. Why make a fresh corpse though when there are so many lying around waiting to be repurposed? Just use Death 2 to mark the cause of Death and who the corpse belongs to. Heck, if you're really short-handed you can just use Death 2 to be a corpse yourself, or get a buddy to take the role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:01:09-08:00","id":1026805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026802#post1026802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Needlessly over complicated. Death 5 ought to be able to provide a corpse, Death 4 can turn one kind of Death related thing into a corpse as well. Why make a fresh corpse though when there are so many lying around waiting to be repurposed? Just use Death 2 to mark the cause of Death and who the corpse belongs to. Heck, if you're really short-handed you can just use Death 2 to be a corpse yourself, or get a buddy to take the role.</div> </div> </div> </div>For my defense, I did that for the &quot;create from nothing&quot; part, but yeah those methods are easier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hey wait, was the Practice of Patterning <i>that </i>flexible? While the idea of spawning corpses from the shadows is too tempting to not try, I don't think you can get a corpse from a ghost, coldness, decay in an object, ectoplasm, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:39:24-08:00","id":1026885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026805#post1026805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For my defense, I did that for the &amp;quot;create from nothing&amp;quot; part, but yeah those methods are easier.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hey wait, was the Practice of Patterning <i>that </i>flexible? While the idea of spawning corpses from the shadows is too tempting to not try, I don't think you can get a corpse from a ghost, coldness, decay in an object, ectoplasm, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no different than transmuting energy or matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:13:53-08:00","id":1026947,"title":"","content":"I'd go with Matter, turn appropriate material into an organic <s>mess</s> mass, then use Death 2/3 to say, &quot;yup, that's dead&quot;.<br /> Death 5 would just circumvent the middle-man, as Making spells usually do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:52:16-08:00","id":1026999,"title":"","content":"<b>Fester the People </b>(Death 3)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina<br /> If you ever mess with a Death mage remember to not be wounded because if you are - better run, better run. With this spell the mage can bolster effects of the damage you received before. <br /> For the duration of the spell every point of Potency doubles the number of bashing wounds target has but is not able to roll them over to lethals.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Damage can now be rolled over and upgraded<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>The spell can now double lethal damage <br /> <b>+2 Reach and 1 Mana:</b> The spell can now double aggravated damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:33:08-08:00","id":1027250,"title":"","content":"I would not allow Fester The People. It just seems like a spell that allows lethal damage at 3 dots without reach, whereas all the other Arcana are very clear that 3 dots is about bashing damage, lethal with reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12787-logos","name":"logos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:57:19-08:00","id":1027272,"title":"","content":"Those rules are only for direct damage spells and that spell is not doing direct damage, it has to bypass stamina and also works only until duration ends. Forces can deal 10 bashing damage with 1 potency spell, Spaces Ban can suffocate you while also excluding you from fight and no one bats an eye. Not to mention Minds 2 &quot;kill yourself&quot; spell. Fester the people is just a cool concept but hardly an overkill or anything close to imbalance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-05-2017, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:06:45-08:00","id":1027279,"title":"","content":"Fate also has a Withstood three dot spell that is capable of inflicting lethal and even aggravated damage. Grave Misfortune on page 137.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T22:51:37-08:00","id":1027464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>logos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027250#post1027250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not allow Fester The People. It just seems like a spell that allows lethal damage at 3 dots without reach, whereas all the other Arcana are very clear that 3 dots is about bashing damage, lethal with reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death already allows lethal damage at 3 dots: see Devouring the Slain.<br /> That said, this spell really kind of tries to occupy the same conceptual space by making existing wounds worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T03:46:52-08:00","id":1027517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1026885#post1026885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's no different than transmuting energy or matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me that doesn't make sense. This is strictly my own interpretation, but I don't think everything under the Arcanum's purview should be considered equivalent. If it did, I could fashion a soul out of ectoplasm, or adding Matter literally from thin air.<br /> <br /> To me a corpse is a transitionary state between Life and Matter. You can't create a corpse ex nihilo because for something to be a corpse it must once have been alive. That's why I like the +Life varint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T04:07:15-08:00","id":1027525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027517#post1027517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me a corpse is a transitionary state between Life and Matter. You can't create a corpse ex nihilo because for something to be a corpse it must once have been alive. That's why I like the +Life varint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can create a chunk of organic matter with Matter (your choice of Practice), then Weave in some Death to make sure it has all the &quot;Yup, it's a corpse&quot; symbols.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T04:13:15-08:00","id":1027529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027517#post1027517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me that doesn't make sense. This is strictly my own interpretation, but I don't think everything under the Arcanum's purview should be considered equivalent. If it did, I could fashion a soul out of ectoplasm, or adding Matter literally from thin air.<br /> <br /> To me a corpse is a transitionary state between Life and Matter. You can't create a corpse ex nihilo because for something to be a corpse it must once have been alive. That's why I like the +Life varint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls aren't exactly the strongest counter-example since they're called out specifically as special, unique snowflakes. Corpses aren't.<br /> <br /> Also you can add Matter out of thin air. Though technically thin air is Matter so I'm not even sure I understand your point there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:26:05-08:00","id":1027551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027529#post1027529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Souls aren't exactly the strongest counter-example since they're called out specifically as special, unique snowflakes. Corpses aren't.<br /> <br /> Also you can add Matter out of thin air. Though technically thin air is Matter so I'm not even sure I understand your point there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that by the proposed logic, I could make a soul literally out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Souls are explicitly called out, but I see that as precedent that not everything is equivalent. Death is weird Arcanum, kind of dumping ground for a lot of little things that either don't fit anywhere else, or would be better in another Arcanum but were put in Death to make it a little more interesting and creates those seeming equivalencies that to me don't make any sense (corpse=shadow=cold)<br /> <br /> Again, this is personal, but I don't think you could create anything resembling a corpse with Matter. You could create ivory, dry bone, leather, gelatin, paper, or wood, but the intricacies of living tissue are the pruview of Life; and it is Death which transforms what once was alive into something that is not. The corpse is a transition. It is no longer alive, but it's not yeat &quot;simple&quot; Matter. The process of the corpse decomposing is Death doing it's work. Sometimes it takes a long time, sometimes it's quicker, but without some kind of magic, it's not instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T05:58:40-08:00","id":1027571,"title":"","content":"I think you may be placing too much weight on the metaphysical value of a corpse. Ill just agree to disagree though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:02:06-08:00","id":1027572,"title":"","content":"Both shadows and cold is the absence of energy (and perhaps symbols of the heat death of the universe). It's still weird how you can manipulate shadows, but it's not completely without logic.<br /> And, again, souls are special. Just like Prime is the Arcanum for dealing with Awakened magic, but you can't use it to forcefully Awaken a Sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:49:39-08:00","id":1027721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027572#post1027572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both shadows and cold is the absence of energy (and perhaps symbols of the heat death of the universe). It's still weird how you can manipulate shadows, but it's not completely without logic.<br /> And, again, souls are special. Just like Prime is the Arcanum for dealing with Awakened magic, but you can't use it to forcefully Awaken a Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can make metaphysical sense out of it and it's ultimately better for the game, but that metaphysical thinking makes me think that transforming cold into a corpse wouldn't work. Ther'e no &quot;Cold&quot; pattern to manipulate, there's an Entropy pattern that dissipates heat, the same with light and shadows. To me turning Entropy into Corpse (or a clay statue with Matter, or sound with Forces, or flies with Life) is simply non-sensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:59:27-08:00","id":1027726,"title":"","content":"But turning a living body into shadow is somehow sensical?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:12:04-08:00","id":1027792,"title":"","content":"You don't turn cold/entropy into a corpse just like a Spirit Mage don't turn the Gauntlet into a Spirit when using the Create Spirit spell. Both the Gauntlet and Spirits fall under the Spirit Arcanum, but they're not directly metaphysically linked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:21:45-08:00","id":1027796,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a> Ha. This will blow your mind then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chicken Time</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Patterning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The caster changes time experienced by the target into a chicken. As you can't really inhabit the CHICKEN* the target is helplessly pushed into the future just like with Temporal Stutter but instead of not remembering anything he remembers the CHICKEN*. Target gets Broken condition for what he experienced.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*ROASTED</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>Remember that this is magic, and Adepts are ridiculusly potent in it. If you can accept Masters creating things from nothing why is it so hard to accept that &quot;4xp less powerfull&quot; Adepts can change anything into anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:21:45-08:00","id":1027797,"title":"","content":"(Double post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:42:54-08:00","id":1027917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027726#post1027726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But turning a living body into shadow is somehow sensical?</div> </div> </div> </div>That spell is kind of a mess, but I guess there should be some kind of niche for doing weid stuff with shadows because there are a lot of classical examples of that kind of magic. So maybe I should take that back.<br /> <br /> But there are things that &quot;make sense&quot; and things that don't. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> commented, a Spirit mage doesn't just turn the Gautlet into a Spirit. A Prime mage doesn't turn Truth into an Active Spell or the above example of turning Time into a chicken. It just doesn't make sense. I wouldn't allow shenanigans like that into a serious game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T17:04:16-08:00","id":1027924,"title":"","content":"&quot;Serious game&quot;, &quot;Magic has sense&quot;. For me the best magic fucks with your brain on a deep level like lets say turning space into time or destiny into matter and MtA lets you do those things if you are creative enough. If I wanted to throw fireballs I would play dnd or dresden files. Liberate yourself.<br /> <br /> Edit. Veiling is enough to turn shadow into ilusion of corpse but Patterning can make this shadow a &quot;real&quot; corpse - for the duration of the spell)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-06-2017, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T18:08:53-08:00","id":1027955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1027924#post1027924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Serious game&quot;, &quot;Magic has sense&quot;. For me the best magic fucks with your brain on a deep level like lets say turning space into time or destiny into matter and MtA lets you do those things if you are creative enough. If I wanted to throw fireballs I would play dnd or dresden files. Liberate yourself.<br /> <br /> Edit. Veiling is enough to turn shadow into ilusion of corpse but Patterning can make this shadow a &quot;real&quot; corpse - for the duration of the spell)</div> </div> </div> </div>Excuse me for taking the game seriously, trying to tell stories that aren't comedies and trying give actual narrative meaning to the mechanics. I guess that's just silly of me. Magic isn't real, and thus can't be meaningful in any way whatsoever so let's turn Gravity into Gravy. It will hilarious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T18:54:17-08:00","id":1027979,"title":"","content":"Look. The game isn't silly just because it lets you do silly things. Thats a horror of it - magic can be surreal but most of all its frightening. Do you call mortal CofD game silly because a player can declare that he starts dancing around a town square's fountain wearing only a diaper and talking like 3 year old? He can do that, but he won't without a very good reason. And you won't call the game silly because of this possibility.<br /> In Mage game he can be forced to do that by a starting willworker. In fact any starting mage can kill a mortal with a single spell. Is that silly? Imagine now what sick bastard someone has to be change your life experience into a chicken. That can break peoples minds and give them years of mental instability. Silly.<br /> We fear of the dark because it is hiding unknown, incomprehensible. In &quot;good&quot; hands magic can be your new darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T05:08:57-08:00","id":1028117,"title":"","content":"I would call it silly if it had merits and mechanics for it, though. I'm not a fan of 4th dot of magic mastery, and ability to transform one thing into another is probably biggest reason for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:01:35-08:00","id":1028178,"title":"","content":"I agree that changing time into space is surreal, abyssal and to some even silly but there is nothing against it in the rules. Remember the scene from Interstelar? That was it. Rules aren't silly but player action's of course can be and while changing gravity into a gravy doesn't sound cool changing gravity into a medalion that you can break to release it and temporarily double existing one is a different thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-07-2017, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T23:28:25-08:00","id":1028893,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T01:41:01-08:00","id":1028930,"title":"","content":"<b>Rigor Mortis (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Medicine, Occult<br /> Your muscles start to tighten and your joints seize locking into place, you fall to the ground ridged and stiff. You can no longer move or physically react to others. For each level of potency the target subtracts 1 dot of dexterity. If the target reaches 0 dexterity then he gains the condition Immobilized for the duration of the spell. There is no chance to break. If someone were to check your vitals they would be able to determine that you were still alive, you are still able to perform any action the does not require you to physical move.<br /> <b>Add Death \u2022\u2022:</b> By adding death to this spell the target appears to be dead as the spell Suppress Life.<br /> <b>Substitute Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> By substituting mind you are able to mentally immobilize the target and they fall limp to the ground. There is no chance to break..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-09-2017, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T03:43:29-08:00","id":1028946,"title":"","content":"I would rather make it Strength+Resolve or even Strength+Stamina. It's okay to sometimes make a Trait+Trait roll, just don't make it a standard routine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:31:25-08:00","id":1028964,"title":"","content":"Ya I was lookingat Strength + resolve but not a big fan of trait + trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:58:06-08:00","id":1028972,"title":"","content":"Strength + Athletics, then? Makes more sense than Medicine, IMO.<br /> <br /> Edit: As the spell seems to work by locking down the body directly, shouldn't it be Withstood by Stamina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T05:55:59-08:00","id":1028989,"title":"","content":"It should be Withstood by Stamina and probably not have the chance to break free because the ability to do so should already be accounted for by having a Withstand in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:23:16-08:00","id":1029008,"title":"","content":"Say, would creating food out of thin air, or even copying one portion of food into many, fall under Matter? I'm toying ideas about a mage trying to gather a cult by emulating the miracles in the Bible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:27:01-08:00","id":1029010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029008#post1029008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, would creating food out of thin air, or even copying one portion of food into many, fall under Matter? I'm toying ideas about a mage trying to gather a cult by emulating the miracles in the Bible.</div> </div> </div> </div>For non-living, non-dead foods, yes. The others would be Life and Death, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although the line where corpses become Matter is blurry, and Matter may well be sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:36:27-08:00","id":1029015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029010#post1029010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For non-living, non-dead foods, yes. The others would be Life and Death, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Edit: Although the line where corpses become Matter is blurry, and Matter may well be sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, I'll make making Manna rain down and duplicating fish and bread Matter spells then. This way my unscrupulous mage can do the walk-on-water and water-to-wine thing more easily, with relative ease and less actual power compared to other mages.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <b>Create Food (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> One or more Mana (variable)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Persuasion, Medicine<br /> While the alchemist is far from creating life from raw Matter, she can learn to sustain it. The mage targets a portion of food, and the spell creates a number of copies of it equal to Potency. She can scale the spell to as she needs it - the spell may duplicate separate apples in a bag, or the entire bag of apples, but the total volume of resultant food including the original must fit within the spell's Scale. All the created food is nutritionally identical to the original, and sustains living organisms normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may create food from nothing. He is limited to creating food that he remembers having eaten in the past.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Mind \u2022\u2022: </b>The mage may create non-existant food out of her imagination. Trying to create foods of particularly intricate recipes and presentation may require a Dexterity + Crafts roll, and modifying their nutritional qualities might call for a Intelligence + Medicine roll.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The mage may infuse the created foods with Mana, making them into tass.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022</b>: The created food is supernaturally filling, and invigorates the living body. Everyone who consumes them is considered having received a full night's rest, and enjoys a doubled natural healing rate for a period of time equal to the spell's Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-09-2017, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:31:51-08:00","id":1029177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029015#post1029015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Create Food (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> One or more Mana (variable)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Survival, Persuasion, Medicine<br /> While the alchemist is far from creating life from raw Matter, she can learn to sustain it. The mage targets a portion of food, and the spell creates a number of copies of it equal to Potency. She can scale the spell to as she needs it - the spell may duplicate separate apples in a bag, or the entire bag of apples, but the total volume of resultant food including the original must fit within the spell's Scale. All the created food is nutritionally identical to the original, and sustains living organisms normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may create food from nothing. He is limited to creating food that he remembers having eaten in the past.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Mind \u2022\u2022: </b>The mage may create non-existant food out of her imagination. Trying to create foods of particularly intricate recipes and presentation may require a Dexterity + Crafts roll, and modifying their nutritional qualities might call for a Intelligence + Medicine roll.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The mage may infuse the created foods with Mana, making them into tass.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022</b>: The created food is supernaturally filling, and invigorates the living body. Everyone who consumes them is considered having received a full night's rest, and enjoys a doubled natural healing rate for a period of time equal to the spell's Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what happens after you've eaten the food and the duration expires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T13:17:31-08:00","id":1029222,"title":"","content":"Updated Rigor Mortis. Withstand Stamina and no break free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T16:05:37-08:00","id":1029311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029177#post1029177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens after you've eaten the food and the duration expires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagined the spell as Lasting, so that the food and its benefits persist after the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:48:58-08:00","id":1029964,"title":"","content":"I have a Question: Death Arcanum states the <u><b>endings</b></u> is in its purview. Does that mean you can create a spell that will end the duration of someone else's spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:51:58-08:00","id":1029967,"title":"","content":"Yes. You need to perceive the spell first .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T01:55:00-08:00","id":1029968,"title":"","content":"Then I would assume that it uses potency and each level of potency subtracts one increment of duration. Would it use withstand? Would the spell count as dispellation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T02:47:00-08:00","id":1029973,"title":"","content":"I would just use the Prime dispellation rules. Heck, Prime 1's version talks about every spell having the capacity to end and manipulating that so it's stepping on Death's toes already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T02:56:15-08:00","id":1029976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029964#post1029964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a Question: Death Arcanum states the <u><b>endings</b></u> is in its purview. Does that mean you can create a spell that will end the duration of someone else's spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Followup - Would this be Making?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:03:26-08:00","id":1029977,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Transportation</u> (Forces </span></b></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> + Matter </span></b></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> Durability</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Crafts, Occult</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">By understanding that all Matter is but Energy bundled together and bound in a physical form, the Mage can turn Matter into a data stream which can then be transmitted to another point to be re-materialized.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can store the data stream to be used later.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can use free-floating energy (such as light, heat, etc.) to Replicate objects.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The Mage can now use this spell to Replicate food as per the previous reach option.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> Add Life </span></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">: This Spell can also be used to Transport living beings (Withstood by Stamina).</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","user":"HTaiji","date":". 01-11-2017, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:36:04-08:00","id":1029988,"title":"","content":"Why would food specifically require an extra Reach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T06:56:10-08:00","id":1030032,"title":"","content":"As per the spells from Matter where making one simple object requires nothing, but more complex stuff requires an extra reach. Reproducing something as complex as food would, IMHO, be harder than say a metal pipe. Perhaps changing it to:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>+2 Reach:</b> The Mage can now use this spell to Replicate complex objects (a car, smartphone, computer) and non-living organic material (food, medicine) as per the previous reach option.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","user":"HTaiji","date":". 01-11-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:41:58-08:00","id":1030049,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't make the Life 4 Option cost any Reach, the triple Adept requirement is high enough and it's not a better option than Teleportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:42:32-08:00","id":1030050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1029976#post1029976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Followup - Would this be Making?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. (Characters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:58:22-08:00","id":1030266,"title":"","content":"The Fate Arcanum section states that Intentions are under its purview. What does this mean exactly? Can I see a characters intentions using a Fate Unveiling spell? Can I hide my own intentions using Fate Veiling? At pattering I can exchange an Aspiration for a new one, does that mean a lower level version could inform me of a characters Aspirations (and could prime probably do the same for obsessions?), extend boons and hexes that can deliberatly mess with Aspirations?<br /> <br /> What about Risk? Risk is an element of chance. Could a Fate Veiling Spell be used to blind someone to potential risks? Compell someone hesitant into action?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:12:02-08:00","id":1030271,"title":"","content":"Intentions I think is less what other people intend and more that Fate spells are more receptive to your intentions when using them. But I could be wrong.<br /> Risk is simply probability. Coin tosses, poker hands, guessing correctly, etc. Not how people think about or react to probabilities. That's Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T18:11:22-08:00","id":1030363,"title":"","content":"In terms of intentions that's definitely what Aspirations are, you have those Aspirations because you intend to act on them. So I think Fate could be used to futz around with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T19:22:50-08:00","id":1030389,"title":"","content":"I would have to disagree with this. Intention and aspiration isn't the same thing. Aspiration is something that you long for, dream to have, try to acquire. Intention is mindfulness, forethought, and premeditation. It isn't assault with the aspiration to commit bodily harm. Aspiration is the goal and intent is the forethought to reach that goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T19:53:55-08:00","id":1030397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030389#post1030389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to disagree with this. Intention and aspiration isn't the same thing. Aspiration is something that you long for, dream to have, try to acquire. Intention is mindfulness, forethought, and premeditation. It isn't assault with the aspiration to commit bodily harm. Aspiration is the goal and intent is the forethought to reach that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations are the game's way of giving the intentions of a character a presence in the mechanics. If you have the Aspiration: Get my homework done. Then in order to gain a Beat your intention is to get your homework done. Mindfulness, forethought and premeditation are methods of accomplishing the thing you intend to do, they are not what intentions are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:47:46-08:00","id":1030447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030397#post1030397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aspirations are the game's way of giving the intentions of a character a presence in the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations are explicitly descibed as a Meta resource. I can have an aspiration for my character to have their S/O die because I want to explore that kind of loss on that character, without my character themselves intending to have their partner die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is also okay to select Aspirations that your character doesn\u2019t want, but that you want to see happen to the char-acter. For example, your character almost certainly doesn\u2019t want to be kidnapped by the man with the gray face that used to be her father, but that might be a story that you are interested in seeing. You can choose Aspirations that repre-sent you trying and failing to do something. You can have an Aspiration like \u201cFail to find proof of the existence of ghosts,\u201d or \u201cFail to reconcile with Jane,\u201d if you think that it will make a more interesting story. Even though the character has failed at what she wants, you as the player still get the reward for completing that Aspiration. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T01:14:49-08:00","id":1030468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030447#post1030447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations are explicitly descibed as a Meta resource. I can have an aspiration for my character to have their S/O die because I want to explore that kind of loss on that character, without my character themselves intending to have their partner die.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In that case Fate probably still would apply, wouldn't it? In sofar as this is an important event with a high likelyhood of happening as decreed by the ooc influences. Not a full blown destiny, but going in the same direction. Regardless my question was mostly about aspirations that a character shares, given that the Acanthus are portrayed as manipulating the path of destiny and choice from the sidelines I think it'd be fitting for them to be able to further or stymie the pursuit of personal goals. An unwanted cause could be made to seem hopeless, unattainable, unbelievably unlikely to ever succeed and impose a penalty along the lines the space spell isolation does for social interactions. Or just be veiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:26:55-08:00","id":1030689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030447#post1030447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspirations are explicitly descibed as a Meta resource. I can have an aspiration for my character to have their S/O die because I want to explore that kind of loss on that character, without my character themselves intending to have their partner die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read CofD the God Machine Chronicle page 177? Because deciding how a story is going tragically end is a special type of Aspiration and that optional rule is called &quot;Fate&quot;. It seems appropriate as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> says. I would say Fate magic would affect that extra plot first if adding fate, or could change an existing one. It might be appropriate to mark aspirations with a (F), (FM), or (M) for Fate ie meta, Fate/Mind ie meta and in game goals, Mind ie in game goal only, to note which Arcanum they fall under and the player's intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-12-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:28:30-08:00","id":1030691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030689#post1030689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read CofD the God Machine Chronicle page 177? Because deciding how a story is going tragically end is a special type of Aspiration and that optional rule is called &quot;Fate&quot;. It seems appropriate as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree Fate would be fitting, I was just addressing the assertion that Aspirations are about the character's intentions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:36:29-08:00","id":1030754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1030691#post1030691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree Fate would be fitting, I was just addressing the assertion that Aspirations are about the character's intentions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree they can be about intentions, but are not necessarily. Philosophical question: What role does intention play in fate? It is definitely related both by the Anglo-Saxon wyrd and destiny as featured in Greek Myth. I'll have to re-read the Arcanum when I get home because there seems to be a fuzzy line between Mind and Fate when it comes to the realm of intentions, based on what you say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-12-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T19:56:18-08:00","id":1035019,"title":"","content":"First edition's Grimoire of Grimoire's had a spell, 'The Metal Dead.' It was 3 Death and 3 Matter, would basically turn a corpse into a skeleton, but the skeleton was made of metal and razor wire, using Durability instead of Health, sort of like a golem, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Because the changing of materials is in Transubstantiation, at 4 dots of Matter, would it now just be 3 Death and 4 Matter? If so, would it still work like a mix of Quicken Corpse and Transubstantiation? With Reaches making a better skeleton servitor, and Potency better metal for potential equipment bonuses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-19-2017, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:00:39-08:00","id":1035020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035019#post1035019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition's Grimoire of Grimoire's had a spell, 'The Metal Dead.' It was 3 Death and 3 Matter, would basically turn a corpse into a skeleton, but the skeleton was made of metal and razor wire, using Durability instead of Health, sort of like a golem, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Because the changing of materials is in Transubstantiation, at 4 dots of Matter, would it now just be 3 Death and 4 Matter? If so, would it still work like a mix of Quicken Corpse and Transubstantiation? With Reaches making a better skeleton servitor, and Potency better metal for potential equipment bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say yes, but you could also argue that Perfecting the corpse to become more resilient is possible, even though it doesn't have the imagery of a metal boned zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:01:29-08:00","id":1035022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035019#post1035019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition's Grimoire of Grimoire's had a spell, 'The Metal Dead.' It was 3 Death and 3 Matter, would basically turn a corpse into a skeleton, but the skeleton was made of metal and razor wire, using Durability instead of Health, sort of like a golem, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Because the changing of materials is in Transubstantiation, at 4 dots of Matter, would it now just be 3 Death and 4 Matter? If so, would it still work like a mix of Quicken Corpse and Transubstantiation? With Reaches making a better skeleton servitor, and Potency better metal for potential equipment bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you can't make the same result with a combined spell of those two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:04:14-08:00","id":1035023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035022#post1035022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing you can't make the same result with a combined spell of those two?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem would be you wouldn't get the sharpened bones aspect, as bones aren't traditionally sharp to begin with, so you would need some Shaping involved too. And whatever is involved in animating a skeleton rather than a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:11:22-08:00","id":1035027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035019#post1035019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition's Grimoire of Grimoire's had a spell, 'The Metal Dead.' It was 3 Death and 3 Matter, would basically turn a corpse into a skeleton, but the skeleton was made of metal and razor wire, using Durability instead of Health, sort of like a golem, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Because the changing of materials is in Transubstantiation, at 4 dots of Matter, would it now just be 3 Death and 4 Matter? If so, would it still work like a mix of Quicken Corpse and Transubstantiation? With Reaches making a better skeleton servitor, and Potency better metal for potential equipment bonuses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd be the same and different, you use Weaving to transpose a (the) property(ies) of metal onto the skeleton. What this wouldn't do is actually make the skeleton out of metal though. It would probably be something basic like: This undead doesn't have Health, it has Structure and Durability and then Reach would add things like sharpened edges that can deal damage, etc on top of the Reach needed to create an undead suitable for combat. Alternatively, a combined casting of Transubstantiation and Quicken Corpse would make it an actually metal skeleton and cost less Reach to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Quicken Corpse for the record should be able to work on a skeleton as well as it does on a regular corpse to make a zombie. I don't see much point trying to make a distinction there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-19-2017, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:22:39-08:00","id":1035031,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, thanks.<br /> <br /> Apologies if this has been asked before, it's a big thread, but talking about this made me wonder.<br /> <br /> How would you create a spell that would spread your zombies? Starting with Quicken Corpse, whenever said zombie killed a living person, make them pop up as a zombie? Would it be doable with just Death? Would the 'second generation' zombies be less powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:54:19-08:00","id":1035044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035031#post1035031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you create a spell that would spread your zombies? Starting with Quicken Corpse, whenever said zombie killed a living person, make them pop up as a zombie? Would it be doable with just Death? Would the 'second generation' zombies be less powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the domain of Dynamics spells and possibly a Scale-based Paradox Reach, pending news on whether any of the carrier spells from Signs of Sorcery allow you to imbue a zombie with the ability to create zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:18:08-08:00","id":1035050,"title":"","content":"Figured the Abyss could do it, but I suppose the answer can wait for Signs of Sorcery. I was thinking maybe if you could make a zombie an imbued item with a trigger of having killed someone, but I'm not very sure about how magic items work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T02:13:04-08:00","id":1035136,"title":"","content":"I'd allow Imbuing a zombie, but only your ground zero zombie would be able to do that and only until it ran out of mana and for its own zombies to be any good or last any length of time would require Zombie 0 to always risk Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:14:46-08:00","id":1035264,"title":"","content":"Think you could link the item with Devouring the Slain, so that once its done Lethal damage it could start harvesting Mana to refill its reservoir?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:23:34-08:00","id":1035268,"title":"","content":"It would just be another triggered Imbuement, so yes.<br /> <br /> The real question is how imbuing entities will work. It might be like Hung Spell where you're only able to suspend a certain number of spells into the matrix of their Pattern and they may not get to choose when or how to use those spells and they might be completely expended when used once. *Shrugs.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T09:24:15-08:00","id":1035269,"title":"","content":"And maybe imbue it with imbuing so it can replicate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T17:41:52-08:00","id":1035907,"title":"","content":"Would a 'Vampiric Touch' spell that Drains Health, doing damage to a target, and gives it to the caster, just be Death 3? Or would you require Life for the healing aspect? Couldn't you manage it somehow to be a drain, like Devouring the Slain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T17:58:42-08:00","id":1035909,"title":"","content":"I think it would be completely a life spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T19:06:06-08:00","id":1035916,"title":"","content":"Add a reach option for Devouring the Slain that allows you to use convert stolen mana into your own health using ratio of Pattern Restoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T00:12:18-08:00","id":1035974,"title":"","content":"Or add a reach to Bruise Flesh (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) allowing you to heal the potency level. I just don't see Death as the healing type, at least not healing the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T02:13:53-08:00","id":1035985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035974#post1035974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or add a reach to Bruise Flesh (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) allowing you to heal the potency level. I just don't see Death as the healing type, at least not healing the body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Healing via Death has been discussed a few times. It tends to come down to table preference.<br /> Fraying the Death out of someone's pattern (removing decay, absence, enervation, endings) is perfectly valid imo.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure a spell that does both fits well into any existing Practices. It should probably just be a Combined Spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T02:34:20-08:00","id":1035991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1035985#post1035985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Healing via Death has been discussed a few times. It tends to come down to table preference.<br /> Fraying the Death out of someone's pattern (removing decay, absence, enervation, endings) is perfectly valid imo.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure a spell that does both fits well into any existing Practices. It should probably just be a Combined Spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Valid point of the Death and healing thing, I hadn't looked at it as removing the decay from their bodies, and in that light it works for me.<br /> <br /> As for the Take and Give Devouring the Slain has already crossed that line, IMHO, so I don't have a problem with it. It could be pushed to a +2 reach if that works better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T02:56:54-08:00","id":1035994,"title":"","content":"Devourering the Slain transfers Willpower and/or Mana from the subject. Is there any kind of life energy that can be transfered that automatically heals you? I do know that Vitae is a life force, but it's not automatically healing. Or is it possible to transfer a wound from one person to another? I'm not sure about that. But it your tables thinks it's possible I'd say the first example requires Life and the second example requires Death.<br /> <br /> The problem with a combined spell is that you're going to cast both spells on the same subject(s). You're going to damage and heal the enemy and/or yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T04:36:37-08:00","id":1036020,"title":"","content":"I haven't seem any example of Empathetic Healing in the spells, I would say that it would be Patterning Magic (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), Transforming wounds closed on one and open on the other. Maybe I am putting to much thought into it and it should just be a reach to a current spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T06:25:54-08:00","id":1036034,"title":"","content":"It could be a Death Weaving spell. You transport a number of wounds equal potency from target to target. If you want it to be Patterning it should transport <i>all </i>wounds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:52:41-08:00","id":1036470,"title":"","content":"<b>Touch of Sacrifice (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Medicine, Politics<br /> The necromancer pushes the shadows of Death looming over someone to another. She may transfer a number of bashing or lethal wounds equal to the spell's Potency from one target to another, both within the spell's Scale. If the mage does not increase the Scale factor, the spell automatically targets herself. When targeting multiple subjects, the mage may divide Potency among them. Any Tilts or Conditions connected to the wounds are also transfered.<br /> Alternatively, the spell may be used to Scour the victim for an equal amount of Mana. This counts towards the daily limit the caster or another mage benefited by the spell may gain Mana from Scouring<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may transfer the wound levels of one target to everyone else within the spell's Scale, divided as he sees fit. Alternatively, he may transfer the wound levels of everyone within the Scale into one target.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to aggravated wounds.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: When used for Scouring, the spell does not count towards the daily limit of Scouring.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to ghosts and their Corpus levels, provided the mage can perceive them. The mage may target Essence in this case, pilfering Essence from one ghost and giving it to another, or stealing Essence from a ghost to heal another ghost or a living creature, or killing a living creature or another ghost to offer Essence to a ghost. She cannot, however, gain Mana by draining the ghost's Essence. Only Scouring the ghost of its Corpus accomplishes that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-23-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:29:48-08:00","id":1036475,"title":"","content":"Its not a direct damage spell so it should have a withstand: Stamina. It should transfer bashing with a reach for lethal. If scouring the damage done is resistant lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:14:36-08:00","id":1036492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036475#post1036475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not a direct damage spell so it should have a withstand: Stamina. It should transfer bashing with a reach for lethal. If scouring the damage done is resistant lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> The Scouring part also seems like a needless tread on Devouring the Slain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:29:45-08:00","id":1036494,"title":"","content":"Good point it doesn't need to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:11:38-08:00","id":1036568,"title":"","content":"Well, all those changes can be arranged for!<br /> <br /> <b>Touch of Sacrifice (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Medicine, Politics<br /> The necromancer pushes the shadows of Death looming over someone to another. She may transfer a number of bashing or lethal wounds equal to the spell's Potency from one target to another, both within the spell's Scale. If the mage does not increase the Scale factor, the spell automatically targets herself. When targeting multiple subjects, the mage may divide Potency among them. Any Tilts or Conditions connected to the wounds are also transfered.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may transfer the wound levels of one target to everyone else within the spell's Scale, divided as he sees fit. Alternatively, he may transfer the wound levels of everyone within the Scale into one target.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to aggravated wounds.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to ghosts and their Corpus levels, provided the mage can perceive them.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also read something in the Beast forums about &quot;Shattered Time&quot; as an Environmental Tilt, apparently modeled after the environment of the Ruins of the Before. Is that a thing represented mechanically? Any ideas on a spell to create that effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:25:24-08:00","id":1036573,"title":"","content":"It should be transfers bashing damage with a reach to allow for lethal. Aggravated shouldn't be in the spell as a reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:07:18-08:00","id":1036595,"title":"","content":"Aggravated as a reach is fine if you consider transferring wounds to be something separate from healing - which on second thought, I would. <br /> This gives the spell a function in a world where you can just heal wounds. Otherwise there's no real reason to ever use this instead of a straight healing spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:27:59-08:00","id":1036605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036573#post1036573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be transfers bashing damage with a reach to allow for lethal. Aggravated shouldn't be in the spell as a reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about with +1 Reach and a point of Mana?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On a tangentially related note, did anyone come up with ways to heal people with the other Arcana too? We have Life for direct healing, Death for sorta-healing-in-a-roundabout-way healing, and Time for &quot;Nope they never existed&quot; healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:34:51-08:00","id":1036609,"title":"","content":"Any command of ephemeral entities with appropriate powers is a pretty obvious route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:44:30-08:00","id":1036616,"title":"","content":"Personally I would say not with a three dot spell. Aggravated damage heal/cause is a reach for a four dot and the cost of one mana is already a requirement, as per the Creative Thaumaturgy rules.<br /> <br /> But that is MHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:01:54-08:00","id":1036627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036616#post1036616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would say not with a three dot spell. Aggravated damage heal/cause is a reach for a four dot and the cost of one mana is already a requirement, as per the Creative Thaumaturgy rules.<br /> <br /> But that is MHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if dealt directly. In this case you are just transporting existing wounds. If it's too strong you can say that it's not lasting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Prime could augment pattern restoration process to get a better mana-health exchange ratio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-23-2017, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T09:40:48-08:00","id":1036682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036627#post1036627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if dealt directly. In this case you are just transporting existing wounds. If it's too strong you can say that it's not lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would not be Lasting by default since it's a magically sustained transfer of wounds from someone that is wounded to someone who may not be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:17:50-08:00","id":1036693,"title":"","content":"I think that too but the line is pretty thin. You can argue both ways. It isn't impossible to sustain without magic so maybe +2Reach and 1 Mana to make it Lasting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:03:26-08:00","id":1036719,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't fly in my game, so any of my players reading 5his, forget it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:25:50-08:00","id":1036731,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> You mean transporting aggravated damage or the whole concept of transporting wounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:43:58-08:00","id":1036743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036719#post1036719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't fly in my game</div> </div> </div> </div>What purpose do you see a spell like this serving vs traditional same-level healing spells if it doesn't work on agg?<br /> <br /> Edit: It could be used to move your own wounds onto an enemy, which would be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:31:45-08:00","id":1036767,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking how cruel it'd be to have as a Hung spell with a conditional Duration for you taking a certain amount of damage. Then you just find someone you don't like and shoot yourself in the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:14:55-08:00","id":1036786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036731#post1036731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> You mean transporting aggravated damage or the whole concept of transporting wounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>The aggravated wounds is my main issue and, I don't mind the Lasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036743#post1036743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What purpose do you see a spell like this serving vs traditional same-level healing spells if it doesn't work on agg?<br /> <br /> Edit: It could be used to move your own wounds onto an enemy, which would be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the benefit that I see. If you have multiple lethal wounds and transfer 1 each to the enemy that isn't hurt than then you just set them up for a Devouring the Slain, or just to dick over the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:18:13-08:00","id":1036828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1036767#post1036767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep thinking how cruel it'd be to have as a Hung spell with a conditional Duration for you taking a certain amount of damage. Then you just find someone you don't like and shoot yourself in the head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool idea. But remember to not kill yourself in the process because the spell won't bring you back I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:16:55-08:00","id":1037441,"title":"","content":"A spell for the Fate Arcanum that is a bit out there.... Not quite sure wether it should be in the Time Arcanum instead (and mind could probably do something very similar aswell).<br /> The concept touched upon here are &quot;consequences&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>No Tomorrow (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Every action, even the tiniest movement, has consequences. This spell renders its subject unable to perceive the long-term consequences of an actions he contemplates taking. For example a man on vacation fails to see the damage an affair could have on his marriage.<br /> <br /> +1 reach: The mage may fabricate a false consequence the subject perceives to be the logical outcome of his actions. Said man might be made to think that having an affair be ultimatly benefical for his marriage.<br /> +2 reach and 1 mana: Short term consequences are hidden aswell. The subject can contemplate the act of jumping from a building, but is unable to perceive what the fall will do to him.<br /> <br /> And another dickish veiling spell.....<br /> <br /> <b>Predetermination (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Intimidation, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> A favourite among Seers that serve Ruin, this spell veils the fact that your own actions matter from the subject. The future seems to be set in stone, no matter what you do it seems impossible for the subject to make a difference. Any attempt the subject makes to further a goal, defined by the mage upon casting the spell, costs 1 Willpower. Even then dicepools are penalized by the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> Normally veiling spells aren't withstood, but since these play havoc with the subjects actions I think a withstand is appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:01:20-08:00","id":1037486,"title":"","content":"For No Tomorrow I'd make the Withstand be Composure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:33:08-08:00","id":1037505,"title":"","content":"Not sure really how relevant or useful this spell is, but I thought it would be fun to share. Came up with it while working on a 2e conversion of Perfected Adepts.<br /> <br /> <b>Bend to the Winds (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Occult, Science<br /> <br /> This spell allows the mage to redirect an aimed Supernal spell or Legacy attainment that is directly targeting her. When a mage could use her Defense against an aimed spell, she may use this spell instead to redirect it as an instant action. If cast with a prolonged Duration, the mage may take a Dodge action each turn and use this spell instead of receiving the normal benefits for Dodging. The spell allows the mage to turn a number of aimed spells directed at her up to this spell\u2019s Potency. She does not have fine control over where each spell is deflected, and the spell cannot make spells reverse direction entirely, only veer off target. By default, the Storyteller determines a random direction for the spell to travel when redirected.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can use Bend to the Winds\u2019 effect as a reflexive action instead<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may control where the spell is redirected to, as long as it is within 90 degrees of the original arc in any direction.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and Add Time \u2022 : </b>The mage can turn spells too fast for her to gain Defense against them.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and Add any Other Arcanum \u2022 : </b>By adding the relevant Arcanum, a mage can turn truly magical effects by other sources of power \u2014 Spirit to turn a Blast Numina, Fate to deflect a Changeling\u2019s Contract, and so on. This would not work against a Werewolf\u2019s claws or car thrown with a Promethean\u2019s prodigious strength.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>The spell is fully reversed and targets their user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:40:13-08:00","id":1037510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1037505#post1037505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure really how relevant or useful this spell is, but I thought it would be fun to share. Came up with it while working on a 2e conversion of Perfected Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it xD<br /> It's a nice alternative to the Counterspell Attainments, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:46:00-08:00","id":1037513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1037441#post1037441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell for the Fate Arcanum that is a bit out there.... Not quite sure wether it should be in the Time Arcanum instead (and mind could probably do something very similar aswell).<br /> The concept touched upon here are &quot;consequences&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>No Tomorrow (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Every action, even the tiniest movement, has consequences. This spell renders its subject unable to perceive the long-term consequences of an actions he contemplates taking. For example a man on vacation fails to see the damage an affair could have on his marriage.<br /> <br /> +1 reach: The mage may fabricate a false consequence the subject perceives to be the logical outcome of his actions. Said man might be made to think that having an affair be ultimatly benefical for his marriage.<br /> +2 reach and 1 mana: Short term consequences are hidden aswell. The subject can contemplate the act of jumping from a building, but is unable to perceive what the fall will do to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>ThisI does look more like a Time spell, and seconding Mrmdubois for making it Withstood by Composure. Maybe a Mind spell that does something similar by Veiling it's victim's logic and rational thoughts would be Withstood by Resolve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And another dickish veiling spell.....<br /> <br /> <b>Predetermination (Fate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstood: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Intimidation, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> A favourite among Seers that serve Ruin, this spell veils the fact that your own actions matter from the subject. The future seems to be set in stone, no matter what you do it seems impossible for the subject to make a difference. Any attempt the subject makes to further a goal, defined by the mage upon casting the spell, costs 1 Willpower. Even then dicepools are penalized by the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> Normally veiling spells aren't withstood, but since these play havoc with the subjects actions I think a withstand is appropriate. </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Willpower cost of the second spell be a +1 Reach effect, but that's just me prefering one effect at a time for spells.<br /> <br /> Great spells, btw. Very evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:39:24-08:00","id":1037549,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10394_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10394\" data-vbnamecard=\"10394\">lladas</a> I'm not sure you should be able to redirect Legacy Attainments, those typically aren't able to be directly interacted with by magic. You counter the effects, not the ability itself. I'm not sure I'm right either though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:49:22-08:00","id":1037558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1037549#post1037549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10394_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10394\" data-vbnamecard=\"10394\">lladas</a> I'm not sure you should be able to redirect Legacy Attainments, those typically aren't able to be directly interacted with by magic. You counter the effects, not the ability itself. I'm not sure I'm right either though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I definitely understand. I guess I was just considering the probability that any given Legacy would have an Attainment that was an aimed effect instead of sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:20:16-08:00","id":1039102,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:25:34-08:00","id":1039107,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:31:28-08:00","id":1039112,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I like it.<br /> <br /> I have to imagine there would be some sort of metaphysical advantage you could tie into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T15:00:25-08:00","id":1039124,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3570_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3570\" data-vbnamecard=\"3570\">lnodiv</a> Keep up the good work! I'm a sucker for new spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:05:30-08:00","id":1039333,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:47:56-08:00","id":1039343,"title":"","content":"I feel like they should have Duration as a primary factor. While Helion Shield looks good with Potency as soak I don't think it has sense for Pyre Ward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most commonly with the Practice of Shielding (\u2022\u2022), a spell<br /> may grant protection from forces under the Arcanum\u2019s purview.<br /> <b>These spells usually provide blanket immunity to natural or<br /> mundane phenomena</b>, <u>while protecting against a number of<br /> supernatural attacks equal to the spell\u2019s Potency</u>. Such attacks<br /> must win a Clash of Wills to affect the target. </div> </div> </div>The underlined part has been proven to be a bygone from early drafts but sadly wasn't corrected. None of the corebook shielding spells abide this Potency rule.<br /> Pyre Ward should provide blanket immunity for fire damage (maybe with a Reach to also block aggravated damage).<br /> <br /> I'm stealing them to my spellbook! If I find time I will translate my own and post them here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:09:55-08:00","id":1039353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1039343#post1039343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like they should have Duration as a primary factor. While Helion Shield looks good with Potency as soak I don't think it has sense for Pyre Ward..</div> </div> </div> </div>Helion Shield was based off of Alchemist's Touch, which uses Potency to shield purely against the harmful effects of something under the Purview of the Arcanum. I think that one should stay as Potency, because it's explicitly not providing blanket immunity to the phenomena in question, as described under Shielding.<br /> <br /> Pyre Ward was honestly just copied from Helion Shield, but in hindsight I think you're right - it works better as a more traditional shielding spell that provides blanket immunity, with Duration as the Primary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:42:46-08:00","id":1039366,"title":"","content":"So here is a spell of one of my players. It might look like a Weaving but I figured that you can go away with Rulling if it's done with 'Potency bursts'<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hand of Benediction</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Space \u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Subterfuge, Athletics, Medicine</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell allows caster to interact physically on a simple basis (e.g. Touch) within sensory range. Number of possible interactions equals potency, while the spell is active. Everything the caster touches or works with have it's full effect on her, e.g. interacting with a flame causes burns and blisters, as if it was touched. Touching a moving object requires usual test (dexterity + athletics/brawl/firearms).</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Subject of the spell may perform more complicated tasks, like fixing a mechanism or writing on a keyboard.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Subject of the spell may perform extended mundane tasks, each interval counting towards the total number of interactions granted by potency.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach and 1 Mana:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tasks may be done remotely. (e.g. through Scrying spell)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:52:43-08:00","id":1039368,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T05:12:58-08:00","id":1039374,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If we're talking about interaction with places.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ariadne</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Prime \u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Compeling</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The travelling willworker uncoils behind a thread that allows to find a way back in even the harshest of conditions. The thread can only be seen with AMS but tests to find it are not penalized by Environmental Tilts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach</b>: Irises can't be closed entirely if the thread was guided through them. They allways leave a mark that can be later reopened with apropriate Arcanum and spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> It's visible even without AMS</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-28-2017, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T09:41:24-08:00","id":1039462,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And another one, for those that like to talk while in combat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anime Combat Conversation</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022) </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perfecting </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every Subject of this spell can communicate (say and hear) through elaborate speeches as a reflexive action. Each of this reflexive actions may contain a number of simple sentences equal to potency of the spell.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Reach and 1 mana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Subject of the spell may, instead of speaking sentences, use High Speech Yantra as a reflexive action, even if it is not primary yantra.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach and 1 mana: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As above, but subject may use High Speech Yantra instead of speaking one of the sentences.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Space \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Multiply distance at which characters can communicate by Potency. This does not allow for talking through obstacles.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"