yle=\"font-family:Arial\">+</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1 Reach and 1 mana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Subject of the spell may, instead of speaking sentences, use High Speech Yantra as a reflexive action, even if it is not primary yantra.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach and 1 mana: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As above, but subject may use High Speech Yantra instead of speaking one of the sentences.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Space \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Multiply distance at which characters can communicate by Potency. This does not allow for talking through obstacles.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely fantastic and I can clearly imagine the circumstances that might have made it necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T11:38:21-08:00","id":1039529,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T00:48:53-08:00","id":1040484,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:14:14-08:00","id":1040775,"title":"","content":"Nice, I like the Death spells. I need more Matter and observable Time stuff, though.<br /> <br /> Could you create an Earthquake, or at least the Earthquake Tilt, with Matter? Nevermind, I see that with Shaping. And Forces 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:20:41-08:00","id":1040778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040775#post1040775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice, I like the Death spells. I need more Matter and observable Time stuff, though.<br /> <br /> Could you create an Earthquake, or at least the Earthquake Tilt, with Matter? Nevermind, I see that with Shaping. And Forces 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:26:41-08:00","id":1040780,"title":"","content":"Not sure if the metaphysics of fetishes allow for them to be ghosts. First edition had ghost-touched items, but they weren't exactly like fetishes. And they had specific rules that made them different from fetishes.<br /> <br /> If you're going to argue that 'if spirit can do it with spirits, death can do it with ghosts' can you make human and animal fetishes with Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:37:47-08:00","id":1040787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040780#post1040780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if the metaphysics of fetishes allow for them to be ghosts. First edition had ghost-touched items, but they weren't exactly like fetishes. And they had specific rules that made them different from fetishes.<br /> <br /> If you're going to argue that 'if spirit can do it with spirits, death can do it with ghosts' can you make human and animal fetishes with Life?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whoa. I just thought of Life 4 'prison' spell that changes target into living brick sized body. Imagine this low maintanance, warm but otherwise harmless pieces of meat in a skin organized neatly on shelves of some GotV dungeon. If you listen closely the hearts are still beating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:41:49-08:00","id":1040793,"title":"","content":"Typically you don't need to turn a ghost into a fetish since it's already intrinsically linked to an item (Or place or person) which serves as its anchor. For those ghosts not anchored to something convenient Revenant is the spell that could be used to create a ghost &quot;fetish.&quot;<br /> <br /> As to living fetishes, animals and humans would be Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:45:47-08:00","id":1040796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040793#post1040793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to living fetishes, animals and humans would be Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting a human or mage inside a wand wouldn't make a Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:46:15-08:00","id":1040797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040780#post1040780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if the metaphysics of fetishes allow for them to be ghosts. First edition had ghost-touched items, but they weren't exactly like fetishes. And they had specific rules that made them different from fetishes.<br /> <br /> If you're going to argue that 'if spirit can do it with spirits, death can do it with ghosts' can you make human and animal fetishes with Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans and animals don't follow the same metaphysical template that Spirits do - you're comparing apples to chainsaws there. A better question would be: &quot;can you make Angel fetishes with Prime and Fate&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar enough with how fetishes work to give you an answer. My understanding of them begins and ends with the spell in Mage, I've played werewolf but not enough to be familiar, and I wouldn't expect a Spirit focused game like werewolf to touch on Death Fetishes anyway.<br /> <br /> The question I'd counter with is: Can ghosts be bound into items, and if so, given that 2E has altered the framework Ephemeral Entities use to be identical across ephemeral beings, is it reasonable to treat items ghosts are bound into in the edition identically, mechanically, as a spirit Fetish? If you find yourself answering that question with &quot;No,&quot; then I'd discard that copy-over as an invalid spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:56:01-08:00","id":1040802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040797#post1040797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans and animals don't follow the same metaphysical template that Spirits do - you're comparing apples to chainsaws there. A better question would be: &quot;can you make Angel fetishes with Prime and Fate&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts and spirits have differences as well, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not familiar enough with how fetishes work to give you an answer. My understanding of them begins and ends with the spell in Mage, I've played werewolf but not enough to be familiar, and I wouldn't expect a Spirit focused game like werewolf to touch on Death Fetishes anyway. </div> </div> </div>They do but that's not on topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question I'd counter with is: Can ghosts be bound into items, and if so, given that 2E has altered the framework Ephemeral Entities use to be identical across ephemeral beings, is it reasonable to treat items ghosts are bound into in the edition identically, mechanically, as a spirit Fetish? </div> </div> </div>While the mechanics to make them are similar, they are not the same. Anchors, their capabilities and where and what they're made from are all different.<br /> <br /> That said, it does seem like Death could easily bind a ghost into an object and allow the possessor to use its Numina and Influences without calling it a fetish. More of a ghost box, I suppose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:57:28-08:00","id":1040803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040802#post1040802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it does seem like Death could easily bind a ghost into an object and allow the possessor to use its Numina and Influences without calling it a fetish. More of a ghost box, I suppose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but then you lose the punny name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T12:05:09-08:00","id":1040804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040803#post1040803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but then you lose the punny name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ghost fetish and ghost box are both doable in that regard.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:06:43-08:00","id":1040881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040796#post1040796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Putting a human or mage inside a wand wouldn't make a Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I misunderstood the question. The answer is no then, you can't make a living organism into a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:42:00-08:00","id":1042004,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T10:57:35-08:00","id":1043037,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:23:25-08:00","id":1043057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1043037#post1043037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New one, based off of Shadow Crafting:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sunstone</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Weaving</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Occult, Science</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Disciple of Forces can shape and harden sunlight into solid, three-dimensional forms. Sunstone has Durability 2, and a Weapon Rating/General Armor Rating/Equipment Bonus of 2. Sunstone reflects all forms of light incredibly brightly, appearing to radiate in even dimly lit rooms, but does not actually emit light on its own and provides no illumination. Sunstone counts as real sunlight for all purposes.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The caster may create a sunstone out of any form of light. This functions as described above, including counting as real sunlight.</span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:15:59-08:00","id":1043112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1043057#post1043057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just gotta be careful not to piss of the kindred. Maybe the ST can decide whether it counts for sunlight damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 02-03-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:29:38-08:00","id":1043118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1043037#post1043037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New one, based off of Shadow Crafting:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sunstone</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Weaving</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#E69138\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Occult, Science</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Disciple of Forces can shape and harden sunlight into solid, three-dimensional forms. Sunstone has Durability 2, and a Weapon Rating/General Armor Rating/Equipment Bonus of 2. Sunstone reflects all forms of light incredibly brightly, appearing to radiate in even dimly lit rooms, but does not actually emit light on its own and provides no illumination. Sunstone counts as real sunlight for all purposes.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The caster may create a sunstone out of any form of light. This functions as described above, including counting as real sunlight.</span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would love an option to add Prime 3 (Platonic Ideal) and/orDeath 3 (Shadow Crafting) and see what do you think should happen when you combine these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T13:48:46-08:00","id":1043132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1043112#post1043112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just gotta be careful not to piss of the kindred. Maybe the ST can decide whether it counts for sunlight damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually made for my heavy mage/vampire crossover for the explicit purpose of doing sunlight damage. <br /> <br /> In our game, any turn a vampire is struck by a Sunstone weapon is meant to count as a turn of exposure to sunlight, but it doesn't modify the actual weapon damage (the strike itself will still do bashing to Kindred). A less finicky way to handle it would be to treat the damage type as whatever the Kindred in question would normally experience from sunlight exposure, but this quickly outclasses the intended lethality if you have multiple foes armed with these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1043118#post1043118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would love an option to add Prime 3 (Platonic Ideal) and/orDeath 3 (Shadow Crafting) and see what do you think should happen when you combine these.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking of a combo with Shadow Crafting already, will have to consider options for Prime as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T14:13:47-08:00","id":1044716,"title":"","content":"Trying to update the Corpse Flesh spell (from the Adamantine Arrow book) from 1e to 2e, how'd I do?<br /> <br /> Corpse Flesh (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Medicine, Occult<br /> The Mage alters a physical living body, introducing many side effects of physiological Death such as the cessation of breathing and blood flow, without deleterious effects. For the duration of the spell, the subject:<ul><li>Does not suffer wound penalties</li> <li>Does not need to breathe, eat, sleep, or perform any other physical act required for the proper healthy maintenance of life</li> <li>Does not suffer from personal tilts except for those caused by Aggravated Damage</li> <li>Does not need to test to remain conscious if their Health Track is filled with damage</li> <li>Does not suffer additional damage from a lack of medical attention if their Health Track is filled with lethal damage</li> <li>May reattach severed or damaged limbs or organs with Death or Life Weaving spells</li> <li>May be affected by any spell which affects either Living or Dead targets</li> </ul><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Pushing now \u201cdead\u201d muscles well beyond safe operation, the subject increases their Strength by the spell\u2019s Potency. If combined with the Reach option below, divide Potency between the two as you see if.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Drawing upon the legendary durability of the undead, the subject increases their Stamina by the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:34:27-08:00","id":1044748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044716#post1044716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to update the Corpse Flesh spell (from the Adamantine Arrow book) from 1e to 2e, how'd I do?<br /> <br /> Corpse Flesh (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Medicine, Occult<br /> The Mage alters a physical living body, introducing many side effects of physiological Death such as the cessation of breathing and blood flow, without deleterious effects. For the duration of the spell, the subject:<ul><li>Does not suffer wound penalties</li> <li>Does not need to breathe, eat, sleep, or perform any other physical act required for the proper healthy maintenance of life</li> <li>Does not suffer from personal tilts except for those caused by Aggravated Damage</li> <li>Does not need to test to remain conscious if their Health Track is filled with damage</li> <li>Does not suffer additional damage from a lack of medical attention if their Health Track is filled with lethal damage</li> <li>May reattach severed or damaged limbs or organs with Death or Life Weaving spells</li> <li>May be affected by any spell which affects either Living or Dead targets</li> </ul><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Pushing now \u201cdead\u201d muscles well beyond safe operation, the subject increases their Strength by the spell\u2019s Potency. If combined with the Reach option below, divide Potency between the two as you see if.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Drawing upon the legendary durability of the undead, the subject increases their Stamina by the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this could be a Death 3 spell, what with added Arcana being largely done away with in 2e. In fact, here's my take on it:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Undead Endurance (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Medicine, Occult, Athletics<br /> The necromancer infuses a living body with entropic energies, making it resistant against damage much like the undead. The subject downgrades all lethal damage from kinetic sources to bashing for a number of attacks equal to Potency. The subject also does not need roll to stay conscious from damage, and does not bleed out when his Health is filled with lethal damage.<br /> Also, the subject's biological functions are held in stasis. He does not need to breathe, eat, or sleep, and does not age. However, this means that he does not heal naturally, and time spent under this spell's effects do not count towards resolving physical Conditions.<br /> Lastly, any Death spell designed to affect corpses, and similar supernatural powers affect the subject normally. If those powers are non-Lasting, they wear off automatically once the spell expires.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell also downgrades all aggravated damage from kinetic sources to lethal, for a number of attacks equal to Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject does not suffer wound penalties, and Personal Tilts caused by non-aggravated damage.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject's wounds and physical Conditions heal naturally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell grants the subject one dot of Strength or Stamina per Potency, divided as the mage sees fit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:45:55-08:00","id":1044770,"title":"","content":"Guess what I've been looking up lately.<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Air (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Weaponry, Science, Larceny<br /> The thaumaturge gathers wind and light around a melee weapon, replacing its true form with a hazy figure. The weapon's exact reach is concealed, imposing a Defense penalty equal to Potency on all opponents attempting to engage with its wielder. This advantage does not apply to opponents who do not rely on sight in combat.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The melee weapon pulses with powerful wind and light, allowing its wielder to apply the Knocked Down Tilt for a number of attacks equal to Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The sheathe of wind expands to a shield of air, repelling harmful gases and projectiles slow enough for the wielder to apply Defense against.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The wind boosts movement, granting a bonus equal to Potency on Dodge rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Cursed Wounds (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>:<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Weaponry, Occult, Medicine<br /> The necromancer coats a weapon with venom of Death. For a number of attacks equal to Potency, wounds inflicted by the enchanted weapon are unable to be healed by natural healing or mundane medical attention. This includes any wound penalties, Personal Tilts, or Condtions tied to the wound. Supernatural healing works normally.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The wound resists even magical healing, provoking a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The weapon, in lieu of wounds that do not heal, inflicts the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036467#post1036467\">Agony Tilt </a>instantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:19:22-08:00","id":1044799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044770#post1044770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess what I've been looking up lately.<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Air (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Weaponry, Science, Larceny<br /> The thaumaturge gathers wind and light around a melee weapon, replacing its true form with a hazy figure. The weapon's exact reach is concealed, imposing a Defense penalty equal to Potency on all opponents attempting to engage with its wielder. This advantage does not apply to opponents who do not rely on sight in combat.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The melee weapon pulses with powerful wind and light, allowing its wielder to apply the Knocked Down Tilt for a number of attacks equal to Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The sheathe of wind expands to a shield of air, repelling harmful gases and projectiles slow enough for the wielder to apply Defense against.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The wind boosts movement, granting a bonus equal to Potency on Dodge rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Forces controls weather, but I don't know if &quot;wind&quot; counts? Like, on a macro-scale I'd say yes, absolutely, but on such a precise level I'd be inclined to say it should've Matter. That's just my opinion though, I don't know what general consensus is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T01:06:47-08:00","id":1044954,"title":"","content":"I think that just light manipulation is enough for the Invisible Air.<br /> <br /> If I want to make a statement of Truth burn like fire, should it be a Prime 3 Forces 3 spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:22:07-08:00","id":1044988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044954#post1044954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to make a statement of Truth burn like fire, should it be a Prime 3 Forces 3 spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it does damage then I'd say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:41:02-08:00","id":1044991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044799#post1044799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Forces controls weather, but I don't know if &quot;wind&quot; counts? Like, on a macro-scale I'd say yes, absolutely, but on such a precise level I'd be inclined to say it should've Matter. That's just my opinion though, I don't know what general consensus is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wind is just a fast moving air, so when Forces are all about movement and energies it should be totally fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044954#post1044954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that just light manipulation is enough for the Invisible Air.<br /> <br /> If I want to make a statement of Truth burn like fire, should it be a Prime 3 Forces 3 spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime should be enough, to burn &quot;like&quot; fire, mana can burn just fine so maybe add some reach to resemble fire. But if you wan't to burn with fire... Forces 3 or 4 and perhaps Prime 4 to just Pattern Truth into Fire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:45:56-08:00","id":1044992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044991#post1044991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wind is just a fast moving air, so when Forces are all about movement and energies it should be totally fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then use telekinetic energy, air falls under Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:59:49-08:00","id":1044994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044992#post1044992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then use telekinetic energy, air falls under Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's like saying that you can't slow down a truck because it falls under Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:00:56-08:00","id":1044995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044994#post1044994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like saying that you can't slow down a truck because it falls under Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is, but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:32:09-08:00","id":1045001,"title":"","content":"Well, I mostly had it Forces just for flavor. Matter works just as fine.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Noble Phantasms...<br /> <br /> <b>Knight of the Willow Branch (Prime </b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022)<br /> Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Weaponry, Brawl, Survival<br /> The theurgist unlocks the hidden potential of violence hidden within everyday objects. When the spell's subject is used as an improvised weapon by the caster, she does not suffer the -1 penalty when attacking, and the weapon does not take damage upon successful attacks. Also, she subtracts Potency from the object's Size for the purpose of determining its Initiative penalty and Strength requirement.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Potency is added to the improvised weapon's damage rating.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Attacks made with the weapon are considered supernatural, for creatures vulnerable to such distinctions.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: People other than the mage can wield the object as an improvised weapon, with all the attendant benefits.<br /> <br /> It's difficult trying to convert the Noble Phantasms into Mage spells, thanks to the different mechanisms in their magics, and how a lot of them are basically hand-held WMDs whose function defaults to &quot;blast.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:37:16-08:00","id":1045003,"title":"","content":"Swallow Cutting(Space 3)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Weaponry, Subterfuge, Brawl<br /> By making the subjects's attacks come from multiple angle, the enemy finds it harder to defend and attack. For the Duration of the spell, any attacks made by the subject inflicts Potency penalty to the opponent's Defense <i>before</i> the attack was made and last for a turn, while the subject ignores Potency penalties to her Defense. This can only effect melee attacks.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell can now effect ranged attacks.<br /> Add Time 3: By spending one Reach she can short burst fire with her melee attacks(or with normally incapable ranged weapons with the above Reach), with another Reach she can medium burst, with one more Reach she can long burst.<br /> <br /> Samurais <i>and </i>Jojo, in my Mastigos? it's more likely than you think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11724,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","user":"backtoback","date":". 02-07-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:30:31-08:00","id":1045025,"title":"","content":"One more...<br /> <br /> Heretical Law(Prime 5)<br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstood by: Rank<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Intimidation, Expression<br /> The mage inflicts blasphemy towards the Supernal by destroying it's being's connection to it. For the Duration of this spell, any Supernal beings effected by this spell suffer the following effects.<br /> *Are always considered to be outside of the summoning circle<br /> *Suffer additional Corpus damage equal to Potency above it's rank for every 30 minutes<br /> *When it 'dies' from anything other than taking damage from Paradox, which will be taken by the Abyss as normal, it's 'body' will remain in the Fallen World for as long as the spell's Duration. When the spell ends, the body is then instantly taken to the Abyss.<br /> +If this spell is inflicted in an area, then any attempt at Supernal summoning will fail and will instead summon an Abyssal being<br /> <br /> Needless to say this spell is a sin towards Falling Wisdom most of the time<br /> <br /> I had the idea for this spell to also supress an Ochemata's Travel All Realm, Take Any Shape, and Supernal Perfection trait, but since we don't have rles for them in 2e yet and I don't know if that's way too OP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11724,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","user":"backtoback","date":". 02-07-2017, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:46:03-08:00","id":1045053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1045001#post1045001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mostly had it Forces just for flavor. Matter works just as fine.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Noble Phantasms...<br /> <br /> <b>Knight of the Willow Branch (Prime </b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022)<br /> Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Weaponry, Brawl, Survival<br /> The theurgist unlocks the hidden potential of violence hidden within everyday objects. When the spell's subject is used as an improvised weapon by the caster, she does not suffer the -1 penalty when attacking, and the weapon does not take damage upon successful attacks. Also, she subtracts Potency from the object's Size for the purpose of determining its Initiative penalty and Strength requirement.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Potency is added to the improvised weapon's damage rating.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Attacks made with the weapon are considered supernatural, for creatures vulnerable to such distinctions.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: People other than the mage can wield the object as an improvised weapon, with all the attendant benefits.<br /> <br /> It's difficult trying to convert the Noble Phantasms into Mage spells, thanks to the different mechanisms in their magics, and how a lot of them are basically hand-held WMDs whose function defaults to &quot;blast.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This spell should be Matter, the second Reach clause should simply be, Add Prime 3, and the third Reach clause is unnecessary, you're changing the object not the wielder so the benefits would append to whomever used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:11:15-08:00","id":1045192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1044992#post1044992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then use telekinetic energy, air falls under Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Telekinetic energy&quot; isn't a thing. You invoke control over wind to influence air and movement. The difference between directly controlling wind and controlling wind by controlling the forces that move air around is completely academic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:15:45-08:00","id":1045196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1045192#post1045192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Telekinetic energy&amp;quot; isn't a thing. You invoke control over wind to influence air and movement. The difference between directly controlling wind and controlling wind by controlling the forces that move air around is completely academic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what does the Telekinesis spell do? Fair point on the rest though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:21:36-08:00","id":1045202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1045196#post1045196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what does the Telekinesis spell do?</div> </div> </div> </div>It alters the forces already acting on a subject to move it around. None of those forces are &quot;telekinetic energy&quot; in any meaningful sense, because the only sense in which those words mean anything is &quot;energy that is being used to do telekinesis.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:19:36-08:00","id":1045458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1045053#post1045053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This spell should be Matter, the second Reach clause should simply be, Add Prime 3, and the third Reach clause is unnecessary, you're changing the object not the wielder so the benefits would append to whomever used it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this, huh?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Knight of the Willow Branch (Matter </b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022)<br /> Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Weaponry, Brawl, Survival<br /> The theurgist unlocks the hidden potential of violence hidden within everyday objects. When the spell's subject is used as an improvised weapon by the caster, she does not suffer the -1 penalty when attacking, and the weapon does not take damage upon successful attacks. Also, she subtracts Potency from the object's Size for the purpose of determining its Initiative penalty and Strength requirement.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Potency is added to the improvised weapon's damage rating.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022</b><b>\u2022</b><b>\u2022</b>: Attacks made with the weapon are considered supernatural, for creatures vulnerable to such distinctions.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:20:51-08:00","id":1048757,"title":"","content":"Here are some Time Spells.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dwHr5L9-hPF537Mx9LlwsRds3e5wOGlaevxI80aUcM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Updated and polished the spells with the help of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T05:37:18-08:00","id":1050443,"title":"","content":"Something on another thread made me want to give this a shot.<br /> <br /> <b>Stuck on You (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving (<i>or should it be Patterning?</i>)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration (<i>or Potency? not sure about this, either</i>)<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> This spell requires at least two subjects who have some sympathetic connection to each other. This connection becomes a kind of tether--albeit an intangible and imperceptible one--making it impossible for the subjects to move any further from each other than they were at the time of the casting. Any attempt to move beyond that distance by either party turns into a tug-of-war, with the winner pulling the loser along as she goes.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The tether grows shorter if the subjects move toward each other.<br /> <br /> Pity the person standing next to a car, connected to the driver by this spell. Come to think of it, the driver would have a pretty bad day, too.<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm fairly new to this creative thaumaturgy thing. Feedback would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","user":"Fortunatus","date":". 02-17-2017, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T06:19:46-08:00","id":1050454,"title":"","content":"Feels like a Patterning Spell, not a Weaving.<br /> <br /> Perfecting the distance between subject may achieve the same result without the sympathetic link rider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-17-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T06:53:37-08:00","id":1050468,"title":"","content":"<b>Detect Machine (Matter \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Complexity<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Investigation, Science<br /> This spell can reveal a hidden mechanism, such as a hidden lock or a hidden mechanical trap in the area. The subject inspects the area that he suspects has a trap in it and for the duration of the spell he can detect the trap and how it is triggered. The complexity of the mechanism is used as withstand for the spell, as listed below. If the mechanism is magically hidden this will trigger a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Complexity:</b><br /> <b>Easy:</b> 1<br /> <b>Uncommon:</b> 2<br /> <b>Difficult:</b> 3<br /> <b>Hard:</b> 4<br /> <b>Near Impossible:</b> 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-17-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:18:08-08:00","id":1050477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1050468#post1050468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Detect Machine (Matter \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Complexity<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Investigation, Science<br /> This spell can reveal a hidden mechanism, such as a hidden lock or a hidden mechanical trap in the area. The subject inspects the area that he suspects has a trap in it and for the duration of the spell he can detect the trap and how it is triggered. The complexity of the mechanism is used as withstand for the spell, as listed below. If the mechanism is magically hidden this will trigger a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say in the description &quot;complexity as listed below&quot; and then don't list complexity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:38:55-08:00","id":1050487,"title":"","content":"OOPS sorry forgot that part. It is added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:45:37-08:00","id":1050493,"title":"","content":"not really familiar with Mage, but are there any existing covert spells that could keep sound being made in one room of a house from being heard in another room? Basically, magical impenetrable sound-proofing. And if not, what Arcanum do you think would be appropriate? I'm thinking Forces 3, but perhaps some Matter also if you want it to be an inherent property of the material when you're constructing the walls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:59:21-08:00","id":1050499,"title":"","content":"Forces 2 ought to do the trick. I think there is a Spell &quot;Control Sound&quot; in the book that can serve this purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:20:59-08:00","id":1050512,"title":"","content":"how much Matter would I need to imbue the wall material with that property while i was creating it? For example, by adding ritual ingredients while mixing concrete or varnish or using consecrated tools while turning a log into wood planks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:27:51-08:00","id":1050541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1050512#post1050512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much Matter would I need to imbue the wall material with that property while i was creating it? For example, by adding ritual ingredients while mixing concrete or varnish or using consecrated tools while turning a log into wood planks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creative Thaumaturgy variant of Wondrous Machine: Wall, meet sound absorbing foam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T09:34:52-08:00","id":1050544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1050541#post1050541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creative Thaumaturgy variant of Wondrous Machine: Wall, meet sound absorbing foam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T17:01:54-08:00","id":1051753,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Slightly altered the original post, and added another spell.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Another edit to the second spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rashomon Effect (Mind \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Subterfuge, Investigation, Persuasion<br /> The human mind and memories are not infallible as many believe, and are subject to distorting events in their own perspectives and self-interests. Those who witness the subject within the spell's Duration will remember a highly subjective version of it, giving different accounts to anyone who should come asking. Using supernatural means of observation or memory-reading provokes a Clash of Wills. Mage Sight always reveal the truth without a Clash.<br /> While this spell does not befuddle supernatural events caused by or transpired around the subject, most people already have flimsy memories regarding such matters.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to supernatural witnesses. One may remember the man across the street spontaneously bursting into flame, while another may remember the same man attacked with a molotov cocktail.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell provokes a Clash of Wills against Mage Sight, and on success befuddles even the Awakened senses. Supernatural phenomena appear to belong to unrelated Arcana, and Nimbuses are likewise confused for someone else's or an entirely made-up one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Subtle Occlusion </b><b>(Mind \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Cost</b>: One Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Occult, Subterfuge, Stealth<br /> The psychonaut may veil a subject under a psychic shroud, away from prodding eyes and meddlesome influences. The subject of the spell is granted dots in the Occultation Merit equal to Potency, even if he is not Awakened. If the subject is a mage who already has the Merit, her rating in it is increased by Potency. In both cases, the Occultation Merit's rating may be raised up to five dots, exceeding its normal limit. If the subject has the Fame Merit, its effects are suppressed until the spell expires. <b>+1 Reach</b>: By spending one point of Mana, The Occultation Merit may be raised above five dots, as much as Potency allows it.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b>: By spending one point of Mana, the mage may make his non-Awakened subjects elligible for purchasing the Occultation Merit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 02-19-2017, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:05:00-08:00","id":1051869,"title":"","content":"Is Clash of Wills something that the participants know to be happening?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T00:34:45-08:00","id":1051887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1051869#post1051869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Clash of Wills something that the participants know to be happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes (characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:21:23-08:00","id":1051969,"title":"","content":"So wouldn't they know something is up even if they fail it then?","signatur