y":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:55:24-08:00","id":1051983,"title":"","content":"Is that the same for anyone going into a clash of wills? Even Changelings, Psychics, Vampires, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:05:37-08:00","id":1051990,"title":"","content":"I can't talk knowledgeably about the other systems but I would hazard to say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T09:29:35-08:00","id":1052032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1051983#post1051983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the same for anyone going into a clash of wills? Even Changelings, Psychics, Vampires, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages always count as aware of the occurrence of a Clash with one of their spells (and a lot of other stuff, courtesy of Peripheral Mage Sight), but generally speaking other monsters need to have some means of knowing there's a magical effect attempting to interfere with one of their powers to be able to spend Willpower on a Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T10:45:19-08:00","id":1052053,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> So, this is more of a Creative Thaumaturgy question versus an actual spell created using the process. I have an NPC Mage that is an Adept using Death in my campaign and I was trying to equip them with some interesting custom spells and I felt myself hitting a road block with the capabilities of the upper tier.<br /> <br /> From the Core Rulebook it says the following about Patterning:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition pg. 124</b><br /> Patterning spells allow a mage to completely transform a target into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s purview. A memory can be replaced wholesale (Mind), the mage can turn herself (or a target) into an animal (Life), or she can teleport by \u201crewriting\u201d her own location (Space). A spell that transforms the target into something that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces), requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the destination Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>Death covers the following based on the Core Rulebook<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition pg. 128</b><br /> Purview: Darkness, decay, ectoplasm, ghosts, the Underworld, souls, cold, absence, enervation, endings. </div> </div> </div>So, this to me says that with Patterning, I could perhaps turn a ghost into a soul? Would this be possible? It is within the arcanum's purview and I am changing it to another item in the purview. I realize that Archmastery is where the creation of a soul happened in 1E, but if we are to use the Practices as a much better guideline in 2E it seems that this could be interpreted in this way. Maybe the Patterned Soul would just be a temporary replacement, but it is not a full on soul but rather something acting as one on the most basic level and thus does not have all the extensive properties of a true soul. Perhaps you can lose the Soulless/Enervated/Thrall Conditions with it in place, but you don't start gaining willpower/gnosis as you would with a normal soul. It is also of course subject to Dispelling.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:45:28-08:00","id":1052074,"title":"","content":"And if you don't spend the Willpower, you automatically lose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:01:43-08:00","id":1052084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052074#post1052074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you don't spend the Willpower, you automatically lose?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Willpower spent on a Clash of Wills grants +2 dice. You still get to roll your normal Clash of Wills dice to resist a power even if you don't know what's going on (and therefore don't have an opportunity to spend willpower).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:46:52-08:00","id":1052119,"title":"","content":"Spending a point of Willpower grants +3 dice on rolls, including Clash of Wills. You might be thinking about resisted actions and Withstand. In those cases a point of Willpower will grant +2 to an attribute for the sake of that roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:06:14-08:00","id":1052132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052053#post1052053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> So, this to me says that with Patterning, I could perhaps turn a ghost into a soul? Would this be possible? It is within the arcanum's purview and I am changing it to another item in the purview. I realize that Archmastery is where the creation of a soul happened in 1E, but if we are to use the Practices as a much better guideline in 2E it seems that this could be interpreted in this way. Maybe the Patterned Soul would just be a temporary replacement, but it is not a full on soul but rather something acting as one on the most basic level and thus does not have all the extensive properties of a true soul. Perhaps you can lose the Soulless/Enervated/Thrall Conditions with it in place, but you don't start gaining willpower/gnosis as you would with a normal soul. It is also of course subject to Dispelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like a pacemaker sort of thing, but for the soul. <br /> <br /> So far as I can tell, there is no making souls in 2E, but Death creating a similar thing to keep a person in an equilibrium of sorts (suppress the Soulless series of conditions for the Duration) sounds perfectly within Death's domain.<br /> <br /> Of course, this being Patterning, you can't just create this new thing. A ghost will do nicely. I would suggest a Wisdom breaking point for this.<br /> <br /> Because at some point, that ghost will revert back from being a Soulpacemaker. And what was that about being Soulless? -2 to posession? Hmm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <b>Echo to Echo</b> (<b>Death</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Resistance<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Occult, Medicine, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By means of this spell the Mage transforms a ghost - the echo of a person - into a Soul Echo. The Soul Echo behaves like a pale imitation of a soul, allowing it to be attached to a person whose soul had been removed, in order to mitigate the seriousness of their situation.<br /> Like a regular soul, it can only be attached to people without a soul - under the Soulless, Enervated, or Thrall Conditions. Attaching the Soul Echo to a person without a soul does not resolve the Soulless, Enervated, nor Thrall Conditions, rather, the person gains the Almost Souled persistent Condition. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Almost Souled</b><br /> <b>(Persistent)</b><br /> The character has been implanted with a Soul Echo, halting their degradation from the lack of a soul. She does not regain Willpower from acting according to her Virtue or Vice.<br /> The Soul Echo functions as a soul replacement, and the character cannot regain her soul while under this Condition.<br /> Soulless, Enervated, and Thrall Conditions are suppressed while the character is under the Almost Souled Condition.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Lose the Soul Echo <br /> <b>Beat</b>: Lose Wisdom or Integrity in a scene where you regain Willpower through surrender.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How's that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:48:46-08:00","id":1052167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cool idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like a pacemaker sort of thing, but for the soul. <br /> <br /> So far as I can tell, there is no making souls in 2E, but Death creating a similar thing to keep a person in an equilibrium of sorts (suppress the Soulless series of conditions for the Duration) sounds perfectly within Death's domain.<br /> <br /> Of course, this being Patterning, you can't just create this new thing. A ghost will do nicely. I would suggest a Wisdom breaking point for this.<br /> <br /> Because at some point, that ghost will revert back from being a Soulpacemaker. And what was that about being Soulless? -2 to posession? Hmm <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <b>Echo to Echo</b> (<b>Death</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Resistance<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Occult, Medicine, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By means of this spell the Mage transforms a ghost - the echo of a person - into a Soul Echo. The Soul Echo behaves like a pale imitation of a soul, allowing it to be attached to a person whose soul had been removed, in order to mitigate the seriousness of their situation.<br /> Like a regular soul, it can only be attached to people without a soul - under the Soulless, Enervated, or Thrall Conditions. Attaching the Soul Echo to a person without a soul does not resolve the Soulless, Enervated, nor Thrall Conditions, rather, the person gains the Almost Souled persistent Condition. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Almost Souled</b><br /> <b>(Persistent)</b><br /> The character has been implanted with a Soul Echo, halting their degradation from the lack of a soul. She does not regain Willpower from acting according to her Virtue or Vice.<br /> The Soul Echo functions as a soul replacement, and the character cannot regain her soul while under this Condition.<br /> Soulless, Enervated, and Thrall Conditions are suppressed while the character is under the Almost Souled Condition.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Lose the Soul Echo <br /> <b>Beat</b>: Lose Wisdom or Integrity in a scene where you regain Willpower through surrender.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How's that? </div> </div> </div>That sounds great! Thanks for making a spell as well, that is appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:57:27-08:00","id":1052169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052132#post1052132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool idea <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Like a pacemaker sort of thing, but for the soul.<br /> <br /> So far as I can tell, there is no making souls in 2E, but Death creating a similar thing to keep a person in an equilibrium of sorts (suppress the Soulless series of conditions for the Duration) sounds perfectly within Death's domain.<br /> <br /> Of course, this being Patterning, you can't just create this new thing. A ghost will do nicely. I would suggest a Wisdom breaking point for this.<br /> <br /> Because at some point, that ghost will revert back from being a Soulpacemaker. And what was that about being Soulless? -2 to posession? Hmm <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Echo to Echo</b> (<b>Death</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Resistance<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Occult, Medicine, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By means of this spell the Mage transforms a ghost - the echo of a person - into a Soul Echo. The Soul Echo behaves like a pale imitation of a soul, allowing it to be attached to a person whose soul had been removed, in order to mitigate the seriousness of their situation.<br /> Like a regular soul, it can only be attached to people without a soul - under the Soulless, Enervated, or Thrall Conditions. Attaching the Soul Echo to a person without a soul does not resolve the Soulless, Enervated, nor Thrall Conditions, rather, the person gains the Almost Souled persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Almost Souled</b><br /> <b>(Persistent)</b><br /> The character has been implanted with a Soul Echo, halting their degradation from the lack of a soul. She does not regain Willpower from acting according to her Virtue or Vice.<br /> The Soul Echo functions as a soul replacement, and the character cannot regain her soul while under this Condition.<br /> Soulless, Enervated, and Thrall Conditions are suppressed while the character is under the Almost Souled Condition.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Lose the Soul Echo<br /> <b>Beat</b>: Lose Wisdom or Integrity in a scene where you regain Willpower through surrender.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How's that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. I do feel for how generous the &quot;Almost Souled&quot; condition is, it should be more delicate, perhaps with resolved via failing Breaking Points or some such, and then reverts the Soul Echo back into the Ghost and the subject now has the Anchor condition in relation to the Ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-20-2017, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:30:27-08:00","id":1052187,"title":"","content":"It's not bad, I think I wouldn't allow someone under the spell to recover Integrity though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:31:43-08:00","id":1052188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052119#post1052119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending a point of Willpower grants +3 dice on rolls, including Clash of Wills. You might be thinking about resisted actions and Withstand. In those cases a point of Willpower will grant +2 to an attribute for the sake of that roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake. Thank you for the correction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:43:07-08:00","id":1052198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052169#post1052169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this. I do feel for how generous the &quot;Almost Souled&quot; condition is, it should be more delicate, perhaps with resolved via failing Breaking Points or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what you mean, but the price is quite steep. The ghost won't be happy about it when it reghosts. And the Conditions then stop being suppressed, so -2 to possession resistance to that.<br /> <br /> So you need to keep the spell up. <br /> <br /> It's basically &quot;suppress 1 condition, but with penalties and inconveniences,&quot; even if it is a severe condition.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure there's rationale to just say &quot;I hereby delay your soulEntropy, Death 4, Soulless is now suppressed.&quot; Thought this would be more atmospheric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:44:25-08:00","id":1052632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052053#post1052053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could perhaps turn a ghost into a soul? Would this be possible? It is within the arcanum's purview and I am changing it to another item in the purview. I realize that Archmastery is where the creation of a soul happened in 1E, but if we are to use the Practices as a much better guideline in 2E it seems that this could be interpreted in this way. Maybe the Patterned Soul would just be a temporary replacement, but it is not a full on soul but rather something acting as one on the most basic level and thus does not have all the extensive properties of a true soul. Perhaps you can lose the Soulless/Enervated/Thrall Conditions with it in place, but you don't start gaining willpower/gnosis as you would with a normal soul. It is also of course subject to Dispelling.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2nd Ed pg 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Origin of Souls<br /> Souls bear one last Mystery even to the Awakened; <u>mages can destroy and manipulate souls with the Arcana, but no mage has ever successfully created one</u>. In theory, it would require the Making Practice with all five subtle Arcana. Fifth-degree masters are vanishingly rare anyway, and all such luminaries to attempt soul creation have failed. Many mages believe that souls originate in the Supernal, and earthly magic can\u2019t replicate the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052053#post1052053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death covers the following based on the Core Rulebook</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition pg. 128</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purview: Darkness, decay, ectoplasm, ghosts, the Underworld, souls, cold, absence, enervation, endings.</div> </div> </div> </div>is just a bit above this text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening 2nd Edition pg. 128</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She can <u>bolster a soul</u>, restore pleasure to a ghost, and reverse the effects of aging just as well as she can <u>destroy souls</u>, rip ghosts from anchors, and steal the life from another.</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Underlining for emphasis</u><br /> <br /> The most likely reason for the prejudice by Mages that ghosts are merely echos and are not the souls of the dead is that magic affects ghosts and souls differently and the lack of their interchangeability. Side stepping the whole creation of souls by transmuting something else into a soul is amazingly obvious and completely makes the Mystery of the Soul meaningless, By the way, if it did work there would be no consistent reason you couldn't transmute whatever you have the appropriate Arcanum for into souls, like vanilla wafers, dogs, spirits, or anything else that can be transmuted from one Arcanum to another.<br /> <br /> However all that said, interesting stop gap measures for soul lost are interesting to contemplate, and have precedence in other templates (looking at you Beast and Promethean). Of course Major Templates is the stuff of archmastery, but temporary conditions that interact with other conditions is much more reasonable for those less than Archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-21-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:03:47-08:00","id":1052640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052632#post1052632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However all that said, interesting stop gap measures for soul lost are interesting to contemplate, and have precedence</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nice. Very cryptic. Is mysterious wizard shit part of the rules?&quot;<br /> &quot;I don't know. I'm not the real Nemean, remember?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:26:22-08:00","id":1052985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1052640#post1052640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Nice. Very cryptic. Is mysterious wizard shit part of the rules?&quot;<br /> &quot;I don't know. I'm not the real Nemean, remember?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I don't know what Khonsu was thinking. Mysterious wizard shit is like the entire existence of Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:50:21-08:00","id":1054602,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>: Made a good point that Potency may be the better primary factor as each level of Potency allows the Mage to pick and choose which type of subject they are able to detect.<br /> <br /> Here is another spell, this might be useful I think given certain circumstances:<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Attendance (Prime \u25cf)<br /> Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Survival, Streetwise<br /> This spell will instantly tell the caster how many Sleepwalkers or Mages or Proximi may be in the area designed by this spell. Each level of Potency allows the Mage to select a different type of subject to be detected by this spell. Those protected by a veiling spell invoke a Clash of Wills with the target along with any other type of spell/effect that might conceal a target from detection.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Mage knows the independent numbers of subjects instead of just a lump sum.<br /> <b>Add Matter \u25cf: </b>The spell will reveal imbued items, enchanted items, and artifacts and Potency must be divided for each type.<br /> <br /> What do you think of this spell? I was trying to think of a good Knowing Spell for Prime since there is not one present. Supernal Vision kind of does a very similar thing, but I feel it is useful if you want to really gather very accurate information versus this is more of a general ping based spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-25-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T20:49:22-08:00","id":1054621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1054602#post1054602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is another spell, this might be useful I think given certain circumstances:<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Attendance (Prime \u25cf)<br /> Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Survival, Streetwise<br /> This spell will instantly tell the caster how many Sleepwalkers, Mages, and Proximi may be in the area designed by this spell. Those protected by a veiling spell invoke a Clash of Wills with the target along with any other type of spell/effect that might conceal a target from detection.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Mage knows the independent numbers of subjects instead of just a lump sum.<br /> <b>Add Matter \u25cf: </b>The spell will reveal imbued items, enchanted items, and artifacts.<br /> <br /> What do you think of this spell? I was trying to think of a good Knowing Spell for Prime since there is not one present. Supernal Vision kind of does a very similar thing, but I feel it is useful if you want to really gather very accurate information versus this is more of a general ping based spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Given how it's supposed to have an area of effect, wouldn't it make sense to have Scale as the Primary Factor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T20:54:16-08:00","id":1054624,"title":"","content":"Hey Deionscribe,<br /> <br /> I wondered that myself, but Scale never seems to be the Primary Factor for any spell I have seen to date, they are typically either Duration or Potency. I felt Duration in this case since it would be helpful if you wanted to keep the ping going for a certain length of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:01:27-08:00","id":1054626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1054624#post1054624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt Duration in this case since it would be helpful if you wanted to keep the ping going for a certain length of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the sense that making it Potency-primary and Withstood by Composure would be better suited to an area-based &quot;ping&quot; spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:07:31-08:00","id":1054629,"title":"","content":"Hey Satchel,<br /> <br /> It seems to me it is not necessary to have Withstand since I am not making any changes or Compelling them to do something. I feel this is more of a general information gathering spell, which should just be a Clash of Wills versus a Veiling Spell/Effect. Even Supernal Vision has no Withstand and it is much more invasive spell.<br /> <br /> Though, it may be the first spell that maybe should be Scale? Though I do feel Duration is more powerful since it allows you to stay up-to-date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  I stand corrected regarding Knowing spells with Withstand. It does appear Know Spirit possesses a Withstand, but it seems this spell is more of an Unveling Spell than a Knowing Spell so I am kind of t 02-25-2017, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T00:24:30-08:00","id":1054674,"title":"","content":"Step 5 of the Creative Thaumaturgy is Primary Spell Factor. It states that it is either Potency or Duration, so scale isn't a choice for Primary Spell Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T05:08:11-08:00","id":1054718,"title":"","content":"I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4720\" data-vbnamecard=\"4720\">Taldorblackfire</a> completely. The spell is not invasive enough to be Withstood, and Duration would have more effect than Potency as the Primary Factor (since Scale can't be a Primary Factor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T04:13:35-08:00","id":1055164,"title":"","content":"How would you create a Force's Shielding spell against damage from kinetic (or any other types of) energy attacks?<br /> <br /> Would a simple repurposing of Matter 2's Alchemist's Touch be acceptable, except instead of types of matter, it would protect against types of energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:38:01-08:00","id":1055192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1055164#post1055164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you create a Force's Shielding spell against damage from kinetic (or any other types of) energy attacks?<br /> Would a simple repurposing of Matter 2's Alchemist's Touch be acceptable, except instead of types of matter, it would protect against types of energy?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I'd do it. There's no reason to reinvent the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:45:19-08:00","id":1055421,"title":"","content":"I don't have time at the moment to fully write out the spell idea, but how does a Space 4, Life 4 spell that turns you into a two dimensional figure sound? What kind of implications would it have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:54:35-08:00","id":1055427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1055421#post1055421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have time at the moment to fully write out the spell idea, but how does a Space 4, Life 4 spell that turns you into a two dimensional figure sound? What kind of implications would it have?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was actually a 1e spell that did that, and then you could fold up whatever you transfigured and take it with you. The biggest problem was dealing with its weight as I recall. Anyways, Death can turn you into a shadow and that's 2d so I don't imagine it would be much different or problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T06:59:30-08:00","id":1055629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1055421#post1055421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have time at the moment to fully write out the spell idea, but how does a Space 4, Life 4 spell that turns you into a two dimensional figure sound? What kind of implications would it have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're interested in exploring the theoretical implications of lacking a dimension, go with convenience: treat it as essentially 3d, with one dimension being infinitesimally small, for purposes of what it can do, and as 2d for fluff.<br /> <br /> Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said, there's a thing that turns you into a shadow, and there is nooo way for that to work with any consideration to physics. It's just magic. Boom convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:16:09-08:00","id":1055639,"title":"","content":"And I don't think that Life 4 component is necessary in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:57:13-08:00","id":1055668,"title":"","content":"If I've understood correctly Life 4 was a requirement for transforming a human body in 1E. This requirement does not appear to be present in 2E.<br /> <br /> Edit: Moinen is right, as per the &quot;Add Life 4:&quot; for Transubstantiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-27-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T09:04:51-08:00","id":1055670,"title":"","content":"It is still true. If you want to change somebody into stone you need Life 4 and Matter 4. But Death can weaken you so much that it changes you into your own shadow and <b>Space can manipulate dimensions, not bodies.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:21:27-08:00","id":1055733,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain that Space can make you proportionally larger or smaller at the adept level. However, making yourself 2d is not proportional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:05:24-08:00","id":1055751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1055733#post1055733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly certain that Space can make you proportionally larger or smaller at the adept level. However, making yourself 2d is not proportional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still a manipulation of dimensional space should be doable with just space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:41:03-08:00","id":1055793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1054629#post1054629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Satchel,<br /> <br /> It seems to me it is not necessary to have Withstand since I am not making any changes or Compelling them to do something. I feel this is more of a general information gathering spell, which should just be a Clash of Wills versus a Veiling Spell/Effect. Even Supernal Vision has no Withstand and it is much more invasive spell.<br /> <br /> Though, it may be the first spell that maybe should be Scale? Though I do feel Duration is more powerful since it allows you to stay up-to-date.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally a Clash of Wills if there is a Veiling spellor other supernatural ability concealing the target, I agree. I think the place for debate here is if the practice as either Knowing or Unveiling. and given your description I think it is clearly a Knowing spell:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA 2nd ed pg123</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing spells deliver knowledge about something directly to the mage (or to another target). A mage can divine the cause of a corpse\u2019s death (Death), sense whether someone has a powerful destiny (Fate), or unerringly know which way is north (Space). This knowledge is a direct awareness of Supernal truth; the mage doesn\u2019t have to interpret evidence based on her senses or try to divine the truth out of cryptic riddles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any knowing spells that have a Withstand which isn't cast across Sypathetic Connections?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:55:37-08:00","id":1055806,"title":"","content":"Know Spirit has Withstand (the spirit's Rank), but that's the only written spell that does. The Death and Mind counterparts would probably also use Withstand, but they aren't actually written out due to word count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T01:35:08-08:00","id":1057024,"title":"","content":"What level of Life spell would it be for Suspended Animation, or would it be a Death Spell or a combination of the 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T03:40:22-08:00","id":1057038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057024#post1057024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of Life spell would it be for Suspended Animation, or would it be a Death Spell or a combination of the 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a Time spell. Body Control could significantly reduce biological activity though and Death could put you in a temporary state of being dead for all intents and purposes, probably at Death 3 or 4 depending on how much of a Pattern change you consider it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T05:57:01-08:00","id":1057060,"title":"","content":"I would agree with Mrmdubois, this is a Time 2 Spell with possibly a Space Component of probably 2 to prevent the target from moving if that is what you are aiming for. Otherwise, the previous suggestions work for all other applications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T06:21:13-08:00","id":1057064,"title":"","content":"Life Weaving spell could do it too with some Reaches. You could also achieve something similar with a couple of clever Shielding spells. Perhaps just a Death to Shield from dying and Death/Mind/Life Veiling added to not suffer while your body deteriorates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T06:55:00-08:00","id":1057071,"title":"","content":"It depends on what's meant by suspended animation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:06:25-08:00","id":1057074,"title":"","content":"What is ment by suspended animation is where your body functions are suspended, no aging, no deterioration, etc, but you are not dead. Like cryogenic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:16:24-08:00","id":1057078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057074#post1057074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is ment by suspended animation is where your body functions are suspended, no aging, no deterioration, etc, but you are not dead. Like cryogenic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 2 then, you can slow things down a lot with Life 2, but I wouldn't let Life fully cease bodily functions, Death 3 or 4 would achieve it, but only because it skips the part about you being alive at all to render you pseudo-dead or by destroying the entropy in your own body.<br /> <br /> Edit: Death 2 could shield against entropy to achieve the desired result as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-02-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:27:38-08:00","id":1057080,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I Am Many (Death ooo)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Connects Targets live forces in such a way that damage dealt to any of them is divided among all of them evenly. Treat 1 lethal damage as 2 bashing and 1 aggravated as 3 bashing for the sake of dividing it. Round damage up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>Round damage down. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>Targets can\u2019t lose consciousness individually - when all their health boxes are filled they continue to function as long as at least one of the linked Targets still has one health box empty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>Targets can\u2019t die individually - when all their health boxes are filled with aggravated damage they continue to live as long as at least one of the linked Targets still has health box not filled with aggravated damage.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Caster can now prioritize Targets making one of them to take damage only when all other have their health boxes full of aggravated damage. This option must be taken separately for every excluded Target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Spell can now include mix of inanimate objects, corpses and generally everything that has the capacity to be damaged. One point of structure equals one point of lethal damage.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:38:33-08:00","id":1057107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057080#post1057080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Spell can now include mix of inanimate objects, corpses and generally everything that has the capacity to be damaged. One point of structure equals one point of lethal damage.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Do atoms count?<br /> Do feelings?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:44:20-08:00","id":1057109,"title":"","content":"Do atoms or feelings have Structure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:32:10-08:00","id":1057126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057107#post1057107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do atoms count?<br /> Do feelings?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I designed this spell inspired by the thread about the nukes and how much Structure the skyscraper has. It must feel great to hijack skyscrapers 100 Structure points and 'transform' them into your health.<br /> But to your question(without gettin into 'on what lvl can magic split atoms' argument). I guess you could cast it on forest fire or something and treat its size or force as Structure and if you insist and can perceive memories - target also them. Use Sympathy Withstand (Connection) guidlines when assessing 'Structure'.<br /> Feelings... I wouldn't allow it but if you want you could treat (if perceived) them as having ~2 points of Structure. Make sure to not die from somebodies mood swings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:36:16-08:00","id":1057148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057080#post1057080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I Am Many (Death ooo)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Connects Targets live forces in such a way that damage dealt to any of them is divided among all of them evenly. Treat 1 lethal damage as 2 bashing and 1 aggravated as 3 bashing for the sake of dividing it. Round damage up.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Aggravated damage should probably count as 2 lethal or 4 bashing damage. Also the minimum damage should be limited to one point of damage (in my mind), otherwise it can get rather ridiculous with higher amount of targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T11:00:58-08:00","id":1057160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057148#post1057148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Aggravated damage should probably count as 2 lethal or 4 bashing damage. Also the minimum damage should be limited to one point of damage (in my mind), otherwise it can get rather ridiculous with higher amount of targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversion rate depends on you preference, I went with the strict in-game one. Bashing upgrades bashing to lethal and then to aggravated, thats how it is in the rules. Since your version is also supported, do however you wish.<br /> Without Reach option the there must be at least one point of damage. Round damage up - at least one point of damage. Reach option bypasses that on purpose since Forces 2 can shield you from any energy and Death 2 imo should Shield you from damage altogether. Using life force of so many people, lets say a neighbourhood, gives you a nice benefit where nothing can kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:06:14-08:00","id":1057180,"title":"","content":"I think it would be best to not downgrade damage at all. Downgrading damage (even if you take more damage, such as downgrading 1L to 2B) is a distinct effect in its own right and should probably not be default for a spell about sharing damage. But I can totally see it as a Reach option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:08:42-08:00","id":1057279,"title":"","content":"Downgrading comes into play only when you get less lethal or aggravated then there is targets of the spell, so not really that big of a deal. Nevertheless I see your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:18:06-08:00","id":1057283,"title":"","content":"Just have the last ones in order not take any damage. You'd have to establish an order anyway since you'll likely not end up with equal amounts of damage even if you do downgrade like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:25:45-08:00","id":1057568,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about using homebrew beer and mead as sacraments for some spells and also for collecting tass, so i thought of this spell mostly for fun:<br /> <br /> \u00d8lrunar (Ale-runes) (Life \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Survival, Science<br /> This spell allows the mage to exert control over the microorganisms involved in the process of fermentation and thus exert an incredible level of control over the entire process. The name is taken from old poems about runes enchanting ales, but it works on anything that is created by the fermentation of organic materials. This spell must be cast before beginning the process, and as long as it is still active once the process is successfully finished, add this spell\u2019s Potency to the finished product\u2019s die bonus and availability rating.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:48:47-08:00","id":1057573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1057568#post1057568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about using homebrew beer and mead as sacraments for some spells and also for collecting tass, so i thought of this spell mostly for fun:<br /> <br /> \u00d8lrunar (Ale-runes) (Life \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Survival, Science<br /> This spell allows the mage to exert control over the microorganisms involved in the process of fermentation and thus exert an incredible level of control over the entire process. The name is taken from old poems about runes enchanting ales, but it works on anything that is created by the fermentation of organic materials. This spell must be cast before beginning the process, and as long as it is still active once the process is successfully finished, add this spell\u2019s Potency to the finished product\u2019s die bonus and availability rating.</div> </div> </div> </div> Compelling will do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T18:43:35-08:00","id":1057864,"title":"","content":"<b>Nothing Between (Space 1)<br /> Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Investigation, Science, Empathy<br /> If space is a lie, it must follow that distance is a lie. By means of this spell, a Mage may scrutinize objects much farther than normally possible: reading small print on the other side of the room or counting hairs on someone's head as though they were right next to it.<br /> Multiply the distance at which the subject can see before suffering penalties by this spell's Potency. Atmospheric conditions may impact this vision, as it effectively creates a telescope.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell allows the subject to see out to a distance of Space miles.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell applies to hearing as well as sight.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell can ignore intervening atmospheric conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Co-Temperus (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Mana Cost:</b> 1<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Larceny, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> By making the present as indeterminable as the future, this spell can allow the subject to participate in multiple \u2018potential presents\u2019 simultaneously. The subject splits into one additional version of themselves per Potency. This is not a true division of the subject, but instead is the subject existing in multiple timelines. They share a single Willpower and Mana pool, but are otherwise treated as separate. At the beginning of the subject\u2019s turn, each version of themselves may perform their actions as normal. However, apply the results of only one version of the subject on the world around them, and each version of the subject completely ignores what the others do (sometimes even occupying the same space). For instance, if one version of the subject opens a door and goes through it, all other versions of the subject still have to open the door and walk through it. If at the end of the turn the subject chooses to apply the changes of another version of themselves who did not open the door on the world, then the door would be closed at the end of the turn (having never been opened). Any supernatural powers that affect one or more versions of the subject affects all of them. When the spell ends or is canceled, only one version of the subject sticks around, and that version suffers all of the damage, conditions and tilts suffered by all other versions of themselves, but also gains all knowledge and experiences from the discarded versions of themselves.<br /> <b>Add Mind (\u2022\u2022): </b>The different versions of the subject may communicate telepathically.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The different versions of the subject are more insulated from each other. When one or more of them is affected by a supernatural power, then they may roll a Clash of Wills to keep all other versions from themselves from being equally affected.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The version of the subject that remains after the spell expires gains the worst damage from all versions of themselves, instead of all of it.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> When the spell expires, the damage, conditions and tilts from the discarded versions of the subject is not applied to the subject.<br /> <b>Note:</b> A Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 equivalent of this spell exists, but relies on a duplication of the character\u2019s spatial presence instead of timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-04-2017, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:39:44-08:00","id":1057889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> I'd let Co-Temperus clones cast spells as normal since only one of them is going to become &quot;real&quot; at the end of their turn anyway just like any of their other potential action options. I'd also assume they don't need to communicate telepathically for the same reason. The last Reach option I'd possibly make into something like a Clone can receive damage and be destroyed thus closing off its chance at being a potential Present. In the main body of the spell I'd note that a target of multiple attacks from multiple clones can use its full Defense (Whatever that is) against any and all of the clones. Cool spell though.<br /> <br /> For Nothing Between I'd let the +1 Reach to increase distance do it for a number of miles equal to Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T19:35:31-08:00","id":1058257,"title":"","content":"Edited Co-Temperus after deciding that breaking action economy was a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:32:51-08:00","id":1058359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1058257#post1058257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edited Co-Temperus after deciding that breaking action economy was a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks a lot better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:01:02-08:00","id":1058453,"title":"","content":"<b>Magic Shield (Prime 2)<br /> Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Athletics, Expression<br /> This simple and tried spell is commonplace in Awakened society; even mages who don't study Prime do try to at least have an Imbued Item with this spell. It simply protects user against any and all spells being cast on him; the other caster need to win Clash of Wills with spell caster to affect the subject of Magic Shield. Moving to Advanced Potency gives +1 die per Potency in this Clash of Wills, and Duration gives it's usual benefits.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The caster can temporarily suppress this spell to allow friendly mage to work his magic on him any time he wants to do that.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Space \u2022\u2022: </b>The mage may act as &quot;shield-bearer&quot;, using his own shield to cover an ally he has sympathetic connection with. The spell needs to use Sympathetic Yantra at casting to allow this effect; the mage needs a separate Yantra for each mage he wants to cover up in that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:04:58-08:00","id":1058482,"title":"","content":"It's just my opinion, but I think having an all-enconpasing anti-magic shield diminishes the value of each of the Arcana specific shielding spells like Mind Shield or Ward. I think Wards and Signs alredy cover the niche pretty well of being a general defense againts magic while levaing space for the other Arcana specific Clash of Wills-based shields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:06:32-08:00","id":1058485,"title":"","content":"I think the basic spell effect is completely fine, but I have some issues with some stuff.<br /> First of all Advanced Potency already has a fixed purpose.<br /> Secondly I think adding dice to a Clash of Wills roll should be a separate spell at a higher Practice due to how potent bonuses to Clash of Wills are and because that's not how any other Shielding spell works.<br /> Thirdly, a spell effect is generally always on. Instead of suppressing the spell effect I'd recommend using a Key.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, since it would be an extremely powerful spell compared to other Shielding spells I'd personally not allow the use of a Key (that is generally a Space thing anyway). Not being able to cast beneficial spells on oneself without cancelling or overcoming the spell would be a fitting drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-05-2017, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:18:05-08:00","id":1058488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1058482#post1058482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Wards and Signs alredy cover the niche pretty well of being a general defense againts magic</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no: it's trivial to blow off through them with dice pool which is large enough. IMO the whole mechanic of Withstand is just plain useless with Exceptional Success being able to blow off through it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:37:14-08:00","id":1058578,"title":"","content":"There are three &quot;layers&quot; of protection from magical effects:<br /> <br /> - You can increase Withstand, or get more Withstands. Wards and Signs are often used to do that. This forces attacker to pump Potency or Fish for Exceptional.<br /> - You can grab something that forces Clash of Wills. This makes attacker suffer from disadvantage if they didn't pump Duration. A lot of shielding spells work like this.<br /> - You can increase your Size, really or virtually. Even a single point of Size increase forces attacker to either use AOE spell against you, or get more Scale.<br /> <br /> As you can see, if you want to &quot;naturally&quot; pierce good Withstand (and it's easy to get 6 or 7 Withstand with Wards and Signs) rating you will have problems with contesting Clash of Wills; if you want to fish for Exceptional Success, you also will have problems with Clash of Wills, because when Praxis Nuking you usually want to leave factors untouched. <br /> Size manipulation gives Space some interesting unobvious way to defend itself, especially if you use a veiling spell to make the subject look different size than you &quot;make&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T03:05:46-08:00","id":1060796,"title":"","content":"I want to introduce a Rune-crazy low Gnosis character who tries her best to compensate lack of power with a lot of know-how, trinkets and highly optimized tools and boons. She is going to be a Prime 3 character and I really, really want her to use some Prime magic to optimize her stuff to the maximum. I know Fate Magic would be perfect for this, but this is a &quot;char gen&quot; character, who basically only uses Prime. <br /> ...which brings me to, anyone got any cool spells that she could sling? I'm totally in for something that targets runes and yantras, because I lack creativity to do something ground breaking here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T06:11:34-08:00","id":1060837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1060796#post1060796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to introduce a Rune-crazy low Gnosis character who tries her best to compensate lack of power with a lot of know-how, trinkets and highly optimized tools and boons. She is going to be a Prime 3 character and I really, really want her to use some Prime magic to optimize her stuff to the maximum. I know Fate Magic would be perfect for this, but this is a &amp;quot;char gen&amp;quot; character, who basically only uses Prime. <br /> ...which brings me to, anyone got any cool spells that she could sling? I'm totally in for something that targets runes and yantras, because I lack creativity to do something ground breaking here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got nothing on spells, but I do have some homebrew Rune-based Merits that might be useful. Feel free to check them out on my hub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:36:55-08:00","id":1060929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1060796#post1060796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which brings me to, anyone got any cool spells that she could sling? I'm totally in for something that targets runes and yantras, because I lack creativity to do something ground breaking here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could imagine Prime 3 weaving would let you &quot;borrow&quot; a location's symbolism and attach it to an object to allow some Potency-limited # of invocations of that location as a yantra while not actually present there. Some random ideas (haven't been keeping up with the thread, apologies if I retread any ground here):<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Memento/Souvenir/Etc. (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Larceny</span></span><br /> <br /> This spell invests an object with the significance of an Environment. The object can be used as a Tool Yantra in situations where the location's symbolism would be relevant, providing the usual +1 bonus. It may be evoked in this fashion up to once per level of Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and 1 mana: </b>The spell may invest an object with a Verge or Demesne's symbolism. The Tool provides a +2 die bonus and, while it cannot totally negate Paradox, does act as a Dedicated Tool.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Palimpsest (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Expression</span></span><br /> <br /> This effect allows additional spells to be anchored to a single set of High Speech runes. Casting an additional spell into the runes requires the expenditure of one mana during formation of its Imago. The secondary spell may make use the yantra bonus of the runes (without having to take a ritual interval to inscribe them) and is also disrupted if the runes are erased or defaced. The Palimpsest can hold a number of spells equal to its Potency (in addition to the first spell.) If the Palimpsest is dispelled or its duration lapses, the secondary spell is lost.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">OotS Reference etc. (Prime \u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Crafts, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <br /> This spell alters the function of a set of High Speech runes. When the runes are invoked as a yantra during the creation of an Imago, in addition to providing the usual dice benefit, they will &quot;contain&quot; the spell anchored to them. If the Potency of this spell meets or exceeds that of the anchored spell, the anchored effect does not take place, remaining ineffectual until OotS Reference is dispelled or lapses. If cast upon an active set of runes that are already anchoring a spell, OotS Reference can temporarily suppress an anchored effect (Potency permitting.)<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>If the runes are marred or defaced, OotS Reference will end and the anchored effect will be <i>released</i> instead of being disrupted, taking effect on whatever the runes were inscribed upon for the rest of its duration.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above, but the released effect will instead turn upon the person or object that damaged the runes, if they are a valid target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:19:48-08:00","id":1060948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1060929#post1060929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could imagine Prime 3 weaving would let you &quot;borrow&quot; a location's symbolism and attach it to an object to allow some Potency-limited # of invocations of that location as a yantra while not actually present there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Prime and Space 3 in order to connect the object to the location in a way that can draw the location's symbolism through the object when not present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:26:06-08:00","id":1060951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1060948#post1060948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Prime and Space 3 in order to connect the object to the location in a way that can draw the location's symbolism through the object when not present.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Space shouldn't be required. Take Words of Truth, the subject of the spell can hear the Mage who cast it speaking to him no matter where he goes after the spell is cast. Oaths Fulfilled works on the same principle.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Scale has to match the size of the whole location that you're drawing from though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T12:35:08-08:00","id":1060979,"title":"","content":"<b>Sense Presence Spells</b><br /> <br /> Mages can't keep their Mage Sight on all the time, but there are times when you need a magical alarm; the spell which detects potential threats and targets. The applications are wide: protection of sanctums, spying, use in combat and others. Unlike Mage Sight, those aren't as taxing and don't require from Mage to filter raw Supernal meaning, instead processing it and giving information.<br /> All those spells are usually cast with Advanced Scale for greater area of Effect and Advanced Duration for longer durations; so while those spells are all technically require just Arcanum 1, in practice they require at least Arcanum 3 to cast without Paradox risk. They also usually being cast ritually, except in combat situations, there duration isn't as useful.<br /> All those spells are Knowing practices; as such, they automatically fail to notice persons who use Veiling practice of Arcanum in question to hide themselves; all those spells can for +1 Reach include Unveiling practice to automatically attempt to pierce deception.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Undead (Death \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Ghosts aren't bound by physical obstacles, and naturally can't be seen or felt by human senses. This spell tell the mage, if something undead enters the area of spell and gives the location of it.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows Rank and Influence of ghost who is entering the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows amount of dots in attributes of ghost who is entering the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Vibrations (Force \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Mages can become invisible, but thought going completely silent don't happen to many of them, because sight is the most important human sense. This spell exploits this error, listening closely to vibrations in the area and telling mage of their location.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows Size and approximate mass of being who is entering the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage can closely listen to being who is entering the area, if he chooses to.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Life (Life \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> The hunter knows the jungle by sight, hearing, and smell. This spells goes further and detects the very feeling of being alive: heartbeat, breathing and desire to be alive. This spell tell the mage, if something alive enters the area of spell and gives the location of it.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows general well being of person who enters the area - it's Health and Conditions like Tired, Poisoned, etc.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows amount of dots in Physical attributes of person who is entering the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows specific amount of dots in one Physical attribute of person who is entering the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Pressure (Matter \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> This spell is different from other is regard that it isn't cast on area, but on structure in question; the mage can feel pressure on structure material and detect location of creatures who move inside of it.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows Size and approximate mass of being who is entering the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Thoughts (Mind \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> The spell listens to thoughts and emotions of being inside of area, telling mage of their location. This spell can be very taxing on psyche of mage who cast it if location is happens to be in area with high human traffic.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows amount of dots in Mental or Social attributes of person who is entering the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows specific amount of dots in one Mental or Social attribute of person who is entering the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Magic (Prime \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Most mages prefer for their sanctums to be devoid of alien magic. This spells tells mage if somebody tries to use magic inside of area and telling mage of their location.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows the exact Arcana and it's level of the person who tries to use magic inside the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows the exact spell which is used inside the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Bending (Space \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Space magic is a great way to enter locations by making your own enters and exits; naturally there is a desire to detect such intruders. This spells tells if some person tried to bend space inside the area (with purpose of move; spells for sympathy and alike don't get noticed) and tells location of him to mage.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows level of Space of the person who tried to bend space inside the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense Spirits (Spirit \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> Ghosts aren't bound by physical obstacles, and naturally can't be seen or felt by human senses. This spell tell the mage, if some spirit enters the area of spell and gives the location of it.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows Rank and Influence of spirit who is entering the area.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage knows amount of dots in attributes of spirit who is entering the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-11-2017, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T13:28:57-08:00","id":1060999,"title":"","content":"General &quot;Alarm&quot; type spells I belive to be covered by Oaths Fulfilled. To sense the general presence of ephemeral beings there's the Death and Spirit 2nd dot attainment.<br /> <br /> Sense Vibrations should be an Unveiling spell.<br /> <br /> Sense thoughts is literally Mind Sight and I wouldn't make a spell out of it. Similarly, Sense Bending wouldn't even be worth it: abything it would detect would also activate PMS and be visible with AMS. Sense Magic is Prime Sight but better.<br /> <br /> I don't think you should be able to mimic Mage Sight with spells. That's why there is even Mage Sight in 2nd edition, so you wouldn't have to bother casting for it. And I belive it to be a -terrible- idea to make spells that make it obsolete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T14:42:03-08:00","id":1061028,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a> You have clearly missed the point of the spells which is to set up a sort of &quot;trap&quot; area that the Mage can stay up to date on while not being in it, they also overcome the MS limitations of requiring the phenomena to be perceived via normal sensory routes.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a> I think the Reach options for the various spells that allow you to determine Rank, Attributes, etc. should have the language cleared up. Spells that determine Attributes either give a total number of dots in an Attribute set, or spend Reach to determine specific Attribute ratings. Spells that determine the Rank and other information of an entity run up against Withstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T19:30:48-08:00","id":1061105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061028#post1061028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12673\" data-vbnamecard=\"12673\">EW-Matias</a> You have clearly missed the point of the spells which is to set up a sort of &quot;trap&quot; area that the Mage can stay up to date on while not being in it, they also overcome the MS limitations of requiring the phenomena to be perceived via normal sensory routes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Scry and Oath's Fulfilled are for. As I said, I don't think you should be able to mimic and even improve on what Mage Sight does with spells. Like, why would I even spend willpower and mana on Mage Sight if I can just cast a Praxis or Rote version of these spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T00:37:38-08:00","id":1061154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1060929#post1060929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could imagine Prime 3 weaving would let you &quot;borrow&quot; a location's symbolism and attach it to an object to allow some Potency-limited # of invocations of that location as a yantra while not actually present there. Some random ideas (haven't been keeping up with the thread, apologies if I retread any ground here):<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Memento/Souvenir/Etc. (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Larceny</span></span><br /> <br /> This spell invests an object with the significance of an Environment. The object can be used as a Tool Yantra in situations where the location's symbolism would be relevant, providing the usual +1 bonus. It may be evoked in this fashion up to once per level of Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and 1 mana: </b>The spell may invest an object with a Verge or Demesne's symbolism. The Tool provides a +2 die bonus and, while it cannot totally negate Paradox, does act as a Dedicated Tool.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Palimpsest (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Expression</span></span><br /> <br /> This effect allows additional spells to be anchored to a single set of High Speech runes. Casting an additional spell into the runes requires the expenditure of one mana during formation of its Imago. The secondary spell may make use the yantra bonus of the runes (without having to take a ritual interval to inscribe them) and is also disrupted if the runes are erased or defaced. The Palimpsest can hold a number of spells equal to its Potency (in addition to the first spell.) If the Palimpsest is dispelled or its duration lapses, the secondary spell is lost.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">OotS Reference etc. (Prime \u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Crafts, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <br /> This spell alters the function of a set of High Speech runes. When the runes are invoked as a yantra during the creation of an Imago, in addition to providing the usual dice benefit, they will &quot;contain&quot; the spell anchored to them. If the Potency of this spell meets or exceeds that of the anchored spell, the anchored effect does not take place, remaining ineffectual until OotS Reference is dispelled or lapses. If cast upon an active set of runes that are already anchoring a spell, OotS Reference can temporarily suppress an anchored effect (Potency permitting.)<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>If the runes are marred or defaced, OotS Reference will end and the anchored effect will be <i>released</i> instead of being disrupted, taking effect on whatever the runes were inscribed upon for the rest of its duration.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above, but the released effect will instead turn upon the person or object that damaged the runes, if they are a valid target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these [insert exclamation mark that I cannot do because my keyboard had a stroke]. While my gut instinct for Souvenir was to add Space to it, I really like the idea of using just Prime to do it by treating the subject like a smaller part of greater Environment Symbolism and kinda like using Prime to rebuild lacking parts around it like a hologram and ducktape it for these few scenes.<br /> Palimpsest is one of the rare spells I would bother to Safely Relinquish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T00:38:59-08:00","id":1061157,"title":"","content":"As for the Magic Sight talk above, sometimes I wish Knowing Unveiling spells would be universally created as a effects that modify Mage Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T02:23:22-08:00","id":1061175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061028#post1061028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;12673&quot;]\u200bThat said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a> I think the Reach options for the various spells that allow you to determine Rank, Attributes, etc. should have the language cleared up. Spells that determine Attributes either give a total number of dots in an Attribute set, or spend Reach to determine specific Attribute ratings. Spells that determine the Rank and other information of an entity run up against Withstand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted and changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061105#post1061105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Scry and Oath's Fulfilled are for. As I said, I don't think you should be able to mimic and even improve on what Mage Sight does with spells. Like, why would I even spend willpower and mana on Mage Sight if I can just cast a Praxis or Rote version of these spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those spells won't let you analyze magical phenomena and Imagos of spells, which is what MS for in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:13:59-08:00","id":1061184,"title":"","content":"But Sense Magic does EXACTLY that, but it's also better.<br /> <br /> And again, that's a very narrow and not at all official view of what Mage Sight is for. I don't need to tell you that you can do whatever you want with your game, but I personally wouldn't recommend it to anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:28:46-08:00","id":1061186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061105#post1061105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Scry and Oath's Fulfilled are for. As I said, I don't think you should be able to mimic and even improve on what Mage Sight does with spells. Like, why would I even spend willpower and mana on Mage Sight if I can just cast a Praxis or Rote version of these spells?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> `1) Scry and Oaths Fulfilled accomplish a different goal than these spells, 2) Just because there are some spells that serve a surveillance purpose in Space and Fate, what's the problem with developing surveillance spells in other arcana? Didn't you know that it's possible to use a variety of different arcana to achieve the same goal? Also, didn't you notice that the goal accomplished by these spells isn't the same as Scry and Oaths Fulfilled? 3) These spells may overlap with some of AMS basic functions, but there's nothing wrong with that. Mana and WP are spent on FMS and these spells have no overlap with FMS at all so your complaint is invalid. 4) Mages are -supposed- to cast spells to solve Mysteries, Mage Sight is the invasive, brute force approach. Mages use it all the time because it's effective, but it comes with risks like running out of WP, or mana, or contaminating the Mystery. Once again though, these spells don't replace Mage Sight.<br /> <br /> Next time you decide to disagree with something it'd be great if you made sure your facts were straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T03:33:36-08:00","id":1061188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061184#post1061184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Sense Magic does EXACTLY that, but it's also better.<br /> <br /> And again, that's a very narrow and not at all official view of what Mage Sight is for. I don't need to tell you that you can do whatever you want with your game, but I personally wouldn't recommend it to anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh. Magic IS better then Mage Sight. Its suppose to. You have two Practices that deal with uncovering things but they can't overlap with MS? Ridiculous and not supported by the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:13:31-08:00","id":1061233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061188#post1061188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Meh. Magic IS better then Mage Sight. Its suppose to. You have two Practices that deal with uncovering things but they can't overlap with MS? Ridiculous and not supported by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual overlap between MS and published spells is minimal (Life Sight telling you someone's general health, the attainments that let you see and interact with Spirits and Ghosts). Most Knowing spells give you information MS doesn't and most unveiling spells expand your senses to complement it.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying no spell could ever give you the same info, what I'm saying is that making spells specifically to circumbent the mechanic would be bad design if you care at all for the game as is presented. Wanting to house rule mage sight away is a different matter. Still a terrible idea in my opinion, but it's not just a little execise in Creative Thaumatugy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T07:58:36-08:00","id":1061247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061233#post1061233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual overlap between MS and published spells is minimal (Life Sight telling you someone's general health, the attainments that let you see and interact with Spirits and Ghosts). Most Knowing spells give you information MS doesn't and most unveiling spells expand your senses to complement it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overlap is minimal because of wordcount. Which is good, I don't need to see the same thing twice in a book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying no spell could ever give you the same info, what I'm saying is that making spells specifically to circumbent the mechanic would be bad design if you care at all for the game as is presented. Wanting to house rule mage sight away is a different matter. Still a terrible idea in my opinion, but it's not just a little execise in Creative Thaumatugy. </div> </div> </div>Magic is specifically designed to circumvent other mechanics, you know. Why bother commuting when you can teleport? Why bother picklocking when you can just command to open? Why bother looking for something when you can just know where it is? Why bother negotiating when you can command to bow?<br /> <br /> Wanting to house rule mage sight away is something that nobody proposed. So thats a miss.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T09:43:14-08:00","id":1061272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061233#post1061233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying no spell could ever give you the same info, what I'm saying is that making spells specifically to circumbent the mechanic would be bad design if you care at all for the game as is presented. Wanting to house rule mage sight away is a different matter. Still a terrible idea in my opinion, but it's not just a little execise in Creative Thaumatugy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not what the spell is doing so your complaint is invalidated by you failing to read it closely enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T07:40:01-07:00","id":1061818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061272#post1061272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not what the spell is doing