opinions and feedback, but make an actual argument or propose different interpretetions or ideas if you want to discuss them. You can't simply say they are invalid and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd already done that earlier, I can't help it that you failed to notice or acknowledge what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T14:15:51-07:00","id":1061981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1061835#post1061835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd already done that earlier, I can't help it that you failed to notice or acknowledge what I said.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1. Respect other people.</span></b></span><br /> <br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rule #1 is being broken here, please stop before I have to take disciplinary action. Thank you.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T05:02:38-07:00","id":1063811,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traverse (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaving</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distance is an Illusion, so is the path between two points. Designate starting and ending point of which both must be inside of area affected by spell. If cast on bended \u2018road\u2019 (area encompassing a few corners) it straightens it in such a way that its ends \u2018see\u2019 each other. Everything around the road twists to accommodate the new shape, but the effect can be seen only from the \u2018road\u2019. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>Chose only one direction from which the road straightens, the other one is unaffected. You can e.g. observe and shoot at your foes without cover penalties, they can\u2019t see you back.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Key the road to determine the condition at which the new shape can be seen. E.g. looking with one eye closed.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If the road is straight add number of new bends equal to potency.<br /> <br /> Language could use a little clearing I guess.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:44:28-07:00","id":1064119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1063811#post1063811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Traverse (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaving</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Distance is an Illusion, so is the path between two points. Designate starting and ending point of which both must be inside of area affected by spell. If cast on bended \u2018road\u2019 (area encompassing a few corners) it straightens it in such a way that its ends \u2018see\u2019 each other. Everything around the road twists to accommodate the new shape, but the effect can be seen only from the \u2018road\u2019. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>Chose only one direction from which the road straightens, the other one is unaffected. You can e.g. observe and shoot at your foes without cover penalties, they can\u2019t see you back.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Key the road to determine the condition at which the new shape can be seen. E.g. looking with one eye closed.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If the road is straight add number of new bends equal to potency.<br /> <br /> Language could use a little clearing I guess.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>So the base effect of the spell is like the Outward and Inward Eye in practice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T18:56:47-07:00","id":1064126,"title":"","content":"If I'm interpreting correctly you could fire a gun down this &quot;road&quot; even if there's a wall in the way. The Outward and Inward Eye is purely sensory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T19:11:39-07:00","id":1064131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1064119#post1064119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the base effect of the spell is like the Outward and Inward Eye in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it goes beyond just sensory information to allow physical travel.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a>, since Ban has a visible spatial distortion outside its area of effect your spell probably should as well. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T19:16:14-07:00","id":1064133,"title":"","content":"Oh, so that's what it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T03:44:33-07:00","id":1064243,"title":"","content":"Like I said. The language could use a little clearing. But yea, it literally straightens the path so you see its end no matter how many corners it has. When Inward and Outward Eye is giving you input, this spell changes the area, bends it to your will.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Maybe. The problem is that this distortion is pretty massive. Inception style in some cases. If it is visible as a base effect it should definitely have a reach option to not be seen. I prefer the other way, like in Co-location where overlap is visible only when you want. You might be right, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T18:40:01-07:00","id":1064599,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gravitic Ward (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Shielding</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span><br /> <br /> Gravity is just another Force, and while a proficient Mage may seek to redirect it as he desires, there may come times when you will simply want protection from any harm it might occasion.<br /> For the duration of the spell, the subject is immune to all Bashing damage suffered from gravitic forces and decreases all Lethal damage from these sources by the spell's Potency.<br /> This is primarily falling damage and the damage from objects falling on you, and does not include non-gravitic damage, such as pneumatic crushing engines, or rock physically thrown downwards by someone (though it will protect against any further kinetic energy imparted to that rock by gravity).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+2 Reach: </b>The subject is immune to Bashing <i>and </i>Lethal damage from gravitic forces, and decreases all Aggravated damage from such sources by the spell's Potency<br /> <br /> <br /> Because one of my players didn't want to have to worry about using Gravity Ruling to create a gravity cushion/pillow, and didn't want to die from a building falling on her.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 03-18-2017, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T20:06:17-07:00","id":1064623,"title":"","content":"There are a lot more applications for not being my affected by gravity than just damage reduction, but it's a good start.<br /> <br /> Then again going fully non-gravitic would get you left behind by the planet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-18-2017, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T20:12:44-07:00","id":1064626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1064623#post1064623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot more applications for not being my affected by gravity than just damage reduction, but it's a good start.<br /> <br /> Then again going fully non-gravitic would get you left behind by the planet...</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that stopping gravity wholesale might be a bit more than shielding can do.<br /> I mean, can using the Practice of Shielding on someone stop them from receiving heat from the environment while still radiating it, causing them to rapidly freeze to death?<br /> Changing the way in which fundamental forces operate with regards to physical objects seems to me to be more in keeping with the Practice of Patterning.<br /> A simple Gravity Ward though I feel should fall under Shielding","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T20:25:15-07:00","id":1064630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1064626#post1064626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that stopping gravity wholesale might be a bit more than shielding can do.<br /> I mean, can using the Practice of Shielding on someone stop them from receiving heat from the environment while still radiating it, causing them to rapidly freeze to death?<br /> Changing the way in which fundamental forces operate with regards to physical objects seems to me to be more in keeping with the Practice of Patterning.<br /> A simple Gravity Ward though I feel should fall under Shielding</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right, Shielding is specifically for protection apparently (Just checked the Practice), but I figured it could be used like that because of some vague recollection of something Dave said about being able to use Shielding to essentially stop being affected by gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T05:43:53-07:00","id":1064718,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In this theme</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stay Down</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Veiling</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A nice way to eliminate someone from a fight is to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>make</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> him stay down. This spell veils gravitic forces from target making it unable maintain vertical position. As long as the spell is in effect the target can\u2019t stand up.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Rapid changes in apparent gravity gives penalty to actions that require focus equal to potency. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:01:29-07:00","id":1064722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1064626#post1064626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling that stopping gravity wholesale might be a bit more than shielding can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? My feeling from 2E is that it got rid of artificial speedbumps and went with straight Practice applications. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, can using the Practice of Shielding on someone stop them from receiving heat from the environment while still radiating it, causing them to rapidly freeze to death? </div> </div> </div>Yes. In the same way that shielding someone from air causes them to suffocate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changing the way in which fundamental forces operate with regards to physical objects seems to me to be more in keeping with the Practice of Patterning. </div> </div> </div>Veil of Moments (Time 2) shields target from being affected by time. It can't age, it can't die from damage that isn't instant death. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T07:56:41-07:00","id":1064751,"title":"","content":"Shield yourself from gravity, and you can be free from it... but the air around you isn't. So I imagine you'd 'swim' through the air, making this spell a poor man's Levitation. <br /> <br /> Seeing as how Ruling gravity can change its direction, and Perfecting/Fraying it can amplify/reduce it, I do wonder what Patterning it can accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T21:14:19-07:00","id":1065585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1064718#post1064718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In this theme</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stay Down</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Forces \u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Veiling</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A nice way to eliminate someone from a fight is to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>make</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> him stay down. This spell veils gravitic forces from target making it unable maintain vertical position. As long as the spell is in effect the target can\u2019t stand up.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Rapid changes in apparent gravity gives penalty to actions that require focus equal to potency. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Because without an ability to sense which way is down or up equilibrium is impossible?<br /> <br /> This makes me wonder what would happen if you veiled kinetic forces, would that render the subject a rag doll unable to move themselves by sensing the direction they apply kinetic force or feel that push back from the matter they are pushing against? I mean I can still see them perceive pain of being shot, nerves are still damaged, but not feel the impact of the bullet. Terrifying magic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-21-2017, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T23:15:50-07:00","id":1065603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065585#post1065585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because without an ability to sense which way is down or up equilibrium is impossible?<br /> <br /> This makes me wonder what would happen if you veiled kinetic forces, would that render the subject a rag doll unable to move themselves by sensing the direction they apply kinetic force or feel that push back from the matter they are pushing against? I mean I can still see them perceive pain of being shot, nerves are still damaged, but not feel the impact of the bullet. Terrifying magic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That's why you fall down when drunk or drugged. And there are real life illneses that affect labyrinth, organ that senses 'down'.<br /> <br /> Yess. 2E is terrifying and first and second arcana dots are really fun to play with.<br /> <br /> Edit: without feeling, cause that's what sensing kinetic forces is, youll get some nasty penalties but proprioception could still work. Maybe add some reach to not feel pain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-21-2017, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T03:41:12-07:00","id":1065653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1065468#post1065468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>The Power of the Will (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</u></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Expression, Survival<br /> The mage raises the subject's Willpower dots by Potency up to the subject's maximum amount of Willpower for the duration of the spell. This maximum is twice the subject's attribute maximum minus lost Willpower dots, or ten for ephemeral entities.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By spending a point Mana, the mage may raise the subject's Willpower dots above their maximum rating.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject also gains a number of Willpower points equal to Potency. The subject loses just as many Willpower points, to a minimum of zero, once the spell ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:11:48-07:00","id":1065689,"title":"","content":"So will I.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1062344-grimoire-of-cursory-dissection-a-thread-for-personal-musings?p=1065261#post1065261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Power Of Mind (Mind 3)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Perfecting</span><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stories of women lifting a car to save her baby are not a myth. Unblocking hidden potential of human body and mind can help a mage in dire times, but it comes with a cost. Every point of potency adds one to the total amount of bonus generated by willpower expenditure which in total cannot exceed 5. Every time WP bonus is applied the target suffers Strain which means taking damage equal potency of this spell.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> By spending a point of Mana, the mage may raise total amount of bonus above 5 </span><br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> The target suffers a weaker version of Strain. Subtract 2 from potency when applying damage.</span><br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> As above but subtract 4 instead of 2.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b>bonus dice can now affect spellcasting. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Surge (Mind 3)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Perfecting</span><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Potency</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">This spell simulates the effect of long lasting and rejuvenating relax. Restore number of Willpower Points equal to potency. Spell doesn't work if the target is in stressful situation e.g combat, chase.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Can be applied in a stressful situation.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Target is pumped and ready. In the next turn he can benefit from WP expenditure for the action of his choosing without actually spending it.</span><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-21-2017, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:20:00-07:00","id":1065691,"title":"","content":"I don't like straight dice adders, and I doubly dislike straight dice adders that can be added directly to magic pools. You can Willpower spellcasting rolls, so Power of Mind basically makes you a better Mage than other mages indirectly, adding another way to destabilize the magic pool system. And yes, I know it isn't infinite increase, but it's already a degenerate one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T05:40:05-07:00","id":1065699,"title":"","content":"You are right. Add +2 Reach: bonus dice can now affect spellcasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:17:22-07:00","id":1065862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065691#post1065691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like straight dice adders, and I doubly dislike straight dice adders that can be added directly to magic pools. You can Willpower spellcasting rolls, so Power of Mind basically makes you a better Mage than other mages indirectly, adding another way to destabilize the magic pool system. And yes, I know it isn't infinite increase, but it's already a degenerate one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the same, however this spell is 'legit', at least with the +2 reach. The way I would handle it as a ST is that I would only allow one diceadding magical effect per roll, meaning it wouldn't stack with exceptional Luck or a prime 2 spell doing the same. I know one could argue that boosting the wp bonus indrectly should mean both should apply, but that's how I'd handle it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I have to say I like power of mind, but I don't think the strain is appropriate for most actions. It's magic, just like gain ability etc. it makes you better at stuff, no need for this backlash. The strain only seems appropriate in situations where you'd use your mind magic to push your body beyond its limits, such as your example of a mother trying to lift a car. Feels to me like that'd be another spell tbh, but in that situation some minor backlash in the form of bashing or even lethal damage depending on what is being done feels appropriate. That said in that case it should not be circumventable with mind magic. You may push yourself to go beyond your limit physically, but your body can't take it and Mind magic can't help with that.<br /> <br /> As for surge... I've seen quite a few effects like that lately and the response in my mind was pretty much &quot;oh hell no&quot; all the time. As allways a storyteller call, but personally I wouldn't allow a spell like that, same as I wouldn't allow a Prime 3 spell that gives you potency mana. As far as the rules go : printed spells assign one reach specifically to regenerate ONE point of wp (not potency points) and even then it is specifically said it comes from a refreshing feeling like having just rested a day, an experience that probably has deminishing returns, which is why I only allow such an effect to help regain wp once a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T11:26:59-07:00","id":1065871,"title":"","content":"I recall a Cr\u00faac ritual in the Circle of the Crone book (VtR) that increases the dice bonus from WP expenditure from 3 to 5 as well as increasing the bonus to resistance attributes from 2 to 3. If I were to rewrite Power of Mind I'd use that as a narrative effect and have Potency determine how many times you can benefit from the spell, similar to how it works for dice tricks and for Fate's Boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:46:53-07:00","id":1065894,"title":"","content":"How would you folks write a spell that replicates the willpower you'd recover after a long period (say 2-3 weeks) of rest?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:50:16-07:00","id":1065896,"title":"","content":"I don't understand what you're looking for. Could you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:51:38-07:00","id":1065897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065862#post1065862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel the same, however this spell is 'legit', at least with the +2 reach. The way I would handle it as a ST is that I would only allow one diceadding magical effect per roll, meaning it wouldn't stack with exceptional Luck or a prime 2 spell doing the same. I know one could argue that boosting the wp bonus indrectly should mean both should apply, but that's how I'd handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW you can rise attributes, skills <i>and </i>dice bonus <i>and </i>penalty reduction <i>and </i>dice effects. RAW. Each of them is a distinct category and is not interfering with the rest so stacking only applies when you have effect affecting the same said category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise I have to say I like power of mind, but I don't think the strain is appropriate for most actions. It's magic, just like gain ability etc. it makes you better at stuff, no need for this backlash. The strain only seems appropriate in situations where you'd use your mind magic to push your body beyond its limits, such as your example of a mother trying to lift a car. Feels to me like that'd be another spell tbh, but in that situation some minor backlash in the form of bashing or even lethal damage depending on what is being done feels appropriate. That said in that case it should not be circumventable with mind magic. You may push yourself to go beyond your limit physically, but your body can't take it and Mind magic can't help with that. </div> </div> </div>You are right. I got that feeling too but for some reason I shut it down :P I can add something like: If the action is physical in nature you suffer Strain.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for surge... I've seen quite a few effects like that lately and the response in my mind was pretty much &quot;oh hell no&quot; all the time. As allways a storyteller call, but personally I wouldn't allow a spell like that, same as I wouldn't allow a Prime 3 spell that gives you potency mana. As far as the rules go : printed spells assign one reach specifically to regenerate ONE point of wp (not potency points) and even then it is specifically said it comes from a refreshing feeling like having just rested a day, an experience that probably has deminishing returns, which is why I only allow such an effect to help regain wp once a day. </div> </div> </div>Don't be that guy. It's better to say &quot;Yes, but..&quot; but in this case there is no <i>but. </i>I can totally see a prime 3 spell, and I have one, that gets you a refund of some mana you spend or even someone else spend. I can translate it and post it here, though I must admit that it requiers some doze of setting assumptions.<br /> Printed spells regenerate one wp because they are not mind spells. Would you say that life can't heal lethal cause you can only heal them naturally once every 2 days? I don't think so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:53:02-07:00","id":1065898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065871#post1065871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall a Cr\u00faac ritual in the Circle of the Crone book (VtR) that increases the dice bonus from WP expenditure from 3 to 5 as well as increasing the bonus to resistance attributes from 2 to 3. If I were to rewrite Power of Mind I'd use that as a narrative effect and have Potency determine how many times you can benefit from the spell, similar to how it works for dice tricks and for Fate's Boons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like this could be a Ruling spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T12:56:21-07:00","id":1065900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065894#post1065894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you folks write a spell that replicates the willpower you'd recover after a long period (say 2-3 weeks) of rest?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. We just did. Surge and Power of the Will can both do that if cast with enough potency. If you are asking for an all or nothing effect it seems to be a Making spell that just gives you <i>all </i>WP. Patterning might give you 2 WP per potency but its not what youre asking I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:52:03-07:00","id":1065952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065897#post1065897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> Don't be that guy. It's better to say &quot;Yes, but..&quot; but in this case there is no <i>but. </i>I can totally see a prime 3 spell, and I have one, that gets you a refund of some mana you spend or even someone else spend. I can translate it and post it here, though I must admit that it requiers some doze of setting assumptions.<br /> Printed spells regenerate one wp because they are not mind spells. Would you say that life can't heal lethal cause you can only heal them naturally once every 2 days? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's better, but not allways feasable. I allowed such spells at mastery where you can literally just create the energies exnihilo. That said I tend to downscale the powerscale of mage games (ascension or awakening) a bit to suit my personal tastes. Many people feel different and that's fine, just my personal way of doing things. That said you're wrong. There is a life spell that does the same, yes, but this is also a reach option for the Mind 3 spell &quot;Clear Thoughts&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T14:55:39-07:00","id":1065958,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would make Power of Mind Duration Primary spell with effect of making your Willpower gaining 9 again, and reach options allowing making it 8 again, boosting the Willpower effect to +5.<br /> Maybe even reach with 1 Mana, gain ability to bestow Rote quality upon one Willpowered roll in exchange for ending the spell prematurely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:12:28-07:00","id":1065969,"title":"","content":"Why would anyone restore their Willpower with magic <i>responsibly</i> when they could instead do something incredibly unwise?<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Snake Within (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Empathy, Streetwise</span></span><br /> <br /> The next time during this spell's duration that its subject would recover Willpower from indulging their Vice, they recover a number of points equal to the spell's Potency, instead of the usual one. If this value exceeds their Resolve, they will develop a Condition related to the rush of the experience, such as Addicted, Guilty, or Obsession.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and 1 mana: </b>The subject may recover Willpower from their Vice under the auspices of this spell even if they have already indulged their Vice in that scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:15:46-07:00","id":1065972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065952#post1065952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's better, but not allways feasable. I allowed such spells at mastery where you can literally just create the energies exnihilo. That said I tend to downscale the powerscale of mage games (ascension or awakening) a bit to suit my personal tastes. Many people feel different and that's fine, just my personal way of doing things. That said you're wrong. There is a life spell that does the same, yes, but this is also a reach option for the Mind 3 spell &quot;Clear Thoughts&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ow, yea. It is. But I don't see a difference between healing body and healing mind. Hmm. I could even see a Mind spell that heals body. Something like a reach option to cut in half the time in which bashing damage heals.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065958#post1065958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I would make Power of Mind Duration Primary spell with effect of making your Willpower gaining 9 again, and reach options allowing making it 8 again, boosting the Willpower effect to +5.<br /> Maybe even reach with 1 Mana, gain ability to bestow Rote quality upon one Willpowered roll in exchange for ending the spell prematurely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that those would be two spells. First would be Generic Dice Trick (Mind 2) - 9 again with 8 again as reach for a number of rolls equal to potency and Generic Rote Quality (Mind 3) - 1 mana of basic cost for rote quality for a number of rolls equal to potency. Both could benefit from reach boosting willpower to +5 I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-21-2017, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:20:49-07:00","id":1065976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065969#post1065969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would anyone restore their Willpower with magic <i>responsibly</i> when they could instead do something incredibly unwise?<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Snake Within (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Empathy, Streetwise</span></span><br /> <br /> The next time during this spell's duration that its subject would recover Willpower from indulging their Vice, they recover a number of points equal to the spell's Potency, instead of the usual one. If this value exceeds their Resolve, they will develop a Condition related to the rush of the experience, such as Addicted, Guilty, or Obsession.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and 1 mana: </b>The subject may recover Willpower from their Vice under the auspices of this spell even if they have already indulged their Vice in that scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very nice. Mana cost might be not necessary like in Devouring the Slain. And I would add reach to prevent the condition. And then the next one to get a positive one in the process. Because why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:34:58-07:00","id":1065990,"title":"","content":"Those reach options would be<br /> 1.) Responsible<br /> 2.) Wise<br /> And that's the sort of Guardians thinking I will not tolerate under my roof.<br /> <br /> (But really, I would not do that because why should a spell include Reach options that make it less exciting? Additional Reach options that rob a spell of its texture may be desirable to characters but they're meh for table play, where we want more Reaching to be <i>risky </i>and <i>irresponsible </i>and we want the use of magic to involve the occasional unintended consequence.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:48:49-07:00","id":1066002,"title":"","content":"I totally understand you and I like your spell. But Reach effect are made to bypass initial limitations of the spell. Characters are mages who like their spell safe and have means to do it. Besides it's 3 Reaches without spell factors. Either have it as a Rote or cast it with risk of paradox. The more Reach effects to tease the player the better IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:53:17-07:00","id":1066007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065896#post1065896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what you're looking for. Could you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you use a spell to recover willpower as 'easily' as you can recover health after a fight. There's no reason in particular why I need such a spell I was just planning out eventualities before my PC's try something.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:01:50-07:00","id":1066012,"title":"","content":"Any spell can potentially recover willpower if you score Exceptional Success on it. Mind 3 has a spell that allows you to restore Willpower as a reach option; cast it multiple times, and you are good to go.<br /> <br /> Mages generally are less limited by their ability to recover WP, and more by their ability to have only as many of them on them at once. They can easily recover when they have a minute or two of calm, but when they need Willpower, they can burn through their whole tank in round or two [no, seriously].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:04:33-07:00","id":1066015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1066007#post1066007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you use a spell to recover willpower as 'easily' as you can recover health after a fight. There's no reason in particular why I need such a spell I was just planning out eventualities before my PC's try something.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a spell that straight up grants Willpower points the way Knit and Mend heals damage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1065689#post1065689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Surge (Mind 3)</b>[/SIZE]<br /> <b>Practice:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Perfecting</span><br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Potency</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">This spell simulates the effect of long lasting and rejuvenating relax. Restore number of Willpower Points equal to potency. Spell doesn't work if the target is in stressful situation e.g combat, chase.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Can be applied in a stressful situation.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Target is pumped and ready. In the next turn he can benefit from WP expenditure for the action of his choosing without actually spending it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>But if you want to use it after a fight you could just as well recast your Praxes until you've filled up due to Exceptional Successes as WHW points out. Then you wouldn't have the Mind 3 requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:10:32-07:00","id":1066018,"title":"","content":"Devouring the Slain also allows you to plunder victims Willpower instead of health. <br /> It's really fun when used together with a big fuckoff nuke that leaves targets Stunned, because if you drained their Willpower to 0 [and Storyteller system tends to assume non PCs have a WP or two at max, maybe three if they are important, so nuking their willpower is easier than nuking their whole healthbar], they can't break the Stun with Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:39:35-07:00","id":1066762,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Transplant Momentum</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Weaving</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cWhen fighting a Disciple of Forces make sure he can\u2019t use it on you.\u201d</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - someone who got propelled by a train and lived to tell a tale. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With this spell a mage can weave and exchange momentum of two objects. If affecting a moving train and a bench the train will stop in minute and the bench will leap in a geographical direction of where the vehicle was heading, most likely ripping itself from the ground.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When exchanging momentum objects slow down or speed up 10 Speed per turn. Their size matters too. Calculate the difference in size: add to Speed of the smaller one with 1 to 10 ratio, and subtract from the Speed of the larger one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example:</span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 452px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Target</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Speed</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After Exchange</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Difference </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">in Size</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exchange </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">with Size</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Motorcycle</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">40</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">120</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">150</span></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Car</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">120</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">40</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-3</span></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">10</span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Firstly exchange unaltered Speed and then translate difference in Size.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exchange is now considerably faster. Multiply Speed exchange by potency. At potency 3 it will be 30 Speed per turn.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+<b>1 Reach:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mage can now determine new vectors for movement. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s a quite complicated spell and I\u2019m not sure if everything is clear or even 'correct' but I've been meaning to write it down for quite a while. I can imagine that Adept version of the spell would have the exchange speed of NOW. It would be fun.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:50:09-07:00","id":1066828,"title":"","content":"<b>Under the Bushel (Mind 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <br /> This spell hides will of the subject from others making it impossible to be aware of CoW against them. Others also can't spend Willpower on the test. ST makes a hidden roll of Power Stat + Power for an unaware participants.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By blurring the edges of mages will the spell assures victory in uncertain circumstances. In the case of a draw the subject wins or rather the opponent loses by giving up too early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-23-2017, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:24:35-07:00","id":1067090,"title":"","content":"I think this would be a prime 2 spell, not mind. The reach option is also not appropriate for a veiling effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:24:46-07:00","id":1067135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067090#post1067090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this would be a prime 2 spell, not mind. The reach option is also not appropriate for a veiling effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It can be both, I went with less obvious one. As to the reach option it's just a matter of fluffing it up.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By blurring the edges of mages will the spell assures victory in uncertain circumstances. In the case of a draw the subject wins or rather the opponent loses by giving up too early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:33:39-07:00","id":1067669,"title":"","content":"<b>Expert System </b>(Mind 3, Forces 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Computer, Expression<br /> <br /> This spell modifies a computing device by adding a program to it that provides the functionality of an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expert_system\" target=\"_blank\">expert system</a> for any skill chosen by the caster. For the duration of the spell, if the device's user is able to use the device as a tool when rolling the relevant skill, the device provides a bonus to the roll equal to Potency. The device's user must have at least one dot in the skill to benefit from the expert system. At the end of the spell's duration, the expert system &quot;uninstalls&quot; itself from the device.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may provide an additional expert system that benefits another skill for each additional reach, subdividing Potency among them.<br /> <br /> This spell provides benefits similar to Enhance Skill, but the benefit is not obviously magical in nature. On the downside, you're not going to be able to use it for combat rolls because your smart phone can't talk you through how to throw a punch when you're in the middle of a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 03-24-2017, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:50:54-07:00","id":1067687,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13121_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13121\" data-vbnamecard=\"13121\">galivet</a> I think it should be just Forces 3. Making it be Mind 3 raises the question of why you aren't just using Enhance Skill which won't be obvious either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:52:29-07:00","id":1067688,"title":"","content":"<b>Dress Code </b>(Matter 4, Spirit 1)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Survival, Socialize<br /> <br /> This spell gauges the dominant spirit of the subject's current location and/or social context and modifies the subject's garb to be appropriate for that setting -- even if the mage (or subject) doesn't have a clue what the appropriate garb would be. Add Potency to the mage's social rolls while in the setting. For determining First Impression as part of a social maneuver, consider the subject to have met the criteria for a Good impression.<br /> <br /> A mountain hermit could walk into da club and immediately adopt fashionable club attire, even if she has no idea what that looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 03-24-2017, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:55:04-07:00","id":1067692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067687#post1067687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13121_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13121\" data-vbnamecard=\"13121\">galivet</a> I think it should be just Forces 3. Making it be Mind 3 raises the question of why you aren't just using Enhance Skill which won't be obvious either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imagine that you want to grant a Sleeper ally a skill bonus. If the Sleeper is just suddenly somehow an expert in how to repair an engine or something... that's hard to explain as non-magical.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, imagine that a mage needs to repair an engine while in the company of Sleeper allies who know damn well that the mage doesn't know anything about auto repair. But she does happen to have this very useful app on her phone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:03:44-07:00","id":1067694,"title":"","content":"Also the computing device could be a web server in proximity to the mage, in which case the subject can access the expert system so long as she has internet access and a browser. Maybe you can't cast Enhance Skill on an ally on the other side of the world due to difficulties with sympathetic magic. In that case this comes in pretty handy. The web server could also be accessed by multiple people at once, multiplying its usefulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:27:18-07:00","id":1067708,"title":"","content":"Still probably shouldn't require Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:07:57-07:00","id":1067725,"title":"","content":"Interesting. That's not intuitive for me. For me, saying you can use Forces to create a computer program to grant skill bonuses without incorporating Mind is like saying you can use Matter to create a &quot;lucky coin&quot; or something that grants Boons without incorporating Fate. It really seems like you need the conjunction to bring in the benefit that's under the other Arcana's purview.<br /> <br /> Is there already a thread on this somewhere I can read to understand? If not maybe I'll start one so we don't continue this here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:25:31-07:00","id":1067732,"title":"","content":"Forces can create or rewrite programs, if all the program is doing is providing an equipment bonus to the roll because it can talk you through the steps...Mind shouldn't be necessary. It's not actually affecting your Mind, it's just a really good tutor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:00:53-07:00","id":1067776,"title":"","content":"You already can modify items using Matter to provide dice tricks and equipment bonuses, so it's kinda on the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:24:59-07:00","id":1067787,"title":"","content":"I'd put it at Forces 3 instead of 2 though since you're Perfecting the program's function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:27:15-07:00","id":1067962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067708#post1067708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still probably shouldn't require Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does the Forces arcanum get the informations about Politics in this case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:17:18-07:00","id":1067966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067962#post1067962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does the Forces arcanum get the informations about Politics in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>The internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:36:01-07:00","id":1067974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067966#post1067966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The internet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great. Generating an expert program is impossible without a highly advanced (as in 'intelligent') sorting algorithm and then actually sorting it. If it is true you could also make this spell:<br /> <br /> <b>Jesus Christ... It's Jason Bourne!</b> <b>(Forces 3)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <br /> By connecting to the digital media around him the mage is able to track target by analyzing his social media accounts, network activities, facial recognitions, gsm, gps and satellite feedback scans.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Something, something, leave no trace of database access.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:48:42-07:00","id":1067979,"title":"","content":"I think the Expert Program would be best used on specific programs and the spell boosts its usefulness, so if you had programs that have access to that info you could do that. Heck you could do that anyway because with Forces 2 you have admin access to everything on the web anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:51:38-07:00","id":1067980,"title":"","content":"Unless you can define every aspect of the tutor/research program you're creating? You're going to need to add Mind 5 to make it an A.I.<br /> Otherwise you're essentially just using Magic to code, which while efficient, doesn't let you do anything you couldn't already do.<br /> I don't think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:16:56-07:00","id":1068090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067980#post1067980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you can define every aspect of the tutor/research program you're creating? You're going to need to add Mind 5 to make it an A.I.<br /> Otherwise you're essentially just using Magic to code, which while efficient, doesn't let you do anything you couldn't already do.<br /> I don't think.</div> </div> </div> </div>AI is getting pretty advanced but it's also clear they're not thinking entities in their own right yet. Still, a data analysis engine that's been Supernally boosted ought to be able to do some pretty crazy things imo. An enhanced equipment bonus doesn't really seem that far fetched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:02:33-07:00","id":1069276,"title":"","content":"Hi wise ones.<br /> I was wondering about how to manage a Veiling Life spell to render a living veign &quot;hidden&quot; or undetectable, like Hidden Hoard (Matter oo). But I have some questions on this regard:<br /> Would only affect a naked person?, if the person has clothes, would the spell fail?, what happens if the subject grabs an object or moves?<br /> <br /> I would rule the spell provides full ocultation for a naked subject. If the subject wear clothes or grabs an item, the spell will begin to fade and the onlookers will detect the subject's presence, but they won't be able to tell who is. Mostly like a ghost presence. If the spell subject drops the item or undresses, he will become undetectable again.<br /> <br /> I will be happy to read how you would manage this spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:30:53-07:00","id":1069288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1069276#post1069276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi wise ones.<br /> I was wondering about how to manage a Veiling Life spell to render a living veign &quot;hidden&quot; or undetectable, like Hidden Hoard (Matter oo). But I have some questions on this regard:<br /> Would only affect a naked person?, if the person has clothes, would the spell fail?, what happens if the subject grabs an object or moves?<br /> <br /> I would rule the spell provides full ocultation for a naked subject. If the subject wear clothes or grabs an item, the spell will begin to fade and the onlookers will detect the subject's presence, but they won't be able to tell who is. Mostly like a ghost presence. If the spell subject drops the item or undresses, he will become undetectable again.<br /> <br /> I will be happy to read how you would manage this spell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have two options. First is to hide a living target from anything, which leaves everything else visible. Everything you carry, including clothes will be visible and will trigger a lot of breaking points before quickly dies with dissonance if your not naked.<br /> Second is to simply veil anyyything from life. You can veil, yourself, your clothes and possible anything you take in hand with some little Reach. No living organism will notice you or your belongings but cameras <i>will</i> register you.<br /> Third, secret option, is to hide life from specific subject. So when you have, lets say, a guard to pass you can cast it on him and make him not see your whole cabal stomping in front of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T06:42:17-07:00","id":1069293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067725#post1067725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. That's not intuitive for me. For me, saying you can use Forces to create a computer program to grant skill bonuses without incorporating Mind is like saying you can use Matter to create a &amp;quot;lucky coin&amp;quot; or something that grants Boons without incorporating Fate. It really seems like you need the conjunction to bring in the benefit that's under the other Arcana's purview.<br /> <br /> Is there already a thread on this somewhere I can read to understand? If not maybe I'll start one so we don't continue this here.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it like saying you can use Matter to make a coin that favors one side, like making both sides heads. Or more relevant saying you could use use matter to make a pair of sneakers and black outfit to help with stealth, or using Matter to make a poncho to help with survival.<br /> <br /> The point is equipment gives bonuses to skills, and Matter can make objects, and programs are equipment too, and are governed by Forces.<br /> <br /> Dice Bonuses reflect many different things, just because mind grants skills (which os mechanically reflected as dice rolled for a skill) doesn't mean it monopolies ways to add dice to that roll. In this system even having a well formed plan counts as equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:13:54-07:00","id":1069613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1069293#post1069293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it like saying you can use Matter to make a coin that favors one side, like making both sides heads. Or more relevant saying you could use use matter to make a pair of sneakers and black outfit to help with stealth, or using Matter to make a poncho to help with survival.<br /> <br /> The point is equipment gives bonuses to skills, and Matter can make objects, and programs are equipment too, and are governed by Forces.<br /> <br /> Dice Bonuses reflect many different things, just because mind grants skills (which os mechanically reflected as dice rolled for a skill) doesn't mean it monopolies ways to add dice to that roll. In this system even having a well formed plan counts as equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highly disagree with this, yes forces can make the bits in a computer turn on and off, but without a base knowledge of what order to turn them on and off in you cant make a program any more that sending electrical current down a line doesn't mean you are sending mores code. Mind gives skills, other Arcana can increase and already existing skill with equipment bonuses but not grant a skill that you do not already have. One dot in computers then go for the gusto forces can increase your ability with equipment bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-28-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:14:51-07:00","id":1070078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1069613#post1069613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I highly disagree with this, yes forces can make the bits in a computer turn on and off, but without a base knowledge of what order to turn them on and off in you cant make a program any more that sending electrical current down a line doesn't mean you are sending mores code. Mind gives skills, other Arcana can increase and already existing skill with equipment bonuses but not grant a skill that you do not already have. One dot in computers then go for the gusto forces can increase your ability with equipment bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we both talking about this post? Because it makes a digital piece of equipment via the Forces Arcanum, using Mind Arcanum to access actually data needed to fill in what the caster doesn't innately know. Also has the advantage of being able to hand the device off to someone who isn't even a mage. If we are talking about different spells I am sorry and hope this clears up the confusion by including the reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1067669#post1067669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Expert System </b>(Mind 3, Forces 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Computer, Expression<br /> <br /> This spell modifies a computing device by adding a program to it that provides the functionality of an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expert_system\" target=\"_blank\">expert system</a> for any skill chosen by the caster. For the duration of the spell, if the device's user is able to use the device as a tool when rolling the relevant skill, the device provides a bonus to the roll equal to Potency. The device's user must have at least one dot in the skill to benefit from the expert system. At the end of the spell's duration, the expert system &quot;uninstalls&quot; itself from the device.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may provide an additional expert system that benefits another skill for each additional reach, subdividing Potency among them.<br /> <br /> This spell provides benefits similar to Enhance Skill, but the benefit is not obviously magical in nature. On the downside, you're not going to be able to use it for combat rolls because your smart phone can't talk you through how to throw a punch when you're in the middle of a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T15:03:36-07:00","id":1070321,"title":"","content":"Would Mind 4 be sufficient to grand a Sleeper one of the &quot;psychic&quot; supernatural merits?<br /> Fate 5 recognises the possibility for any individual to develop supernatural abilities, and ultimately psychokinesis and so forth would possible fall under the purview of Mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Unlock Potential </b>(Mind 4)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The Mortal Mind is not quite so frail as many mages would believe, indeed those who investigate such things find it has incredible power hidden within, just waiting to be unlocked.<br /> With this spell, the mage can short-cut the Sleeper or Sleepwalker's mind to access these powers, stepping around whatever inherent blocks stop them from accessing them. For the duration of the spell, the subject gains dots in a &quot;mental&quot; Supernatural Merit equal to the spell's Potency. These can include such merits as Psychometry, Telekinesis, and Telepathy. Due to the Supernatural nature of the these merits for the duration of the spell the subject counts as a Sleepwalker, and does not trigger Paradox or Dissonance until the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Mage may grant the subject an additional psychic Merit, dividing Potency between them, this Reach option may be taken additional times<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>The Psychic Merits do not have their normal Drawbacks<br /> <br /> Additional Arcanum: Fate/Forces/Other 2<br /> The Mage may grant other supernatural merits which relate to phenomenon other than the mind alone, requiring the appropriate Arcanum at 2 dots.<br /> e.g. Forces 2 for Pyrokinesis, and Fate 2 for Thief of Fate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Clarity 03-29-2017, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:47:15-07:00","id":1070955,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <b>Killer Eyes</b>(Death 1*)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling*<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Weaponry, Empathy<br /> <br /> Everything dies, sooner or later. This spell allows the subject to assess how effective would be an attempt at accelerating observed objects, persons, or phenomenas demise. For example, subject might realize that trying to destroy a vampire using weapons and guns are futile at best, and that their efforts should focus on fire and sunlight instead.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Subject gains Potency dots in Killer Instinct Merit for the duration of the spell.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b> As above, but Killer Instinct is Advanced.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Subject gains Potency dots in Demolisher Merit for the duration of the spell.<br /> <b>1 Mana: </b> Subject may ignore observation requirement of both Advanced and normal Killer Instinct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I feel this should be at least 2nd dot spell, but hey, practices are practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:39:44-07:00","id":1070971,"title":"","content":"Granting Merits is generally two dots if I recall correctly. You could have the Demolisher Merit as the main effect and have the purely narrative effect as a Reach.<br /> Btw, where's Killer Instinct from? I don't recognize it and couldn't find it when searching MtA, CofD and Hurt Locker.<br /> Edit: Nevermind. I realized it had to be Beast since you mentioned an Advanced version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-30-2017, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:55:53-07:00","id":1070978,"title":"","content":"How would you fluff the effect as a 2nd dot spell? I'm biased towards it being Unveiling or Knowing, and I can't see it as a Ruling / Shielding / Veiling spell. And I reaaaaaaaaaaally enjoy things that emulate Mystic Eyes Of Death Perception (honestly, I want to write this up as a spell so I can turn it into a Legacy attainment)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:14:45-07:00","id":1070988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1070978#post1070978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you fluff the effect as a 2nd dot spell? I'm biased towards it being Unveiling or Knowing, and I can't see it as a Ruling / Shielding / Veiling spell. And I reaaaaaaaaaaally enjoy things that emulate Mystic Eyes Of Death Perception (honestly, I want to write this up as a spell so I can turn it into a Legacy attainment)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be a Ruling spell that grants you the merits while wielding the thing that's most likely to destroy your foe, the information becomes incidental at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T23:51:25-07:00","id":1071097,"title":"","content":"I don't think a conservative version of the effect is any more impactful than, say, Quantum Flux? If it merely replicated an effect similar to the Merits, would it seem unbalanced?<br /> <br /> I'm avoiding the Advanced version of Killer Instinct (and working from the publicly-posted pass, as I don't own Beast, so I may not know exactly what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> is trying to get from it) as I think its benefits may be too extensive to grant.<br /> ----------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Something Like This (Death \u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Firearms, Survival</span></span><br /> <br /> Everything dies, sooner or later. This spell allows a subject to assess how to best expedite that process. While it is in effect, when the subject focuses upon a person or object, an inkling akin to peripheral mage sight will emphasize any nearby objects or phenomena that threaten that target, with greater stress placed on more dangerous things. A subject might find that their gun feels lighter when trained upon a vampire, while a candle's flame pulses and roils with ill-concealed animosity towards the undead.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject may take turns to aim hand-to-hand attacks. For each bonus die gained from aiming, an attack (ranged or melee) gains Armor-piercing (1), up to a maximum of (3).<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>For each die gained from aiming, reduce the threshold for an attack (ranged or melee) to be considered an exceptional success by one, to a minimum of two successes.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Each action spent aiming grants Potency bonus dice, instead of one, up to the character's limit on bonus dice from aiming.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Increase the subject's limit on bonus dice from aiming (usually +3) by the Potency of the spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the subject scores an exceptional success on an attack, one level of inflicted damage is upgraded one step (bashing to lethal, etc.)<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: If the subject scores an exceptional success on an attack, the Armor rating or Durability of their target is reduced by 1 until they heal or are repaired.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> While under the effects of this spell and using Active Death Sight, a subject is always considered as having spent the last two turns aiming prior to making an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:49:38-07:00","id":1071185,"title":"","content":"The spell should be cast on the thing that's going to be assaulted in order to avoid breaking Scale by allowing the Mage to retarget in the same way that most spells that provide specific information do. I.e. Divination, Mental Scan, Know Spirit, etc. If it provided more general information it'd be fine using the Mage as a subject, but it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:15:44-07:00","id":1071309,"title":"","content":"Mmm I don't like straight dice manipulators. I picked Demolisher and Killer Instinct, because they offer non-dice options that fulfill the concept. I also don't want to make it cast at a scanned target, because I want specifically to make the core of the spell ability to perceive and interact with shatterpoints and (often hidden by the Lie) weak points of stuff around the subject. <br /> Maybe I will redo it as a Weaving Spell, Weaving might work as a Practice for this kind of effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T13:23:01-07:00","id":1071393,"title":"","content":"I think it would need to be made similar to Pierce Deception. So instead of revealing particular information it would tell you how far along things are to death, and reveal with a Reach, symbols that can be pieced together to discover more specific weaknesses without just telling you that you need to get your hands on some cyanide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T14:40:23-07:00","id":1071422,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mana Vine (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Highly valued for producing wine, pastries, jams, or eating out of hand the cultivation of this plant is a large source of income in more rural Consilium. It's important enough that most are willing to turn a blind eye to the troublesome nature of the plant. The spell creates an infestation of thick thorny vines which grow outwards until they've completely encircled a Hallow. Afterwards the plant absorbs <b>Potency </b>points of mana per day up to the limits of the Hallow. The plant produces a single </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">fleshy </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">fist sized fruit pod per day which can be consumed to restore mana equivalent to the amount absorbed. Harvesting the fruit will most likely require additional magic as the plant will violently defend itself from harvest or destruction. If the Hallow goes inactive the plant will wither and die. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The plant is fertile and will spread it's seeds to other Hallows<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The spell is Lasting<br /> <br /> <br /> Comments and critiques? I'm not sure if the should be a Prime conjunctional. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T14:49:48-07:00","id":1071428,"title":"","content":"Would doubtless require Prime 3 conjunctional to Weave the Mana into Tass form, from whatever normal form its Tass would take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:27:55-07:00","id":1071442,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12298\" data-vbnamecard=\"12298\">Enlightened_Milkman</a> Vegetation that grows in Hallows are frequently infused with the ambient mana and become edible tass as a result, that's a fairly natural process already. I'd make it a Life Perfecting spell to make plants growing in a Hallow more likely to suck up the mana than say, the rocks it used to go into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-31-2017, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:42:48-07:00","id":1071451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1071442#post1071442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12298\" data-vbnamecard=\"12298\">Enlightened_Milkman</a> Vegetation that grows in Hallows are frequently infused with the ambient mana and become edible tass as a result, that's a fairly natural process already. I'd make it a Life Perfecting spell to make plants growing in a Hallow more likely to suck up the mana than say, the rocks it used to go into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks for the advice. The central mystery for the next chapter of my game is going to be an homage to 'attack of the killer tomatoes' and this was going to be the spell responsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T21:52:46-07:00","id":1074991,"title":"","content":"This is a... Pretty powerful and customisable spell, given its various reach options.<br /> But I wanted a spell which fused minds together, and this was the best I could come up with bar Archmastery.<br /> <br /> <b>Communion (Mind 4)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve<br /> Verbal communication is such a crude thing, words a poor vehicle for meaning, a direct mind-to-mind link is superior in almost every aspect. That is precisely what this spell achieves, linking the minds of its subjects on an intimate level. Not merely are they capable of reading each other\u2019s thoughts and memories, but instead they experience them as if they were their own. This can allow a rapid communication of nuanced concepts otherwise impossible to express through language. A single discussion held amongst such individuals might not be able to be transcribed in an entire library\u2019s worth of books.<br /> In addition, this permits each individual insight into each other participant\u2019s memories, feelings, perspectives, as well as their current sensory information. Effectively allowing each participant to exist as a combination of multiple people for the duration of the spell. Due to the potential for disagreement and conflict in perspectives, as well as the potentially addictive rush of such sensations, extended or strenuous usage may inflict conditions upon subjects.<br /> When this spell ends, each subject is left with mere memories of what he experienced, unless he immediately spends Experiences to have learned a copy of what was shared with him. Some Mages use this spell to quickly and easily teach Rotes to one another.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Subjects may share the use of each other\u2019s skills<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Subjects may share the use of each other\u2019s mental merits<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Only desired information is shared between subjects, the limits of which may be expressly changed at any time, and may be subconsciously decided upon, rather than explicitly stated.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell cannot impose negative conditions upon its subjects<br /> Additional Arcana:<br /> <b>Prime 1:</b> Subjects may share the use of each other\u2019s Rotes, and may utilise each other\u2019s Mage Sight (but must spend Mana to activate it, if not a Ruling Arcana).<br /> <b>Prime 3: </b>Subjects may perform cooperative, ritual spellcasting, utilising a combination of the Arcana of the participants, so long as each has each requisite Arcana at at least one dot. E.g. To cast a Prime 4, Matter 3, Mind 5 spell, all participants would need Prime 1, Matter 1, and Mind 1, but the levels of Prime 4, Matter 3, and Mind 5 could be contributed by separate Mages.<br /> <b>Prime 4: </b>As above, however each participant need not have at least 1 dot in each requisite Arcanum.<br /> <b>Space 2: </b>Subjects may share use of Sympathetic Links<br /> <b>Fate 4: </b>Subjects may share use of Destiny<br /> <b>Time 3: </b>Such is the speed at which communication is achieved that all attempts at social interaction between subjects are performed as instant actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 04-08-2017, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T21:40:58-07:00","id":1075360,"title":"","content":"Is adding Toxicity to something (for example, making air Toxic) Matter 3 or Matter 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T22:21:36-07:00","id":1075376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1075360#post1075360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is adding Toxicity to something (for example, making air Toxic) Matter 3 or Matter 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's changing the properties of matter, without changing the material into something else, which means Weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T22:22:35-07:00","id":1075378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1075360#post1075360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is adding Toxicity to something (for example, making air Toxic) Matter 3 or Matter 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Matter 3 to make something toxic in much the same way Life 3 can give someone tentacles. You're not 'changing' the subject you're altering a property of the subject that's under the domain of the arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:57:12-07:00","id":1076636,"title":"","content":"Would you say Weaving to fuse two distinct minds into a single integrated mind, e.g. for forming a hive mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:24:37-07:00","id":1076641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1076636#post1076636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you say Weaving to fuse two distinct minds into a single integrated mind, e.g. for forming a hive mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaving alters properties, without changing the subject(s) into something new.<br /> I think you'd need patterning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T21:40:19-07:00","id":1078750,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to come up with some Ruling effects for Prime, specifically its purview over magic. These would be effects that provide a degree of control over a spell without fundamentally altering its abilities.<br /> <br /> Could a Ruling Prime spell affect another spell in a similar way to Paradox? Examples:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Impose a dice penalty equal to Potency to the roll to cast a spell (targeting the spell's Imago I suppose)</li> <li>Win a CoW to change the target of a spell -- either a spell that is in the midst of being cast, or a spell that has not yet exhausted its duration (e.g. a relinquished spell)</li> <li>Change one spell factor of a spell by one rank per Potency</li> </ol>These effects could be useful if the caster has not the arcana needed to Counterspell, or (for 2 and 3) the spell has already been cast, and caster is not able to succeed at Supernal Dispellation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T21:47:38-07:00","id":1078751,"title":"","content":"Similar question, but this time Veiling effects for Prime, specifically it's purview over Magic.<br /> <br /> How about, &quot;conceal a target from magic&quot;, i.e. from being incorporated into a spell Imago. The general effect would be that the subject of the Veiling spell cannot be targeted by another spell unless the caster of the other spell wins a CoW against the caster of the Veiling spell.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think this ought to be kosher; it actually seems a touch less far-reaching than Incognito Presence. Surely a mage cannot target the subject of the Incognito Presence spell without first winning the CoW to notice that subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-15-2017, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:34:49-07:00","id":1078768,"title":"","content":"1) I assume that would be a function of a Shielding spell, might be better handled simply by using Wards and Signs<br /> 2) I don't see why not.<br /> 3) You can only change factors by decreasing them, and I assume this would be a spell that counters spells as cast so probably requires a Reach for Reflexive, but otherwise probably yes.<br /> <br /> Second post: Sounds like it would definitely work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T23:18:32-07:00","id":1078781,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback.<br /> <br /> One more question: A Perfecting effect for Prime, &quot;Improved Active Mage Site&quot;. Something along the lines of, no Willpower cost for AMS for the duration of the spell, and reduce the mana cost for incorporating Common and Inferior arcana by one per Potency.<br /> <br /> Seem okay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:16:18-07:00","id":1078792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1078781#post1078781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the feedback.<br /> <br /> One more question: A Perfecting effect for Prime, &quot;Improved Active Mage Site&quot;. Something along the lines of, no Willpower cost for AMS for the duration of the spell, and reduce the mana cost for incorporating Common and Inferior arcana by one per Potency.<br /> <br /> Seem okay?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems right. But it maybe should cost mana to cast. You can see benefits after few scenes of using AMS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:04:39-07:00","id":1078825,"title":"","content":"I recently had a sleepless night so I wrote a few spells at around six in the morning. They might not make as much sense as I thought at the moment. In fact, I almost expect them not to:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Channel Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure (or Resistance for Strix)<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Survival<br /> This spell allows the mage to draw Vitae into her Pattern from a collection of Vitae (such as Vitae infused blood or shadow), or from her Pattern to a vampire, Strix, or suitable receptacle. The mage may transfer an amount of Vitae equal to the spell\u2019s Potency. However, she cannot channel more Vitae per turn than her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn rate.<br /> Vitae stored within the mage\u2019s Pattern remains even after the Duration expires; however, she can only hold a combined amount of Mana and Vitae equal to her Gnosis-derived maximum Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may ignore her Mana per turn limit, channeling as much Vitae as she desires as an instant action.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may siphon Vitae directly from a vampire or Strix, though they may Withstand the spell with Stamina or Resistance respectively. The Vitae channeled comes in the form it is bound in; blood for vampires and smoke-like shadow matter for Strix, and as such cannot be directly drawn into the mage's Pattern wthout additional Potency or a second application of this spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may spend Vitae to heal herself or another living subject of two points of bashing or one point of lethal per Vitae.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Vitae Drain (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unravelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion<br /> The mage drains the very life energies that sustain a living Pattern. This involves rending that Pattern, causing horribly painful internal wounds and unspecific tissue damage. This is an attack spell, inflicting lethal damage equal to its Potency. In addition the spell generates an amount of Vitae equal to the damage inflicted, drawing it into her Pattern, however, she can only hold a combined amount of Mana and Vitae equal to her Gnosis-derived maximum Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage draws Vitae from the target in physical form. The damage inflicted is due to blood loss as the victim hemorrhages Vitae-filled blood that seeps from a wound or orifice of the mage's choice, instead of being drawn into the mage's Pattern. Can only be used on living victims.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Death \u2022\u2022:</b> The mage draws Vitae from the target in shadow form. The damage inflicted causes internal wounds and unspecified tissue damage as Vitae-filled shadowy smoke flows from a wound or orifice of the mage's choice, instead of being drawn into the mage's Pattern. Can only be used on living victims.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By carefully unravelling the victim's Pattern the mage causes two points of bashing damage per Potency instead of lethal.<br /> <b>Add Arcanum \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>; the mage can cast this spell on ephemeral, supernal or unliving beings under the Arcanum's purview. For example Death for ghosts, vampires and Strix, Mind for goetia, Spirit for spirits and werewolves, and Prime for supernal entities.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Vitae Fountain (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult<br /> This spell generates a quantity of Vitae equal to the spell\u2019s Potency within the subject\u2019s Pattern.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell generates the Vitae in physical form. Instead of forming inside the subject's Pattern the Vitae forms a pool of thick blood. When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, so does the created Vitae.<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Death \u2022\u2022:</b> This spell generates the Vitae in shadow form. Instead of forming inside the subject's Pattern the Vitae forms a cloud of shadowy smoke. When the spell\u2019s Duration expires, so does the created Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I realise that these spells work under the assumption that Vitae falls squarely under Life despite being used by two highly Death related creatures, and that Death is only involved when it's bound in Strix's shadow form. Another interpretation could be that Vitae falls under both Life and Death since it's life that is taken by inflicting damage, and used to fuel undead and shadow creatures.<br /> Another less supported assumption that I don't know if I personally agree with is that Vitae doesn't need to be bound in blood or shadow. Thinking about it after some sleep I'd remove the ability to store Vitae in the mage's Pattern. In that case I'd add a spell for creating receptacles for Vitae, something like Theban Sorcery's Vitae Reliquary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-15-2017, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:04:37-07:00","id":1078890,"title":"","content":"I would leave whether or not these spells can fall under Life to ST discretion; reasonable people can disagree. Vitae's main properties when applied to a mortal are to extend lifespan and grant improved physical abilities and both of those effects fall under the purview of Life. But it also has a Mind-like effect, the Blood Bond.<br /> <br /> Vitae Drain seems like a Patterning spell that transforms common life energy into Vitae. I advise you to consider what it would take to transform Blood into a new substance that perfectly emulates the properties of Vitae as defined in the rulebook, build the spell that way for the mechanics purposes, and then the RP flavor is that it yields VItae (walks like a duck, quacks like a duck...).<br /> <br /> Same recommendation for Vitae Fountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T08:44:34-07:00","id":1078904,"title":"","content":"I actually wrote Patterning in my notes but changed it to Unravelling when posting here since it's based on Life-Force Assault (to the point where I previously had it named Life-Force Drain) and the fact that you basically rip the Vitae from the victim's Pattern.<br /> <br /> Now I'm tempted to make a Death/Life vampiric legacy with Attainments based around stealing and using Vitae, who technically aren't Reapers because they're only using the life-force of people instead of souls. (Unless I add something like the Strix Dread Power Soul Bite that farms souls for Vitae.) Definitely a Lich legacy since there's no way they wouldn't have all the upsides of being a ghoul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T14:36:37-07:00","id":1079047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1078904#post1078904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually wrote Patterning in my notes but changed it to Unravelling when posting here since it's based on Life-Force Assault (to the point where I previously had it named Life-Force Drain) and the fact that you basically rip the Vitae from the victim's Pattern.<br /> <br /> Now I'm tempted to make a Death/Life vampiric legacy with Attainments based around stealing and using Vitae, who technically aren't Reapers because they're only using the life-force of people instead of souls. (Unless I add something like the Strix Dread Power Soul Bite that farms souls for Vitae.) Definitely a Lich legacy since there's no way they wouldn't have all the upsides of being a ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine such a legacy would also be branded left handed fairly quickly. As for vitae I theorize vitae is what is leftover if your manage to perfect blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T16:08:08-07:00","id":1079098,"title":"","content":"That's really not a bad idea at all. And yes, they'd definitely be branded Left-Handed even if it's completely possible to take Vitae from willing subjects, from yourself, or even creating it directly with Making. And Liches are listed in the Left-Handed section even though they seem to be somewhat tolerated depending on how their lichdom is sustained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T10:42:00-07:00","id":1079429,"title":"","content":"This One Thread (Space)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Empathy, Investigation, Occult<br /> <br /> The function of this spell is to glean information about the Sympathetic thread that forms between a Mage and someone else that he's interacting with. By monitoring this he can gain insight into how others look at him adding a dice bonus to his next use of the Empathy skill equal to Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T11:39:45-07:00","id":1079448,"title":"","content":"I believe that you could instead have a number of direct questions regarding the relationship answered by the ST equal to Potency. That's both more useful and more inline with other similar powers on record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:42:00-07:00","id":1079497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1079448#post1079448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that you could instead have a number of direct questions regarding the relationship answered by the ST equal to Potency. That's both more useful and more inline with other similar powers on record.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a narrower application of a regular one dot dice effect, I don't see the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:50:23-07:00","id":1079747,"title":"","content":"No controversy that the spell is fine as-is so long as the purpose of the Empathy roll is inline with the spell description. Might want to clarify whether the Empathy roll must be made during the spell's Duration. I think that gaining useful knowledge about something is always a Lasting effect.<br /> <br /> Another option, you could grant the 9-again effect for all Social skill rolls affecting the subject that are influenced by how the subject sees the caster. 8-again with a Reach. I think that understanding the mutual connection could be just as useful to Subterfuge or Socialize or even Animal Ken if the subject is an animal.<br /> <br /> But yeah the effect you described is fine; it's right out of the rules: &quot;The spell grants a one-die bonus or penalty, deals one point of weapon damage, or heals one wound.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T05:06:54-07:00","id":1079750,"title":"","content":"That's starting to encroach on the 3-dot spell Perfect Sympathy.<br /> While Knowing is a great practice, I think you should definitely limit any mechanical benefits from using that Practice aside from purely getting knowledge. Not even Mind Knowing is capable of gaining bonus dice on Empathy and Subterfuge. That's the effect of Telepathy, a Ruling spell. And if Mind has that limit then Knowing on a Sympathetic Connection should really, really not be able to grant bonus dice, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-17-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T05:14:34-07:00","id":1079752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1079750#post1079750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's starting to encroach on the 3-dot spell Perfect Sympathy. While Knowing is a great practice, I think you should definitely limit any mechanical benefits from using that Practice aside from purely getting knowledge. Not even Mind Knowing is capable of gaining bonus dice on Empathy and Subterfuge. That's the effect of Telepathy, a Ruling spell. And if Mind has that limit then Knowing on a Sympathetic Connection should really, really not be able to grant bonus dice, imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence using the bonus dice truck instead of lowering the reroll thresh hold and keeping the skills the spell applies to very limited. Sympathetic threads carry emotional information, and this is supposed to monitor only that information which is pertinent to what's going on between Mage and someone he's interacting with. It being a building block toward Perfect Sympathy is actually a good thing imo since that spell is much more potent and widely applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T06:54:36-07:00","id":1079773,"title":"","content":"In my suggestion I compared the spell to Craftsman's Eye, which is a Knowing spell. I feel like &quot;look a tool and completely understand it&quot; is analogous to &quot;look at an interpersonal connection and completely understand it.&quot;<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would at least allow the deep understanding of the interpersonal connection garnered through the use of this spell to serve as a <b>circumstance bonus</b> to subsequent skill rolls.<br /> <br /> Trying to achieve balance between different arcana is... not something that interests me. You can in the right circumstances do things with Spirit 1 applied to matter that Matter can't do without higher-rank practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 04-17-2017, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T07:37:55-07:00","id":1079784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1079752#post1079752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence using the bonus dice truck instead of lowering the reroll thresh hold and keeping the skills the spell applies to very limited. Sympathetic threads carry emotional information, and this is supposed to monitor only that information which is pertinent to what's going on between Mage and someone he's interacting with. It being a building block toward Perfect Sympathy is actually a good thing imo since that spell is much more potent and widely applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with the notion that Knowing on a sympathetic connection would grant that much information. The nature of the relationship is a part of the connection, but that's the extent of information you can get. There's a reason you need Perfecting for Perfect Sympathy. And you can still only do it on Strong Connections (and Medium with a Reach).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1079773#post1079773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to achieve balance between different arcana is... not something that interests me. You can in the right circumstances do things with Spirit 1 applied to matter that Matter can't do without higher-rank practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, in this case compare Mind being able to pick the required information straight out of the mind of a person with this application of Space that would pick information from a source that in turn only gets limited information from the person.<br /> <br /> Of course, you're all free to disagree and run it however you think is best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:22:11-07:00","id":1079800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1079784#post1079784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with the notion that Knowing on a sympathetic connection would grant that much information. The nature of the relationship is a part of the connection, but that's the extent of information you can get. There's a reason you need Perfecting for Perfect Sympathy. And you can still only do it on Strong Connections (and Medium with a Reach).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't grant that much information though, it specifically only grants just enough information for you to get a deeper level of understanding of your relationship to the person you're interacting with without rendering changes on either of you on a fundamental level like Perfect Sympathy. It doesn't even magically grant that information, the magic simply facilitates one particular kind of skill that could grant that kind of information regardless of the use of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:55:42-07:00","id":1080298,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a><br /> Really like the idea of exchanging momentums. But why not just make it so they exchange their speed at a rate of Potency x 2 or similar?<br /> I know there are some things about mass, but maybe would have so little effect that making extra rules for it would make the spell much more complicated?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12298\" data-vbnamecard=\"12298\">Enlightened_Milkman</a><br /> I really like your Mana Vine spell, but couldn't you do something similar to an already existing plant? Also, Prime would definatly be needed.<br /> <br /> But, a dot 5 spell like this could be made. Maybe where it doesn't have to be near a Hallow. Where it actually generates the mana from absorbing allot of the ambient mana from the world or ley lines. Maybe it could even spread along ley lines.<br /> \u200b <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\">================================================== ==============</div> </div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">New Spells from me</span></b></div> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spider Sense (Life \u25cf)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Survival, Animal Ken<br /> <br /> By keeping tap on the adrenalin levels in living beings around her, the subject becomes more aware of those who would bring her harm. The subject gains a bonus to notice dangers like ambushes or someone feeling highly aggressive, equal to the spells Potency. Logically, this spell won\u2019t alert the subject when the beings aren't alive.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> When a fight breaks out, the subject is able to get that extra advantage. If a fight starts while this spell is active, the subject also gains a bonus to Initiative equal to the spells Potency.<br /> <br /> ====================<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Predator\u2019s Cloak (Life \u25cf\u25cf)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Stealth, Streetwise<br /> <br /> The best way to move among the sleeping masses is to not be seen at all. The subject is shrouded from being noticed by living beings and Life magic. Any supernatural effect that would detect her provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> This spell does not prevent those around her from noticing the effects of the subjects passing. Like speaking, stepping on grass, ect. Which in the case of sleepers, could trigger Dissonannce.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: The target of the spell leaves no scent trail.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>NOTE:</b> </span>I am not sure about the Reach. But I really would love more options for the player.<br /> <br /> ====================<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Live the Other Side (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve/Rank<br /> <br /> The subject is completely turned into a rank 1 spirit and follows all the rules for beings made of ephemera. Essence bleed in the material world,uses essence for sustenance, needs payment for its help, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>For Living beings</b><ul><li>\u200b<i>Power: Highst of Intelligence, Strength or Presence</i></li> <li><i>Finesse:</i> Highst of Wits, Dexterity or Manipulation<br /> <i>Resistance: </i>Highst of Resolve, Stamina or Composure</li> <li><i>Influence:</i> The target gains one Influence chosen by the mage</li> <li><i>Numina:</i> The target gains one Numina chosen by the mage.</li> <li><i>Manifestations:</i> The target gains the Twilight Form Manifestation along with one more Manifestation chosen by the mage.</li> <li><i>Ban &amp; Bane:</i> The Ban and Bane of the subject becomes something appropriate to their personality, wants and fears.</li> <li><i>Skills:</i> Living beings lose their skills and use Power + Finesse instead. If the action they are taking doesn\u2019t match with their \u201cspirit type\u201d, the ST may add penalties.</li> <li>Resonant Essence for the subject is dependent on its nature. A human subject is Resonant with humans and mages is Resonant with magic (ST\u2019s discretion).</li> <li>A mage that transforms into a spirit loses access to his magic for the duration of the spell.</li> </ul><b>For Spirits</b><ul><li><i>Attributes: </i>Divide the spirits Power, Finesse and Resistance among the appropriate Attributes (See above), adding to those that would fit the spirits nature.</li> <li><i>Skills:</i> The spirit gains skills fitting to its nature, were those that suit it most being around 3 or more dots.</li> <li><i>Death: </i>If a spirit is killed while being \u201calive\u201d, they simply turn back into a spirit when the spell ends.</li> </ul><b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject gains one additional Numina/Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject gains one additional Influence.<br /> <b>+2 Reach, 1 Mana:</b> The Mage may turn the subject into a Rank 2 spirit and the target adds the spells Potency as a bonus to Power, Finesse and Resistance. The target also gains an additional dot of Influence.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf:</b> if the mage is a subject, she will still have access to her Arcana\u2019s, however, she is unable to spend Mana.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">NOTE:</span></b> I had many ideas for how this could be done, but I think this might be the simplest, and most balanced one... &quot;Might&quot; being the <i>magic</i> word<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>UPDATE:</b></span> Reworked it abit after Five Eyes reminded me that Spirits usually have a certain amount of Attributes and a maximum.<br /> ====================<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hide Ban &amp; Bane (Spirit \u25cf\u25cf)</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Subterfuge, Occult, Survival<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Spirit Rank<br /> <br /> Another tool that a Mage can use when negotiating with Spirits is to offer protecting their secrets from their enemies. The mage hides the mystical ban, banes, influences or Numina of the subject amongst other information. The spell obscures up to one piece of information per Potency. This doesn't actually do anything to remove or mitigate their effects. Any attempt to discern those qualities either through mundane research is reduced to a chance die. Supernatural powers that may uncover the information cause a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can provide false results for each piece of information hidden by the spell. If the mage wins the clash of wills or the mundane research rolls fail, the false information is provided instead of the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 04-21-2017, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:00:52-07:00","id":1080429,"title":"","content":"This is more of an update than anything but...<br /> <br /> <b>Petrification (Life </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>+ Matter</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Subterfuge, Occult<br /> <br /> Calling on the legendary power of the Gorgons, the Mage turns flesh to stone with their terrible gaze. The target turns into a statue of themselves, with Structure and Durability as appropriate for a solid stone object of their size and composition (marble is very different than granite, for example).<br /> <br /> Targets turned to stone are not dead, but they aren't &quot;alive&quot; either; the target is rendered unconscious and unaware for the Duration of the spell, during which they do not age or hunger. If the statue is damaged in any way, the target receives comparative wounds when turned back to flesh, but is otherwise unaware of any harm done to them. If the damage is repaired before this time, no harm occurs. If sufficient damage is dealt to reduce the statue to Structure 0, the target dies, and reconstructing the statue does nothing to restore them.<br /> <br /> Petrified targets, despite their quiescent state, <i>can</i> be communicated with. Mind spells that allow the reading of minds or telepathic contact can interact with the victim as they would any mortal. The target experiences this as a panicked, dream-like state, though sufficient communications in this manner may allow them to become aware of their situation. If they have any magical abilities, such powers are available to them in these moments.<br /> <br /> Many mystagogue apprentices report never looking at the statues in their local Athenaeum the same way after learning of the existence of this spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T11:09:22-07:00","id":1080433,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6718_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6718\" data-vbnamecard=\"6718\">Neros</a> I know. It's not the most elegant solution but I really like the idea of shooting someone into a building with a train.<br /> Inspiration: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2UHS883_P60\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2UHS883_P60</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T23:46:42-07:00","id":1080761,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6718_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6718\" data-vbnamecard=\"6718\">Neros</a> Thank you, I was thinking perhaps Life\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022;Prime\u2022. The spell would transform existing crops into 'Mana Vine'. The other possibility I was toying with would it being a 'gift' from a summoned Atavism perhaps the denizens of the Primal Wild have a mischievous streak.<br /> <br /> As for the Life 'cloaking' spell. A Thyrsus in my current campaign has been using something like this with surprising creativity.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hiss Filter (Life \u25cf\u25cf)</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Survival, Animal Ken<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <br /> A relatively recent discovery by sleeper science and an obvious truth to the Awakened is that the senses perceive far more than is ever made cognizant by sapient thought. The world at large is constantly attenuated, filtered, and edited long before any 'decision' is made. The spell uses this to the mages advantage. For the duration the subject of the spell simply cannot be perceived by biologic senses.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage can choose specifically what is filtered e.g. deactivating red cone cells and turning someone color blind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:08:29-07:00","id":1080873,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> Which doesn't need to many rules and complicated mechanics to do so (or I don't think so at least). I was brain storming some ideas earlier, but then I thought about the Velocity control spel; couldn't your idea be a Reach for that spell? It does basically exactly what you describe (decrease speed and increase speed). It just needs some additional targets and in case of a train, a increase in its size aspect.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12298\" data-vbnamecard=\"12298\">Enlightened_Milkman</a> Uuuh.. I could defiantly imagine it as something from the primal wilds. Could be a great source for some political turmoil and strif with such a plant.. Until it turns out it might be generating more problems than benefits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For your Hiss Filter, I would say that Mana isn't needed. It basically does the same as the Forces spell, Invisibility, which doesn't require any Mana.<br /> <br /> NOTE: Made some changes to my &quot;Living the other Side&quot; spell. Remembered there was some things that needed addressing like skills and if it is used on a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 04-19-2017, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T09:14:36-07:00","id":1081461,"title":"","content":"&quot;Living the Other Side&quot; seems to produce Attribute totals that are quite high for a &quot;weak&quot; spirit - am I reading it right that a human with 1 in every Attribute will turn into a Rank 1 spirit with more Attribute points than the typical range for Rank 1 ephemerals?<br /> <br /> One thing that came to mind when I read <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a>'s momentum spell was you might be able to crib the scale and relationships from the vehicle crash rules (always tidy) and not worry about gradual exchange. (Size-Scale also effectively limits how much oomph the spell can produce, while still letting you use a passing family sedan at a sedate Speed 60 to launch a pedestrian with Strength 12.)<br /> <br /> <i><b>Snap Exchange (Forces 3 Weaving) </b></i>Each target is pushed or thrown in the direction of movement of the other target with an effective Strength equal to half of the other subject's Size (round down), plus 1 for every 10 full Speed that the donor is moving. If Scale factor is not increased, one of the partners is the caster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T11:58:58-07:00","id":1081522,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> Good idea. I might have overdo my spell just because I wanted same scaling but this seems very elegant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T05:26:03-07:00","id":1081785,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a> Hmm.. That is True.. Gona change it back to Highest of the relevant stat instead and when they use Reach to make it a Rank 2 spirit, they can add the spells potency as well.<br /> <br /> Also, remember they are still limited to the Ranks maximum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 04-21-2017, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T16:32:08-07:00","id":1082051,"title":"","content":"What do you think about copying a spell with Prime? Two dots with knowing all arcana involved and four dots without knowing them. Non Lasting and costs 1 mana. It would be nice to copy imbued items like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:16:24-07:00","id":1082063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082051#post1082051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about copying a spell with Prime? Two dots with knowing all arcana involved and four dots without knowing them. Non Lasting and costs 1 mana. It would be nice to copy imbued items like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it would make all other arcana redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:20:37-07:00","id":1082065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082051#post1082051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about copying a spell with Prime? Two dots with knowing all arcana involved and four dots without knowing them. Non Lasting and costs 1 mana. It would be nice to copy imbued items like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No way. You can duplicate Rotes because they're essentially spell formulae, you can see the pattern that was transcribed and duplicate it in theoretical form without being actually able to perform it.<br /> But duplicating an entire spell including all of the practices for potentially an Arcanum you have literally no comprehension of?<br /> No way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T03:36:43-07:00","id":1082204,"title":"","content":"You don't need to understand a sentence in a different language to copy it. I'm not saying that you are able to change it in any way, just that you could make a copy like with Borrow Sympathy. No factor changing so you would end with e.g. two same Bans in the same place. It has some utility though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082063#post1082063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it would make all other arcana redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Copy' doesn't mean 'cast without them'. You still need the original to perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-22-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T05:21:23-07:00","id":1082214,"title":"","content":"Imagos aren't writing on a piece of paper that you're copying, or someone's slowly spoken sentence you're enunciating.<br /> It's a comprehension of the fundamental principles of reality and the power of the Supernal, manifest through the Gnosis-modified power of the human soul.<br /> <br /> If you went by a strict, and very lenient application of principles, Prime would require the Practice of Making to copy another's Imago.<br /> However even that I would believe wouldn't be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T05:39:44-07:00","id":1082220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082214#post1082214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagos aren't writing on a piece of paper that you're copying, or someone's slowly spoken sentence you're enunciating.<br /> It's a comprehension of the fundamental principles of reality and the power of the Supernal, manifest through the Gnosis-modified power of the human soul.<br /> <br /> If you went by a strict, and very lenient application of principles, Prime would require the Practice of Making to copy another's Imago.<br /> However even that I would believe wouldn't be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that I wanted to copy Imago, which to be honest would require something like second dot. You could then examine it but not cast I think.<br /> And Prime isn't exactly a pen. It's a comprehension of the fundamental principles of reality and the power of the Supernal, manifest through the Gnosis-modified power of the human soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:27:44-07:00","id":1082229,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand what you mean by &quot;copying&quot; other spells. Could you explain further what you're after?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:45:21-07:00","id":1082235,"title":"","content":"Sure. We know that besides lowering you can't really change spell factors, right? It means that copying can't really do it either. What it can do is multiply a spell and possibly put it under Prime users spell control. Example:<br /> Pete the Prime Guy and Frank the Forces Guy are fighting a Monster of the Week. Frank casts some penalty spell on the Monster but soon wishes cast some more spells so he has let go of the penalty spell(he could have just relinquish it but whateva). Here comes Pete with his cloning spell. Now he has an identical spell, targeting same target and will end at the same time Frank spell would. But it's under Petes control. There are now two spells doing same thing, one belonging to Frank and one to Pete. Frank stops his spell to do different things but Pete maintains his spell and is a hero.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:50:41-07:00","id":1082238,"title":"","content":"And Pete would be able to do this with just Prime?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:58:19-07:00","id":1082240,"title":"","content":"He would have to follow guidance from Dispel Magic and Supernal Dispellation so 4th dot for copying with Prime only and lower (2nd or 3rd) for when you have all relevant arcana on 1st or maybe 2nd dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:15:06-07:00","id":1082250,"title":"","content":"Supernal Dispellation disrupts a spell while your copying spell would actually create a new spell <i>and</i> have the spell being under your control. I would not allow someone to do that without having at least one or two dots in all Arcana used in that spell.<br /> <br /> A simpler spell with the same effect as in your example (but not necessarily in other applications) would be to simply transfer the spell control of a spell using Prime Weaving plus one dot in all Arcana used in the spell, Withstood by the total Arcanum dots of all Arcana used in the spell being transfered (and Resolve as a separate Withstand if cast on an unwilling subject).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:31:02-07:00","id":1082261,"title":"","content":"Overall you might all be right about 'creating' a spell, but isn't it the same case with Borrow Threads? You create a sympathetic connection with a 2 dot spell.<br /> Word of Command can already activate spells. Stealing spell control should work like Dispelations I think. At least on 4th dot. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:55:16-07:00","id":1082267,"title":"","content":"Sympathetic connections are a whole lot simpler than spells. They're naturally occuring, can be formed by absolutely anything, and exists independently of supernal magic. I don't think that's a good analogue.<br /> <br /> As for stealing spell control; I added the Arcanum prerequisite because I don't think a mage should be able to have spell control over a spell (in the way that mages have; sleepwalkers hold spells differently) without knowing at least the basics (represented by the first dot) of the Arcana involved in that spell. My take on Supernal Dispellation is that it disrupts the spell, which in my mind requires the knowledge about how spells in general work, in contrast to having to maintain a spell which would require more in depth knowledge about how that particular type spell works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T04:54:27-07:00","id":1082559,"title":"","content":"Hmm. So copying is mostly done at 4th dot. You can shape things that already have some plasticity with Ruling though: sympathy, matter of all kinds, change type of resonance(?). But at that level you need some good canvas.<br /> <br /> Word of Command(1st dot spell) can bypass the key and activate any imbued item or artifact without a single dot of relevant Arcanum. Added other Arcana are needed to activate e.g. a Fetish. Which is weird, imo, that you need 1 dot of Prime in addition to 1 dot of Spirit to do something like that and I don't agree with it. - But that's a different topic. Anyway. While lower levels of Prime might require a dot in relevant Arcana to hijack the spell control it shouldn't be the case at 4th dot. It makes Prime mages proper scary.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T05:56:14-07:00","id":1082568,"title":"","content":"Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:09:00-07:00","id":1082591,"title":"","content":"Price of Hubris (Prime 3 + relevant Arcanum at 1) from 1E Banishers book allows to redirect any direct damage spell back to source. When ported to 2E it should be able to use some Reach to allow any spell to be redirected. I imagine that at 4th dot you should be able to hijack the spell control entirely. I'm still not certain it should have 'relevant Arcana' requirement when cast at 4th dot.<br /> -----------------<br /> I'll change the topic a little. What it would take to stop a mage from casting spells?<br /> 2nd dot. We could craft version of Wards and Signs that shields target from Supernal but still it's just a withstand that can be bypassed by a ex. success.<br /> 3rd dot. With Fraying we could possibly give penalties to casting rolls equal to potency. It's good but no bulletproof. Mystic Shackles from TotM<br /> 4th dot. Again, Banishers book has a Master lvl spell called Scorched Earth. It is build in tiers that could be translated to Reach effects:<ul><li>all spells suffer -3 dice penalty</li> <li>ana costs for spells are doubled</li> <li>mana is leached from every mage present at the rate of one mana per turn</li> <li>the effective gnosis rating of any mage in the zone is reduced by 2</li> <li>any roll for Paradox gains the 8th again</li> </ul>It looks more of a Unraveling spell for me.<br /> 5th dot. Unmaking should be able to create a Dead Zone on par with the Ansho. - Is this possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> All of the above seems a lot weaker than 'Don't cast any spells, ever' Psychic Domination. Any Ideas for a Prime or life spell that could accomplish the same thing?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:58:45-07:00","id":1082612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082591#post1082591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Price of Hubris (Prime 3 + relevant Arcanum at 1) from 1E Banishers book allows to redirect any direct damage spell back to source. When ported to 2E it should be able to use some Reach to allow any spell to be redirected. I imagine that at 4th dot you should be able to hijack the spell control entirely. I'm still not certain it should have 'relevant Arcana' requirement when cast at 4th dot.<br /> -----------------<br /> I'll change the topic a little. What it would take to stop a mage from casting spells?<br /> 2nd dot. We could craft version of Wards and Signs that shields target from Supernal but still it's just a withstand that can be bypassed by a ex. success.<br /> 3rd dot. With Fraying we could possibly give penalties to casting rolls equal to potency. It's good but no bulletproof. Mystic Shackles from TotM<br /> 4th dot. Again, Banishers book has a Master lvl spell called Scorched Earth. It is build in tiers that could be translated to Reach effects:<ul><li>all spells suffer -3 dice penalty</li> <li>ana costs for spells are doubled</li> <li>mana is leached from every mage present at the rate of one mana per turn</li> <li>the effective gnosis rating of any mage in the zone is reduced by 2</li> <li>any roll for Paradox gains the 8th again</li> </ul>It looks more of a Unraveling spell for me.<br /> 5th dot. Unmaking should be able to create a Dead Zone on par with the Ansho. - Is this possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> All of the above seems a lot weaker than 'Don't cast any spells, ever' Psychic Domination. Any Ideas for a Prime or life spell that could accomplish the same thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that most of what was in Banishers is gobbledegook that will never see revision in 2e. Not saying hijacking spell control can't be done, just that Banishers isn't a great source to pull your citations from.<br /> <br /> So let me throw this in the mix. Spell control seems to involve some level of Sympathetic strength since a Sympathetic bond with a Sleepwalker is required for passing it off and Mages share a level of Sympathy with their own spells. So I think you could argue that simply using Borrow Threads to steal a Mage's own Sympathetic connection with their spell would be enough to gain control over their spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-23-2017, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:28:19-07:00","id":1084405,"title":"","content":"Or, in other words, Space+Prime=no-buffs-for-you, right? Or would you say that you could hijack someone's sympathetic connection to their spells without Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:42:39-07:00","id":1084408,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I've been told that my take on magic is quite left handed. Not once <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a> If you allow for stealing spells with sympathy it should be a Reach option for Borrow Threads. But. It's not very combat friendly when you must cast 2 spells to achieve something. Since you don't <i>see </i>spells with Space Sight you need to first identify sympathies with Correspondence.<br /> With Prime you can just activate Sight and cast it directly on the spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:53:16-07:00","id":1084412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1084408#post1084408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I've been told that my take on magic is quite left handed. Not once <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> If you allow for stealing spells with sympathy it should be a Reach option for Borrow Threads. But. It's not very combat friendly when you must cast 2 spells to achieve something. Since you don't <i>see </i>spells with Space Sight you need to first identify sympathies with Correspondence.<br /> With Prime you can just activate Sight and cast it directly on the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about the ethics of the magic in Banishers, but the fact that more than a little of it was basically incoherent in comparison with the rest of the Mage line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T04:59:30-07:00","id":1084415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1084412#post1084412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not talking about the ethics of the magic in Banishers, but the fact that more than a little of it was basically incoherent in comparison with the rest of the Mage line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Redirecting a spell to its owner is not a far stretch. It's a logical expansion of counterspell. And Scorched Earth works on thinning the connection with supernal. Which too should be possible with Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:10:38-07:00","id":1084417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1084415#post1084415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redirecting a spell to its owner is not a far stretch. It's a logical expansion of counterspell. And Scorched Earth works on thinning the connection with supernal. Which too should be possible with Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was a far stretch. I said Banishers isn't a great source for backing a well reasoned discussion of the setting. Could you stop completely missing my actual point please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:30:16-07:00","id":1084422,"title":"","content":"I don't understand. You say that Banishers book is incoherent with the rest of the line but far stretched means '<a href=\"http://www.webster-dictionary.org/definition/Far-stretched\" target=\"_blank\">Stretched beyon dordinary limits</a><span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">.' If coherent means that every piece falls nicely into a desired shape I say that incoherent starts when you breach the limits of the mentioned shape. Translation: Not far stretched - coherent.<br /> I can agree that not everything that this book contains is good. I just defended two spells that I mentioned earlier and you referred to.<br /> <br /> Edit: It might be issue with my english but it's not my intention to miss your point. I was specifically addressing it. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:34:04-07:00","id":1084673,"title":"","content":"The problem doesn't lie with the spells, it lies with the source. Two small pieces that aren't a far stretch from a largely incoherent book shouldn't make it into the discussion just because they happen to be not a far stretch; you're still citing from an incoherent source. This is a problem because the source itself needs to be credible, regardless of whether or not you're pulling the most reasonable portion from it. At least, that's my take on what Mrmdubois is saying.<br /> <br /> Personally the Banishers book was one of my least favorite in the 1ed, so I avoid it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:46:37-07:00","id":1084708,"title":"","content":"Thank you Falcon.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> The problem with excising a source is finding the place where you should stop. Is it a whole book? A chapter written by specific person? Every content 1E written by specific person? That said, I don't really care. I haven't read the Banishers book and I probably wont. I just skimmed through it in search of spells and applied my knowledge and understanding of 2E to handpick those which I find interesting and compatible. Never stated that they are 'canon', I used them as examples of what I want to achieve with Prime. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1082591#post1082591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of the above seems a lot weaker than 'Don't cast any spells, ever' Psychic Domination. Any Ideas for a Prime or life spell that could accomplish the same thing?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As you can see didn't 'back' anything. I just asked the question that you answered rather nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T02:11:49-07:00","id":1084934,"title":"","content":"Eh, this shows my problems with Psychic Domination. Maybe if you are worried that Psychic Domination does better job at it that competition, add another layer of Withstanding to the spell - ~the number of Doors that it would take to Social Manuever the target into doing the thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T04:15:06-07:00","id":1084953,"title":"","content":"I don't see a problem with P.Domination, it's a great spell. I'm just searching for an equivalent for Prime and spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T07:23:41-07:00","id":1085015,"title":"","content":"From 1E core book.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Siphon Integrity (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> The mage can pull the Mana out of a mundane lifeless object. He may either add this Mana to his own or disperse it into the Tapestry, as he wishes. Most such Patterns have but little Mana invested in them and siphoningi t all away (or simply dispersing it) damages the item.<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Unraveling<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Lasting<br /> <b>Aspect:</b> Vulgar<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> Each success gives the mage one Mana and inflicts one point of Structure damage to the object, making it brittle. (This damage circumvents the object\u2019s Durability.) Only one point of Mana may be gleaned per three points of Size (rounding down); mundane objects smaller than Size 3 simply do not have enough material substance and presence to hold a full point of Mana.<br /> The caster can replenish his own Mana reserves with this spell only once every 24 hours. The frayed Mana from successive castings cannot be integrated into the mage\u2019s Pattern during that time, although he could use the \u201cChannel Mana\u201d spell, p. 224, to divert it elsewhere. Enchanted items cannot be siphoned with this spell.<br /> <b>Mysterium Rote: </b>Hidden Stores<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Occult + Prime<br /> For a Mysterium mage skilled in the Prime Arcanum, stores of Mana are hidden in plain sight throughout the Tapestry. Providing a much-needed boost on short notice, this rote draws on the willworker\u2019s immediate environment to replenish his power.<br /> Members of the Adamantine Arrow use similar magics (Strength + Occult + Prime) to simultaneously strip their opponents of needed items or protections while recouping their own stores of Mana. </div> </div> </div>Can it be ported to 2E as Weaving spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T14:16:20-07:00","id":1085144,"title":"","content":"The spell should still be unravelling as it does not draw on mana stored in a pattering but rather destroys a pattern by force-extracting the mana contained inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T14:29:30-07:00","id":1085148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1085144#post1085144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell should still be unravelling as it does not draw on mana stored in a pattering but rather destroys a pattern by force-extracting the mana contained inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like Devouring the Slain (Death 3) which specifically mentions scourging Pattern for Mana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T14:35:09-07:00","id":1085151,"title":"","content":"Just because it is a 3 dot effect for death does not mean it has to be an equivalent level effect for prime. Devouring the Slain uses the existing destruction of a person/object to get it's metaphysical claws in, so to speak. It latches onto an existing death pattern. The spell you propose is destroying the the hold the lie has on the mana making up that item, which to me sounds more like a Unravelling practice, rather than a fraying one. Definitly not weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 04-28-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:13:40-07:00","id":1085211,"title":"","content":"Rotting Flesh is a Perfecting spell in spite being direct attack because it perfects decay inside of target. Similarly if you change something into another thing(partialy) it's Weaving. Depending on the description it can be both but violent Fraying version sounds cooler and might be forbidden by Consilium which is neat.<br /> Siphon Integrity 1E is basically a mixture of Devouring the Slain and Decay which are 3rd and 2nd dot respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-28-2017, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T17:05:19-07:00","id":1085231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1085211#post1085211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rotting Flesh is a Perfecting spell in spite being direct attack because it perfects decay inside of target. Similarly if you change something into another thing(partialy) it's Weaving. Depending on the description it can be both but violent Fraying version sounds cooler and might be forbidden by Consilium which is neat.<br /> Siphon Integrity 1E is basically a mixture of Devouring the Slain and Decay which are 3rd and 2nd dot respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's not because it isn't Death. What Siphon Integrity does is basically the same as Transubstantiation but instead of converting something from one type of Matter to another it converts Matter to Mana, the damage done to the object is a secondary effect of this process, and not the cause of the mana that's produced. In 2e I'm pretty sure it would be a conjunction spell now requiring Matter 4+ Prime 4, because things are not &quot;made&quot; of mana anymore like they were in 1e, and the only reason it was that way in 1e was because it was a holdover from Ascension in which you needed the Prime Sphere to make -anything- real.<br /> <br /> The reason that Devouring the Slain produces mana is because it's inducing the Scouring mechanic that Mages are able to employ without magic on themselves in order to produce mana, and not because the damage is being magically converted into mana or because people are mystically made of mana. Although it is a mystical process that produces mana, but so are legacy oblations.<br /> <br /> In summary, you're seeing a parallel that doesn't actually exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-28-2017, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T02:06:10-07:00","id":1085403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1085231#post1085231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> because things are not &quot;made&quot; of mana anymore like they were in 1e, and the only reason it was that way in 1e was because it was a holdover from Ascension in which you needed the Prime Sphere to make -anything- real.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point, conunctional Matter, Life or Forces should probably be required and the practice be Pattering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T02:34:52-07:00","id":1085406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1085231#post1085231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it's not because it isn't Death. What Siphon Integrity does is basically the same as Transubstantiation but instead of converting something from one type of Matter to another it converts Matter to Mana, the damage done to the object is a secondary effect of this process, and not the cause of the mana that's produced. In 2e I'm pretty sure it would be a conjunction spell now requiring Matter 4+ Prime 4, because things are not &quot;made&quot; of mana anymore like they were in 1e, and the only reason it was that way in 1e was because it was a holdover from Ascension in which you needed the Prime Sphere to make -anything- real.<br /> <br /> The reason that Devouring the Slain produces mana is because it's inducing the Scouring mechanic that Mages are able to employ without magic on themselves in order to produce mana, and not because the damage is being magically converted into mana or because people are mystically made of mana. Although it is a mystical process that produces mana, but so are legacy oblations.<br /> <br /> In summary, you're seeing a parallel that doesn't actually exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, I think that Devouring The Slain works like it works because Scouring is inherently Death-y, invoking the whole theme of &quot;Die as X to be Reborn as Y&quot;, or less evocatively, &quot;destructive change that leads to something new and different&quot;. Your health boxes &quot;die&quot; and are reborn into Mana, (are destructively changed into Mana). It's the Alchemist part of Death, me thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:18:08-07:00","id":1086614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1085231#post1085231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it's not because it isn't Death. What Siphon Integrity does is basically the same as Transubstantiation but instead of converting something from one type of Matter to another it converts Matter to Mana, the damage done to the object is a secondary effect of this process, and not the cause of the mana that's produced. In 2e I'm pretty sure it would be a conjunction spell now requiring Matter 4+ Prime 4, because things are not &quot;made&quot; of mana anymore like they were in 1e, and the only reason it was that way in 1e was because it was a holdover from Ascension in which you needed the Prime Sphere to make -anything- real.<br /> <br /> The reason that Devouring the Slain produces mana is because it's inducing the Scouring mechanic that Mages are able to employ without magic on themselves in order to produce mana, and not because the damage is being magically converted into mana or because people are mystically made of mana. Although it is a mystical process that produces mana, but so are legacy oblations.<br /> <br /> In summary, you're seeing a parallel that doesn't actually exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. Matter 4 + Prime 4 is a most sure way to do it. It depends on ST but it cold work like Shadow Flesh requiring only Prime to Unravel the pattern and absorb the released mana, though. Setting assumptions and all that.<br /> But. It might be better off as a Reach option to Aetheric Winds (Prime 3) and Celestial Fire (Prime 4).<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above but Instead of destroying target's Mana you can absorb it to your Pattern.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> Even inanimate objects hold Mana but extraction requires for it to be destroyed in the process. Gather 1 Mana per 3 points of objects Size(smaller structures have not enough material substance to hold Mana). Object must be destroyed with a single spell for this Reach to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:31:31-07:00","id":1086624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1086614#post1086614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are right. Matter 4 + Prime 4 is a most sure way to do it. It depends on ST but it cold work like Shadow Flesh requiring only Prime to Unravel the pattern and absorb the released mana, though. Setting assumptions and all that.<br /> But. It might be better off as a Reach option to Aetheric Winds (Prime 3) and Celestial Fire (Prime 4).<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As above but Instead of destroying target's Mana you can absorb it to your Pattern.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> Even inanimate objects hold Mana but extraction requires for it to be destroyed in the process. Gather 1 Mana per 3 points of objects Size(smaller structures have not enough material substance to hold Mana). Object must be destroyed with a single spell for this Reach to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Reach option on those spells only apply to things that actually have mana in their Pattern in the first place, like Mages or Imbued Items. It's not the same as Siphon Integrity, and like I said before things are not inherently made of mana anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:31:22-07:00","id":1086698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1086624#post1086624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Reach option on those spells only apply to things that actually have mana in their Pattern in the first place, like Mages or Imbued Items. It's not the same as Siphon Integrity, and like I said before things are not inherently made of mana anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reread the Mana description in 2E and you're right, it doesn't underline everything anymore. My +3 Reach option and anything other than Prime/Matter 4 Patterning cant extract Mana inanimate objects if they don't already posses Mana. Thank you for help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:02:07-07:00","id":1089496,"title":"","content":"Date (Time 1)<br /> <br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Academics, Investigation<br /> <br /> Casting this spell upon a subject tells you how long it's existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:28:18-07:00","id":1089554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089496#post1089496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Date (Time 1)<br /> <br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Academics, Investigation<br /> <br /> Casting this spell upon a subject tells you how long it's existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean since the beginning of time?<br /> Shouldn't that take a conjunctive Arcanum relating to the point in time you're reaching back to?<br /> Such as Matter for when steel was shaped into a tool, Life for when the dog was born, Mind for when sapience was reached, or Death for when a Vampire was embraced?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:10:56-07:00","id":1089599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089554#post1089554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean since the beginning of time?<br /> Shouldn't that take a conjunctive Arcanum relating to the point in time you're reaching back to?<br /> Such as Matter for when steel was shaped into a tool, Life for when the dog was born, Mind for when sapience was reached, or Death for when a Vampire was embraced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells in 2e generally cut down required conjunctional Arcana for affecting subjects outside the spell's primary Arcana. Like how you don't need Life when casting Weight of Years (Time 3) to age and decay someone's Health.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Granted, this isn't a universal rule, but one that's mostly kept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:54:10-07:00","id":1089631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089599#post1089599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells in 2e generally cut down required conjunctional Arcana for affecting subjects outside the spell's primary Arcana. Like how you don't need Life when casting Weight of Years (Time 3) to age and decay someone's Health.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Granted, this isn't a universal rule, but one that's mostly kept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that doesn't mean in this case it isn't required.<br /> I generally consider that character in DaveB's game with the &quot;Time of Death&quot; praxis requiring Time/Death 1 to determine time of death to be persuasive precedent.<br /> <br /> Considering your Time example, all you need to do there is speed up time. Otherwise you'd always need a Conjunctional Arcanum to affect anything with Time.<br /> In this case, you're trying to specifically know something about Time, however time doesn't really have markers you can just read without knowing when they were, so you have to add a conjunctive Arcanum to determine exactly when that previous Arcanum-related event occured.<br /> <br /> It's like having the tools to look back, but nothing to look back with. Life can tell you all about a subject's patter, and Time can tell you when those events happened. So combining the two you can tell when any specific biological event happened within the individual's life.<br /> <br /> I feel that otherwise any difficulty in finding exactly when you need to scry to is rendered pointless by single Knowing spell before you prep your Postcognition Unveiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 05-08-2017, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:15:52-07:00","id":1089635,"title":"","content":"A thousand and one people have already designed their own immortality spells (much as Liches are wont to do), but here's mine for the pile. Based on a conjunctional use of both Time and Life to modify the functionality of a Mage's biological cells such that they maintain their capacity to perform their functions, but the aging process is halted. Basically Veil of Moments, on a cellular scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Stop the Biological Clock (Time \u2022\u2022, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> The Mage alters the functionality of the target's biological patterning, ensuring that while all normal biological functions are performed as normal, cells replicate perfectly, avodiing the ravaging effects of time, and ensuring that the biological aging process is halted. The practical upshot of this is that while the Mage's body otherwise functions exactly as it normally would, she does not biologically age. This will not halt the effects of cancers, diseases, poisons or other maladies of form, nor will it stop the psychological effects of aging, however it will work to counteract certain mental afflictions with a physical aspect, such as dementia.<br /> <br /> This spell is a quick and easy, albeit risky way to embrace the path of Lichdom. It's use is not considered quite as inherently threatening as the other forms of Lichdom, due to their inherently inhuman nature. However it is seen as something of a gateway-spell to those later paths, as the Mage grows older and starts to obsess over the threat of untimely death. As such, while some merely use to to enhance their quality of life for as long as reasonable, you can never truly trust them not to start body snatching or resorting to more permanent, and less dispellable methods. What's more, should the spell be dispelled, the cumulative weight of all of those years of time come crashing down upon the Mage.<br /> <br /> For this reason, some Mage have developed their own Legacies based on this spell, to avoid such eventualities. Such Mages are almost uniformly declared as Liches. This does not however stop them from accumulating small cults of worshippers, enchanted by the possibility of eternal life, willing to bind themselves forever to the desires of their Master, only to later realise that he could render them crippled or dead with but a thought, as he removes his blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 05-08-2017, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:48:29-07:00","id":1089645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089496#post1089496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Date (Time 1)<br /> <br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Academics, Investigation<br /> <br /> Casting this spell upon a subject tells you how long it's existed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Valid. Maybe it should be a reach effect with steps? Like base effect could be to know timestamps of when temporal sympathy changed e.g. from strong to medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:13:46-07:00","id":1089658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089631#post1089631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but that doesn't mean in this case it isn't required.<br /> I generally consider that character in DaveB's game with the &quot;Time of Death&quot; praxis requiring Time/Death 1 to determine time of death to be persuasive precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now why would he need a conjunctive spell for Time of Death using Time/Death when Forensic Gaze will do the same thing and it is a 1 dot Death spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:18:26-07:00","id":1089662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089658#post1089658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now why would he need a conjunctive spell for Time of Death using Time/Death when Forensic Gaze will do the same thing and it is a 1 dot Death spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was pointed out to Dave in the same thread but he didn't address this issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:28:39-07:00","id":1089664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089662#post1089662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was pointed out to Dave in the same thread but he didn't address this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because DaveB didn't address it doesn't make it any less that spell to turn to when determining the time of death. Dave doesn't answer alot of rebuttal questions, that doesn't invalidate the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:55:38-07:00","id":1089670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089664#post1089664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because DaveB didn't address it doesn't make it any less that spell to turn to when determining the time of death. Dave doesn't answer alot of rebuttal questions, that doesn't invalidate the question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, those were dry facts. You said what I didn't wan't mention because I'm tired of Dave's poltergeist appearances caused by him not being paid to finish his products. Aand I didn't constrain myself again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:14:01-07:00","id":1089675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089670#post1089670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, those were dry facts. You said what I didn't wan't mention because I'm tired of Dave's poltergeist appearances caused by him not being paid to finish his products. Aand I didn't constrain myself again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is nothing to fear. Dave is only Human, I think, and he makes mistakes as well as anyone. Yes he is the Developer of this product and he not only knows the product better than almost anyone out there be he is one of the few that is allowed to state what the intent of the product is. To question him isn't anything to fear it just <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">emphasizes</span> the fact that he is human. No one expects him to walk on water, but to expect him to answer and validate every rebuttal is rediculous because he would never get off the forums, and we need him doing what he does best, developing. I have the highest respect for Dave but it doesn't mean that I always agree with him or expect to much.<br /> <br /> But as I said no rebuttal doesn't invalidate the question or that fact that there is a spell that is not a conjunctive effect that would cover the c<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">ircumstance, there could have been extenuating circumstances in Daves game that he forgot to mention that required the player to use a conjunctive effect.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:49:59-07:00","id":1089691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089635#post1089635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thousand and one people have already designed their own immortality spells (much as Liches are wont to do), but here's mine for the pile. Based on a conjunctional use of both Time and Life to modify the functionality of a Mage's biological cells such that they maintain their capacity to perform their functions, but the aging process is halted. Basically Veil of Moments, on a cellular scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Stop the Biological Clock (Time \u2022\u2022, Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> The Mage alters the functionality of the target's biological patterning, ensuring that while all normal biological functions are performed as normal, cells replicate perfectly, avodiing the ravaging effects of time, and ensuring that the biological aging process is halted. The practical upshot of this is that while the Mage's body otherwise functions exactly as it normally would, she does not biologically age. This will not halt the effects of cancers, diseases, poisons or other maladies of form, nor will it stop the psychological effects of aging, however it will work to counteract certain mental afflictions with a physical aspect, such as dementia.<br /> <br /> This spell is a quick and easy, albeit risky way to embrace the path of Lichdom. It's use is not considered quite as inherently threatening as the other forms of Lichdom, due to their inherently inhuman nature. However it is seen as something of a gateway-spell to those later paths, as the Mage grows older and starts to obsess over the threat of untimely death. As such, while some merely use to to enhance their quality of life for as long as reasonable, you can never truly trust them not to start body snatching or resorting to more permanent, and less dispellable methods. What's more, should the spell be dispelled, the cumulative weight of all of those years of time come crashing down upon the Mage.<br /> <br /> For this reason, some Mage have developed their own Legacies based on this spell, to avoid such eventualities. Such Mages are almost uniformly declared as Liches. This does not however stop them from accumulating small cults of worshippers, enchanted by the possibility of eternal life, willing to bind themselves forever to the desires of their Master, only to later realise that he could render them crippled or dead with but a thought, as he removes his blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the difference between this and Veil of Moments with its Reach clauses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:27:48-07:00","id":1089745,"title":"","content":"Even with reach options, Veil of Moments doesn't let you spend Experiences.<br /> This is a way to step around that limitation, also losing its protection from diseases and so forth.<br /> However Life can already do that easy, so there's little problem which arises from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T07:38:32-07:00","id":1089772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1089745#post1089745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with reach options, Veil of Moments doesn't let you spend Experiences.<br /> This is a way to step around that limitation, also losing its protection from diseases and so forth.<br /> However Life can already do that easy, so there's little problem which arises from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'd let this version sidestep the XP expenditures either. You aren't stopped from accumulating XP, so theoretically you could just drop Veil of Moments occasionally long enough to burn through accumulated XP and then put it back again. You'd still age, but at a vastly decreased rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:14:08-07:00","id":1093710,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Bug </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Mind </span></span></b><b>\u2022</b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Knowing</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell nests itself on subject mind and leaks informations in the real time. Pick a topic that this spell keeps eye on to get a descriptive output. It should be moderately precise - work life, commuting, sports competition, news. Whenever something that falls under this topic occurs the caster(or anyone that he chose at the time of casting) gets a description of the event. </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the topic is \u201ccommute\u201d the caster gets</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i> \u201c<i>...at the corner, right behind the butcher shop he turnes left and goes straight down the street to the town hall\u2026\u201d.</i></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> It wont reveal that he met his girlfriend on the way since it\u2019s not the topic. It might however tell that he stopped and asked someone for an advice of how to get there. When you choose \u201cimago\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">it will describe the spell that she craft when she crafts it <i>\u201c...she burns the tiger-monster-thing and Brian with the winds of Aether\u2026\u201d</i> or reveals the conversation she has with her mentor <i>\u201c...she asks how harmful for the soul is to kill with magic and the master says that it depends on\u2026\u201d. </i>Descriptions should be a little vague, unless the caster specifies a narrowed topic with a Reach option below.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GM should apply penalty ranging from -1 to -3 when mage for example actively listens to \u201csoap operas\u201d while trying to read a book on his own.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Pick another topic. Can be taken multiple times.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The topic may be more precise - \u201cspying\u201d can now become \u201cspying on a member of the Black Lotus organization\u201d but it will only work on situation where the target </span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>thinks </i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the Black Lotus is involved.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Even thoughts can betray the target giving away what he thinks at the moment about the topic. Now you know what the target will do before he does it, at the moment of its decision. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+2 Reach:</b> As above but when making an opposed check, pertaining the topic, against the subject of the spell you may add potency as bonus equipment. It can\u2019t go above 5. <b>Example:</b> If you want to tail someone with \u201ccommute\u201d Bug pinned on him. Or seduce when \u201cintimacy\u201d is active.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage can tap in and out as an instant action. It\u2019s a safety switch since the surveillance can be distracting at times.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mage can tap in and out as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure what practice is this so I went with the lowest possible. Its something between Mental Scan and Telepathy though. It might be Ruling.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-18-2017, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:43:30-07:00","id":1093722,"title":"","content":"I think it would be Knowing since the information is purely one way and has no other effect except to provide information (Telepathy does a bit more than that), and I'd switch the main effect of the spell and the second +1 Reach option because the general use of the spell as it stands now is way more useful in general terms than that option. I'd also make the tapping feature a Reach option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:07:14-07:00","id":1093726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093722#post1093722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be Knowing since the information is purely one way and has no other effect except to provide information (Telepathy does a bit more than that), and I'd switch the main effect of the spell and the second +1 Reach option because the general use of the spell as it stands now is way more useful in general terms than that option. I'd also make the tapping feature a Reach option.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be Knowing, yea. It's a spying tool so I thought that it should follow this theme. When youre surveying a target the hardest part is to wait and actively sift all those unnecessary information. The thing that is extremely useful is the &quot;trigger&quot; that lets you pay attention to only important moments. Like when NSA allegedly listens when someone talks about bombs - it would do nothing without this triggers.<br /> <br /> Reach gives you option to tap in <i>reflexively </i>instead of <i>instantly. </i>You think that I should ditch <i>instant </i>activation in the base spell and go straight for <i>reflexive </i>activation with a Reach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-17-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:25:28-07:00","id":1093862,"title":"","content":"How would you guys make a spell that converts a character from a videogame into something on the Fallen Word, but still controlled by your videogame?<br /> I was thinking in doing something like that to a Warcraft character and still be controlling him do to my biding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T16:05:50-07:00","id":1093880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093862#post1093862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you guys make a spell that converts a character from a videogame into something on the Fallen Word, but still controlled by your videogame?<br /> I was thinking in doing something like that to a Warcraft character and still be controlling him do to my biding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces + Mind to make him a Goetia seems like the simplest solution, but you'd need something to give him Manifestation Effects, so tack on Spirit or Death 4.<br /> <br /> He could be controlled via Mind, the video game would function as a Yantra in a spell to do so.<br /> <br /> If you want to utilize your <i>idea</i> of the character instead of actually extracting him from the game, you could drop Forces.<br /> <br /> Actually, just going straight Forces + Spirit avoids needing 3 Arcana and still allows control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-17-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T19:04:53-07:00","id":1093944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093726#post1093726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be Knowing, yea. It's a spying tool so I thought that it should follow this theme. When you're surveying a target the hardest part is to wait and actively sift all those unnecessary information. The thing that is extremely useful is the &amp;quot;trigger&amp;quot; that lets you pay attention to only important moments. Like when NSA allegedly listens when someone talks about bombs - it would do nothing without this triggers.<br /> <br /> Reach gives you option to tap in <i>reflexively </i>instead of <i>instantly. </i>You think that I should ditch <i>instant </i>activation in the base spell and go straight for <i>reflexive </i>activation with a Reach?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, you have a lot of Reach options and I didn't say anything about the one that lets you tap in and out reflexively. I said that the ability to tap on and off should be a Reach because it instantly reduces the chances of being incapacitated due to information overload to almost nil. In other words, you're not charging enough Reach for an obvious benefit. The Reach cost for making it Reflexive should be 2 Reach though now I've thought about it.<br /> <br /> That wasn't my main point though, I said make the spell's main effect what the -second- +1 Reach option is. In other words &quot;spying on a member of the Black Lotus organization &quot; is -way- more specific and useless compared to the original purpose of the spell which triggers off of less specific criteria. Make the spell only detect -very- specific things, and make the Reach able to track less specific categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:18:59-07:00","id":1094005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093944#post1093944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That wasn't my main point though, I said make the spell's main effect what the -second- +1 Reach option is. In other words &amp;quot;spying on a member of the Black Lotus organization &amp;quot; is -way- more specific and useless compared to the original purpose of the spell which triggers off of less specific criteria. Make the spell only detect -very- specific things, and make the Reach able to track less specific categories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I addressed this already. I don't need all this trash information about where the target goes, all the time. Kitchen, bathroom, bedroom, kiosk, Starbucks, work, bathroom. It requires an effort and focus on the target but what for? When you can narrow it down to &quot;commute to a hideout&quot; and be prompted only then.<br /> Any detective would be in love with something like that. Also &quot;street names along his path&quot; is a valid narrowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:38:51-07:00","id":1094009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093944#post1093944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, you have a lot of Reach options and I didn't say anything about the one that lets you tap in and out reflexively. I said that the ability to tap on and off should be a Reach because it instantly reduces the chances of being incapacitated due to information overload to almost nil. In other words, you're not charging enough Reach for an obvious benefit. The Reach cost for making it Reflexive should be 2 Reach though now I've thought about it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Co-location has reflexive teleportation as a base effect and <i>twice</i> that for a Reach. But A Bug is 1st dot spell... so yea, it might be better with tapping in and off packed inside of Reach entirelly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:48:00-07:00","id":1094029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1094005#post1094005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe I addressed this already. I don't need all this trash information about where the target goes, all the time. Kitchen, bathroom, bedroom, kiosk, Starbucks, work, bathroom. It requires an effort and focus on the target but what for? When you can narrow it down to &quot;commute to a hideout&quot; and be prompted only then.<br /> Any detective would be in love with something like that. Also &quot;street names along his path&quot; is a valid narrowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imo, more information is better than less, even if what you pick up isn't relevant to what you're actually interested in it can help you build a more complete picture of the other person. Much like how internet companies collect all the information on you that they can so they can build profiles that they then use to select ads that are targeted at you. I can see how Mages might want the prompts in only very narrow circumstances, but ultimately knowledge is power and knowing more for slightly more effort is worth more than knowing less for the same amount of effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:54:37-07:00","id":1094030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1094029#post1094029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imo, more information is better than less, even if what you pick up isn't relevant to what you're actually interested in it can help you build a more complete picture of the other person. Much like how internet companies collect all the information on you that they can so they can build profiles that they then use to select ads that are targeted at you. I can see how Mages might want the prompts in only very narrow circumstances, but ultimately knowledge is power and knowing more for slightly more effort is worth more than knowing less for the same amount of effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>My intention was to make the base effect of description a little vague just like the topic. The more precise topic the more details you get. I'll clarify that in spell later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:16:27-07:00","id":1094038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1093862#post1093862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you guys make a spell that converts a character from a videogame into something on the Fallen Word, but still controlled by your videogame?<br /> I was thinking in doing something like that to a Warcraft character and still be controlling him do to my biding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way would be to rip the part of the program and grant it physicality based on Forces. Forces 4 should be able to do it but you would still need gamepad or other controller to move your new minion. It would act like in pre-alpha since the world is not a program and scripted tasks and animations would fail or be very clunky - it could be mitigated by some Reach I think. If you shut down the computer the program will shut down too, but again, Reach should prevent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:21:21-07:00","id":1099376,"title":"","content":"What sphere combinations do you guys think would be necessary to emulate a bond like the one depicted in Sense8?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:51:17-07:00","id":1099382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1099376#post1099376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sphere combinations do you guys think would be necessary to emulate a bond like the one depicted in Sense8?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't watched it, so no idea on the full extend of the bond, but Mind would suffice for a telepathic link. Maybe adding Space to fiddle with emotional bonds.<br /> <br /> And seeing how you're referring to Spheres... are you sure you're in the right forum you want to ask of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T04:09:18-07:00","id":1099437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1099376#post1099376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sphere combinations do you guys think would be necessary to emulate a bond like the one depicted in Sense8?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space, Mind, Possibly Life, Possibly Fate. Space is is there to link all of their minds together and they have an intimate connection. Mind/life it appears to me that they can use the Physical/Mental Attributes/Skills of everyone that they are linked to. As an example just knowing the martial arts maneuvers that the one member has would not allow you to accurately perform them without a boost to the Dexterity and/or Strength of the one mimicking them. It also appears that they are connected by Fate, if no more that interconnections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:41:31-07:00","id":1099492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1099376#post1099376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sphere combinations do you guys think would be necessary to emulate a bond like the one depicted in Sense8?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Mind 4 was enough to link all of their minds sufficiently to share skills and experiences.<br /> You're essentially Patterning several minds together so they can share information.<br /> Each full functional within a greater whole.<br /> <br /> I actually made a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition/page57\">spell</a> for this exact purpose a while ago, &quot;Communion&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T03:10:51-07:00","id":1102473,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T08:52:17-07:00","id":1102517,"title":"","content":"<b>Obliterate</b> (Time 5)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unmaking<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Weaponry, Occult or Academics<br /> <br /> The spell obliterates a targets thread in the timeline burning it back. If the spell is successful the target ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> <b>+3 Reach</b> - Not only is the target erased from the time line, they are removed from the timeline retroactively backwards in time to a point based on the spells duration. Remember that Temporal Sympathy comes into play with this Reach option.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> <i>So anyone that's read the Wheel of TIme series probably gets where this spell comes from. Is it even possible with Time 5? It definitely seems like something an Unmaking spell should be able to do but I have some reservations. Any input is appreciated</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:22:48-07:00","id":1102855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1102517#post1102517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Obliterate</b> (Time 5)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unmaking<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Weaponry, Occult or Academics<br /> <br /> The spell obliterates a targets thread in the timeline burning it back. If the spell is successful the target ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> <b>+3 Reach</b> - Not only is the target erased from the time line, they are removed from the timeline retroactively backwards in time to a point based on the spells duration. Remember that Temporal Sympathy comes into play with this Reach option.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> <i>So anyone that's read the Wheel of TIme series probably gets where this spell comes from. Is it even possible with Time 5? It definitely seems like something an Unmaking spell should be able to do but I have some reservations. Any input is appreciated</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Quarantine (Space 5), has this as supplemental affect when you add Time 5, but it has a duration and isn't Lasting, meaning that it rejoins the timeline when the duration ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T05:41:58-07:00","id":1104246,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Removed (for now).</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:14:02-07:00","id":1107063,"title":"","content":"<b>Spell: Transform Life (Life </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> As the base spell (<i>Mage: The Awakening, 2nd Ed.</i>, pg. 150), with additional adaptations:<br /> <br /> <i>Electroshock Touch</i>: Electric eels can produce shocks that put commercial stun guns and Tasers to shame. The mage can mimic this capability, based on the rules for stun guns found on pg. 277 of <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>. Rolls to shock a target use Dexterity+Brawl (touch) or Strength+Brawl (strike or grapple) and inflict one lethal damage per round, in addition to any damage inflicted by striking or grappling. Each round's successes subtract from the victim's next dice pool; once the accumulated successes exceed the victim's Size, he collapses into neuromuscular incapacitation. Assuming the mage doesn't want to kill him, this lasts for (10-Stamina) minutes once the shock ends. Most armor will not protect against electrical damage; exceptions include special-purpose gear (e.g. ThorShield), electrically-conductive fencing lam\u00e9s, and certain forms of Mage Armor (Forces &amp; Matter). Vampires, as well as mages benefiting from Death Armor, reduce the damage to bashing and are immune to the neuromuscular incapacitation effect: while the spastic jerking of dead muscle can still impede their movements (represented by the penalties to dice rolls), the Curse sustains them past the point at which tendons and synapses fail.<br /> <br /> <i>Danger Sense: </i>Human reaction times average between 200-300 milliseconds; cats and snakes can cut that time by half to two-thirds. By mimicking an array of adaptations, including greater visual acuity and more efficient synaptic structures, the mage can apply Defense against Firearms attacks, reacting to the minute cues of fingers tightening upon triggers and barrels shifting into line. (Requires the <i>Senses</i> adaptation [adding Potency to Perception rolls].)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:15:25-07:00","id":1107066,"title":"","content":"<b>Spell: Human Torch (Forces </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>+ Life </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Medicine, Science<br /> <br /> The mage transmutes his flesh into fire, trusting his knowledge of Forces to keep the heat from burning vulnerable internal organs. Striking an opponent with a limb has an equivalent size (and base damage) of a torch (1), while grappling increases the amount of exposure to that of a bonfire (2). Each level of Potency increases the heat of the flames, to a maximum intensity of +3 (equivalent to molten metal). If the mage grapples an opponent (or is grappled) for two consecutive turns, the opponent ignites and is subject to the Burning Tilt. The mage is immune to heat and fire of equivalent or lesser intensity, including the Burning and Extreme Heat Tilts.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The planes of force shielding you from the harmful effects of your own fire become more refined, protecting your worn armor and other equipment.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can &quot;flare&quot; your fiery nimbus into a column of superheated air, with explosive results. As an instant action, you can attack at short range with Dexterity + Athletics, using a weapon modifier equal to Potency. Opponents apply Defense, but the &quot;spread&quot; of your attack is difficult to avoid, not unlike a shotgun; your roll benefits from 9-Again. Alternatively, you can use the explosive burst for propulsion, making a Strength + Athletics roll to jump and multiplying your successes by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":"Human Torch tweaked accordingly. 09-20-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:16:47-07:00","id":1107067,"title":"","content":"<b>Spell: Colossus (Matter </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf <b>+ Life </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Crafts, Medicine<br /> <br /> The mage transmutes entire portions of his anatomy into living wood, stone, or metal. The mage's skin, muscle, and bone become a material with Durability equal to Potency, to a maximum of 5 (equivalent to multiple reinforced layers of steel). This Durability is added to the mage's Health and Armor; per the normal rules for Objects, this additional Armor does not apply against aggravated damage. The mage's unarmed attacks are now lethal weapons with damage rating [Durability]. Unless an attack deals aggravated damage, the mage is immune to the Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack tilts.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The transmutation turns inward, magic replacing cardiovascular, digestive, nervous, and respiratory functions. For the duration of the spell, the mage no longer needs to breathe or eat, does not suffer wound penalties, and is immune to the Bleeding, Drugged, Poisoned, Sick, and Stunned Tilts.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage's metal flesh can mimic the alchemical properties of a rare or precious material, such as silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":"Subtle Arcana don't require Life to transmute you, and Death is just the odd duck in being a Subtle Arcanum that can manipulate a physical 09-20-2017, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:58:29-07:00","id":1107078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1107066#post1107066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spell: Human Torch (Forces </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Athletics, Medicine, Science<br /> <br /> The mage transmutes his flesh into fire, trusting his knowledge of Forces to keep the heat from burning vulnerable internal organs. Striking an opponent with a limb has an equivalent size (and base damage) of a torch (1), while grappling increases the amount of exposure to that of a bonfire (2). Each level of Potency increases the heat of the flames, to a maximum intensity of +3 (equivalent to molten metal). If the mage grapples an opponent (or is grappled) for two consecutive turns, the opponent ignites and is subject to the Burning Tilt. The mage is immune to heat and fire of equivalent or lesser intensity, including the Burning and Extreme Heat Tilts.<br /> <b>Add Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf:</b> Apply the spell's effects to another person.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The planes of force shielding you from the harmful effects of your own fire become more refined, protecting your worn armor and other equipment.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can &quot;flare&quot; your fiery nimbus into a column of superheated air, with explosive results. As an instant action, you can attack at short range with Dexterity + Athletics, using a weapon modifier equal to Potency. Opponents apply Defense, but the &quot;spread&quot; of your attack is difficult to avoid, not unlike a shotgun; your roll benefits from 9-Again. Alternatively, you can use the explosive burst for propulsion, making a Strength + Athletics roll to jump and multiplying your successes by Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use just Forces to cover yourself in fire that isn't burning you, but to actually transmute yourself into flame would be Life 4 +Forces 4. You don't need Life to cast a spell on another person that you can already cast on yourself. Those same rules also apply to your Colossus spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T12:20:57-07:00","id":1107087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1107078#post1107078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could use just Forces to cover yourself in fire that isn't burning you, but to actually transmute yourself into flame would be Life 4 +Forces 4. You don't need Life to cast a spell on another person that you can already cast on yourself. Those same rules also apply to your Colossus spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Death 4's &quot;Shadow Flesh&quot; lets you become living shadow without mentioning a supplemental Life requirement. IIRC, there was a thread somewhere discussing whether that's a unique-to-Death fluke, a typo inconsistent with text on pg. 124 (&quot;... like transforming into a living pillar of fire [Life and Forces]...&quot;)<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that there's a happy resolution to this issue with a bit of in-universe logic. Consider: every mage, no matter their skill or lack thereof with Life, can still change their own Pattern. They do it every time they heal themselves with Mana, or Scour themselves to gain Mana. So if you want to impact <i>your own </i>Pattern with transformative magic, its unique familiarity to you can substitute for your ignorance of Life... but if you want to grant your Sleepwalker buddy the same effect, you'll need the knowledge of Life to make sure you don't accidentally incinerate his kidneys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T05:28:59-07:00","id":1107607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1107087#post1107087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Death 4's &quot;Shadow Flesh&quot; lets you become living shadow without mentioning a supplemental Life requirement. IIRC, there was a thread somewhere discussing whether that's a unique-to-Death fluke, a typo inconsistent with text on pg. 124 (&quot;... like transforming into a living pillar of fire [Life and Forces]...&quot;)<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that there's a happy resolution to this issue with a bit of in-universe logic. Consider: every mage, no matter their skill or lack thereof with Life, can still change their own Pattern. They do it every time they heal themselves with Mana, or Scour themselves to gain Mana. So if you want to impact <i>your own </i>Pattern with transformative magic, its unique familiarity to you can substitute for your ignorance of Life... but if you want to grant your Sleepwalker buddy the same effect, you'll need the knowledge of Life to make sure you don't accidentally incinerate his kidneys.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My personal resolution to Shadowflesh was that &quot;the Subtle Arcana do not require Life in conjunction to transform a living body.&quot; Like how the Spirit spells that turn you into ephemera by chucking you into the Shadow don't require Life to function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T06:54:28-07:00","id":1107619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1107607#post1107607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My personal resolution to Shadowflesh was that &amp;quot;the Subtle Arcana do not require Life in conjunction to transform a living body.&amp;quot; Like how the Spirit spells that turn you into ephemera by chucking you into the Shadow don't require Life to function.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's quite ingenious. It makes sense too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T17:22:08-07:00","id":1107819,"title":"","content":"Has this one been done before? And/or is it an acceptable spell.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dead-eye&quot;<br /> Time \u2022\u2022<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Firearms, Crafts, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The mage slows time while aiming their weapon or alternatively speeds it up on someone aiming theirs. For the Duration the next Potency# of shots gain a dice as though the mage spent a turn aiming.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach The spell applies the maximum aim bonus (+3) or doubles the amount of time a target must spend to gain an aim bonus.<br /> +1 Reach (mana?) The spell works on automatic weaponry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T01:36:42-07:00","id":1107942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1107819#post1107819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this one been done before? And/or is it an acceptable spell.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dead-eye&quot;<br /> Time \u2022\u2022<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Firearms, Crafts, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The mage slows time while aiming their weapon or alternatively speeds it up on someone aiming theirs. For the Duration the next Potency# of shots gain a dice as though the mage spent a turn aiming.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach The spell applies the maximum aim bonus (+3) or doubles the amount of time a target must spend to gain an aim bonus.<br /> +1 Reach (mana?) The spell works on automatic weaponry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concept is good but it could use some added clarity.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't work on automatic weapons without Reach, that should be specified in the main description, along with any other restrictions. If you can apply a penalty to a subject's ability to aim without a Reach (implied in the description) you should include what the penalty is before Reaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T04:30:06-07:00","id":1107967,"title":"","content":"The maximum aim bonus can be increased further by use of Merits so the parenthesis can become contradictory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:21:25-07:00","id":1108142,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice here is Mk. II<br /> <br /> &quot;Dead-eye&quot;<br /> Time \u2022\u2022<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Firearms, Crafts, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The mage slows time while aiming their weapon or alternatively speeds it up on someone aiming theirs. For the Duration the next Potency # of shots gain a dice as though the mage spent a turn aiming. Alternatively, the spell can double the amount of time a target needs to gain an aiming bonus (e.g. two turns instead of one for a +1 bonus). The spell doesn't provide a benefit to auto fire weapons.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The spell applies the maximum aim bonus or nullifies the target's aim bonus<br /> +1 Reach &amp; 1 mana: The spell works with auto fire weaponry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T04:22:21-07:00","id":1108344,"title":"","content":"I decided to redo my Spirit Marriage spell that turns a mage into a living fetish. I used the Body Control spell as a model. \u200bBasically this spell is a wet dream for me as a fan of the Spirit Arcanum, enhancing it's versatility and potential for flavour even more.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit Marriage (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> \u200bPractice: Patterning<br /> Withstand: Rank<br /> \u200bPrimary Factor: Duration<br /> \u200bSuggested Rote Skills: Intimidation, Expression, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The mage invites (or forces) a spirit to co-habit her body and bequeath their strength to the mage. For every dot of Potency, the mage can gain one of the following:<ul><li>One dot of Influence that the spirit has. The roll to activate the Influence is Gnosis + Spirit and if it costs Essence the mage may opt to use Mana instead. The mage cannot gain more Influence dots than what the spirit has.</li> <li>One Numen that the spirit has. The roll to activate the Numen is Gnosis + Spirit and if it costs Essence the mage may opt to use Mana instead. The mage cannot gain more Numen than what the spirit has.</li> <li>One of the mage\u2019s Attribute dots may be boosted by the Attribute dots of the spirit on a 1-1 basis. The spirit\u2019s Power dots can boost Intelligence, Strength and Presence. Finesse dots can boost Wits, Dexterity and Manipulation. Resistance dots can boost Resolve, Stamina and Composure. No Attribute can be boosted beyond the allowed maximum of the Mage.</li> </ul>This spell has a slight cosmetic effect as well, depending on what type of spirit is co-habiting the mage\u2019s body. A fire spirit may make the mage smell like smoke and have a slight orange tint to their eyes, while a leech spirit makes the mage much more pale than normal. These cosmetic effects are usually more noticeable for higher rank spirits.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The cosmetic alteration is ignored, making the mage look just like they did before the spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage may boost one Attribute beyond the mage\u2019s natural maximum.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T02:49:02-07:00","id":1109164,"title":"","content":"<b>Falsify Timeline:</b> (Time \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> For the duration of this spell the Mage can Falsify the subject\u2019s action within the Timeline. If someone tries to view the subjects past it will provoke a Clash of Wills. If they fail the Clash of Wills then the Caster of this spell can send an altered image of events to the onlooker. This does not alter what really happened just what the onlooker perceives happened.<br /> If the onlooker Records this Falsified Timeline, in any fashion, the effects become lasting in that the recorded history remains even after the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Mind \u25cf\u25cf:</b> By adding Mind to this spell the Falsified Timeline becomes contagious. The Onlooker believes the visions so completely that anyone they communicate the Falsified visions to also believes it.<br /> <b>Add Prime \u25cf\u25cf: </b>The effects stand up to any form of Lie Detection be it mundane or supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 06-29-2017, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T03:28:56-07:00","id":1109170,"title":"","content":"My players have found a vampire, and of course, this means they want to make Vitae. I have created three spells to deal with Vitae. I based them on spells presented earlier in this thread, as well as the first edition rules for creating blood that vampires can drink. I have discarded the 1e notion that Prime is required to make actual vampiric VItae, instead ruling that it is under the purview of Life (although maybe there's also an argument for Death). Due to the alien nature of the vampiric curse, these spells depart a tiny bit from the regular creative thaumaturgy rules. This mostly concerns the inflicting of damage, representative of the vampiric curse's cost. It always gets what it desires, one way or another.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Channel Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage is able to channel Vitae between herself and vampires, strix, ghouls, other living targets, or inanimate receptacles.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Weaving</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Survival</li> </ul>The spell allows the mage to move a quantity of Vitae up to the spell's Potency between one or more vessels she can touch, including herself, vampires, ghouls, strix, other living targets, or physical containers. Transferring the vitae into a subject forces the effects of Vitae consumption upon the it: vampires gain more Vitae, living targets may become ghouls, and so forth. If the Vitae is transferred into a container, it maintains its nature as Vitae for the Duration of the spell before reverting to normal blood.<br /> <br /> The mage may channel a number of points of Vitae per turn equal to her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may channel as much Vitae as she wants in one turn, ignoring her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and +1 Mana:</b> When the vitae is transferred into a subject, the effects of the Vitae are suppressed for the Duration of the spell. This effect suppresses the effects of Vitae for one subject, and can be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampirism (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage patterns the blood of a living subject into vampiric Vitae and draws it from the victim.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana</li> </ul>The Vitae drawn is usually in the form of blood oozing from wounds, but can be a more exotic substance, depending on the method the mage uses to &quot;feed&quot; on the subject. This spell generates one Vitae per Potency. Since the spell directly patterns Life into Vitae, the subject is not harmed. The quality of the Vitae is relative to the subject (animals produce animal-quality Vitae and humans produce human-quality).<br /> <br /> The Vitae remains supernatural until the Duration of the spell expires, at which point it turns back into regular substance, unless it has been consumed. The use of this spell is an affront to the vampiric Curse, and damns the mage: the mage must include themselves as a subject in the spell, and they take 1 resistant Lethal damage per Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may apply one suitable Condition or Tilt to the subject per level of Potency, representative of the vampiric feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may freely divide the damage between subjects in the spell. While the Curse damns the one who meddles with it directly, it is less &quot;concerned&quot; with other subjects. Other subjects do not suffer resistant damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death, Mind, or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage may draw from ghosts (Death), goetia (mind), or spirits (Spirit).<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage can convert the Vitae into tass in a form of her choosing. The tass functions as Vitae and Mana, and if ingestible, can be consumed by Vampires. The tass created has the resonance keyword of &quot;vampirism.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Create Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This spell creates Vitae from nothing.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Making</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Blood Potency, Stamina, or Resistance (depending on target)</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1+ Mana</li> </ul>The spell creates an amount of pure, inert Vitae equal to Potency in the subject, which may be a vampire, strix, living target, or container. If created outside of an animate subject, the mage chooses the form the Vitae takes (and must have a way to contain the resulting Vitae), and the spell is Withstood by the mage's own Stamina.<br /> <br /> As always, the vampiric curse takes its debt: the mage must include themselves as a subject in the spell, and they suffer 1 resistant lethal damage per point of Potency.<br /> <br /> Vitae created by this spell is not addictve. Furthermore, the vitae created by this spell can sustain a vampire of any Blood Potency. The Vitae created by this spell becomes normal substance after the Duration expires, unless it has been consumed.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may freely divide the damage between subjects in the spell. While the Curse damns the one who meddles with it directly, it is less &quot;concerned&quot; with other subjects. Other subjects do not suffer resistant damage.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may bypass the vampiric curse almost completely by substituting Mana for suffering. The Mage may spend Mana to reduce the damage the spell inflicts, one-for-one. The mage can spend as much Mana as desired, though they are still limited by their Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T18:46:44-07:00","id":1109531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109170#post1109170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players have found a vampire, and of course, this means they want to make Vitae. I have created three spells to deal with Vitae. I based them on spells presented earlier in this thread, as well as the first edition rules for creating blood that vampires can drink. I have discarded the 1e notion that Prime is required to make actual vampiric VItae, instead ruling that it is under the purview of Life (although maybe there's also an argument for Death). Due to the alien nature of the vampiric curse, these spells depart a tiny bit from the regular creative thaumaturgy rules. This mostly concerns the inflicting of damage, representative of the vampiric curse's cost. It always gets what it desires, one way or another.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Channel Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage is able to channel Vitae between herself and vampires, strix, ghouls, other living targets, or inanimate receptacles.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Weaving</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Survival</li> </ul>The spell allows the mage to move a quantity of Vitae up to the spell's Potency between one or more vessels she can touch, including herself, vampires, ghouls, strix, other living targets, or physical containers. Transferring the vitae into a subject forces the effects of Vitae consumption upon the it: vampires gain more Vitae, living targets may become ghouls, and so forth. If the Vitae is transferred into a container, it maintains its nature as Vitae for the Duration of the spell before reverting to normal blood.<br /> <br /> The mage may channel a number of points of Vitae per turn equal to her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may channel as much Vitae as she wants in one turn, ignoring her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and +1 Mana:</b> When the vitae is transferred into a subject, the effects of the Vitae are suppressed for the Duration of the spell. This effect suppresses the effects of Vitae for one subject, and can be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampirism (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage patterns the blood of a living subject into vampiric Vitae and draws it from the victim.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana</li> </ul>The Vitae drawn is usually in the form of blood oozing from wounds, but can be a more exotic substance, depending on the method the mage uses to &quot;feed&quot; on the subject. This spell generates one Vitae per Potency. Since the spell directly patterns Life into Vitae, the subject is not harmed. The quality of the Vitae is relative to the subject (animals produce animal-quality Vitae and humans produce human-quality).<br /> <br /> The Vitae remains supernatural until the Duration of the spell expires, at which point it turns back into regular substance, unless it has been consumed. The use of this spell is an affront to the vampiric Curse, and damns the mage: the mage must include themselves as a subject in the spell, and they take 1 resistant Lethal damage per Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may apply one suitable Condition or Tilt to the subject per level of Potency, representative of the vampiric feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may freely divide the damage between subjects in the spell. While the Curse damns the one who meddles with it directly, it is less &quot;concerned&quot; with other subjects. Other subjects do not suffer resistant damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death, Mind, or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage may draw from ghosts (Death), goetia (mind), or spirits (Spirit).<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage can convert the Vitae into tass in a form of her choosing. The tass functions as Vitae and Mana, and if ingestible, can be consumed by Vampires. The tass created has the resonance keyword of &quot;vampirism.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Create Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> This spell creates Vitae from nothing.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Making</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Medicine, Occult</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Blood Potency, Stamina, or Resistance (depending on target)</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1+ Mana</li> </ul>The spell creates an amount of pure, inert Vitae equal to Potency in the subject, which may be a vampire, strix, living target, or container. If created outside of an animate subject, the mage chooses the form the Vitae takes (and must have a way to contain the resulting Vitae), and the spell is Withstood by the mage's own Stamina.<br /> <br /> As always, the vampiric curse takes its debt: the mage must include themselves as a subject in the spell, and they suffer 1 resistant lethal damage per point of Potency.<br /> <br /> Vitae created by this spell is not addictve. Furthermore, the vitae created by this spell can sustain a vampire of any Blood Potency. The Vitae created by this spell becomes normal substance after the Duration expires, unless it has been consumed.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may freely divide the damage between subjects in the spell. While the Curse damns the one who meddles with it directly, it is less &quot;concerned&quot; with other subjects. Other subjects do not suffer resistant damage.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may bypass the vampiric curse almost completely by substituting Mana for suffering. The Mage may spend Mana to reduce the damage the spell inflicts, one-for-one. The mage can spend as much Mana as desired, though they are still limited by their Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add a Death 5 add on for ways to produce Vitae which gives it the Property to create Revenant (as per Vampire the Requiem), but through the normal means of what happens when someone who has previously had Vitae in their system dies or is exsanguinated.<br /> <br /> That side effect being a Lasting opt in to the fickle nature of accidental Revenant creation inherent in the Curse.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's too close to Archmastery, or maybe it is more similar to a side effect of a minor template, ghouldom, and thus okay. Is wolfbloodedness attainable with Spirit? I mean now it's a possible side effect of Lunacy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-29-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T05:27:28-07:00","id":1109705,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Firstly, I think this is something that should be rare, difficult and dangerous. To that end I like the health cost. I\u2019d also add that this shouldn\u2019t be something anyone with enough dots in the Arcanum could do - I\u2019d charge an Arcane Experience for the privilege, or at least add the roleplaying requirement that you have to have experimented on a vampire or been taught by someone who has, kind of like the Scelestus Paradox control. I\u2019d also add the requirement that the mage needs to have Vitae in her system, at least at some point during the learning process. I like the idea that a mage can\u2019t replicate the curse of vampirism, but she </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>can</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> harness it - if she\u2019s willing to let it touch her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondly, I would strongly argue that since vampires are fundamentally creatures of Death, manipulating them and their essential energies falls under the purview of that Arcanum. If you really wanted to hammer home that this is weird, rare magic though you could rule that it requires both Death and Life. After all, what is Vitae but the energies of Life converted into fuel for Death?</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Channel Vitae (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage is able to channel Vitae between herself and vampires, strix, ghouls, other living targets, or inanimate receptacles.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Weaving</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Occult, Survival</li> </ul>The spell allows the mage to move a quantity of Vitae up to the spell's Potency between one or more vessels she can touch, including herself, vampires, ghouls, strix, other living targets, or physical containers. Transferring the vitae into a subject forces the effects of Vitae consumption upon the it: vampires gain more Vitae, <b>living targets may become ghouls</b>, and so forth. If the Vitae is transferred into a container, it maintains its nature as Vitae for the Duration of the spell before reverting to normal blood.<br /> <br /> The mage may channel a number of points of Vitae per turn equal to her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may channel as much Vitae as she wants in one turn, ignoring her Gnosis-derived Mana per turn limit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and +1 Mana:</b> When the vitae is transferred into a subject, the effects of the Vitae are suppressed for the Duration of the spell. This effect suppresses the effects of Vitae for one subject, and can be applied multiple times. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Small nitpick: creating a ghoul is an intentional act of will on the part of the vampire. Just having Vitae injected into your system isn\u2019t going to turn you into one outside of ST fiat.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampirism (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> The mage patterns the blood of a living subject into vampiric Vitae and draws it from the victim.<ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion</li> <li><b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana</li> </ul>The Vitae drawn is usually in the form of blood oozing from wounds, but can be a more exotic substance, depending on the method the mage uses to &quot;feed&quot; on the subject. This spell generates one Vitae per Potency. <b>Since the spell directly patterns Life into Vitae, the subject is not harmed.</b> The quality of the Vitae is relative to the subject (animals produce animal-quality Vitae and humans produce human-quality).<br /> <br /> The Vitae remains supernatural until the Duration of the spell expires, at which point it turns back into regular substance, unless it has been consumed. The use of this spell is an affront to the vampiric Curse, and damns the mage: the mage must include themselves as a subject in the spell, and they take 1 resistant Lethal damage per Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may apply one suitable Condition or Tilt to the subject per level of Potency, representative of the vampiric feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may freely divide the damage between subjects in the spell. While the Curse damns the one who meddles with it directly, it is less &quot;concerned&quot; with other subjects. Other subjects do not suffer resistant damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death, Mind, or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage may draw from ghosts (Death), goetia (mind), or spirits (Spirit).<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Mage can convert the Vitae into tass in a form of her choosing. The tass functions as Vitae and Mana, and if ingestible, can be consumed by Vampires. The tass created has the resonance keyword of &quot;vampirism.&quot; </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bolded part doesn\u2019t make sense to me. How does pulling part of the subject\u2019s Pattern out and turning it into Vitae not harm them, especially if it manifests as bleeding wounds? Further, the fact that this has no additional downside means it\u2019s just better than Create Vitae in most circumstances.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T07:29:29-07:00","id":1109751,"title":"","content":"Somewhat related, I think Space should definitely be included in any spell to manipulate/emulate the Blood Bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:56:08-07:00","id":1109878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109705#post1109705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Firstly, I think this is something that should be rare, difficult and dangerous. To that end I like the health cost. I\u2019d also add that this shouldn\u2019t be something anyone with enough dots in the Arcanum could do - I\u2019d charge an Arcane Experience for the privilege, or at least add the roleplaying requirement that you have to have experimented on a vampire or been taught by someone who has, kind of like the Scelestus Paradox control. I\u2019d also add the requirement that the mage needs to have Vitae in her system, at least at some point during the learning process. I like the idea that a mage can\u2019t replicate the curse of vampirism, but she </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>can</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> harness it - if she\u2019s willing to let it touch her.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I would enforce it as a role-playing requirement: the characters would first have to research and experiment with vampirism before they could truly replicate it. This seems to be a common theme with MtAw 2e: basically anything is possible... if you know how to do it. I don't think charging XP is a good solution, unless maybe it's a one-time deal to learn the arcane secrets required for these spells. I certainly wouldn't charge 1 Arcane XP per spell casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondly, I would strongly argue that since vampires are fundamentally creatures of Death, manipulating them and their essential energies falls under the purview of that Arcanum. If you really wanted to hammer home that this is weird, rare magic though you could rule that it requires both Death and Life. After all, what is Vitae but the energies of Life converted into fuel for Death?</span></span> </div> </div> </div>It could definitely be a Life + Death conjunctional spell. It depends on how the Storyteller rules vampires. In my case, I've already ruled that it's a Life spell in my game and I don't think it'll really be necessary to change it since the occurrences are so rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Small nitpick: creating a ghoul is an intentional act of will on the part of the vampire. Just having Vitae injected into your system isn\u2019t going to turn you into one outside of ST fiat.</span> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps this could be specified as a Reach +Mana effect on the spell, then. I think ghoul creation is better suited to Patterning though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bolded part doesn\u2019t make sense to me. How does pulling part of the subject\u2019s Pattern out and turning it into Vitae not harm them, especially if it manifests as bleeding wounds? Further, the fact that this has no additional downside means it\u2019s just better than Create Vitae in most circumstances.</span> </div> </div> </div>The spell went through several revisions before the form presented here. Originally I had it inflicting Resistant damage to the victim, but then I decided just to make the mage suffer damage. I suppose it could inflict damage to both the mage and the victim(s). The reason I chose not to have it deal damage to the victim without a Reach effect is because of the Patterning practice, plus it's the mage who pays the price (by default). The description could use some work--but I think &quot;it's magic&quot; is a sufficient enough in-world explanation as to why the target wouldn't be injured despite having bleeding wounds.<br /> <br /> The mechanical argument for having it damage the target is very relevant though.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, what do you think makes the spell better than Create Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:18:35-07:00","id":1109895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109878#post1109878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would enforce it as a role-playing requirement: the characters would first have to research and experiment with vampirism before they could truly replicate it. This seems to be a common theme with MtAw 2e: basically anything is possible... if you know how to do it. I don't think charging XP is a good solution, unless maybe it's a one-time deal to learn the arcane secrets required for these spells. I certainly wouldn't charge 1 Arcane XP per spell casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh goodness, I didn't mean one experience for each cast. I meant paying one experience to learn how to cast all these spells. On reflection I'd go with your option unless I decided to give them some other benefit for paying the exp, like maybe the ability to store Vitae - but at that point you're basically designing a new Legacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109878#post1109878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could definitely be a Life + Death conjunctional spell. It depends on how the Storyteller rules vampires. In my case, I've already ruled that it's a Life spell in my game and I don't think it'll really be necessary to change it since the occurrences are so rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109878#post1109878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell went through several revisions before the form presented here. Originally I had it inflicting Resistant damage to the victim, but then I decided just to make the mage suffer damage. I suppose it could inflict damage to both the mage and the victim(s). The reason I chose not to have it deal damage to the victim without a Reach effect is because of the Patterning practice, plus it's the mage who pays the price (by default). The description could use some work--but I think &quot;it's magic&quot; is a sufficient enough in-world explanation as to why the target wouldn't be injured despite having bleeding wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would make more sense if it were a Death spell. As it is, you could stipulate that you have to drain the blood and turn that into Vitae at the usual rate of one lethal/one Vitae. You can still just Knit it back, but futzing with needles and bags (or knives and buckets if that\u2019s how you roll) adds both the edge of madness you want blood magic to have and an obstruction that really differentiates it from Create Vitae.<br /> <br /> e: on that note, I suggest adding a cosmetic rider to Create Vitae that makes it a little more Vampire-y. Like you have to cut yourself (doing no additional damage) and physically bleed the Vitae into the container.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1109878#post1109878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, what do you think makes the spell better than Create Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does pretty much the same thing but at a lower dot rating, and is therefore accessible to lesser mages and can be stuffed with more Reach. Especially because, though I'm pretty sure this wasn't your intention, you always have a living thing at hand; yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 06-30-2017, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:01:36-07:00","id":1109997,"title":"","content":"Patterning the blood itself would certainly make the 4-dot spell less powerful. But in some ways, that's ... <i>boring</i>! I want to capture the idea of vampirism in a spell. I can't have the spell damage the victim because then the mage loses the interaction with the vampiric curse (essentially they just get a better version of the Life 4 damage spell). Patterning blood directly also doesn't cover the more exotic vampire-esque beings in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, patterning blood directly is much simpler, and probably is what most mages would do in order to make Vitae using Life 4. I feel like if you pattern blood directly, then there's no need for resistant damage.<br /> <br /> What about simply removing the Reach effect on the Patterning spell that allows damage to be redistributed? That would make meddling with the Curse quite dangerous... A Master might be able to get away with circumventing the Curse, but not an Adept!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T03:05:01-07:00","id":1110107,"title":"","content":"Personally I think it's less boring. Since the spell as it stands doesn't really affect the subject, you're more or less conjuring Vitae out of thin air. That's not very vampiric at all! Why are you so opposed to dealing damage to both mage and subject, anyway? Then it's not a better damage spell.<br /> <br /> Another option is to make a spell that allows the mage to transform part of themselves into an organ that processes blood into Vitae. May or may not come with free fangs. This wouldn't be my preferred option though, because I'd rather have mages toy with Vitae in a weird, mage-y way than transforming themselves into knockoff vampires. Or maybe go really weird with it and allow them to hork up part of their liver and turn it into a semi-autonomous leech-thing that drinks blood and produces Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T07:07:39-07:00","id":1110148,"title":"","content":"I agree that taking Vitae should cause damage. Vitae is the literal life stolen from a victim. I believe dealing lethal is an integral part in natural generation of Vitae. The Strix deal lethal through their breath-drinking without taking any important bodily fluids. If you're not dealing lethal then you're not actually converting anything to Vitae. You're Making it instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:29:09-07:00","id":1110227,"title":"","content":"If it's the Patterning bit that bothers you, remember that that Practice isn't just about benign transformation. Patterning can be used destructively, like how you can effectively destroy a building by Patterning the concrete into ice cream. In this case you're transforming the subject's blood into something that is a) not blood and b) not in their body any more.<br /> <br /> On a tangent, there's actually no reason the Life 4 direct damage spell has to be Unraveling. It's the obvious choice, but it could just as easily be a Patterning spell that causes the subject to get stabbed by their own bones.<br /> <br /> e: or indeed, pulls their blood out through their nostrils","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:57:45-07:00","id":1111437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1069276#post1069276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi wise ones.<br /> I was wondering about how to manage a Veiling Life spell to render a living veign &quot;hidden&quot; or undetectable, like Hidden Hoard (Matter oo). But I have some questions on this regard:<br /> Would only affect a naked person?, if the person has clothes, would the spell fail?, what happens if the subject grabs an object or moves?<br /> <br /> I would rule the spell provides full ocultation for a naked subject. If the subject wear clothes or grabs an item, the spell will begin to fade and the onlookers will detect the subject's presence, but they won't be able to tell who is. Mostly like a ghost presence. If the spell subject drops the item or undresses, he will become undetectable again.<br /> <br /> I will be happy to read how you would manage this spell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When in doubt, add Reach effects or Additional Arcana. The spell at its basic effect would result in something like The Invisible Man, where you have a bunch of objects and clothing tracing out a man's silhouette walking around. Veiling objects that are on the subject's person at the moment of casting should be a +1 Reach effect, and/or a Add Matter 2 effect.<br /> <br /> When the subject grabs an object, don't make the spell fade. Instead, it would appear that the object grabbed is floating around on its own. If a Sleeper noticed this, Dissonance would unravel the spell anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:44:32-07:00","id":1111458,"title":"","content":"A Life spell can probably Veil your clothes as well pretty easily, like the way that Incognito Presence touches the mind of everyone you walk past and you just slip out of their memory it would touch the senses of everyone you walked past and delete your presence (Clothes and all) from their senses. It has the same problem as Incognito Presence though which is that it has no effect on non-living eyes or technology and likewise wouldn't effect anyone viewing you via technology. Should probably cost a mana.<br /> <br /> Every Path can probably Veil its members to be beyond casual notice with at least one of their arcana. Fate I imagine would basically just cause a series of small coincidences that let you be basically invisible to everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-04-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:42:25-07:00","id":1111487,"title":"","content":"But Inc\u00f3gnito Presence altersand veils perception, Life would only make invisible the biological parts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T20:26:09-07:00","id":1111533,"title":"","content":"Incognito Presence futzes with your perception after the fact (Hence the memory edit it throws in for free), Life could easily futz with your ability to perceive in the first place.<br /> <br /> Veiling in general is the Practice on which illusion(s) are premised. So for me it's not at all a stretch to say that a Life Veiling effect clouds the vision of living beings such that it misses you and your clothes in one go.<br /> <br /> Obviously, YMMV, I'm just throwing in my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T03:21:07-07:00","id":1111598,"title":"","content":"True, Veiling does two things basically, hiding or altering what is perceived of the things under its purview and what is perceived by the things under its purview. You could totally use Life to be undetectable by living beigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T09:23:54-07:00","id":1111679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1111598#post1111598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, Veiling does two things basically, hiding or altering what is perceived of the things under its purview and what is perceived by the things under its purview. You could totally use Life to be undetectable by living beigns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally True, I am picturing the first attempt at veiling Life ending up as the Invisible Man as the mage attempt to hide his Living Pattern but noticing it doesn't affect his Cloths.<br /> <br /> Then realizing that didn't work he as he hoped then envisions in his Imago as hiding him and his possessions from Living things, which works a world better, until he realizes either through thought experiment or actual experience that does nothing to hide him from unliving beings, like corporeal undead, goetia, ghosts, spirits and the like.<br /> <br /> The attempt to make the veil the &quot;best possible&quot; he mixes both approaches through mental gymnastics, but now his body invisible to everyone including the unliving, but this possessions being only invisible to the living, possibly drawing more attention from the non-living as to why a set of empty cloths are walking down the street and none of the mortals notice something so strange. In fact I think that is a fun plot hook for introducing a vampire to an inexperienced mage NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-05-2017, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:53:46-07:00","id":1112046,"title":"","content":"Hi there !<br /> <br /> Since I like homebrewing things for Mages (Legacies in particular), I took the initiative of gathering &quot;completed&quot; Spells into a google doc. I tried to avoid redundancies and still-in-progress Spells : the name disclaimer is only the name of the one who posted the Spell in its final version, not necessarily the original ideas (feel free to make reclamation if you feel prejudiced).<br /> <br /> Edit: I counted 199 Spells. Cool, isn't it ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta-9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","user":"Adrasalieth","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T06:44:42-07:00","id":1112082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112046#post1112046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there !<br /> <br /> Since I like homebrewing things for Mages (Legacies in particular), I took the initiative of gathering &quot;completed&quot; Spells into a google doc. I tried to avoid redundancies and still-in-progress Spells : the name disclaimer is only the name of the one who posted the Spell in its final version, not necessarily the original ideas (feel free to make reclamation if you feel prejudiced).<br /> <br /> Edit: I counted 199 Spells. Cool, isn't it ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta-9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's all kinds of awesome, thanks for your work.<br /> <br /> I propose that link be added to the OP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:09:32-07:00","id":1112088,"title":"","content":"Are those the spells in their final versions after commentary from the forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:01:22-07:00","id":1112107,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I tried to only copy those who had been reworked to integrate the feedback. If the Spell didn't had any more critique, I picked it as the final version. Nut then again, if I skipped over one or made a mistake, I opened the doc for modifications, so don't hesitate to correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:22:57-07:00","id":1112512,"title":"","content":"<b>Spell: Reveal the Shadows' Secrets (Death </b>\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Occult, Stealth<br /> <br /> Let the Obrimos magnify trace glimmers of starlight and the Thyrsus borrow the eyes of cats; the Moros claim they know what it is to truly see in darkness. The shadows hold no secrets from the mage, but she loses the ability to see colors; the eyes of the dead see only ten thousand shades of grey.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The shadows do more than lift their veils; they <i>whisper</i>, and in their susurrus reveal a myriad of hidden secrets. The mage can see in all directions and from all points within her sensory range simultaneously, ignoring walls and other obstacles, so long as those points have some substantial measure of shadow or darkness; beneath the blazing eye of a noontime sun or the moonscape glare of a stadium's floodlights, the shadows are too weak and thin to offer much guidance. While within or targeting such a point, the mage penalizes ambush attempts by Potency.<br /> <br /> (Reference to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F157geaXp_w\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F157geaXp_w</a> while casting may, at GM's option, be used as a +1-die Yantra.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":". 07-07-2017, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:42:26-07:00","id":1112615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112512#post1112512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spell: Reveal the Shadows' Secrets (Death </b>\u25cf)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Occult, Stealth<br /> <br /> Let the Obrimos magnify trace glimmers of starlight and the Thyrsus borrow the eyes of cats; the Moros claim they know what it is to truly see in darkness. The shadows hold no secrets from the mage, but she loses the ability to see colors; the eyes of the dead see only ten thousand shades of grey.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The shadows do more than lift their veils; they <i>whisper</i>, and in their susurrus reveal a myriad of hidden secrets. <b>The mage can see in all directions and from all points within her sensory range simultaneously, ignoring walls and other obstacles,</b> so long as those points have some substantial measure of shadow or darkness; beneath the blazing eye of a noontime sun or the moonscape glare of a stadium's floodlights, the shadows are too weak and thin to offer much guidance. While within or targeting such a point, the mage penalizes ambush attempts by Potency.<br /> <br /> (Reference to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F157geaXp_w\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F157geaXp_w</a> while casting may, at GM's option, be used as a +1-die Yantra.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded sentence is the Purview of space, By definition the sensory range is blocked by obstacles, and shifting your senses to a different location is remote viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:06:05-07:00","id":1112624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112615#post1112615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bolded sentence is the Purview of space, By definition the sensory range is blocked by obstacles, and shifting your senses to a different location is remote viewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean it's solely the purview of that Arcanum, especially if other Arcana only have access to limited versions appropriate to their purview. Life for example has spells that shift your senses into other living beings. If Death alone lets you create physical objects from shadows and bodily turn into shadow, I'd say it lets you extend your senses through them as well.<br /> <br /> The phrasing is a little weird, though. I guess &quot;sensory range&quot; is meant to imply the same thing as the Space version (&quot;She cannot perceive things farther away than her normal perceptions might allow&quot;) but either way I'd personally key it to the spell's Scale factor.<br /> <br /> The description of the Reach effect also implies something more narratively interesting than &quot;see everywhere all the time&quot;. I prefer the idea that the shadows actually talk, pointing out objects of obvious interest such as hostiles but have to be actively questioned on matters such as &quot;on what floor lies the Chalice of Arat?&quot;<br /> <br /> e: or rather, something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean you can't achieve similar results with other Arcana","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-07-2017, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:32:20-07:00","id":1112734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112624#post1112624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean it's solely the purview of that Arcanum, especially if other Arcana only have access to limited versions appropriate to their purview. Life for example has spells that shift your senses into other living beings. If Death alone lets you create physical objects from shadows and bodily turn into shadow, I'd say it lets you extend your senses through them as well.<br /> <br /> The phrasing is a little weird, though. I guess &quot;sensory range&quot; is meant to imply the same thing as the Space version (&quot;She cannot perceive things farther away than her normal perceptions might allow&quot;) but either way I'd personally key it to the spell's Scale factor.<br /> <br /> The description of the Reach effect also implies something more narratively interesting than &quot;see everywhere all the time&quot;. I prefer the idea that the shadows actually talk, pointing out objects of obvious interest such as hostiles but have to be actively questioned on matters such as &quot;on what floor lies the Chalice of Arat?&quot;<br /> <br /> e: or rather, something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean you can't achieve similar results with other Arcana</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this is where we disagree, and that is ok. I would have no problem if the Reach stated something to the effect of - Add Space: \u2022\u2022 The shadows do more than lift their veils; they <i>whisper</i>, and in their susurrus reveal a myriad of hidden secrets. The mage can see in all directions and from all points within her sensory range simultaneously, ignoring walls and other obstacles, so long as those points have some substantial measure of shadow or darkness; beneath the blazing eye of a noontime sun or the moonscape glare of a stadium's floodlights, the shadows are too weak and thin to offer much guidance. While within or targeting such a point, the mage penalizes ambush attempts by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:02:59-07:00","id":1112761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112624#post1112624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean it's solely the purview of that Arcanum, especially if other Arcana only have access to limited versions appropriate to their purview. Life for example has spells that shift your senses into other living beings. If Death alone lets you create physical objects from shadows and bodily turn into shadow, I'd say it lets you extend your senses through them as well.<br /> <br /> The phrasing is a little weird, though. I guess &quot;sensory range&quot; is meant to imply the same thing as the Space version (&quot;She cannot perceive things farther away than her normal perceptions might allow&quot;) but either way I'd personally key it to the spell's Scale factor.<br /> <br /> The description of the Reach effect also implies something more narratively interesting than &quot;see everywhere all the time&quot;. I prefer the idea that the shadows actually talk, pointing out objects of obvious interest such as hostiles but have to be actively questioned on matters such as &quot;on what floor lies the Chalice of Arat?&quot;<br /> <br /> e: or rather, something being the purview of one Arcanum doesn't mean you can't achieve similar results with other Arcana</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much, yes. I borrowed from &quot;The Outward &amp; Inward Eye&quot; verbatim for that line, because I wanted to stay on the right side of &quot;it's fine if different Arcana accomplish similar things at different ratings&quot; vs. &quot;this application of Arcana X makes a core capability of Arcana Y obsolete.&quot; Death will let you know there's someone hiding in the shadow behind a closed door; Space would let you trace his silhouette on the door, which is why Space 1 keeps exclusive access to reducing range/cover/concealment penalties and reduces ambush attempts to chance dice (and Space would function regardless of ambient lighting). <br /> <br /> I like the idea of having to pause to make out details. I'm not sold on the shadows literally talking at one dot; giving them that kind of &quot;life&quot; feels more comfortable at higher ratings (like 1e's &quot;Shadow Slave.&quot;) But I could see a situation in which the shadows reveal five men creeping up the stairs in the darkened apartment building, and you have to take an instant action to scrutinize their faces and pinpoint which one is the Seer leading the mooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:13:08-07:00","id":1112768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112734#post1112734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would have no problem if the Reach stated something to the effect of - Add Space: \u2022\u2022 ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Food for thought: if you had that level of Space already, you wouldn't need this spell to accomplish this kind of see-past-corners; you'd just cast &quot;Outward &amp; Inward Eye&quot; and get the &quot;full&quot; version.<br /> <br /> And in support of the proposition that purviews aren't meant to be exclusive, I can't say it any better than whoever wrote the sidebar on pg. 124: &quot;Astute players will likely figure out a multitude of ways to accomplish similar effects with different Arcana, sometimes at different dot levels. <i>This is okay.</i> Just because a Fate 3 spell can do a thing doesn't mean a Forces 1 spell that does a similar thing is &quot;broken&quot; or should be disallowed.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's room to defend the exclusivity of Arcana where a spell would tread on its core capabilities: e.g. if &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot; let you make equipment with ratings equal to Potency, you'd have a strong argument that Matter's core role as &quot;the best forge &amp; crafting magic&quot; would be rendered obsolete. I don't think that's the case here; if I'd tried to go with a Death 2 effect that let you scry through shadows on the other side of the city, that would be a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:21:10-07:00","id":1112773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112768#post1112768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Food for thought: if you had that level of Space already, you wouldn't need this spell to accomplish this kind of see-past-corners; you'd just cast &quot;Outward &amp; Inward Eye&quot; and get the &quot;full&quot; version.<br /> <br /> And in support of the proposition that purviews aren't meant to be exclusive, I can't say it any better than whoever wrote the sidebar on pg. 124: &quot;Astute players will likely figure out a multitude of ways to accomplish similar effects with different Arcana, sometimes at different dot levels. <i>This is okay.</i> Just because a Fate 3 spell can do a thing doesn't mean a Forces 1 spell that does a similar thing is &quot;broken&quot; or should be disallowed.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's room to defend the exclusivity of Arcana where a spell would tread on its core capabilities: e.g. if &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot; let you make equipment with ratings equal to Potency, you'd have a strong argument that Matter's core role as &quot;the best forge &amp; crafting magic&quot; would be rendered obsolete. I don't think that's the case here; if I'd tried to go with a Death 2 effect that let you scry through shadows on the other side of the city, that would be a different story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that is my whole point seeing past physical objects is stepping on the toes of Space, you are extending your sensory range beyond the normal allowed. And the Adder that I talked about would give you something over the space. It would allow you to see in the dark where space doesn't allow that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:37:27-07:00","id":1112850,"title":"","content":"So, I've made this list to get a better picture how a technomage would work technology (mostly computers) into spells. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <b>Accessible Computing (Forces \u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Compelling and Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Computer, Expression, Persuasion<br /> <br /> This spell allows the mage to give commands directly to a device without the need for any input devices like keyboards, computer mice, touchpads, etc. As well as allowing the mage the mage to see the computers responses without any output devices like monitors or speakers. Both effects still happen at about the same speed as if those devices were used however.<br /> <br /> This spell can bypass any penalties from Condition or Tilts that would normally prevent or hinder the use of any electronic devices (like Blind, Arm Wreck, etc.).<br /> <br /> <b>Magnetoreception (Forces \u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Science, Survival, Animal Ken<br /> <br /> The earth's magnetic field has a strength of 0.5 Gauss (Unit) and animals use it to orient themselves. But this presents a paradox, for the strength of these fields is many orders less than an elementary chemical act.<br /> As well as not being strong enough to generate appreciable heating of tissue or cause irritation. So, how do animals sense it? who knows? I don't! But with this spell the mage can sense and use the earth's fields as well as most any animal.<br /> <br /> This spell gives the mage the benefit of the Direction Sense Merit, but only so long as the earth's magnetic field can be detected and isn't being altered by any strong magnetic forces in the area.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: In addition to the earth's magnetic fields the mage can sense electrical fields in general. This can be used to locate living beings, in the same way as some sharks do. These sharks can locate prey even when said prey has buried itself, the mage now has the same ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Firewall (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Computer, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> A shielding spell knows what harms its subject and prevents it. Much like how a Matter shielding spell can protect the mage from a caustic atmosphere and yet allow a normal one. So too does this spell prevent any harmful software and traffic from reaching its technological subjects while still allowing the harmless.<br /> <br /> Supernatural attempts to cause digital harm provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Rewrite System (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Computer, Expression<br /> <br /> With this spell a mage can change a system\u2019s programming. This means she can rewrite existing programs or install wholly new ones. This can be used to create handy applications or to instantly give systems a virus or spyware.<br /> <br /> The changes are not instant. The spell gives the system all the information and commands needed to make the changes, but the system still needs time to install/apply these.<br /> <br /> The effects of this spell are lasting which means that the changes made can be noticed.<br /> If the mage makes only subtle changes however apply the following rules for discovery by any users:<br /> <br /> - A user knowledgeable about either this specific system or about systems of this type in general may make a reflexive Intelligence + Computer roll penalized by the mage's Computer Skill to discover any changes the mage made.<br /> - If the user is not familiar with the system, or failed the reflexive roll, but still suspects tampering they may make an extended Intelligence + Computer penalized by the Mage's Computer Skill with a target number of Potency to discover it.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The effects of this spell take place instantly.<br /> <br /> <b>The Future Is Now (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Computer, Science<br /> <br /> This spell allows computer hardware to go far beyond its limits. For every level of Potency double the hardware\u2019s performance. For example, Potency 3 would be eight times the performance.<br /> <br /> This spell increases a computers equipment bonus. For personal computers, this bonus is equal to Availability and normally ranges from +1 to +4. This spell doubles the bonus per level of Potency to a maximum of +4.<br /> <br /> Die bonuses for anything beyond the scale of PCs and similar devices are Storyteller fiat. This includes things like supercomputers.<br /> <br /> For supercomputers, as a rule of thumb assume that they are about 10.000 times faster at the calculations they were designed for than your average pc. So, you\u2019d need Potency 11 to bring an average pc up to supercomputer level. Using this spell on a supercomputer would probably result in record breaking performance.<br /> <br /> <b>Digital Citizen (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Computer, Intimidation, Persuasion<br /> <br /> With this spell the mage can temporally make digital systems aid the subject regardless of the subject's actual skill in interacting with such devices. Systems will try to consider the subject's intentions rather than only following his physical inputs into the system. This spell doesn't actually increase the subject's knowledge, but effectively increases the subject's Computer Skill by Potency up to the normal maximum.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: By spending a point of Mana, the Computer Skill may be raised above the normal maximum.<br /> <br /> <b>Technostress (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Computer, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> In the face of ever more ubiquitous recording devices and a greater ability for people to communicate with one another, the Guardians often have a difficult time protecting the Veil. But the Guardians have ways of denying people these advantages, such as this spell.<br /> With this spell the mage can temporally make digital systems oppose the subject. Every system and device that the subject uses will start having problems or otherwise do anything but what the subject requires.<br /> This prevents the subject from gaining any aid from electronic devices whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <b>Hologram (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Science, Expression<br /> <br /> The mage can bend light fields to create holograms. These hologram looks like the real thing for all intents and purposes. But make no sound and any attempt to touch them will reveal they are not real but holograms.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The holograms can now also create sound.<br /> <br /> Add Death 3: If a ghost is included in the spell's subjects, the ghost may control the holograms.<br /> Add Mind 3: If a goetia is included in the spell's subjects, the goetia may control the holograms.<br /> Add Spirit 3: If a spirit is included in the spell's subjects, the spirit may control the holograms.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Engineering (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Politics, Socialize, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Social media facilitates the creation and sharing of information and ideas, with this spell the mage creates social networks where none existed before.<br /> <br /> The mage chooses a target organization or group and fabricates a favorable digital history between the mage and the target. How this history looks is entirely up to the mage, maybe records show the mage has worked there, that he is an important customer or that he has an appointment at three. None of this history actually happened of course and people won't recognize the mage. But so long as the mage pretends it did, and nobody calls his bluff, they may make use of these organizations as the Merits Allies, Contact, Status or even Resources.<br /> <br /> For each level of Potency, the subject gains one dot in one of the following Merits: Allies, Contacts, Status or Resources.<br /> <br /> Drawback: This spell takes advantage of the fact that in large organizations nobody can know everybody. Consequently, this spell cannot be used effectively on smaller groups as they are far more likely to see through your ruse.<br /> <br /> <b>Neo-Luddite (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Within the area of the spell the mage destroys all manifestation of electromagnetic forces that are commonly used in technology. Electric currents, wireless transmissions, lasers, etc.<br /> This spell is used in a process called &quot;rewildening&quot; by a Free Council anarcho-primitivist philosophy that supposes that technology is purely an instrument of the Lie and that the future Atlantis will be ruled by magic utterly without technology.<br /> <br /> Add Matter 5: This spell also destroys any manifestation of advanced materials. This could be plastics as well as any alloy more advanced than bronze. Although the specifics depend on the mage casting the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Update:</b><br /> Changed 'Cyber self-defence' to 'Firewall'.<br /> Updated 'Rewrite System' to include Potency as a target number.<br /> Rewrote description of 'Social Media' and renamed it as 'Social Engineering'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","user":"BeyondTheGrave","date":". 07-08-2017, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:18:12-07:00","id":1112982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112850#post1112850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cyber self-defense (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>My only nitpick is that this spell should be called Firewall.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Rewrite System needs a target number on that extended roll (Potency?), and Social Media strikes me as odd (besides the strangeness behind a Forces spell granting social merits, why is Resources not on the list?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:58:56-07:00","id":1113399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112982#post1112982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only nitpick is that this spell should be called Firewall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Firewall is better. I think I was trying too hard to be clever with my spell names on that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than that, Rewrite System needs a target number on that extended roll (Potency?), </div> </div> </div>Updated the spell to include target number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and Social Media strikes me as odd (besides the strangeness behind a Forces spell granting social merits, why is Resources not on the list?). </div> </div> </div>I've rewritten and renamed the entire thing to much better express what I actually wanted for this spell to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:07:05-07:00","id":1113736,"title":"","content":"<b>Speed Reading (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Computer, Expression<br /> <br /> The subject of this spell finds their ability to comprehend and process information. They can do so at Potency + 1 times the normal speed. This allows them to read a book, watch a movie, and or research with Extended rolls.<br /> <br /> Reach +1: Able to correctly project shots and thereby react before the shooter can, the subject can now apply their Defense against firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T07:59:07-07:00","id":1114153,"title":"","content":"First, I really love these!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112850#post1112850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've made this list to get a better picture how a technomage would work technology (mostly computers) into spells. What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> <b>Technostress (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Computer, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> In the face of ever more ubiquitous recording devices and a greater ability for people to communicate with one another, the Guardians often have a difficult time protecting the Veil. But the Guardians have ways of denying people these advantages, such as this spell.<br /> With this spell the mage can temporally make digital systems oppose the subject. Every system and device that the subject uses will start having problems or otherwise do anything but what the subject requires.<br /> This prevents the subject from gaining any aid from electronic devices whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider whether this shouldn't have some sort of Fate aspect, maybe? Could Forces alone actually do this? I'm not experienced at all with designing new spells, but feels like Forces on its own could maybe cause a person to actually break things (e.g. by having them emit some sort of magnetic fields or shortcircuit technology). But that more generic malfunctions would require some sort of &quot;bad luck&quot; aspect as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Social Engineering (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Politics, Socialize, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Social media facilitates the creation and sharing of information and ideas, with this spell the mage creates social networks where none existed before.<br /> <br /> The mage chooses a target organization or group and fabricates a favorable digital history between the mage and the target. How this history looks is entirely up to the mage, maybe records show the mage has worked there, that he is an important customer or that he has an appointment at three. None of this history actually happened of course and people won't recognize the mage. But so long as the mage pretends it did, and nobody calls his bluff, they may make use of these organizations as the Merits Allies, Contact, Status or even Resources.<br /> <br /> For each level of Potency, the subject gains one dot in one of the following Merits: Allies, Contacts, Status or Resources.<br /> <br /> Drawback: This spell takes advantage of the fact that in large organizations nobody can know everybody. Consequently, this spell cannot be used effectively on smaller groups as they are far more likely to see through your ruse.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Same with this, would it really be Forces alone? Shouldn't it require something like Mind to know what is required for it to be plausible, and Space to remotely put this information into any systems that have to be rewritten?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","user":"Razikale","date":". 07-11-2017, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T08:17:59-07:00","id":1114164,"title":"","content":"Forces is basically the programming arcana, Technostress is basically like creating a program that makes using the machine unintuitive enough that it's difficult to use, like a highly personalized version of Linux that doesn't use a GUI or something. The spell is basically doing that, but the mechanics are generic.<br /> <br /> Social Engineering is basically creating a bunch of falsified information and then relying on the system being large enough that no one does a thorough authentification check on that information so you can fraudulently take advantage of those merits.<br /> <br /> Both spells make perfect sense to me as being just Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:20:45-07:00","id":1114275,"title":"","content":"<b><u>NOTE: The mind spells have been combined into one and altered a little based on input from</u></b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <br /> <br /> Havn't been able to find any spells that allowed a mage to change memories. There was one to hide them and one to destroy them.<br /> I tried to compare these two spells to them in terms of power and how it worked.<br /> <br /> The third one isn't a mind spell, but could be, but I like the idea of the Arcanums being able to lap over in some situations.<br /> =================================<br /> <br /> <b><u>Blur the Past (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</u></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academia, Stealth, Subterfuge <br /> The mage can change a memory without the need to read the subjects mind, as long it is a memory he knows the subject has. Either the mage experienced it himself, saw a video or a photo with an accurate description. The changed memory must still be within the same context of the original memory. The number of changes that can be made is equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> Once the Duration expires, the subject instantly reverts to its original memory. Memories of the time spent \u201cblurred\u201d will seem distant and hazy, dreamlike, but the subject will remember the altered perspective at least to some degree. But if the memory that is changed is very trivial to the subject and the duration is long enough, the subject may have naturally forgotten the change as time passes, even when the spell ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> A Willworker can completely rework what the subject can remember. One memory per Potency can be changed to anything the mage wishes.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>The effect is lasting.<br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Doorway Effect (Space \u2022\u2022)</span></u></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academia, Survival, Expression<br /> <br /> The Doorway Effect is what happens when you leave a room and forget why you left it. This spell however ensures that the effect happens, making the subject forget the reason they left a room. This can happen a number of times equal to the spell's Potency and only non-threatening or urgent reasons can\u2019t be forgotten.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Even something threatening and urgent will be forgotten. However, if the danger or the urgency is still there, it would remind the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":".  Changed it based on input 07-12-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:09:58-07:00","id":1114305,"title":"","content":"<b>Defy Artifice (Matter \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Brawl, Survival, Athletics<br /> All worked Matter can change back to dust, and humanity's beloved tools are no exception. Bullets are crunched into scrap metal, swords fail to penetrate skin, and even random non-weapon objects lose their strength. The subject is immune to any bashing damage from man-made objects, while downgrading lethal damage equal to Potency to bashing. Aggravated damage is unaffected.<br /> Objects that have not been worked by human hands, such as a normal rock or a hunting knife forged by a werewolf bypass the protection. Barehanded assault is also an option, as are natural materials and substances wielded by a human.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The spell extends to natural objects that are used by a human as a weapon.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b>: The subject is immune to both bashing and lethal damage from artificial objects, and downgrades aggravated damage equal to Potency to lethal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Till Death Do Us Part (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Practice</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Unraveling</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Primary Factor</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Potency</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Empathy, Intimidation, Weaponry</span><br /> While some say our attachments shackle us, the more twisted warlocks can turn them into razor wires. This spell inflicts lethal damage equal to the strength of the sympathetic Connection between the mage and the victim. Magically altered sympathies do count, with spells like &quot;Web-Weaver&quot; increasing damage and &quot;Borrow Threads&quot; allowing the mage to attack with sympathies that are not her own. Magic that reduces sympathetic strength merely decreases the damage, but magic that conceals sympathies provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: With every attack, the sympathetic connection used is weakened by one step. The spell becomes Withstood by Connection strength, and it cannot weaken Connected sympathies.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: For a point of Mana, the spell inflicts aggravated damage instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  fixing wrongly bolded text 07-10-2017, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T16:46:38-07:00","id":1114315,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6718_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6718\" data-vbnamecard=\"6718\">Neros</a> changing memories is a Reach clause on Read the Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T02:06:10-07:00","id":1114483,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Didn't notice that one :P<br /> But why is completely changing a memory into something else at dot 3? Shouldn't it be a dot 4 effect to change the arcanum purview into something else?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Really nice spells. But if you look at many of the shielding spells there already is, they do not distinguish between Bashing or Lethal. The completely protect against the arcanum. Like ghost shield doesn't distinguish between being attacked by a ghost dealing bashing, lethal or aggravated damage. It just strait up sais &quot;nope&quot;.<br /> <br /> With &quot;Till Death do Us Part&quot;, I am having trouble visualizing how the spell actually deals the damage (the idea is still very nice. Really want a spell like this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T02:11:26-07:00","id":1114485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114483#post1114483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Didn't notice that one :P<br /> But why is completely changing a memory into something else at dot 3? Shouldn't it be a dot 4 effect to change the arcanum purview into something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Editing memory is more like sculpting an object than turning one thing into another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T02:40:37-07:00","id":1114493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114483#post1114483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Really nice spells. But if you look at many of the shielding spells there already is, they do not distinguish between Bashing or Lethal. The completely protect against the arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one that does though. &quot;Alchemist's touch&quot; is Matter Shielding spell that distinguishes between Bashing and Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","user":"BeyondTheGrave","date":". 07-11-2017, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T03:50:07-07:00","id":1114505,"title":"","content":"I have redone two of the vampire-related spells after considering criticism from the forum. The 4-dot spell now deals damage to the subjects in the spell as well as the mage. I removed the ability to divide damage between subjects in the spell, and the mage is no longer considered a subject in the spell itself, to prevent the requirement of Advanced Scale/dice penalties. The alien nature of the Curse is enough to deal the damage. I removed the &quot;bypass the debt&quot; Reach effect on the 4-dot spell, and added a Reach effect to the 5-dot spell to make it more exciting. I also reworked the &quot;bypass the Debt&quot; effects on the 5-dot spell to be less costly and more choice-y.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampirism</b></span><br /> The mage patterns the blood of a living subject into vampiric Vitae and draws it from the victim.<ul><li><b>Practice</b>: Patterning</li> <li><b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency</li> <li><b>Withstand</b>: Stamina (or Resistance)</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Brawl, Intimidation, Persuasion</li> <li><b>Cost</b>: 1 Mana</li> </ul>The mage patterns the blood of a living subject into vampiric Vitae and draws it from the victim.The Vitae drawn is usually in the form of blood oozing from wounds, but can be a more exotic substance, depending on the method the mage uses to &quot;feed&quot; on the subject. This spell generates one Vitae per Potency and deals 1 Lethal damage per Potency to the subject. The Vitae created is treated as if it came from the subject.<br /> <br /> The Vitae remains supernatural until the Duration of the spell expires, at which point it turns back into regular substance, unless it has been consumed. The use of this spell is an affront to the vampiric Curse, and damns the mage: the mage takes 1 resistant Lethal damage per Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may apply one suitable Condition or Tilt to the subject per level of Potency, representative of the vampiric feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death, Mind, or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The Mage may draw from ghosts (Death), goetia (mind), or spirits (Spirit).<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The Mage can convert the Vitae into tass in a form of her choosing. The tass functions both as Vitae and Mana, and if ingestible, can be consumed by Vampires. The tass created has the resonance keyword of &quot;vampirism.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Create Vitae</b></span><br /> This spell creates Vitae from nothing.<ul><li><b>Practice</b>: Making</li> <li><b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Empathy, Medicine, Occult</li> <li><b>Cost</b>: 1 Mana</li> </ul>The spell creates an amount of pure, inert Vitae equal to Potency in the subject, which may be a vampire, strix, living target, or container. If created outside of an animate subject, the mage chooses the form the Vitae takes (and must have a way to contain the resulting Vitae), and the spell is Withstood by the mage's own Stamina.<br /> <br /> Vitae created by this spell is not addictive. Furthermore, the vitae created by this spell can sustain a vampire of any Blood Potency. The Vitae created by this spell becomes normal substance after the Duration expires, unless it has been consumed. As always, the vampiric curse takes its debt: the mage suffers 1 resistant Lethal damage per point of Potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may explicitly specify the properties of the created Vitae, such as quality. With the proper knowledge, the mage can duplicate Vitae that originates from a specific person or vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may somewhat bypass the debt of the Curse. The damage inflicted to the mage is Bashing, instead of Lethal.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach and +1 Mana</b>: The mage may bypass the debt of the Curse by substituting Mana for suffering. The damage inflicted to the mage is non-Resistant.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The Mage can create the Vitae as tass in a form of her choosing. The tass functions both as Vitae and Mana, and if ingestible, can be consumed by Vampires. The tass created has the resonance keyword of &quot;vampirism.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:58:30-07:00","id":1114588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114164#post1114164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces is basically the programming arcana, Technostress is basically like creating a program that makes using the machine unintuitive enough that it's difficult to use, like a highly personalized version of Linux that doesn't use a GUI or something. The spell is basically doing that, but the mechanics are generic.<br /> <br /> Social Engineering is basically creating a bunch of falsified information and then relying on the system being large enough that no one does a thorough authentification check on that information so you can fraudulently take advantage of those merits.<br /> <br /> Both spells make perfect sense to me as being just Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But since it targets a specific person, not a system, it feels more like a curse, or something like that. If it had targetted a specific system or network of systems (e.g. like making a virus) it would've felt like just Forces. But if it targets a person ... does this person then spread the virus to any system they interact with? Could you implant a computer virus into a person with just Forces? Or make a Forces spell that acts on a specific trigger (e.g. the spell is attached to a person and will affect any electronic system the person uses, but only do that).<br /> <br /> For Social Engineering, my main concern was whether it'd work on a system the target has no access to (as would be the case with some internal security systems). Felt like maybe it needed something more, but maybe I'm reading it as more powerful than it was intended. Or maybe Mind (?) could be added for the mage to gain insight into what would be a plausible story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:07:04-07:00","id":1114591,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, that looks great. I just have a few minor questions/suggestions:<br /> <br /> When you use Vampirism, it's a bit unclear to me how you extract the Vitae and where it ends up. Do you have take the blood out yourself, or does the spell do that? And once it &quot;oozes from wounds&quot; do you have to collect it or does the spell place it in a designated vessel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may apply one suitable Condition or Tilt to the subject per level of Potency, representative of the vampiric feeding. </div> </div> </div>This should probably just be one Condition, not scaling. Coming up with and keeping track of 3+ Conditions would be a massive ballache. Personally I'd design a specific Condition (suggestion: 'Anemic', -2 to physical rolls, resolves when the damage heals) but leaving it at &quot;a suitable Condition or Tilt&quot; is also fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may explicitly specify the properties of the created Vitae, such as quality. With the proper knowledge, the mage can duplicate Vitae that originates from a specific person or vampire. </div> </div> </div>I love this, but I'd require the use of a Sympathetic Yantra. Maybe specifically some of that blood/Vitae? I feel you'd need at least some connection to perfectly copy someone's blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-11-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:19:16-07:00","id":1114596,"title":"","content":"I agree about one Condition instead of one per Potency, if only for book-keeping. I think Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines say one Condition per Potency though, although that's for main spell effects and not Reach effects.<br /> <br /> I also did consider sympathetic casting for the Reach effect on create Vitae. I suppose it could be Reach to enable the effect, and if the mage wants they can specify traits like quality (animal, human, vampiric) and whether or not the vitae is addictive... Although if the Vitae is addictive, I'm not sure who a blood bond would be formed with. Then if they want precise duplication, they need to include the target as a subject in the spell (which can either mean they're standing right next to you, or you can target them sympathetically).<br /> <br /> How about changing it to this?<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may explicitly specify the properties of the created Vitae, such as quality or addictiveness. By including another subject in the spell, the mage can even duplicate Vitae that originates from that subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:33:20-07:00","id":1114601,"title":"","content":"Looks good. I can't find the &quot;Conditions equal to Potency&quot; stuff you're talking about, but even if it's in there, yeah, I would advise against it solely because of the book-keeping issues.<br /> <br /> A point about addiction: Vitae addiction and blood bonds are two different things. You can be addicted without being blood bound, and you can be blood bound without being addicted, though for obvious reasons they often go hand-in-hand. One notable exception is elders - vampires whose Blood Potency is so high they can only drink from other Kindred are immune to Vitae addiction, but not blood bonds.<br /> <br /> You could also give the option that the Vitae causes the drinker to form a blood bond with the mage, though I think that should be a Reach effect in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:42:56-07:00","id":1114605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114601#post1114601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good. I can't find the &quot;Conditions equal to Potency&quot; stuff you're talking about, but even if it's in there, yeah, I would advise against it solely because of the book-keeping issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like I was mistaken. Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines present spells as creating one Condition, so that means my spell was out of wack regarding Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A point about addiction: Vitae addiction and blood bonds are two different things. You can be addicted without being blood bound, and you can be blood bound without being addicted, though for obvious reasons they often go hand-in-hand. One notable exception is elders - vampires whose Blood Potency is so high they can only drink from other Kindred are immune to Vitae addiction, but not blood bonds.<br /> <br /> You could also give the option that the Vitae causes the drinker to form a blood bond with the mage, though I think that should be a Reach effect in its own right. </div> </div> </div>It can be a third Reach effect, yes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T09:07:54-07:00","id":1114620,"title":"","content":"Here are the new proposed reach effects. Should probably reword the second one.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may explicitly specify the properties of the created Vitae, such as quality, addictiveness, and whether or not the Vitae can form blood bonds. Any effects dependent on another subject (such as blood bonds) require that subject to be included as a target in the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The created Vitae violates its own nature. This effect allows the mage to specify paradoxical properties, such as animal-quality Vitae of human origin, or allows the Vitae to form a blood bond with a living target (including the mage themselves).<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage may somewhat bypass the debt of the Curse. The damage inflicted to the mage is Bashing, instead of Lethal. Additionally, for one Mana, The damage inflicted to the mage is non-Resistant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T09:25:35-07:00","id":1114634,"title":"","content":"There is one spell that does grant a number of Conditions equal to Potency, but as a Reach effect it should be limited to one Condition or Tilt, and preferably a specific and predesigned one at that.<br /> Of course, it would be possible to grant several Conditions and/or Tilts but only if there are several Reach options for different ones or if the Condition or Tilt is stackable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T10:16:11-07:00","id":1114661,"title":"","content":"Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 07-11-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:05:14-07:00","id":1114817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114483#post1114483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> Really nice spells. But if you look at many of the shielding spells there already is, they do not distinguish between Bashing or Lethal. The completely protect against the arcanum. Like ghost shield doesn't distinguish between being attacked by a ghost dealing bashing, lethal or aggravated damage. It just strait up sais &quot;nope&quot;.<br /> <br /> With &quot;Till Death do Us Part&quot;, I am having trouble visualizing how the spell actually deals the damage (the idea is still very nice. Really want a spell like this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like BeyondTheGrave said, I was basing it off Alchemist's Touch. I figured that's closer to what I had in mind, since the spells that don't distinguish damage types used Clash of Wills, not a pseudo-armor effect.<br /> <br /> With Till Death Do Us Part, I imagined something like whiplashes appearing across the victims' body, since fluff-wise it's the &quot;chains&quot; of sympathy that choke them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T07:51:03-07:00","id":1115092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> <br /> \u200bJust did a refresh of Alchemist's Touch, and I think it is rather weird when compared with the other shielding spells, which with reach, can ignore all damage (looking at Spirit and Death here mainly). Also, I don't think it would be that powerful to say you degrade the damage from that specific source by Potency... Also simplere :P<br /> <br /> Hmm.. I am imagening the saying: &quot;You are killing our relationship&quot;, but instead: &quot;our relationship is killing us&quot; :P<br /> Couldn't a Reach effect be to have both &quot;ends&quot; of the connection be affected?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <br /> I changed the spells a little and merged them into one spell instead of two. I don't think it is &quot;taking over&quot; Read the Depths, it just does it in a different way now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T15:52:55-07:00","id":1115281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1115092#post1115092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a><br /> \u200bJust did a refresh of Alchemist's Touch, and I think it is rather weird when compared with the other shielding spells, which with reach, can ignore all damage (looking at Spirit and Death here mainly). Also, I don't think it would be that powerful to say you degrade the damage from that specific source by Potency... Also simplere :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Shielding via Clash is an all-or-nothing defense, so there's both pros and cons I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm.. I am imagening the saying: &quot;You are killing our relationship&quot;, but instead: &quot;our relationship is killing us&quot; :P<br /> Couldn't a Reach effect be to have both &quot;ends&quot; of the connection be affected? </div> </div> </div>Probable. Feel free to adapt the spell as needed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T14:22:43-07:00","id":1116111,"title":"","content":"Second edition added cold to Death's purview. So I decided to make some spells dealing with cold. A cryomancer's toolkit:<br /> <br /> <b>Coldproof (Death \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Become immune to any damage caused by cold. Note that this only stops cold related damage, a blizzard may not harm you but it's perception penalties would still apply, same with penalties for a slippery ice floor.<br /> <br /> Supernatural attempts to cause cold-related harm provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Body Heat Camouflage (Death \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage invites cold to surround the subject, distorting any heat they radiate. This leaves the subject invisible to any thermal imaging technologies or heat detecting abilities.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The heat is now funneled away from the subject, leaving a thermal image of the subject somewhere else in sensory range. Somebody looking around through thermal goggles might think the subject is on the far left side of the room when he is actually on the far right.<br /> <br /> <b>Freezing Slash (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Science, Weaponry<br /> <br /> Infuse a weapon with the ability to inflict biting cold to its targets.<br /> <br /> This spell increases a weapons weapon damage by Potency to a maximum of 5. But has no effect on creatures unaffected by extreme temperature lows.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: This spell may affect unarmed attacks and grapples. Without negatively harming the user with its cold.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell applies the Knocked Down Tilt.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell applies the Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryo-Phasing (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Empathy, Intimidation<br /> <br /> This spell enhances any subject in Death-attuned Twilight to radiate cold into the material world. Every material object the subject phases through will find ice forming on it, this can cause surfaces to give the Ice Tilt. This is involuntary, the subject cannot choose to not freeze something.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The subject has more control and may now choose to not freeze anything she doesn't desire to.<br /> +1 Reach: The subject may now choose to radiate even higher levels of cold than before. This can give the area around the subject the Extreme Cold Tilt for so long as he stays there.<br /> <br /> <b>Freezing-point depression (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Survival, Persuasion<br /> <br /> Raise or lower a material's freezing point, this can cause water to freeze at room temperature or remain liquid even when well below 0 degrees Celsius (32 F)<br /> <br /> By lowering a material's freezing point ice and snow can be melted. And so remove the Ice Tilt and reduce the Blizzard Tilt to an Extreme Cold and/or Heavy Winds Tilts.<br /> By raising the freezing point. Materials will freeze even add high temperatures. This can be used to create the Ice Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Bomb disposal (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Science, Firearms<br /> <br /> In the latter parts of WWII, the British, in order to disarm German bombs started soaking them in liquid nitrogen. This froze the battery within until it couldn't pass a current and so the bomb could no longer trigger.<br /> With this spell the mage can perform the same trick. Though instead of using liquid nitrogen the mage simply drops the temperature directly with magic.<br /> <br /> Despite the name this spell works on all types of batteries, not just those used in bombs.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The Germans didn't know the British were using this trick and thus developed no counter. Today's bomb makers do know however and may develop their bombs to either be immune or to go off when this trick is tried. Any mage would be wise to investigate before using this spell on any bomb.<br /> <br /> <b>Pykrete (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> During World War II, Geoffrey Pyke proposed pykrete as a candidate material for a supersized aircraft carrier for the British Royal Navy. Pykrete features unusual properties, like only being useable in cold temperatures, having a relatively slow melting rate due to its low thermal conductivity, as well as being equal in strength and toughness to concrete.<br /> <br /> With this spell the mage patterns matter into pykrete. Death is used to create it with the cold temperatures required though without a cold environment or further cooling it will heat up and start to sag.<br /> <br /> Pykrete has a Durability of 3 and a Structure of 9. *<br /> <br /> Add Matter 5: Create the material out of nothing.<br /> Add Death 5: With this the material maintains its own cold temperature.<br /> <br /> *See also 'How Strong Is Pykrete?' - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UtIwPfrvTyw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UtIwPfrvTyw</a> and 'Shooting Pykrete' - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OzhFnNY0OQI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OzhFnNY0OQI</a><br /> <br /> <b>Megacryometeor (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Firearms, Survival<br /> <br /> With this spell the mage changes the weather to cause a very large chunk of ice, a megacryometeor, to impact the current location of a chosen target. Megacryometeors are an actual real-life phenomenon. They weight between 0.5 kilograms (1.1 lb.) to several tens of kilograms.<br /> <br /> The meteor will form in several minutes, the target location is set however. The meteor is thus easily avoided by moving around. Impact by the meteor deals 10 Lethal damage but Armor and Defense both apply. When impacting objects the damage is 10 minus Durability in Structure<br /> <br /> Add Fate \u2022\u2022: The impact location is no longer set. And will instead try to impact whatever target the mage desires. A roof or other such cover might still save the target however.<br /> +2 Reach: A megacryometeor in Brazil has been recorded to weigh in at more than 50 kilograms (110 lb.) and one in Scotland was reportedly 2 meters (6 ft. 7 in.) in size. Your meteor is now in the same class as these and can now deal even greater damage. 15 instead of 10.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryonic Sleep (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> <br /> The body is brought to a state close to death while low temperatures are used to preserve organic tissue. This allows the subject to be cryonically preserved to be revived at a later date. This is not perfect however and causes one Aggravated damage per year that cannot be healed until the subject has been revived. If the entire health track is filled with Aggravated damage revival is no longer possible.<br /> <br /> Add Mind 2: The subject's mind remains active. If the subject is a mage this will allow them to keep casting spells.<br /> +2 Reach: Spend one Mana. The preservation process has been perfected, the subject no longer suffers Aggravated damage and can be revived no matter how much time has passed.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Fire (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Science, Intimidation<br /> <br /> By combining the properties of death, cold and fire; cold flames are created. These flames function like normal fire, except that they do not radiate any heat at all, this does not prevent them from burning anything suitably flammable.<br /> In addition to this these flames cannot be put out by lowering the temperature or suffocating them. Only the running out of fuel or the use of Magic can end these flames.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: For one Mana, the flames are particularly destructive they now deal Aggravated damage.<br /> +1 Reach: The flame burns the souls of those who touch it. This causes the Soul Shocked Condition.<br /> +1 Reach: When burning a souled being instead of dealing damage based on the size and 'heat' of the flame, deal damage solely based on the sins (Integrity) of the soul. A person with high Integrity could survive infernos, whereas a person with incredibly low Integrity might not even survive contact with a small candle. Also see <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta-9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Neros' Soul Fire</a>.<br /> +2 Reach: Not even the lack of fuel stops these flames as they feed on the entropy that would normally end them. Only Magic or other supernatural means can end these flames now.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00c9liv\u00e1gar's Ice<b> (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></b><br /> <br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Survival, Intimidation<br /> <br /> Rather than creating normal cold, this spell creates cold filled with the power of entropy and death. Anybody who touches the ice this cold creates will find themselves in excruciating pain and feel terribly, terribly cold.<br /> <br /> Mechanically the victim suffers the Extreme Cold Environmental Tilt, however, this Tilt doesn't disappear until the spell expires.<br /> Until then no attempts to warm or heat the subject will have any effect unless it's supernatural. In that case, it causes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Absolute Zero (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Science, Intimidation<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> <br /> The mage dissipates all heat from the subject leaving it at almost absolute zero. This spell will prove instantly lethal if used on any living creature not capable of resisting extreme cold. If cast on an area the it will kill virtually all life there as well as any life that wanders into the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Update:</b><br /> Added two Reach options to 'Ghost Fire' for dealing with Souls<br /> <b>Update2:</b><br /> Added a new Reach option to 'Body Heat Camouflage'<br /> Removed thrown weapon Reach on 'Freezing Slash'<br /> Renamed 'Freezing Point Depression' to 'Freezing Point' and added the option to heighten the freezing point rather than just lowering it.<br /> Can now apply Defense to 'Megacryometeor'<br /> Added an optional Mind effect to 'Cryonic Sleep', also added Withstand<br /> Renamed 'Demonic Ice' to '\u00c9liv\u00e1gar's Ice'<br /> Expanded the description of 'Absolute Zero', also added Withstand","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","user":"BeyondTheGrave","date":". 07-16-2017, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T16:24:07-07:00","id":1116149,"title":"","content":"I think Bomb Disposal might actually be possible at Death 2 like Control Heat.<br /> <br /> Ghost Fire seems to lack a Reach clause to burn souls as well as flesh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T02:54:22-07:00","id":1116311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116149#post1116149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Bomb Disposal might actually be possible at Death 2 like Control Heat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that would work it would have to be cast at high Potency though. The battery needs to freeze not just to the point that it struggles (like some car batteries in winter), but needs to freeze until it cannot pass a current at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghost Fire seems to lack a Reach clause to burn souls as well as flesh... </div> </div> </div>Good idea I'm adding that one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T13:49:45-07:00","id":1116542,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11914_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11914\" data-vbnamecard=\"11914\">BeyondTheGrave</a> Overall, good spells. I love thematical magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Some are very &quot;small&quot; in their effect, but not all spells have to be grand, covering many mechanics. I however miss Reach effects for some of the first ones, but Reach effects can be hard :P<br /> <br /> But here are my thoughts on some of them. I just hope its not to much. Been working on a good while to get all my thoughts out and trying not to make it sound negative:<br /> <br /> <b>Freezing Slash</b><br /> Why the &quot;Thrown Weapon&quot; Reach effect? It is not mentioned that it can't be used on a thrown weapon, and I can't see why it normally couldn't apply to a thrown weapon. <br /> I mean, you cast the spell on the weapon and then throw it and as long as the spell hasn't run its full duration, it would still be there.<br /> <br /> <b>Freezing-point Depression</b><br /> How about also being able to increasing the freezing point of things? Like water doesn't freeze at 0 degrees Celsius but at 20 degrees Celsius instead. Kinda like giving the substance the freezing/melting point of another substance.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryo-Phasing</b><br /> This actually does what the &quot;Cold Snap&quot; does, just where it is limited to ghosts only. But you can also cast Cold Snap on a ghost.<br /> But it could just be a different name for the same spell.. However, having a Reach or similar to have it affect things in Twilight could be &quot;cool&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Pykrete</b><br /> I would say this is a dot 5 spell since you are creating something out of nothing (making chipped wood and water). In 2nd edition, there is no &quot;You can do this pratice at a lower dot level&quot; anymore. <br /> <br /> But did abit of search on it, and it sounds like what it basically does is make a substance that is as hard as concrete.<br /> <br /> <b>Megacryometeor</b><br /> Seems very odd and gimmicky, not following how allot of the other spells work. The closest I could find is the &quot;Adverse Weather&quot; Force spell.<br /> \u2022 Not sure about the Pratice since it sounds allot like a Making effect (you are making it from nothing).<br /> \u2022 How many are &quot;several&quot; minutes?<br /> \u2022 Shouldn't the targets Defense count since the projectile isn't moving faster than a bullet?<br /> \u2022 Why does it deal 10 lethal damage? Seems like allot.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryonic Sleep</b><br /> There should be a Withstand since many will surely try to resist this.. Especially in combat :P<br /> You could add a &quot;Add Mind \u2022\u2022&quot;, where the subject's mind is still active for the duration of the spell<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Fire</b><br /> This should &quot;<i>kinda</i>&quot; be a dot 3 effect. Granting the properties of something to another is a Weaving effect. But because of the Reach effect with Aggravated damage, it should be dot 4 (I believe you can only deal Aggravated at dot 4?)<br /> The Soul Shock Reach is a really nice idea for such a spell. Very neat<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Ice</b><br /> I feel like it should be called something else since Death doesn't really cover Demons.. Stygian Ice? Drawing fourth from the deepest part of the river Styx.<br /> Also, how about a Reach effect to allow the target to get rid of the effect by indulging in their Virtue/Vice? Or worsen/extend its effect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Absolute Zero</b><br /> What does this mechanically do? It kinda sounds like it works like the &quot;Salt the Earth&quot; life spell. <br /> Not sure why I feel like saying it, but remember; the subject of a spell can be anything really. So an area, a person.. Really depends on how you wish to bring this great curse down upon the masses. You could put it on a rock and it could be that VERY bad luck rock, freezing those whom touch it almost instantly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T06:43:39-07:00","id":1116827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116542#post1116542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11914_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11914\" data-vbnamecard=\"11914\">BeyondTheGrave</a> Overall, good spells. I love thematical magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Some are very &quot;small&quot; in their effect, but not all spells have to be grand, covering many mechanics. I however miss Reach effects for some of the first ones, but Reach effects can be hard :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Reach effects are difficult, though I think I know one to add to 'Body Heat Camouflage'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But here are my thoughts on some of them. I just hope its not to much. Been working on a good while to get all my thoughts out and trying not to make it sound negative: </div> </div> </div>Don't worry I love reading people's thoughts on these things. I think it helps improve the spells a lot too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Freezing Slash</b><br /> Why the &quot;Thrown Weapon&quot; Reach effect? It is not mentioned that it can't be used on a thrown weapon, and I can't see why it normally couldn't apply to a thrown weapon.<br /> I mean, you cast the spell on the weapon and then throw it and as long as the spell hasn't run its full duration, it would still be there. </div> </div> </div>Looking at it again the throwing weapon thing indeed doesn't make much sense. I based this spell on Forces' Kinetic Blow, but it doesn't make much sense there either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Freezing-point Depression</b><br /> How about also being able to increasing the freezing point of things? Like water doesn't freeze at 0 degrees Celsius but at 20 degrees Celsius instead. Kinda like giving the substance the freezing/melting point of another substance. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that does give me an idea. If lowering the freezing point can remove the Ice Tilt, then raising should be able to cause it. I think I'll add than in.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if it's possible to do anything with boiling and melting points. But that is perhaps for another spell write-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cryo-Phasing</b><br /> This actually does what the &quot;Cold Snap&quot; does, just where it is limited to ghosts only. But you can also cast Cold Snap on a ghost.<br /> But it could just be a different name for the same spell.. However, having a Reach or similar to have it affect things in Twilight could be &quot;cool&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I liked the idea of ghosts freezing an area and leaving ice wherever they pass. This spell is pretty much just 'Cold Snap' but allows you to send a ghost out to do the freezing for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pykrete</b><br /> I would say this is a dot 5 spell since you are creating something out of nothing (making chipped wood and water). In 2nd edition, there is no &quot;You can do this pratice at a lower dot level&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> But did abit of search on it, and it sounds like what it basically does is make a substance that is as hard as concrete. </div> </div> </div>I wrote this spell with the assumption that existing matter would be Patterned into pykrete. So it's not creating out of nothing.<br /> <br /> Also, I suppose if the mage already has water and wood pulp lying around the could probably do this spell as Matter 3. But that all seemed a bit too lengthy to put into the description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Megacryometeor</b><br /> Seems very odd and gimmicky, not following how allot of the other spells work. The closest I could find is the &quot;Adverse Weather&quot; Force spell. </div> </div> </div>This spell is supposed to be a stronger version of 'Call Lightning'. Just like that spell you were supposed to change the weather to create a single attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Not sure about the Pratice since it sounds allot like a Making effect (you are making it from nothing). </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't consider this spell Making. Creating rain or hail with 'Control Weather' isn't Making either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 How many are &quot;several&quot; minutes? </div> </div> </div>The description for 'several minutes' is also used in 'Control Weather'. I'm not sure how long it's supposed to be. Keep it at maybe 5 to 10? minutes for now, huge hailstones take time to create.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Shouldn't the targets Defense count since the projectile isn't moving faster than a bullet? </div> </div> </div>Yes, it should. Adding that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Why does it deal 10 lethal damage? Seems like allot. </div> </div> </div>I had no idea how much damage a big ice rock falling from the sky should be doing. So I used the falling damage rules, people falling at terminal velocity take 10 Lethal.<br /> It's not a perfect fit but I couldn't think of any better ways to model this. If anybody has any ideas for this I would love to hear them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cryonic Sleep</b><br /> There should be a Withstand since many will surely try to resist this.. Especially in combat :P<br /> You could add a &quot;Add Mind \u2022\u2022&quot;, where the subject's mind is still active for the duration of the spell </div> </div> </div>So, we now have a body that is cryonically preserved (and doesn't age). Combined with a method to remain active (Mind Magic, 'Telepathy', 'Psychic Projection').<br /> <br /> Wow, I think we just invented a new form of Lichdom XD. <br /> <br /> Also I'll add Withstand, probably Stamina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ghost Fire</b><br /> This should &quot;<i>kinda</i>&quot; be a dot 3 effect. Granting the properties of something to another is a Weaving effect. But because of the Reach effect with Aggravated damage, it should be dot 4 (I believe you can only deal Aggravated at dot 4?)<br /> The Soul Shock Reach is a really nice idea for such a spell. Very neat </div> </div> </div>Yes, Aggravated is a dot 4 effect. Also the +2 Reach effect patterns entropy into flames so that's 4 dots too. Remove those two effects and the spell should be Forces 3 + Death 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Demonic Ice</b><br /> I feel like it should be called something else since Death doesn't really cover Demons.. Stygian Ice? Drawing fourth from the deepest part of the river Styx.<br /> Also, how about a Reach effect to allow the target to get rid of the effect by indulging in their Virtue/Vice? Or worsen/extend its effect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>The river Styx, while connected to the underworld, is never actually descripted as cold. None of the other rivers in Greek mythology are descripted as cold or frozen over either.<br /> <br /> There is a river in Norse mythology that is descripted as cold and frozen that leads to Niflheim, a realm of cold and ice that is descripted as a potential afterlife. The river is called \u00c9liv\u00e1gar (Ice-waves). I think I'll rename the spell '\u00c9liv\u00e1gar's Ice'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Absolute Zero</b><br /> What does this mechanically do? It kinda sounds like it works like the &quot;Salt the Earth&quot; life spell.<br /> Not sure why I feel like saying it, but remember; the subject of a spell can be anything really. So an area, a person.. Really depends on how you wish to bring this great curse down upon the masses. You could put it on a rock and it could be that VERY bad luck rock, freezing those whom touch it almost instantly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically it's meant to be an insta-kill spell. Like 'Eradicate Energy' or a Life Unmaking spell. I should probably add a Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll add a description of the effects when cast upon an area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:43:46-07:00","id":1117413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at it again the throwing weapon thing indeed doesn't make much sense. I based this spell on Forces' Kinetic Blow, but it doesn't make much sense there either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looked at Kinetic Blow as well.. Forgot it said unarmed only for some weird reason.. Can't see why it can't work with a weapon as well o.O ??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that does give me an idea. If lowering the freezing point can remove the Ice Tilt, then raising should be able to cause it. I think I'll add than in.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder if it's possible to do anything with boiling and melting points. But that is perhaps for another spell write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't it be within the same spell? Many spells that increase or decrease their Arcanum's aspects are usually in the same spell.<br /> Mmmh.. Just imagine reversing the boiling and freezing point of something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the idea of ghosts freezing an area and leaving ice wherever they pass. This spell is pretty much just 'Cold Snap' but allows you to send a ghost out to do the freezing for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say you can cast Cold Snap on ghosts since spells seems not to be picky about what you cast it on, as long as it is something you can hit with touch, sensory or scrying range.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote this spell with the assumption that existing matter would be Patterned into pykrete. So it's not creating out of nothing.<br /> <br /> Also, I suppose if the mage already has water and wood pulp lying around the could probably do this spell as Matter 3. But that all seemed a bit too lengthy to put into the description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaah. Okay.. Hmm.. Well, I guess you could still kinda achieve it without having the materials. You could just give the material the properties of wood bulp and freeze it... Seems like a long way to get pukrete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spell is supposed to be a stronger version of 'Call Lightning'. Just like that spell you were supposed to change the weather to create a single attack</div> </div> </div> </div>Aah, so the weather is a requirement. Well, then I don't think it should take minutes to form like with lightning (nevermind logic. Unless you really want it to deal lots of damage. Then for balance..). But you could have it inflict Lethal damage equal to the spell's Potency (thematically, the more potency the bigger the frozen ball of death is). Maybe add an extra bonus..<br /> <br /> And about the lethal damage; when it comes down to termal velocity, it should be lower (smaller object = lower max energy), and the damage in the book is based on a human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we now have a body that is cryonically preserved (and doesn't age). Combined with a method to remain active (Mind Magic, 'Telepathy', 'Psychic Projection').<br /> <br /> Wow, I think we just invented a new form of Lichdom XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>.. Icedom? Froztdom.... Uuuuh.. Add some Forces with levitation and you have a Popsicle Mage that can actually move around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a river in Norse mythology that is descripted as cold and frozen that leads to Niflheim, a realm of cold and ice that is descripted as a potential afterlife. The river is called \u00c9liv\u00e1gar (Ice-waves). I think I'll rename the spell '\u00c9liv\u00e1gar's Ice'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't it be the same river? All rivers lead to the realm of the dead... Kinda... Allot of cultures have that &quot;put the dead into the river&quot; tradition, so there must be some kind of connection.<br /> But now the spell sounds much more fitting for a mage that can manipulate death <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BeyondTheGrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1116827#post1116827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically it's meant to be an insta-kill spell. Like 'Eradicate Energy' or a Life Unmaking spell. I should probably add a Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll add a description of the effects when cast upon an area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did a read of Eradicate Energy, and it sais that it is instantly fatal, just like your spell... So I guess its okay if we use the current spells as an example.. If you can exceed the target's Stamina which normally will demand a Potency of 3 - 6 O_O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:13:54-07:00","id":1117568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1117413#post1117413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say you can cast Cold Snap on ghosts since spells seems not to be picky about what you cast it on, as long as it is something you can hit with touch, sensory or scrying range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casting Cold Snap on a ghost would inflict the Ice Tilt on the ghost. The above spell sounds like it would bestow the ability to inflict the Ice Tilt via touch on the ghost, instead of freezing the ghost itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:57:17-07:00","id":1118647,"title":"","content":"Not much experience making spells but we were talking about casting spells for other people which were not meant to let them use themselves. I thought a cool idea would maybe be a way to catch a spell someone when they try to cast on you and recast it later on someone else. Possible create an imbued item with the spell so you can store it there to use as you will. I imagine It would need to have at least time 2 and be some variation of the Hang Spell Attainment. Im thinking make it a prime spell so it would work on all arcana but am not sure what practice I would need. My only real problem with it so far is that would it still count as an active spell cast by another mage once you catch it? Would they be able to relinquish it still? It could work well for giving an ally access to spells they cant cast themselves though.<br /> <br /> How about....<br /> <br /> Bind Another\u2019s Imago (Time 2 + Prime 3)<br /> Practice: ?<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Survival, Intimidation<br /> Any Apprentice of Time can hold their own Spells. Mages proficient in Prime as well can \u2018catch\u2019 another's spell as it has been cast and hold it to release at another target.<br /> System:<br /> The mage casts the spell and the next spell cast on them provokes a clash of wills. If won the caster has successfully hung another mages spell and may pick a new target to release it on. No other spell factors may be altered. The spell still counts towards the total limit of spells the original caster can have active even if they have another spell hung. The original caster may attempt to dispel their imago but it provokes another clash of wills. The original caster is always aware of their spells location.<br /> Add Reach<br /> +1 Reach and Space 2<br /> The caster may attempt to catch spell cast on targets other then themselves<br /> +2 Reach and 1 Mana<br /> The catcher may hold the spell on their own pattern, counting as their active spell as opposed to the original casters. The Original caster still possesses a sympathetic connection to the spell for purposes of space magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13691,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","user":"Margul","date":". 07-20-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:56:39-07:00","id":1118735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=933840#post933840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple way to make basic potion brewing work.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Brew Potion</u> (Matter ***)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Magical potions and unguents are widely recognized as part of the wizard\u2019s trade. This spell prepares a material compound to hold a supernal charge. A mage may then cast another spell into the potion, specifically shaping their Imago and spending a point of Mana. The potion may contain up to its Potency in spells, but using the compound triggers all of them. While within the potion, a spell counts against the caster\u2019s spell control, but its Duration is held.<br /> <br /> Potions come with certain limitations. Whomever imbibes the potion becomes the subject of its spells, although a cream or oil might be spread or splattered. If <i>Brew Potion</i>\u2019s Duration runs out while it still contains spells, the held spells are lost and the potion visibly spoils.<br /> <br /> Usually this spell is cast on a liquid that resonates with the spell effect, but it could also be cast on a piece of fruit to be eaten, a powder to be inhaled, a breakable object to be tossed like a grenade, etc. \u201cIngredients\u201d act as Sacrament Yantras.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may add a Key to the activation of the potion. Perhaps it will only work once a certain reagent is mixed in, or it only has an effect on a certain person.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The potion\u2019s ingredients lose any effect they may have had on an imbiber; so an Acceleration potion of quicksilver won\u2019t inflict mercury poisoning.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The potion may contain multiple doses. If the same spell is cast into it multiple times, each adds an additional use to the potion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it would need some Prime for sure, as it messes with the basics of spellcasting and how magic works. Just Matter doesn't allow you to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-20-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:06:33-07:00","id":1118739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1118735#post1118735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like it would need some Prime for sure, as it messes with the basics of spellcasting and how magic works. Just Matter doesn't allow you to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. Time and Fate both have spells that alter the basics of spellcasting, this doesn't seem any more complex than Hung Spell. Spellcasting is a core part of the Mage template, I think there's some room for other Arcana to interact with it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:19:09-07:00","id":1118747,"title":"","content":"Hung Spell is applying a piece of Time onto a spell. It makes sense that Hung Spell can postpone the effects of the spell. It doesn't make sense that Matter can store a spell in a potion because Matter isn't about storing stuff. Rather, this seems to be something akin to Imbue Item, a Prime Attainment. I can see a Prime/Matter Legacy focused around brewing potions, though.<br /> <br /> On a related note I think it's a boring concept in Mage. Not because the concept itself is boring but because there's no reason it has to be potions rather than snackbars or pills. There's nothing inherent in the ingredients chosen to make the potion that makes it work. It's a spell cast on the potion that makes it magical, making the potion itself incidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T07:27:36-07:00","id":1118947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1118739#post1118739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about that. Time and Fate both have spells that alter the basics of spellcasting, this doesn't seem any more complex than Hung Spell. Spellcasting is a core part of the Mage template, I think there's some room for other Arcana to interact with it directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what Tessie said. Time can adjust the timing of a spell, Space can adjust the targeting properties, but there is nothing in your average spell that has anything to do with matter.<br /> <br /> Fate is the arcanum that can make a spell matter, so Matter doesn't even have that!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:57:42-07:00","id":1119163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1114164#post1114164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces is basically the programming arcana, Technostress is basically like creating a program that makes using the machine unintuitive enough that it's difficult to use, like a highly personalized version of Linux that doesn't use a GUI or something. The spell is basically doing that, but the mechanics are generic.<br /> <br /> Social Engineering is basically creating a bunch of falsified information and then relying on the system being large enough that no one does a thorough authentification check on that information so you can fraudulently take advantage of those merits.<br /> <br /> Both spells make perfect sense to me as being just Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I did not get that impression at all from the Forces entry in the book. It seemed like it was more about gross control over lots of energy, not fine detailed control over small amounts of energy. <br /> <br /> Though, many of the arcana do seem like the effects are lacking in spells that allow fine control over their purview. If I wanted to use an effect to do something that needed a lot of precision or specialized knowledge, would that be best modeled as a Reach Effect, a specific level of Potency, an additional Attribute+Skill roll, an Exceptional Success result, or could it be any/all of these depending on the specifcs of the spell?<br /> <br /> For example, the Matter 3 effect Alter Conductivity allows the caster to change how easily electricity flows through something. However, if a mage wanted to use the spell to turn a brick into a complex microprocessor, by selectively altering the conductivity of all the molecules in said brick, it feels like that should require dots in Computers or Craft (Electrical Engineering) or something rather than just Reaching for it. But I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:13:45-07:00","id":1119170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119163#post1119163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I did not get that impression at all from the Forces entry in the book. It seemed like it was more about gross control over lots of energy, not fine detailed control over small amounts of energy.<br /> <br /> Though, many of the arcana do seem like the effects are lacking in spells that allow fine control over their purview. If I wanted to use an effect to do something that needed a lot of precision or specialized knowledge, would that be best modeled as a Reach Effect, a specific level of Potency, an additional Attribute+Skill roll, an Exceptional Success result, or could it be any/all of these depending on the specifcs of the spell?<br /> <br /> For example, the Matter 3 effect Alter Conductivity allows the caster to change how easily electricity flows through something. However, if a mage wanted to use the spell to turn a brick into a complex microprocessor, by selectively altering the conductivity of all the molecules in said brick, it feels like that should require dots in Computers or Craft (Electrical Engineering) or something rather than just Reaching for it. But I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's a hold-over attitude from 1e which was more explicit about the fact that Forces could control the language by which computers function. It still basically holds true though since a computer relies on electrical impulses in order to faithfully follow it's programming. There's definitely some overlap with Matter though, much like how corpses might have some overlap between Matter and Death depending on the spell you may want to cast.<br /> <br /> A spell specifically to craft or modify programming via a burst of electrical impulses wouldn't require a Reach, but giving that program specialized or empowered ability to execute its function would. In other words, a spell to modify a program is not just a Reach tacked onto Influence Electricity, it's a completely different spell. Theoretically, you could create a microprocessor using just Alter Conductivity and that it would be reasonable to append a Reach cost to, but it would be simpler to create a spell whose purpose is to turn an object into a microprocessor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:27:59-07:00","id":1119178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119163#post1119163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the Matter 3 effect Alter Conductivity allows the caster to change how easily electricity flows through something. However, if a mage wanted to use the spell to turn a brick into a complex microprocessor, by selectively altering the conductivity of all the molecules in said brick, it feels like that should require dots in Computers or Craft (Electrical Engineering) or something rather than just Reaching for it. But I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In most cases the mage doesn't need to know how something works in order to do it with magic. The spell fills in the blanks for you. It's only when a spell allows you to craft stuff that you need to make Crafts rolls, but if the spell directly creates something you wouldn't need any additional rolls.<br /> <br /> Also, no spell specific effects comes from or requires an Exceptional Success on spellcasting. The possible bonuses are just positive side effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:44:58-07:00","id":1119182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119170#post1119170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, it's a hold-over attitude from 1e which was more explicit about the fact that Forces could control the language by which computers function. It still basically holds true though since a computer relies on electrical impulses in order to faithfully follow it's programming. There's definitely some overlap with Matter though, much like how corpses might have some overlap between Matter and Death depending on the spell you may want to cast.<br /> <br /> A spell specifically to craft or modify programming via a burst of electrical impulses wouldn't require a Reach, but giving that program specialized or empowered ability to execute its function would. In other words, a spell to modify a program is not just a Reach tacked onto Influence Electricity, it's a completely different spell. Theoretically, you could create a microprocessor using just Alter Conductivity and that it would be reasonable to append a Reach cost to, but it would be simpler to create a spell whose purpose is to turn an object into a microprocessor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, sure. But Alter Conductivity is the closest canon effect in the book, so it seems reasonable to use it as a benchmark for what Matter rating you need to have to be able to perform the hypothetical Turn Brick into a Microprocessor spell. Such a spell presumably turns a brick (or whatever you have handy) into the equivalent of a computer with availability equal to the spell's Potency, or, if the ST preferred to use the extended craft rules, maybe it just counts as Potency successes on a roll to build a computer. Something like that. <br /> <br /> But what other requirements might such a spell have? None? A cap on Potency based on your dots in Computer? A required Int+Computer roll? Something else?<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Could a mage create a computer entirely out of electricity using Forces? What rating would that have? I'd think Forces 3 minimum, but Control Electricity is Forces 2, so I could see an argument for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T05:08:31-07:00","id":1119230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119182#post1119182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Could a mage create a computer entirely out of electricity using Forces? What rating would that have? I'd think Forces 3 minimum, but Control Electricity is Forces 2, so I could see an argument for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think it's possible, since a computer is essentially just electricity moving in complicated ways, but what Practice it falls under depends on what you mean by &quot;entirely out of electricity&quot;. If you have blank circuit boards to direct the electricity through it's arguably a Ruling spell, but probably with some Reach for the complexity. In the case of just pulling a computer out of a wall socket though it is definitely at least Weaving.<br /> <br /> Note that unless you have a keyboard and a screen at hand to &quot;plug into&quot; the electricity-computer, you're going to need additional spells to give it commands and receive its output. It would take a Forces 4 Patterning spell to make it display as an actual screen, but reading information straight from a computer is arguably just Forces 1 Knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:19:44-07:00","id":1119250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119182#post1119182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes, sure. But Alter Conductivity is the closest canon effect in the book</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderful Machine is actually closer imo since you could have a brick that is also a computer. Patterning would be the best Practice for brick to computer however since that would encompass transubstantiation and a finer level of control over the elements to configure them into a computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T09:19:37-07:00","id":1119265,"title":"","content":"A potentially useful spell I just thought of:<br /> <br /> <b>House Whisperer (Space</b> <b>\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Streetwise, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage tunes into a location to learn its secrets. With an instant action, the mage can ask a number of the following questions equal to the spell's Potency:<ul><li>What is the purpose of this location?</li> <li>How is the location demarcated?</li> <li>Where are the entrances and exits?</li> <li>What is the location's dot rating in Safe Place/Sanctum/Haven/etc?</li> <li>What is the nature of the location's inhabitants?</li> <li>Are there any Irises within the location?</li> <li>What is one of the location's flaws?</li> </ul><b>+1 Reach:</b> When asking about Irises, the mage also learns the location of one Iris (if there are any) and a general idea of where it leads.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death </b><b>\u2022:</b> The mage can ask if there are any anchors in the location, or if the location itself is an anchor.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Forces </b><b>\u2022:</b> The mage can ask for the location for a source of energy within the location, or if the location is under the effects of an Extreme Environment.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Spirit </b><b>\u2022:</b> The mage can ask for one of the location's Resonant Conditions, or if the space is a Locus.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Time </b><b>\u2022:</b> The mage can ask how the location has changed since a given time or event. Temporal Sympathy applies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T14:58:55-07:00","id":1119339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119250#post1119250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wonderful Machine is actually closer imo since you could have a brick that is also a computer. Patterning would be the best Practice for brick to computer however since that would encompass transubstantiation and a finer level of control over the elements to configure them into a computer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderful Machine says it moves properties from a mechanical machine to another mechanical machine.<br /> <br /> A computer is an electronical machine, not a mechanical one. A brick is not at all a machine.<br /> <br /> Any electronics cannot be affected by Wonderful Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T19:17:35-07:00","id":1119382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119339#post1119339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wonderful Machine says it moves properties from a mechanical machine to another mechanical machine.<br /> <br /> A computer is an electronical machine, not a mechanical one. A brick is not at all a machine.<br /> <br /> Any electronics cannot be affected by Wonderful Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still closer and there's no reason you couldn't use Matter to transpose electrical device components.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T01:19:46-07:00","id":1119434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1119382#post1119382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still closer and there's no reason you couldn't use Matter to transpose electrical device components.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the entire components you could move and put in something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:54:55-07:00","id":1120714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1040484#post1040484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Faces of Death</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Weaving </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand: Stamina </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A64D79\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Stealth, Subterfuge </span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage may physically alter the subject corpse\u2019s body in any way, within the confines of species and age. Rather than an illusion as with \u201cCorpse Mask,\u201d the transformation caused by this spell is entirely physical \u2014 subjects can be granted radically altered weight and fitness, and the apparent source of injuries, and nature of damage, may be altered, although they cannot be healed, and missing limbs cannot be regenerated. </span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The target may be one of the \u2018living\u2019 dead instead of a simple corpse - a Revenant or Vampire, or other undead being. The mage may rearrange up to the spell\u2019s Potency in Physical Attribute dots, for example moving a dot of Strength to Stamina, but cannot change the total number of dots, bring any to 0, or raise them above the subject\u2019s limit. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't really see why the primary factor would be Duration, because this seems as if it would be Lasting anyway. It's pretty much like sculpting matter with State Change+Shaping combo, and the changes done there don't snap back into place either. Once you've changed the physical aspects of the corpse, you'd need more energy to actually change it a second time back to the &quot;old&quot; form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:52:10-07:00","id":1120725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1120714#post1120714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't really see why the primary factor would be Duration, because this seems as if it would be Lasting anyway. It's pretty much like sculpting matter with State Change+Shaping combo, and the changes done there don't snap back into place either. Once you've changed the physical aspects of the corpse, you'd need more energy to actually change it a second time back to the &quot;old&quot; form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The changes wouldn't be Lasting for the same reason that they aren't when you use Many Faces which this spell is obviously modeled on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:06:04-07:00","id":1120735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1120725#post1120725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The changes wouldn't be Lasting for the same reason that they aren't when you use Many Faces which this spell is obviously modeled on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I find the guidelines concerning Lasting or not incredibly confusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T04:46:15-07:00","id":1120746,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said. A massive chunk of the spells I put together are just vanilla spells reflavored for to use a different Arcana or affect a different class of subject, or both. This is 'Many Faces, but for vampires/dead things.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:14:01-07:00","id":1120782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1120735#post1120735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I find the guidelines concerning Lasting or not incredibly confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lasting typically means those changes which are side effects of a spell that can be maintained without further magic. There are some exceptions, Scribe Grimoire for instance, but otherwise that's how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:00:45-07:00","id":1120874,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I feel I have a better idea about what is an isn't Lasting now. So for a Life Healing spell that boosts the natural recovery speed of the target, since the healing is a &quot;side effect&quot; of the increased recovery speed, it is Lasting, but the improved recovery speed itself is tied to the duration of the spell, and thus will disappear when the spell's duration is up. That's correct?<br /> <br /> By the way, could a Death Shielding spell be made that gives protection against dispellation of spells? Since Shielding protects against things under the purview of the Arcanum, and &quot;ending&quot; is under Death's purview, so you could Shield your spells against being ended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-26-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:41:30-07:00","id":1124951,"title":"","content":"This is just a random idea, but it popped out at me and so I felt like I'd share it. Some sort of Life 2 spell that fakes emotional reactions. When someone is embarassed, they blush. When they're angry, they might flush, when they're lying, there are special and specific cues that many people have that can be very, very hard to hide. If a Mage could generate these 'tells' they could look truthful when they were lying, or seem angry when they are cooly calculating the potential advantage of faked anger, or so on and so forth. I'm not sure what the mechanical advantage would be. 9-again on Subterfuge? Not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:59:51-07:00","id":1125369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1124951#post1124951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is just a random idea, but it popped out at me and so I felt like I'd share it. Some sort of Life 2 spell that fakes emotional reactions. When someone is embarassed, they blush. When they're angry, they might flush, when they're lying, there are special and specific cues that many people have that can be very, very hard to hide. If a Mage could generate these 'tells' they could look truthful when they were lying, or seem angry when they are cooly calculating the potential advantage of faked anger, or so on and so forth. I'm not sure what the mechanical advantage would be. 9-again on Subterfuge? Not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be a Veiling effect, Alter Mental Pattern is probably a close enough equivalent you could just copy it directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:47:09-07:00","id":1128923,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, here's an interesting question... making a serious quantum computer, Matter, Forces, or both? My gut says Matter 4 could probably do it, but might need Forces 3 to make sure it ran properly... because honestly, I can't see you running Windows on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:54:07-07:00","id":1128969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1128923#post1128923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm, here's an interesting question... making a serious quantum computer, Matter, Forces, or both? My gut says Matter 4 could probably do it, but might need Forces 3 to make sure it ran properly... because honestly, I can't see you running Windows on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am remembering correctly one of the big deals about quantum computing is quantum entanglement and that would be space 3 co-location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:32:07-07:00","id":1128984,"title":"","content":"Actually, thinking about it, if you had a processor/motherboard using brontium instead of copper or gold, you could probably make a far faster computer since it's a superconductor and won't be producing waste heat. Now I'm just wondering about the best ways for a Matter mage to go about that.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: talking to a friend, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar728_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"728\" data-vbnamecard=\"728\">CrownedSun</a> Fate could be useful in that instead of Space. I hadn't thought about that, but it makes perfect sense. Time too, thinking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 08-14-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T17:49:29-07:00","id":1129049,"title":"","content":"I don't want to be a stick in the mud but what would a quantum computer give a mage that magic could not?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T18:26:04-07:00","id":1129067,"title":"","content":"A) The satisfaction of making it using magic and B) a computer like that could be used by multiple people. Magically made tools can help people (including mages) to accomplish things they might not be capable of or assist in things they are. Not everyone in a cabal might have Forces, but they might have Computer. And you could use such a computer as private &quot;cloud computing&quot; even from a cell phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T07:49:32-07:00","id":1129225,"title":"","content":"Ex Nihilo has a clause that explicitly forbids things that do not &quot;operate according to known physical principles&quot;, which I'd presume applies to other applications of Matter. It's a little unclear to me what the in-universe justification for that is, but since a mage doesn't have to know anything about cell phones except that cell phones exist to make one it's not simply a matter of learning how a quantum computer would work, were one to exist.<br /> <br /> You could definitely create a magical better-than-quantum computer with some additional Arcana, though. Which ones depend on what you want to be using it for. Fate for complicated probability models, Time for crunching huge amounts of numbers very quickly, Life for advanced biological simulations, Space for calculating relativistic distortions etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T09:53:45-07:00","id":1129274,"title":"","content":"Well, note, the &quot;heavy lifting&quot; Arcana of this would be Fate. On a discussion of the Arcana needed to make one, we came up with a set of ones required with an optional one. Namely Fate 5 (though I suspect you could do the same with Space, though that'd be a more classical one), Matter 4, (optional) Time 4, and Forces 1 or 2. This is sort of an end-game project, but the sort of thing I can see a Mage doing for the very sort of modeling, number crunching, and encryption.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the record, thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13628_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13628\" data-vbnamecard=\"13628\">Terrorforge</a>, this is actually helping a lot to solidify ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T04:41:04-07:00","id":1130769,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Removed (for now).</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T01:44:09-07:00","id":1131653,"title":"","content":"So, this a list of spells that don't really have much of a unifying theme. More of a bag tricks really.<br /> <br /> <b>Protect the Balance (Spirit \u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Science, Animal Ken<br /> <br /> With this spell the user can see the interaction between flesh and shadow and thereby the natural order of things, or at least what is natural for a given locale, and anything that would disturb it.<br /> <br /> This allows the subject to see the Resonance of an area, and so figure out what spirits would be attracted to it.<br /> <br /> The subject can now tell which Choirs are the most Dominant in the area<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The subject\u2019s ability to sense Resonance is enhanced. The subject can now detect which Descants are the most Dominant in the area<br /> +1 Reach: The subject\u2019s senses are now particularly attuned to the Resonance of human sin. This allows the subject to know if any Immundi inhabit the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult Leader (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Persuasion, Intimidation<br /> <br /> This spell causes the very air around the subject to be filled with what sparse mystical and magical potential is still present in the Fallen World, a reflection of the Aether itself.<br /> As a result people feel as thought they are in the presence of some sort of great authority, some might even mistakenly believe the subject is an angel or some other form of divine agent.<br /> <br /> In Social Maneuvering this removes Doors equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Secret Identity (Space \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> This spell enhances the Shadow Name Merit's ability to hide one's mundane identity. Any investigation to uncover the subject's mundane identity that uses evidence created while in their Shadow persona automatically fails.<br /> <br /> Any attempt to use any Sympathy or Temporal Sympathy created while the subject is in their Shadow persona to identify their mundane persona provokes a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> This spell has no effect on those that already know that both the subject's Shadow and mundane persona are one person.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Rather than a Clash of Wills any Sympathy or Temporal Sympathy created in the subject's Shadow persona cannot be used at all while in their mundane persona.<br /> Any attempt to do so will only tell the scrying mage that the target 'does not exist'.<br /> +1 Reach: The spell can now affect any mage with a Shadow name regardless of whether they have the Shadow Name Merit or not.<br /> +2 Reach: The spell can now affect anybody with the Alternate Identity Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Strongman (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Athletics, Brawl<br /> <br /> The mage may improve the strength of the kinetic forces used by the subject's body. This improves the subject\u2019s Strength by Potency. This increase affects any Advantages or other traits derived from the Attribute\u2019s level. The effects are subtle, though observers can detect subtle hints of changes to balance or strength of the body. Strength cannot be raised above the subject\u2019s maximum (5 for normal human beings).<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: By spending a point of Mana, the mage may raise Strength above the maximum rating for the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Power Glows (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Occult, Expression<br /> <br /> Mana is normally invisible and intangible. Under Mage Sight it may appear as a fiery, fluid energy of pure white or a prismatic color. With this spell the mage condenses the Mana in his pattern into a more concentrated form.<br /> The benefit of this is that the mage's pattern can contain more of this condensed Mana than regular Mana, increasing the mage's Mana capacity by Potency.<br /> <br /> However, the drawback to this is that the condensed Mana is visible to all and causes the mage's body to emit a faint light. At high Potency the mage's veins may even start to glow up and light may emit from the eyes and throat.<br /> <br /> If the spell expires, any Mana beyond the mage's capacity is lost.<br /> <br /> Add Any Other Arcanum \u2022: By using the relevant Arcanum/Arcana the mage may now condense the mystical energy (Essence, Vitae, etc) of other supernatural entities as well.<br /> This will carry the same drawback of making that energy visible in some way for all to see however.<br /> <br /> <b>Anima (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Survival, Empathy, Expression<br /> <br /> There is a symbiotic relationship between the Shadow and Material world, for example, if there is a Barren in the Shadow than on the physical side plants will wither and people will feel passionless and apathetic.<br /> With this spell the mage improves the beneficial effects of this relationship for the subject. Plants and animals will have improved health and people will feel more alive and creative.<br /> <br /> If the subject is human, and already has one dot in Expression, then increase Expression by Potency.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: By spending a point of Mana, the mage may raise Expression above the maximum rating for the subject.<br /> +1 Reach: If the other side of the Gauntlet is a Barren then this spell will negate any penalties to spiritual powers that it would normally generate for the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Spiritual Symbiosis (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Intimidation, Persuasion<br /> Withstand: Rank<br /> <br /> The mage must cast this spell on a Claimed subject. This spell causes the spirit's and host\u2019s mind to clash against one another rather than merge as per normal, the result is that one will dominate.<br /> <br /> All the normal effects of the Claimed Condition (Changed appearance, can use Influences not Numina, Dread Powers, susceptible to Ban and Bane, etc) still apply.<br /> <br /> The spirit may now try to take complete control over the merged subject.<br /> To resist, the subject has to roll Resolve + Composure penalized by the amount of Attribute dots the Claimed Condition has granted.<br /> If the roll fails the spirit takes control for the rest of the scene but cannot choose to end the Claimed Condition if the spell is still in effect.<br /> If the roll succeeds the subject remains in control for at least one scene and is no longer affected by the Urged Condition, though if the user tries to ignore the spirit's Ban that provokes another roll immediately.<br /> <br /> A particularly unwilling and uncowed spirit may force a roll every single scene, whereas a weaker and more intimidated spirit may only force a roll once a day or less.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The spirit may no longer try to take control over the subject. But only so long as the amount of distributed Attribute Dots does not surpass Potency. Ignoring the Spirit's Ban still provokes a roll however.<br /> +1 Reach: The number of gained Attribute dots no longer increases past Potency. Combined with the previous Reach option this means the subject no longer needs to fear losing control over time.<br /> <br /> <b>Gestalt form (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> <br /> This spell allows two or more living being to fuse into one, creating a fused life form. The minds of the subjects fuse together forming a new merged personality with access to all the memories, knowledge and Skills of the subjects. The mage may determine which Attributes and appropriate Merits the being inherits. No Attribute can be higher than the highest level of that Attribute found among the subjects.<br /> <br /> If the subjects are all of the same supernatural template, then this template remains preserved after the fusion. The mage must determine what abilities the fused being has, again, no ability can be higher that the highest among the subjects. If the subjects are of differing templates then the mage determines which one template the fused being becomes, only the abilities specific to that template can be inherited.<br /> A mage can only have so many spells active, when fusing mages determine which spells will be under the new entities spell control.<br /> <br /> Once the Duration ends the subjects return to normal and any damage sustained is split equally among all subjects regardless of how much damage they had before. Willpower values are unchanged from their pre-merger values.<br /> Memories of the time spent fused will seem distant and hazy, dreamlike, but the subjects will remember the experience to some degree.<br /> <br /> Add Mind 4: The mage may determine to which of the subjects' memories, knowledge and Skills the fused being has access to.<br /> <br /> <b>Update:</b><br /> Added Reach options to 'Secret Identity'<br /> Rewrote both 'Protect the Balance' and 'Spiritual Symbiosis'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","user":"BeyondTheGrave","date":". 08-20-2017, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T03:16:14-07:00","id":1131660,"title":"","content":"Having Shadow Name \u2022 as a prerequisite for Secret Identity implies that the mage requires the Merit regardless of who they cast the spell on, which shouldn't be the case. Besides, it's quite possible to have a Shadow Name without having the Merit, meaning your taken Persona isn't yet representing you metaphysically. It seems to me you should easily be able to cast the spell on such subjects as well by using a Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T05:36:47-07:00","id":1131673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1131660#post1131660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Shadow Name \u2022 as a prerequisite for Secret Identity implies that the mage requires the Merit regardless of who they cast the spell on, which shouldn't be the case. Besides, it's quite possible to have a Shadow Name without having the Merit, meaning your taken Persona isn't yet representing you metaphysically. It seems to me you should easily be able to cast the spell on such subjects as well by using a Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thx for the feedback, I've updated the spell. I've also decided to add a Reach option to affect the Alternate Identity Merit as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:16:43-07:00","id":1131680,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11914_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11914\" data-vbnamecard=\"11914\">BeyondTheGrave</a> That first spell doesn't work as written. Spirit cannot detect Acamoth, goetia, ghosts, or souls by itself.<br /> <br /> Spiritual Symbiosis is redundant with Bind Spirit and requires Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> Gestalt Lifeform should not be able to be made Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T06:48:26-07:00","id":1131685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1131680#post1131680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11914_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11914\" data-vbnamecard=\"11914\">BeyondTheGrave</a> That first spell doesn't work as written. Spirit cannot detect Acamoth, goetia, ghosts, or souls by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goetia, ghosts and souls, no, but Gulmoths draws fuel from the Resonant Condition, meaning Spirit is most likely to detect disturbances caused by Gulmoths such as feeding from Resonances or applying further Manifestation Conditions. But I do agree that the spell wouldn't be able to just detect the presence of Gulmoths.<br /> If I were to rewrite the spell I'd probably also add that it detects the active effects of Immundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:22:49-07:00","id":1131693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1131680#post1131680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11914_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11914\" data-vbnamecard=\"11914\">BeyondTheGrave</a> That first spell doesn't work as written. Spirit cannot detect Acamoth, Goetia, ghosts, or souls by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1131685#post1131685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Goetia, ghosts and souls, no, but Gulmoths draws fuel from the Resonant Condition, meaning Spirit is most likely to detect disturbances caused by Gulmoths such as feeding from Resonances or applying further Manifestation Conditions. But I do agree that the spell wouldn't be able to just detect the presence of Gulmoths.<br /> If I were to rewrite the spell I'd probably also add that it detects the active effects of Immundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Spirit has no inherent ability to detect ghost, Goetia, souls, etc <br /> <br /> The idea was that It's a workaround to achieve the same effect as those Arcana. The spell detects what is 'unnatural' it could not detect ghosts in the Underworld or Goetia in the Astral for example because there is nothing out of place in those cases, it only works in select cases.<br /> <br /> I can't see the spell working as it is written anymore either though. I'll see what I can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spiritual Symbiosis is redundant with Bind Spirit and requires Spirit 4. </div> </div> </div>Your right creating Manifestation like Claimed (and it's prerequisites) requires Spirirt 4. But 'redundant'? The spell contains a lot of options on how to wrangle control from the spirit to the subject. <br /> <br /> I think I'll rewrite the spell and remove the part about creating the Claimed Condition and require the subject to already have it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gestalt Lifeform should not be able to be made Lasting. </div> </div> </div>What can and can't be made Lasting is pretty arbitrary. But the idea of the original people's personalities being subsumed into a new one, have you thought about that one? If the spell is made Lasting then the original personalities are gone forever, dead really. I found that appropriately dramatic a possibility to give it the Lasting option. Also think how the merged entity would feel, created from the lives of others, it\u2019s a Promethean-lite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:27:41-07:00","id":1131696,"title":"","content":"It shouldn't be made Lasting because a gestalt entity like that cannot exist without magic perpetuating its existence. Lasting assumes that the results or side effects of the spell can exist without the continued assertion of magic to make it so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T08:25:49-07:00","id":1131727,"title":"","content":"I've updated both Spiritual Symbiosis and Protect the Balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1131696#post1131696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn't be made Lasting because a gestalt entity like that cannot exist without magic perpetuating its existence. Lasting assumes that the results or side effects of the spell can exist without the continued assertion of magic to make it so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I guess. Though with things like even Soul Jar getting a +2 Lasting option it all still feels rather arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11914-beyondthegrave","name":"BeyondTheGrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11914_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T05:56:15-07:00","id":1132573,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Removed (for now).</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:26:05-07:00","id":1132618,"title":"","content":"It feels a little weird that a temporary (or at least removable) spell would give you the ability to permanently spend experience points on something like Rites. It would make more sense as an Attainment, and/or False Rite could be its own spell.<br /> <br /> I'm also not wild about keying the regeneration to the subject's Supernatural Tolerance. It don't see the in-universe justification; Gnosis, Blood Potency, Primum etc. represent very different things from Primal Urge, and neither Spirit nor Life has any real way of manipulating the things they represent. Maybe with conjunctional Prime (or as appropriate for the subject, e.g. Death for a vampire) I could see it, but I'd just lock it at regenerating as PU 1. If you don't want to do that (and even if you do) consider giving the appropriate penalties for the simulated Primal Urge, like the dietary restrictions and need to hunt. Bonus points if the spell explicitly <i>does not</i> give the subject a werewolf's cast-iron stomach, and/or the spell applies further side effects. One way or another I feel that trying to steal the Uratha's thunder should singe you a bit. The most obvious way would be to staple some sort of pseudo-Death Rage &quot;berserk mode&quot; to the spell's effects.<br /> <br /> Oh, and is it meant to give the subject honorary Rank as a werewolf with her fake Renown? Whether the answer is yes or no it should probably be spelled out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T08:35:52-07:00","id":1132624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and is it meant to give the subject honorary Rank as a werewolf with her fake Renown? Whether the answer is yes or no it should probably be spelled out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know a lot about Werewolf, but is their honorary Rank different than that of Spirit Mages? I mean, wouldn't they have one of 4 or 5 with the Arcana 4 Spirit attainment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:04:27-07:00","id":1132645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132624#post1132624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know a lot about Werewolf, but is their honorary Rank different than that of Spirit Mages? I mean, wouldn't they have one of 4 or 5 with the Arcana 4 Spirit attainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's based on their total Renown dots (0-3 is Rank 1, 4-7 is Rank 2 etc.) but otherwise works the same.<br /> <br /> The question is mainly relevant if you're casting the spell on someone other than yourself, though it could also come into play if your fake honorary Rank is low and someone sees you rending middling spirits apart because of your high honorary Rank from the Attainment.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, to what degree does the the spell fake Renown? If you're actually trying to fool werewolves into thinking you're one of them, stepping into the Shadow and not showing any brands is a dead giveaway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:09:55-07:00","id":1132647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd just lock it at regenerating as PU 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reach probably should just give the option of allocating potency to the regeneration option, pushing the fake regeneration up a notch. That said mages allready have a life spell that simulates increased regenerative capabilities in Body Control. Not sure the system should just arbitrarily deviate because you want to mimic werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:31:56-07:00","id":1132657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132647#post1132647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reach probably should just give the option of allocating potency to the regeneration option, pushing the fake regeneration up a notch. That said mages allready have a life spell that simulates increased regenerative capabilities in Body Control. Not sure the system should just arbitrarily deviate because you want to mimic werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like it would make pumping it way up a little too tempting.<br /> <br /> And yeah that spell exists, but this is conjunctional Spirit 4/Life 4 we're talking about. Mimicking base werewolf regeneration is about equivalent to Body Control with Potency 7 and +2 Reach. Considering that you get none of the other benefits of Body Control and the base effects of Lul'uratha aren't exactly mindblowing that doesn't sound super out of line to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T09:38:26-07:00","id":1132665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels a little weird that a temporary (or at least removable) spell would give you the ability to permanently spend experience points on something like Rites. It would make more sense as an Attainment, and/or False Rite could be its own spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Pack member can already purchase Pack Rites, and Mages can join Packs at the same level as humans (or potentially Wolf-Blooded) by default. The standard-effect text allowing them to purchase/lead with them is meant more as an in-character justification than a mechanical extension.<br /> <br /> Extending that option to purchasing Wolf Rites via Reach doesn't feel that weird, imo. Feel free to change it if you use it! This was something I cooked up in about ten minutes for a game I was playing in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not wild about keying the regeneration to the subject's Supernatural Tolerance. It don't see the in-universe justification; Gnosis, Blood Potency, Primum etc. represent very different things from Primal Urge, and neither Spirit nor Life has any real way of manipulating the things they represent. Maybe with conjunctional Prime (or as appropriate for the subject, e.g. Death for a vampire) I could see it, but I'd just lock it at regenerating as PU 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was done entirely for keeping the spell relatively simple by not adding extra conjunctionals for the various Power Stats. That said, locking it at PU 1 is even simpler, so I'll probably change that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way or another I feel that trying to steal the Uratha's thunder should singe you a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Mages with the Arcana this spell requires can already give themselves more potent abilities than this spell allows with much less work. Adding on negatives just gives people more reasons not to use it, and there's already very little reason to do so. You can get better regeneration, better forms to shift into, better attribute enhancement, etc already. The intent here is just to give Mages the option to 'fake it' like Demons/Beasts can (also without suffering Silver Weakness/Death Rage/Etc)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132618#post1132618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and is it meant to give the subject honorary Rank as a werewolf with her fake Renown? Whether the answer is yes or no it should probably be spelled out.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Mage's Honorary Rank remains the same as it was set to via the Attainment. The line about Renown was thrown in because I don't remember if there are any abilities that key into specific Renown for mechanical effects. If those aren't a thing (ie, 'This Power does damage equal to xyz Renown) I'll just remove it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 08-22-2017, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:10:38-07:00","id":1132683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132665#post1132665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Pack member can already purchase Pack Rites, and Mages can join Packs at the same level as humans (or potentially Wolf-Blooded) by default. The standard text allowing them to purchase/lead with them is meant more as an in-character justification than a mechanical extension.<br /> <br /> Extending that option to purchasing Wolf Rites via Reach doesn't feel that weird, imo. Feel free to change it if you use it! This was something I cooked up in about ten minutes for a game I was playing in.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to my book, &quot;Only werewolves can learn Wolf Rites, but both werewolves and Wolf-Blooded can learn Pack Rites.&quot; To me that doesn't sound like it includes other splats, even if they &quot;count as&quot; wolf-blooded in terms of pack dynamics. I'd probably allow it as a houserule, though, so sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132665#post1132665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Mages with the Arcana this spell requires can already give themselves more potent abilities than this spell allows with much less work. Adding on negatives just gives people more reasons not to use it, and there's already very little reason to do so. You can get better regeneration, better forms to shift into, better attribute enhancement, etc already. The intent here is just to give Mages the option to 'fake it' like Demons/Beasts can (also without suffering Silver Weakness/Death Rage/Etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a power level concern. I just don't like the idea of a mage playing consequence-free with another splat's toys. I also happen to find it more narratively interesting - a mage who arrogantly plays at being a werewolf (because how hard could it possibly be, right?) only to get smacked with more of Luna's &quot;favor&quot; than they bargained for is precisely the kind of hubris Mage is all about. You're probably right that the benefit isn't worth the cost, but in that case I'd rather improve the base effect and stick a drawback on than leave it as is. Besides, a character who's gone so far as to buy Rites with xp is probably Obsessed enough with werewolves that they're willing to do stupid things that aren't really worth it for a taste of the life lupine.<br /> <br /> That's just me, though. I don't like too much cross-contamination so I'd prefer to keep any &quot;imitation&quot; powers at a level where they're only appealing if you're heavily invested. If that doesn't bother you, don't let me bother you either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132665#post1132665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Mage's Honorary Rank remains the same as it was set to via the Attainment. The line about Renown was thrown in because I don't remember if there are any abilities that key into specific Renown for mechanical effects. If those aren't a thing (ie, 'This Power does damage equal to xyz Renown) I'll just remove it entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a bunch of Gifts and some other miscellaneous powers that do, but iirc none of the powers granted by this spell. The one thing that comes to mind is, as I mentioned, not having any Renown brands show up in the Shadow is intensely suspicious. Even the greenest werewolf should have at least one Renown from her Auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 08-22-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:43:07-07:00","id":1132726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132683#post1132683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to my book, &quot;Only werewolves can learn Wolf Rites, but both werewolves and Wolf-Blooded can learn Pack Rites.&quot; To me that doesn't sound like it includes other splats, even if they &quot;count as&quot; wolf-blooded in terms of pack dynamics. I'd probably allow it as a houserule, though, so sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I mis-remembered. Of course, Mages <i>can</i> be Wolf-Blooded, but I suppose that's neither here nor there. I'll leave that part, we don't have issues using buffed attributes or other statistics to qualify for expenditures at our table, the only caveat being that if the spell is dispelled or you cancel it, you lose access to whatever it qualified you for until you bring it back up (an idea we originally got from one of Dave's posts, iirc). In this case, if you buy Rites, you won't be able to use them unless you have this spell up, which seems reasonable enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132683#post1132683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a power level concern. I just don't like the idea of a mage playing consequence-free with another splat's toys. I also happen to find it more narratively interesting - a mage who arrogantly plays at being a werewolf (because how hard could it possibly be, right?) only to get smacked with more of Luna's &quot;favor&quot; than they bargained for is precisely the kind of hubris Mage is all about. You're probably right that the benefit isn't worth the cost, but in that case I'd rather improve the base effect and stick a drawback on than leave it as is. Besides, a character who's gone so far as to buy Rites with xp is probably Obsessed enough with werewolves that they're willing to do stupid things that aren't really worth it for a taste of the life lupine.<br /> <br /> That's just me, though. I don't like too much cross-contamination so I'd prefer to keep any &quot;imitation&quot; powers at a level where they're only appealing if you're heavily invested. If that doesn't bother you, don't let me bother you either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's honestly just not for me. I prefer the consequences for Hubris to be grounded in the story being told, not baked into the powers. Neither way is better, just different approaches.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1132683#post1132683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a bunch of Gifts and some other miscellaneous powers that do, but iirc none of the powers granted by this spell. The one thing that comes to mind is, as I mentioned, not having any Renown brands show up in the Shadow is intensely suspicious. Even the greenest werewolf should have at least one Renown from her Auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to cut that part out then. As for it being suspicious...that's good, I think. Good opportunity for consequences, there that I hadn't considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T09:36:26-07:00","id":1133047,"title":"","content":"Would a spell that changes a Boon into a Hex (or vice versa) be Weaving or Patterning, do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T10:21:06-07:00","id":1133067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1133047#post1133047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a spell that changes a Boon into a Hex (or vice versa) be Weaving or Patterning, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Patterning I'd say after a look at Sever Oaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T02:10:05-07:00","id":1134787,"title":"","content":"Two new spells for review: one developed by the Ministry of Panopticon for watching, and another for using Time as an illusion.<br /> <br /> Surveillance Station is a souped-up version of Scrying that allows the mage to watch a number of locations simultaneously. It's sort of a combination between the Scrying, Co-Locaiton, and Ioslation spells from the Space Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Surveillance Station (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Weaving</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Computers, Occult, Subterfuge</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The mage weaves disparate locations together so that they may watch over all of them simultaneously. The mage can link together one location per Potency of the spell, and any locations outside of sensory range require the use of a sympathetic Yantra. The resulting scrying window allows the mage to perceive with perfect clarity what is happening at every location simultaneously, although an action may only affect a single place at once. For example, the mage cannot use one action to remotely cast a spell at targets in multiple locations through the window. Additionally, as long as they observe the scrying window, the mage is immediately aware of any person in the surveilled locations starting to act against that location's intended purpose. For example, the mage will immediately become aware of someone attempting to rob a bank as soon as they start their heist (although not before).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022:</b> The mage becomes aware of the intentions of people in the observed areas, if those intentions are not in line with the location's intended purpose. The mage becomes aware of the intentions a number of turns equal to Potency before the action would be committed, if possible. Quick, impulsive decisions may leave less time for the mage to react.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage instills a strong sense of &quot;being watched&quot; at the observed locations. People in the affected locations must spend a point of Willpower to obviously act against the intended purpose of the location. For example, the bank robber would have to spend Willpower to overcome his nervousness to start the heist.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+ 1 Reach:</b> The mage is alerted if anything out of the ordinary happens at one of the locations under surveillance, even if they are not observing the scrying window. This does not tell the mage what happened, just that something did happen. By adding Fate \u2022 when casting the spell, the mage also learns the exact nature of the event.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> The next one is Veil Finality, a Time Veiling spell that allows the mage to create an illusion from the subject's own past. Think Temporal Summoning, but without actually changing the subject.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Veil Finality (Time \u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><ul><li><b>Practice:</b> Veiling</li> <li><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Temporal Sympathy</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Stealth, Subterfuge</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The mage creates an illusion of the self that draws from the self's own past. The subject appears to be in the state they were at the specified point in time. The subject's physical appearance and surface mental state appear to be as they were at the given point in time, although actual Attributes and Skills are not masked. This spell cannot hide supernatural attributes, such as the state of the subject's soul or any ongoing magical effects. It also cannot hide transformations like a mage's Awakening or a vampire's Embrace. By default, the spell can only access the subject's Unchanged history, but by adding Temporal Sympathy, the spell can reach into any point in the subject's past. Attempts to supernaturally pierce the illusion trigger a Clash of Wills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Add Life \u2022\u2022: </b>The subject's Physical Attributes and Skills are also hidden, appearing to be what they were at the given point in time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022:</b> The subject's Mental and Social Attributes and Skills are also hidden, appearing to be what they were at the given point in time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell hides supernatural attributes, such as the state of the subject's soul or ongoing spells.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell also hides drastic supernatural transformations, such as mage's Awakening or a vampire's Embrace.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 08-28-2017, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T07:04:16-07:00","id":1134823,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13082\" data-vbnamecard=\"13082\">projectmoon</a> You can use just the regular Scrying spell to open multiple windows, it would just require an increase in Scale for Subjects. Also doing it that way or with your spell you'd need to use a number of Sympathetic Yantras equal to the number of subjects being viewed which caps your possible scrutiny windows at six.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T08:04:54-07:00","id":1134838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1134823#post1134823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13082\" data-vbnamecard=\"13082\">projectmoon</a> You can use just the regular Scrying spell to open multiple windows, it would just require an increase in Scale for Subjects. Also doing it that way or with your spell you'd need to use a number of Sympathetic Yantras equal to the number of subjects being viewed which caps your possible scrutiny windows at six.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about this, yes. The main differentiator is that multiple regular scrying windows do not allow you to simultaneously perceive what's happening in each place. You'd need to focus on each one to make sure you don't miss important details. However, I'm not sure that's a compelling mechanical reason to use the spell like that. I could downgrade this spell to ruling. If it's kept at Space 3, maybe it needs something a bit more powerful to make it work the 3 arcanum dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T08:26:47-07:00","id":1134842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1134838#post1134838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about this, yes. The main differentiator is that multiple regular scrying windows do not allow you to simultaneously perceive what's happening in each place. You'd need to focus on each one to make sure you don't miss important details. However, I'm not sure that's a compelling mechanical reason to use the spell like that. I could downgrade this spell to ruling. If it's kept at Space 3, maybe it needs something a bit more powerful to make it work the 3 arcanum dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monitoring multiple windows would be a function best handled by something like One Mind, Two Thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T01:43:00-07:00","id":1138248,"title":"","content":"Played a bit with Spirit and good old psychic imprints. They fell under the purview of Mind in owod, but due to Essence being literally created and colored by (emotional) actions, it seems to me like spirit can get in on the action for nwod.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Read Imprint (Spirit \u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Occult, Empathy<br /> The Shadow is a reflection of the phenomenal world, build from Essence strongly colored in its Resonance by human action and emotion. A savy shaman can use this fact to learn of the origin of strong Resonance, calling upon supernal knowledge to recreate the events leading to the formation of the Resonance in question. Performing this spell on a resonant area, object or person will reveal a number of events that reinforced or created the Resonance equal to the Potency of the spell. As the spell draws upon the warped perspective of the Shadow, this knowledge often needs further interpretation.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>If the Essence spawned from the source produced a Spirit which since then has become active, the mages becomes aware of this fact.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>Ithe If a Spirit was spawned the mage may, in place of the normal effect, substitute the effects of the spell &quot;Know Spirit&quot; (withstood by the newly created Spirits rank as normal). Treat the spell as if it was cast on the Spirit at the moment it became active, even if the Spirit has since then changed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-07-2017, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T02:50:22-07:00","id":1138256,"title":"","content":"I would make that a Time 1 Spirit 1 spell, and I'm not sure the +2 Reach option should be possible since that is essentially allowing you to indirectly cast a spell on a target which is something Mage doesn't really allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T04:30:56-07:00","id":1138272,"title":"","content":"That +2 Reach option would also bypass the need to cast Know Spirit with temporal sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T07:08:31-07:00","id":1138315,"title":"","content":"The spell doesn't mess with time at all, it targets the essence and yields the information of what exactly caused the resonance the essence is carrying. Think of it as the equivalent to the reach on Forensic Gaze, which does something very similar for death.<br /> <br /> As for the +2 Reach action: This is essentially the same thing, it targets the essence and sees what spirit would have been created by it. It doesn't target the spirit at all, rather deduces details about it from it's birthplace. Though I can see that this one is pushing the envelope a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T18:48:10-07:00","id":1138773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1138315#post1138315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell doesn't mess with time at all, it targets the essence and yields the information of what exactly caused the resonance the essence is carrying. Think of it as the equivalent to the reach on Forensic Gaze, which does something very similar for death.<br /> <br /> As for the +2 Reach action: This is essentially the same thing, it targets the essence and sees what spirit would have been created by it. It doesn't target the spirit at all, rather deduces details about it from it's birthplace. Though I can see that this one is pushing the envelope a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of overlaps with Time imo, getting flashes from the past that led to the creation of the thing you're casting on in the present. But! You present a really good point with Forensice Gaze, and with that, yeah I'd let this fly as is. Except for that +2 Reach option, I see where you're coming from, but magic doesn't deduce, it informs and has to be used directly on a target to be able to function. If it flies in your games though, more power to you. I'm just saying it wouldn't fly in mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T07:18:13-07:00","id":1145213,"title":"","content":"A few spells I cooked u up for low level forces. First up is a sort of surveilance spell. It can either be used to get a picture of something you can perceive but you cannot see (a character of mine for example got a phonecall from a mysterious benefactor and used it to get a picture of him) or alternativly if cast at advanced scale with some potency it can give awesome situational awareness as you can see the interior of an entire building or neighbourhood like some sort of detailed minimap.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Lightwarden (Forces \u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Practice: </b>Knowing</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Science, Survival<br /> Where there is light, an initiate of Forces can see, even if the light never reaches his eyes. This spell shows the caster the photons emitted and reflected from the subject or area that is the target of the spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>When targeting a large area this spell can overwhelm the mages senses with a flashflood of light, this reach allows the mage to compensate for sensory overload.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly the classic spell every blind mage wants to have (aside from actually regenerating his sight). Can also be used to shrug off temporary blindness.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Blind Man's Eyes (Forces \u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Practice: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Unveiling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Duration</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Science, Athletics, Socialize<br /> Unveiling the visual spectrum to the subject, the mage allows the blind to see once more. For the duration of the spell the subject ignores the effects of the blinded tilt and condition. A smiliar spell takes care of deafness. </span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> A spell to detect electronical devices, possibly to tamper with them further with other spells.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Electronic Awareness (Forces \u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Practice: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Unveiling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Duration</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Crafts, Investigation, Science<br /> This Spell reveals all Electronic devices to the subjects senses by highlighting the electrical currents and voltages. The subject can see the flow of electrons, hear the buzz of power and smell a faint whiff of ozone in the presence of electronical devices.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Why limit yourself to listening to ongoing phonecalls? Just read their Texts, find out where they live and how much money they have in the bank!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Technopathy (Forces \u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Practice: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Knowing</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Potency</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> Investigation, Science, Streetwise<br /> In the modern world there is little information that does not exist in the digital format. A person's adress, the names of loved ones, incriminating pictures, all of it is readily available on his cellphone and to an Initiate of Forces a cellphone is an open book. This spell reveals up to potency pieces of information the mage was looking for, that are stored on the targeted electronic device. </span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Just to be on the safe side... and maybe for blackmail.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\">Copy and Paste (Forces \u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Practice: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Ruling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Primary Factor: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Potency</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#004f6d\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> Science, Larceny, Streetwise<br /> In Just knowing is never enough. With this spell information can be transferred from one digital device to another.</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-29-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T04:09:53-07:00","id":1146295,"title":"","content":"Lightwarden should be Unveiling. Knowing spells cannot overwhelm the mage, as it is Supernal knowledge directly dumped into the brain. You should probably also add a clause about locations out of sensory range requiring the use of Sympathetic Range.<br /> <br /> I would only allow Technopathy to work on unecrypted devices, since you're simply unveiling data that's already there. An unveiling spell will not unravel encryption. I think Forces 2 or 3 (Ruling or Fraying, depending on how you interpret it) would be able to decrypt data though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T07:40:18-07:00","id":1146334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1146295#post1146295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lightwarden should be Unveiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I designed it following the Life 1 spell &quot;Web of Life&quot;, which is a Knowing spell. The rationale for this being a knowing spell is simply that it can reveal sources of light you could not normally see (in fact unveiling light mostly in the visible spectrum would be what I did with the next spell I posted). This spell allows you to know what light is being emitted/reflected, which is useful in three cases. A) you can perceive the subject with another sense than your sense of sight and want to get an image of it. In this case unveiling would also work, as hearing the photons over a phonecall would work just aswell I suppose. Not sure you'd really see all of the subject then though... I'd personally stay with knowing here.<br /> B) You have a sympathetic link to the subject and want to know what it looks like (requiring space 2 of course), in this case knowing works while unveiling does nothing<br /> C) And imo most importantly, you can cast this spell on an area of which parts are not in your sensory range. Wih advanced scale you can target large areas around you, even exceeding your usual sensory range. Casting this spell with an area large enough to encompass the building you are in would allow you to see everything in this building, which in return kind of expands your sensory range (though casting on the subject you perceive this way and only this way will probably be considered as seeing them remotly).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Knowing spells cannot overwhelm the mage, as it is Supernal knowledge directly dumped into the brain. </div> </div> </div>And a dump of overwhelming amounts of information seems like it would be very... well overwhelming. See &quot;Web of Life&quot; which as a knowing spell mentions the possibility of sensory overload.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You should probably also add a clause about locations out of sensory range requiring the use of Sympathetic Range. </div> </div> </div>Sympathetic range doesn't really need mention here, as it works the same as for any other spell. If you want to cast this spell on a subject outside of your sensory range you need sympathetic range, otherwise you're fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would only allow Technopathy to work on unecrypted devices, since you're simply unveiling data that's already there. An unveiling spell will not unravel encryption. I think Forces 2 or 3 (Ruling or Fraying, depending on how you interpret it) would be able to decrypt data though. </div> </div> </div>Forces 1 specifically is able to unlock password protected devices with a compelling spell (see &quot;Influence Electricity&quot;), a Knowing spell could easily tell you the devices password. As long as the information was encrypted digitally/the device is able to decrypt it you should be fine. If the phone you're scanning has a picture of an ancient stone tablet on it it couldn't translate it though unless the device has the ability to do so (adding in Mind 1 would get rid of that though. Or working on it quite extensivly with Fate 2 via &quot;Lucky Number&quot; afterwards I guess).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T13:16:36-07:00","id":1146420,"title":"","content":"Manifest Truth<br /> <br /> Prime 4<br /> Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Recommended Skills: Occult, Craft, Expression<br /> <br /> Taking a lesson from the Ascended who leave behind bodies of crystallized Resonance a Mage with Prime can cause other sources of Resonance to similarly crystallize. The Resonance always takes a form that's appropriate to the Resonance's flavor, for instance Life Resonance might take the form of a crystalline flower. Unlike the artifacts left behind by the Ascended these objects have no artifact like powers. They do however serve as +1 Persona Yantra on an applicable spell like a Mage drawing on the power of a Ley Line or Node. They also count as Resonant to appropriate ephemeral creatures.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The Mage can choose the appropriately themed form that the Resonance takes.<br /> <br /> Add another Arcana at 4 dots: The crystallized Resonance doesn't have to adhere to a crystalline structure. Fire Resonance burns and Flower Resonance can be planted and bloom in its season.<br /> <br /> Line in the Sand<br /> <br /> Prime 5<br /> Making<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Recommended Skills: Occult, Academics, Streetwise<br /> <br /> A Mage may create a ley line from nothing and determine its Resonance. The ley line can only extend as far as the Scale of the spell permits. This sends mystical shockwaves throughout the affected area similar to the creation of a new Hallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-03-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:19:19-07:00","id":1146933,"title":"","content":"Re: Manifest truth, with additional arcanum, namely life<br /> How do you envision it being used? When i read it, i thought, cool idea... you could use this to change the resonance of an area without moving ley lines (which may have other effects in the long run). <br /> Also, why persona? i would have thought sacrament.<br /> <br /> I think Prime Weaving would be sufficient if you had a sample and were just &quot;infusing it with resonance&quot;, but i guess that overlaps with having tass with that resonance and spending mana on the spell...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what do you think of using Transform life with Conjunctional prime, indefinite duration and the +2 reach option to pass it on to the creature's descendants. infuse the resonace into plants and animals, and make life forms that naturally shift the resonance of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> Ahh... hubris at its best?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T01:37:26-07:00","id":1146940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1146933#post1146933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Manifest truth, with additional arcanum, namely life<br /> How do you envision it being used? When i read it, i thought, cool idea... you could use this to change the resonance of an area without moving ley lines (which may have other effects in the long run).<br /> Also, why persona? i would have thought sacrament.<br /> <br /> I think Prime Weaving would be sufficient if you had a sample and were just &quot;infusing it with resonance&quot;, but i guess that overlaps with having tass with that resonance and spending mana on the spell...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what do you think of using Transform life with Conjunctional prime, indefinite duration and the +2 reach option to pass it on to the creature's descendants. infuse the resonace into plants and animals, and make life forms that naturally shift the resonance of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> Ahh... hubris at its best?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I just saw it as something cool that you can do. <br /> <br /> I don't think it would work to shift Resonance in an area, unlike ley lines it's basically been locked into a non-leak lattice. At least that's been my assumption since the remains of the Ascended are Resonance but don't seem to change the Resonance of the area they're in as far as I know and that's what this is based on. Since it works as Resonant for ephemeral entities however, if you stuck a Love resonant crystal into an area filled with Hate Resonance, and a love spirit Fettered to the Love crystal it would certainly be able to start using its Influence to change the local Resonance. <br /> <br /> I figured it would be a Persona Yantra because mana from a Hallow that's intersected by a ley line counts as a Persona Yantra and this is kind of the same idea, though you don't get the benefit of having also spent a point of mana. You could double up and also treat it as a Sacrament. I could actually see a +1 Reach Option that lets you get a +2 out of it if you do use it as a Sacrament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T18:15:51-07:00","id":1147904,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 10-07-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T18:24:10-07:00","id":1147905,"title":"","content":"The fact that trait increasing spells generally can't be made Lasting. Of course, there's the indefinite option, but with the drawbacks of having an effective cost of 1 XP, and can be dispelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T05:46:29-07:00","id":1147978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1147905#post1147905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that trait increasing spells generally can't be made Lasting. Of course, there's the indefinite option, but with the drawbacks of having an effective cost of 1 XP, and can be dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The question was, &quot;Is there a reason other than game balance?&quot; I realized the answer was, &quot;No, there is no in universe reason.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T06:06:29-07:00","id":1147983,"title":"","content":"In that case the answer is probably just yes. It's just that the actual explanation isn't necessarily known to the players. Just because it isn't known to the player doesn't mean there is no explanation. I'm pretty sure all the Orders (Mysterium in particular) has many long, in-depth discussions about Supernal magic that players couldn't hope to emulate because it's an entire field of science based on premises that doesn't exist IRL. This holds true for most settings where magic exists and is studied.<br /> I would not be surprised if the mage community has written many theses, dissertations and research papers on the subject of the ephemeral nature of the higher Practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-08-2017, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T06:28:06-07:00","id":1149068,"title":"","content":"Just had a thought. This seems like something freaky you could do with Space and Mind combined, maybe? Like, you know how gangs have territory? Or there's &quot;Parts of town&quot; where &quot;Those kind&quot; of people aren't welcome, or nobody goes if they don't want to get mugged, etc, etc. Various forms of social, racial, economic, etc, etc, segregation/categorization of space itself?<br /> <br /> Imagine if there was a spell that let you see those boundaries? Like, you could look at a city from a tall building and sort of 'see' the lines that divide one 'type' of Space (as defined by one's connections, and perhaps also the nature of the Minds) from another. It sounds almost too grand, and definitely situational as hell, but it does seem like something that a Mage should be able to do, even if it's difficult? <br /> <br /> Basically, it's taking the geographic and connection-based elements of Space in a very, very different way. <br /> <br /> Am I insane to think this is possible for a Mage? I know, of course that it'd be very difficult. In order to see a whole city, you'd need an insane Range or whatnot. I'm more talking about theoretically possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T06:52:06-07:00","id":1149078,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12866\" data-vbnamecard=\"12866\">The_Laurent</a> you\u2019re basically talking about Sacred Geometry at Prime 1, reason being that areas are separated like that by the Resonance in them. Like criminals will be more active in areas that have Resonance like Theft, or Violence, reason being that they\u2019re contributing to the Resonance and being influenced by it.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it you could also use Correspondence targeting an area to determine the areas strongest Sympathetic connections in rough terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-12-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:10:54-07:00","id":1149380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1149078#post1149078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12866\" data-vbnamecard=\"12866\">The_Laurent</a> you\u2019re basically talking about Sacred Geometry at Prime 1, reason being that areas are separated like that by the Resonance in them. Like criminals will be more active in areas that have Resonance like Theft, or Violence, reason being that they\u2019re contributing to the Resonance and being influenced by it.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it you could also use Correspondence targeting an area to determine the areas strongest Sympathetic connections in rough terms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The latter would certainly work. The former could work for some things, but not others. Think about a bar that caters to a certain type. Someone who's not that type, in various reasons, comes in. He's not welcome. He could feel it in the air, he can sense it even without any magic, often enough.<br /> <br /> (Actually, what started all of this was the thinking of a character in a Mage game set in 20s Chicago. She was thinking about how even if you used magic to gain a lot of wealth, there were still some neighborhoods you couldn't move into without having to risk being burned out of your house, or assaulted, or worse. She being black, and Chicago having de-facto, violence enforced segregation at the time, including covenants and redlining and so on. And she thought 'there are lines, even if you can't see them' and that led her to thinking about whether magic could highlight them. The places where one sort of person wasn't welcome, and another was. That sort of thing. So it wouldn't really quite be Resonance, unless there's a &quot;No Blacks Allowed&quot; Resonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:27:53-07:00","id":1149387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Laurent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1149380#post1149380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter would certainly work. The former could work for some things, but not others. Think about a bar that caters to a certain type. Someone who's not that type, in various reasons, comes in. He's not welcome. He could feel it in the air, he can sense it even without any magic, often enough.<br /> <br /> (Actually, what started all of this was the thinking of a character in a Mage game set in 20s Chicago. She was thinking about how even if you used magic to gain a lot of wealth, there were still some neighborhoods you couldn't move into without having to risk being burned out of your house, or assaulted, or worse. She being black, and Chicago having de-facto, violence enforced segregation at the time, including covenants and redlining and so on. And she thought 'there are lines, even if you can't see them' and that led her to thinking about whether magic could highlight them. The places where one sort of person wasn't welcome, and another was. That sort of thing. So it wouldn't really quite be Resonance, unless there's a &amp;quot;No Blacks Allowed&amp;quot; Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>There could certainly be a Racist, Segregrated, etc Resonance flavors to places if it\u2019s the prevailing Resonance in the area. Knowing the Resonance would tell you how best to blend into the environment though, if you match the Resonance as best as possible (Say showing up in a gentrified white neighborhood in a maid\u2019s uniform) it can be a kind of camouflage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T17:19:56-07:00","id":1150238,"title":"","content":"Since Darkness is part of its purview, do people think it would be possible to create a Death spell that allows the caster to see through shadows? The Necromancer conjuring darkness to blind his adversaries with spells like Deepen Shadows is a very cool and evocative image. Him then tripping up over a rock because he just blinded himself as well as the opposition takes away from that slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T17:25:38-07:00","id":1150240,"title":"","content":"Actually, I wrote up a spell that let you treat darkness like light, with Death 1. It's not really that different from seeing in infrared or ultraviolet. Just takes a different sort of thinking. I came up with it as a spell version for a Legacy dedicated to &quot;becoming a shadow&quot;. Since you'll tend to stick to darkness to hide, you'd want to not be hindered by it, I figured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:50:00-07:00","id":1150327,"title":"","content":"Death unveiling should be able to reveal that which is hidden by darkness, functioning mechanically similar to the Forces spell &quot;Nightvision&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:54:55-07:00","id":1151003,"title":"","content":"Okay, I don't know if anyone has built this or not, but I had the idea of trying to create a &quot;Doombot&quot; spell. The general gist would be that, at the moment of your death, the spell activates, teleports you back to your Sanctum, and leaves an exact duplicate of you behind to get killed. I'm having difficulties figuring out exactly what the most efficient means of doing this would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:23:31-07:00","id":1151017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1151003#post1151003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I don't know if anyone has built this or not, but I had the idea of trying to create a &amp;quot;Doombot&amp;quot; spell. The general gist would be that, at the moment of your death, the spell activates, teleports you back to your Sanctum, and leaves an exact duplicate of you behind to get killed. I'm having difficulties figuring out exactly what the most efficient means of doing this would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be a combination of spells probably set up in a Hung Spell with a Fate contingency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:23:13-07:00","id":1152296,"title":"","content":"Unlocking the Brighter Road [Prime 3]<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Survival, Occult<br /> <br /> This spell reinforce the supernal connection between the mage and his tower, thus providing a safer route to bring forth Supernal entities<br /> It grants [Potency] extra rolls to the extended action.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: the extra rolls are extra safe so there can't be abyssal incursion [edited]<br /> +1 Reach: the extra rolls get 9-again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":13158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","user":"Sir Bardiel","date":". 11-03-2017, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:36:37-07:00","id":1152298,"title":"","content":"I would make the first Reach clause a +2 Reach option, good spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T16:43:56-07:00","id":1152328,"title":"","content":"I'll need some help.<br /> something like stepping into shadows and re-emerging from another shadows<br /> <br /> how do you think I can make this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:04:21-07:00","id":1152332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Bardiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1152328#post1152328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need some help.<br /> something like stepping into shadows and re-emerging from another shadows<br /> <br /> how do you think I can make this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space+Death is you mean it as a Teleport. Death 4 to become a Shadow and slip in and out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:28:12-07:00","id":1152431,"title":"","content":"Space 4 alone could optically accomplish the Teleportation part on it's own. A death 1 knowing spell casts on the area should make you aware of all shadows you could step to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:33:10-07:00","id":1152434,"title":"","content":"If I had Space I wouldn't need Death at all :\\<br /> So no means of &quot;shadowstep&quot; ok","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:34:57-07:00","id":1152435,"title":"","content":"You could use a shadow as a doorway to twilight, thus disappear and reappar. But you'd have to move the distance between the shadows normally within twilight. So yeah teleportation without Space isn't really a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:17:52-07:00","id":1152620,"title":"","content":"Is there any interest in a compilation of all of these spells that people are coming up with? I don't want to start one if there's already one out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:58:36-07:00","id":1152625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1112046#post1112046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there !<br /> Since I like homebrewing things for Mages (Legacies in particular), I took the initiative of gathering &quot;completed&quot; Spells into a google doc. I tried to avoid redundancies and still-in-progress Spells : the name disclaimer is only the name of the one who posted the Spell in its final version, not necessarily the original ideas (feel free to make reclamation if you feel prejudiced).<br /> <br /> Edit: I counted 199 Spells. Cool, isn't it ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta-9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1152620#post1152620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any interest in a compilation of all of these spells that people are coming up with? I don't want to start one if there's already one out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them are here, there have been new spells since then that you should feel free to compile though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T07:01:52-07:00","id":1152792,"title":"","content":"Ok. Thanks. I'm glad I asked, because I would have wasted my time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:29:13-08:00","id":1159540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Bardiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1152434#post1152434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had Space I wouldn't need Death at all :\\<br /> So no means of &quot;shadowstep&quot; ok</div> </div> </div> </div>You should bear in mind that these &quot;rulings&quot; aren't exactly binding and you can do whatever you and your group happen to find the most fun. Basically all tabletop RPGs have deep flaws in their rules that render games unfun for whatever reason, or they imply things that they didn't mean to.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they have this in 2E in Mage: the Awakening, but in 1E, they had this blurb about how you can analogize Temporal Sympathy to Spatial Sympathy, which implied you could just add Time 2 to any spell to cast it retroactively. Now, I'm pretty sure they didn't <i>mean </i>to insinuate that, but they did. Then there were also plenty of spell combos that were RAW OP.<br /> <br /> So I think the real question is, do you think that using Death to shadow stepping makes sense, narratively? Sure. I'd say it does. So just do it. Make something up you and your friends think is cool and go with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22803-ex-favilla-surgo","name":"Ex Favilla Surgo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22803_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T05:07:03-08:00","id":1159784,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question to see if I get things right. There's a spell Erode Resonance that removes the Resonant/Open Condition on the target as a Lasting effect. Can the same spell be cast in reverse (that is, adding the Resonant Condition to the target) with the same Arcanum requirement (Spirit 3)? Or what does it take to magically add this Condition to something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/341797-aids-for-beginners\" target=\"_blank\">CoD Rules Summary</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2593-ynas-midgard","name":"Ynas Midgard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:32:47-08:00","id":1159837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ynas Midgard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1159784#post1159784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question to see if I get things right. There's a spell Erode Resonance that removes the Resonant/Open Condition on the target as a Lasting effect. Can the same spell be cast in reverse (that is, adding the Resonant Condition to the target) with the same Arcanum requirement (Spirit 3)? Or what does it take to magically add this Condition to something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check Opener of the Way, Spirit 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:50:44-08:00","id":1159844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1159837#post1159837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check Opener of the Way, Spirit 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it, Opener of the Way either turns Resonant into Open or Open into Resonant, but you cannot add Resonant onto something from thin air.<br /> <br /> Follow up question regarding Erode Resonance. Say, I remove the Resonant Condition from my car in order to save it from a certain car/traffic spirit's attempts to control it through Manifestations. Now, it says the effects are Lasting, but clearly, once the spell's Duration is over, it would eventually become Resonant again, right? (I mean, it _is_ a car, after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/341797-aids-for-beginners\" target=\"_blank\">CoD Rules Summary</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2593-ynas-midgard","name":"Ynas Midgard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:58:27-08:00","id":1159850,"title":"","content":"Weaving could probably add the resonant tag for the duration of the spell, but I don't think it should be lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:10:13-08:00","id":1159858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ynas Midgard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1159784#post1159784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or what does it take to magically add this Condition to something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bind Spirit and its equivalents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T01:21:16-08:00","id":1162658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex Favilla Surgo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1159540#post1159540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should bear in mind that these &quot;rulings&quot; aren't exactly binding and you can do whatever you and your group happen to find the most fun. Basically all tabletop RPGs have deep flaws in their rules that render games unfun for whatever reason, or they imply things that they didn't mean to.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they have this in 2E in Mage: the Awakening, but in 1E, they had this blurb about how you can analogize Temporal Sympathy to Spatial Sympathy, which implied you could just add Time 2 to any spell to cast it retroactively. Now, I'm pretty sure they didn't <i>mean </i>to insinuate that, but they did. Then there were also plenty of spell combos that were RAW OP.<br /> <br /> So I think the real question is, do you think that using Death to shadow stepping makes sense, narratively? Sure. I'd say it does. So just do it. Make something up you and your friends think is cool and go with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> thanks mate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T19:40:03-08:00","id":1165203,"title":"","content":"Step 1: Get a lighter.<br /> Step 2: Use Forces 1 (with Reach 2) to make lighter flame size 2, then use Reach to make it into a long, thin shape.<br /> Step 3: Find a use for your new flame sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18145-goatmanofcoffee","name":"Goatmanofcoffee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T09:48:16-08:00","id":1171252,"title":"","content":"Trying to create more first level Death spells, I came up with this.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestral S\u00e9ance (Death </b>\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Occult, Socialize<br /> The Mage calls upon the wisdom of the dead, getting in touch with the Underworld. He or she feels like one or more spectral presences are watching over him or her, and are constantly granting him suggestions and advice on the present situation. Select a Mental or Social Skill. The Mage benefits from the spell Potency as a bonus to that skill for the remainder of the spell. Mantaining this contact can be really stressful for a mage, being influenced by outside entities, and he gains a Ban Condition appropriate to ghostly entities.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>The bolstered Skill might be Physical instead of Mental or Social.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>Once per chapter while under this spell, the recipient can benefit from the Common Sense Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Channelling (Spirit \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Occult, Socialize<br /> The Mage calls upon the wisdom of spirits, getting in touch with the Shadow Realm. He or she feels like one or more alien and spiritual presences are watching over him or her, and are constantly giving him suggestion and advice on the present situation. elect a Mental or Social Skill. The Mage benefits from the spell Potency as a bonus to that skill for the remainder of the spell. Mantaining this contact can be really stressful for a mage, being influenced by outside entities, and he gains a Ban Condition appropriate to spirit entities.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>The bolstered Skill might be Physical instead of Mental or Social.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>Once per chapter while under this spell, the recipient can benefit from the Common Sense Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:26:39-08:00","id":1171274,"title":"","content":"These should only give a +1 to Skill, not Potency level of Skill. Mind's Enhance Skill is a 3-dot Perfecting spell after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T11:36:43-08:00","id":1171279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171274#post1171274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These should only give a +1 to Skill, not Potency level of Skill. Mind's Enhance Skill is a 3-dot Perfecting spell after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears they\u2019re built on a similar vein to Quantum Flux.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d let those spells fly at all though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:45:18-08:00","id":1171306,"title":"","content":"Well I guess I could decrease to +1. Reposting.<br /> <br /> <b>Ancestral S\u00e9ance (Death </b>\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Occult, Socialize<br /> The Mage calls upon the wisdom of the dead, getting in touch with the Underworld. He or she feels like one or more spectral presences are watching over him or her, and are constantly granting him suggestions and advice on the present situation. Select a Mental or Social Skill. The Mage benefits from +1 to that Skill for the remainder of the spell. Mantaining this contact can be really stressful for a mage, being influenced by outside entities, and he gains a Ban Condition appropriate to ghostly entities.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>The bolstered Skill might be Physical instead of Mental or Social.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>Once per chapter while under this spell, the recipient can benefit from the Common Sense Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Channelling (Spirit \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Rote Skills: </b>Investigation, Occult, Socialize<br /> The Mage calls upon the wisdom of spirits, getting in touch with the Shadow Realm. He or she feels like one or more alien and spiritual presences are watching over him or her, and are constantly giving him suggestion and advice on the present situation. elect a Mental or Social Skill. The Mage benefits from +1 to that Skill for the remainder of the spell. Mantaining this contact can be really stressful for a mage, being influenced by outside entities, and he gains a Ban Condition appropriate to spirit entities.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>The bolstered Skill might be Physical instead of Mental or Social.<br /> <b>Reach +1: </b>Once per chapter while under this spell, the recipient can benefit from the Common Sense Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T16:24:46-08:00","id":1171364,"title":"","content":"I will say that they pass the cool factor test, but do they pass the game mechanics test?<br /> <br /> The &quot;Knowing&quot; needs to be about something in Death and Spirit's purview IMO. So Ancestral Seance to gain skill in Crafts doesn't work, as Crafts is not in Death's purview.<br /> <br /> So as cool as these are, I'm going to have to agree that these don't really fly.<br /> <br /> What you need is to use Ghost Summons to force a Ghost to use it's own skills for whatever it is you're trying to do instead, or to get a Teamwork bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T16:39:41-08:00","id":1171367,"title":"","content":"Compelling could get a ghost or spirit to do something it may have done anyway. Basically, in a 50/50 (Not a real estimate of odds) situation you could compel an ephemeral entity to do something. This is exemplified in Coaxing the Spirit pretty well, but you could build a spell for a different sort of circumstance, say forcing a ghost to Manifest since that\u2019s a power it has and is something it might do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T23:51:54-08:00","id":1171472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171364#post1171364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that they pass the cool factor test, but do they pass the game mechanics test?<br /> <br /> The &quot;Knowing&quot; needs to be about something in Death and Spirit's purview IMO. So Ancestral Seance to gain skill in Crafts doesn't work, as Crafts is not in Death's purview.<br /> <br /> So as cool as these are, I'm going to have to agree that these don't really fly.<br /> <br /> What you need is to use Ghost Summons to force a Ghost to use it's own skills for whatever it is you're trying to do instead, or to get a Teamwork bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be one of Death's purview literally, but it could be a ghost's purview (maybe the ghost was a carpenter or an artist?). Death also has precedents for giving ghosts the ability to learn Numina that don't directly relate to Death as an effect (Firestarter or Blast? Forces or Matter. Most mind-affecting powers? Mind). The ghost(s) is simply granting his knowledge from when he/she was alive. I guess I could restrict the spell further to a couple skills, or even just to Attribute rolls (this way we don't get too specific).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T01:59:55-08:00","id":1171486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171472#post1171472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not be one of Death's purview literally, but it could be a ghost's purview (maybe the ghost was a carpenter or an artist?). Death also has precedents for giving ghosts the ability to learn Numina that don't directly relate to Death as an effect (Firestarter or Blast? Forces or Matter. Most mind-affecting powers? Mind). The ghost(s) is simply granting his knowledge from when he/she was alive. I guess I could restrict the spell further to a couple skills, or even just to Attribute rolls (this way we don't get too specific).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the spell(s) doesn\u2019t actually require the presence of a ghost, or spirit. Instead there\u2019s a vague attunement to the realm from which it comes, both of which have no concrete association with any skill except that through it\u2019s denizens which the spell doesn\u2019t require the presence of. You could have the spell require the presence of an ephemeral entity, but then the question arises of why you\u2019re not just having them do the heavy lifting instead since they\u2019re the ones actually suited to the task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:42:50-08:00","id":1171550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171486#post1171486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the spell(s) doesn\u2019t actually require the presence of a ghost, or spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the problem. Granting a larger than +1 bonus is fine (see Quantum Flux) but it should require the presence of an entity that actually has the requisite knowledge, and probably a turn of direct communion with them (again, see QF).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T11:51:01-08:00","id":1171579,"title":"","content":"Yes, this is an attempt at a Knowing spell. Not a Weaving spell to copy Ghost Numina from a Ghost standing next to you. Too powerful for 1-dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:07:05-08:00","id":1171585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171579#post1171579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is an attempt at a Knowing spell. Not a Weaving spell to copy Ghost Numina from a Ghost standing next to you. Too powerful for 1-dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has nothing to do with the spell\u2019s power, but with the fact that it\u2019s not thematically fitting. Mechanically it\u2019s fine. It doesn\u2019t work with the game\u2019s metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:48:49-08:00","id":1171597,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Knowing is a 1-dot practice for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T12:59:39-08:00","id":1171604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1171597#post1171597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but Knowing is a 1-dot practice for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has literally nothing to do with this conversation. Knowing could be something you only get with Mastery and it wouldn\u2019t change the fact that thematically the spells in question do not fit the arcana in terms of what they set out to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:18:56-08:00","id":1172345,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of broadening the use of Forces and I would welcome criticism of this spell. It is basically a poor mans Psychic Domination. This way, an Obrimos may <i>force </i>her will upon someone. I am not sorry for that pun. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Superstimulus </b>(Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Computer, Expression, Science<br /> <br /> With this spell the mage uses light, sounds and other such stimuli to affect the perceptions and brain processes of the subject, producing a superstimulus powerful enough to override the will of the subject. This does not work on anything without a physical brain, so only humans and animals may be targeted. The mage may give a number of commands to the subject equal to Potency that the subject feels a need to go through with despite themselves. The commands must be simple, one-word orders \u2014 such as to sleep, eat, sit, or defend. It cannot be commands that seriously violates the subject's sense of self or makes them hurt themselves. Storyteller discretion is applied here.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage is capable of taking control of her subject, forcing him to take actions against his will. The mage can force the subject to perform one task. The task can be as complex or simple as the mage desires, giving the subject detailed mental instructions on how to go about completing the task. She cannot force the subject to act in a way that would put him in serious danger, or to commit suicidal acts.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b>: The mage must spend one Mana when casting the spell. As with +1 Reach above, but the mage can force her subject to take any kind of action without limitations. For example, the mage could direct her victim to shoot himself in the head, or to run into a burning building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T13:30:10-08:00","id":1172365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1172345#post1172345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of broadening the use of Forces and I would welcome criticism of this spell. It is basically a poor mans Psychic Domination. This way, an Obrimos may <i>force </i>her will upon someone. I am not sorry for that pun. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b>Superstimulus </b>(Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Computer, Expression, Science<br /> <br /> With this spell the mage uses light, sounds and other such stimuli to affect the perceptions and brain processes of the subject, producing a superstimulus powerful enough to override the will of the subject. This does not work on anything without a physical brain, so only humans and animals may be targeted. The mage may give a number of commands to the subject equal to Potency that the subject feels a need to go through with despite themselves. The commands must be simple, one-word orders \u2014 such as to sleep, eat, sit, or defend. It cannot be commands that seriously violates the subject's sense of self or makes them hurt themselves. Storyteller discretion is applied here.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage is capable of taking control of her subject, forcing him to take actions against his will. The mage can force the subject to perform one task. The task can be as complex or simple as the mage desires, giving the subject detailed mental instructions on how to go about completing the task. She cannot force the subject to act in a way that would put him in serious danger, or to commit suicidal acts.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b>: The mage must spend one Mana when casting the spell. As with +1 Reach above, but the mage can force her subject to take any kind of action without limitations. For example, the mage could direct her victim to shoot himself in the head, or to run into a burning building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should probably work more like Control Instincts from Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:18:29-08:00","id":1172384,"title":"","content":"Or like Shaping (Matter \u2022\u2022). You can control all sensory input, but controlling a person through sensory inputs isn't part of Forces, so you have to manually manipulate the senses with a mundane Intelligence + Something roll. In such a case the spell could use Weaving instead of Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T05:57:01-08:00","id":1172619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1172365#post1172365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should probably work more like Control Instincts from Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that's a much better model for the spell. I will redo it then.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Superstimulus </b>(Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Computer, Expression, Science<br /> With this spell the mage uses light, sounds and other such stimuli to affect the perceptions and brain processes of the subject, producing a superstimulus powerful enough to override the will of the subject. This does not work on anything without a physical brain, so only humans and animals may be targeted. This cannot give fine mental manipulation but rather floods the target with a very strong stimulus that is hard to shake off or ignore. A raging animal can be made to flee by triggering its instincts to flight, a spider may weave its web in an inadequate environment or a rabbit may approach food despite obvious dangers. Only beings with a physical brain may be affected, and all supernatural creatures are unaffected.<br /> Last but not least, this spell only shapes stimuli to allow this manipulation to happen (in other words, it only provides the tool) but the mage herself has to do the actual manipulating. This might require a Manipulation + Empathy roll for affecting humans and Manipulation + Animal Ken to affect animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T10:48:00-08:00","id":1174071,"title":"","content":"What's the necessary Forces required to intensify or diminish the global effects of climate change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T11:00:38-08:00","id":1174076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174071#post1174071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the necessary Forces required to intensify or diminish the global effects of climate change?</div> </div> </div> </div>The upper limit on Advanced Scale means you would need an Order bigger than any existing Order of Forces Mages working in concert, but you'd really only need a Fraying or Perfecting spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T11:46:02-08:00","id":1174095,"title":"","content":"It seems reasonable that to me that there is some 6+ value where a single mage could perform the feat. Is that untrue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T17:04:28-08:00","id":1174152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174095#post1174095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems reasonable that to me that there is some 6+ value where a single mage could perform the feat. Is that untrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters can accomplish anything, so obviously yes they could do it. I didn't bother to mention them because they're only tangentially related to Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:11:40-08:00","id":1174167,"title":"","content":"That answer is equally vague and unhelpful. I'll wait for another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:37:15-08:00","id":1174174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174167#post1174167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That answer is equally vague and unhelpful. I'll wait for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not going to get much better, considering the answer is that any 6+ rating in an Arcanum requires a character to have irrevocably changed the way they relate to the world as a mage to such a degree that they're practically playing a different game and breaking the limits of Area Scale necessitates more than five dots in an Arcanum.<br /> <br /> A 6+ rating exists literally in the realm of plot device in the abilities of characters who are themselves plot devices. &quot;A single mage&quot; is only capable of that if they've gone well and truly beyond being &quot;a mage.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:42:18-08:00","id":1174175,"title":"","content":"So you're saying there's a massive hole in the system where 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10 in an arcanum all mean the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:46:12-08:00","id":1174177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174175#post1174175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying there's a massive hole in the system where 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10 in an arcanum all mean the same thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the system doesn't of Mage the Awakening doesn't have arcana ratings of those levels. Imperial Mysteries does, but 1 it's 1e, and 2 it's a different game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:50:14-08:00","id":1174180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174177#post1174177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the system doesn't of Mage the Awakening doesn't have arcana ratings of those levels. Imperial Mysteries does, but 1 it's 1e, and 2 it's a different game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me go look that up.<br /> Alright, so yeah, it appears to be 1e, but the claim that it's a different game seems wrong? According to the blurb.<br /> <br /> &quot;A supplement for Mage: the Awakening<br /> <br /> - Full Rules for archmasters, including the Practices of the sixth to ninth Arcana dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds right to me. I'll go squirrel away some funds to find the answer then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T18:52:28-08:00","id":1174181,"title":"","content":"Like I said, it's only tangentially related to Mage in that its derived from Mage. It's like when Friends did a spinoff about Joey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T20:27:32-08:00","id":1174199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174180#post1174180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so yeah, it appears to be 1e, but the claim that it's a different game seems wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is <i>literally impossible</i> for a character to get a sixth dot of an Arcanum without changing the way the universe works to make themselves an archmaster, which is a thing that occupies broadly the same narrative space as Werewolf accords to the Firstborn and Luna or Changeling accords to the greater powers of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> No amount of arcane might in a Mage game is going to make a regular mage capable of geographically affecting even something as small as a city with a single spell, because that degree of influence shares space with plot devices like the self-sustaining spells, template surgery, soul-reduplication, and raw-thematic-fiat effects of the Practices of Dynamics, Excision, Entities, Dominions, and Transfiguration, which are archmagic used by mages who've dived so deep into their obsession with occult power that they've warped their entire place in reality out of shape and <i>live inside their own souls</i>.<br /> <br /> You could hypothetically affect the entire world with a spell with six dots in the Arcanum and no more, but <i>getting the sixth dot in an Arcanum is the kind of thing you can build the end of a chronicle around</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T20:34:42-08:00","id":1174201,"title":"","content":"Could not agree more, and in fact the main dev Dave did in fact do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T23:03:18-08:00","id":1174212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174199#post1174199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IYou could hypothetically affect the entire world with a spell with six dots in the Arcanum and no more, but <i>getting the sixth dot in an Arcanum is the kind of thing you can build the end of a chronicle around</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool? Not sure where this weird lecture is coming from? Like, first of all, assuming I was asking as a player who wants their mage to do something super cool, still would be weirdly condescending. But as a storyteller I can design whatever character I want? And have them start at whatever power I want them to start with? I was just curious about what level an important characters forces would be. I'll make a note not to dare to ask simple power level questions in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T08:54:22-08:00","id":1174290,"title":"","content":"Thing is, the answer to any such question as the Storyteller is &quot;whatever I think works for this story&quot; You could just devise an Artifact or a place of power or any other thing that increases the reach of magic way beyond what is ussually assumed to be the max limits and as long as is interesting, what else matters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T10:52:12-08:00","id":1174313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174212#post1174212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool? Not sure where this weird lecture is coming from?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What level of power would it take for an Awakened character to do this thing that exceeds the specifically-stated limits of Awakened magic?&quot;<br /> &quot;The specifically-stated limits of Awakened magic mean you would need a lot of separate characters maintaining their own instances of the spell at once, but that level of power would be covered by Practices around the middle of the Arcanum dot ladder.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah but it seems like if a single character had a level of power that specifically breaks the limits they could do it on their own.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yes, but that single character would have to be breaking the limits, which means a specific thing in Mage: the Awakening. We don't bother mentioning them in questions about what the average Awakened character can do because they're the furthest thing from the average Awakened character.&quot;<br /> &quot;That's vague and unhelpful. Another answer, please.&quot;<br /> &quot;The first answer is saying that the specific thing breaking the limits of Awakened magic means in Mage: the Awakening happens to relegate most of those characters to plot devices and deus ex machina. The difference between an archmaster with six dots in Forces and an archmaster with nine dots in Forces is mostly academic to anyone who isn't looking at their character sheet.&quot;<br /> &quot;So the game is broken and there's no difference between a character that's one order of magnitude past the limits and a character that's five orders of magnitude past the limits?&quot;<br /> <br /> You asked how a character could change the world on a grand scale with a singular use of magic, and when told the answer to that was &quot;by being the kind of incredibly uncommon and inhumanly driven entity you have to change the world to become in the first place, at which point the specific limits of your powers beyond the particular things they can mess with are largely gone,&quot; you started Having An Attitude about it.<br /> <br /> Archmaster spells that aren't just souped-up versions of the Common Practices need ritual components that take entire stories to acquire, which is a thing that was known by name since Tome of the Mysteries. That same book also lays out why archmasters don't usually do world-shaking magic on a world-shaking scale in social terms and contains a sidebar in the same section with advice on how to run Imperial Magic. Tome of the Mysteries has been out for over ten years and much of the broad strokes of its content on archmasters is repeated in the 2e corebook's section on archmasters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll make a note not to dare to ask simple power level questions in the future. </div> </div> </div>You'd be better served making a note to <i>ask for clarification</i> when you're not satisfied by the level of detail in an answer instead of <i>calling it vague and unhelpful and putting out an open call for someone else to engage with you right after you insulted an answer that didn't meet your standards</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Typos. 01-08-2018, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T10:42:37-08:00","id":1174585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174095#post1174095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems reasonable that to me that there is some 6+ value where a single mage could perform the feat. Is that untrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries translates fairly well to 2e, but you need patch rules. These are fairly complete: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kIDr9_-oBGLEPwmfmtTyTefnSh9d5D62LdY1fCa7UHI/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...Y1fCa7UHI/edit</a><br /> <br /> To affect the entire world is not possible as a single regular mage. Forces 6, with the Practice of Dynamics, could make a spell that propagates around the world and dynamically alters conditions of global warming on an international scale.<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries isn't really a separate game per se, but the way archmasters are played are fundamentally different from regular mages because of what they can do. The book literally has an optional system called Imperium which calls for running sub-games of regular Mage: the Awakening in order to advance archmages' agendas. In that sense, it's a different game. The subject matter is also different. Archmages are not focused around urban sorcery and solving local problems. They have cosmic agendas and are usually amoral self-interested actors. They deal with gods and worlds beyond human comprehension on a regular basis. A single spell or Imperium rite from an archmage can completely change the world and the rules by which it operates.<br /> <br /> That being said, it can be really fun to blow up the universe with imperial magic (only likely to have someone restore it and then come after you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T17:12:24-08:00","id":1174702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174167#post1174167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That answer is equally vague and unhelpful. I'll wait for another.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1174212#post1174212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool? Not sure where this weird lecture is coming from? Like, first of all, assuming I was asking as a player who wants their mage to do something super cool, still would be weirdly condescending. But as a storyteller I can design whatever character I want? And have them start at whatever power I want them to start with? I was just curious about what level an important characters forces would be. I'll make a note not to dare to ask simple power level questions in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>I am only infracting one of these posts because they are, functionally the same offense. Please keep in mind that you are not required to respond to posts you don't like. If you do take the time to respond, take the time to be courteous.</b></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rule 1: Respect other people</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don\u2019t personally attack other users, members of their gaming groups, and so on. Also, don\u2019t attack groups of people. That means avoiding racist, sexist, homophobic, transphobic and similar insults. Racial, sexual, and other slurs, as well as misgendering, count as insults. Please also avoid broad declarations that attack a group of people to get around making a \u201cpersonal\u201d attack. Like all rules, this rule applies equally to people working for Onyx Path, White Wolf, Paradox, and CCP.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rule 2: Respect the conversation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t try to incite others to break the rules, or distract from the subject at hand. This includes threadcrapping, the posting of short messages or images which add nothing to a thread and serve only to express a user\u2019s displeasure with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T15:22:27-08:00","id":1175294,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has been asked before, but has anyone homebrewed some spells for creating illusions with either Prime or Forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T18:19:02-08:00","id":1175322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1175294#post1175294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been asked before, but has anyone homebrewed some spells for creating illusions with either Prime or Forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>In many cases Veiling is the Practice that covers illusions regardless of arcana, making something seem like what it isn\u2019t is part of Veiling after all.<br /> <br /> Saying \u201cillusion\u201d is too vague. Define the term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T11:18:09-08:00","id":1175514,"title":"","content":"This is a spell I've been considering for a while. I'm not entirely certain about it, whether it should require a point of Mana, etc. But, this is what I have:<br /> <br /> <b>Hasten Symbolism (Time </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Expression, Occult<br /> <br /> The mage enhances the target's ability to conceptualize the symbols of magical power, condensing what would take multiple moments into a single, graceful movement. The next time the target casts a spell during this spell's Duration, the target may utilize an additional number of Yantras equal to this spell's Potency in the same reflexive action. This does not affect Yantras that normally require more than a reflexive action to employ (such as High Speech or Runes), nor does it increase the Gnosis-derived number of Yantras the target may access.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target can use the High Speech Yantra as a reflexive action.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Add this spell's Potency to the target's Gnosis for the purpose of determining how long it takes to draw runes.<br /> <b>+1 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> The target benefits from this spell's effects on a number of spells equal to Potency.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T12:48:33-08:00","id":1175535,"title":"","content":"You should change Reflexive to Instant, since actual Reflexive spells are rare. Also wouldn't it make some sense to incorporate at least Prime 3 as well, since Yantras sort of fall under that purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T13:07:58-08:00","id":1175543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1175535#post1175535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should change Reflexive to Instant, since actual Reflexive spells are rare. Also wouldn't it make some sense to incorporate at least Prime 3 as well, since Yantras sort of fall under that purview?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, you\u2019re not affecting the Yantra, you\u2019re compressing the time it takes to use them.<br /> <br /> Also, the spell isn\u2019t reflexive, it\u2019s the use of Yantras that\u2019s being made Reflexive which is already partially part of the Yantra rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-12-2018, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T07:07:46-08:00","id":1176942,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this spell?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Supernal Disconnect (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Cost: Varies (See Below)<br /> Withstand: Gnosis<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Larceny, Intimidation<br /> A mage can reduce the Supernal Connection a person possesses making it harder for them to use magical tools with a connection to the Supernal World. Any attempts to use a magical item by the subject of this spell suffers a penalty equal to Potency on a number of uses equal to Potency.<br /> +2 Reach: This spell inflicts a penalty equal to Potency on all spells cast by the subject for a number of rolls equal to Potency.<br /> +1 Reach: This spell can effect Focused Mage Sight acting as a penalty equal to Potency on a number of Scrutiny Rolls equal to the Potency.<br /> +1 Reach and 1 Mana: This spell can reduce the number of merit dots equal to Potency available to Sleepwalkers involving their connection to the Supernal Realms (Banner-Bearer, Relic Attuned, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-18-2018, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T09:23:04-08:00","id":1176975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1176942#post1176942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this spell?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Supernal Disconnect (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Cost: Varies (See Below)<br /> Withstand: Gnosis<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Larceny, Intimidation<br /> A mage can reduce the Supernal Connection a person possesses making it harder for them to use magic or utilize tools with a connection to the Supernal World. Any attempts to cast a spell or use a magical item by the subject of this spell suffers a penalty equal to the Potency of this spell.<br /> +1 Reach: This spell reduces the caster's effective Gnosis equal to Potency for determining the number of Yantras available. (Minimum 1)<br /> +1 Reach: This spell can effect Active Mage Sight removing the 10-again on Clash of Wills to pierce veiling effects.<br /> +1 Reach: This spell can effect Focused Mage Sight acting as a penalty to Scrutiny Rolls equal to the Potency of this spell.<br /> +1 Reach and 1 Mana: This spell can disable the effects of certain merits available to Sleepwalkers involving their connection to the Supernal Realms (Banner-Bearer, Relic Attuned, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept of the spell.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that you're not supposed to use Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand spells. At least not usually. I say this as someone who designed a spell that was Withstood by Blood Potency! If you keep the Withstand as Gnosis, you should technically put &quot;Supernatural Tolerance&quot; as the Withstand trait. Maybe Resolve should be the Withstand trait instead?<br /> <br /> The penalty should affect only a number of rolls equal to Potency. This is from the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines.<br /> <br /> Normally spells that affect spellcasting require 2 Reach. Even Blink of an Eye, a Time 5 spell, requires 2 Reach and 1 Mana to affect spellcasting rolls. I would suggest that the spell only give a penalty to using Artifacts, Imbued Items, and other items connected to the Supernal Realms. Add a +2 Reach and 1 Mana option to make it affect spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is a single thing in the book that alters the nature of Clash of Wills rolls beyond bonuses granted by Duration, so I would remove this Reach effect.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect for disabling Sleepwalker merits is a cool idea. Instead of outright disabling them, I think it would make more sense if it reduces the dots of the merits by Potency, down to zero dots.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect for reducing Yantras used sounds to me more like an Unraveling (4 dots) effect, but this is personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T09:51:26-08:00","id":1176989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that you're not supposed to use Supernatural Tolerance to Withstand spells. At least not usually. I say this as someone who designed a spell that was Withstood by Blood Potency! If you keep the Withstand as Gnosis, you should technically put &quot;Supernatural Tolerance&quot; as the Withstand trait. Maybe Resolve should be the Withstand trait instead? </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought about that, but one of the spells released in Signs of Sorcery spoilers uses Opacity which can range from 1 to 10. Also, I felt it is the Supernal Connection being targeted versus the actual person itself, so I felt Gnosis would be the best trait representing how much of a connection a mage had to the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The penalty should affect only a number of rolls equal to Potency. This is from the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines. </div> </div> </div>Quite right, and has been corrected. Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Normally spells that affect spellcasting require 2 Reach. Even Blink of an Eye, a Time 5 spell, requires 2 Reach and 1 Mana to affect spellcasting rolls. I would suggest that the spell only give a penalty to using Artifacts, Imbued Items, and other items connected to the Supernal Realms. Add a +2 Reach and 1 Mana option to make it affect spellcasting rolls. </div> </div> </div>I hesitated on this, but I think you are correct despite Prime's purview being &quot;Magic&quot;, so I have instead used +2 Reach option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think there is a single thing in the book that alters the nature of Clash of Wills rolls beyond bonuses granted by Duration, so I would remove this Reach effect. </div> </div> </div>You are correct, I may revisit this at another time because I imagine there is a way to influence Clash of Wills in a negative fashion, but it may be game breaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Reach effect for disabling Sleepwalker merits is a cool idea. Instead of outright disabling them, I think it would make more sense if it reduces the dots of the merits by Potency, down to zero dots. </div> </div> </div>This has been implemented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Reach effect for reducing Yantras used sounds to me more like an Unraveling (4 dots) effect, but this is personal opinion. </div> </div> </div>I feel this might actually be unmaking and have removed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T10:14:17-08:00","id":1182021,"title":"","content":"Some mean Fate Spells:<br /> <br /> <b>Erase Name (Fate </b><b>4</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Politics, Streetwise<br /> <br /> This spell disconnects a target from one of his identities. When cast, the mage chooses one name the target is known by: This can be his sympathetic name, a nickname, an online handle, special title, or the like. For the spell's duration, no one can make the connection between the target and that name. Reduce a social merit connected to the name (such as Fame, Status, or Alternate Identity) by the spell's Potency. For as long as the identity is suppressed, the name cannot be used as a Sympathetic Yantra to cast spells on the subject. If the subject's sympathetic name is erased, the Withstand rating of spells cast on him does not increase from not knowing it. This spell can erase Shadow Names and the Shadow Name merit, but requires a point of mana to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can split the spell's Potency among multiple social merits.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject also gains the Anonymity merit at a dot rating equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Downfall (Fate 5)<br /> Practice: </b>Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Larceny, Persuasion<br /> <br /> A Witch who wants you dead can do so much more than just blast you to smithereens. She can set up the entire world against you if she so chooses, and if you've crossed her bad enough. When the mage casts this spell, she chooses something the target will lose permanently, and by what means that will happen (uranium, wasps, true love's kiss, etc). For the spell's duration, everything possible will converge to make the loss come about; rolls to help bring the target's downfall add the spell's Potency to the dice pool, while rolls to hinder the downfall are penalized by the same amount.<br /> <br /> With this spell, a mage can kill a target, inflict a Persistent Condition or Tilt, or permanently remove access to a given merit (PCs targeted by this spell are still subject to the Sanctity of Merits, but cannot reallocate Experiences until the spell's duration expires). The means the mage chooses when casting the spell will play a pivotal role in the downfall: The target kisses the woman of his dreams, but it turns out he has a lethal allergy to a rare ingredient in her lipstick, or a calamitous misadventure involving a misplaced wasp nest leads to his impeachment from office.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the spell is meant to kill the target, the means of his death is treated as a Bane.<br /> <b>+1 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> Successful rolls to bring about the downfall are automatically exceptional successes; failed rolls to prevent the downfall are automatically dramatic failures.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 02-03-2018, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T11:27:37-08:00","id":1182028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182021#post1182021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Erase Name (Fate </b><b>4</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Politics, Streetwise<br /> <br /> This spell disconnects a target from one of his identities. When cast, the mage chooses one name the target is known by: This can be his sympathetic name, a nickname, an online handle, special title, or the like. For the spell's duration, no one can make the connection between the target and that name. Reduce a social merit connected to the name (such as Fame, Status, or Alternate Identity) by the spell's Potency. For as long as the identity is suppressed, the name cannot be used as a Sympathetic Yantra to cast spells on the subject. If the subject's sympathetic name is erased, the Withstand rating of spells cast on him does not increase from not knowing it. This spell can erase Shadow Names and the Shadow Name merit, but requires a point of mana to do so.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can split the spell's Potency among multiple social merits.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject also gains the Anonymity merit at a dot rating equal to the spell's Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I\u2019d actually have that as a Space spell since you\u2019re effectively eroding Sympathetic connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T11:40:29-08:00","id":1182033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182028#post1182028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I\u2019d actually have that as a Space spell since you\u2019re effectively eroding Sympathetic connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back and forth on that. There's some interesting (or odd) overlap between Space and Fate when it comes to sympathy. I was thinking of this spell as an extension of Fate's connection to the Name part of the soul. What I might do is reword it so that the subject can't make or be held to promises with that identity, to make it more distinct from Space's purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T11:46:28-08:00","id":1182035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182021#post1182021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some mean Fate Spells:<br /> <br /> <b>Downfall (Fate 5)<br /> Practice: </b>Making<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Larceny, Persuasion<br /> <br /> A Witch who wants you dead can do so much more than just blast you to smithereens. She can set up the entire world against you if she so chooses, and if you've crossed her bad enough. When the mage casts this spell, she chooses something the target will lose permanently, and by what means that will happen (uranium, wasps, true love's kiss, etc). For the spell's duration, everything possible will converge to make the loss come about; rolls to help bring the target's downfall add the spell's Potency to the dice pool, while rolls to hinder the downfall are penalized by the same amount.<br /> <br /> With this spell, a mage can kill a target, inflict a Persistent Condition or Tilt, or permanently remove access to a given merit (PCs targeted by this spell are still subject to the Sanctity of Merits, but cannot reallocate Experiences until the spell's duration expires). The means the mage chooses when casting the spell will play a pivotal role in the downfall: The target kisses the woman of his dreams, but it turns out he has a lethal allergy to a rare ingredient in her lipstick, or a calamitous misadventure involving a misplaced wasp nest leads to his impeachment from office.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the spell is meant to kill the target, the means of his death is treated as a Bane.<br /> <b>+1 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> Successful rolls to bring about the downfall are automatically exceptional successes; failed rolls to prevent the downfall are automatically dramatic failures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This, is why Fate is my favorite Arcanum for offensive magic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T06:36:31-08:00","id":1182244,"title":"","content":"One I've been playing around with a while, sort of updated to 2e:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>Supernal Block Model</i> (Fate 3, Prime 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Practice:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote skills:</b> Science, Philosophy<br /> <br /> The caster may select an axis on which his research is to be optimized. There are four choices: Mean, Modeled Deviation, Uncontrolled Deviation, and Sampling Precision. Modeled deviation means that the results will heavily skew towards the actual deviation of the modeled variables. Uncontrolled deviation means that the results will skew to clarify elements that should have gone into the model. (If more of these than potency exist, the results are muddled together.) Mean indicates that the more important variable is the mean of the examined population, so Fate conspires to make that the result. Sampling precision simply removes sampling error that is random and not indicative of the true reaction of the pool.<br /> <br /> This doesn't alter the traits of the elements studied and only has effect as long as the duration lasts, so the spell can only help while it is active. If the selection of the pool is made outside the effects, it won't skew the results in the selection, just in the variable factors such as sampling error. The best thing is to cast it and maintain the effect throughout the planning and execution of the study.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach (Reqs. Time 3):</b> With Reach, the spell can be made to work with a time effect and grant results along a different axis, as well. Each use of this effect requires an extra reach. If a timeline in which the effect never took place is desired, that requires reach, as well, to tell the effect to stand down. This only makes the spell mutable to temporal shenanigans, but it doesn't actually cause them. That requires a Combined Spell of some sort. Casting without this reach and combining them with the temporal effect can be done, but the results are distinct through the timelines, then, and not coordinated.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T06:57:31-08:00","id":1182249,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> Why the Prime component? It doesn\u2019t seem to actually do anything st first glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T00:34:28-08:00","id":1182518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182249#post1182249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> Why the Prime component? It doesn\u2019t seem to actually do anything st first glance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate manipulates probabilities pretty flexibly, so you could argue it could do this without any help, but I figure that isolating the <i>most true</i> result makes it kinda need a little Prime. That's all that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T02:53:22-08:00","id":1182526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182518#post1182518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate manipulates probabilities pretty flexibly, so you could argue it could do this without any help, but I figure that isolating the <i>most true</i> result makes it kinda need a little Prime. That's all that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don\u2019t see that as necessary. Your spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:03:42-08:00","id":1182656,"title":"","content":"what Arcana do you need to, for a joke, literally transmogrify a vampire into a pile of ash without using fire or the sun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:09:10-08:00","id":1182657,"title":"","content":"Death+Matter, both at 4, but won't necesarily be lethal and will get back to be a vampire after the duration runs out, wich for a joke I suppose is ideal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T11:47:38-08:00","id":1182671,"title":"","content":"Before I first posted, I considered making this work like Ban where you need other Arcana to lock in the spell. I rather like that notion, but it's messy to describe.<br /> <br /> Maybe drop Prime as a conjunctional requirement and move it to a Reach prerequisite. Something more like:<br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>Supernal Block Model</i> (Fate 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Practice:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote skills:</b> Science, Philosophy<br /> <br /> The caster selects a specific study and declares his intention to perform it to the fates. While the spell is active, chance conspires to minimize noise. Fortune favors the efforts.<br /> <br /> While the spell remains active the following benefits apply as lasting effects to a given stage, but only if performed while active: <br /> Selection of candidates tends towards a proper distribution of the sample. Treatments tend to be properly applied. The responses to the treatments tend towards typical for that sample. Together, this means that the research goes more smoothly than normal and are very close to the best possible results for the study performed. (logical errors and faulty assumptions are, unfortunately, intrinsic to the study defined and not subject to the benefits of this spell.)<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The spell reveals the primary source of uncontrolled deviation as a series of portents. These are often subtly encoded into the response statistics. One per Potency is revealed.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach (Reqs. Prime 4 or All applicable Arcana at 1):</b> The spell can be used to peer deeper into the nature of the topic at hand to reveal the results of the study on the population as well as the selected sample. The results remain limited by any flaws in the statistical model design, but no longer by the pool of test subjects and materials. The study still has the normal, optimized effects.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach (Reqs. Time 3):</b> With Reach, the spell can be made mutable to Time effects involving the specific investigation. Each use of this effect requires an extra reach, a bit like a charge. A spell might allow temporarily altering the past can be used to apply a different model to the study, using up one of the &quot;charges&quot; and revealing the altered results immediately. Casting this effect with this Reach option also permits use of future examinations such as Prophecy to use a charge and get significant feedback before the study is even run.</span> <hr /><br /> It occurs to me that the description could be thoroughly redone and this could be approached as a Mystery, unlocking the use of Mage Sight and Knowing effects on arbitrary scientific study. That would be extremely fitting for the Free Council, but be more like an attainment than a spell. If you do <i>that</i> the spell would functionally reduce to a simple good luck spell applied to a specific study. Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T15:29:50-08:00","id":1184110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1182671#post1182671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I first posted, I considered making this work like Ban where you need other Arcana to lock in the spell. I rather like that notion, but it's messy to describe.<br /> <br /> Maybe drop Prime as a conjunctional requirement and move it to a Reach prerequisite. Something more like: <hr /><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#008080\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>Supernal Block Model</i> (Fate 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Practice:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote skills:</b> Science, Philosophy<br /> <br /> The caster selects a specific study and declares his intention to perform it to the fates. While the spell is active, chance conspires to minimize noise. Fortune favors the efforts.<br /> <br /> While the spell remains active the following benefits apply as lasting effects to a given stage, but only if performed while active:<br /> Selection of candidates tends towards a proper distribution of the sample. Treatments tend to be properly applied. The responses to the treatments tend towards typical for that sample. Together, this means that the research goes more smoothly than normal and are very close to the best possible results for the study performed. (logical errors and faulty assumptions are, unfortunately, intrinsic to the study defined and not subject to the benefits of this spell.)<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The spell reveals the primary source of uncontrolled deviation as a series of portents. These are often subtly encoded into the response statistics. One per Potency is revealed.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach (Reqs. Prime 4 or All applicable Arcana at 1):</b> The spell can be used to peer deeper into the nature of the topic at hand to reveal the results of the study on the population as well as the selected sample. The results remain limited by any flaws in the statistical model design, but no longer by the pool of test subjects and materials. The study still has the normal, optimized effects.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach (Reqs. Time 3):</b> With Reach, the spell can be made mutable to Time effects involving the specific investigation. Each use of this effect requires an extra reach, a bit like a charge. A spell might allow temporarily altering the past can be used to apply a different model to the study, using up one of the &quot;charges&quot; and revealing the altered results immediately. Casting this effect with this Reach option also permits use of future examinations such as Prophecy to use a charge and get significant feedback before the study is even run.</span> <hr /><br /> It occurs to me that the description could be thoroughly redone and this could be approached as a Mystery, unlocking the use of Mage Sight and Knowing effects on arbitrary scientific study. That would be extremely fitting for the Free Council, but be more like an attainment than a spell. If you do <i>that</i> the spell would functionally reduce to a simple good luck spell applied to a specific study. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your call, it just feels a little bit redundant to have a specific spell just for research in this way when the Fate Arcanum is already filled with spells that boost ALL mundane actions that you can use, such as Quantum Flux or Exceptional Luck. It's like having a Rote to specifically boost one single aspect of a skill when you could just buy a Rote that can boost all skills for any use.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut also, some constructive criticism:<br /> \u200bThere are usually 3 suggested Rote Skills for every spell and Philosophy isn't a skill. I would suggest you use Academics, Investigation, Science as Rote Skills for this spell. Possibly Computer if you want a slightly less obvious but still relevant (I Think) skill for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T22:54:07-08:00","id":1192519,"title":"","content":"How many dots in space would you need to make it impossible from someone to hide? That is, anyone who wants to find the person knows where they are and what they are doing.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something along the lines of Pariah, from Fate 5, but the effects of the curse being that everyone trying to find you benefits from Know location and Perfect sympathy when acting against the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:36:52-08:00","id":1192534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1192519#post1192519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many dots in space would you need to make it impossible from someone to hide? That is, anyone who wants to find the person knows where they are and what they are doing.<br /> <br /> I was thinking something along the lines of Pariah, from Fate 5, but the effects of the curse being that everyone trying to find you benefits from Know location and Perfect sympathy when acting against the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could follow Pariah\u2019s example, and say the spell works by Unmaking the victim\u2019s personal space/private location, making them exposed to everyone at every distance. Dunno if this could be done with Unraveling, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T03:16:52-08:00","id":1192567,"title":"","content":"Makes me think of a weirdly inverted version of Empty Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T20:24:35-08:00","id":1194125,"title":"","content":"Why should Matter get all of the fun with the Golem spell?<br /> Death can already shape, and solidify shadows, why not animate them and turn them into servants?<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Servant</b><b> (Death </b><b>4</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Expression, Persuasion<br /> <br /> This spell animates, and hardens the shadow of a subject, turning it into a 3-dimensional physical servant under the Mage's control. Each level of Potency effectively grants the mage a dot of the Retainer Merit. The shadow servant\u2019s \u201cfield\u201d includes simple physical labor, combat, and other uncomplicated tasks. The servant is completely mindless, and can only execute whatever order the caster gave it last. Orders must be very simple. If attacked, the shadow has no Defense, but has a Durability of 2, and Structure equal to Durability + Size. The size of these shadows is equal to that of the phenomena which cast their shadow, and they take on the shape of these objects, but with a shadowy appearance and they cast no shadow of their own.<br /> <br /> In the case of normally inanimate object, so long as there could be some ambulatory movement were the shadow granted some degree of flexibility, then the servant is capable of movement. For example, the animated shadow of a chair could walk, a sword could crawl like a worm, a statute could walk, and a car could drive.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can reinforce the durability of their servants, splitting the spell's Potency between the Retainer merit, and increasing Durability, which will increase by 1 for each point of Potency distributed to it.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can change the size of the servant they create up to a maximum of the Scale factor of their spell. In such a way, the shadow of a Size 5 human could for example loom larger than life as a Size 20 servant.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: Bind a ghost or spirit into the servant to serve as an animating intelligence. The servant still uses its Retainer rating to determine dice pools, but the ephemeral being can use any of its powers, and the shadow\u2019s \u201cfield\u201d is whatever the entity is capable of.<br /> <b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: Create an intelligence from nothing that will guide the servant and inform its \u201cfield.\u201d See \u201cPsychic Genesis\u201d on p.159 for creating a mind from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Minor clarifications 03-10-2018, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T09:53:16-07:00","id":1198014,"title":"","content":"Would Death+Life 4 be sufficient to make a Vampire &quot;alive&quot;? Specifically able to conceive a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T10:04:00-07:00","id":1198018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1198014#post1198014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Death+Life 4 be sufficient to make a Vampire &quot;alive&quot;? Specifically able to conceive a child.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems vary reasonable to my understanding. However it can't be made lasting, that would be an Imperial practice, and most likely an offence to the Pax.<br /> Even though, the child would be a damphir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T03:44:20-07:00","id":1198991,"title":"","content":"My first attempt at a spell<b>.</b> Feedback welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Slapstick</b><b> ( Fate: 3</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Attack spell<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Crafts, Expression<br /> <br /> The core book doesn't have a Fate attack spell, so I thought of making one. Weird shit happens to people who mess with a Fate magus, from banana peels left on the floor to slip on to villains falling because they step on their shoe laces to being hit by a bird cage accidentally tossed out of a window.<br /> It causes potency bashing damage. In addition to that, witnesses of the scene get a +1 to their next social roll against the target because of the embarrassing silliness of it all, like &quot;Aren't you the guy who was run over by a toddler on a tricycle?&quot; (All attack spells seems to have a minor side effect like that, more cosmetic than relevant, really)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24034-spaghetti","name":"Spaghetti","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T04:11:49-07:00","id":1198999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaghetti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1198991#post1198991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first attempt at a spell<b>.</b> Feedback welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Slapstick</b><b> ( Fate: 3</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Attack spell<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Crafts, Expression<br /> <br /> The core book doesn't have a Fate attack spell, so I thought of making one. Weird shit happens to people who mess with a Fate magus, from banana peels left on the floor to slip on to villains falling because they step on their shoe laces to being hit by a bird cage accidentally tossed out of a window.<br /> It causes potency bashing damage. In addition to that, witnesses of the scene get a +1 to their next social roll against the target because of the embarrassing silliness of it all, like &amp;quot;Aren't you the guy who was run over by a toddler on a tricycle?&amp;quot; (All attack spells seems to have a minor side effect like that, more cosmetic than relevant, really)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the \u201cside effects\u201d involve Tilts representing falling over and losing balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T08:39:56-07:00","id":1199071,"title":"","content":"The social bonus should be a reach option.<br /> <br /> That said I personally handle fate as very indirect, needing to work through the fallen world rather than influencing patterns directly, so a spell like this (or shared fate for example) would in my games apply there effect at the earliest opportunity, allmost allways within the same scene (unless it is for some reason really really impossible), but not necessarily on the exact same turn. But that's just me and not RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:26:13-07:00","id":1199087,"title":"","content":"Look at Grave Misfortune. I'm not saying Slapstick would be a bad spell, but Grave Misfortune is what the writers chose to do instead of direct damage spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T09:44:55-07:00","id":1199093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaghetti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1198991#post1198991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practice: [/B]Attack spell</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no Practice: Attack Spell. You're going to want to change the Practice to one of the 3 that are available at three dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T10:33:25-07:00","id":1199108,"title":"","content":"Slapstick spell?<br /> Practice: Weaving, or maybe perfecting (who cares attack spells that cause bashing are three dots), but let's say weaving because that sounds like a convincing bit of metaphysical bullshitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24034-spaghetti","name":"Spaghetti","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T14:20:41-07:00","id":1199185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaghetti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1199108#post1199108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slapstick spell? Practice: Weaving, or maybe perfecting (who cares attack spells that cause bashing are three dots), but let's say weaving because that sounds like a convincing bit of metaphysical bullshitting</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to maintain setting metaphysics if you use the language the game provides, so when talking about Practices to use one of the 13 established Practices, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T04:25:27-07:00","id":1199980,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sum of All Parts (Prime 2)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice</b>: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Veiling</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor</b>: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craft, Stealth, Subterfuge</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spell masks the connection of an item with its Supernal idea, which makes recognizing its purpose impossible. A table becomes a flat surface raised on four legs; a car is perceived as a metal contraption on wheels. Other people can still try to improvise and deduce properties of the occluded item: if something has wheels, for example, it almost certainly can be pushed around. Using it effectively, however, is nearly impossible - a fencer may still wield a sword as an improvised cutting weapon, but it doesn\u2019t give him more advantage than a sharp piece of metal would.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This provides an opportunity to hide a weapon in plain sight, or make a piece of contraband pass a casual search. This still carries a risk - the airport security guard may still react with suspicion, seeing someone with a steel cylindrical implement in their hands. A careful examination of an item (which may require dismantling) lets someone sufficiently curious determine what the item actually is. For a Sleeper, this almost always triggers Disbelief. Seeing the veiled tool actually work as intended may have the same effect.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spell also connects the object with the Supernal idea of decoration. This lets the mage blend the item with their clothes or home appliances - a bomb displayed proudly on the table is just a weird-looking knick-knack.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Allows an object to pass for another one: a sword may look perfectly normal on a dinner table when it registers as cutlery.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","user":"Gantolandon","date":". 03-27-2018, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13425-gantolandon","name":"Gantolandon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T04:45:18-07:00","id":1199985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gantolandon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1199980#post1199980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sum of All Parts (Prime 2)</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool spell, but I'd add a mana cost similar to Mind's Incognito Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T01:05:58-07:00","id":1201873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gantolandon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1199980#post1199980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sum of All Parts (Prime 2)</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:15:48-07:00","id":1202889,"title":"","content":"While others might just use Veiling to disguise their extravagent clothing, armour, or weaponry, I've thought of another spell which might help in seeming inconspicuous. Rely on your clothing. It's just another tool to use, and Matter can enhance tools.<br /> <br /> <b>Clothes Make the Man (Matter </b><b>\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> All tools carry within them the symbols of their purpose, and all clothing carries with it the symbolic purpose of expressing a certain persona. By drawing upon that symbology and bringing it to the forefront, the Mage can let their clothing speak for them. So long as the spell\u2019s Potency exceeds the Composure of any witness, any wearer of the subject article/suit of clothing cannot be identified by any others in a persona that does not naturally accommodate the subject article/suit.<br /> In such a way, while a person in a police officer\u2019s uniform may act completely out of character for a police officer, any witnesses who do not Withstand the spell will merely see the subject as being horribly unprofessional, rather than being duplicitous about his identity. This is not flawless however, as symbolism can be interpreted in different ways. Where one law abiding citizen might see a police officer as a symbol of benevolent authority, another might see them as a corrupt pillar of a tyrannical organization. In addition, at its base, this does not provide any benefit to social interaction beyond that which would be provided by acknowledgement of the individual\u2019s identity.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>This spell can accommodate for \u2018imperfections\u2019 in the appearance of a suit of clothing. The dirty, unwashed nature of a subject\u2019s suit may be disregarded, or the \u2018fake\u2019 police uniform of a kissogram or entertainer might be looked past by any witness who cannot Withstand the spell's Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> When undertaking a social action against individuals who have not seen past the symbology of the subject\u2019s clothing, the subject gains a bonus to all social tests in keeping with that symbolism equal to the spell\u2019s Potency (based on how much it exceeds their Composure)<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>When casting the spell, the caster may specify a single aspect of the subject\u2019s symbolism to enhance above all others. In this way, rather than being seen as an authority figure, or as a suspicious entity, the wearer of the classic 90s black suit and shades combo might be ignored as merely another faceless drone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T01:44:58-07:00","id":1202911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1202889#post1202889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clothes Make the Man (Matter [/B]<b>\u2022\u2022)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. But wouldn\u2019t it be better to model it after Incognito Presence so that it costs 1 Mana but auto-succeeds in the disguises? At least, that\u2019s how I see Withstand rules working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T01:56:33-07:00","id":1202914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1202911#post1202911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome. But wouldn\u2019t it be better to model it after Incognito Presence so that it costs 1 Mana but auto-succeeds in the disguises? At least, that\u2019s how I see Withstand rules working.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want, I prefer it this way given that the spell isn't ultimately on the person, but their clothing.<br /> <br /> If you're composed enough, you should be able to push past the message their clothing is screaming at you, and realize that they're not who their clothes says they are.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*<br /> Also the focus on Potency ties nicely into the Reach effect that grants a dice pool bonus to social actions when you act in the projected persona.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 04-04-2018, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T03:24:04-07:00","id":1202932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1202914#post1202914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want, I prefer it this way given that the spell isn't ultimately on the person, but their clothing.<br /> <br /> If you're composed enough, you should be able to push past the message their clothing is screaming at you, and realize that they're not who their clothes says they are.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*<br /> Also the focus on Potency ties nicely into the Reach effect that grants a dice pool bonus to social actions when you act in the projected persona.</div> </div> </div> </div>Withstand only applies to the direct target of the spell.<br /> <br /> I think it would be better to model this spell on Alter Mental Pattern with Potency going to creating a bonus on rolls boosted by Disguise equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T03:50:37-07:00","id":1202937,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I thought I'd messed something up when I was writing that first Reach option, but I couldn't put my finger on what.<br /> Ah well, going to scrap the idea because at that point you're either really just using a tool-boosting spell, or Hidden Hoard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T04:33:15-07:00","id":1204831,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Agonizing Intent</i></b><br /> <i>Life (Compelling)</i><br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstood: Stamina<br /> <br /> Each Potency inflicts a cumulative -1 wound penalty as all the nerves and receptive cells in a subject behave incorrectly (misfiring, or other inconveniences causing great pain)<br /> <br /> <b>1 Reach:</b> Can go above the usual -3 limit.<br /> <b>2 Reach + Time 4: </b>Inflict this agony retroactively from a point of their lives (can be as simple as when they were born) If they know you're the cause gain the potency as a bonus to rolls (# of rolls equal to potency) to coerce or intimidate the subject while the wound penalties are in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T06:40:05-07:00","id":1204844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1204831#post1204831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Agonizing Intent</i></b><br /> <i>Life (Compelling)</i><br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstood: Stamina<br /> <br /> Each Potency inflicts a cumulative -1 wound penalty as all the nerves and receptive cells in a subject behave incorrectly (misfiring, or other inconveniences causing great pain)<br /> <br /> <b>1 Reach:</b> Can go above the usual -3 limit.<br /> <b>2 Reach + Time 4: </b>Inflict this agony retroactively from a point of their lives (can be as simple as when they were born) If they know you're the cause gain the potency as a bonus to rolls (# of rolls equal to potency) to coerce or intimidate the subject while the wound penalties are in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is beyond the effects of Compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T06:50:41-07:00","id":1204847,"title":"","content":"Agreed. At least when it comes to inflicting wound penalties. Instead you should be able to worsen existing wound penalties or lower the threshold for when wound penalties apply, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:25:31-07:00","id":1204901,"title":"","content":"I wrote that first thing in the morning with a combat scenario in my head. Just about all living things have a system of nerves or other phenomenon that tell them when something distinctly bad is happening. (Flight or fight, pain, and in the opposite direction dopamine and serotonin) a weaving or patterning work could easily take those pieces and make them haywire. A ruling spell could do it on existing systems since it can make them act against their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T10:34:29-07:00","id":1204906,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a> you probably can make it work as Compelling, if you cast the spell on a person already suffering from wound penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T13:48:29-07:00","id":1206151,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Pythagorean's Razor</b></i><br /> Space (Ruling)<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: <i>Athletics, Firearms, Academics</i><br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Essentially &quot;Quantum Flux&quot; but with Space - pinching it, bending it, calculating ranges and angles, calculating away deleterious factors, instead of any mundane actions it's specifically actions that could benefit from having the distance of travel reduced or the vector nudged to &quot;slightly unnatural&quot; accuracy.<br /> Mainly for ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Gladiator's Glare</b></i><br /> Life (Ruling)<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Athletics, Brawl, Firearms<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> The Potency of this spell is applied as a bonus to your next physical roll provided you aim for a turn sacrificing your defense beforehand. Similar to Perfect Timing but in this case it's tuning your senses (including your kinesthetic sense) alongside your reflexes, adrenaline, and any other subtle bodily processes to the task.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Fake Ephemera</b></i><br /> Space (Weaving)<br /> Similar to Ban, or other spells that play with the properties of space - only this time it's you or your subject. While under the effects of this spell you can't interact physically with the world or vice versa. You can still sense and speak and move around, but objects appear to pass through you effortlessly.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Blunt Blessing</i></b><br /> Life (Perfecting)<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Gain Potency as temporary health for the duration of the spell. Not the same as granting attribute dots or anything drastic, just increasing a trait for a while that might buy you some precious time between you and the great beyond. Likely requires a reach and 1 mana to even use since your health is by nature at it's &quot;cap&quot;<br /> <br /> Would it be reasonable to say, for 2 reach change &quot;add/subtract&quot; to &quot;multiply/divide&quot; for the spell &quot;Ground Eater&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-13-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:05:36-07:00","id":1206187,"title":"","content":"I've been tossing around the idea of introducing a spell like this to my game as a 'quest reward' for the completion of the current story-arc. Has this been done before and/or am I opening a can of worms by breaking the action economy?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Spell Steal</b></i><br /> <i>Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Patterning)</i><br /> <i>Primary Factor: Duration</i><br /> <i>Withstand: Arcanum Rating of target spell</i><br /> <i>Cost: 1 mana (Not sure about this)</i><br /> <br /> Instead of merely dispelling a spell the mage takes control of an active spell as though they were the one to cast it. (i.e. takes up spell control slots).<br /> <br /> +1 reach: Alternatively, the mage can use the spell to switch the targets of an active spell or a spell being cast (e.g. a spell that drains the life of everyone in the area will instead funnel the life of the original caster towards everyone in the area).<br /> <br /> The mage must be able to perceive the spell either through active Mage Sight or other means.<br /> <br /> Time \u2022\u2022; +2 Reach; 1 Mana: The spell can be cast reflexively.<br /> Spirit \u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022\u2022, Death \u2022\u2022: The spell can now steal Numina from the relevant ephemeral entity (Withstand changes to Rank. Cannot be used on Rank 6+) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T16:14:19-07:00","id":1206190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1206187#post1206187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been tossing around the idea of introducing a spell like this to my game as a 'quest reward' for the completion of the current story-arc. Has this been done before and/or am I opening a can of worms by breaking the action economy?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Spell Steal</b></i><br /> <i>Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (Patterning)</i><br /> <i>Primary Factor: Duration</i><br /> <i>Withstand: Arcanum Rating of target spell</i><br /> <i>Cost: 1 mana (Not sure about this)</i><br /> <br /> Instead of merely dispelling a spell the mage takes control of an active spell as though they were the one to cast it. (i.e. takes up spell control slots).<br /> <br /> +1 reach: Alternatively, the mage can use the spell to switch the targets of an active spell or a spell being cast (e.g. a spell that drains the life of everyone in the area will instead funnel the life of the original caster towards everyone in the area).<br /> <br /> The mage must be able to perceive the spell either through active Mage Sight or other means.<br /> <br /> Time \u2022\u2022; +2 Reach; 1 Mana: The spell can be cast reflexively.<br /> Spirit \u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022\u2022, Death \u2022\u2022: The spell can now steal Numina from the relevant ephemeral entity (Withstand changes to Rank. Cannot be used on Rank 6+) <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Had a similar idea a while ago when thinking about the Timori. Didn\u2019t fully write it, but it was a Prime spell/Attainment that involved assuming Spell Control of relinquished spells. As a spell, Mind 4 could be added to wrest control of a spell still inside someone else\u2019s Spell Control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T17:15:32-07:00","id":1206729,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Feral Grit</b></i><br /> Life (Perfecting)<br /> Suggest Rote Skills: Athletics, Brawl, Survival<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Normally you're defense is reduced by 1 per attack after the first. Add the potency of this spell to the number of attacks before you suffer a penalty as you manipulate your reflexes and senses to respond with the speed of an animal, impulsive and unhindered by slow, rational assessment.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Interpose</i></b><br /> Space (Weaving)<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Take damage in place of another at the caster's choice a number of times up to Potency while the spell lasts by manipulating space between the &quot;supposed point of impact&quot; and the subject. This only works for melee and ranged combat. Spells cast for direct damage can't have their wounds redirected.<br /> 1 reach + Prime 3 - can redirect damage spells.<br /> 2 reach - cast this spell reflexively<br /> <br /> <b><i>Duplicate</i></b><br /> Time (Making)<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> For a number of actions equal to potency, create a small temporal warp the span of seconds in which time repeats itself for a subject.<br /> Any duplicated action performed by the subject will be doubled<br /> as though they had performed the action twice.<br /> Any expenditure required by the repeated action must<br /> be paid for twice, and any penalties accrued by that<br /> action will be inflicted twice.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Actaeon's Blessing</i></b><br /> Space (Perfecting)<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> This spell grants 8-agains to ranged attack rolls equal to potency.<br /> <br /> 1 reach - For one point of Mana, the object grants the rote<br /> action quality on a number of ranged attack rolls equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.<br /> As long as the spell\u2019s Duration lasts, the subject may spend one<br /> point of Mana at any time to \u201crecharge\u201d this effect, granting<br /> the rote action quality on an additional number of rolls equal<br /> to the spell\u2019s Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-15-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:59:04-07:00","id":1207229,"title":"","content":"Hi guys ! Just a reminder that I keep uploading finalized rotes in the Google doc <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H0BBs20Ta-9RKnWirld02c8GiWoRGU5gTb9QvljIOCw/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Don't hesitate to check it out and say if I missed something !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T19:50:04-07:00","id":1207491,"title":"","content":"Okay, this spell is funky. People have been wanting to get Lasting matter transmutations.<br /> And really, given the Free Council's methodology, here's how I thought it should go.<br /> It'll either requires Forces 3, Matter 3, and an advanced understanding of Science, and some time to kill.<br /> Or Forces 4, Matter 4, and a general idea of what you're doing.<br /> <br /> <b>Subatomic Matter Suspension (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Durability<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Investigation, Science<br /> Modern science teaches that atoms are constitued of various sub-atomic particles, and that the phenomenal expression of the nature of matter is defined by how many of these particles, and in what proportions they are combined. Through an advanced understanding of the relationship between Matter and Energy (Forces), a Mage may learn how to temporarily weaken the forces holding together both atoms, and mollecules, allowing enhanced flow of atoms, and subatomic particles, while maintaining the cohesion of the subject-matter.<br /> In mechanical terms, should the spell affect a physical substance, then any Science or Crafts roll relating to its use as a reactive element will be provided a dice pool bonus equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, and a Point of Mana: </b>Beyond merely ensuring the increased reactivity of a substance, the Mage may weaken the bonds between atoms in such a matter that he may, with the use of other Magic, transfer sub-atomic particles throughout the subject matter, effectively unlocking the nucleus of the atom and allowing an entirely 'mundane' transformation of matter from one element into another. In such a manner, lead might be turned into gold, ashes into diamonds, or air into helium, just to name a few applications.<br /> To do this requires either a Matter 4, Forces 4 Patterning spell to wholly rearrange the structure of the subject matter, and a Potency equal to the durability of the Matter you seek to craft, or a Matter 1, Forces 1 Compelling spell and an extended Intelligence + Science spell (as well as Forces 2 &quot;Zoom In&quot; with the Reach effect for mollecular bond levels to see what you're doing), achieving a set number of successes as set by the ST. The ST should feel free to set the number of successes equal to the complexity of what is to be created.<br /> The interval for this test should be no shorter than 1 hour. Invariably there will be 'runoff' particles that are not usable to create more of whatever you are intending to make, these can usually be safely released from the structure of the subject as your extended test continues, with minimal side effects.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Yes, there's an argument that the requirements could be lower. No, I don't think they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T09:48:03-07:00","id":1207684,"title":"","content":"Another approach to lasting transfiguration would be to have said transfiguration be a side effect of the magic, and not the direct result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:18:37-07:00","id":1207768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1207684#post1207684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another approach to lasting transfiguration would be to have said transfiguration be a side effect of the magic, and not the direct result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or do what everyone else does and cast it as indefinite duration then relinquish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:44:46-07:00","id":1207782,"title":"","content":"However that requires expenditure of a Willpower Dot, which is equivalent to an experience, and can be dispelled.<br /> <br /> Also having the transfiguration be a side effect of the Magic is exactly what I did.<br /> The spell enables the movement of sub-atomic particles.<br /> End that spell, and they stay where they are, in the new atoms.<br /> <br /> A comparison would be the State Change spell.<br /> Turn a steel block into liquid, and it will lose its original shape and turn into a puddle of steel on the ground.<br /> End the spell, and it remains a puddle, but returns to its solid state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 04-16-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T20:18:11-07:00","id":1207854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1207768#post1207768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or do what everyone else does and cast it as indefinite duration then relinquish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the flaws there involve vulnerability to dispellation, and either an experience cost (willpower dot) or the chance that your magic is going to wreak havoc on the material and everything surrounding it as time passes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T03:55:53-07:00","id":1207924,"title":"","content":"I figure if the devs wanted lasting transmutation they'd have put it in like the scribe Grimoire spell. Assuming this fits in your setting, why not just make it a 2 or 3 reach option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-18-2018, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T04:50:33-07:00","id":1207936,"title":"","content":"The Scribe Grimoire example is different, because the existence and proliferation of Grimoires throughout Mage society works on the assumption that you don't need to spend a Willpower dot to relinquish them, or you can only maintain a number at a time.<br /> <br /> Also sure you can just add a +2 Reach option to Matter 4's Tramutation spell.<br /> But that's incredibly boring.<br /> <br /> I wanted to add a bit of a reward for someone reaching second degree Disciple-dom with a strong scientific Praxis, or second degree Adept-hood and a general idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T04:57:50-07:00","id":1207938,"title":"","content":"Been a long time since I've done this; my take on Prime illusion spells:<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Beholder</b><b> (Prime 2</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> The Arcanum of Prime holds domain over truth itself, but in this Fallen World truth is not so absolute as it is in the Supernal. This spell veils a particular truth of an object from detection, suppressing the ability of others to be able to acknowledge that truth. With this spell, a mage could veil a person's identity such that people seeing them would only know that it is &quot;a person&quot; without being able to acknowledge or recognize the person even if they are intimately familiar with them. They could veil the remote control to a particular television, causing people to disregard it as belonging to some other device. On a more sinister note, a mage could veil faulty wiring or a weak floor to make it seem functional. This is an incredibly delicate and subtle spell, and does not hold up to dedicated scrutiny. Recorded media in particular do not carry the effects of this spell, and a person or object veiled in such a way is still recognizable to anyone who would know it.<br /> <br /> <b>From a Certain Point of View</b><b> (Prime 3</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> Truth is malleable in this world, especially in the hands of the willworker. This spell weaves an object's truth into another form, making one thing seem like another of the same general type and size. The illusion weaved by this spell affects all senses but doesn't hold up to actual use. A stick could be made to look like a sturdy club and will feel like a sturdy club right up until it's used, at which point it'll break just like a stick. Living (and undead) creatures cannot be the target of this spell; their constant sense of self instantly erodes any attempt at changing their truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Well Now You're Just Screwing With Me</b><b> (Prime 4</b><b>)<br /> Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> A philosophy professor asks his class to disprove the existence of a chair for their final grade. Sleeping students will frantically attempt to enact such a feat using complex ideologies while the Awakened philosopher merely asks, &quot;What chair?&quot; The mage transforms an object's truth into some other truth, transforming the object in all but a real sense. The applications of this spell are manifold, but none are lasting. Any attempt to truly interact with a transformed object beyond cursory examinations instantly ends the spell, with objective reality snapping the object's truth back into place. A mage could make a chair seem like a refrigerator, but any attempt to open the fridge will result in a person swinging a chair around. Simply seeing the refrigerator or touching it won't do it, but leaning against it or hitting it will. Living (and undead) creatures cannot be the target of this spell; their constant sense of self instantly erodes any attempt at changing their truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","user":"Frishman","date":"adjusted Prime 3 version to not be applicable to living objects. 04-17-2018, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T07:27:05-07:00","id":1208430,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is a version of the &quot;True love&quot; spell from silver ladder. Originally it was a 5 dot effect, but i stripped out most of the &quot;functions&quot; of it, and added them back as reach options.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oath of Friendship (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Weaving</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Potency</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand: Composure</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Socialize, Persuasion, Politics</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spell sanctifies an existing bond of friendship, giving it supernatural depth. All subjects of the spell gain the benefits of The True friend with respect to each other. If a subject of the spell is turned against the others, they suffer a Hex. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As long as the spell is within spell control, the caster of the spell knows which of the subjects are benefitting from the spell, and which of their number has gotten a hex.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: If a subject enters the oath with false feelings of friendship, they suffer a Hex instead of the benefits of the spell.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The subjects the spell also know which of their number have gotten a hex.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The subjects of the spell are aware if one of the participants dies.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+0 Reach: When cast with exactly two participants that already have the true Friend merit, the spell grants the Loved merit. This variation is usually called \u201cTrue love\u201d.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: The subjects may spend Willpower on behalf of each other. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: Damage received by one subject is shared equally between the subjects of the spell.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: Supernatural effects that would turn one subject against the others cause a clash of wills.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T11:28:49-07:00","id":1208956,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Prime 2 Life 1 : Liar's mark<br /> Practice : Ruling/unveiling</b><br /> P<b>rimary factor Duration<br /> Withstand by composure<br /> Suggested rote skills : medecine, empathy, survival</b><br /> By linking his mind to the estatic truth of the primal wilds, the subject eyes are more alert o the telltale signs of lies and the is more quick to catch up on body language, the subject gains the informed condition for the purpose of determining what are the reasons of a person for lying to him.<br /> <b>+1 reach</b> the mage remove social doors equal to the potency of the spells as his body is in tune with his victim in a primal level<br /> <b>+1 reach and 1 mana </b>: the mage knows what are his vicitms lies and impose the guilty or leveraged condition<br /> <b>+1 reach and 1 mana : </b>the mage brand the subject with an invisible rune marking the victim as a liar, thus lowering by one impression level of the victim by level of potency</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 04-19-2018, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:27:00-07:00","id":1209216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1208956#post1208956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prime 2 Life 1 : Liar's mark<br /> Practice : Ruling/unveiling</span></span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, spells only have one practice. This should be Unveiling or Knowing (there's no reason for Prime 2), that said...<br /> <br /> This doesn't fit any of Life's purviews, and though Prime's purview is Truth, there's already a Prime spell that does something similar. If you want to know someone's <i>reasons </i>for lying, you'd be better off with Prime 1 / Fate 1, since intent falls under Fate. I can see the desire to add Life to explain how the subject is processing the information they receive (instinctual awareness of body language) but Second Edition has entirely eliminated secondary arcana for that purpose - Knowing &amp; Unveiling spells already allow you to fully interpret the information you receive by default.<br /> <br /> The branding should probably be a separate spell. It's the only part of the spell that requires a higher level of Arcana, and doesn't actually seem that linked to the other effects of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 04-20-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:15:29-07:00","id":1209232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209216#post1209216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, spells only have one practice. This should be Unveiling or Knowing (there's no reason for Prime 2), that said...<br /> <br /> This doesn't fit any of Life's purviews, and though Prime's purview is Truth, there's already a Prime spell that does something similar. If you want to know someone's <i>reasons </i>for lying, you'd be better off with Prime 1 / Fate 1, since intent falls under Fate. I can see the desire to add Life to explain how the subject is processing the information they receive (instinctual awareness of body language) but Second Edition has entirely eliminated secondary arcana for that purpose - Knowing &amp; Unveiling spells already allow you to fully interpret the information you receive by default.<br /> <br /> The branding should probably be a separate spell. It's the only part of the spell that requires a higher level of Arcana, and doesn't actually seem that linked to the other effects of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hum i tought adding life for the first reach maked sense, but the idea of the brand was more a thematic reaction to the effect of the spells. So does the spell makes no sense or is it just inneficient and coule be done with less arcana ? I liked the life part because it fits the thrysus theme, attuning your body language and chemistry with those of the subject of the spell to know more about them, knowing someone emotional state of level of stress fits with Life theme","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:54:44-07:00","id":1209245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209232#post1209232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hum i tought adding life for the first reach maked sense, but the idea of the brand was more a thematic reaction to the effect of the spells. So does the spell makes no sense or is it just inneficient and coule be done with less arcana ? I liked the life part because it fits the thrysus theme, attuning your body language and chemistry with those of the subject of the spell to know more about them, knowing someone emotional state of level of stress fits with Life theme</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make yourself hyper-sensitive to another person\u2019s body language and chemistry with just Life if that\u2019s the effect you want, you don\u2019t need Prime. It probably wouldn\u2019t tell you for sure if someone was lying though, probably just a die bonus on lie detection rolls. It also wouldn\u2019t reveal why someone is lying.<br /> <br /> Prime by itself can tell you if someone is lying automatically, but also can\u2019t tell you why, I agree with @Inodiv that would be better handled with Fate.<br /> <br /> The brand Reach I also agree should be a different spell, probably Prime 3. Technicall, invisible runes are Prime 2, but only Mages would react to that.<br /> <br /> Taking a look at just the spell, it can be done better with fewer arcana, and should be split into more than one spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:23:31-07:00","id":1209260,"title":"","content":"Well you need at least a practice of two to create most mundane condition, and the spell words of truth can affect non mage on a soul deep level, that was what i was tryingnto emulate with the brand reach but yeah i kinda see why i should be another spell","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:27:06-07:00","id":1209263,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear i'm not arguing against you, it's just my first spell and i kinda want to know why it don't work for you guys, the life aspect is really here for the first reach and the thematic aspect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:30:17-07:00","id":1209267,"title":"","content":"The first Reach ought to just be a Life spell by itself. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a great idea to add arcana requirements to a spell just so you can throw in a neat Reach effect. If you\u2019re thinking of doing it then the Reach effect is probably better off as a separate spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:38:15-07:00","id":1209270,"title":"","content":"Isn't that what spell why multiples arcana are for ? More tailored and diverse effect balanced by the fact you need to invest in multiple arcanum ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:42:00-07:00","id":1209271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209270#post1209270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that what spell why multiples arcana are for ? More tailored and diverse effect balanced by the fact you need to invest in multiple arcanum ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the Reach effect shouldn\u2019t be doing something the base spell isn\u2019t doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:57:41-07:00","id":1209276,"title":"","content":"The base spells attune your body to those of the others and to truth , that don't seem to far fetched to add a reach to attune your body even more to those of the subject, <br /> <br /> Lots of spell in the base book have reach effect that does something the base spell isn't doing, i tought that was the point of reaching, Like reaching with spirit summon helps you control spirits, or the reach in alter conductivity wich let you alter other forms of forces withtout the Force arcana, or that by adding force to state change you can transmute plasma, or like reaching with Fool rush in, allow you to modify your spellcasting pool even though you didn't add Prime, again, just trying to understand i'm a noob to Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:08:47-07:00","id":1209279,"title":"","content":"Icarus' plight<br /> Life (unraveling or unmaking)<br /> Regeneration, inverted. Can do lethal damage with a reach but I'd mainly used to cripple foes in a direct way<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:10:28-07:00","id":1209280,"title":"","content":"In addition to what's been raised so far - spells should pretty much do one thing (even some of the core spells abuse this a bit [Looking at you, Fate]), and the reach effects should be tuned towards doing that same thing but differently or better.<br /> <br /> This spell:<br /> 1) Tells you when someone is lying and why<br /> 2) Freely opens doors in SM<br /> 3) Imposes Conditions<br /> 4) Gives them a social debuff.<br /> <br /> The subject of the spell isn't consistent. The description describes that the subject is the person that gets the extra knowledge about people lying to them, but then:<br /> Reach 1: The mage is opening doors to the victim...because he helped them tell when people are lying? It doesn't really make sense as written<br /> Reach 2: This is written as if the subject is the person doing the lying, not the person that gains insight into lies. Which is it?<br /> Reach 3: Same issue as Reach 2<br /> <br /> A lot of this stuff doesn't really fall in the purviews of these Arcana either. Most of this should be Mind or Fate. That doesn't mean you <i>can't</i> use other Arcana, but you should approach it carefully. I'd split this up into a bunch of different spells, personally.<br /> <br /> 1) Add a Fate \u2022 +1 Reach effect to Pierce Deception, that informs you of the intent behind the deception<br /> 2) For your Life themes, here's an alternative:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Societal Adaptation (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Socialize, Subterfuge</b><br /> All of human interaction is underwritten by a constant stream of instinctual responses and unconscious ticks - our society is as much a product of our biology as it is a product of the mind. A Disciple of Life can enhance the social instincts that drive her subject, making her keenly (and consciously) aware of the subtle body language that drives human interaction. This spell provides its subject a bonus on all social rolls to detect a living human\u2019s intentions equal to Potency, for a number of rolls equal to Potency. This also applies to rolls to detect lies.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> In addition to enhancing instincts and perception, this spell affords the subject some conscious control over their own body language and microexpressions. The bonus may also be applies to rolls to mask one\u2019s own intentions, or to other social actions at Storyteller discretion.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> 3) For your brand/social debuff thing:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Brand of the Deceiver (Prime \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Empathy, Socialize</b><br /> The world listens when an arbiter of Truth proclaims the guilt of a deceiver. An Apprentice of Prime is capable of placing a Rune, visible only to those with Mage Sight, on a subject with the Guilty Condition that clearly marks them as a liar or a traitor. What\u2019s more, although non-Mages cannot see the rune, its Supernal Truth leaks into the subject\u2019s pattern regardless, causing them to start any social maneuvering attempt at one impression level lower than they normally would.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell may be replaced on a subject without the Guilty Condition, so long as the caster knows they have lied about something within the current scene. Note that it has to be a lie - simply being factually incorrect won\u2019t allow the use of this Reach effect.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> As the above Reach effect, but the subject also gains the Guilty Condition.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not actually a huge fan of either of those spells and would not use them in my game - they seem like they're trying to hard to step into the domain of other Arcana to me (namely, Mind), but if you want to stick to Prime and Life, I'd have the spells look something like that. They took about 5 minutes each, so with a decent amount of tuning, the issues of thematic overstep could probably be resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:40:04-07:00","id":1209319,"title":"","content":"Hum okay that makes sense thanks for clarifying that for me, but yes these spells could also be in the domain of mind but then again, you got multiple ways to cast the same spell with different arcanas, but as Prime as the purview of revelations, i tought adding the informed condition without fate could be acceptable, it's more like you are informed to guessing why they lie to you, dunno is that makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":