ubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T12:16:45-07:00","id":1209348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209344#post1209344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought you could by altering body chemistry, but okay, tanks everyone and very sorry it derailed</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it didn't derail. Discussions like this are why the thread exists.<br /> <br /> One thing to remember is that magic operates off of symbolism, not science or physics or biology. You can definitely provoke emotional reactions with Life (see 'Control Instincts') but there's some level of nuance to be grasped in how that will actually manifest compared to using Mind outright (compare to Emotional Urging from Mind).<br /> <br /> Back to your original spell, focusing on Revelation as an aspect of Prime totally works - but then we're back to 'why do you actually have Life in the spell?'<br /> Also, don't forget the Combined Spells exist, and these are the go-to whenever you're trying to create a spell with multiple distinct effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank"