on?p=1209474#post1209474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why ? Are the arcana weirdly mixed up ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's no reason to mix them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:04:12-07:00","id":1209479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209476#post1209476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because there's no reason to mix them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reach is reason enough no ? I mean at this point and with what you guys have been saying i'm beginning to think spell with multiple arcana aren't even a thing anymore. Just to be clear, i'm not trying to be a pain in the ass, just trying to understand, even if there is no other mechanic reason, thematic one should be good enough no ? Mage are defined by what kind of spells they cast, no ? Sorry again and thanks you guys for taking the time to explain all the mage stuff to little poor old me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 04-20-2018, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:05:14-07:00","id":1209480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209474#post1209474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why ? Are the arcana weirdly mixed up ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie said it. I think Spirit could be used to enhance the certain ways the object could be used (unlike Matter, which just flat-out enhances the object itself), which is where the Skill dot bonus could apply. Prime could be where the Informed Condition comes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:07:43-07:00","id":1209482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209479#post1209479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reach is reason enough no ? I mean at this point and with what you guys have been saying i'm beginning to think spell with multiple arcana aren't even a thing anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Conjunctional Arcana spells are rarer, yes, but still a thing looking at some of the Signs of Sorcery previews. I think the line is not \u201cCan the spell work with this combination of Arcana?\u201d and \u201cDoes this spell really need all these Arcana?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:11:18-07:00","id":1209483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209465#post1209465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this one will be at least passable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !<br /> <br /> <b>Know thy tool (Prime \u2022\u2022/Spirit \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice : Rulling<br /> Primary factor : Duration<br /> Wisthood by : Rank<br /> Suggester rotes skills : Investigation, occult , empathy</b><br /> Prime is the realm of truth, resonance and revaltion, but by reading both the resonance and the essence of spirit being inhabiting he innanimate and gaining its cooperation<br /> the mage can pick and object and knows it innermost nature and workings and gains the informed condition relating to the use of the object<br /> <b>+1 reach </b>if the mage doesn't have any dots in the skill required to use the object (such as a scapel for medecine) the mage gains a bonus dice equal to the potency of the spell (this bonus does not negate the penalty for not having said skill)<br /> <b>+1 reach</b> If the object is a weapon, the mage instead gains a weapon modifier, if it's an armor, the mage lessen the penalty to speed or defense equal to the spell potency</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would do it like this though.<br /> <br /> <b>Understand the Platonic Form (Prime </b>\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice : Ruling<br /> Primary factor : Potency<br /> Suggester rotes skills : Academics, Crafts, Expression</b><br /> <br /> The Aether is where the platonic forms exists, and fallen objects are mere flawed versions of perfect symbols. However, objects are still these symbols given flawed form in Fallen reality and this spell allows the mage to perceive its true symbolism and align the object more closely to its symbol and by doing so getting a clearer understanding of the use of the object. <br /> This spell gives the user of the object the 9-again quality for rolls to use the object for a number of rolls equal to Potency for the Duration.<br /> +1 reach: gets the 8-again quality. <br /> +1 reach: the user gets the Informed condition about the use and function of the item.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:21:17-07:00","id":1209487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209482#post1209482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conjunctional Arcana spells are rarer, yes, but still a thing looking at some of the Signs of Sorcery previews. I think the line is not \u201cCan the spell work with this combination of Arcana?\u201d and \u201cDoes this spell really need all these Arcana?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame, i really like spell that use two arcana to achieve something, i didn't thought it was an overpowered spell as you would need two arcana to cast it and it's still basicly one effect so it's not really a combined spell , would really like some guidelines for spell that use multiple arcanum, like in the preview on grimoire, Living Grimoire (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) doesn't really need life at this level to scribe supernal runes into a living being, does it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:25:08-07:00","id":1209488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209487#post1209487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a shame, i really like spell that use two arcana to achieve something, i didn't thought it was an overpowered spell as you would need two arcana to cast it and it's still basicly one effect so it's not really a combined spell , would really like some guidelines for spell that use multiple arcanum, like in the preview on grimoire, Living Grimoire (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) doesn't really need life at this level to scribe supernal runes into a living being, does it ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do think so. If im not mistaken Living Grimoire lets you redesign some basic building blocks of life to hold supernal information. For instance, changing the DNA-sequence to work as a grimoire with protein-chains written in High Speech but still allows it to be copied, carried and occupy &quot;space&quot; in the DNA without interfering with the normal life and such DNA is responsible for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:38:17-07:00","id":1209491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209479#post1209479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reach is reason enough no ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In such cases you should probably make just the Reach require the additional Arcanum.<br /> <br /> As for conjunctional spells, while the book claims they still exist there are literally zero examples of them in published books. They're rare because in second edition spell effects needs less justification. As long as it is thematically appropriate for one Arcanum you're generally set to go. A spell that would require several Arcana for its basic effect (unlike Reach options that modifies or adds an effect) would have to be something that isn't wholly appropriate for a single Arcanum. Living Grimoire is an example of such a spell because it's both scribing a Grimoire (something Life can't do) and transforming a living being (something Prime can't do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:39:20-07:00","id":1209492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209488#post1209488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I do think so. If im not mistaken Living Grimoire lets you redesign some basic building blocks of life to hold supernal information. For instance, changing the DNA-sequence to work as a grimoire with protein-chains written in High Speech but still allows it to be copied, carried and occupy &quot;space&quot; in the DNA without interfering with the normal life and such DNA is responsible for.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's my point, you could use a living grimoire with just prime by inscribing tattoo, the life addition add to the effect but doens't mechanycly od fundamentally change the spell, it's still one effect and builds up the theme of two arcana to work together, so why is this one good but my spell isn't ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T19:50:54-07:00","id":1209495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209492#post1209492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's my point, you could use a living grimoire with just prime by inscribing tattoo, the life addition add to the effect but doens't mechanycly od fundamentally change the spell, it's still one effect and builds up the theme of two arcana to work together, so why is this one good but my spell isn't ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we have a bit of values dissonance here. My side of the argument is that while a spell can incorporate multiple Arcana as the mage sees fit, it\u2019s better if it doesn\u2019t. Which the list of currently published spells seems to agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T20:31:57-07:00","id":1209499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1209492#post1209492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's my point, you could use a living grimoire with just prime by inscribing tattoo, the life addition add to the effect but doens't mechanycly od fundamentally change the spell, it's still one effect and builds up the theme of two arcana to work together, so why is this one good but my spell isn't ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Living Grimoire is a Patterning spell it means that part of the subject's essential substance is changed, it's no longer just a living being, but a living being that's also got Supernal magic mixed up in its essential nature. The spell might manifest certain signs, such as tattoo markings, but it's not just a tattoo. If it were just a tattoo, I agree, Prime alone would probably be able to handle it. I imagine that as magically induced genetic traits can be passed on to future generations from Life 3 onwards it's unlikely that a Patterning spell of this nature wouldn't have similar consequences for its subject. This is especially pertinent since Living Grimoire seems to impose a shorter lifespan on its subject.<br /> <br /> Conjunctional arcana spells manage to accomplish something that one arcana simply cannot achieve on its own. The primary example is turning yourself into living flame. Flame is clearly under Forces, but it can't be alive. Living beings are clearly under Life but they can't be fire. Only by having the two work together can you make a being that is both alive, and made of fire.<br /> <br /> This means spells that require conjunctional arcana should be very carefully considered, not because they're &quot;OP (A concept I don't give a damn about in Mage),&quot; but because it has to make sense inside the framework that the arcana have been presented as having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-20-2018, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T23:43:56-07:00","id":1209528,"title":"","content":"So if Apocalypse wich is also a patterning spell can run just fine affecting and modifying the very core of living being by imprinting them with supernal symbols, going so far as to blind them by burning their eyes or cutting out their senses if they ran out of willpower, without life, living grimoire should also be able to inscribe supernal truth into their flesh without needing life, if you want to inscribe it into genes and &quot;bloodlines&quot; then sure, you need Life, wich is part of my point, my spell call to supernal truth and the help of the spirit to further enlightening the mage (who knows better how a knife works than a knife spirit ?)<br /> Both arcana could alone do what the spell is doing with the two of them, linking Prime and Spirit is a big part of my character theory and view of magic. So it may be a weird spell or even wrong, but it makes sense to my character, to me and to my gm so i'm keeping it :/ and the argument that it is better to not incorporate as many arcanum as the mage sees fit as long as it works and make sense at least to the player, gm and other at the table is really not an argument at all, or if it is i'm missing the point, i tought the idea free form magic (and of growing your understanding of magic itself) was to improvise and experiment.<br /> <br /> Again sorry for derailling this will be my last post trying to argue for my spell, i can see why it would begin to annoy people, thanks all for your patience and i'm sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T01:35:36-07:00","id":1209555,"title":"","content":"I just explain a spell\u2019s narrative effects in the simplest way possible, and derive Arcana and Practice from it. <br /> <br /> Living Grimoire turns a lifeform into a Grimoire. Lifeform is Life. Grimoire is Prime. Turning A to B is Patterning. Thus, Life 4 + Prime 4. <br /> <br /> Apocalypse grants Mage Sight to people. Mage Sight is about truth, thus of Prime. Granting something fundamental is Patterning. Thus, Prime 4. <br /> <br /> And so on. And once again, I at the least am not saying that Prime + Spirit spell is impossible or absolutely undesirable, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12946_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12946\" data-vbnamecard=\"12946\">Emerick</a>, but that it can be \u201ctrimmed down\u201d so to speak, which is usually what players and arguably characters themselves find desirable. Not trying to flat-out deny it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T04:41:54-07:00","id":1209578,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12946_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12946\" data-vbnamecard=\"12946\">Emerick</a> I\u2019m not saying no to the spell, I\u2019m saying the spell can be done more efficiently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:39:32-07:00","id":1210124,"title":"","content":"If the exercise is to combine Prime+Spirit: You could use it to create platonic tools and weapons for spirits or direct conversion to directly convert to essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T14:35:28-07:00","id":1210601,"title":"","content":"Yeah, converting Essence to Mana would be a Prime + Spirit Ruling spell, as that's something that neither could do by itself. You'd need to add Death or Mind to extract directly from a ghost or a goetia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T02:24:35-07:00","id":1210871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210601#post1210601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, converting Essence to Mana would be a Prime + Spirit Ruling spell, as that's something that neither could do by itself. You'd need to add Death or Mind to extract directly from a ghost or a goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Patterning, not Ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T04:27:27-07:00","id":1210896,"title":"","content":"Not a whole new spell, but by adding Time 2 to the Mind spell &quot;No Exit&quot; you can change their perception of time in their little horror-scape/loop so that minutes for the real world are hours, centuries, or even thousands of years. Every time I look at Mind, I laugh at how OP people think some of the other arcanum are. Nothing is so invasive or powerful as stripping someone of their identity, memories and life, and making them into whatever you want even if that's the most hellish place on earth and trapping them in it - in their head.<br /> <br /> Practitioners of Mind likely don't value human connections much since those connections are so malleable and exploitable - and once you slip down that path a few millenia in a mental torture chamber is trivial for a reasonably competent user of Mind.<br /> <br /> Throw in some Forces with Mind 2, and their mouths are lacerated if they utter a lie - subtle but painful. The endless myriad of uses for Mind are mostly subtle and incredibly good.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:23:27-07:00","id":1210907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210896#post1210896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a whole new spell, but by adding Time 2 to the Mind spell &amp;quot;No Exit&amp;quot; you can change their perception of time in their little horror-scape/loop so that minutes for the real world are hours, centuries, or even thousands of years. Every time I look at Mind, I laugh at how OP people think some of the other arcanum are. Nothing is so invasive or powerful as stripping someone of their identity, memories and life, and making them into whatever you want even if that's the most hellish place on earth and trapping them in it - in their head.<br /> <br /> Practitioners of Mind likely don't value human connections much since those connections are so malleable and exploitable - and once you slip down that path a few millenia in a mental torture chamber is trivial for a reasonably competent user of Mind.<br /> <br /> Throw in some Forces with Mind 2, and their mouths are lacerated if they utter a lie - subtle but painful. The endless myriad of uses for Mind are mostly subtle and incredibly good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a reason why the Path whose Ruling Arcana includes Mind are associated with demons, after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T05:53:55-07:00","id":1210915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210896#post1210896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a whole new spell, but by adding Time 2 to the Mind spell &amp;quot;No Exit&amp;quot; you can change their perception of time in their little horror-scape/loop so that minutes for the real world are hours, centuries, or even thousands of years. Every time I look at Mind, I laugh at how OP people think some of the other arcanum are. Nothing is so invasive or powerful as stripping someone of their identity, memories and life, and making them into whatever you want even if that's the most hellish place on earth and trapping them in it - in their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I picked Mastigos for my first mage game I was told by my more experienced coplayers that they're definitely the best Path, based on ruling Arcana. (My next mage is probably going to be Acanthus, though. Exceptional Luck is also great, and Fate is probably more fun to play. Especially if I'd otherwise use the same Arcana twice in a row.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210896#post1210896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practitioners of Mind likely don't value human connections much since those connections are so malleable and exploitable - and once you slip down that path a few millenia in a mental torture chamber is trivial for a reasonably competent user of Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a risk when encountering mages using Mind, but it's also possible they're instead focusing on Mind because they wish to bolster themselves (increasing or granting Attributes, Skills and Merits; something I did a lot), deal with Goetia, or explore the Astral.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210896#post1210896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw in some Forces with Mind 2, and their mouths are lacerated if they utter a lie - subtle but painful. The endless myriad of uses for Mind are mostly subtle and incredibly good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Triggering a spell or effect based on a criterion is Fate, not Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:40:28-07:00","id":1211755,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <b>Word of Silence </b>(Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Mana Cost: 1+<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Investigation, Intimidation<br /> <br /> The symbols of creation are stored within the Supernal realms and brought fourth inside the Imago of the mage, enabling them to summon magic. This spell erodes the Imago of the subject while it is forming, weakening the connection toward the subjects Watchtower. For a number of spells equal to Potency the Subject looses a number of dice on spell-casting rolls equal to potency during its duration. The mage has no control of which spells are affected by this spell.<br /> <b>Add Fate </b>\u2022\u2022 <b>:</b> The mage may choose on a case by case basis which Imago that's eroded. Though without further insight, choosing is pure guesswork.<br /> <b>+2 reach and another point Man</b>a: The spell instead removes successes instead of dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:08:35-07:00","id":1211837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1210871#post1210871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Patterning, not Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can see the argument for that, since it's changing a fundamental. I was basing it on the Spirit 2 spell that lets you extract Essence from a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:23:11-07:00","id":1211844,"title":"","content":"But that's just moving Essence from one container to another. Transforming Essence into Mana is definitely Patterning, if possible at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:29:44-07:00","id":1211882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1211837#post1211837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I can see the argument for that, since it's changing a fundamental. I was basing it on the Spirit 2 spell that lets you extract Essence from a spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> said, moving a thing isn\u2019t the same as changing it from one thing to another.<br /> <br /> At the point where you want to use Patterning to create a mana-Essence conversion though you might as well just find a weak spirit that won\u2019t mind being your Familiar and then you can just use Spirit 4, Prime not needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:45:38-07:00","id":1212304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1211882#post1211882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> said, moving a thing isn\u2019t the same as changing it from one thing to another.<br /> <br /> At the point where you want to use Patterning to create a mana-Essence conversion though you might as well just find a weak spirit that won\u2019t mind being your Familiar and then you can just use Spirit 4, Prime not needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I hadn't thought that far out when I made the suggestion, honestly. Thanks for the catch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:43:33-07:00","id":1213172,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I haven't seen much in the way of improvising with Time, I imagine something you could do with Weaving/Patterning is healing by essentially dilating time for specific parts of a subject (ie whatever they could heal naturally with time, being healed <i>faster</i> than it otherwise might be at least to the perception of the subject and others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:48:43-07:00","id":1213175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1213172#post1213172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I haven't seen much in the way of improvising with Time, I imagine something you could do with Weaving/Patterning is healing by essentially dilating time for specific parts of a subject (ie whatever they could heal naturally with time, being healed <i>faster</i> than it otherwise might be at least to the perception of the subject and others.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the holistic nature of magic you\u2019d have to accelerate the healing rate of the entire Pattern rather than just a specific part. You could do it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T14:05:22-07:00","id":1213180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1213175#post1213175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the holistic nature of magic you\u2019d have to accelerate the healing rate of the entire Pattern rather than just a specific part. You could do it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I more meant that I was only accelerating the healing, not say, aging or other aspects of how they interact with time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T17:21:13-07:00","id":1213228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1213180#post1213180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I more meant that I was only accelerating the healing, not say, aging or other aspects of how they interact with time.</div> </div> </div> </div>A reach effect to avoid the deleterious affects of a time based healing spell would be fair imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T18:01:13-07:00","id":1213246,"title":"","content":"Body Control (Life **)<br /> <br /> As the base spell, <i>M:tA </i><i>2nd </i>ed. pg. 148, with the following additional Reach option:<br /> <br /> &quot;Add Time *: with Time 1, one Mana, and a Reach, the Mage can apply Defense against ranged attacks, as enhanced reflexes are supported with precognitive insight.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","user":"AmusedByIrony","date":"Time 3) and various Mage Armors.) 05-16-2018, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T13:46:21-07:00","id":1213523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1213246#post1213246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Body Control (Life **)<br /> <br /> As the base spell, <i>M:tA </i><i>2nd </i>ed. pg. 148, with the following additional Reach option:<br /> <br /> &quot;Add Time *: with Time 1 and a Reach, the Mage can apply Defense against ranged attacks, as enhanced reflexes are supported with precognitive insight.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's pretty legit if you don't have a mana for the reflexive mage armour.<br /> <br /> Not a whole new spell but my own creative reach effect for Animal Minion is to leave your body &quot;in a loop&quot; of actions or leave it with an instinctive urging instead of just dropping uselessly and whatnot. The most notable advantage being that you can hide or give yourself a rudimentary defense (or alarm) depending on what the situation requires.<br /> <br /> <b>Repeater</b><br /> Time: ruling<br /> Primary factor: duration<br /> When in combat, you may use short bursts even if your weapon would otherwise not be able to as time contracts and you appear to complete simple actions with startling speed. Effectively increase one step up on the auto-fire chart for any weapon the subject is a using. This can be applied to any simple or menial action such as splitting logs or kicking a door, in those cases add potency as a die bonus<br /> <br /> 1 reach: raise an additional step on the chart, this reach effect can be applied multiple times to access cover fire and longer bursts. Melee weapons cannot use covering fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T01:35:09-07:00","id":1219559,"title":"","content":"A few from me.<br /> <br /> Transplant (Life 2 - Rulling)<br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> Regrowing lost limbs and organs is moderately difficult with Magic but with the advent of modern transplantology it wasn't long till Mages found an easier way. This spell allows to transplant a part of a body from one person to another. The magic used in the spell mean that unline mundane transplants you don't have to worry about rejection, immunosupresants or rehab, the &quot;new&quot; part is fully fuctional from the get go. Parts must be taken from a still living subjects.<br /> + 1 Reach: Parts can be a taken from a recently dead person<br /> + 2 Reach: Parts might come from a different species, for instance the Mage can implant a predators claw if place of the subjects hand. For specific effects this might grant check the spell &quot;Transform Life&quot; (MtAw core pg.150) <br /> <br /> Reinforce Patern (Prime 2 - Rulling)<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> This spell allows the Mage to infuse the subject with mana restoring Health or Structure up to a maximum egual to potency. It takes 3 mana to restore a point of lethal or bashing dmg or structure. Alternatively 3 mana can be spent to remove a single physical Tilt or mental condition. <br /> +1 Reach: For 3 mana the subject gains a single dot in a physical attribute.<br /> <br /> Words Unbound (Prime 3 - Perfecting)<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Although god twisted human tongues for the sin of constructing a tower to heaven, all languages are still a way of transfering truth between people. The mage can bolster that truth making it pierce through the barrier of worlds and phrases. The subject is understood by anyone present regardless of any languague she is speaking. He may even speak gibberish and other will still understand the meaning behind his words.<br /> <br /> Leaden Feathers (Matter 3 - Perfecting/Fraying)<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> The Mage alters the weight of an object, each point of potency either doubling or halving the subjects weight.<br /> +1 Reach: The object becomes lighter than air causing it to float up.<br /> <br /> \u200bAny comments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T05:53:56-07:00","id":1219596,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2636_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2636\" data-vbnamecard=\"2636\">Menace</a> Transplant can be Lasting for +2 Reach, and a mana I think. Unless using the Reach effect to transplant cross species organs, that shouldn\u2019t be Lastihg.<br /> <br /> Reinforce Pattern should be like Devouring the Slain, 3 dots and limited to the number of times the Mage can reinforce his Pattern per day based on Gnosis. +1 Reach can get around that limitation.<br /> <br /> Words Unbound is good, I\u2019d just leave out the option to speak gibberish. Gibberish isn\u2019t language, and deliberately isn\u2019t so, it\u2019s purpose is to be unintelligible.<br /> <br /> Leaden Feathers is good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-17-2018, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T06:21:30-07:00","id":1219605,"title":"","content":"nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:13:40-07:00","id":1219717,"title":"","content":"Light of Elder Days (Matter 3, Time 2)<br /> Practices: Unveiling, Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Temporal Sympathy<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Academics, Occult<br /> <br /> Almost always cast with advanced area, this spell restores a building to its original state. If the Potency of the spell at least equals the highest Durability of any material present in the original structure, the spell succeeds. An exceptionally large building, such as a skyscraper or hospital, can be restored if the areas being restored are intuitively obvious, such as a wing of a hospital ora floor of a skyscraper. Note that this spell restores only the building, not its contents. As a good rule, if something can simply be picked up and removed, it's not part of the building.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: the restoration is Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:29:44-07:00","id":1219724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1219717#post1219717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light of Elder Days (Matter 3, Time 2)<br /> Practices: Unveiling, Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Temporal Sympathy<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Academics, Occult<br /> <br /> Almost always cast with advanced area, this spell restores a building to its original state. If the Potency of the spell at least equals the highest Durability of any material present in the original structure, the spell succeeds. An exceptionally large building, such as a skyscraper or hospital, can be restored if the areas being restored are intuitively obvious, such as a wing of a hospital ora floor of a skyscraper. Note that this spell restores only the building, not its contents. As a good rule, if something can simply be picked up and removed, it's not part of the building.<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: the restoration is Lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically just the Time 3 spell Temporal Summoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:47:37-07:00","id":1219734,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thanks for the feedback. As for transplant I didnt want to include a lasting option because the effect is intented for a particular legacy I'm thinking about. I agree about the others after thinking a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:52:24-07:00","id":1219737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1219734#post1219734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Thanks for the feedback. As for transplant I didnt want to include a lasting option because the effect is intented for a particular legacy I'm thinking about. I agree about the others after thinking a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fail to see the problem with adding a Lasting option just because you\u2019re building a legacy that won\u2019t use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T18:07:15-07:00","id":1220380,"title":"","content":"A few spells I used for my homebrew conversion of Cult of the Doomsday Clock:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Cut History (Time \u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Unraveling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Withstand</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Sympathy (Connection)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Subterfuge, Politics, Empathy</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The past need not haunt the present with its ills, nor blind it with bygone bliss. This spell destroys the subject's temporal sympathy with a specific moment in her life as designated by the mage. Destroying one subject's sympathy with more of her past selves is done by increasing Scale as the Number of subjects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While this spell does not directly affect memories, the fading sympathy will slowly cause people to simply forget naturally. T</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">he spell's effect is Lasting, but if the subject or anyone else is still aware of the fading history, they can make efforts to reconnect. This means that histories of objects not particularly famous are in more danger of being cut away without recovery.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Add Mind \u2022\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The spell now does affect minds, suppressing people's memories of the targeted history for the spell's Duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Killer's Eye (Death \u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Unveiling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Weaponry, Brawl, Intimidation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The necromancer invites Death's own gaze, revealing the fragile threads that hold life together. For the spell's Duration, her subject gains the Killer Instinct Merit (as per</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Beast: The Primordial</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">) at a rating equal to the spell's Potency, up to the normal three-dot limit. The subject must still spend an instant action assessing their target to activate the Merit, but is free to divide the granted dots among the usual effects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: With a point of Mana, the spell may grant Killer Instinct beyond three dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The subject no longer needs to spend a turn assessing his target, doing so as a reflexive action.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Disperse Wounds (Death \u2022<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Fraying</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Medicine, Survival, Empathy</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A skilled necromancer can not only draw death but repel it. This spell downgrades levels of lethal damage equal to its Potency to two levels of bashing damage. If the bashing damage exceeds the subject\u2019s Health, it overflows into lethal damage as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The spell can affect bashing damage, downgrading it into non-damage. Potency may be split between damage types.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The spell also clears Physical Tilts tied to affected Health boxes, despite the damage still being present.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Add Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The spell now extends to objects, healing their Structure damage. Objects restored this way however gain a variant of the Fragile Condition (as per</span></span> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">), the resolution of which returns the past Structure damage.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T19:04:16-07:00","id":1220392,"title":"","content":"<b>Bath Time </b>(Matter 2)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Exactly what it says on the tin. This spell forces all dirt, grime, etc. on the subject's body to fall away. The spell makes no attempt to distinguish, for example, makeup from dried mud: if it's not alive, it goes away. Note that hair and skin are part of a living being's Pattern, and thus unaffected. It is recommended the subject be unclad unless a need to visit a laundry should also be desirable. The target is now as clean as if she had just taken a very thorough shower, and brushed her teeth completely. Larger-than-human targets require increased Size. The resulting clean state lasts as long as it normally would.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can be used to selectively remove or not remove particular things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-19-2018, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T02:32:02-07:00","id":1220762,"title":"","content":"Something that I thought up today<br /> <br /> Crystalize memory (Mind 4 + Prime 4)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Crafts, Science, Empathy<br /> Cost: 1 mana (minimum)<br /> <br /> The mage congels a memory into pure tass removing it from his mind. Properties of the tass are determined the same as for the creating it with Prime alone. As the tass doesn't have the same safeguards and complexities as a mind of a living being anyone can read the memory using a Mind Unveiling spell but the attempt is withstood by the Durability of the tass. If a mage absorbs the tass the memory enters that mage's mind.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage copies the memory instead of removing it from his mind.<br /> <br /> Akashic Repository (Mind 3)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Socialize, Academics, Science<br /> <br /> Though the Akashic Records are unaccesible as far as any willworker knows, a Mage can turn himself into a smaller repository of knowledge. The spells allows all of it's subjects share a number of the mage's of a number of skills. Choose a number of skills equal to the spells potency. Whenever one subjects needs to make a skill with one of the choses skills roll he or she can use the mage's dot rating. This doesn't effect rolls to activate supernatural powers such as rotes or the abillities of other beings.<br /> +1 Reach: The subjects share the use of skill with each other not only with the mage<br /> +2 Reach: The subjects share all skills, not just the chosen ones<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can also choose a single mental merit to share, this reach effect can be taken a number of times, each time choosing a different merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:06:03-07:00","id":1220823,"title":"","content":"I like Crystalize Memory a lot, but I'm not sure that the Withstand for reading it is necessary. I've noticed that there are something like 20-25 Knowing/Unveiling spells in the book and only 3 have Withstand - and a couple of <i>those</i> are nonsensical for various reasons.<br /> <br /> Kind of feels like these Practices should generally not be Withstood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:25:50-07:00","id":1220826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1220762#post1220762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that I thought up today<br /> <br /> Crystalize memory (Mind 4 + Prime 4)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Crafts, Science, Empathy<br /> Cost: 1 mana (minimum)<br /> <br /> The mage congels a memory into pure tass removing it from his mind. Properties of the tass are determined the same as for the creating it with Prime alone. As the tass doesn't have the same safeguards and complexities as a mind of a living being anyone can read the memory using a Mind Unveiling spell but the attempt is withstood by the Durability of the tass. If a mage absorbs the tass the memory enters that mage's mind.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage copies the memory instead of removing it from his mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following what Inodiv said, perhaps make magical attempts to read the memory-crystal provoke a Clash of Wills? And maybe there's room to add a Reach clause where the crystallized memory is a <i>false </i>one...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:39:29-07:00","id":1220886,"title":"","content":"<b>Create Tass </b>(Prime 3)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Craft, Occult<br /> <br /> With this spell, a mage can channel mana (normally a cabal-mate's) into a tangible form, such as water in a sports bottle, creating tass. This tass is subject to the normal rules concerning its use. Each point of Potency creates approximately 120ml of drinkable liquid tass, 100 grams of edible solid tass, or 80 grams of non-edible tass. Edible or drinkable tass are the most common forms. By way of reference, 120ml is effectively a third of a typical soft drink can, and 100 grams is the mass of a large sausage roll or a small orange.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach</b>: the effect is Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 06-12-2018, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T01:43:54-07:00","id":1221103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1220826#post1220826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following what Inodiv said, perhaps make magical attempts to read the memory-crystal provoke a Clash of Wills? And maybe there's room to add a Reach clause where the crystallized memory is a <i>false </i>one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't creating a memory be Making practice? Though modifing it for a reach sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> @LadyLens: That's just basically Platonic Form from the core book only more limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T01:46:53-07:00","id":1221104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221103#post1221103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't creating a memory be Making practice? Though modifing it for a reach sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> @LadyLens: That's just basically Platonic Form from the core book only more limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking less of making whole new memories to crystallize out of thin air, and more disguising the crystallized ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T10:36:10-07:00","id":1221199,"title":"","content":"<b>Cool Water</b> (Matter 2)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Water is everywhere, often in places one would not expect. This spell draws water from the very air, condensing vapour into a usable liquid. Each point of Potency yields enough water for one person for one day, assuming it's kept in a suitable container. This effect is Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage can draw water from the extremely dry air of cold deserts, such as glaciers and the polar regions. Contrary to popular belief, hot desert air typically holds a very great deal of water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T01:00:57-07:00","id":1221409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221199#post1221199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cool Water</b> (Matter 2)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Water is everywhere, often in places one would not expect. This spell draws water from the very air, condensing vapour into a usable liquid. Each point of Potency yields enough water for one person for one day, assuming it's kept in a suitable container. This effect is Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage can draw water from the extremely dry air of cold deserts, such as glaciers and the polar regions. Contrary to popular belief, hot desert air typically holds a very great deal of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Scale matters more than Potency here, there\u2019s only so much water in any given area, increased Potency can\u2019t change that, increased Scale can change how much water vapor you can reach. A small room in Scale can provide a day\u2019s worth of water.<br /> <br /> Also, you don\u2019t need to say the effects are Lasting, first of all it would be weird if casting this spell created a permanent area of water vapor condensation. Second of all the part you probably mean is Lasting is the collected water, but obviously it is, that\u2019s just a side effect of what the spell does. Think of it like this, if you had a machine that could do this same trick, and you turned it on, collected the water, and then smashed the machine, would that affect the water you already collected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T01:40:13-07:00","id":1221417,"title":"","content":"Lasting generally refers to side effects. In this case Lasting means the water doesn't immediately return to vapour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T11:46:36-07:00","id":1221512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221417#post1221417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting generally refers to side effects. In this case Lasting means the water doesn't immediately return to vapour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The water remains liquid as long as it normally would.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221409#post1221409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Scale matters more than Potency here, there\u2019s only so much water in any given area, increased Potency can\u2019t change that, increased Scale can change how much water vapor you can reach. A small room in Scale can provide a day\u2019s worth of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose Potency simply to avoid arguments or difficulties arising from determining the needed Scale in varied environments: in mid-ocean, a rain forest, the Canadian Prairies, the Rocky Mountains, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-23-2018, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T13:40:35-07:00","id":1221535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221512#post1221512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. The water remains liquid as long as it normally would.<br /> <br /> I chose Potency simply to avoid arguments or difficulties arising from determining the needed Scale in varied environments: in mid-ocean, a rain forest, the Canadian Prairies, the Rocky Mountains, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't cause arguments if you just add a note that on average a small room carries sufficient water vapor to provide enough water to meet a human's needs for a day. Then it's up to the ST to decide whether or not you're in an area that's too dry for that and he can tell you that you need to expand your Scale. With the spell as it's written now you don't worry about Scale at all, and can basically create water ex-nhilo, 27-37 liters of it per Potency, meaning you can squeeze an amount of water out of the air that literally isn't there in most conditions. I'm down for magic trumping science which is why you can use inexact Scale factors, but Potency as the deciding factor for determining how much water you get is a bit silly.<br /> <br /> Also, as I noted for reasons above, the clause about it being Lasting isn't necessary, the fact that the water remains after the spell ends is obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:01:49-07:00","id":1221562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221535#post1221535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can basically create water ex-nhilo, 27-37 liters of it per Potency</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither experience nor research supports those figures; indeed, both suggest that those figures are off by a factor of at least ten. I know that I certainly do not require the equivalent of seven to twelve jugs of milk every day just to survive, and if you require that much, then you should see a doctor because there's something very strange going on in your biology.<br /> <br /> Concerning Lasting, many things that seem &quot;obviously&quot; Lasting are not. Ontological inertia can be weird in this game, so I felt it wise to specify that no, the water does not automatically return to vapour state when the Duration lapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-23-2018, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:40:35-07:00","id":1221575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221562#post1221562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither experience nor research supports those figures; indeed, both suggest that those figures are off by a factor of at least ten. I know that I certainly do not require the equivalent of seven to twelve jugs of milk every day just to survive, and if you require that much, then you should see a doctor because there's something very strange going on in your biology</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual figures used is beside the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T17:37:42-07:00","id":1221580,"title":"","content":"On the contrary, it is very much the point. Such a wildly inaccurate, if not positively hyperbolic, claim undermines your entire argument, especially since the Scale factors, particularly the Advanced Scale factors, are extremely non-linear. A small warehouse, for the values of small I'm familiar with, is three to six times the volume of a large house, and the general pattern is similar: each step of Scale encompasses roughly three to six times the volume of the step before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T18:23:03-07:00","id":1221585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221580#post1221580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contrary, it is very much the point. Such a wildly inaccurate, if not positively hyperbolic, claim undermines your entire argument, especially since the Scale factors, particularly the Advanced Scale factors, are extremely non-linear. A small warehouse, for the values of small I'm familiar with, is three to six times the volume of a large house, and the general pattern is similar: each step of Scale encompasses roughly three to six times the volume of the step before.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn\u2019t the point, you have to cast the spell over an area anyway otherwise you can only affect water vapor you\u2019re physically in contact which I guarantee you is not enough to meet a person\u2019s daily needs even if mathed my earlier estimates wrong, and you certainly can\u2019t meet the needs of multiple people simply because you increased the Potency you\u2019re using on the water vapor you\u2019re touching. Potency isn\u2019t always the metric by which you achieve more, and this is one of those cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-23-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T01:24:22-07:00","id":1221630,"title":"","content":"The lasting effect doesn't have to be mentioned. The kind of changes that the spell makes tend to stick by default.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Scale might make more sense, but spells have either Potency or Duration as a primary factor and having the primary factor not matter at all feels wonky game design wise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, some forces spells I came up with yesterday:<br /> <br /> Transfer Charge - Forces 2 (Rulling)<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Science, Socialize, Emphaty<br /> <br /> Every child had done the trick with hair and the baloon but a willworker can apply the same principles to a greater effect. The spell transfers an electric charge from one subject to another, charging one positevely and the other negatively. As a result, both subjects attract each other with a Strenght equal to Potency. The subjects remain stuck together for the spells Duration. Trying to force them appart is a contested roll against the attractions strenght. Unless scale factor is increased the Mage is treated as one of the subjects.<br /> <br /> Grasp the Elements - Forces 3 (Weaving)<br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skill: Larcery, Crafts, Athletics<br /> <br /> Sometimes a sorcerer versed in Forcese might find herself with a limited selection of things to manipulare. The answer is simple: take them with you wherever you go.The spell allows the mage to grab and manilupulate a manifestation of forces such as fire, light of electricity as if it wear a physical object. The forces forms an orb in the willworker hand, which the mage can manipulate as if it was a lump of clay. For instance, he may throw it with a Dex + Athletics roll. The effects of getting hit by the orb depend on its nature, fire might burn things and sound might cause the deafened tilt. Creating more orbs can be possible with increasing the scale factor.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Instead of an orb the force takes a more threatening form. It might be used as a weapon though the damage is dependant on the nature of the force (dmg is the same as for eniromental hazards so only some forces have any use with with this effect)<br /> <br /> +2 Reach: The willworker can control the orbs remotely without having to physically hold them. They float around the willworker withing arms reach. They can be thrown with a Gnosis + Forces roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:50:40-07:00","id":1221657,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2636_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2636\" data-vbnamecard=\"2636\">Menace</a> who said anything using Scale as the primary factor? I\u2019d actually use Duration for that and then you\u2019d have a reliable watering hole as water vapor moves into the area.<br /> <br /> Transfer Charge should probably be Perfecting since it seems to be strengthening electrical charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T05:19:28-07:00","id":1221661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221657#post1221657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;2636&quot;]<br /> Transfer Charge should probably be Perfecting since it seems to be strengthening electrical charges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe my understaing of physics is wrong but what I meant is that one subject gets a negative charge and the other gets a positive charge with the general electric charge not changing at all. That's why it's &quot;transfer&quot; charge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:19:31-07:00","id":1221681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221661#post1221661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe my understaing of physics is wrong but what I meant is that one subject gets a negative charge and the other gets a positive charge with the general electric charge not changing at all. That's why it's &amp;quot;transfer&amp;quot; charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you\u2019re boosting the attraction effect via Potency though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:07:49-07:00","id":1221693,"title":"","content":"I envivioned it so that the Potency affects the amount of electric charge transfered, not strictly increase it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T21:50:01-07:00","id":1221941,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>New Flesh</b> (Life 3)</span><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Size<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Medicine, Science<br /> <br /> This spell creates a new living being from the bones of a formerly living being. The complete skeleton is required. If the spell succeeds, a new living thing rises from the bones. It is alive, well, and very hungry, but it is not automatically hostile to the caster. This spell is not a resurrection; the new being is just that, new, and possesses only instincts at first. The new being can learn normally after the spell is completed, and will live as long as normal. With Mind 3, the new being can be given a rudimentary education appropriate to its nature: a dog can be paper-trained and know some simple commands, a human can talk and use the bathroom, and so on.<br /> <br /> Using this spell on the bones of a supernatural entity can have varied effects. A changeling's bones or vampire's will produce a human, as will a Sin-eater's. A werewolf's bones would produce a human, wolf, or wolf-man as applicable, which might or might not be an actual werewolf, as the ST chooses.. Other supernaturals are at the ST's discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-25-2018, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T21:54:28-07:00","id":1221942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221941#post1221941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>New Flesh</b> (Life 3)</span><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Size<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Medicine, Science<br /> <br /> This spell creates a new living being from the bones of a formerly living being. The complete skeleton is required. If the spell succeeds, a new living thing rises from the bones. It is alive, well, and very hungry, but it is not automatically hostile to the caster. This spell is not a resurrection; the new being is just that, new, and possesses only instincts at first. The new being can learn normally after the spell is completed, and will live as long as normal. With Mind 3, the new being can be given a rudimentary education appropriate to its nature: a dog can be paper-trained and know some simple commands, a human can talk and use the bathroom, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... doesn\u2019t look like a Weaving spell. A corpse becoming a life form sounds like a fundamental change, so I\u2019d say Patterning at least. And may also require Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T22:02:26-07:00","id":1221946,"title":"","content":"I chose not to include Death because I regard the generation of a soul as being an emergent function of the generation of the body. But having reviewed the definitions of the Practices, I'd say that a good case can be made for Patterning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-25-2018, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T22:55:24-07:00","id":1221952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221946#post1221946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chose not to include Death because I regard the generation of a soul as being an emergent function of the generation of the body. But having reviewed the definitions of the Practices, I'd say that a good case can be made for Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only said it may require Death because the spell changes a corpse. Dunno about souls - not with my pdf now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T02:36:38-07:00","id":1221972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221941#post1221941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>New Flesh</b> (Life 3)</span><br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Size<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Medicine, Science<br /> <br /> This spell creates a new living being from the bones of a formerly living being. The complete skeleton is required. If the spell succeeds, a new living thing rises from the bones. It is alive, well, and very hungry, but it is not automatically hostile to the caster. This spell is not a resurrection; the new being is just that, new, and possesses only instincts at first. The new being can learn normally after the spell is completed, and will live as long as normal. With Mind 3, the new being can be given a rudimentary education appropriate to its nature: a dog can be paper-trained and know some simple commands, a human can talk and use the bathroom, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls can\u2019t be created via anything less than archmastery, so this spell should require Death and Life Patterning and will result in a soulless human if that\u2019s the direction you go. Their life will also be entirely dependent on the Duration of the spell, though they could manage to die again before then.<br /> <br /> You could use just Life 4 if you turned one living thing into another via Shapeshifting. You could create life ex nihilo with Life 5, though lifespan would still be determined by Duration and humans would still be soulless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-25-2018, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T06:39:50-07:00","id":1222012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1221972#post1221972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Souls can\u2019t be created via anything less than archmastery, so this spell should require Death and Life Patterning and will result in a soulless human if that\u2019s the direction you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet souls clearly come into existence without need of archmaster intervention. So since they clearly come into existence somehow, why wouldn't a newly created human have one? Yes I know Prometheans don't have true souls, but they're weird, and extremely rare, and they can gain a true soul in time. Indeed, that's the entire point of the Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T06:48:02-07:00","id":1222014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222012#post1222012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet souls clearly come into existence without need of archmaster intervention. So since they clearly come into existence somehow, why wouldn't a newly created human have one? Yes I know Prometheans don't have true souls, but they're weird, and extremely rare, and they can gain a true soul in time. Indeed, that's the entire point of the Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mrmdubois meant \u201csouls can\u2019t be created by Supernal magic, save for that of archmasters.\u201d <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, can anybody confirm whether Create Life had anything to say about souls? I\u2019m still not with my laptop, so I can\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T06:49:25-07:00","id":1222015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222012#post1222012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet souls clearly come into existence without need of archmaster intervention. So since they clearly come into existence somehow, why wouldn't a newly created human have one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because humans are not created out of whole cloth and souls are a limited resource.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222014#post1222014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, can anybody confirm whether Create Life had anything to say about souls? I\u2019m still not with my laptop, so I can\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>It directly states that if you make a human body it has the Soulless Condition by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T07:04:57-07:00","id":1222020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222015#post1222015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It directly states that if you make a human body it has the Soulless Condition by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thanks. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking more on Awakened soul magic, I\u2019m starting to think that while Supernal magic is the easiest and simplest method of manipulating souls, it\u2019s far from the most potent, nor the most versatile. I blame the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T07:23:06-07:00","id":1222025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222015#post1222015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It directly states that if you make a human body it has the Soulless Condition by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this statement? I haven't yet read the book through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T16:51:26-07:00","id":1222128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222025#post1222025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this statement? I haven't yet read the book through.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the writeup for Create Life, the spell used to spontaneously generate a new lifeform, found in the last part of the section on the Life Arcanum and its example spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T00:43:16-07:00","id":1222179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222025#post1222025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this statement? I haven't yet read the book through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really recommend doing that before trying to come up with custom stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T14:29:53-07:00","id":1222304,"title":"","content":"Mirage (Forces 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> This spell manipulates atmospheric conditions to create a mirage, an image of a far-distant object that anyone can see. It can be an inferior mirage, a superior mirage, or a Fata Morgana. This is <i>not</i> obvious magic, as mirages are quite real and normal phenomena, though often very striking and provoking of amazement. The Scale parameter determines the area over which conditions are right for the mirage to be seen; most castings involved advanced Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T16:59:23-07:00","id":1222327,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">From The Mysterium (1E book):<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Reveal Enigmas (Mind \u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Knowing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Investigation, Science, Academics</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The psychonaut heightens her mental acuity in face of puzzles and mysteries, dissecting their patterns to discover the solution. Simple puzzles require no more than a glance to solve. In case of more complex mysteries represented by an investigation effort (as per <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>), this spell adds its Potency to a Clue's number of elements. Scale may be increased to target multiple Clues, which requires the mage to divide Potency between them. Such additional elements last only for the spell's Duration.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The spell grants inspective insight, allowing the mage to double-check established leads. The spell can be used to remove the Incomplete or Tainted tags from a Clue for a level of Potency, instead of providing extra elements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Add Forces \u2022</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">: The mage can now solve &quot;puzzles&quot; in the form of computer codes and digital ciphers.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-26-2018, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T05:53:10-07:00","id":1222385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222304#post1222304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirage (Forces 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> This spell manipulates atmospheric conditions to create a mirage, an image of a far-distant object that anyone can see. It can be an inferior mirage, a superior mirage, or a Fata Morgana. This is <i>not</i> obvious magic, as mirages are quite real and normal phenomena, though often very striking and provoking of amazement. The Scale parameter determines the area over which conditions are right for the mirage to be seen; most castings involved advanced Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could still be obvious magic, because what\u2019s obvious or not depends entirely on the circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T08:33:19-07:00","id":1222430,"title":"","content":"Laundry Day (Matter 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Exactly what it says on the tin. This spell cleans even the most heavily soiled of garments, removing any inert matter not an actual part of the garment or garments in question as determined by the Scale factor. This can include iron-on logos and similar, but will not normally affect silk-screen designs. The garments remain clean as long as they normally would. The addition of Life 2 allows the garments to be made pest-free and sterile, as well as simply clean.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The spell operates selectively, allowing iron-on transfers to be left behind, or for specific stains to be removed and others left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-27-2018, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T09:22:31-07:00","id":1222443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222430#post1222430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but will not normally affect silk-screen designs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Silk is also an expression of Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T09:27:01-07:00","id":1222445,"title":"","content":"The silk is part of the process of silk-screen painting, but it's actually paint on the fabric. Still, the paint should be just as susceptible or non-susceptible to this spell as iron-on logos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-27-2018, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T19:08:38-07:00","id":1222564,"title":"","content":"Most Iron-ons are just overlays, which is why they peel off over time. Silk screen design are usually impregnated into the fibres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T02:51:27-07:00","id":1222596,"title":"","content":"That doesn't really matter. Looking at your post you seem to missing that magic in Magic isn't a manipulation of physics but a manipulation of symbols so you don't really have to make things work on &quot;logic&quot;. <br /> <br /> My second comment is that the spell is very narrow, try this instead:<br /> <br /> Purify - Matter 2, <br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Rote skills: Crafts, Survival, Science<br /> The mage can purify a manifestation of matter from impurities expelling outwards any parts of the subject object or substance that aren't part of it. A muddy pool of water can be made crystal clear ,cloth can be cleaned from any stains and print-ons or the content of a paper document can be erased.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can leave or erase specific impurities. This effect allows to either remove a number of impurities equal to potenty OR to expel everything but that number.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T16:05:48-07:00","id":1222728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222596#post1222596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't really matter. Looking at your post you seem to missing that magic in Magic isn't a manipulation of physics but a manipulation of symbols so you don't really have to make things work on &quot;logic&quot;.<br /> <br /> My second comment is that the spell is very narrow, try this instead:<br /> <br /> Purify - Matter 2,<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Rote skills: Crafts, Survival, Science<br /> The mage can purify a manifestation of matter from impurities expelling outwards any parts of the subject object or substance that aren't part of it. A muddy pool of water can be made crystal clear ,cloth can be cleaned from any stains and print-ons or the content of a paper document can be erased.<br /> +1 Reach: The mage can leave or erase specific impurities. This effect allows to either remove a number of impurities equal to potenty OR to expel everything but that number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can that affect solids? I'd specify.<br /> Perhaps add a Reach effect and make it Withstood by Durability to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T23:08:50-07:00","id":1222832,"title":"","content":"The description mentions cloth and that's a solid.. I don't think the withstand is needed, it's not a harmfull/invasive spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T23:13:23-07:00","id":1222833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222832#post1222832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description mentions cloth and that's a solid.. I don't think the withstand is needed, it's not a harmfull/invasive spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I meant more can it expel the impurities from within solids.<br /> e.g. Refinement of gold by removing impurities, without reducing it to a molten state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T07:17:52-07:00","id":1222888,"title":"","content":"Well as I conceived the original it was basically for surface cleaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T07:22:22-07:00","id":1222891,"title":"","content":"We can have both - a Matter 1 Compelling spell for cleaning, and a Matter 2 Ruling spell for purifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T11:48:20-07:00","id":1222957,"title":"","content":"Tongues (Mind 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Expression, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> There are times when a mage needs to learn a language in a tearing hurry, and this spell allows just that. For each level of Potency, the mage gains a dot of Language Merits. These dots are assigned in order as the mage is exposed to unknown languages, so if the mage wants to learn, for example, Egyptian Arabic, casting this spell in a multilingual crowd of tourists might not be wise. This spell is not and cannot be Lasting, but can be used to justify spending Experiences to acquire Language merits quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T11:55:13-07:00","id":1222959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222957#post1222957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tongues (Mind 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Expression, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> There are times when a mage needs to learn a language in a tearing hurry, and this spell allows just that. For each level of Potency, the mage gains a dot of Language Merits. These dots are assigned in order as the mage is exposed to unknown languages, so if the mage wants to learn, for example, Egyptian Arabic, casting this spell in a multilingual crowd of tourists might not be wise. This spell is not and cannot be Lasting, but can be used to justify spending Experiences to acquire Language merits quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see basically no good reason for this spell to not have Duration as its Primary Factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T13:19:37-07:00","id":1222985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222959#post1222959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see basically no good reason for this spell to not have Duration as its Primary Factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the primary determinant for a spell's primary factor is &quot;what would a stronger version be?&quot; In this case, the stronger version would be one that lets the mage acquire more languages. That's Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T13:25:49-07:00","id":1222986,"title":"","content":"I could see the effect as a Knowing spell. Perhaps the base version allowing to understand languages with a reach allowing to speak them. Might be too much though, just an idea.<br /> <br /> You also don't need to add &quot;can't be made lasting&quot; to every effect since, well, most effects can't. In general most of the effects that CAN be lasting are those that create a state with less abnormalities aka mostly effects that restore a previous state. Healing, repairing stuff, removing conditions, dispelling magic, that kind of stuff. Also effects that are an indirect effect of what the spell does. There's exceptions but it's safe to assume that an effect isn't lasting unless stated otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 05-29-2018, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T13:35:12-07:00","id":1222987,"title":"","content":"Acquiring Merit dots is typically a two dot effect according to the breakdown on p. 126, so that's what I went with. And yes, a Knowing effect could be used to simply understand a language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T13:38:08-07:00","id":1222990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1222985#post1222985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the primary determinant for a spell's primary factor is &quot;what would a stronger version be?&quot; In this case, the stronger version would be one that lets the mage acquire more languages. That's Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule of thumb. Which does not mean &quot;how does the spell get stronger?&quot; or else they would <i>all</i> be Potency.<br /> <br /> This is a spell that gives you access to instances of the Language Merit that you did not have previously. That's an effect that is primarily used over a long term \u2014 knowing five more languages is not terribly useful in a span of three seconds, but knowing one more language for thirty seconds is substantially closer to spec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:18:00-07:00","id":1223006,"title":"","content":"Replace &quot;stronger&quot; with &quot;more useful&quot; and I think you get close to the intention of that guideline.<br /> I definitely agree with Satchel about Duration making a lot more sense than Potency in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:20:03-07:00","id":1223007,"title":"","content":"And that's why you'd normally use advanced Duration. Even one scene is useful. Duration would be the primary factor for binary spells, either on or off, such a gateway into the spirit world. It's open, or it's not. This spell allows acquiring multiple languages; acquiring more languages is more potent than acquiring fewer. If it only allowed one language, then Duration would be primary. Here's the direct quote form page 113: <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Potency matters for spells that grant bonuses, impose penalties, or provide graduated levels of effects, such as dealing damage or increasing dot-ratings of traits. The effect of a spell\u2019s Potency is described in the individual spell write-up \u2014 each level of Potency increases the spell\u2019s main effect. Each level of Potency beyond the first imposes a \u20132 penalty to the casting roll. Mages may spend Reach to gain Advanced Potency, which increases the spell\u2019s Withstand ability against dispellation by +2.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:26:22-07:00","id":1223009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223007#post1223007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duration would be the primary factor for binary spells, either on or off, such a gateway into the spirit world. It's open, or it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, but that's not the only spells that use Duration as their primary factor. There are examples in the book where spells have Duration primary despite also using Potency.<br /> Borrow Threads is one example. It both has a Withstand rating and transfers a number of sympathetic connections equal to Potency, yet Duration is considered more useful as the primary factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:35:20-07:00","id":1223015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223007#post1223007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why you'd normally use advanced Duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primary Factor of a spell is the last one to lose levels from Dissonance and is the factor that Exceptional Success can benefit from extra levels or free Reaches. &quot;Reach is cheap&quot; is not a legitimate excuse for making a spell's Primary Factor Potency over Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T14:39:17-07:00","id":1223017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223009#post1223009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely, but that's not the only spells that use Duration as their primary factor. There are examples in the book where spells have Duration primary despite also using Potency.<br /> Borrow Threads is one example. It both has a Withstand rating and transfers a number of sympathetic connections equal to Potency, yet Duration is considered more useful as the primary factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Potency is the main factor because its main effect, transferring sympathetic connection, comes in graduated levels: the higher Potency, the more connections are moved. It's the same with Tongues: the higher the Potency, the more languages the mage can acquire. Duration is also important, but to a lesser degree in terms of mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T15:07:01-07:00","id":1223025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223017#post1223017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Potency is the main factor because its main effect, transferring sympathetic connection, comes in graduated levels: the higher Potency, the more connections are moved. It's the same with Tongues: the higher the Potency, the more languages the mage can acquire. Duration is also important, but to a lesser degree in terms of mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should go back and reread Borrow Threads, Duration is the main factor, not Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T15:28:19-07:00","id":1223039,"title":"","content":"Body Control is relevant example as well, Potency is used for a whole host of benefits, and yet Duration is still the Primary Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T16:33:37-07:00","id":1223056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223039#post1223039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Body Control is relevant example as well, Potency is used for a whole host of benefits, and yet Duration is still the Primary Factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, to point to the opposite scenario, Bolster Spirit and Shape Spirit are both Potency-Primary because, despite their ability to create long-term bonuses for their targets, their core use is &quot;heal damage to spirits,&quot; which is a Lasting effect that doesn't care about Duration at the ground level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T22:11:22-07:00","id":1223113,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dissolution (Matter 3)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Structure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> <br /> This spell separates the target into its various elemental components. A piece of graphite will collapse into carbon nanopowder, a sapphire into aluminum dust, which will immediately react with the oxygen to form alumina nanopowder. Water becomes hydrogen and oxygen gas, and so on. This spell is normally used to neutralize dangerous or otherwise unwanted compounds and mixtures such as hydrogen cyanide or toxic waste, or to refine out metals, as with the production of mercury from cinnabar (mercuric oxide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T23:09:46-07:00","id":1223125,"title":"","content":"I like that one.<br /> <br /> Something that came up in my last game.<br /> <br /> Blind (Forces 2)<br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Survival, Subtefuge<br /> <br /> The Mage robs the subject of his sense of sight, disabling it's abillity to percieve the electromagnetic spektrum. This causes the severe version of the Blinded titl.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The mage also takes away their hearing causing the Deafened tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:37:58-07:00","id":1223176,"title":"","content":"that sounds more like Life ... 3 maybe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:40:15-07:00","id":1223177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223113#post1223113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dissolution (Matter 3)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Structure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Science<br /> <br /> This spell separates the target into its various elemental components. A piece of graphite will collapse into carbon nanopowder, a sapphire into aluminum dust, which will immediately react with the oxygen to form alumina nanopowder. Water becomes hydrogen and oxygen gas, and so on. This spell is normally used to neutralize dangerous or otherwise unwanted compounds and mixtures such as hydrogen cyanide or toxic waste, or to refine out metals, as with the production of mercury from cinnabar (mercuric oxide).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How much material can this effect at once? I think this counts as Lasting too, not sure what that means though. Also, I assume this doesn't work on animals and plants without conjunctional Life 3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:56:09-07:00","id":1223184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223177#post1223177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much material can this effect at once? I think this counts as Lasting too, not sure what that means though. Also, I assume this doesn't work on animals and plants without conjunctional Life 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have to affect an amount of material equal to Scale, probably Size specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:57:10-07:00","id":1223185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quot