://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:50:27-07:00","id":1223210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223199#post1223199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size is already factored into the Withstand. Good luck pulling this on a house (Structure 33), or even a car (Structure 13). Scale would be needed to affect multiple subjects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Withstand of objects is determined by Durability, not Structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:02:04-07:00","id":1223220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223185#post1223185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not, light is something that falls under the purview of Forces, and as such light can be Veiled by Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the description threw me off. I guess it's more like you're veiling the subject's eyes from light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:33:29-07:00","id":1223234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223220#post1223220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah the description threw me off. I guess it's more like you're veiling the subject's eyes from light.</div> </div> </div> </div>More accurately you\u2019re Veiling the light from their eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:49:39-07:00","id":1223245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223208#post1223208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you need Death 3 for it to work on a corpse? Would Spirit 3 allow you to see what spirits are made of?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you'd need Death to use it on a corpse, and spirits aren't composed of conventional matter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223210#post1223210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Withstand of objects is determined by Durability, not Structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose Structure because the purpose of the spell is to break down the entire object, and the best way to represent that is with Structure for the Withstand. It's meant primarily as a lab or workshop tool, not an attack spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-30-2018, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:52:48-07:00","id":1223246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223245#post1223245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'd need Death to use it on a corpse, and spirits aren't composed of conventional matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But maybe they are composed of something similar but out of phase with matter as we know it.<br /> <br /> Wait, are you saying you could just do it with Spirit 3 if you don't care about messing up the local Shadow like a chain of Dominoes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T07:57:17-07:00","id":1223248,"title":"","content":"I suppose that in principle, one could do something similar with Spirit 3, assuming spirits are composed of something analogous to elements. I have no idea what effect this would have on the material world, and it's safe to assume that other spirits in the vicinity are likely to become very hostile toward anyone who does such a thing, or even tries it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:17:18-07:00","id":1223261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223245#post1223245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you'd need Death to use it on a corpse, and spirits aren't composed of conventional matter.<br /> I chose Structure because the purpose of the spell is to break down the entire object, and the best way to represent that is with Structure for the Withstand. It's meant primarily as a lab or workshop tool, not an attack spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Withstand you\u2019re supposed to use the trait that represents resistance, for objects that trait is Durability. Structure is the representation of an object\u2019s health, if this was an attack spell to destroy objects it would just reduce structure by Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-30-2018, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:51:10-07:00","id":1223277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223208#post1223208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you need Death 3 for it to work on a corpse? Would Spirit 3 allow you to see what spirits are made of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are made of Essence that\u2019s coalesced into a sentient being. You could undo a Spirit but it would require attacking it with Fraying, Unraveling or Unmaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T09:37:29-07:00","id":1223298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1223245#post1223245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chose Structure because the purpose of the spell is to break down the entire object, and the best way to represent that is with Structure for the Withstand. It's meant primarily as a lab or workshop tool, not an attack spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mrmdubois is right. You always use a Resistance trait when deciding Withstand. Hence why spells that affect the body of a person will have Stamina as Withstand rather than Health or Size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:45:42-07:00","id":1224759,"title":"","content":"Find the Balance (Matter 2)<br /> <br /> As the base spell (<i>M:tA 2nd</i>, pg. 155), with the following additional Reach option:<br /> <br /> &quot;+1 Reach: The tool seems to zig and zag almost of its own accord. It won't quite move on its own, but by shifting the internal composition of its balance from moment-to-moment, the mage can wield it in ways that even the greatest masters might envy. Add a number of equipment tags (<i>Hurt Locker</i>, pg. 141) equal to Potency, choosing from the following list: Accurate, Bleed, Brawl, Enhance, Grapple, Guard, Knockdown, Piercing, Reach, Stun, Thrown. If you also possess Forces 2, you can add the Incendiary tag as well. (References to Ghost Rider when doing so may, at Storyteller discretion, add a +1 bonus to the casting roll...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T06:03:14-07:00","id":1224937,"title":"","content":"Reading rainbow<br /> Time unveiling<br /> <br /> While postcognition allows for a detailed vision and &quot;video scrubbing&quot; this allows you to broadly learn the past of subjects in an area.<br /> <br /> learn the number of dots in each skill category and attribute category of each subject. Also learn of notable events in their past (use temporal sympathy chart for a guideline)<br /> <br /> 1 reach: apply potency as a bonus to social and investigation rolls, knowledge of the past is a powerful tool in building rapport and casing crime scenes.<br /> <br /> 1 reach: apply potency to surprise rolls - this isn't so much a preternatural awareness as a prediction based on patterns of past violence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T06:22:57-07:00","id":1224940,"title":"","content":"Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T05:11:43-07:00","id":1225548,"title":"","content":"One of my players in my chronicle has a dot of Fate but struggles a bit what he can do with dot. Anyone got some low-dot Fate effects that aren't &quot;You're lucky now&quot; and &quot;Deal with destiny in some way&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T05:18:37-07:00","id":1225549,"title":"","content":"Well, simple compelling is enough to make a coin flip in your favor or a slot machine pay out big (or small for a competitor) you'll win any non supernatural gambling with ease and pinache. Anything with clear odds can be compelled towards a desired outcome.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite abilities in a game is Final Shot.A melee variant called Final Hit let you maintain a combo without knocking enemies away and teleporting from enemy to enemy. Essentially allowing you to aim much faster and teleport during a fight. The Korean grindfest Mabinogi still has my favorite combat system of any MMO.<br /> <br /> <br /> Final Shot/Hit<br /> Space Patterning (or weaving if modeled after a large area Co-Location)<br /> The subject may teleport to a spot in sensory range a number of times equal to potency, while the spell is active.<br /> 1 reach: The subject may choose to teleport reflexively.<br /> 1 reach: ignore penalties to called shots equal to potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 06-07-2018, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T06:05:57-07:00","id":1225554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1225548#post1225548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players in my chronicle has a dot of Fate but struggles a bit what he can do with dot. Anyone got some low-dot Fate effects that aren't &quot;You're lucky now&quot; and &quot;Deal with destiny in some way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Luck and Destiny is basically it for Fate, but they're so wide fields that you can do quite a lot as long as you're just creative about it. Here are some smaller themes I've recognised:<br /> Blessings, Hexes, probabilities, oaths, destinies and conditional effects.<br /> \u2022 Blessings are most useful if you use them to grant Steadfast and Charmed to yourself and your cabal. Extra dice and dice tricks can also be nice if you have a turn to prepare yourself. Anyone who dabbles in Fate should get Exceptional Luck as a Rote just because of this.<br /> \u2022 Hexes can be used to apply Arm Wracks, Leg Wracks and Blinded to enemies in a combat situation.<br /> \u2022 Probabilities can be manipulated to make a fortune in gambling, as mentioned, but also to make you find the person you're looking for or even allow you to correctly guess passwords and phone numbers. With Serendipity you can even stumble upon stuff you didn't even know you needed, but can't be guaranteed to be particularly effective.<br /> \u2022 At the first dot you can use oaths to find out whether or not someone has fulfilled or broken an agreement. At the third dot you can supernaturally enforce any stated punishments for breaking the agreement.<br /> \u2022 You can recognise or shield an existing destiny at low dot levels, but most interesting effects are at later dots.<br /> \u2022 At two dots you get Conditional Duration as an Attainment, which allows spells to end when they're no longer useful. This is particularly useful in combination with Hung Spell from Time 2. Warding Gesture is at the same dot, allowing you to selectively exclude your subjects from AoE spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:03:05-07:00","id":1225564,"title":"","content":"Yeah those are core book spells but if you just limit things to that it makes the whole arcanum pretty umaginative. The core has some nice cool spells that aren't luck or destiny based (Shared Fate for instance) so I was wondering whether someone has some nice low-dot examples.<br /> <br /> I know the Arcanum can be pretty usefull. I just want to give my player some ideas without it being &quot;get bonus dice/rerolls&quot; or it being incredibly safe contained like Oaths. Just some general usefull effects, found a few in this thread when i was browsing it earlier but I'd really appreciate more. Cause my player has a bit of problem in what he can do with the Arcanum<br /> <br /> Things I got for one dot:<br /> - winning games of chance<br /> - identifying Bans and Banes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 06-07-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:23:31-07:00","id":1225570,"title":"","content":"Identifying Bans and Banes would be a Knowing spell for the Arcanum/Arcana mostly related to that being. I don't think Fate alone can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:35:49-07:00","id":1225573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1225564#post1225564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah those are core book spells but if you just limit things to that it makes the whole arcanum pretty umaginative. The core has some nice cool spells that aren't luck or destiny based (Shared Fate for instance) so I was wondering whether someone has some nice low-dot examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shared Fate is braiding two destinies together you reap what you sow.<br /> <br /> You can probably read Dooms with Fate 1, but Bans and Banes are something different as noted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> Technically, to even be able to read a Ban or a Bane from an ephemeral creature with Fate alone you'd have to get lucky enough to meet them when they're manifested, otherwise you need the appropriate arcana to even detect them in the first place at which point you might as well use that arcana to read their Ban and Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T07:54:53-07:00","id":1225580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1225564#post1225564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah those are core book spells but if you just limit things to that it makes the whole arcanum pretty umaginative. The core has some nice cool spells that aren't luck or destiny based (Shared Fate for instance) so I was wondering whether someone has some nice low-dot examples.<br /> <br /> I know the Arcanum can be pretty usefull. I just want to give my player some ideas without it being &quot;get bonus dice/rerolls&quot; or it being incredibly safe contained like Oaths. Just some general usefull effects, found a few in this thread when i was browsing it earlier but I'd really appreciate more. Cause my player has a bit of problem in what he can do with the Arcanum<br /> <br /> Things I got for one dot:<br /> - winning games of chance<br /> - identifying Bans and Banes</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Knowing spell to discover Aspirations, perhaps? They fit with the purview of &quot;intentions.&quot; Speaking of intentions, maybe an Unveiling spell where you sense what the other person is trying to get out of you, ie. their goal in their Social Maneuvering actions against you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:33:40-07:00","id":1225591,"title":"","content":"Fate spells outside of the core would be (knowing) aspirations, obsessions, presence of the Destiny merit, perhaps detection of beings with a strong Fate or recent turn of luck (like a web of life but for people who's intentions involve you in some way or have had an exceptional/dramatic during the spell)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:42:39-07:00","id":1225595,"title":"","content":"I think it should be able to do it. Bans and Banes feel like those secret laws a entity must obey, higher levels of Fate can create similar effects. Also stuff like &quot;The one ring can only be destroyed by the fires of the mountain where it was created&quot; feel both very Fate'y and like a Bane. Off course the entity would already have to be manifested or be material to begin with (Horrors and Cryptids are a thing and can have bans of banes) Perhaps a Reach effect on a spell that reads Dooms?<br /> <br /> And I get that Shared Fate bings destinies but what I mean here are effects that you don't use specific things that reference the Destiny merit. Because while those can be naturally present it's not like most people have them.<br /> <br /> I forgot intentions are a part of Fate purview so knowing Apirations is something I haven't considered. Detecting dramatic fail/success can be done by Fate sight so should be able usable as a spell.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What about these, technically they deal with propabillity just not in a &quot;I'm now lucky&quot; manner:<br /> <br /> Calculate odds (Fate 1)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> <br /> The subject of the spell becomes aware of the chance of success of his actions before attempting any action. He always knows if an action will surely fail or surely succed. This might give the subject hints about certain unknown factors existing. And in any other case it will give him a general idea of his success chance. This In normal or resisted rolls it lets him know whether the penalties bring his dice pool above or below 2 dice, while in contested rolls it lets him know whether the opponents dice pool is larger, smaller or equal to his opponent.<br /> +1 Reach: the subject knows the exact penalties and the exact size of an opponents dice pool<br /> <br /> <br /> Flip of a Coin (Fate 1)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> <br /> When faced with 2 choices and no other knowledge the act of choosing is just like a coinflip. The mage determines which of set of 2 courses of action has better consequences for the subject of the spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 06-07-2018, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T05:51:59-07:00","id":1225856,"title":"","content":"Throwing this in there because it's cool. Obviously credit goes to Tessie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224943-space-question?p=1225296#post1225296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Separation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina or Durability<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggest Rote Skills:</b> Intimidation, Larceny, Occult<br /> When distance is a lie, physical connections no longer necessitates spatial connections. This spell causes one part of the subject per Potency to disconnect. The part is still fully functional and anything that would pass through the severed area, such as air, blood, electricity, et.c, simply continues where it would if the part was still connected to the subject. This allows a severed head to breathe, speak, and even eat (if someone were to feed it). When the spell ends the spatial separation is lost and all severed parts return to the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:18:25-07:00","id":1225914,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Frequency Shift</b> (Forces 2)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Science, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By means of this spell, the mage can change the radiation frequency of a given electromagnetic source: shift a fire's light down into the radio spectrum, shift microwaves up into the gamma range, or even turn the IR radiation from her palm into a (weak) night light.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: If applicable, the modulation of a signal can be altered, so an AM signal shifted into FM, or an FM signal shifted into short wave, will remain comprehensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:31:06-07:00","id":1225917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1225914#post1225914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Frequency Shift</b> (Forces 2)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Science, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> By means of this spell, the mage can change the radiation frequency of a given electromagnetic source: shift a fire's light down into the radio spectrum, shift microwaves up into the gamma range, or even turn the IR radiation from her palm into a (weak) night light.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: If applicable, the modulation of a signal can be altered, so an AM signal shifted into FM, or an FM signal shifted into short wave, will remain comprehensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is Weaving at least, but it has some overlap with Transmission, so I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:31:06-07:00","id":1225918,"title":"","content":"Edit: Double-posted somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:42:23-07:00","id":1226484,"title":"","content":"<b>Ignition</b> (Forces 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage causes a combustible object to ignite. Potency 1 is enough for a normally flammable object such as candles, wood or gasoline; a more difficult item such as wet wood, avgas or a tire requires Potency 2. Once begun, the fire burns normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T11:10:59-07:00","id":1226516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1226484#post1226484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ignition</b> (Forces 3)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage causes a combustible object to ignite. Potency 1 is enough for a normally flammable object such as candles, wood or gasoline; a more difficult item such as wet wood, avgas or a tire requires Potency 2. Once begun, the fire burns normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Create Energy does. The fire doesn't yet exist so there's nothing to apply Ruling/Weaving/Perfecting/Fraying on. (Ruling is a two dot Practice while the spell uses Forces 3, which made it a little confusing.)<br /> Making is needed to create fire where there is none while Patterning can seemingly do the same thing by transforming a different type of energy into fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T11:40:52-07:00","id":1226526,"title":"","content":"So... lighting a fire is only barely shy of Archmagery? Are you serious? It's actually easier to fly, a blatantly unnatural act, than to start a normal chemical reaction?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I meant to type Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T11:56:29-07:00","id":1226532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1226526#post1226526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... lighting a fire is only barely shy of Archmagery? Are you serious? It's actually easier to fly, a blatantly unnatural act, than to start a normal chemical reaction?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I meant to type Forces 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lighting a fire is incredibly easy. <i>Creating</i> a fire is a whole different matter. You can probably use Forces 2 or 3 to increase the existing heat until the object self combusts, thereby lighting it.<br /> The Practices has defined effects. That's the price to pay for a consistent magic system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T12:18:27-07:00","id":1226542,"title":"","content":"So why were you saying that igniting a flammable object takes Forces 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T12:25:52-07:00","id":1226546,"title":"","content":"I think what he meant is that lighting a flamable object fire indirectly (like, say by manipulating heat) is incredibly easy but your spell states &quot;stuff ignites&quot; which actually requires Making practice.<br /> <br /> Yes, despite it being a simple magic trick in other games it's incredibly difficult in Mage, same as some other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T12:35:25-07:00","id":1226550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1226542#post1226542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why were you saying that igniting a flammable object takes Forces 5?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>I didn't.</i><br /> <br /> I said that &quot;Making is needed to create fire where there is none&quot; which I wrote because your spell seems to create fire spontaneously since you included no explanation for how it does it. <i>In the very same sentence</i> I also offered a lower dot alternative to light a fire without creating it.<br /> I get that the magic system can be confusing if you're not used to it, but once you do get a hang of it it's actually a huge advantage to have so clearly defined Practices since that gives you a great guideline for homebrew spells rather than trying to just estimate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T12:38:00-07:00","id":1226551,"title":"","content":"It does seem rather odd, but you have to consider the basis of how magic works in Mage the Awakening. Flying is basically Patterning the forces around the designated area (typically yourself) to allow you to move through the air. You also will notice that you are not very fast while doing this since you are actually not &quot;flying&quot; in a normal sense. However, a Life 4 spell could grant you wings to allow yourself to literally fly.<br /> <br /> That being said, lighting an object on fire would be a Patterning Practice (based on 1E Adamantine Arrow Source Book included a spell called 'Firebolt') not near Archmastery, but a significant power for sure. Create Energy allows you to make fire in a space that is completely devoid of oxygen for example, while not extremely useful it is something<br /> <br /> One could also argue Create Energy allows you to use Fireball when you are in the state of twilight since technically &quot;Firebolt&quot; may not work there. However, I think that comes down to a ST decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T14:57:26-07:00","id":1226575,"title":"","content":"<b>Ignition</b> (Forces 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Thermal energy is abundant and omnipresent in all but the most frigid of environments; by concentrating this ambient energy into a very small volume, the mage causes a combustible object to ignite. Potency 1 is enough for a normally flammable object such as candles, wood or gasoline; a more difficult item such as wet wood, avgas or a tire requires Potency 2. Add one to the required Potency in sub-freezing environments. Once begun, the fire burns normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T15:11:59-07:00","id":1226579,"title":"","content":"You really don\u2019t have to say that fire acts like fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T15:57:37-07:00","id":1226596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1226575#post1226575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ignition</b> (Forces 2)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Thermal energy is abundant and omnipresent in all but the most frigid of environments; by concentrating this ambient energy into a very small volume, the mage causes a combustible object to ignite. Potency 1 is enough for a normally flammable object such as candles, wood or gasoline; a more difficult item such as wet wood, avgas or a tire requires Potency 2. Add one to the required Potency in sub-freezing environments. Once begun, the fire burns normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that I'm the one who suggested that it could be done using &quot;Forces 2 or 3&quot; but it might be a little more complicated than that. Since the effect of the spell is about increasing the heat until the object ignites, the spell should primarily be about controlling the heat rather than jumping straight to the ignition. I think it would be a version of the already existing Control Heat spell, but one that works on objects rather than environments. Since there is already a chart about different energy levels used by various Forces spells, I'll reference that. Here's my take on it:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Control Temperature (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Science, Survival<br /> The mage may change the internal temperature of an object. For each level of Potency, the mage chooses to decrease or increase the temperature by one level (see the chart under Transform Energy on page 146). If used to raise the temperature enough, the subject may spontaneously ignite.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> By focusing the heat to a specific point within the subject, the effective temperature threshold for autoignition is lowered by one level. If the threshold is outside the scope of the chart but still within 400\u00b0 C, it will ignite if the spell reaches level 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since I've replied to you several times now, I think it might be good to explain this about myself: I know that I can come off as condescending when I try to correct or explain stuff, but that is not my intention. I'm just trying to be educational and helpful, and I hope that's the tone I'm expressing. Also, since I'm not a writer this is just my subjective take on the system so I might actually be off about some of the stuff, even if I think I have a pretty good grasp on it. Regardless, you're always free to redefine the limitations of the system to create your own balance, if you'd prefer that. It's always more important to have fun with the game than following the rules to the letter, as long as all players agree on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-11-2018, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T22:16:02-07:00","id":1230747,"title":"","content":"I do hope that you realize that this spell, as written, makes it harder to start a fire by magical means than by using stone age methods. Literally. Potency 5 is -10 dice to the spell casting role, so to be able to roll one success with even modest reliably (let's say two chances in three) after that requires at least three dice. So the caster needs Concentration, High Speech and Runes for +6 dice. That's still six dice short of the two in three threshed of 13 dice. So Gnosis 4, Forces 2, and you're at 12. Add a second ritual period for an extra die, at that's the 13 dice minimum. So that's a fairly powerful mage spending two hours to light ordinary tinder. And that's the absolute minimum requirement. I suppose you could lower the Gnosis a little by dropping Yantras and increasing the extra intervals, but it's still pretty ridiculous that a spell to ignite a flammable object (my original intent) is so difficult that in practical terms, it's utterly worthless. This spell as written is inferior to Survival 1 as a method of lighting a fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T22:40:56-07:00","id":1230750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230747#post1230747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that you realize that this spell, as written, makes it harder to start a fire by magical means than by using stone age methods. Literally. Potency 5 is -10 dice to the spell casting role, so to be able to roll one success with even modest reliably (let's say two chances in three) after that requires at least three dice. So the caster needs Concentration, High Speech and Runes for +6 dice. That's still six dice short of the two in three threshed of 13 dice. So Gnosis 4, Forces 2, and you're at 12. Add a second ritual period for an extra die, at that's the 13 dice minimum. So that's a fairly powerful mage spending two hours to light ordinary tinder. And that's the absolute minimum requirement. I suppose you could lower the Gnosis a little by dropping Yantras and increasing the extra intervals, but it's still pretty ridiculous that a spell to ignite a flammable object (my original intent) is so difficult that in practical terms, it's utterly worthless. This spell as written is inferior to Survival 1 as a method of lighting a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious fix is to spend 1 Reach and change the primary factor to Potency. Although, I think perhaps the primary factor ought to be Potency from the outset. Maybe it should also be Perfecting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-28-2018, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T05:48:30-07:00","id":1230775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230747#post1230747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that you realize that this spell, as written, makes it harder to start a fire by magical means than by using stone age methods. Literally. Potency 5 is -10 dice to the spell casting role, so to be able to roll one success with even modest reliably (let's say two chances in three) after that requires at least three dice. So the caster needs Concentration, High Speech and Runes for +6 dice. That's still six dice short of the two in three threshed of 13 dice. So Gnosis 4, Forces 2, and you're at 12. Add a second ritual period for an extra die, at that's the 13 dice minimum. So that's a fairly powerful mage spending two hours to light ordinary tinder. And that's the absolute minimum requirement. I suppose you could lower the Gnosis a little by dropping Yantras and increasing the extra intervals, but it's still pretty ridiculous that a spell to ignite a flammable object (my original intent) is so difficult that in practical terms, it's utterly worthless. This spell as written is inferior to Survival 1 as a method of lighting a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The increase from level 1 to level 5 requires 4 Potency, and you always start with 1 Potency so the required increase of 3 Potency results in a -6 penalty. At Gnosis 4, Forces 2 you're at zero dice before adding Yantras. With both mantra and concentration you increase that to 4 dice. The Reach is spent on Instant Casting, meaning it takes two turns to cast the spell. How long does it take for someone with Survival to start a fire?<br /> <br /> If the mage instead has Forces 3, they gain one additional Reach. If that Reach is spent on changing the Primary Factor to Potency, the spell automatically starts with 3 Potency. That's a -2 penalty to increase to 4. At lowest possible Gnosis this means the mage has a dice pool of 2 before adding any Yantras. Destroy some kindling for a +1 sacrament if you need to get the casting time down to 1 turn instead of using a mantra.<br /> <br /> Or the mage comes prepared with something with a lower autoignition temperature, like a tablet of white sulphur to put in an unlit fireplace. Then you don't need to increase Potency at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-28-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:08:49-07:00","id":1230803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230747#post1230747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope that you realize that this spell, as written, makes it harder to start a fire by magical means than by using stone age methods. Literally.</div> </div> </div> </div>A starting character will succeed at this in the space of less than ten seconds, more often than not, with a simple willpower expenditure and minimal (or zero, depending on the circumstances) risk of material consequences from Paradox. Literally.<br /> <br /> Reach: Primary Factor, Instant, Ignition Threshold (Adv. Dur is not needed, once the material ignites it will be Lasting)<br /> Potency: 5 (-6 dice from Base Potency 2)<br /> Yantras: +3 (High Speech, Path Tool)<br /> Dice Pool: 3 (0 Base, +3 for WP)<br /> <br /> A mage with more experience, or access to better Yantras (eg. Shadow Name) will obviously have proportionally higher levels of success and require less resources - this writeup is for a character that meets the <i>bare minimum </i>requirements of the spell. The spell does seem like it makes this a bit harder than maybe it should be, though I think that'd be resolved by allowing the Reach effect for lowering the auto-ignition threshold by a level to be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> While I agree with the vague sentiment of your post, your use of hyperbole when taken with your apparent lack of experience with the system <b>do you no credit</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-28-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:26:18-07:00","id":1230810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230775#post1230775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Reach is spent on Instant Casting, meaning it takes two turns to cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just plain wrong. P327:<span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ritual casting may extend casting time. +1 die per ritual interval, max. +5. Ritual interval is not instant. Ritual interval is determined by Gnosis, so </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">that's</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> two hours, not two turns. I happen to know that lighting a fire with a neolithic fire kit takes about twenty minutes on average. Less if you have particular good conditions. Stepping up to Iron Age methods, flint and steel takes a few seconds if you're practiced and have a tinderbox handy.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:29:08-07:00","id":1230811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230803#post1230803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your use of hyperbole when taken with your apparent lack of experience with the system <b>do you no credit</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't being hyperbolic. As far as I could tell, I was being accurate. That said, I like this formulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T07:55:42-07:00","id":1230816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230810#post1230810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just plain wrong. P327:<span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ritual casting may extend casting time. +1 die per ritual interval, max. +5. Ritual interval is not instant. Ritual interval is determined by Gnosis, so </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">that's</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> two hours, not two turns. I happen to know that lighting a fire with a neolithic fire kit takes about twenty minutes on average. Less if you have particular good conditions. Stepping up to Iron Age methods, flint and steel takes a few seconds if you're practiced and have a tinderbox handy.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Common Reach Effects<br /> Most spells list Reach effects, and several<br /> Attainments that modify spellcasting require Reach<br /> to use. In addition to these, one Reach may:<br /> <b>\u2022 Move the spell from Ritual to Instant Casting Time</b>&quot;<br /> Page 112<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>By using a Reach, a caster may instead cast immediately, in a<br /> single turn.</b> Immediate spells cannot gain extra dice from taking<br /> extra time, but may take several turns of preparation to use all<br /> the Yantras the caster wishes to include.&quot;<br /> Page 114","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T10:25:40-07:00","id":1230855,"title":"","content":"Casting time and ritual interval are not automatically the same thing. It is possible to cast a spell instantly rather that casting it over the course of a ritual interval. You spend this reach to move from Ritual to Instant Casting Time. Ritual Interval is a type of Casting Time. Moving from Ritual Interval to Instant Casting does not change the value for Ritual Interval. Ritual Interval is determined by Gnosis. And from the quote you yourself supplied, &quot;Immediate spells cannot gain extra dice from taking extra time.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T10:48:56-07:00","id":1230861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230855#post1230855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting time and ritual interval are not automatically the same thing. It is possible to cast a spell instantly rather that casting it over the course of a ritual interval. You spend this reach to move from Ritual to Instant Casting Time. Ritual Interval is a type of Casting Time. Moving from Ritual Interval to Instant Casting does not change the value for Ritual Interval. Ritual Interval is determined by Gnosis. And from the quote you yourself supplied, &quot;Immediate spells cannot gain extra dice from taking extra time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No one argued that they were the same, they were pointing out that you do not -have- to spend several hours starting a fire with magic if you don't want to. They provided that information because you seemed to be operating under the misconception that Mages have to spend more time starting a fire than mortals, which is obviously and patently untrue if you move to Instant Casting time.<br /> <br /> Now if you're specifically grumbling about the constraints of GRI on making fire, then in most cases magic moves slower than mortal means to do mundane things until you hit higher levels of Gnosis and I fail to see why fire making should be any exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-28-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T11:42:06-07:00","id":1230878,"title":"","content":"No, I was speaking of Tessie's claim that you can spend Reach to reduce casting time to instant, then spend turns instead of full ritual intervals to gain the benefits of spending time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T11:54:04-07:00","id":1230880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230878#post1230878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I was speaking of Tessie's claim that you can spend Reach to reduce casting time to instant, then spend turns instead of full ritual intervals to gain the benefits of spending time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the reason Tessie said it takes two turns to cast the spell is because of the fact that there are two yantras involved and only one of them can be used reflexively; each yantra after the first adds a turn of casting time to an instant cast spell.<br /> <br /> It's not about stacking ritual interval. You can note that her write-up does not include any bonuses for extra interval, unless I'm missing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T12:38:45-07:00","id":1230895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230878#post1230878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I was speaking of Tessie's claim that you can spend Reach to reduce casting time to instant, then spend turns instead of full ritual intervals to gain the benefits of spending time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230880#post1230880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that the reason Tessie said it takes two turns to cast the spell is because of the fact that there are two yantras involved and only one of them can be used reflexively; each yantra after the first adds a turn of casting time to an instant cast spell.<br /> <br /> It's not about stacking ritual interval. You can note that her write-up does not include any bonuses for extra interval, unless I'm missing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I never claimed that it's possible to spend turns to gain bonus dice, and if you look at the math you'll see that the only bonuses comes from Yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T14:09:29-07:00","id":1230917,"title":"","content":"I think that the...practicality? physicality? of Forces and Matter contributes to fairly legalistic effect design, whereas we see less argument about, say, how much Potency it takes to stretch or compress <i>spacetime</i>.<br /> <br /> I suspect I'd let someone with kindling and two sticks use Forces Compelling to accelerate lighting the fire (just as you can use Influence Electricity to instantly hot-wire a car.)<br /> <br /> Given that you can use Control Sound and Light to replicate some changes in shape (that might fall under Weaving or Patterning if the subject was something else), I'd be inclined to imagine that you can use Ruling to condense room temperature heat into a lighter's worth of ignition (they're both on the same line of Transform Energy) which would be sufficient to ignite materials that a lighter could, but that'd be the limit of that - you couldn't add Potency to the effect to burn more durable materials, etc.<br /> <br /> (If you used Shielding to keep an object from radiating the heat it receives ambiently from the environment, about how quickly would that accumulate to ignition levels?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T14:24:15-07:00","id":1230920,"title":"","content":"For a spell whose sole purpose is igniting tinder, I think a simple Compelling spell would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> For a broad-spectrum temperature control spell, Tessie's works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T21:20:06-07:00","id":1231006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1230917#post1230917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(If you used Shielding to keep an object from radiating the heat it receives ambiently from the environment, about how quickly would that accumulate to ignition levels?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just off the top of my head, assuming clear summer weather and a piece of untreated dry pine, just over a month. Assume a gain of approximately 1 degree Celsius per hour and an initial temperature of 20, that means 407 degrees. With about twelve hours a day of useful sunlight, that comes to 407 hours, call it 408 to keep the arithmetic simple. 408/12=34 days. You're better off using Forces 1 to make a burning glass equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T22:12:39-07:00","id":1231018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1231006#post1231006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just off the top of my head, assuming clear summer weather and a piece of untreated dry pine, just over a month. Assume a gain of approximately 1 degree Celsius per hour and an initial temperature of 20, that means 407 degrees. With about twelve hours a day of useful sunlight, that comes to 407 hours, call it 408 to keep the arithmetic simple. 408/12=34 days. You're better off using Forces 1 to make a burning glass equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 degree per hour seems way too low. I'd guess it takes more like a few minutes. Let's say a burning glass focuses sunlight x100, and sets fire to something in 10 seconds. With our hypothetical spell to make no heat dissipate from the surface (or percolate too far down into the body of the object), that means that with x1 focus, you'd need 1000 seconds.<br /> <br /> So yeah, burning glass is totally the way to go (10 seconds, rather than 1000) if you've got sunlight. I'd say that's Forces 2 rather than 1 though, since it sounds exactly like Control Light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T22:31:41-07:00","id":1231020,"title":"","content":"That's a distinct oddity in the Forces spells. Forces 1 can influence electricity, fire and heat, transduce radio energy to sound, but can't do a thing with light if you go by the Control Light write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T23:49:30-07:00","id":1231035,"title":"","content":"Forces 1 can nudge a preferred, but possible outcome of things light can already do. Some of the things that Control Light can do probably fit comfortably under the Compelling Practice (For instance, prismatic diffraction, or simulating a heat mirage), though dimming, brightening or changing its direction is under the 2 dot Practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:44:26-07:00","id":1234763,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Slow Fall (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> While under the influence of the this spell, the subject falls less quickly than normal. Reduce the effective distance fallen by (3*Potency). Any fall not onto a damaging surface, such as sharp rocks or a spike fence, does bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T15:22:14-07:00","id":1234799,"title":"","content":"I like it. Dividing the effective distance per Potency would be more elegant, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T23:58:20-07:00","id":1234878,"title":"","content":"You could also go the route of Alchemist's Touch, Potency converts Lethal damage to Bashing and for +2 Reach you could simply say no damage is taken at all regardless of the drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T01:12:40-07:00","id":1234889,"title":"","content":"With this description I think the Shielding practice is the wrong one. To actually directly slow the fall would be a fraying practice, though ruling could essentially achieve the same effect by optimising wind pressure and friction. A shielding spell would simply protect the beneficient from the negative effects of the impact.<br /> <br /> Systems wise I'd let a shielding spell negate one point of damage per potency and reduce all lethal damage from the fall to bashing damage as a reach effect. Dividing the fall distance by potency would be the mechanics I'd use for a fraying spell (and actually that spell does allready exist, it's just another use of Velocity Control).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:33:05-07:00","id":1235001,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Slow Fall (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> While under the influence of the this spell, the subject falls less quickly than normal. Divide the effective distance fallen by the spell's Potency for purpose of determining damage. Any fall not onto a damaging surface, such as sharp rocks or a spiked fence, does bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T02:07:36-07:00","id":1235219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1235001#post1235001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any fall not onto a damaging surface, such as sharp rocks or a spiked fence, does bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part would imo work better as a reach effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T02:03:20-07:00","id":1237440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1235001#post1235001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Slow Fall (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> While under the influence of the this spell, the subject falls less quickly than normal. Divide the effective distance fallen by the spell's Potency for purpose of determining damage. Any fall not onto a damaging surface, such as sharp rocks or a spiked fence, does bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably replace Occult with Science but otherwise it looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:13:17-07:00","id":1237470,"title":"","content":"As far as Shielding and Forces go, what about a Faraday Cage? A spell to keep electromagnetic signals out (or in)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T06:58:05-07:00","id":1237484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1237470#post1237470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Shielding and Forces go, what about a Faraday Cage? A spell to keep electromagnetic signals out (or in)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly valid, I would say. Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T07:02:46-07:00","id":1237486,"title":"","content":"Slightly edited:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Slow Fall (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> While under the influence of the this spell, the subject falls less quickly than normal. Divide the effective distance fallen by the spell's Potency+1 for purpose of determining damage.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>Any fall not onto a damaging surface, such as sharp rocks or a spiked fence, does bashing damage.<br /> <br /> I realized that as written, the spell was useless at Potency 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:38:50-07:00","id":1240692,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Umbrella (Matter \u2022\u2022)</i><br /> Practice: </b>Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> While under the influence of this spell, a liquid chosen at the time of casting is repelled from the subject. This reduces penalties or damage caused by that liquid by Potency. This does not allow the subject to walk on liquids, because the liquid is forced away from the person, but does allow for such things as walking across a lake's bottom, or the channel of a lava flow (though the radiant heat would still be a problem). If used against water, it works as a truly superb umbrella at even Potency 1.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The caster can permit specific instances of the chosen liquid to pass, as with a magician repelling water who wants to take a drink or a shower.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The caster can walk on the chosen liquid (Dex+Athletics rolls might be required)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 01-23-2019, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:45:20-07:00","id":1240708,"title":"","content":"I would change the wording to a liquid being repelled from the subject of the spell, not the caster, even if usually those are the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:16:07-07:00","id":1240878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1240692#post1240692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Umbrella (Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Lodestone (Matter \u2022) can already do that. Only the second Reach is outside the scope of Lodestone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-31-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T10:00:38-07:00","id":1240920,"title":"","content":"I considered that, but Lodestone can only make things move in directions they could move naturally. You can't even draw water across a flat surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T22:46:54-07:00","id":1241180,"title":"","content":"So, how do people feel about this optional reach on Wards and Signs? A version you cast on your enemies instead of your friends.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Wards and Signs (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Withstand provided by this spell cannot be voluntarily lowered by its subject, only by the spell's caster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T00:21:30-07:00","id":1241192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1241180#post1241180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do people feel about this optional reach on Wards and Signs? A version you cast on your enemies instead of your friends.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Wards and Signs (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Shielding<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The Withstand provided by this spell cannot be voluntarily lowered by its subject, only by the spell's caster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly legit, I assume this is to debuff a potential spell subject by making them too difficult to cast on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:35:04-07:00","id":1241217,"title":"","content":"I believe the only Withstand that can be voluntarily lowered in the first place are those based on the subject's own traits. For example, you can't voluntarily lower temporal or sympathetic Withstand.<br /> Here's my counter proposals:<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The caster is now able to voluntarily lower the Withstand rating granted by this spell if he is aware that a spell is cast on the subject.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject is now able to voluntarily lower the Withstand rating granted by this spell if she is aware that a spell is cast on her.<br /> <br /> Combining the two into one Reach option also makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T17:33:34-07:00","id":1246483,"title":"","content":"Whoa Ophidimancer! You're still kickin' it in the Mage Sphere huh? It's Aenru from the early days. Do you remember me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>..............","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21103-mindflower","name":"Mindflower","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T01:53:34-07:00","id":1246576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mindflower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1246483#post1246483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa Ophidimancer! You're still kickin' it in the Mage Sphere huh? It's Aenru from the early days. Do you remember me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ophidimancer's last activity on this forum was over a year ago. You'll have to PM them and hope they have mail notifications for PMs if you want to contact them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T08:00:28-07:00","id":1252216,"title":"","content":"So, Dispel Magic and Supernal Dispellation both use the &quot;Spells can be cancelled&quot; quality to work. Hung Spell interacts with another spell's Imago to work.<br /> <br /> What would be the Practice (Arcana being Prime) for rewriting a spell (or, ideally, a subject's spells) Target parameter to a fixed value (like &quot;Self&quot;)? Goal it to prevent magic being cast upon others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T09:14:35-07:00","id":1252233,"title":"","content":"Messing with spells of other mages has been stated to fall under the imperial practices iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:26:29-07:00","id":1252265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1252233#post1252233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Messing with spells of other mages has been stated to fall under the imperial practices iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cite Dispel Magic and Hung Spell as examples to the contrary. Those <i>are</i> limited interactions (and voluntary, in Hung Spell's case), I'll grant, but they are there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T09:11:24-07:00","id":1252523,"title":"","content":"I don't think that restriction is explicitly stated anywhere in 2E anyway, and it wouldn't be the first example of something that used to require archmastery in 1E that no longer does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T14:05:05-07:00","id":1252599,"title":"","content":"So, would Prime 4 (Patterning) make sense? Single spell, or would all spells cast by the target(s) make sense? Would it need Space in addition to or instead to represent the warping of &quot;Target&quot; to &quot;Here&quot;? Any other caveats or limitations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T21:35:02-07:00","id":1256885,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood Magic (Space 3 + Life 1)</b><br /> <b>Practise:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Brawl, Medicine<br /> <br /> Some would argue vampires or hedge mages are practitioners of blood magic. Tamers of the Blood or those who find a grimoire with this spell will disagree. A stern and resolved twist of more common warping or healing magic, Blood magic inflicts one bashing damage to a target per point potency by violently drawling blood out of a living target through frayed space. This particular spell, to those that know about or lived through it know the terrifying affects that a tamer of the blood can reap through this spell and the connections they can drawl from it.<br /> +1 reach: Blood drawn from the target is drawn to a caster's hand or person and held in a tiny ban in the mages hand or on their person for the duration of the spell. This sphere of blood counts as a material sympathy yantra (+2 two dice) against the target, or a +1 die sacrament yantra.<br /> +1 reach: For one point of mana blood held by the above reach can be reflexively spent as +1 sacrament yantra on the <i>next</i> spell cast during the duration as long as the target's blood could count as one.<br /> +1 reach: Blood maybe drawn in the most painful way possible. The spell also inflicts an additional \u20131 wound penalty on top of any already suffered by means other then this spell. This may count as a sin against enlightened wisdom with a unproved attacked.<br /> Add Prime Three: For every one mana and potency spent captured blood may endure to be used as a sacramental yantra one more time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","user":"HarbingerLeo","date":".  Tweaked based on lnodiv's comments. 09-30-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T22:07:08-07:00","id":1257089,"title":"","content":"<b>Lullaby (Life 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> Sometimes you need to be subtle. Sometimes you have to chase a dangerous ghost into a museum, and the security guards pulling their guns don't know your trying to save their life. They just know the mage looks a awful lot like a person breaking in! Sometimes your a comic book super villain that wants to gloat over the sleeping bodies of your enemy while you carry out your dastardly plan. A common tactic is to use this spell in tandem with smoke grenades or hissing sound noise makers, allowing a sleeper's quintessence to fill in the gaps that the smoke or unseen gas is what poisons them. Later (or later magics) leaving no traces to find.<br /> <br /> Lullaby takes control of a bodies natural energy reserve rhythms. Then proceeds to rapidly draining a body of it's energy reserves and prevents them from renewing. A subject may not heal bashing damage while under the affects of Lullaby. Any life spells cast against this subject that inflicts bashing damage may be have their imago altered at no penalty to not rollover bashing damage to lethal or aggravated damage.<br /> +1 reach: Lullyaby may add a stacking -1 die any roll to stay conscious per point of potency. This is withstood by a subject's stamina.<br /> +1 reach: If rendered unconscious while under the affects of Lullaby the subject immediately enters their natural sleep cycle. While Lullaby stays in affect they may not wake without another spell provoking a clash of wills. Afterward they continue to sleep, but may wake whenever they naturally would.<br /> +1 reach: A mage may actually sing. Rolling express or other storyteller approved skill rolls with this spell. Each success in that roll counts as one extra bashing damage to be used only when checking to see if a subject remains conscious. If the spell last more then one turn successes may accumulate toward this goal. A story teller may add or remove dice depending on how appropriate a particular song is. Singing a actual lullaby may provide a bonus. Singing a punk rock song about fighting may provide a penalty.<br /> Add any arcanum: Any spell of that arcaum that inflicts bashing damage may have their imago altered to not roll bashing damage over to lethal or aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","user":"HarbingerLeo","date":"cleaned the description. 09-26-2018, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T09:37:45-07:00","id":1258218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HarbingerLeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1256885#post1256885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blood Magic (Space 3 + Life 3)</b><br /> <b>Practise:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Brawl, Medicine<br /> <br /> Some would argue vampires or hedge mages are practitioners of blood magic. Tamers of the Blood or those who find a grimoire with this spell will disagree. A stern and resolved twist of more common warping or healing magic, Blood magic inflicts one bashing damage to a target per point potency by violently drawling blood out of a living target through frayed space. This particular spell, to those that know about or lived through it know the terrifying affects that a tamer of the blood can reap through this spell and the connections they can drawl from it.<br /> +1 reach: Blood drawn from the target is drawn to a caster's hand or person and held in a tiny ban in the mages hand or on their person for the duration of the spell. This sphere of blood counts as a material sympathy yantras (+2 two dice) against the target, or a +1 die sacrament yantras.<br /> +1 reach: For one point of mana blood held by the above reach can be reflexively spent as +1 sacrament yantras on the <i>next</i> spell cast during the duration as long as the target's blood could count as one.<br /> +1 reach: Blood maybe drawn in the most painful way possible. The spell also inflicts an additional \u20131 wound penalty on top of any already suffered by means other then this spell. This may count as a sin against enlightened wisdom with a unproved attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space doesn't seem to do much here. It wouldn't be required for the base effect, and the only thing in the Reach that explicitly requires it is the whole 'held in a tiny ban' line in one of them.<br /> Blood is already a material sympathy Yantra, so you don't need Space to make it one.<br /> <br /> I'd make this a Life spell, drop the ban mention entirely, and add Prime for the reach effects that manipulate how the Yantras can be utilized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T13:07:10-07:00","id":1258254,"title":"","content":"Ah. Space is for getting blood from point A to point B at range, Something Life can't do easily, and is used to specifically target blood. It's also part of a theme, Tamer of Blood likely has Space+Life just being a Tamer of Blood. You could certainty throw in prime's 'As Above, So Below' or something else with it. Also you are correct you don't need the spell for any of those yantra bonuses. I might it with some 'Add Prime 2' now that you point it out...<br /> <br /> Thanks for pointing that out!<br /> <br /> As a example of the two themes I had in mind: Bloodhunter ,a tamer of blood, is in the shape of a dire wolf hunting down a dangerous villain in possession of a clue. Bloodhunter tracks them to a abandon cabin in the woods, and in a ambush tries to snap his teeth around the villain's throat. He misses. Surprise! The villain has set a ambush for him! A melee starts, and Bloodhunter could easily loose this. Hurt he runs for cover. Setups up a three point co-location. Teleporting from where he is, to a high vantage point to get a parting shot on a mook, and then to safe spot. Back at safe place Bloodhunter uses his legacy to build a strong web of connection out from that mook to the rest of the ambush. He spends a few turns casting nasty spell. He quickly teleports back, steps over all the dead bodies, and gets the clue he came for.<br /> <br /> For a lasting warning to others he calls on life magic to harden the blood to a long crystal shard (+3 dice Life-Force Assault), and drives it through the villains heart.<br /> <br /> Edit: There, pulled down the Life requirement to one. Letting Space filter for things covered by Life (Blood). I also put in a prime option to charge the blood for more then one +1 die use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","user":"HarbingerLeo","date":". 09-30-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T13:32:56-07:00","id":1258257,"title":"","content":"Honing Violence's Edge (MInd \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rotes Skills: Brawl, Weaponry, Firearms<br /> <br /> The Mage hones their instincts for violence, becoming more aware of their surroundings, perfecting their timing, and donning a minor psychosis. Choose a skill - they gain 8-again on a number of rolls to attack using it equal to the spell's potency.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: All attack rolls benefit, regardless of the skill used.<br /> +1 Reach, 1 mana: They also gain the Rote quality on those rolls. They loose 10-again on all Composure rolls not related to violence as long as the spell lasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T22:31:52-07:00","id":1258500,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Foundation of Truth</i></b><br /> <b>Prime 2, Mind 1<br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary: Duration</b><br /> The mage can grab one truth in their mind and protect it. (Multiple subjects can be selected to protect more.)<br /> This truth cannot be lost form the mage's mind. Opinions about the truth can twist a bit but are somewhat protected by the truth being sacrosanct. If the <i>truth</i> ceases to remain true, the protection ends. <br /> <br /> This effect provides a Clash of Wills before some mystical effect that affects memory. If the caster of this succeeds on that roll, the protected understanding is immune to the tampering. The effect takes place otherwise unaffected and could be an otherwise complete mind wipe, an alteration of a subject's history to prevent learning the truth, or even The Duel Arcane. The other effects happen exactly as expected, otherwise, but the truth remains. <br /> <br /> Mundane changes simply fail. The truth is a blazing and unforgettable part of the mind. <br /> <br /> This spell has visible effect in the Oneiros.<br /> <br /> 3 Reach: The truths of the mind can be protected en masse. Gnosis and Arcana are protected and any eternal truths, but many truths are temporal and subject to change. The moment a thing becomes untrue, it is removed from protection, permanently. Because of how this works, though, one would always have a locked memory of the parts of their history that they correctly recalled at the time of casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T02:10:12-07:00","id":1258513,"title":"","content":"I don't think Mind 1 is needed for this. Either Prime 2 or Mind 2 can achieve this effect on their own.<br /> <br /> The reach effect likewise seems unessecary, since a Mind Shielding spell can grant blanket protection of all your memory without any reach (or even scale) attached.<br /> <br /> Since the spell makes mundane attempts to challenge the truth fail automatically it should cost one Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T09:15:38-07:00","id":1258545,"title":"","content":"Also, what does it mean Gnosis and Arcana are protected?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T19:04:36-07:00","id":1258644,"title":"","content":"On the bright side it could throw attackers in that your rolling prime in a clash of will instead of mind, and they have access to prime to remove the spell. Which if your prime focused fighting a might focused mage that could be nice. Wards and Signs doesn't protect you so much as make them work harder, once they juice a spell to over come the extra withstand they're unopposed.<br /> <br /> The Prime 1 spell Pierce Deception could work defensively as a cure (not preventative). Your mind would still be changed, but if it was changed in some untrue way Pierce Deception would instantly (or with a clash of wills) reveal the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24652-harbingerleo","name":"HarbingerLeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-18T23:37:44-07:00","id":1261493,"title":"","content":"Touch Gauntlet (Spirit 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> <br /> Some spirit mages have found that <i>failing</i> to pierce the Gauntlet can be useful too. This spell allows the subject to physically push against the gauntlet as if it were a tangible wall. This allows the subject to do things like walk on &quot;air&quot; if the Gauntlet is strong enough to support the subject's weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","user":"Lareath","date":". 10-19-2018, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-26T16:16:11-07:00","id":1262969,"title":"","content":"Removed (for now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-27-2018, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T03:34:47-07:00","id":1263524,"title":"","content":"First of all, this post is amazing, lots of rotes to play with. Second, I'm trying to make a Void Arcanum for the main Antagonist of my story. This came to me while reading on the Lef-Hand Legacies book about the Elder Diadem, and how certain mages could wield paradox almost as an Arcanum, then I thought... but, what if Void were actually an Arcanum? And this is what came out of this. Please be gentle, this is my first time :$<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ozjjcVs_pqTkZ6T8r4YXRKMW8ceE3aoUVS5gXWDZikQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, a few rotes of my own brew:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>Shadow Puppet (Death </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Practice</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Weaving</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Primary Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Duration</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Withstand</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Stamina</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Brawl, Persuasion, Occult </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By chaining the Mage\u2019s pattern to the shadow of its enemy, he is able to immobilize him, or even control his movements, as long as the Mage maintains concentration. This spell requires the usage of the concentration Yantra, and modifies the subject shadow into tendrils that immobilize him. Both the tendrils and the objective are automatically considered grappling, and the shadow has a free Hold move as the spell is cast.<br /> The shadow is created with base 1 Strength, and gains 1 Strength per point of Potency, up to a maximum of 5, and is considered to have the same initiative as the subject (since it\u2019s is own shadow).<br /> The only actions the shadow can do while grappling are Hold and Restrain.<br /> f the objective breaks the grapple the spell ends.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>:</b> Strength can be increased over 5 points.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach, 1 mana</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: The shadow gains access to a the maneuver \u201cPuppeteer\u201d which allows it to control the physical actions of the objective until the next turn. The shadow can only use this move if it has already succeeded in a Restrain move.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>Black Coffin (Death</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Practice</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Unraveling (Patterning?)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Primary Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Potency</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Occult, Crafts, Weaponry </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This rote is a feared one. It animates the surrounding shadows to create a shadow coffin over the target and pierces his flesh using tendrils made of shadows, like an iron maiden. When casting this spell the mage can spend the Potency points between the Durability of the shadows animated and the damage done. This spell deals lethal damage equal to the Potency applied to damage, and lasts for the Duration of the spell. The shadows are animated with base Durability of 1.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach, 1 mana</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: The mage can instead inflict aggravated damage on her subject.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","user":"Eleizel","date":". 11-02-2018, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T10:27:43-08:00","id":1265308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1262969#post1262969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Prime spells focused on Yantras, primarily Magical Tools with a focus on Path Tools (Order Tools have a higher potential for complex interactions due to Techne and Exarchal symbols, and would require a bit more thought than I gave these to write spells for):<br /> <br /> ...Path Tools under the effect of this spell provide a +2 Yantra Bonus for spellcasting...<br /> <br /> ...A mage may apply the rote quality alongside the enhanced bonus to ritual spellcasting rolls with the tool...<br /> <br /> ...The Verity provides a +2 bonus when used as a Yantra, instead of the usual +1 bonus...</div> </div> </div> </div>Allowing these sorts of effects will *massively* increase the power of Mages in your setting compared to some other tables. Adding dice to spellcasting (and especially Rote, which is not that dissimilar from doubling your dice pool) is a very powerful effect and can change the feel of the game. If that's what you're interested in and ok with, then by all means go for it - these spells are reasonable enough.<br /> <br /> The reach option on Aetherial Foci should cost a mana regardless. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T22:59:14-08:00","id":1266100,"title":"","content":"One with nature (Life 1)<br /> Practice: Knowing<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Survival, Animal Ken, Stealth<br /> The mage almost literally becomes one with nature, using magically innate knowledge to come in tune with the way nature around her breathes, works, behaves and can be used to her advantage. This manifests in a bonus modifier equal to Potency to split between the skills Survival, Animal Ken and Stealth if used in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 11-10-2018, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T23:11:19-08:00","id":1266105,"title":"","content":"The laws of probability (Forces 1)<br /> Practice: Compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Athletics, Firearms<br /> There is no Fate, some people would say, only a game of calculating probabilities and outcomes from physical laws interacting with each other. Some Obrimos took this a step further and developed a method to become acutely aware of of the probabilities of physical forces and how to use them, not unlike what an Acanthus would do with Fate magic. Every turn that the mage spends actively analyzing a situation she may gain a bonus die to a physical action up to a limit of the Potency of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T09:05:56-08:00","id":1268878,"title":"","content":"<b>Tether (Time </b>\u2022\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b<b>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Computer, Crafts, Survival<br /> <br /> Students of the Time Arcanum first learn the secrets of glimpsing possible futures, then the art of correcting mistakes; an Adept can do both at the same time, exploring the river of happenings before safely returning to a secure present.<br /> <br /> When this spell is cast, the subject's temporal pattern is &quot;fixed&quot; to the present moment. When the spell's Duration expires, the subject is returned to that moment. As with Hung Spell, it is not uncommon for mages to cast Tether with a Conditional Duration, such as &quot;If I am lethally wounded&quot; or &quot;If Ialdabaoth completes the Ritual of 49 Hells&quot; in order to escape dangerous situations. Like Shifting Sands, any Beats gained by players in the now-obsolete timeline remain.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> The subject, when returned to the present, is also restored to how she was at the casting of the spell. Damage taken is healed, Conditions gained fade, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 11-19-2018, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T19:20:02-08:00","id":1269063,"title":"","content":"<b>Finish Business (Death </b>\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b\u2022\u200b<b>)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Rank<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Occult, Persuasion<br /> The unquiet Dead are bound to existence by more than just Anchors, their unfinished business tying them to the world long after their Anchors have faded to dust. Through this spell, a Mage may alter a Ghost's unfinished business, providing them with another means by which they may escape their tortured existence.<br /> <br /> For each point of Potency, the Mage may alter one part of the Ghost's unfinished business in any way they choose, this may involve changing its unfinished business to be aspects of its unlife that it has already achieved, or that have been achieved for it. While this spell can be used to assist the mournful dead, it can also be used to 'force' a Ghost to rest by denying it the will to pursue matters left unresolved.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> If the Ghost no longer has any unfinished business when the spell is cast, it immediately 'passes on'. If the Ghost has any remaining Anchors, it may spend a point of Essence in a last-ditch attempt to avoid passing on, rolling Rank + Influence in a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Clarity of what is involved in the Clash of Wills 11-22-2018, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T03:24:33-08:00","id":1269165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1269063#post1269063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Ghost has any remaining Anchors, it may contest this with a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clashes of Wills usually don't happen without a power. In the few exceptions that exists a dice pool has to be specified.<br /> <br /> All in all this spell is dependent on the interpretations of ghosts and unfinished business. Geist 2e allows Rank 1-2 ghosts to pass on after they've resolved all their Anchors (the Anchors representing all or at least most of their unfinished business). Rank 3+ ghosts don't have Anchors and have to go through a slightly different process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T03:57:19-08:00","id":1269175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1269165#post1269165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clashes of Wills usually don't happen without a power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the Unmaking of Spirits.<br /> And given this is essentially the same thing, I thought it prudent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:56:56-08:00","id":1269318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1269175#post1269175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the Unmaking of Spirits.<br /> And given this is essentially the same thing, I thought it prudent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. It's one of the only exceptions I know of (hence &quot;usually&quot;) and the reason to why I said you should specify the dice pool since Annihilate Spirit uses a non-standard CoW dice pool. The standard CoW dice pool for ephemeral entities is Rank. Influence dots added if the power that Clashes is an Influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T05:50:11-08:00","id":1269794,"title":"","content":"I'd say Finish Buisness should be Pattering, it reminds me a lot of Fate's Atonement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:27:30-08:00","id":1269966,"title":"","content":"While it is reminiscent, Atonment introduces a termination clause into Destiny-enforced phenomena which didn't previously have one, which is why it needs to be Patterned to create one. If the effect already had a way to get out of it, you could change that with Weaving.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a Ghost's unfinished business is already a part of it, and changing it is thus only Weaving, because you're editing something that already exists, rather than having to reinvent the subject to introduce it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T11:05:14-08:00","id":1270640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1265308#post1265308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding dice to spellcasting (and especially Rote, which is not that dissimilar from doubling your dice pool) is a very powerful effect and can change the feel of the game. </div> </div> </div> </div>A further breakdown of some pretty intense discussion around these themes is in the thread I copied this over from, but yeah, that discussion has been had. <br /> \u200b<br /> I disagree on any of this being a massive power increase; all of the spells are highly limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1265308#post1265308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>...Path Tools under the effect of this spell provide a +2 Yantra Bonus for spellcasting...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is only a net increase of +1, and comes with the restriction that you <i>can't use any other Tools in the spell</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1265308#post1265308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>...A mage may apply the rote quality alongside the enhanced bonus to ritual spellcasting rolls with the tool...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a copy/paste from an existing spell, lol, and it already costs Mana.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1265308#post1265308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>...The Verity provides a +2 bonus when used as a Yantra, instead of the usual +1 bonus...</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Net change of +1, for being a Master in an Arcanum which has Yantras under it's Purview. That's valued at a single Merit dot or less, based on existing material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T19:18:39-08:00","id":1275705,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spacial Limitation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Spell Potency<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Firearms, Expression<br /> <br /> The ability to fold space in on itself is a highly respectable ability, but a troublesome one in the hands of an adversary. With this spell, a mage can make it harder to crease that illusive lie known as distance. Any Space magic used will fall short of its target. Portals will end up half the distance toward their destination. Scrying windows will end up half the way from their proposed sight. A Ban will end up half as big as it was intended.<br /> <br /> Edit: Spelling errors and removed reach clause","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 12-20-2018, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T21:08:05-08:00","id":1275717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1275705#post1275705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Portals will end up half the distance toward their destination. Scrying windows will end up half the way from their proposed sight. A Ban will end up half as big as it was intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem with this spell, is that the 'distance' angle focuses on something that the entire Space Arcanum stresses, is a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T06:00:24-08:00","id":1275773,"title":"","content":"First off, no spell should fall short of its intended subject. That would be a direct change to what a spell is supposed to do, and makes little sense as well, imo. How would that even work for non-AoE spells? They randomly hit a valid target around the halfway mark? Which one would be the subject of the spell? The one you chose as subject within your Imago or the other guy? If the former you allow someone to cast spells on people who aren't subjects to those spells which is a great defence against sympathetic counter attacks, and if the latter you actively change the spell's Imago.<br /> It also doesn't make much sense in how casting works since there is no distance component of either sensory or sympathetic casting. Any distance is bypassed. Only thrown spells should be affected.<br /> Regardless you'd end up with a way to cast spells into areas or on subject you can't see or sympathetically cast into/on by virtue of aiming past the unknown. Use Space Sight to determine the exact distance to a sealed room, cast twice as long, have the spell take effect inside this sealed room. If you cast Co-Location you could now see into and enter the sealed room.<br /> <br /> What I would do with the spell is to decrease the size of any AoE effects subject to this spell. A portal won't end up halfway to its destination but it will be uncomfortably small if not impossible to pass through if not made big enough. A Ban would decrease its area as you wrote.<br /> I would also split up the distance effect as a different spell altogether (probably Weaving) that affects targeting that is dependent on range, such as thrown spells and ranged attacks. The effective distance for calculating ranges would be decreased or increased based on some Potency factor I don't have the energy to come up with right now.<br /> <br /> Edit: You could also have the range effect be primary and AoE effect be a Reach option that costs Mana. In that case it would be a Patterning spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-21-2018, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T12:33:15-08:00","id":1275865,"title":"","content":"If the goal is to avoid scrying, teleportation, or spacial manipulation, doesn't Ward cover all of those?<br /> <br /> I'm curious about the idea of altering targets. Would people allow something like this at their table?<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Misassociation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Sympathetic range (and Resolve if unwilling)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Stealth, Socialize</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage shapes a channel along one of the subject's connections, causing the sympathetic magic of others to &quot;slide&quot; to another target. Choose one of the subject's sympathetic links. For the Duration, spells cast upon the subject using Sympathetic Range provoke a Clash of Wills. If the mage wins, the spell is shunted along the sympathetic connection, and is instead resolved as if the other end of that link was the intended target.<br /> <br /> (<b>Alternatively: </b>An Unravelling version that collapses the distinction between the two, such that sympathetic spells will affect both as a single subject.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T17:32:04-08:00","id":1275956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1275865#post1275865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the goal is to avoid scrying, teleportation, or spacial manipulation, doesn't Ward cover all of those?<br /> <br /> I'm curious about the idea of altering targets. Would people allow something like this at their table?<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Misassociation (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Sympathetic range (and Resolve if unwilling)<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Politics, Stealth, Socialize</span></span><br /> <br /> The mage shapes a channel along one of the subject's connections, causing the sympathetic magic of others to &quot;slide&quot; to another target. Choose one of the subject's sympathetic links. For the Duration, spells cast upon the subject using Sympathetic Range provoke a Clash of Wills. If the mage wins, the spell is shunted along the sympathetic connection, and is instead resolved as if the other end of that link was the intended target.<br /> <br /> (<b>Alternatively: </b>An Unravelling version that collapses the distinction between the two, such that sympathetic spells will affect both as a single subject.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this basically just that one Reach effect from Perfect Sympathy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T05:44:27-08:00","id":1276035,"title":"","content":"Huh, I didn't know Perfect Sympathy could do that. I guess it's not a heretical notion, then (though it still may be safe to go up a Practice for &quot;any degree of link strength&quot; as a valid target.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T18:47:17-08:00","id":1277574,"title":"","content":"I've been giving more thought to the spell that I contributed to this (an updated version of 1e's Suspension spell), and I realized that I really shouldn't have added in the key to bypass the effect. Keys are more appropriate for spells that deal with, as the book describes (yes yes, I know), liminal spaces. Suspension definitely does not in either edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:31:25-08:00","id":1279536,"title":"","content":"Here are some spells I just created, let me know what you think:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Create Ghost Mage (Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Practice: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Making</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Primary Factor: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Special (see below)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Suggested Rote Skills: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Occult, Persuasion, Brawl</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">This spell allows for the creation of a Ghost Mage with some requirements: the subject must have left behind a ghost and you have the subject\u2019s soul stone. You must have enough mana to fill the ghost with its Rank in Essence (ex. 10 Mana for a Rank 1 Ghost). Creating a Ghost Mage is considered an act of Hubris for Falling Wisdom as the act manipulates a shard of a soul and a ghost. The soul stone is destroyed in the process of casting this spell meaning this spell can only be cast a finite number of times for the subject.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">A Ghost Mage does not possess ghostly Numina, but instead utilize all known rotes and activate them like a ghost would a Numina. A Ghost Mage is limited to the Free Reach of the rote when casting the spell, but can modify the spell factors like a normal mage. Ghost Mages can risk Paradox like a normal mage, but they cannot contain them and the paradox affects their anchors. Ghost Mages cannot spend Essence to reduce the paradox die pool. Ghost Mages can suffer overreaching from having more spells active than their limit equal to Rank and add 1 Paradox die per additional spell. Use the standard rules for creating a ghost to generate other statistics swapping Integrity for Wisdom. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">+2 Reach: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">The Ghost Mage is Rank 2.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">+2 Reach and 1 Mana: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">This spell\u2019s effect is lasting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Supernal Armor (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Practice: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Patterning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Primary Factor: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Potency</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">1 Mana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Suggested Rote Skills: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Crafts, Athletics, Empathy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">The subject of the spell is infused with magical armor resistant to supernatural attacks, converting lethal to bashing damage or reducing bashing damage by an amount equal to Potency. This armor is only effective against supernatural attacks that target the subject directly.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">+1 Reach and 1 Mana: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">This spell can convert aggravated damage to lethal by an amount equal to Potency.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 01-08-2019, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T16:38:59-08:00","id":1279593,"title":"","content":"If you need the ghost of a mage, why just not say it creates a clone of the ghost mage you already have? And what's with the Anchor and the having been in the Underworld requirements? They seem arbitrary to me.<br /> Also, Making generally don't have Lasting options. If you want it anyway it should cost Mana in addition to the already hefty Mana cost.<br /> <br /> I like the second spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T18:31:36-08:00","id":1279624,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I considered adding 1 point of Mana for the lasting since that is standard form.<br /> <br /> As for the Underworld and Anchor requirements, I agree, those do seem pretty arbitrary, I think just having the ghost would work fine as long as you have the soul stone. As for creating a clone of the ghost mage you already have? I am confused, maybe I need to clarify. The ghost has no special powers other than being a ghost of a mage that died, so basically I am using Death + Prime and the soul stone to enhance it to be able to use magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T03:19:47-08:00","id":1279665,"title":"","content":"A ghost of a mage is already a mage ghost of the kind you describe. One that has access to Rotes as Numina but not the actual Arcana (unless they get a hold of a mage's soul, in which case they regain access to their Arcana).<br /> <br /> There's also the voluntary lich type of mage ghosts which is more of a mage who becomes a ghost without losing anything in the process rather than a ghost who echoes the original mage.<br /> <br /> Source for this is comments from Dave that I can't really dig up while on phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T04:45:40-08:00","id":1279675,"title":"","content":"Interesting, if you could find this comment it would be great. Because as my understanding, it would be possible for a mage to leave behind a mundane ghost with no powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T07:45:28-08:00","id":1279695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1279675#post1279675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, if you could find this comment it would be great. Because as my understanding, it would be possible for a mage to leave behind a mundane ghost with no powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/269051-ghosts-of-supernaturals?p=269980#post269980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two different sorts of ghost mages - ghosts who happen to be created from mages, who have inluences / Numina based on their former Praxes, and proper ghost-liches, where a mage has magically bound their Awakened soul and mind to stay bound to their ghost so they keep their self-awareness and all their powers. But almost always go completely insane with Wisdom loss, to the point that they're sometimes considered a rare type of Mad One.<br /> <br /> But as Death 5 now allows you to create the ghost of someone <i>even if they're still alive</i>, expect weirdness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't find the mention that the first type of ghost mage can regain their Arcana by getting a soul in them. Luckily most ghost mages of that type can't steal them directly and just having Praxes (not Rotes as I first said) and Manifestations might not be enough to &quot;convince&quot; a mage to &quot;procure&quot; a soul for the ghost. If they'd even figure out that's a possibility and are willing to carry it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T07:57:55-08:00","id":1279699,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that Tessie. So given all this new information, would you think it is feasible to use a Soulstone to create a ghost mage in the spell description?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:22:01-08:00","id":1279705,"title":"","content":"You might just be able to do it with Create Ghost, no extra requirements other than perhaps conjunctional Prime (or, if we take a page from Imperial Mysteries, conjunctional Arcana equal to the Arcana known by the mage or the mage's Path Arcana). Spells usually don't have requirements (other than Mana costs in certain cases like Create Truth) unless the requirements are on the subject. With Making you <i>create</i> the subject from nothing so no requirements should be necessary.<br /> The Mana cost should be based on Rank instead of Essence pool, imo. Something like 5 times Rank dots (so either 5 or 10). None of the Mana converted into Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T08:54:50-08:00","id":1279717,"title":"","content":"Interesting tidbit here: As of Tome of Mysteries it's possible to summon the ghost of a mage using its soulstone, even if said mage never left a ghost or it had been destroyed. 1e of course, but still an interesting connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T10:50:59-08:00","id":1279740,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, thanks Flinty. So I wonder if you could fuse the soulstone with the ghost to grant some benefit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:20:06-08:00","id":1281151,"title":"","content":"I dont have the 2e book yet, and Im playing at a 1e table currently. That said, I'd like to try to design my spells based as closely to the 2e model as I can. Ive read every page of this thread to try to get a feel for it. Anyway, I was hoping I could drop some ideas and see what people think up. If these are in the 2e book already, Ill have a read when I get it. These are all death arcanum.<br /> <br /> Decay Spell - A death counterspell. In short, it causes the target spell to reach finality before it resolves to its purpose.<br /> <br /> Fated Demise - A death mage once had a fundamental disagreement about the nature of fate with a colleague. &quot;Any magic that affects luck or fate makes the whole concept rather arbitrary,&quot; he said. He created this spell as an attempt to mimic true fate as he saw it. It works by fraying the connection between the target mages soul and his spell. Without this connection, the spell loses direction, and any targets it previously had are scratched out of its pattern. Yet, the spell must still resolve. Anything that -could- be a target is now fair game as the spell fires off wildly. ST assigns all possible targets a number and rolls a die. The winner(or loser) is the new target.<br /> <br /> Revealing the Mortal Coil - Spell that brings its victim intimately close to deaths cold hands. Victim brushes so closely with death that he feels it calling to him as if he were already at its door. For turns equal to potency, victim takes negative modifiers to all rolls as if having a full health track.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach <br /> If victim's health track is actually full at the end of this spell (where he had at least 3 open health boxes before before), he suffers a mental tilt, as his mind begins to fray from his brush with death. (Not great with wording here. Basically the target cant tell if he was actually near death or not and it twists his perception of reality.) <br /> <br /> Waning Faculties - This is the scalpel to the crude cudgel type death spells that slough bone and sinew wholesale from the body. A practiced mage can decay very specific parts of anatomy at the smallest levels. Want to give a rival alzheimers? Wear away the myelin sheath. Cripple someone? Target the spinal cord. Rote roles use science or medicine.<br /> <br /> Distilling the Underworld<br /> The necromancer who has attained this level of understanding recognizes the presence of mana everywhere within the purview of death, and may cleave it to himself at will. <br /> When casted on a target that generates or uses some aspect of deathly fuel as energy, the mage leeches it away at a rate equal to potency for the duration. Ghostly Essence,vitae, and bound plasm leeched this way restores mana to the mage at a rate of 1 mana per 2 units of deathly fuel. This can be used to draw mana from the plasm stored in cenotes or other locales where death keeps a heavy hand, as well as from the underworld itself.<br /> <br /> Eschew the Ether: <br /> The mage wielding this spell harnesses the aspect of death that pertains to the bond between the targets soul and magic itself, and withers it. The cold chill of this absence settles over the target, as they feel their souls connection to the supernal waning. No longer able to hold onto their fuel, mana leaks from the mage uncontrollably. <br /> Target is forced to reflexively spend mana each turn equal to spell potency. This mana cannot be used for spell casting, as it is escaping a body that can no longer contain it. If potency exceeds target's gnosis, they must spend mana up to their gnosis each turn until the potency is met.<br /> <br /> -I saw the above spell previously in this thread. I believe it was prime 3. This is an effort to do it with death arcanum.- <br /> <br /> Exorcising the Shade - The mage that uses this spell snuffs out the pesky hurdle of emotion within his target. For the duration of this spell the target cannot be manipulated emotionally, either mundanely or supernaturally, and all roll attempts on the part of another to detect lies or motives from him fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24949-ratcheteffect","name":"RatchetEffect","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:28:29-08:00","id":1281156,"title":"","content":"Also, I saw a while back that someone wanted to use shadows to teleport. Could you not improvise a spell that not only makes you shadow, but extends your shadow self to the size of all connected shadows? I.E. I become shadow and melt into the shadows of the morgue. I wither away the light in the room until it is pitch black. The shadow of x room is size 15, and I, as being shadow am also size 15. I can step out of any part of myself at will and return to size 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24949-ratcheteffect","name":"RatchetEffect","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:35:32-08:00","id":1281161,"title":"","content":"Rates in Distilling the Underworld are poorly worded. Each dot of potency draws 2 units of deathly fuel from a source, then draws mana from said fuel at a rate of 1 mana per 2 units.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24949-ratcheteffect","name":"RatchetEffect","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T20:08:26-08:00","id":1281242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RatchetEffect</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1281156#post1281156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I saw a while back that someone wanted to use shadows to teleport. Could you not improvise a spell that not only makes you shadow, but extends your shadow self to the size of all connected shadows? I.E. I become shadow and melt into the shadows of the morgue. I wither away the light in the room until it is pitch black. The shadow of x room is size 15, and I, as being shadow am also size 15. I can step out of any part of myself at will and return to size 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s Death 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T16:46:58-08:00","id":1285727,"title":"","content":"So, I decided that if a Mage can give Mage Sight logically they should also be able to remove Mage Sight and came up with the following spell, see what you think:<br /> <br /> Deny Sight (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Subterfuge, Larceny, Crafts<br /> The mage can give sight and they can take it away allowing them to make it much harder for a mage to solve the mysteries around them. This spell removes the ability of the subject to use Arcana related to the Path of the caster in their Active &amp; Focused Mage Sight for the duration of the spell.<br /> Add Any Arcana \u2022: The subject is unable to use the specified Arcana in their Active &amp; Focused Mage Sight but must pay 1 Mana for each Common &amp; Inferior Arcana involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T04:13:41-08:00","id":1286657,"title":"","content":"It's... complicated.<br /> Mechanically speaking I think the Awakening is the result of an imperial spell cast by the Watchtowers and to remove it or any part of it even temporarily you'd have to best them in a Clash of Wills - which as a non Archmaster you loose automatically. So while this spell is theoretically possible, it's utterly useless for regular mages.<br /> <br /> That said I personally tend to deviate from this setting detail and allow Prime unmaking to temporarily shut a mage's magic down completely, so personally I think this is a neat spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T03:57:36-08:00","id":1287013,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I was tinkering with an Obrimos Legacy, and while doing that, this spell came to my mind. Any thoughts about it?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>No Need to Dodge (Forces </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Practice</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Unmaking</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Primary Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Potency</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Intimidation, Persuasion, Athletics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Have you ever dreamed of being Neo in the Matrix, stopping bullets mid-flight? Now you can. This spell utterly eliminate all the speed of a moving target. If applicable, the target will suffer damage since it\u2019s speed is reduced from whatever it was to zero in a negligible amount of time. This damage is calculated as per the rules for Crashes, as if the target had hit a heavy object of size 5, which may be increased improving the Scale Factor of the spell, moving at 0 speed. This means that the target suffers half the max size of the Scale Factor (rounded down) points of bashing damage plus one tenth the relative speed in bashing damage. Any damage that exceeds the targets Durability is also applied as bashing damage to the driver and passengers, if applicable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: The mage can use No Need to Dodge\u2019s effect as a reflexive action instead.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Damage dealt is now Lethal.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>+1 Reach, add Time \u2022</b>: With Time 1 and a Reach, the mage can stop objects too fast for her to gain Defense against them.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","user":"Eleizel","date":". 02-12-2019, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T17:48:41-08:00","id":1287778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1286657#post1286657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's... complicated.<br /> Mechanically speaking I think the Awakening is the result of an imperial spell cast by the Watchtowers and to remove it or any part of it even temporarily you'd have to best them in a Clash of Wills - which as a non Archmaster you loose automatically. So while this spell is theoretically possible, it's utterly useless for regular mages.<br /> <br /> That said I personally tend to deviate from this setting detail and allow Prime unmaking to temporarily shut a mage's magic down completely, so personally I think this is a neat spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I see your point. I didn't realize this, but mechanically you are correct that would be a CoW against an imperial spell which you auto lose if you are not an Archmage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>No Need to Dodge (Forces </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\"><i>)</i></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Practice</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Primary Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Potency</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Intimidation, Persuasion, Athletics</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Have you ever dreamed of being Neo in the Matrix, stopping bullets mid-flight? Now you can. This spell utterly eliminate all the speed of a moving target. If applicable, the target will suffer damage since it\u2019s speed is reduced from whatever it was to zero in a negligible amount of time. This damage is calculated as per the rules for Crashes, as if the target had hit a heavy object of size 5, which may be increased improving the Scale Factor of the spell, moving at 0 speed. This means that the target suffers half the max size of the Scale Factor (rounded down) points of bashing damage plus one tenth the relative speed in bashing damage. Any damage that exceeds the targets Durability is also applied as bashing damage to the driver and passengers, if applicable.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: The mage can use No Need to Dodge\u2019s effect as a reflexive action instead.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">+1 Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Damage dealt is now Lethal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>+1 Reach, add Time \u2022</b>: With Time 1 and a Reach, the mage can stop objects too fast for her to gain Defense against them.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><br /> <br /> This spell is pretty weak in my opinion for a Forces 5 Mage. You can use a Forces 3 &quot;Turn Momentum&quot; effect reflexively that can basically send bullets flying back against the target with ease causing them to hurt themselves which is another added bonus. Sure, it is not as awe stopping as suddenly full stopping a truck in mid-movement, but it is less practical.<br /> Also, if you really wanted to have some fun and not need to dodge you could add Forces 4 &quot;Rend Friction&quot; to basically tear apart the truck/bullets as they come toward you basically causing them to be hunks of metal that you side-step.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T01:09:42-08:00","id":1287885,"title":"","content":"A Forces Unmaking spell just makes the momentum the target had go poof, they wouldn't suffer any detrimental effects from deacceleration. It's just has momentum to has no momentum in an instant (which can have very lethal consequences of its own depending on what kind of velocity you were targetting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T04:01:10-08:00","id":1287903,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree. I just think the other two mentioned spells already accomplish similar goals. Turn momentum into a wall or rend friction to literally disintegrate bullets.<br /> <br /> Also for a Master they can reflexively cast both spells with little Paradox. This spell would be a big paradox die pool to cast reflexively since you would be suffering 4 die versus maybe 2 for Rend and 0 for turn momentum. You could even combine both effects at Master level and only risk 2 Paradox to flip the target and disintegrate them based on momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Added additional explanation. 02-14-2019, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T04:55:21-08:00","id":1287907,"title":"","content":"Small clarification: Neither spell can be cast reflexively without house ruling how reflexive casting works. Turn Momentum can, however, be precast and then &quot;activated&quot; reflexively.<br /> <br /> Rend Friction and bullets seem like a horrible combination, though. If the bullets don't travel enough of a distance to be reduced to dust that is stopped by air resistance while under the effect of the spell (or you don't have enough Potency) you just risk creating a cone of shrapnel instead of bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T05:08:03-08:00","id":1287908,"title":"","content":"According to the book Turn Momentum can be cast reflexively. You are correct some House Ruling would be necessary for Rend Friction. The book is not one hundred percent on how reflexive spells work combined. I would argue that spell casting time is shared with combined spells. But I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> As for your point about friction, after about 9 yards I would say the bullet is gone. You might think it is higher but I don\u2019t think a bullet would have that much structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-14-2019, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T08:56:51-08:00","id":1287959,"title":"","content":"&quot;+1 Reach: The mage can use Turn Momentum\u2019s effect as a<br /> reflexive action instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think you've misread this part. Like I said, no reflexive casting, only reflexive &quot;activation&quot; on the spell instead of the instant action it generally takes to redirect things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:08:07-08:00","id":1288069,"title":"","content":"You are correct, I did. My bad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T10:54:09-07:00","id":1300328,"title":"","content":"I have a character in my game that has been cursed so that bad things happen to anyone he gets close to. I'm still learning the system but wanted to figure out what kind of spell that would be. Fate for sure, and maybe Space because of sympathetic connections? Just not sure about the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:05:24-07:00","id":1300351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1300328#post1300328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a character in my game that has been cursed so that bad things happen to anyone he gets close to. I'm still learning the system but wanted to figure out what kind of spell that would be. Fate for sure, and maybe Space because of sympathetic connections? Just not sure about the specifics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Fate, and any level of Fate can do curses, but this doesn\u2019t sound like like something that is a typical Fate spell since it uses the character as a carrier and the actual subjects are whoever interacts with him. Maybe some variant of Monkey\u2019s Paw makes sense though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T12:39:09-07:00","id":1300361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1300351#post1300351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just Fate, and any level of Fate can do curses, but this doesn\u2019t sound like like something that is a typical Fate spell since it uses the character as a carrier and the actual subjects are whoever interacts with him. Maybe some variant of Monkey\u2019s Paw makes sense though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the idea would sorta be as soon as a sympathetic connection forms it starts to work it\u2019s hex or whatever on the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T18:15:23-07:00","id":1300437,"title":"","content":"To be honest, it would be an interesting mystery that is not Supernal at all. However, if you want to make it out of the Supernal World then I think you have three options:<br /> #1. This is an archmage spell that allows for this type of conditions and would possibly have some sort of lasting or conditional based duration that could span the entire lifespan of the character where it constantly targets only those that are close to the subject.<br /> #2. This is a Fate 3 Monkey Paw spell mixed with Space 2 and Life 1 to target living beings close to the character with an indefinite duration and an extremely low potency from a Mage (since if it was high it could affect weak targets).<br /> #3. Maybe this was inflicted by a Supernal Being, thus you can have it removed by another Supernal Being or a powerful mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T20:29:57-07:00","id":1300461,"title":"","content":"You wouldn\u2019t need Life 1, but option 2 might work well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T04:20:50-07:00","id":1300511,"title":"","content":"Normally, I would agree with you Mrmdubois, but I believe Life is an essential part of this spell because it targets living things and by default Space &amp; Fate can target non-living things. I believe the conjunction of Life is justified in this case. However, if the OP doesn't care if the spell targets nonliving things then yes, it would be fine to exclude Life 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T07:43:20-07:00","id":1300549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1300437#post1300437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it would be an interesting mystery that is not Supernal at all. However, if you want to make it out of the Supernal World then I think you have three options:<br /> #1. This is an archmage spell that allows for this type of conditions and would possibly have some sort of lasting or conditional based duration that could span the entire lifespan of the character where it constantly targets only those that are close to the subject.<br /> #2. This is a Fate 3 Monkey Paw spell mixed with Space 2 and Life 1 to target living beings close to the character with an indefinite duration and an extremely low potency from a Mage (since if it was high it could affect weak targets).<br /> #3. Maybe this was inflicted by a Supernal Being, thus you can have it removed by another Supernal Being or a powerful mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> These are all pretty good options. The character in question is actually an Acanthus Mage so I imagine the effect would be pretty hard to remove. I like #3 because it could be a hook for summoning Supernal Beings. Although honestly now that you bring it up, it being a non-Supernal Mystery is interesting too. What kind of beings in the COD could do such a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T09:55:25-07:00","id":1300577,"title":"","content":"You\u2019d probably have to make one up. Demons or Changelings come to mind though as splat possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:36:55-07:00","id":1300625,"title":"","content":"To add to Mrmdubois's suggestion, Demons, the infernal kind (from Inferno), are another possibility","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":".  Spelling errors. 03-28-2019, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T12:34:52-07:00","id":1303814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=888636#post888636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Foreshadow (Fate </b><b>\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Expression, Subterfuge<br /> When a mage casts this spell, he chooses a destiny (or Destiny) of which he is aware. The spell causes the strings of fate to manifest one symbol per dot of Potency of that destiny between the time of casting and when the fated event occurs. For instance, if a Sleeper is destined to get into a car crash, the spell might cause her to see a commercial about auto insurance, or she might drive by the site of a car crash the day before. The effects of this spell are normally minor and subtle, but they can be useful for getting someone to believe in the power of fate and symbolism. Alternatively, the mage might wish to cause foreshadowing to manifest for particularly obscure destinies in order to analyze a mystery from a different point of view.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage chooses how the foreshadowing manifests.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was messing about in my homebrew document, trying to do something with Apophenia and Pareidolia; got inspired by the above spell; and made this. Yes, that's quite a lot of reach effects <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . So, good, or overdesigned?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Foreshadow (Fate \u2022)</span></span></b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Compelling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Academics, Expression, Subterfuge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell manifests one symbol per point of Potency that gives insight to the subject about their destiny. The effects of this spell are minor and subtle, but they can be useful for getting someone to believe in the power of fate and symbolism. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prolonged exposure to this spell (roughly a day per dot of the subject\u2019s Composure) causes the spooked condition.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A character that is aware of the Destiny may drop pertinent hints during a social encounter and reduce the subject\u2019s doors by 1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The omens are not really subtle, and sometimes quite frightening; while the subject has the spooked condition granted by this spell, witnessing further symbols grants the shaken condition. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The subject is subconsciously primed to pertinent events related to their destiny. When reacting to events related to their destiny, the subject gains a +potency bonus to initiative.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The subject witnesses omens pertinent to a Destiny belonging to someone else.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As long as the caster is aware of the destiny, they may choose how the omens manifest.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+mind</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the spell causes the Obsessed condition instead of the spooked condition. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","user":"MovingMind","date":". 04-10-2019, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T17:30:18-07:00","id":1305357,"title":"","content":"What kind of spell would be used to ward any sort of ephemeral entity from entering an area of effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:08:14-07:00","id":1305374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1305357#post1305357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of spell would be used to ward any sort of ephemeral entity from entering an area of effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ban, a Space 3 spell, is the baseline effect; having two dots in Forces, Matter, Death, and Life would allow you to let in only physical things under those purviews, blocking ephemeral entities by exclusion.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that a Space 3 + Prime 3 spell should be able to do it as well, based on Prime 3's Ephemeral Enchantment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:48:00-07:00","id":1305476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1305357#post1305357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of spell would be used to ward any sort of ephemeral entity from entering an area of effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 2, Command Spirit, cast on an area, &quot;Stay out!&quot; would work for spirits, add Death 2 and Mind 2 to get the rest of the ephemeral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:05:59-07:00","id":1305491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1305476#post1305476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 2, Command Spirit, cast on an area, &quot;Stay out!&quot; would work for spirits, add Death 2 and Mind 2 to get the rest of the ephemeral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Death 2+Mind 2+Spirit 2 should be enough, though it's not foolproof. Both in that ephemeral entities can successfully Withstand the spell (or ignore it if they're Rank 6+, iirc) and it will only cover three groups of ephemeral entities and not anything else that is in Twilight (such as G-M angels that aren't subject to either Arcanum, ephemeral objects, anyone who's just translated to ephemera like Ghost-Gated people or psychic projections, and Quashmallim that simply aren't ephemeral despite being in Twilight).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T23:26:56-07:00","id":1305915,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to cast a spell without it being detected while you\u2019re casting it. I\u2019m really wondering about Supernal Veil in particilar. Would using it in a combined spell hide it\u2019s usage from Peripheral Mage sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T23:59:18-07:00","id":1305917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1305915#post1305915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to cast a spell without it being detected while you\u2019re casting it. I\u2019m really wondering about Supernal Veil in particilar. Would using it in a combined spell hide it\u2019s usage from Peripheral Mage sight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would, for more general consideration, casting a Veiling spell at all doesn't seem to invoke Peripheral Mage Sight. Veiling spells are supposed to be something that slips by notice after all. That said, a Mage who employs MS, or an appropriate spell, with the right arcana might be entitled to a CoW and pierce it. This is perfectly in-line with Mages being among the ultimate investigators of supernatural goings-on. One of the core themes of Mage after all is piercing deception, and the other is being so obsessed with piercing falsehoods that they will burn the world down to do so. It can be less a question of if they find out and more what they'll do when they do so.<br /> <br /> One saving grace for the ST is that unless they use a spell to gain the CoW they won't know it's happened. Though naturally if they win the CoW even if a spell isn't involved they gain all information that such a victory would make them privy to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:54:10-07:00","id":1305957,"title":"","content":"Supernal Veil wouldn't really take effect until after the spellcasting is done. It would hide the combined spell once it's on the subject, but whether the casting itself is also veiled depends on whether the whole combined spell is considered a Veiling spell or if PMS would trigger on the component spells individually.<br /> <br /> I'd personally go with the entire combined spell being veiled from PMS if one of the component spells is a Veiling spell, but that allows all Gnosis 3+ mages to hide their spells from PMS and not just those who can precast Supernal Veil on themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:19:40-07:00","id":1307258,"title":"","content":"How would you create the following effects?<br /> A spell that sustains the body without food, drink or sleep<br /> Life only (3?), Life + Mind? - something based on sleep of the just, maybe<br /> 'cheat' version would be to use life and mind magic to cure the damage deprivation would do... but that's not what i am looking for.<br /> <br /> A spell that causes fire to burn anything, regardless of flammability, and resist being extinguished?<br /> Forces 3 (perfecting) would be my guess... but could require forces 4 patterning, thoughts?<br /> Cheaty way would be Matter 3 effect &quot;alter flammability&quot; ala &quot;alter conductivity&quot;, but that doesn't help with the 'resists being extinguished'<br /> <br /> Celestial fire that spreads like normal fire?<br /> I think Prime 4, given celestial fire exists, but i suspect it should be Making, so Prime 5<br /> Cheaty way would be forces veiling to make normal fire look like celestial fire...<br /> <br /> Ideas/Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T12:21:53-07:00","id":1307276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1307258#post1307258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you create the following effects?<br /> A spell that sustains the body without food, drink or sleep<br /> Life only (3?), Life + Mind? - something based on sleep of the just, maybe<br /> 'cheat' version would be to use life and mind magic to cure the damage deprivation would do... but that's not what i am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 2 or Life 3, depending on whether you can justify Shielding as the Practice. No Mind should be required for the physical need for sleep, but you won't get any WP due to not getting any mental refreshment. I can also see people developing negative mental Conditions if they don't fulfil their mental need to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1307258#post1307258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celestial fire that spreads like normal fire?<br /> I think Prime 4, given celestial fire exists, but i suspect it should be Making, so Prime 5<br /> Cheaty way would be forces veiling to make normal fire look like celestial fire...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually just the Celestial Fire spell with the Reach option. Of course, the spreading fire will just be normal fire. Since the celestial fire is supernatural in origin you need to actively uphold it with a spell. Spreading additional celestial fire would likely just be additional Reaches and maybe a Mana. It goes away when the spell goes away and I would personally limit it to not be able to spread outside the AoE scale factor.<br /> It would not require Prime 5, though, as &quot;creating&quot; celestial fire is a Prime 4 spell. Any subsequent modifications to celestial fire would be Patterning at most (if possible at all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T11:11:30-07:00","id":1310778,"title":"","content":"Is Diplomat's Protection from the 1E Silver Ladder book still doable under the new rules or has something changed that would make it not really work anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T22:34:58-07:00","id":1310926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1310778#post1310778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Diplomat's Protection from the 1E Silver Ladder book still doable under the new rules or has something changed that would make it not really work anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are several ways of replicating &quot;people can't attack you.&quot; A Mind Ruling (two dot) spell should be able to inflict the Beaten Down tilt. Something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Overawe<br /> Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Intimidate, Brawl, Persuasion<br /> The Mage inflicts the subject of this spell with the Beaten Down tilt, making it difficult for them to take any hostile action.<br /> +1 Reach: The tilt instead applies only to a specific subject, allowing the targets to act freely against anyone else. This option can be taken multiple times, adding a new subject that the tilt applies against each time.<br /> <br /> Or you could just leverage the extant Psychic Domination spell to give everyone the command &quot;fear&quot; or &quot;obey&quot; or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-09-2019, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T06:29:02-07:00","id":1310962,"title":"","content":"Logical inverse of Gremlins. Gremlins make failure --&gt; dramatic failure. So this makes success --&gt; exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Loyal Tool (Spirit \u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <br /> The spirit of an object can be cajoled into helping its owner during its use. When a character succeeds on a roll using this spell's subject as equipment, the spell converts the success into an exceptional success. The spell converts a number of successes equal to its Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> As long as the object is within sensory range, the mage can choose which successes become exceptional successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25264-neetzsche","name":"NEETzsche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T01:40:44-07:00","id":1311181,"title":"","content":"That's definitely too much for a 1 dot spell... if you achieve one success, it's more powerful than Miracle at potency 4. And it works for multiple rolls... <br /> <br /> Maybe reduce it to Exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T04:37:33-07:00","id":1311195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1311181#post1311181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely too much for a 1 dot spell... if you achieve one success, it's more powerful than Miracle at potency 4. And it works for multiple rolls...<br /> <br /> Maybe reduce it to Exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>But it follows from other spells already published. And they kind of abandoned the &quot;balance&quot; concept from 2e completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25264-neetzsche","name":"NEETzsche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T06:22:34-07:00","id":1311206,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that its all a matter of catering to different niches. Spirit 1 can probably get you an exceptional success, but you still need one success for it to work. Plus its restricted to using tools only.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Luck can guarantee success in most mundane tasks by granting boon Conditions. But it can also add a dice bonus to spellcasting for extra Reach. Its not bound to tools, so its a harder Practice, but more flexible.<br /> <br /> If I read Miracle correctly, its big selling point is that it can be used on absolutely anything. Casting a mana consuming spell ? Cast Miracle before to get an exceptional success and you can get your mana back plus a bonus point or you can bypass Withstand or even get an extra Reach. Scrutinizing a Mystery with Mage Sight ? Miracle can help. Your Obrimos cabal mate is dreading using up a lot of mana to make a Hallow ? Miracle can fix that. Miracle uses up no mana to give you all that, which is huge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-10-2019, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T13:13:21-07:00","id":1311273,"title":"","content":"Idk, still seems a bit much for one dot, but ehh, whatever.<br /> <br /> Coming to think of it, it's not a fair comparison at all... your spell just gives the &quot;side effects&quot; of an exceptional success, as opposed to actual successes.<br /> <br /> Perhaps add a note that conditions gained from exceptional successes that result from this spell don't grant beats unless the spell itself was an exceptional success?<br /> <br /> Next question: how much forces would you need to allow you to lift objects that normally wouldn't be able to lift without them breaking under their own weight, or simply because you don't have the leverage, and how would you write it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T16:30:57-07:00","id":1311303,"title":"","content":"Its just a normal XP beat, mages care more about Arcane Beats. You get one per scene this way. Anything beyond that is due to exceptional roleplaying or story milestones. And like you said, you might need to use Willpower, spells or any other means in case its a skill where your dice pool is not great. So long as you stick to that 1 beat sanity check, everything else is just for narrative effect, which I say is fair enough.<br /> <br /> Regarding Forces, the elegant and precise solution is Telekinesis at Forces 3. But maybe you can use a Control Gravity from Forces 2 to make the center of gravity an object falls towards be your destination point. Problem is that the object is falling towards that point, so fragile ones would be at risk. In addition, if the point is too far away, inertia will make the object overshoot the goal, effectively colliding it at high speed against whatever is nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T22:03:17-07:00","id":1312487,"title":"","content":"What arcana would be needed to absorb the contents of a book directly into your mind?<br /> <br /> Mind arcana technically lists language and communication under its purview, but everything you read on it implies that this only applies to working with actual minds, rather than anything in the physical world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T22:24:45-07:00","id":1312490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1312487#post1312487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What arcana would be needed to absorb the contents of a book directly into your mind?<br /> <br /> Mind arcana technically lists language and communication under its purview, but everything you read on it implies that this only applies to working with actual minds, rather than anything in the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably just a Matter 1 Knowing spell to know the contents. If you flipped through the book physically you could use Mind 1's <i>Perfect Recall</i>, which explicitly mentions &quot;words written on a piece of paper&quot; as one of the things you can recall, if you wanted to peruse the book later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T02:28:53-07:00","id":1312515,"title":"","content":"Flipping through the book and using Perfect Recall does have some drawbacks. First off it takes a significantly longer amount of time than casting a non-ritual spell since you need to get a good view on each page (but certainly a lot shorter than actually reading the book). Secondly, it's more akin to storing the book in your mind rather than absorbing the contents of it. You need to cast the spell and &quot;reread&quot; the book in your memories to access the information rather than just storing it. It being a purely mental process should speed it up, and with One Mind, Two Thoughts it wouldn't even take time away from other activities.<br /> <br /> A spell that actually transfers the information would be Matter for the physical medium, and possibly Mind because of the type of information you're getting information from (language and communication in the form of the written word). I can see arguments both for and against Mind and I'm undecided about whether it's necessary or not.<br /> <br /> If it's only Matter Knowing I'd give the player some cursory information about the book, and with a Reach or two (maybe even a Mana) grant a simplified version of the contents; Matter is not for this kind of communication and Knowing doesn't usually grant that much information.<br /> <br /> If it's a Matter/Mind Knowing spell I'd grant a number of facts or pages of transferred infromation based on Potency and information density. Two Reaches and a Mana might grant the entire book directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T14:03:06-07:00","id":1312642,"title":"","content":"A book is obviously a form of communication and a representation of language. The material aspects of a book's symbolism isn't what you want to interact with for this spell, anyway. Mind can do that without help. Seems it would be a straight Knowing effect.<br /> <br /> Matter is the one that is arguable. Solids and shaping are the only purviews that apply to a book. Knowing the meaning of squiggles, lines, and whatnot is language and that is not on it's list. (Spirit would be an easier sell since a book's spirit involves communication.)<br /> <br /> Reading a book without needing to open it is <i>certainly</i> a Matter Knowing effect.<br /> <br /> I lean towards a Reach option to divide time required to read it by Potency and another that requires Mind 1 which renders absorption instantaneous. Could apply these to Discern Composition if you'd like to use an existing rote.<br /> <br /> Ed: In hindsight, pure Matter should simply speed up reading by removing the material constraints, so something like multiplying the reading rate by around a flat 3x seems better than a Potency based multiplier. All books affected, though, would be accessible from anywhere, so casting over a library would make everything within available on a whim. That's pretty darn cool. Research would be similarly multiplied by not needing to move to look at another book and would this would render such an action entirely mental if all the materials in question were present. That's still a mighty nifty effect to have handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 05-16-2019, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T01:19:26-07:00","id":1313083,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Intense Dream (Mind \u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Intimidation, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The mage compels a sleeping target to begin dreaming, and do so in a vivid and psychologically compelling fashion. The caster does not dictate or even influence the content of the dream, he merely causes them to have one. To do this, she should cast Dream Reaching (Mage: the Awakening, p. 160); otherwise the Storyteller controls the nature and subject matter of the dream. <br /> <br /> In the state of this intense dream, the subject may experience Breaking Points and collect Beats as though they were awake. The entirety of the dream counts as one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The dream is extended in the subject's mind. It lasts for an additional scene. Each additional scene requires the use of another Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25264-neetzsche","name":"NEETzsche","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25264_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T13:40:51-07:00","id":1315929,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Create Touch Stone (Life \u2022\u2022 , Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Craft, Expression, Academics<br /> <br /> This extracts the taste or smell of an object into up to [Potency] small spherical objects around the size of a marble. The ones containing smells are meant to be popped and release a foul flavor when eaten. Those containing flavors are meant to be eaten and release foul odors when popped. Seers and hubristic Ladders are very fond of them, offering them to visitors. Those without the means to know which kind they were given often need to ask the mage or risk embarrassment, feeding the caster's ego. More artistically inclined mages are also likely to use them, a musician may provide special scents or tastes to complement a symphony or chef may use them in molecular gastronomy. Its rumored some casters even create stink bombs or a cheap approximation of tear gas (using onions and the like).<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Potency can instead be allocated at a one to one ratio to increase the number of flavors/smells the touch stone contains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-01-2019, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T14:23:11-07:00","id":1315941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1315929#post1315929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Create Touch Stone (Life \u2022\u2022 , Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Craft, Expression, Academics<br /> <br /> This extracts the taste or smell of an object into up to [Potency] small spherical objects around the size of a marble. The ones containing smells are meant to be popped and release a foul flavor when eaten. Those containing flavors are meant to be eaten and release foul odors when popped. Seers and hubristic Ladders are very fond of them, offering them to visitors. Those without the means to know which kind they were given often need to ask the mage or risk embarrassment, feeding the caster's ego. More artistically inclined mages are also likely to use them, a musician may provide special scents or tastes to complement a symphony or chef may use them in molecular gastronomy. Its rumored some casters even create stink stink bombs or a cheap approximation of tear gas (using onions and the like).<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Potency can instead be allocated at a one to one ratio to increase the number of flavors/smells the touch stone contains.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me a very Harry Potter vibe (Bertie Bott's Every Flavour Beans). I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T14:30:16-07:00","id":1315943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1315941#post1315941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gives me a very Harry Potter vibe (Bertie Bott's Every Flavour Beans). I like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, it was inspired by the ones Jerec used in the SW: Dark Forces. But now that you mention it, yeah, I can see it as well. Not sure if the 1 Reach effect should remain so or just be the result of increasing the Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T18:13:34-07:00","id":1317714,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Glimpsing The Pareto Frontier (Mind \u2022 , Time \u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling <br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Socialize, Streetwise <br /> <br /> A savvy th\u00e9arch knows that the first step to climb the ladder of existence is to know how to use their time wisely. This grants the Good Time Management merit and allows anyone affected to use it in teamwork mundane actions with anyone else who also possesses the merit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: A unifying vision drives creativity and efficiency further up, granting [Potency] dots of the Vision merit. For an extra Reach and a mana, it can exceed 5 points.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Also grants the targets the ability to purchase the Good Time Management and/or Vision merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-11-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T18:19:07-07:00","id":1317924,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Walking The Road of the Dhy\u0101na (Mind \u2022\u2022 )</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling <br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Academics, Investigation <br /> <br /> Being able to keep a centered mind amidst chaos is invaluable to an Arrow, using magic to aid the process even more so. This grants [Potency] points in Meditative Mind, or extra points in case the target already has it, up to a limit of four points.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: A warrior may be called to duty in the Astral. In such cases, being able to forego the need of Hallows reduces vulnerabilies. This grants the Astral Adept merit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Also allows the purchase of the Astral Adept merit, provided the target is an Awakened or Sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T08:02:14-07:00","id":1318227,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Plumb Text (Mind \u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Knowing</span><br /> <b>Primary Factor</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Potency</span><br /> <b>Withstand:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> N/A</span><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Academics, Investigation, Occult</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sometimes a mage doesn't have time to pour through pages upon pages of arcane lore to find the tidbit they're looking for. This spell allows the mage to sift through the contents of text much like a document viewing program can search for specific words or phrases in a document. For each level of potency the mage can ask a question regarding the contents of a book, scroll, manuscript or any other similar object of text and absorb relevant passages and where in the text it is located directly into their mind as if having freshly read them. If a mage targets multiple texts with this spell they are aware of which text the passage belongs to.</span><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The mage may simply absorb the full contents of the target(s) into their mind as if having freshly read it in its entirety from beginning to end.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">----------</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is my first time making a Rote based off of the question I asked previously regarding absorbing the contents of a book directly into the mind. It was inspired while reading Broken Diamond by DaveB, when he had pondered on the very topic of such a spell and what arcana that would require. It captured my own imagination and had me thinking on it for a good while before posting here to confirm if Mind would simply be sufficient thanks to its dominion over language and communications.<br /> <br /> This spell assumes that the Mind Arcana does not simply limit itself to the confines of the human mind, but stretches out to envelop the construct of language and communication that humanity has collectively built and passed down over thousands of years by taking sounds, symbols and ideas and forming sympathetic connections from them to people, objects, places, and abstract concepts.<br /> <br /> Let me know if or where I went astray on this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Included information in the case of targeting multiple texts. Tidied up the wording.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-13-2019, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T12:43:51-07:00","id":1318289,"title":"","content":"<b>Cycle of Nature (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> Tapping into the temporal patterns of the world, the mage alters the current season. When cast on an area, the targeted location's climate changes to match the desired season; the mage might create a spring garden in the middle of winter, or call on the monsoons of the rainy season during a period of aridity. When cast on an individual, the target behaves as if the desired season were in effect; a plant might reach its peak height in summer, for example, or a metal lamp-post in winter might turn cold and develop a veneer of ice. On human targets, this spell allows the individual to reduce the severity of Environmental Tilts caused by the weather by the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can apply an Environmental Tilt to the affected area relevant to the desired season, with an effective strength equal to the spell's Potency. If cast on an individual, the target suffers from the Environmental Tilt as if it were a Personal Tilt, and the spell is Withstood with Stamina.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space </b><i><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: </b></i>The mage can change the season to one not normally experienced in the target location (such as monsoon season in Alaska).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:14:48-07:00","id":1318333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1318227#post1318227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Plumb Text (Mind \u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Knowing</span><br /> <b>Primary Factor</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">: Potency</span><br /> <b>Withstand:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> N/A</span><br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Academics, Investigation, Occult</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sometimes a mage doesn't have time to pour through pages upon pages of arcane lore to find the tidbit they're looking for. This spell allows the mage to sift through the contents of text much like a document viewing program can search for specific words or phrases in a document. For each level of potency the mage can ask a question regarding the contents of a book, scroll, manuscript or any other similar object of text and absorb relevant passages and where in the text it is located directly into their mind as if having freshly read them. If a mage targets multiple texts with this spell they are aware of which text the passage belongs to.</span><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The mage may simply absorb the full contents of the target(s) into their mind as if having freshly read it in its entirety from beginning to end.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">----------</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is my first time making a Rote based off of the question I asked previously regarding absorbing the contents of a book directly into the mind. It was inspired while reading Broken Diamond by DaveB, when he had pondered on the very topic of such a spell and what arcana that would require. It captured my own imagination and had me thinking on it for a good while before posting here to confirm if Mind would simply be sufficient thanks to its dominion over language and communications.<br /> <br /> This spell assumes that the Mind Arcana does not simply limit itself to the confines of the human mind, but stretches out to envelop the construct of language and communication that humanity has collectively built and passed down over thousands of years by taking sounds, symbols and ideas and forming sympathetic connections from them to people, objects, places, and abstract concepts.<br /> <br /> Let me know if or where I went astray on this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Included information in the case of targeting multiple texts. Tidied up the wording.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems sensible to me. Anything can become a symbol, language is just a more common way to abstract them and only the mind gives it meaning. So scanning a book for its content should be just as viable as scanning a painting for its meaning or the emotional state of the artist, or using Matter to scan a device to learn how it works. In my Legacy this principle is used to allow the first Attainment to scan and dissect plans.<br /> <br /> By the way, if you think <i>Broken Diamond </i> is good, then you have seen NOTHING yet. Wait until you get to <i> The Soul Cage</i>, the followup AP. After reading it, it became one of my favorite stories ever, look forward to more awesomeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T16:57:54-07:00","id":1318343,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Book of Life (Matter \u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022 )</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling <br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Academics, Investigation <br /> <br /> Quickly obtaining large amounts of information can make all the difference to an archeomancer, allowing them to safely parse it later for new leads. This spell reads the target's memories and instantly records all important events in a chosen medium. A stone statue will have the letters carved into it, a plaque or a book will have the ink move to write the information. More ink or similar materials can be added as yantras and with Life 2 organic substances can be used (blood, milk to act as invisible ink, etc). If the information is too much for the medium to hold, the font size decreases until it fits. <br /> <br /> The creator of this rote was a Mysterium scholar who used it on an ancient Bound, only to find the pages of his research journal turned black. He was later arrested by the Lex Magicka after attempting to steal a Prime Mover's electron microscope and taught it as restitution, since then it has enjoyed widespread use by Awakened scholars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-13-2019, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T10:53:51-07:00","id":1318502,"title":"","content":"<b><i>The Emperor's New Meal (Life \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Socialize, Expression <br /> <br /> Diplomacy sometimes requires one to sample unusual cuisines, failure to uphold the proper decorum in these situations can be disastrous, this spell was created to facilitate that. It can alter or remove the taste, texture or smell of any organic substance. Sometimes its also used as the means to deliver a potent poison. With Matter 2 it can even affect inorganic substances.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Temporal Echo (Time \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b>: Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Sometimes called the Acanthus Alibi or Temporal Invisibility. Upon casting, the target's first [Potency] turns are recorded, they then become invisible and silent as the echo falsifies their temporal presence (but does nothing to mask interactions with the environment), repeating the actions in a loop until duration expires. This is for all intent and purposes an illusion, it can replicate sounds, but cannot be interacted with. If the mage finished the actions in a different point or position, the loop &quot;jumpcuts&quot; back to the start, making the ruse very obvious.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The loop adds extra &quot;animations&quot; to create a smooth transition from start to finish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-14-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T13:06:35-07:00","id":1319111,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I think something like this existed in 1e, but I haven't seen it lately in 2e.<br /> Sensory Shutdown (Mind 2)<br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> By means of this </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">spell</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> a Mage can turn off any of a subject's five senses, one sense per point of potency. While a useful application to keep from being overwhelmed by pain or sound, prolonged exposure to this spell has been known to cause accidental injury and even insanity. Use with caution.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 06-17-2019, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T14:33:09-07:00","id":1319124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1319111#post1319111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I think something like this existed in 1e, but I haven't seen it lately in 2e.<br /> Sensory Shutdown (Mind 2)<br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Stamina<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> By means of this</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">spell</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> a Mage can turn off any of a subject's five senses, one sense per point of potency. While a useful application to keep from being overwhelmed by pain or sound, prolonged exposure to this spell has been known to cause accidental injury and even insanity. Use with caution.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could be a Ruling effect, since you are effectively telling the brain not to process the sensory input, its a lot more overt. Veiling would be for the brain to not even know its missing data or misinterpreted data, such as what the <i>Impostor</i> and <i>Incognito Presence</i> spells do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T21:38:48-07:00","id":1319191,"title":"","content":"<b>Change of Plans (Fate</b> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The Fate Arcanum cannot directly control someone's heart, but it can alter the consequences of a person's intentions. By means of this spell, a mage can change the declared intent of a subject in action scenes, Social Maneuvering, and similar contexts. Even if the subject does nothing differently, circumstances nudge her actions toward fulfilling her new goal. If she comes out victorious in an action scene, she walks away with her new intent fulfilled rather than her original; if she opens all of a target's Doors, the mark might misinterpret her request, or she might blurt out her altered intent accidentally instead, or the mark thinks he's giving her one thing when it's actually another. Using this spell can end up changing factors related to the intent, such as whether enemies can surrender or the number of Doors required to open, but it cannot make the new intent something that would cause a Breaking Point for the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can change the subject's intent to an action that would cause a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Mind</b> </span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>:</b> The subject fully believes her new intent has always been her original desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T23:33:29-07:00","id":1319210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1319191#post1319191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Change of Plans (Fate</b> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The Fate Arcanum cannot directly control someone's heart, but it can alter the consequences of a person's intentions. By means of this spell, a mage can change the declared intent of a subject in action scenes, Social Maneuvering, and similar contexts. Even if the subject does nothing differently, circumstances nudge her actions toward fulfilling her new goal. If she comes out victorious in an action scene, she walks away with her new intent fulfilled rather than her original; if she opens all of a target's Doors, the mark might misinterpret her request, or she might blurt out her altered intent accidentally instead, or the mark thinks he's giving her one thing when it's actually another. Using this spell can end up changing factors related to the intent, such as whether enemies can surrender or the number of Doors required to open, but it cannot make the new intent something that would cause a Breaking Point for the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can change the subject's intent to an action that would cause a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Mind</b> </span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>:</b> The subject fully believes her new intent has always been her original desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say straight up changing one Intention for another would be Patterning, but adding to or subtracting clauses to that Intention could be at the right level for 3 dots. So for instance, if someone in the scene had the Intention of stealing a car, you could use a spell at 3 dots to say that they intend it to be a red car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-28T09:38:21-07:00","id":1321405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1319210#post1319210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say straight up changing one Intention for another would be Patterning, but adding to or subtracting clauses to that Intention could be at the right level for 3 dots. So for instance, if someone in the scene had the Intention of stealing a car, you could use a spell at 3 dots to say that they intend it to be a red car.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that. My reasoning was that an Adept already has broader options available with spells such as Strings of Fate and Chaos Mastery, but you might be right.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's a strange little spell I thought of this morning:<br /> <br /> <b>Exit Stage Left (Death </b>\u2022\u2022 <b>+ Fate \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Intimidation, Politics<br /> <br /> The Awakened know that endings are rarely the end. Through acts of magic, plot twists, or blind luck, anything can happen: The dead might return to life, or an enemy's defeat is far from certain. Some mages have devised a way to keep finality final. Through this spell, once a subject has been consigned to irrelevancy, it can't be brought back until Duration expires. If cast on a subject's corpse, the subject cannot be revived; a totaled car can't be rebuilt; etc. This spell functions on more than just literal death and destruction, however; if the subject has been fired from her job, nothing she does will get her rehired for the spell's Duration. In this case, the spell won't prevent the subject from getting another job somewhere else (ideally someplace far away), but from the mage's point of view, the subject won't be returning to this particular story. Any sort of loss, defeat, or elimination real or symbolic is a valid target for this spell. As per usual, magical attempts to restore the subject's relevancy provoke a Clash of Wills. Some mages use this power to ensure that powerful evils remain vanquished or bound, but many Consilia also consider certain applications to be cruel, bordering on Left-Handed practice.<br /> <br /> This spell cannot override the Sanctity of Merits rule.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T18:04:35-07:00","id":1321565,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Quickcarpet (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Craft, Science, Survival<br /> <br /> This makes an object unable to properly support weight, making anyone or anything that stands upon it sink past it. The creator famously used this to defend her Sanctum from a Banisher attack. After casting it on the floor, she hid it from the Peripheral Sight by placing a carpet over it. When the Banishers arrived, they fell into a basement full of sharp spikes.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> You can specify up to [Potency] materials that do not sink when making contact with it. With conjunctional Life 1 or Fate 1, you can instead allocate Potency on a 1 to 1 basis to specify people or living beings (eg &quot;Sentinel Prospero and any ferret&quot;) that do not sink.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Bowling Bomb(Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Craft, Science, Weaponry<br /> <br /> This gives an object the ability to either slide like a pinball or bounce like a rubber ball, allowing the mage to pull of impossible trick shots that ignore [Potency] points of cover. Some Arrows use it to deliver sleeping gas, tear gas to end encounters non-lethaly, or to even use dynamite and grenades when its not possible.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hardlight (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Craft, Science <br /> <br /> This shapes light into any form the mage desires and fixes it as a solid. The object has Durability 2, weapon rating 2 if it's a weapon and armor rating 2 if it's armor. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify up to [Potency] light types that cause it to become insubstantial once more while exposed, such as torchlight, candlelight, infrared light, ultra violet light, flashlights or even colored lights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-04-2019, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-29T21:00:53-07:00","id":1321575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1321565#post1321565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Hardlight (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Craft, Science<br /> <br /> Light is both a wave and a particle, depending on how it is interacted with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, the wave-particle duality of quantum objects is very complicated and hotly debated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This shapes it into any form the mage desires and fixates it as a particle. </div> </div> </div>fixate <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>cause (someone) to acquire an obsessive attachment to someone or something.</li> <li>direct one's eyes toward.</li> </ol><br /> The word you're looking for is &quot;fixes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, this doesn't achieve what you want. Forcing light to only behave as a particle only (which doesn't make sense, everything behaves as both a particle and a wave) would not turn it &quot;hard,&quot; it still would not have mass in the non-quantum, non-relativistic sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The object has Durability 2, weapon rating 2 if it's a weapon and armor rating 2 if it's armor. Any spells to further strengthen it require Matter 3 conjunctional. </div> </div> </div>These are properties of mass, and therefore would inherently require Matter 3 conjunctional as part of the base spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may specify up to [Potency] light types that cause hardlight to become a wave while exposed, such as torchlight, candlelight, infrared light, ultra violet light, flashlights or even colored lights. </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really make any sense as worded. Like, does it cause the &quot;hardlight&quot; to disperse with this reach option? What do you think &quot;become a wave&quot; means?<br /> <br /> Basically, Hardlight should be Forces 3 + Matter 3 out of the box, you're giving non-quantum properties to quantum things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-30-2019, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T05:13:39-07:00","id":1321596,"title":"","content":"Symbolically speaking Forces deals with forces while it is Matter that deals with solids, so definitely Forces+Matter. It would arguably also require Patterning instead of Weaving since it's less about granting a property and more about transforming it into something it is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T08:33:21-07:00","id":1321607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1321596#post1321596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Symbolically speaking Forces deals with forces while it is Matter that deals with solids, so definitely Forces+Matter. It would arguably also require Patterning instead of Weaving since it's less about granting a property and more about transforming it into something it is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically I am not turning light into matter, I am giving it the property of being solid and then treating it like ectoplasm, which arguably requires Matter. But I am not turning it into steel, titanium, nitinol or anything like that. Did you mean that it transforms it into a halfway point between light and matter ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-30-2019, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T09:34:50-07:00","id":1321610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1321607#post1321607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically I am not turning light into matter, I am giving it the property of being solid and then treating it like ectoplasm, which arguably requires Matter. But I am not turning it into steel, titanium, nitinol or anything like that. Did you mean that it transforms it into a halfway point between light and matter ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;arguably&quot; because the distinction between granting something the property of a solid and transforming it into a solid is purely academical. Regardless, it should definitely require Matter because <i>solidity as a property</i> isn't something that Forces deals with.<br /> <br /> Ectoplasm is a false analogue because it's a Death related substance that happens to be solid in its natural state. Shaping ectoplasm only requires Ruling because you're merely shaping it, not granting it additional properties. You could use Forces in a similar way to shape, say, fire into a variety of shapes, but it wouldn't make the fire solid because it's not solid in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T16:16:33-07:00","id":1321660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1321610#post1321610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said &quot;arguably&quot; because the distinction between granting something the property of a solid and transforming it into a solid is purely academical. Regardless, it should definitely require Matter because <i>solidity as a property</i> isn't something that Forces deals with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can turn Shadows solid with Death 3, too, though...<br /> <br /> This spell is literally just a published spell (Shadow Crafting) with the serial numbers filed off. That spell doesn't require Matter and neither should this. The precedent for requiring Matter to give things solidity in 2E is incredibly weak <i>at best.</i><br /> <br /> 'Solids' <i>is</i> listed as being under the purview of Matter, but that doesn't necessarily make them sacrosanct and untouchable by any other Arcanum in any way; language is the purview of Prime and yet Universal Language is a Mind Spell (sensibly and reasonably so).<br /> <br /> For reference:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadow Crafting</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The caster can shape and harden shadows into solid, three-dimensional forms. The object gains a Durability of 2. If it is a weapon it gains a weapon rating of 2; if it is armor it gains an armor rating of 2; otherwise the object gains a +2 equipment bonus. Objects made of shadow retain a shadowy appearance and cast no shadow of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardlight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This shapes light into any form the mage desires and fixes it as a solid. The object has Durability 2, weapon rating 2 if it's a weapon and armor rating 2 if it's armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-30-2019, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-30T18:14:15-07:00","id":1321675,"title":"","content":"The Death shadow spells are bad examples because they break the guidelines, causing quite a bit of head scratching for everyone who's tried to figure out why.<br /> The best answers I can come up with is that Death deals with other things that are solid (such as dead bodies) as well as being one of two Arcana that can apply Manifestation effects. It's not great explanations, I know.<br /> <br /> Universal Language works because language, despite being a Prime thing, is also a subset of learned knowledge, a Mind thing. No, purviews aren't sacrosanct, but there should still be a good reason for one Arcanum to deal with another's purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T19:17:30-07:00","id":1321813,"title":"","content":"Agreed, it can be tremendously confusing. In Prime's case I can see the spell exercising its domain of truth. But for the Death shadow spells I never figured out a better answer than &quot;this was fun to do with the Lasombra, so mages will probably want to do it too&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Prepare Rations (Life \u2022\u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Craft, Survival<br /> <br /> The modern age has seen mages more commonly live in cities, where foraging skills are rarely necessary. But the supernatural can be treacherous and a mage can find themselves stranded without supplies. For an adept of Life this is a trivial matter to solve, for everyone else the Arrow recommends this spell.<br /> <br /> This allows a mage to transform any supply of meat or fish into pemmican, a simple mix of dried meat and fat. Pemmican is filling, easy to carry and can last for years (or even a decade with proper storage). If any berries or spices are in hand, they can be added into the spell to make the end product more palatable. The water extracted by drying the meat can be stored away in a canteen or similar container nearby.<br /> <br /> <i>Observation:</i> For comparison's sake, a rabbit can produce enough to feed a person for 3 days of intense exercise, an elk can feed a party of 6 for a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-02-2019, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T13:24:44-07:00","id":1322095,"title":"","content":"All these creative space spells flying around, and I have yet to see one create something as banal but useful as a hole in a wall.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ingress (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The empty space between the atomic cloud of an atom and its nucleus is just that: empty space. No matter how infinitesimally small, that space is still a Lie; one that a scientifically-minded Awakened can manipulate. This spell widens that space, creating an opening that a mage can exploit to simply step through a wall in situations where the front door makes for a less than savory entrance.<br /> <br /> The Scale spell factor must encompass the full length, height, and width of the intended passage created through the wall. The volume of the passage is increased a number of steps along the area scale factor equal to the spell's potency. Anyone or anything within the passage when the spell expires is ejected from the near end of the passage.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> I used the rote Secret Room to help craft this one. I figure weaving should be all that's needed, as we're simply altering the properties of sub-atomic space, widening that to an accommodating volume.<br /> <br /> My only question is would an unveiling or similar spell of Space be needed to observe the tiny gaps? Or would simply being able to see the wall, knowing how atoms work, and that those infinitesimally tiny gaps exist be sufficient? I plan to edit the rote to reflect that if one is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T09:22:05-07:00","id":1322432,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i><b><i>Bottled Lighting (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022, Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</i></b></i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Primary factor:</b> Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Crafts, </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Expression, </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Science</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Even if you\u2019re an acanthus you don\u2019t always have a convenient electrical socket or bonfire from which to bring down your wrath. Sometimes you need to pack your own heat. This spell allows you to isolate and compress one of the forces under the purview of the Forces arcana within a sphere of space. The transparent sphere is small enough to fit in your hand and can be moved and carried freely.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">The force can be manipulated as normal within the sphere using the Forces arcana, but the inclusion of Space<b> \u2022\u2022\u2022</b> is required for any spell that would attempt to remove or extend the influence of the force outside the orb. Upon the spell's end, any remaining force within the orb decompresses violently, dealing bashing damage equal to the potency of the spell if applicable\u2014or inflicting a condition\u2014to anything within an area of effect equal to the scale of the spell originating from the spell\u2019s location.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage can specify a Key that allows the Force within to be drawn upon by a spell without the inclusion of </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Space <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022.</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">- - -</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A portable source of forces, a gnarly topper for a wizard staff, and in a pinch a magical grenade! I figure the force within can't diminish because it's literally trapped in a bubble of isolated space. The energy has nowhere to dissipate or ground out to so it just sort of furiously swirls or bounces around within. Even fire, which needs fuel, is just air superheated to the point that it glows, so with no way for the heat to escape even a fire would stay within. I didn't limit the damage done from a separate spell to the potency of this spell because it's literally just a source and they're already paying the cost of casting at higher potencies for a separate spell at that point. Not to mention the added Space arcana they need to pull it out without the reach.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-10-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T10:44:10-07:00","id":1322452,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Shielding alone could prevent energy from discharging, and Scale covers size. I think I'd let you do something similar with just Forces 2. You end up with say, a copper rod with a ridiculous amount of charge on it, or at least the maximum amount of charge it could be expected to hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:18:08-07:00","id":1322459,"title":"","content":"<b><i> Hold the Defiant Breath (Fate \u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Expression, Indimidation<br /> <br /> A favorite spell amongst agents of the Lex Magicka, for it allows them to place subjects on probation. They can specify up to [Potency] conditions, which must be things they could see if present, breaking any of them instantly removes most of the air from the target, instantly knocking them out. They keep receiving just enough air to stay alive without damage, but not enough to regain consciousness. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: You get a brief vision of the target when the breach occurs.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: You can track the target until the duration ends - not by location, but as a sense of a path that will take you to them.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The trigger can be something only perceived by Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-05-2019, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:08:15-07:00","id":1322479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322459#post1322459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i> Hold the Defiant Breath (Fate \u2022, Matter \u2022\u2022)</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks good. But correct me if I'm wrong, but wouldn't this spell require Fate <b>\u2022\u2022 </b>to match Matter <b>\u2022\u2022</b>? I was under the impression that all arcana used in the spell had to be at the same dot level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:48:52-07:00","id":1322490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322479#post1322479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks good. But correct me if I'm wrong, but wouldn't this spell require Fate <b>\u2022\u2022 </b>to match Matter <b>\u2022\u2022</b>? I was under the impression that all arcana used in the spell had to be at the same dot level.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just requires the practices it needs of each. In this case a Ruling of Matter for moving the air and a Knowing of Fate for Oaths Fullfilled.<br /> <br /> Another example, a Weaving of Life and Matter would be needed to give the properties of a machine to an animal (Matter to cover the machine's characteristics and Weaving of Life to affect the properties of a living being) or both Arcana at 4 to transform a chair into a fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-05-2019, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T13:49:35-07:00","id":1322491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322479#post1322479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good. But correct me if I'm wrong, but wouldn't this spell require Fate <b>\u2022\u2022 </b>to match Matter <b>\u2022\u2022</b>? I was under the impression that all arcana used in the spell had to be at the same dot level.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:33:23-07:00","id":1322516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322490#post1322490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It just requires the practices it needs of each. In this case a Ruling of Matter for moving the air and a Knowing of Fate for Oaths Fullfilled.<br /> <br /> Another example, a Weaving of Life and Matter would be needed give the properties of a machine to an animal (Matter to cover the machine's characteristics and Weaving of Life to affect the properties of a living being) or both Arcana at 4 to transform a chair into a fish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, its only if they use the same practices. That's where my thought process was off. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T07:52:16-07:00","id":1322593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322095#post1322095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All these creative space spells flying around, and I have yet to see one create something as banal but useful as a hole in a wall.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ingress (Space \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The empty space between the atomic cloud of an atom and its nucleus is just that: empty space. No matter how infinitesimally small, that space is still a Lie; one that a scientifically-minded Awakened can manipulate. This spell widens that space, creating an opening that a mage can exploit to simply step through a wall in situations where the front door makes for a less than savory entrance.<br /> <br /> The Scale spell factor must encompass the full length, height, and width of the intended passage created through the wall. The volume of the passage is increased a number of steps along the area scale factor equal to the spell's potency. Anyone or anything within the passage when the spell expires is ejected from the near end of the passage.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> I used the rote Secret Room to help craft this one. I figure weaving should be all that's needed, as we're simply altering the properties of sub-atomic space, widening that to an accommodating volume.<br /> <br /> My only question is would an unveiling or similar spell of Space be needed to observe the tiny gaps? Or would simply being able to see the wall, knowing how atoms work, and that those infinitesimally tiny gaps exist be sufficient? I plan to edit the rote to reflect that if one is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason people haven't made such a spell is that break boundary already does that when you include the reach option.<br /> <br /> Edit: Granted, your interpretation of the +2 reach option could be different from my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 07-06-2019, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:07:56-07:00","id":1322596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322593#post1322593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason people haven't made such a spell is that break boundary already does that when you include the reach option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. It only allows you to bypass an obstacle blocking an actual path. It calls out in the spell that you cannot go through a solid wall. The reaches just allow you to fit through small openings you wouldn't be able to otherwise or to outright &quot;blink&quot; through the obstacle if you're unable to move.<br /> <br /> I guess using my argument above you could constitute the &quot;atomic space&quot; as a small opening you wouldn't be able to fit through otherwise but then you're trying to pull yourself in through an opening you can't even see at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:24:15-07:00","id":1322597,"title":"","content":"The &quot;unable to move&quot; part of the +2 reach option is where I see the spell allowing you to bypass walls. Nobody is ever placed into a situation where they truly cannot move unless they are bound stiff or paralyzed, which, quite frankly, is so rare that I disagree with that being the only interpretation of that clause.<br /> <br /> Edit: It can also be argued that adding a +2 reach option to bypass solid barriers that block your path would not be unreasonable. Word count limits are a thing.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Furthermore, as an aesthetic thing: when designing a spell that has universal application, I find it better to not call upon science as the justification for the knowledge necessary to do something. Gnosis and symbolism, not science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 07-06-2019, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:43:25-07:00","id":1322599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322597#post1322597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;unable to move&quot; part of the +2 reach option is where I see the spell allowing you to bypass walls. Nobody is ever placed into a situation where they truly cannot move unless they are bound stiff or paralyzed, which, quite frankly, is so rare that I disagree with that being the only interpretation of that clause.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to respectfully disagree. Going back to the original text, &quot;This spell can only bypass a physical obstacle obstructing an actual path...but can not blink through a solid wall.&quot; I would think if the +2 Reach option were for going through objects that were not obstructions to actual paths it would have used that exact terminology. It goes to immense pains in the body of the spell to specify what can and cannot be constituted as an &quot;obstruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Reach only states that it allows you to go through &quot;obstructions&quot; even if you are unable to move but it does not redefine what obstruction means. It seems to be exactly what it appears, strange as it is.<br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it better to not call upon science as the justification for the knowledge necessary to do something. Gnosis and symbolism, not science. </div> </div> </div>The Free Council would like a word with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-06-2019, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T08:52:14-07:00","id":1322601,"title":"","content":"If I already posted some of these then sorry, I haven't figured out how to looks for a specific persons posts in a specific thread.<br /> <br /> Meaning of Life (Fate 1) - Knowing<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> Skill: Empathy, Academics, Occult<br /> <br /> The mage learns one of the subjects Aspirations per point of potency.<br /> Add Prime 1: can also reveal an obsession<br /> Mnd 1: can also reaveal the subjects Virtue and Vice<br /> <br /> <br /> Catalyst (Matter 2) - Rulling<br /> Primery factor: Potency<br /> Skill: Science, Occult, Persuassion<br /> <br /> Innate matter is always in the state of balance between the forces that wish to transform it and forces that wish it stayed the same. As thermodynamics teach us wood wants to burn, it just needs a nudge in the right direction.. Still spell cause a substance to interact with another one in a way it would if given the proper nudge to start things up. So wood exposed to air will burn, a a lump of rocksalt will disolve in water without the need for a lot of stirring. The spell needs a certain level of potency to work depending on how hard is it to force the reaction per storyteller discretion.<br /> <br /> Basal ingredients (Matter 3) - Fraying<br /> Primary factor: Potency<br /> Withstand: Durabillity<br /> <br /> The spell can separate a substance into it's elemental compotents. Water splits into oxigen and hydrogen gas and organic matter becomes lumps of mostly coal, some oxigen, hydrogen and nitrogen and small amount of other substances. The spell disolves one point of Structure per dot of potency, inflicting that as damage.<br /> Reach +1: The separation doesn't have go down to elemental levels, sugar can be transformed into water and carbon dioxide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T09:04:41-07:00","id":1322602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322599#post1322599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to respectfully disagree. Going back to the original text, &quot;This spell can only bypass a physical obstacle obstructing an actual path...but can not blink through a solid wall.&quot; I would think if the +2 Reach option were for going through objects that were not obstructions to actual paths it would have used that exact terminology. It goes to immense pains in the body of the spell to specify what can and cannot be constituted as an &quot;obstruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Reach only states that it allows you to go through &quot;obstructions&quot; even if you are unable to move but it does not redefine what obstruction means. It seems to be exactly what it appears, strange as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, if you wish to acknowledge all of that you immediately add the +2 reach option that says: This spell now allows the subject to bypass solid barriers that would block its path so long as the area factor would not need to be increased.<br /> <br /> Break boundary should allow you to go through walls. Maybe just my opinion, but I will not change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T09:11:47-07:00","id":1322604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322602#post1322602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which, if you wish to acknowledge all of that you immediately add the +2 reach option that says: This spell now allows the subject to bypass solid barriers that would block its path so long as the area factor would not need to be increased.<br /> <br /> Break boundary should allow you to go through walls. Maybe just my opinion, but I will not change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can respect that, a storyteller is able to interpret things in whatever way is convenient to them. My first point still stands though: there still isn't a Space spell that creates something so banal and useful as a hole in a wall. =P<br /> <br /> (Baring further commentary, I'm aware that other spells fulfill similar purposes, or can even be construed in such a way that it looks like there is a hole in the wall, such as co-location.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T10:24:03-07:00","id":1322620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1322604#post1322604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can respect that, a storyteller is able to interpret things in whatever way is convenient to them. My first point still stands though: there still isn't a Space spell that creates something so banal and useful as a hole in a wall. =P<br /> <br /> (Baring further commentary, I'm aware that other spells fulfill similar purposes, or can even be construed in such a way that it looks like there is a hole in the wall, such as co-location.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Matter can accomplish it with Shaping, as well as other things like wall elevators, levitating rocks, etc. I think the draw of this spell is giving a Mastigos a way to deal with a solid,opaque obstacle which does not leave evidence behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-06-2019, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T21:32:33-07:00","id":1322704,"title":"","content":"<b><i> Occlude Mantra (Prime \u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Expression, Occult<br /> <br /> Mages are a paranoid lot, so it is considered proper decorum to cast using mantras at Consilium events. When negotiating on the field with a volatile willworker, it is a necessity. This allows the mage to mask their High Speech for the duration, allowing it to register as the blueprints for any other spell they could cast (such as making Sleep of the Just sound like Words of Truth). If anyone suspects the deception and attempts to pierce it, it causes a Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-07-2019, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:50:06-07:00","id":1323680,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Edit: The new version of the first Rote can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition/page105#post1323877\">here.</a> Grayed out this one to preserve the post yet reinforce that this one is incorrect in its execution.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">Combustion (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary</b> <b>Factor:</b> Potency Suggested<br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Science<br /> <br /> This spell gathers and temporarily suppresses the molecular bonds of the hydrogen and oxygen within the water vapor in the air before rapidly compressing them down to a point. This causes an adiabatic reaction, heating the hydrogen above its autoignition temperature and setting it alight. The resulting fire and decompressing air creates a fiery explosion that deals bashing damage equal to the Potency of this spell. This spell works best in areas of high humidity.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The explosion releases black, sooty smoke causing the Blinded Tilt.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The explosion has significant force behind it causing the Knocked Down or Stunned Tilt.</span><br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Even before I knew Mage existed, this was always my reasoning for how my characters made fiery explosions. Do you know what the best part of this is? When you ignite something it basically takes it and bonds it to oxygen atoms. In this case, you're igniting the hydrogen and the output of that is literally water vapor. Even if the rules of spellcasting made everything Lasting by default, you'd be able to do this same spell over and over again.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, the four dot lethal version.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">Explosion (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Science<br /> <br /> This spell gathers the air and directly converts it to hydrogen before rapidly compressing it down to a point. This causes an adiabatic reaction, heating the hydrogen above its autoignition temperature and setting it alight. The resulting fire and decompressing air creates a blazing explosion that deals lethal damage equal to the Potency of this spell. This spell significantly increases the humidity within the area </span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">determined by the Scale of the spell</span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> for the duration of the spell and may potentially start fires on flammable surfaces.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The spell deals aggravated damage. Cost: 1 Mana.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell increases the heat and humidity within the area dramatically, creating the Extreme Heat Environmental Tilt.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The explosion releases black, sooty smoke causing the Blinded Tilt.<br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b>The explosion has significant force behind it causing the Knocked Down or Stunned Tilt.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-12-2019, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:18:20-07:00","id":1323760,"title":"","content":"I think people get too caught up in real world &quot;fallen&quot; science, and it doesn't really map that well to in-game Supernal Truth. Matter affects the physical property of Things, and yes, air and water vapor are Things, but once you get down to molecular bonds, you are really tangling with electromagnetic forces, the purview of... well, Forces.<br /> <br /> I think you can use Matter in more indirect ways, like changing the temperature at which a Thing ignites. Isn't that the same thing? Maybe, from a scientific point of view, but it's different from a Mage's point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:37:47-07:00","id":1323765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323760#post1323760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people get too caught up in real world &quot;fallen&quot; science, and it doesn't really map that well to in-game Supernal Truth. Matter affects the physical property of Things, and yes, air and water vapor are Things, but once you get down to molecular bonds, you are really tangling with electromagnetic forces, the purview of... well, Forces.<br /> <br /> I think you can use Matter in more indirect ways, like changing the temperature at which a Thing ignites. Isn't that the same thing? Maybe, from a scientific point of view, but it's different from a Mage's point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could argue that yes, but then you're also able to change water to ice or vapor with the same Weaving practice. Whether water is a liquid, solid, or gas depends on how much energy the particles have. The more they move and bounce off each other, the less &quot;solid&quot; the state of water is. That is also encroaching on the realm of Forces if we analyze it that way.<br /> <br /> In this case, I could make the argument that I'm suppressing the attributes of the molecules that allow them to bond via electrons in the first place, temporarily separating the water into its base components. I'm sure I could come up a few other ways to frame it by just messing with the individual matter molecules, but I think you get the idea.<br /> <br /> I understand that symbolism is a big thing in Mage, but the existence of the Free Council to me ensures that sleeper science has a place within magic symbolism. I tend to lean in that direction myself because its what I enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-11-2019, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:23:43-07:00","id":1323777,"title":"","content":"The existence of the Free Council allows you to us Science as a rote skill, and scientific parafernalia as yantras. But science, as we understand it, is a Lie. If it were true, Magic would be impossible. The fact you can change the state of water or the properties of air with Magic, means that The Truth of their nature and the laws that rule them is very different.<br /> <br /> As I say, igniting the air with Matter seems possible to me, but you change the way you look at it and possibly the consequences. Magically introducing or eliminating a form of Energy is what Forces does. Matter just makes things glitch out and act in ways they wouldn't normally act and that can create weird consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T16:26:31-07:00","id":1323802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323777#post1323777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of the Free Council allows you to us Science as a rote skill, and scientific parafernalia as yantras. But science, as we understand it, is a Lie. If it were true, Magic would be impossible</div> </div> </div> </div>Using magic to operate within the bounds of the Lie isn't sacrilege here. Mages still need to exist within the Lie. They're ruled by it. One can still realize that reality is a Lie and play along with it. It's just another way to use magic as far as I'm concerned. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323777#post1323777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I say, igniting the air with Matter seems possible to me, but you change the way you look at it and possibly the consequences. Magically introducing or eliminating a form of Energy is what Forces does. Matter just makes things glitch out and act in ways they wouldn't normally act and that can create weird consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I consider the electrons to be as much an attribute of the matter as the molecules are. Plus &quot;alter conductivity&quot; is within the bounds of Matter, so altering the molecules in such a way that it temporarily releases their electron bond should be within the bounds of Matter as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T16:29:28-07:00","id":1323804,"title":"","content":"FWIW I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25329\" data-vbnamecard=\"25329\">RobinCoyote</a> that if Matter can alter conductivity it <i>must</i> have the ability to manipulate electron association with a particular nucleus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T18:20:24-07:00","id":1323815,"title":"","content":"Well, not must but certainly lends credence to the possibility.<br /> <br /> My problem with both spells is that they compress the air, aka cause movement and/or pressure, both concepts that fall more naturally under Forces. Now you could change the density of a material using Matter to achieve similar effects, but that's a separate effect from these spells and would likely require an immense amount of Potency to reach the same results.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be an inherent stability/stasis factor to Matter, as evidenced by Transubstantiation being unable to change an object into a volatile material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:00:17-07:00","id":1323820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323815#post1323815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not must but certainly lends credence to the possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how conductivity has everything to do with what energy states electrons are in and how &quot;bound&quot; they are to a specific nucleus, it is a must.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:15:49-07:00","id":1323823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323815#post1323815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with both spells is that they compress the air, aka cause movement and/or pressure, both concepts that fall more naturally under Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like there's already precedence from Windstrike and Piercing. It seems like any gross arcana can at the very least induce motion within their purview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323815#post1323815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There also seems to be an inherent stability/stasis factor to Matter, as evidenced by Transubstantiation being unable to change an object into a volatile material.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got me there. It's a lot of weight to put on the word 'inert' in one spell though. I feel like people throw that word around regarding matter without realizing its definition. Not to mention that means that matter has trouble somehow influencing a good chunk of the periodic table which I find hard to believe.<br /> <br /> But look at me, flip-flopping between my support of precedence. x3<br /> <br /> I mostly was basing the second spell off the definition of Weaving, which is, &quot;Patterning spells allow a mage to completely transform a target into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s purview.&quot; But who really knows, I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:28:44-07:00","id":1323826,"title":"","content":"A similar topic came up when there was a discussion about using Matter to turn steel into liquid. Some had the assumption that it would necessarily be molten. We got the clarification that nope, it would just be liquid. I\u2019m inclined to think Matter is unlikely to cause an explosion or burn things just because you effect the bonds between the subject\u2019s constituent parts or alter its conductivity, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:49:51-07:00","id":1323831,"title":"","content":"I find it bizarre that its easier to transmute something as invisible and untouchable as time into a tangible inanimate object than it is to make matter explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:47:25-07:00","id":1323843,"title":"","content":"You can make Matter explode easily enough, you just can\u2019t cause it to have energetic reactions through Matter alone. For instance you could Transubstantiate something into inert potassium, but it won\u2019t be long before it reacts with the atmosphere. That\u2019s more physics and chemistry taking over than the results of your magic though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:59:53-07:00","id":1323848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323831#post1323831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it bizarre that its easier to transmute something as invisible and untouchable as time into a tangible inanimate object than it is to make matter explode</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a very specific assumption you're making in this sentence that relies on a very literalistic reading of the Practice of Patterning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T22:39:12-07:00","id":1323865,"title":"","content":"<b>Crab-Brain (Life</b><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or One Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Crafts, Empathy<br /> <br /> I don't really know why you'd cast this spell, but here we are. The mage who decides to do this sort of thing transforms one of the subject's thought-patterns into a living organism. This can turn a Mental Condition into an animal; the subject no longer suffers from the Condition's effects. This can also transform a memory, dream, or passing thought. To affect a Persistent Condition or fundamental part of the subject's personality requires a point of Mana. This spell can be cast with an animal symbolic of the affected thought in mind, but this is not necessary; depression can be transformed into a giraffe, and reality won't really care. When the spell's Duration ends, the animal disappears and the Condition remanifests; if the animal is killed in the meantime, the Condition is permanently removed, but the subject gains no Beat for the excisement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:33:46-07:00","id":1323872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323865#post1323865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crab-Brain (Life</b><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or One Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Crafts, Empathy<br /> <br /> I don't really know why you'd cast this spell, but here we are. The mage who decides to do this sort of thing transforms one of the subject's thought-patterns into a living organism. This can turn a Mental Condition into an animal; the subject no longer suffers from the Condition's effects. This can also transform a memory, dream, or passing thought. To affect a Persistent Condition or fundamental part of the subject's personality requires a point of Mana. This spell can be cast with an animal symbolic of the affected thought in mind, but this is not necessary; depression can be transformed into a giraffe, and reality won't really care. When the spell's Duration ends, the animal disappears and the Condition remanifests; if the animal is killed in the meantime, the Condition is permanently removed, but the subject gains no Beat for the excisement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have watched this anime, pretty sure everyone involved got Beats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T23:50:37-07:00","id":1323877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323848#post1323848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a very specific assumption you're making in this sentence that relies on a very literalistic reading of the Practice of Patterning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's vague.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to admit though that based on what I've gleaned from you guys, the first spell doesn't work. The hydrogen and oxygen atoms would retain the qualities of water vapor because the spell would not produce a Lasting effect. The particles are still water, I've just separated it into parts; it would snap back together on spell end. But I'm not one to give up because something didn't work the first time, so here we are. Same spell. Same mechanics. Different flavor text. <br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">Combustion </span><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">(Matter </span><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b><span style=\"color:#134F5C\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><b>)</b></span></span><br /> <b>Practice: </b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Weaving</span><br /> <b>Primary</b><b>Factor:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Potency Suggested</span><br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Academics, Crafts, Science</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">This spell gathers the air in an area and increases its flammability before rapidly compressing it down to a point. This causes an adiabatic reaction, heating the air above its autoignition temperature and setting it alight. The resulting fire and decompressing air creates a fiery explosion that deals bashing damage equal to the Potency of this spell. </span><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> The explosion releases black, sooty smoke causing the Blinded Tilt.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">The explosion has significant force behind it causing the Knocked Down or Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> The second Rote from the previous post still works as written. Even if transforming one periodic element into another doesn't give it the same attributes as the matter you've transformed it into, it falls within the purview of the practices of three dots or higher to simply alter the attributes of something that falls under the purview of the Arcanum. So I could technically convert all air into hydrogen and also give it the attributes of hydrogen, specifically flammability.<br /> <br /> @</span>Mrmdubois<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> pointed out that liquid steel wouldn't be motlen as an example earlier\u2014the reason for that, from what I can figure, is that matter can only alter attributes but would not be able to instill or remove heat as that falls under Forces. So you'd have liquid steel but it wouldn't need to be hot to be such, nor could you render it such without Forces.<br /> <br /> (It should be noted that no </span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Arcana is directly applying the heat for ignition within these Rotes. The Rotes instead &quot;game&quot; the laws of thermodynamics to produce it.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T00:55:01-07:00","id":1323884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323877#post1323877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's vague.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed you were bright enough to put two and two together and also that you didn't come up with the notion of changing Time into Matter (in this system where &quot;having four dots in two Arcana is required to completely change something in the purview of one into something in the purview of another&quot; is part of the spellcasting quick-reference list) completely on your own.<br /> <br /> The system very obviously can't be as unconditionally open-ended as &quot;anything listed in the purviews of an Arcanum can have anything covered by the Practices of a given dot rating done to or with it, even if it breaks the setting or doesn't make sense.&quot; The game doesn't provide any real workable precedent for converting discrete units of time into discrete physical substances apart from maybe in the abstract outcome of a powerful combined spell, nor does it offer much of any guidance to suggest that spells to manipulate time do so in a way analogous to how the three gross Arcana covering directly palpable phenomena work; the closest it gets is the fact that Time spells occupy phenomenal reality just like other spells do.<br /> <br /> Of course it's bizarre for it to be easier to transmute time into an inanimate object than to make matter explode. That's a bizarre state of affairs, not least because it describes the opposite of how the game works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T03:37:20-07:00","id":1323901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323865#post1323865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crab-Brain (Life</b><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None or One Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Animal Ken, Crafts, Empathy<br /> <br /> I don't really know why you'd cast this spell, but here we are. The mage who decides to do this sort of thing transforms one of the subject's thought-patterns into a living organism. This can turn a Mental Condition into an animal; the subject no longer suffers from the Condition's effects. This can also transform a memory, dream, or passing thought. To affect a Persistent Condition or fundamental part of the subject's personality requires a point of Mana. This spell can be cast with an animal symbolic of the affected thought in mind, but this is not necessary; depression can be transformed into a giraffe, and reality won't really care. When the spell's Duration ends, the animal disappears and the Condition remanifests; if the animal is killed in the meantime, the Condition is permanently removed, but the subject gains no Beat for the excisement.</div> </div> </div> </div>While i appreciate the reference this is pretty much a variant of Goetic Summons with additional Life component to make stuff have a body.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T05:32:14-07:00","id":1323925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323884#post1323884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed you were bright enough to put two and two together</div> </div> </div> </div>Opening with condescension and a thinly-veiled insult. Bless your heart, dear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I came into this thread to share something I thought was a cool, nifty idea for a Matter combat Rote. I am a new player/storyteller and still lack some understanding, but I was open to criticism, politely defended my reasoning, and even backed off and admitted I was wrong when I realized that the rules and precedence were arrayed against me. The comment you responded to was admittedly one I made of frustration because I was tunnel-visioned with making my Rote work a specific way and needed to derail and rethink.<br /> <br /> Your comment<ul><li>provided no new or relevant information.</li> <li>did not add anything to the conversation.</li> <li>was slightly condescending.</li> </ul>So I decided that your comment warranted and was worth a two-word, noncommittal response. &quot;That's vague.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I do thank you for your second post despite the initial hostility, it was helpful in its own unique way to my understanding of the system. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323865#post1323865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Crab-Brain (Life</b><b> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> I don't really know why you'd cast this spell, but here we are. The mage who decides to do this sort of thing transforms one of the subject's thought-patterns into a living organism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picture a bored Mastigos using this to toy with his apprentice and amuse himself ala the Dodgeball method of training. &quot;If you can catch your libido, you can counter a spell!&quot; While their apprentice wildly chases their psyche-made-manifest pleading it not to get run over and to come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 07-12-2019, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:42:11-07:00","id":1323976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323872#post1323872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have watched this anime, pretty sure everyone involved got Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what anime? Based on Menace's response this is apparently accidentally a reference to something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:53:12-07:00","id":1323978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RobinCoyote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323877#post1323877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's vague.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to admit though that based on what I've gleaned from you guys, the first spell doesn't work. The hydrogen and oxygen atoms would retain the qualities of water vapor because the spell would not produce a Lasting effect. The particles are still water, I've just separated it into parts; it would snap back together on spell end. But I'm not one to give up because something didn't work the first time, so here we are. Same spell. Same mechanics. Different flavor text.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">Combustion </span><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">(Matter </span><span style=\"color:#134F5C\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b><span style=\"color:#134F5C\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><b>)</b></span></span><br /> <b>Practice: </b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Weaving</span><br /> <b>Primary</b><b>Factor:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Potency Suggested</span><br /> <b>Rote Skills:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Academics, Crafts, Science</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">This spell gathers the air in an area and increases its flammability before rapidly compressing it down to a point. This causes an adiabatic reaction, heating the air above its autoignition temperature and setting it alight. The resulting fire and decompressing air creates a fiery explosion that deals bashing damage equal to the Potency of this spell. </span><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> The explosion releases black, sooty smoke causing the Blinded Tilt.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">The explosion has significant force behind it causing the Knocked Down or Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> The second Rote from the previous post still works as written. Even if transforming one periodic element into another doesn't give it the same attributes as the matter you've transformed it into, it falls within the purview of the practices of three dots or higher to simply alter the attributes of something that falls under the purview of the Arcanum. So I could technically convert all air into hydrogen and also give it the attributes of hydrogen, specifically flammability.<br /> <br /> @</span>Mrmdubois<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> pointed out that liquid steel wouldn't be motlen as an example earlier\u2014the reason for that, from what I can figure, is that matter can only alter attributes but would not be able to instill or remove heat as that falls under Forces. So you'd have liquid steel but it wouldn't need to be hot to be such, nor could you render it such without Forces.<br /> <br /> (It should be noted that no </span><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Arcana is directly applying the heat for ignition within these Rotes. The Rotes instead &quot;game&quot; the laws of thermodynamics to produce it.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a less tortured way to go about this which is to create an area of air that reacts to the air around it like a highly reactive substance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:10:14-07:00","id":1323989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323976#post1323976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what anime? Based on Menace's response this is apparently accidentally a reference to something?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://myanimelist.net/anime/5081/Bakemonogatari\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Bakemonogatari</i></a>, the first arc<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">is about a girl whose emotional (and, consequently, physical) &quot;weight&quot; has been turned into a giant crab; the main character of the series helps her.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:24:49-07:00","id":1323994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323989#post1323989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://myanimelist.net/anime/5081/Bakemonogatari\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Bakemonogatari</i></a>, the first arc<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">is about a girl whose emotional (and, consequently, physical) &quot;weight&quot; has been turned into a giant crab; the main character of the series helps her.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, interesting. I honestly had no idea. I was just a little tipsy and thinking about how cool crabs are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T14:16:08-07:00","id":1324045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1323820#post1323820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how conductivity has everything to do with what energy states electrons are in and how &quot;bound&quot; they are to a specific nucleus, it is a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that`s real world science, not in-game Supernal Truth. The way I see it, for a Matter spell conductivity doesn't really have anything to do with electrons. It's just a property of an object, and it can be changed like any other. To Matter, electrons and molecules don't really matter (pun not intended), Forces can deal with all that. Matter is about Tings, and the properties they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T14:58:24-07:00","id":1324050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324045#post1324045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that`s real world science, not in-game Supernal Truth. The way I see it, for a Matter spell conductivity doesn't really have anything to do with electrons. It's just a property of an object, and it can be changed like any other. To Matter, electrons and molecules don't really matter (pun not intended), Forces can deal with all that. Matter is about Tings, and the properties they have.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the properties have Fallen world preconditions.<br /> <br /> Fluidity can exist at room temperature, even if a particular object isn't a liquid at room temp without magic the concept still exists.<br /> <br /> Conductivity is <i>solely</i> a description of electron mobility, that's what conductivity <i>is</i> and thus that's what altering conductivity means. The electrons have to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T04:59:31-07:00","id":1324186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324050#post1324050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the properties have Fallen world preconditions.<br /> <br /> Fluidity can exist at room temperature, even if a particular object isn't a liquid at room temp without magic the concept still exists.<br /> <br /> Conductivity is <i>solely</i> a description of electron mobility, that's what conductivity <i>is</i> and thus that's what altering conductivity means. The electrons have to matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>When altering conductivity you apply one symbol that alters a material property of the subject. Now when examined through the perspective of Fallen science it will be what you say, a change in the force binding electrons to a nucleus (I think it might be more complicated than that, though, but whatever), but that doesn't mean Matter can change that force however it wants. Conductivity is symbolically a material property (despite fundamentally being dependent on a force) and Matter can change material properties. Matter <i>can't</i> change these forces however you want, only as a result of changing something that symbolically falls under Matter. If you want to change these forces directly, you go to Forces.<br /> <br /> That is the nature Supernal magic. Don't fall into the trap of thinking it needs to adhere to Fallen science in any way whatsoever. It's the result (and how it symbolically resonates with the Arcana and Practices) that matter. Anything else is just fudged by the magic to make it work regardless of how it breaks the laws of our reality, and it can be as inconsistent as is necessary for the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T11:34:21-07:00","id":1324236,"title":"","content":"That property of not affecting forces open up all kinds of interesting problemsolving opportunities to a Matter mage. Use State Change on hot water to make boiling ice, or apply it on a rock to create room temperature magma. If you use it to vaporize liquid nitrogen you can create an instant Extreme Cold environmental tilt.<br /> <br /> The Explosion spell looks good to go, provided a spark is independently supplied to trigger the materials. But since we are talking about Free Council style science shenanigans, I would like to suggest another approach that only requires two dots: dust explosions.<br /> <br /> Dust explosions are created by a high saturation of explosive solids (dust, sand, sugar, flour) in the air being set ablaze, provided air humidity is low. So lets leverage the practice of Ruling for this one. It drives out humidity and concentrates enough oxigen in the target area for a spark to cause [Potency] points of lethal damage. This means you still need to prime the explosion somehow, but it can lead to something akin to Roy Mustang's fire alchemy in FMA. It also means it causes temporary asphyxiation on anyone inside the area due to the oxygen being stolen for the effect, making this even more deadly in closed spaces.<br /> <br /> For every Size point of combustible powder inside the target area (or on the person for individual targeting), the explosion gains one more point of damage. By instead casting it with Matter 3, using a Reach and a mana, the damage becomes aggravated as you temporarily create &quot;perfected dust&quot;. At the lowest end of the spectrum you play as Roy Mustang, with proper preparations you wield the power of a thermobaric weapon.<br /> <br /> Is this too much for a two dot spell ? Surprisingly, it isn't. With the proper preparations, a master of Matter can lift an entire campus several feet into the air, then drop it, causing horrible damage as he safely floats away in a comfy flying sofa. That approach is overt and causes a lot of damage near the drop site.<br /> <br /> Dust explosions are very well documented, seeing ample use in the movie industry. So technically they are the safer, less overt, more predictable and probably the preferred method to deal with a large scale threat without causing tremendous damage to the Veil, even if it carries the additional complication of setting up a method to prime the explosion. Mages with proper time to prepare can be terrifying indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-13-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T22:29:49-07:00","id":1324356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324186#post1324186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When altering conductivity you apply one symbol that alters a material property of the subject. Now when examined through the perspective of Fallen science it will be what you say, a change in the force binding electrons to a nucleus (I think it might be more complicated than that, though, but whatever), but that doesn't mean Matter can change that force however it wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not mention forces, I mentioned electron energy states. While there are fundamental forces involved in the electron energy states I intentionally did not mention them, because the energy states are intrinsic to the concept of the &quot;matter&quot; being discussed, regardless of the forces involved.<br /> <br /> And yes, it <i>is</i> more &quot;more complicated than that,&quot; if you'd like to understand more and discuss it further, I recommend <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Introduction-Electrodynamics-David-J-Griffiths-dp-1108420419/dp/1108420419/ref=mt_hardcover?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=1563081177\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Introduction to Electrodynamics</i> by David Griffiths</a>; it has an easy to follow topic progression and Griffiths' wit is sharp and dry, making the read enjoyable, I would recommend brushing up on your line integrals and ordinary differential equations and have at least some familiarity with partial differential equations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conductivity is symbolically a material property (despite fundamentally being dependent on a force) and Matter can change material properties. Matter <i>can't</i> change these forces however you want, only as a result of changing something that symbolically falls under Matter. If you want to change these forces directly, you go to Forces. </div> </div> </div>Given the context in which I was replying, you seem to be implying a rejection of the idea that Matter can have control over chemical bonds and that only Forces can manipulate such bonds. Are you, in fact, asserting that Matter, the arcanum of alchemy and chemistry, cannot manipulate chemical bonds, breaking complex compounds down into their constituent components or forcing chemical bonds that otherwise would not occur in nature?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is the nature Supernal magic. Don't fall into the trap of thinking it needs to adhere to Fallen science in any way whatsoever. It's the result (and how it symbolically resonates with the Arcana and Practices) that matter. Anything else is just fudged by the magic to make it work regardless of how it breaks the laws of our reality, and it can be as inconsistent as is necessary for the results. </div> </div> </div>I did not &quot;fall into the trap,&quot; thanks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T22:50:21-07:00","id":1324359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324356#post1324356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the context in which I was replying, you seem to be implying a rejection of the idea that Matter can have control over chemical bonds and that only Forces can manipulate such bonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the context in which you were replying was &quot;the existence of a magic spell that changes a quality of a material object that can be observed with macroscopic senses necessarily implies that the category of magic that engages with material objects through a symbolic lens must be able to ignore the narrative-conceptual definitions of 'material' and 'force' because of a scientific fact that in practice has no more reason to be relevant to this form of magic than does <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato,_&amp;quot;the_way_up_and_the_way_down&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Heraclitus's statement that everything is fire</a>,&quot; no, I don't think that's Tessie's assertion at all.<br /> <br /> Conductivity is &quot;does this thing conduct this/these force/s?&quot; and in practical terms that is all that matters to its applicability to a spell that alters it. There's a symbolic difference between using Matter to make Matter explode and using Matter to make Matter into Matter that will explode under circumstances that you've arranged to be present, and we don't need to rehash <i>every argument on this subject from the last ten years</i> to make that any plainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T23:01:00-07:00","id":1324364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324359#post1324359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the context in which you were replying was &quot;the existence of a magic spell that changes a quality of a material object that can be observed with macroscopic senses necessarily implies that the category of magic that engages with material objects through a symbolic lens must be able to ignore the narrative-conceptual definitions of 'material' and 'force' because of a scientific fact that in practice has no more reason to be relevant to this form of magic than does <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus#Hodos_ano_kato,_&quot;the_way_up_and_the_way_down&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Heraclitus's statement that everything is fire</a>,&quot; no, I don't think that's Tessie's assertion at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Electrical conductivity cannot be observed with macroscopic senses. The consequence of something being a conductor can, under the right circumstances, be so observed, but the actual capacity for conduction is not something humans are capable of observing directly. Your premise is ill-founded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conductivity is &quot;does this thing conduct this/these force/s?&quot; and in practical terms that is all that matters to its applicability to a spell that alters it. </div> </div> </div>No, it is a lot more complicated than that, even if you wish to pretend otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a symbolic difference between using Matter to make Matter explode and using Matter to make Matter into Matter that will explode under circumstances that you've arranged to be present, and we don't need to rehash <i>every argument on this subject from the last ten years</i> to make that any plainer. </div> </div> </div>I never said there wasn't a difference between using matter to make matter explode and using matter to make matter into matter that will explode, you seem to be saying I said that. Don't put words into my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-14-2019, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T23:34:42-07:00","id":1324368,"title":"","content":"Mages don't fly by playing around the actual constants, they fly because the dream of flying is greater than reality. Trying to infer things based the logic of the real ignores that this is a game powered by the ideal over the real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T23:49:05-07:00","id":1324369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324368#post1324368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages don't fly by playing around the actual constants, they fly because the dream of flying is greater than reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty, but devoid of meaning.<br /> <br /> Mages absolutely fly by mucking around with physics. With Forces 2 they can alter the direction gravity points, soaring through the air. With Forces 3 and 4 more direct alteration of their velocity vector occurs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to infer things based the logic of the real ignores that this is a game powered by the ideal over the real. </div> </div> </div>Asking no questions and seeking no answers is boring. Which is more interesting:<br /> <br /> a) musing over why Forces 5 can create high energy Helium nuclei, but not low energy Helium nuclei.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> b) not asking the question and just saying it's because whoever wrote the descriptions didn't know what an alpha particle is.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather choose (a) and then ponder the cutoff between Forces and Matter <i>vis a vis</i> a Hydrogen atom as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T00:06:02-07:00","id":1324371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324369#post1324369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty, but devoid of meaning.<br /> <br /> Mages absolutely fly by mucking around with physics. With Forces 2 they can alter the direction gravity points, soaring through the air. With Forces 3 and 4 more direct alteration of their velocity vector occurs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Asking no questions and seeking no answers is boring. Which is more interesting:<br /> <br /> a) musing over why Forces 5 can create high energy Helium nuclei, but not low energy Helium nuclei.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> b) not asking the question and just saying it's because whoever wrote the descriptions didn't know what an alpha particle is.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather choose (a) and then ponder the cutoff between Forces and Matter <i>vis a vis</i> a Hydrogen atom as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) &quot;Pretty, but devoid of meaning&quot; in a game where open text once says &quot;In our field, poetry is our technical language.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages fly around by imposing the ideal as filtered through the Arcana upon reality. Mages <i>sidestep</i> physics. <i>Demons</i> fly around by fucking with physics.<br /> <br /> 2) Entertaining misapplied questions, providing wrong answers, and perpetuating them on to other people is an aggravation I've had to deal with the conseqeunces of way too much over my time here as a forumite and a professional. You'll excuse me if I nip this in the butt.<br /> <br /> You wanna ask questions and seek answers, I'm down for that, but when someone does the equivalent of trying to explain chaos theory fundamentals by discussing the history of Little Bunny Foo Foo, I'm gonna at least attempt a course correction. Physical logic isn't going answer a problem founded on ideal metaphysics.<br /> <br /> 3) Also, &quot;pretty, but devoid of meaning?&quot; You do remember who I am and how I do things, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-14-2019, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T00:18:24-07:00","id":1324375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324371#post1324371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) &quot;Pretty, but devoid of meaning&quot; in a game where open text once says &quot;In our field, poetry is our technical language.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Poetry has meaning, even if it's metaphoric rather than literal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages fly around by imposing the ideal as filtered through the Arcana upon reality. Mages <i>sidestep</i> physics. <i>Demons</i> fly around by fucking with physics. </div> </div> </div>Demons fly around by exploiting irrational nonsense that people think about physics by piggybacking on the God-Machine ([edit]or absolutely ludicrous thrust to weight ratios[/edit]).<br /> <br /> Mages clearly alter physics. They don't necessarily know that they're doing that, or what they're altering it to, but changing physical reality is altering physics <i>by definition</i>.<br /> <br /> I sometimes get the feeling that a lot of people on this forum have severe misapprehensions about what physics <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Entertaining misapplied questions, providing wrong answers, and perpetuating them on to other people is an aggravation I've had to deal with the conseqeunces of way too much over my time here as a forumite and a professional. You'll excuse me if I nip this in the butt. </div> </div> </div>My questions are not misapplied and my answers are not wrong just because you don't agree with them.<br /> <br /> And the idiom is &quot;nip this in the bud.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You wanna ask questions and seek answers, I'm down for that, but when someone does the equivalent of trying to explain chaos theory fundamentals by discussing the history of Little Bunny Foo Foo, I'm gonna at least attempt a course correction. Physical logic isn't going answer a problem founded on ideal metaphysics. </div> </div> </div>Physical logic still describes the consequence of altering the rules of physical logic. Dismissing observable consequence and genuine incongruity is &quot;Little Bunny Foo Foo.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Also, &quot;pretty, but devoid of meaning?&quot; You do remember who I am and how I do things, right? </div> </div> </div>I talked to you once, like, three years ago. I like some of the stuff you write on the forum, that does not mean I like everything you write on the forum. Don't try and turn this into some sort of personal attack on your character, because it's not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 07-14-2019, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T08:05:44-07:00","id":1324473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1324364#post1324364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said there wasn't a difference between using matter to make matter explode and using matter to make matter into matter that will explode, you seem to be saying I said that. Don't put words into my mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that actually. It was flippant and wasn't supposed to be taken literally, but it was taken literally.<br /> <br /> To return to the tracks of discourse we seem to be derailing from, I honestly feel like both arguments can be true. I can't remember where I read it, but somewhere it was implied that as humanity advanced in understanding of the world, more became possible with magic, other things became easier.<br /> <br /> Mages operate by imposing Supernal symbolism on the world to make their imaginations reality. However, I feel like that symbolism isn't so linear as to alienate the ideology of either side. A Diamond Obrimos magnifying the heat in the room is subverting the Lie and imposing Supernal truth upon the heat to intensify it. A Libertine Obrimos magnifying the heat in the room is subverting the Lie and imposing supernal truth upon the latent kinetic energy in the world and infusing that into particles to excite them, generating more heat.<br /> <br /> Both of them understand that they're overriding or warping the Lie to accomplish their goals, their methods simply differ based on their understanding and beliefs. Going back to the allegory of Plato's Cave, mages merely see the shadows on the wall, or semiotics, as filtered through the Lie. Each interpretation is different dependant on perspective, experience, and belief.<br /> <br /> One mage might feel something is impossible because they believe the realm of their arcana can't possibly encompass something that clearly belongs to another, while another mage might laugh and proclaim them mistaken, using specific knowledge, belief systems, or semiotics as a workaround. Neither is really wrong, magic is fueled by belief and understanding as much as it is by Truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T19:41:25-07:00","id":1324602,"title":"","content":"You have hold over Ascension mentality. Supernal Truth is not up for debate or a matter of perspective. Of course, some supernal truths seem hard to reconcile with one another, and those Mysteries obsesses many Mages. But the Truth that let's an Obrimos use it's mastery of Forces to warm up a room is the same, no matter their Sect, yantras or knowledge of Fallen science. The Truth that let's a Moros transform something in a way that creates an exothermic reaction in contact with the air is a very different Truth. And it has nothing to do with molecular bonds, energy states, or anything of the sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T04:08:54-07:00","id":1324688,"title":"","content":"Second edition (both the core book and Signs of Sorcery) has specified that different paths view the Arcana differently, but not quite in that way. It's particularly noticeable in Mage Sight wherein different Paths see wildly different things despite looking at the same symbols. It doesn't quite stretch as far as into the Arcana and Practices, though, and it has little to do with Orders and past experiences. Both the Thyrsus and the Obrimos will apply the Supernal symbols of perfecting heat to the already existing heat. The Yantra chosen to do this does carry its own symbolism, but not to those extremes. They also doesn't change how the spell works (Yantra that become parts of the spell, like runes or concentration, do change the spell but not in the same way) because they merely reinforce the symbols that allow the spell to take effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T12:28:06-07:00","id":1327038,"title":"","content":"<b>Mask of Janus (Time \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Investigation, Stealth, Subterfuge <br /> <br /> This disguises a target's appearance as that of a possible future self. They can simulate just about anything that is justifiable (if they have a health condition or practice an activity that could account for it) such as growing taller or shorter, changing their hairstyle, aging gracefully or decrepidly, burns, scars, greying hairs, dirt, wear and tear on their clothes, plastic surgery, etc. With Fate 2, any change that is possible can be simulated and the target's clothes can be altered to any they own and the caster knows about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-23-2019, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T16:48:02-07:00","id":1327088,"title":"","content":"Cool spell, but I\u2019d get rid of the disclaimer paragraph at the end. I\u2019d also allow faking surgical produced features because that is a potential future. I\u2019d get rid of the bit about Fate changing clothing, that\u2019s more a Matter thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T17:01:49-07:00","id":1327090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1327088#post1327088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool spell, but I\u2019d get rid of the disclaimer paragraph at the end. I\u2019d also allow faking surgical produced features because that is a potential future. I\u2019d get rid of the bit about Fate changing clothing, that\u2019s more a Matter thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not sure how good a surgeon would be fair game, since I was worried it was getting into Mutable Mask's territory. For clothes, I restricted it to the ones they have so it did not overlap with a Veiling of Matter, while still remaining within the possibilities of what they could use in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-23-2019, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T08:49:35-07:00","id":1328956,"title":"","content":"<b>The Truth Is Out There (Fate \u2022\u2022, Time \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Persuasion, Occult, Subterfuge <br /> <br /> This convinces a target that a future the caster selected will come to pass. It creates fake omens, &quot;evidence&quot;, dreams and the occassional daydream about it, making the target believe its an absolute certainty, every small clue further reinforcing it. <br /> <br /> Whenever the target or anyone else attempts to divine about it, the results conform to the fake future, any attempts to pierce the illusion causes a Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> With conjunctional Mind 2, it can be used to make the target &quot;discover&quot; about and/or believe any conspiracy (real or otherwise) the caster chooses, associating it with the fake future.<br /> <br /> This spell was famously invented by a Kingmaker called Scully, who used it to Awaken a Sleepwalker investigator by secretly guiding him on a hunt for Exarch cults and agents of the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target becomes exceptionally capable in regards to the fake future, further reinforcing they idea that they are a key linchpin in its creation. This grants them the Vision merit at a rate of [Potency], useable only when working towards an outcome selected by the caster (making sure it comes to pass, preventing it, etc). Furthermore, the omens change to direct them towards believing it is the best possible resolution. For another Reach and a mana, the merit can exceed the cap of 5 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-02-2019, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T17:27:29-07:00","id":1330325,"title":"","content":"<b>Mana Stitches (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>: 1 Mana<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Medicine, Science <br /> <br /> The mage creates threads of mana to stitch together wounds, then sends a pulse of it to invigorate the target's pattern, causing them to agglutinate and stabilizing them.<br /> <br /> It can also be used to reattach severed limbs, but only if they have not started to rot and if they originally belonged to the target, otherwise they risk transplant rejection. <br /> <br /> While it is a less efficient type of healing, this spell has saved countless lives in situations where a Life mage is not available.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The effect is Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-14-2019, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T20:59:10-07:00","id":1330344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330325#post1330325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mana Stitches (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b>: 1 Mana<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Pattering<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Crafts, Medicine, Science <br /> <br /> The mage creates threads of mana to stitch together wounds, then sends a pulse of it to invigorate the target's pattern, causing them to agglutinate and heal [Potency] points of lethal damage. <br /> <br /> It can be used to reattach severed limbs, but only if they have not started to rot and if they originally belonged to the target, otherwise they risk transplant rejection. <br /> <br /> The target should not over exert for about a week after being healed by this spell or risk the stitches opening. <br /> <br /> While it is a less efficient type of healing, this spell has saved countless lives in situations where a Life mage is not available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you\u2019d be better off with a version that enables Pattern Restoration in a similar way to Death being able to do Pattern Scouring. Mana by itself isn\u2019t really a panacea of any kind. Otherwise this is basically Platonic Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T07:59:04-07:00","id":1330382,"title":"","content":"I considered it, but I imagined it would need Life 3 and Prime 3. I was trying to come up with a type of emergency healing that could be done using the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos, beyond the obvious cauterization with fire. So a variation of Platonic Form seemed like the way to go.<br /> <br /> Mana is not seen as a panacea in this case, this is more of a quick and dirty solution for when mana is running low and a proper Life mage is not accessible. So you stich the wounds together haphazardly, it solves the issue for the moment and gets the target back on their feet. Its not as good as Life magic and will definitely leave a scar, but in a desperate situation, a solution that is good enough is better than nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T10:23:12-07:00","id":1330402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330382#post1330382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered it, but I imagined it would need Life 3 and Prime 3. I was trying to come up with a type of emergency healing that could be done using the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos, beyond the obvious cauterization with fire. So a variation of Platonic Form seemed like the way to go.<br /> <br /> Mana is not seen as a panacea in this case, this is more of a quick and dirty solution for when mana is running low and a proper Life mage is not accessible. So you stich the wounds together haphazardly, it solves the issue for the moment and gets the target back on their feet. Its not as good as Life magic and will definitely leave a scar, but in a desperate situation, a solution that is good enough is better than nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 3 can just do it by itself, Prime controls mana, and one of the ways Mages use Mana is to perform Pattern Restoration. A Weaving spell can impute that onto a subject in the same way that Death imputes the ability to Pattern Scour onto a subject from which the Mage can benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T10:23:12-07:00","id":1330403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330382#post1330382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered it, but I imagined it would need Life 3 and Prime 3. I was trying to come up with a type of emergency healing that could be done using the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos, beyond the obvious cauterization with fire. So a variation of Platonic Form seemed like the way to go.<br /> <br /> Mana is not seen as a panacea in this case, this is more of a quick and dirty solution for when mana is running low and a proper Life mage is not accessible. So you stich the wounds together haphazardly, it solves the issue for the moment and gets the target back on their feet. Its not as good as Life magic and will definitely leave a scar, but in a desperate situation, a solution that is good enough is better than nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 3 can just do it by itself, Prime controls mana, and one of the ways Mages use Mana is to perform Pattern Restoration. A Weaving spell can impute that onto a subject in the same way that Death imputes the ability to Pattern Scour onto a subject from which the Mage can benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T15:33:18-07:00","id":1330458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330382#post1330382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered it, but I imagined it would need Life 3 and Prime 3. I was trying to come up with a type of emergency healing that could be done using the Ruling Arcana of the Obrimos, beyond the obvious cauterization with fire. So a variation of Platonic Form seemed like the way to go.<br /> <br /> Mana is not seen as a panacea in this case, this is more of a quick and dirty solution for when mana is running low and a proper Life mage is not accessible. So you stich the wounds together haphazardly, it solves the issue for the moment and gets the target back on their feet. Its not as good as Life magic and will definitely leave a scar, but in a desperate situation, a solution that is good enough is better than nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that effect I would make it similar to Veil of Moments, in that it stops bleeding and stabilizes someone with their health track full of lethal damage, but doesn't really heal them. Maybe Weaving would be enough for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T21:25:17-07:00","id":1330694,"title":"","content":"How the deuce do you justify Prime doing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T22:21:38-07:00","id":1330701,"title":"","content":"Maybe because in 1e, tass was inert. I seem to remember a dog turned to tass looking like a statue of a dog. Which might be slightly reminiscent of temporal stasis. Just spit balling...<br /> <br /> The only way I would allow prime to restore limbs is with making. A variant on 'eidolon'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T01:31:26-07:00","id":1330716,"title":"","content":"If i am understanding it right prime 4 can impart mages template trait on others, like the spell Apocalypse granting mage sight, so it would be possible to give also pattern restoration if the mage pays the mana cost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T05:03:17-07:00","id":1330728,"title":"","content":"Pattern restoration can't restore limbs though. I would allow prime weaving to do pattern restoration on others, yes. But the effect proposed is almost as potent as what life can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T08:13:29-07:00","id":1330748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MovingMind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330728#post1330728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern restoration can't restore limbs though. I would allow prime weaving to do pattern restoration on others, yes. But the effect proposed is almost as potent as what life can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lost limbs are physical tilts turned permanent by aggravated damage, direct or upgraded, (see hurt locker) and pattern restoration CAN remove physical tilts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:20:39-07:00","id":1330759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330748#post1330748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost limbs are physical tilts turned permanent by aggravated damage, direct or upgraded, (see hurt locker) and pattern restoration CAN remove physical tilts</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent Tilts are actually persistent Conditions. Tilts resulting from injuries disappear once those injuries are healed. If healing an injury wouldn't remove a Tilt, it's actually a Condition with the effects of a Tilt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:27:21-07:00","id":1330763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330748#post1330748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lost limbs are physical tilts turned permanent by aggravated damage, direct or upgraded, (see hurt locker) and pattern restoration CAN remove physical tilts</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I looked it up; and you're right<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ending the Tilt: If the Tilt is inflicted as a result of an attack, <br /> mark an \u2018x\u2019 under the leftmost Health box inflicted in that attack;<br /> the Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed.<br /> If aggravated damage inflicts this Tilt, the character loses the use<br /> of his arm (or straight up loses his arm) permanently. </div> </div> </div>In that case then I would base it on Knit (Life 3), with lethal healing and removing tilts as Reach options. And I would also make Regeneration work this way... as it is, temporary regeneration is kind of useless, and Prime becomes the go-to healing arcanum. <br /> <br /> Maybe limit the Prime version so that the aggravated damage which inflicted the tilt must still be present (your pattern has not yet settled in the new broken shape), which is why you can use pattern restoration to fix it. As a side effect the Aggravated damage is upgraded to resistant damage (to represent the natural healing bit). Life Regeneration would not have that limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:34:01-07:00","id":1330766,"title":"","content":"This is the important part: &quot;<i>If aggravated damage inflicts this Tilt, the character loses the use</i><br /> <i>of his arm (or straight up loses his arm) permanently.</i>&quot;<br /> You can Pattern Restore away this Tilt, but it doesn't remove the effects that lingers after the Tilt is gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T09:54:23-07:00","id":1330771,"title":"","content":"But... that is not removing the Tilt at all. I honestly don't think Pattern Restoration should remove Persistent Conditions and Tilts, but the rules seems to allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T10:55:54-07:00","id":1330779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330771#post1330771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... that is not removing the Tilt at all. I honestly don't think Pattern Restoration should remove Persistent Conditions and Tilts, but the rules seems to allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The effect lingers whether you're removing the Tilt supernaturally or heal it naturally, because that effect is not quite part of the Tilt. It's a consequence of having taken enough aggravated damage to cause the Tilt in the first place.<br /> If you don't think that is removing the Tilt, then healing it naturally wouldn't remove the Tilt either, despite this: &quot;[..]<i>the Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Once the Tilt is removed you should gain a Persistent Condition that probably imposes the effects of the Tilt in combat, and since it's a physical Condition it can't be Pattern Restored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T17:01:22-07:00","id":1330860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330779#post1330779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The effect lingers whether you're removing the Tilt supernaturally or heal it naturally, because that effect is not quite part of the Tilt. It's a consequence of having taken enough aggravated damage to cause the Tilt in the first place.<br /> If you don't think that is removing the Tilt, then healing it naturally wouldn't remove the Tilt either, despite this: &amp;quot;[..]<i>the Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed.</i>&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Once the Tilt is removed you should gain a Persistent Condition that probably imposes the effects of the Tilt in combat, and since it's a physical Condition it can't be Pattern Restored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re reading hurt locker i think you are right, pattern restoration cannot heal aggravated damage and regenerating lost limbs require the damage to be healed.<br /> So pattern restoration can only heal damaged (lethals) limbs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-14T06:54:48-07:00","id":1330922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1330458#post1330458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that effect I would make it similar to Veil of Moments, in that it stops bleeding and stabilizes someone with their health track full of lethal damage, but doesn't really heal them. Maybe Weaving would be enough for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stabilizing them is actually a lot closer to what I was going for, I altered the spell to reflect that, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":