not how Dooms work.<br /> <br /> A Doom is a form of dramatic change to be reached, which affects the benefits the bearer of the Merit derives from using Willpower to avoid or advance toward that state \u2014 &quot;you lose the Merit&quot; is nowhere near the likes of &quot;[your] life as [you] know it [is brought] to a tragic end.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Destiny that can change bearers is likewise out of the scope of Traveler-scale magic to grant, being the textbook definition of a Dynamics spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T19:45:03-08:00","id":1474103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1474100#post1474100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also not how Dooms work.<br /> <br /> A Doom is a form of dramatic change to be reached, which affects the benefits the bearer of the Merit derives from using Willpower to avoid or advance toward that state \u2014 &quot;you lose the Merit&quot; is nowhere near the likes of &quot;[your] life as [you] know it [is brought] to a tragic end.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Destiny that can change bearers is likewise out of the scope of Traveler-scale magic to grant, being the textbook definition of a Dynamics spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further modifications have been edited in","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T10:00:26-08:00","id":1474206,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Claim Cloister (Prime \u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Shielding </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Politics, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A cabal's Demesne is where they are at their strongest, allowing them to prepare and experiment extensively, unhindered by the Lie. The easiest way to combat them is with a well warded Sleeper shock troop, but this is normally loud and messy. A cabal going in unaware risks a very deadly encounter. In order to provide a more tactically sound approach, the Arrow have devised this as a way to usurp control of these magical bunkers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When cast upon all the soul stones creating a Demesne or within the entire area they are in, it completely suppresses its benefits for the duration. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Whenever facing highly defended Sanctums, this spell is usually utilized as part of the opening salvo. While the mages inside deal with containing spells that suddenly risk Paradox and summons being corroded by Fallen exposure, the edge of the battle can be seized.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach or conjunctional Fate 2:</b> The caster is allowed to specify the conditions necessary to access the Demesne's benefits. The caster may specify up [Potency] conditions necessary to receive the benefit, as well as whether some or all need to be fulfilled in order to qualify. Possible conditions include being of a certain Path, specific Nimbus signatures, Legacies, Shadow Name, yantra type or theme (including Cabal Theme) .</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seers are fond of setting specific yantras as </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keys, using this to tempt invading Pentacle mages to use their patron's symbols. A few others prefer to use it as a political statement, forcing visiting Pylons to pay homage to their Exarchs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There have even been cabals that use temporal pockets alongside this spell to create, on the fly, Demesnes only they can use, rapidly overwhelming the opposition.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-19-2022, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T12:00:44-08:00","id":1474215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1474206#post1474206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Claim Cloister (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Weaving </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Politics, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A cabal's Demesne is where they are at their strongest, allowing them to prepare and experiment extensively, unhindered by the Lie. The easiest way to combat them is with a well warded Sleeper shock troop, but this is normally loud and messy. A cabal going in unaware risks a very deadly encounter. In order to provide a more tactically sound approach, the Arrow have devised this as a way to usurp control of these magical bunkers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When cast upon all the soul stones creating a Demesne or within the entire area they are in, it allows them to specify the conditions necessary to access its benefits. The caster may specify up [Potency] conditions necessary to receive the benefit, as well as whether some or all need to be fulfilled in order to qualify. Possible conditions include being of a certain Path, specific Nimbus signatures, Legacies, Shadow Name, yantra type or theme (including Cabal Theme) .</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Seers are fond of setting specific yantras as </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keys, using this to tempt invading Pentacle mages to use their patron's symbols. A few others prefer to use it as a political statement, forcing visiting Pylons to pay homage to their Exarchs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever facing highly defended Sanctums, this spell is usually utilized as part of the opening salvo. While the mages inside deal with containing spells that suddenly risk Paradox and summons being corroded by Fallen exposure, the edge of the battle can be seized.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There have even been cabals that use temporal pockets alongside this spell to create, on the fly, Demesnes only they can use, rapidly overwhelming the opposition.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Well this is nice! I have one issue, that being that I\u2019m pretty sure this is Shielding with a reach to allow keys. The idea being that you first put a barrier between the Demesne and the Fallen, and then complicate the spell by letting certain conditions through the ward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T12:15:58-08:00","id":1474218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1474215#post1474215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well this is nice! I have one issue, that being that I\u2019m pretty sure this is Shielding with a reach to allow keys. The idea being that you first put a barrier between the Demesne and the Fallen, and then complicate the spell by letting certain conditions through the ward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, that makes it have even more free Reach. I have edited the changes in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T11:03:10-08:00","id":1474305,"title":"","content":"<b>Prince to Pauper (Fate 3)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Larceny, Politics, Socialize<br /> <br /> So often destiny is determined by one's standing in the world, stemming from choices in which one has no say, subject to forces beyond any individual's control. By means of this spell, a Disciple of Fate can engage in a bout of coercive redistribution, transferring power from those born into wealth and privilege to the more unfortunate and needy. Alternatively, an avid mage might cast this spell to undermine another's hard work, stealing all the glory at the last moment.<br /> <br /> This spell transfers dots in a Social Merit from one subject to another, up to a number of dots equal to the spell's Potency. Without increasing the Subjects Factor, the caster must be on one end or the other of the transfer. Merits transferred must be those connected to an external source, such as Allies, Status, or Resources. For the duration, the donor loses access to the transferred Merit dots, while the recipient gains such. Merits with scaling dot ratings may be split up, but those with fixed ratings cannot.<br /> <br /> If cast on more than two subjects, the mage chooses one to be the donor, and determines which of the other recipients gains how much of the transferred Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can transfer multiple Merits from one subject to the other, with a total dot rating not exceeding Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can swap Merits between both subjects, trading Allies for Resources, for instance, with a total dot rating not exceeding Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space 2:</b> Any Sympathetic connections associated with the Merit are transferred as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kingmaker (Fate 4)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Computer, Politics, Streetwise<br /> <br /> With a wave of the magic wand, an Adept of Fate can grant your every wish. Make sure it's what you really want, though. The subject of this spell gains up to Potency dots in a Social Merit of the mage's choosing for the spell's duration. This must be a Merit connected to an external source, and at Storyteller discretion, can include Merits that while not technically Social in scope are still externalized in some way, such as Soul Stone or Library, although the spell cannot grant a unique, specific example of such (the soul stone of a particular mage, for instance). Fate conspires to bring the bounty to the subject as expediently as possible.<br /> <br /> Caveat emptor: Although this spell can grant a subject great power and prestige in the Fallen World, it does not confer any ability to use such power effectively. One might become the CEO of a corporation without a lick of knowledge of finance or business politics, which could spell ruin in the long run. Such lead-crowned monarchs rely heavily on delegation and can often be sussed out by the ring of advisors, viziers, and lackeys with which they surround themselves to keep their holding running smoothly. Furthermore, attempting to hijack the upper echelons of Sleeper governance is difficult, and generally ill-advised; our world's presidents, queens, popes, emperors, and firsts among equals are watched very carefully from myriad shadowed corners. On more than one occasion the unwise casting of this spell has led to the manifestation of an Ananke or worse, an Exarchal Ochema, to set things back to the way they were.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell may grant a number of different Merits with a total dot rating no greater than Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space 2:</b> The subject also gains any Sympathetic connections the Merit would entail.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Time 2:</b> The caster can dictate how exactly the subject gains access to the Merit. With Temporal Sympathy, the mage can grant a Merit retroactively through events in the subject's past (though having no effect until the present moment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":".  I am an undiligent Communist, getting my terminology mixed up like that, mixed up like an incredibly strange creature who stopped living and learned how to love pi\u00f1a coladas. 02-09-2022, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T00:16:54-08:00","id":1474551,"title":"","content":"Five spells attempting to connect Mage with the core's subsystems. In this case, Building Equipment.<br /> <br /> Two of these spells have been already posted, at here and at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded?p=1464237#post1464237\">Chronologues Legacy fan-made 2E expansion writeup</a>, but I'm reposting them for completion's sake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spell: Master Tinkerer (Matter </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Ruling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Crafts, Expression, Survival</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Sometimes, what an alchemist really needs is a way to get things done normally, albeit with a subtle boost. For its Duration, this spell augments the caster's Build Equipment action (including repairs, etc) when building a Physical Object</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"> as per the Building Equipment system (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">, etc), such that any Built-In Penalties are negated by Potency. Scale is used to determine the number and the size or volume of Physical Objects the caster may craft or tinker with.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: Potency may be directly added to the Physical Object's equipment bonus, beyond negating penalties. With <b>1 Mana</b>, said bonus may exceed +5.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Add Death </b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The subject may tamper with a Physical Object such that it gains the Fragile or Volatile tag. Alternatively, he may prematurely trigger them such that a Fragile item immediately breaks down, or the Volatile item immediately blows up and gains a -2 reduction.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spell: Exquisite Repository (Forces </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Weaving</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Computer, Academics, Expression</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">A thaumaturge hears history in the winds, and writes codices into digital signals. This spell collects and compiles information memorized by or accessible-at-the-moment to the caster into a medium broadly falling under Forces' purview (a computer, a bonfire, a neon sign, a wind chime, etc), instantly building a Repository as per the Building Equipment system (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">, etc). It has a +(Potency) equipment bonus, and breaks down after Duration expires. Built-In Penalties do not apply, and the Fragile and Volatile tags are ignored unless the mage includes them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: Anyone accessing the Repository benefits from a variant of the Eidetic Memory Merit (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">), gaining a +2 bonus to recall minute pieces of information from the Repository, and a perfect memory over experiences of applying the Repository's information. Once the spell expires, the former effect ceases immediately, and the latter effect gives way to normal degradations of memory.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Add Prime </b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The caster may draw Resonance from a ley line or Node and compile it into the Repository. Users' perceptions are thus colored by the Resonance; a cooking recipe Resonant with 'Murder' may feel like a cannibal's poetic memoir, and a case file detailing brutal tortures may feel oddly refreshing when made Resonant with 'Serenity.'</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spell: Expert Planner (Time </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Perfecting</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Academics, Investigation, Science</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Even without directly manipulating time, an enchanter is never caught without a working plan. This spell projects the caster's thoughts into the future, instantly building a Plan as per the Building Equipment system (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">, etc). It has a +(Potency) equipment bonus, and breaks down after Duration expires. Built-In Penalties do not apply, and the Fragile and Volatile tags are ignored unless the mage includes them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: A number of (Scale; Subject) actors benefit from the Good Time Management Merit (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">), halving the interval for extended actions. Without increased Scale, the caster herself benefits.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Add Fate </b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022\u2022</b>: When adding the Fragile or Volatile tags to the Plan, the mage may designate them to affect only certain users. The designation may be as broad as &quot;anyone other than myself,&quot; or as narrow as &quot;the last person to hack into my account.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spell: Uncanny Organizer (Space </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Patterning</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Persuasion, Politics, Socialize</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">A deft warlock can always find people willing to lend a hand. This spell convinces people within Scale that the mage is a likable person in need of help, </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">instantly building an Organization as per the Building Equipment system (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">, etc). It has a +(Potency) equipment bonus, and breaks down after Duration expires. Built-In Penalties do not apply, and the Fragile and Volatile tags are ignored unless the mage includes them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>+1 Reach and 1 Mana</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The Organization doubles as the Staff Merit (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">). Divide Potency between the Organization's equipment bonus and dots in Staff; for each of the latter, the Organization has one Skill on which it grants 1 automatic success on non-contested rolls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Add Mind </b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The helpers are confused into perceiving the mage and each other as casual acquaintances. Magic smoothes over fine details and memories both during and after the act, until an outsider calls out the oddities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spell: Theriaca Magica (Life </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2022</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Practice</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Patterning</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Primary Factor</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Suggested Rote Skills</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Occult, Science, Survival</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">An ecstatic can release the potential of an animal body's magic into the Fallen World. This spell converts an animal body part freshly separated for no longer than a few minutes into a minor magical item, instantly building a Mystical Equipment as per the Build</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">ing Equipment system (</span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Chronicles of Darkness</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">, etc). </span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">It has a +(Potency) equipment bonus, and breaks down after Duration expires. Built-In Penalties do not apply, and the Fragile and Volatile tags are ignored unless the mage includes them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">Mystical Equipment conjured by this spell must have a symbolic link between its material and its function; a bezoar stone could offer a +1 to resist poisons and diseases, a fox's tail could offer a +2 to Social rolls to sexually seduce someone, and so on. Mystical Equipment may have non-dice effects, such as a turtle's shell helping resist infirmity, but ideally they should not approximate actual supernatural powers (especially Enhanced Items, Imbued Items, etc).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>+1 Reach</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The caster may enchant a body part while it is still on the animal's living body. Depending on the effect, anyone in the animal's vicinity could benefit from the dice bonus, or they might have to interact with the animal in some way to do so. Alternatively, the caster can draw symbolic power from the entire animal itself; a white-furred dog could help banishing ghosts, a black cat aids sabotage and slipping of poisons, and so on.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Add Spirit </b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>\u2022</b></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">: The Mystical Equipment becomes a channel for spiritual powers. Any spirit can benefit from its dice bonus when using Influences, Manifestations, and Numina. It also offers a +1 tool Yantra to any Spirit spells that target it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Links 02-13-2022, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T09:33:11-08:00","id":1474630,"title":"","content":"<b>Bestow Attainment (Prime 4)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> One Mana<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Occult, Persuasion, Socialize<br /> <br /> The student sometimes requires a taste of enlightenment to continue down a path of tribulation. The subject of this spell, who must be a mage, gains access to one of the caster's chosen Arcanum Attainments for the duration. The subject pays all costs associated with activating the Attainment, and uses their actual Arcanum rating for calculating dice pools and effects. This spell cannot bestow Legacy Attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject uses the caster's Arcanum rating at time of casting for calculating dice pools and effects.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> If the Create Rote Attainment is bestowed, any rotes the subject makes from it will register as having been created by the caster rather than the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T13:55:53-08:00","id":1474759,"title":"","content":"<b>Outlaw Brand (Fate 3)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Intimidate, Subterfuge, Weaponry<br /> <br /> Sometimes in the course of your willworking, you just have to knock do-gooders down a peg. When this spell is cast, the mage chooses one promise the subject has made or law to which he his subject (such as by dint of citizenship in a certain country); for the spell's duration the subject is treated as though he had broken the stipulated promise or law. This does not fabricate evidence of crimes, but supernatural effects and bureaucratic systems will treat him properly, which may impose Conditions such as Notoriety or Hunted. This spell works on supernaturally sealed promises, such as those upheld by the Sworn Oaths spell or changeling pledgecraft, and for the duration the subject suffers the drawbacks for transgression, such as any hexes or Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> The spell's effects are Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Mind 2:</b> The spell can dispel the effects of a fae Contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T11:59:27-08:00","id":1474815,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inverse Causality (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Computers, Science</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The linear progression of events is one of the most basic ways we experience the flow of time in the Fallen World. However, sometimes even causality must yield to the needs of the moment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell allows the subject to invert the relationship between cause and effect, allowing results to occur immediately for actions that have yet to happen. Within its duration, it allows the subject to reflexively perform up to [Potency] actions in addition to the current one, each being taken from a turn in the future. However, this locks them into performing the motions for the action in the next immediate turns. Should the spell's duration run out before they can perform the cause of an action, the effect is undone, a fact which Banishers leverage to break the will of their captives.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An enemy could be hit by a gunshot suddenly materializing, but the subject would need to fire the gun in the next turn. Similarly, they could cast a spell that takes up to [Potency] turns to prepare, paying all costs beforehand, then run away the next few turns as they focus on the yantras for that spell. Some even use it to open locks that would require multiple people to act simultaneously. However, this spell does not affect extended actions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Display Thoughts (Mind \u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Unveiling </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Empathy, Expression</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> Sometimes a picture can be worth more than a thousand words. Whether providing explanations about a complex subject, retelling a riveting tale or concisely presenting a plan of action, a mage well versed in the Mind Arcanum can easily build visualizations of their ideas.<br /> <br /> This allows the caster to project a hologram of their thoughts to the subject, allowing them to recall and neatly organize the data being projected. While it is clearly an illusion, the audio and visual aid can be a powerful method to convey one's vision. This allows them to add [Potency] to any social rolls regarding what is being shown.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Arrow strategists use it to show elaborate battle plans, with troop movement, terrain and contingencies clearly laid out. Mysterium and Libertine researchers employ it to show visuals of uncovered ruins, inscriptions, tablets, Artifacts, tests or the result of their expeditions. Th\u00e9archs utilize it alongside computer yantras to improvise stunning &quot;slides presentations&quot; for their Cryptopolies and Guardians use it to drive home the danger of certain secrets. Seers of the Chancellor are especially fond of this rote, using it to show people's dreams come true and tempt them into signing terrible bargains.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With conjunctional Prime 2, the illusions look realistic.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-16-2022, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T09:39:58-08:00","id":1475539,"title":"","content":"<b>Briar Invasion (Fate 4 + Mind 2)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> One Mana<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> Sometimes the best way to protect one's keep is to entangle it in a copse of thorns. This spell, which must be cast using the Area factor, causes its targeted location to be treated as part of the Hedge, allowing those with Glamour or magic to shape the surroundings through their actions. The mage chooses when casting whether the area is considered a trod, the Thorns, or regular Hedge. This enchantment brings with it the more insidious aspects of those border marches as well, such as penalties to Acts of Hubris and, most importantly, self-shaping. Landscapes warp in reflection of the thoughts of those within, trapping the fearful, tempting the greedy, abjuring the weak. Any changes wrought from Hedgespinning fade when the spell's duration ends.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage may designate a theme for the area, such as &quot;moonlit desert&quot; or &quot;information wants to be free.&quot; Whenever the pseudo-Hedge shifts itself reactively, it always does so in alignment with the specified theme. Active Hedgespinning rolls that align with the theme gain bonus dice equal to the spell's Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space 4:</b> Moving through the location also uses the rules for Hedge navigation. If the area is designated a trod, with the use of the Sympathetic Casting Attainment, the mage can also connect the area to another specified location. With an additional Reach, the mage treats their Gnosis as an equivalent Wyrd rating when navigating through the space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T00:49:31-08:00","id":1475721,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parachronistic Artifice (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Patterning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>Composure</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 mana</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Stealth, Subterfuge </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perhaps one of the oldest unsolved Mysteries is the Count of Saint Germaine. This legendary occultist has been spotted in multiple European courts and Concilia across the ages, wearing different faces, Nimbus and following different Paths, yet always having a consistent array of lost knowledge, memories and resources no one else should have possessed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A few whisper they are mobile carriers of a lost Mysterium Athaneum, waiting for someone to pay the right price for their knowledge. Some say that they are the apprentices of a Guardian Exemplar, creating a Nameless Order that creates Labyrinths for the Threshold Seeking itself. Whatever the truth may be, it is this rote that has allowed multiple mages to assume the role throughout the ages, composing Germaine's current incarnation from a vault of plundered and bartered histories.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell binds a part of the subject's history to a target item, transferring it entirely to whoever wears it. The caster is able to transfer up to [Potency] dots of skills, merits or parts of the target's life (their family life, career, relationship, criminal past, etc) into the item. Whoever wears the item receives that part of the subject's life. A user can only acquire merits that are compatible with their template.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Without additional scale factors, the caster's history is transferred by default. The user acquires all the knowledge, experience, status (or infamy) and physical components associated with the history. A user that takes the knowledge of a master swordfighter might find themselves plagued by occasional pain from a knee injury and taking the Status of a company president might mean potential kidnappers now focus on them. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When the item is not being worn, that history is effectively phased out of the timeline. Depending on the caster's choice, either other people would have performed the actions or they never having happened at all. Memories of the stored time grow hazy and distant to all involved. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes Saint Germaine has used this rote to claim membership in different Orders. In a few cases, they have joined cabals and helped them build their reputation, only to store their historical contributions to their Sanctum in a trinket, making the cabal unknowingly defend the temporaly rewritten site. A few times they have plundered the resources of entire cabals, gaining access to libraries, imbued items and Sanctums that they can call upon on the fly. Indeed some theorize certain stores, office complexes and apartments buildings could be potential highly defended troves of lost knowledge, waiting to be activated by a bauble from Saint Germaine's collection. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some even say they have amassed histories dating back hundreds of years, passing on a cornucopia of life pieces from one generation to the next, perhaps explaining the extensive yet often confusing results of investigating the Count with Time magic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With conjunctional Mind 1, the user also receives the emotional context of the history.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The caster takes the history violently from the subject, leaving such a powerful gap in their chronology that it inflicts the Amnesia condition regarding the stolen history.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reserve of Will (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> N/A</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Subterfuge </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A focused mind can make the supernatural yield more easily before a mage, therefore having greater stores available will be able to accomplish greater feats. This spell allows an item to hold Willpower, allowing mages to resist supernatural effect longer or focus their will more often into difficult spells.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The item can hold up to [Potency] points of Willpower and a user can replenish from its stores by touching it. Alternatively, they can expend Willpower points from its reserve while touching it. Refilling its stores requires a Weaving of Mind. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fortress of the Mind (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Making</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Craft, Occult</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A persistent problem of being a member of the Mysterium is that there will always be someone who tries to bypass the cost of knowledge. Some prefer to steal it from the mage's Oneiros, others to convince their subconscious, but the end result is theft all the same. This rote was made to shore up the mental defenses of knowledge keepers, creating a dedicated mental defense processing center for the brain.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It reconfigures the mind to secure it from intruders, making it more difficult to breach, grants [Potency] in the Mental Fortification merit, up to trait limits. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This merit makes any travel into or outside the Oneiros without the owner's permission suffer a [Potency] penalty to the rolls. In addition, the mindscape facilitates the action of the owner and anyone they recognize as an ally, adding a bonus of [Potency] to initiative. Lastly, the caster can set up traps within the Oneiros, dealing up to [Potency] bashing or lethal dream health damage when triggered, distributed amongsts a given number of traps. With Potency 3, for example, a single trap worth 3 lethal can be placed or one inflicting 2 and one 1 lethal or 3 traps inflicting 1 lethal. Intruders avoid them with Power + Finesse, penalized by Mental Fortification dots.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach and a mana: </b>The merit can go beyond trait limits.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach and a mana: </b>The damage done is aggravated.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-03-2022, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T10:28:51-08:00","id":1475844,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scrolls of Djhuty (Fate \u2022</span></span></b></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span></b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Making</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Occult, Expression</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernal magic is wondrous and incredibly adaptable, however, only a foolish mage would dismiss it as the only type of willworking. Occultists and religious figures have developed rituals to harness the inherent supernatural powers of existence, refining them over the course of millennia into a form accessible to anyone. Some of the most potent ones leverage the symbolism of death to create powerful effects. This spell was created to furnish a mage with knowledge of these practices without spending extensive amounts of time learning them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This grants a target [Potency] dots of Ceremonies for the duration. Trespassing cabals that were confident in their dispellers were turned away as the Black Cat's Crossing sapped the will of those uninvited to the Sanctum. The Lover's Telephone allows for reliable communication even in areas where sympathetic magic is warded and Death Watch has proven invaluable in keeping injured cabalmates alive until a healer can be found.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-09-2022, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T11:59:29-08:00","id":1475848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475844#post1475844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scrolls of Djhuty (Death/Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Occult, Expression</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Supernal magic is wondrous and incredibly adaptable, however, only a foolish mage would dismiss it as the only type of willworking. Occultists and religious figures have developed rituals to harness the inherent supernatural powers of existence, refining them over the course of millennia into a form accessible to anyone. Some of the most potent ones leverage the energies of death to create powerful effects. This spell was created to furnish a mage with knowledge of these practices without spending extensive amounts of time learning them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This grants a target [Potency] dots of Ceremonies for the duration. Trespassing cabals that were confident in their dispellers were turned away as the Black Cat's Crossing sapped the will of those uninvited to the Sanctum. The Lover's Telephone allows for reliable communication even in areas where sympathetic magic is warded and Death Watch has proven invaluable in keeping injured cabalmates alive until a healer can be found.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When cast with Mind 4, the Ceremonies can be modified to work on goetia. They can also be adapted to better fit the Astral's nature. The Diviner's Jawbone can be modified to create worry dolls that bestow the Dream merit and Persephone's Return can be reworked to create Synesnes. One of the most unusual ones summons the conductor of the Midnight Train, allowing one to barter for a ticket.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With conjunctional Spirit 4, the Ceremonies can be altered to affect spirits or to resonate more with the Shadow's power. The Bloody Codex can be made to write down the target's emotions instead, even when they have a hard time expressing them themselves and Forge Anchor can be used as a basis to forcefully Fetter a spirit to a target until the binding is destroyed. There is even a variation of the rite that sets where the spirit will recorporate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A few hushed whispers say that the Mysterium is working on ways to have them affect Supernal beings by adapting the rituals with Prime, but the details are very sparse. Some even say that a Fate variation is being researched to attempt to create Ceremonies to influence the Hedge. Whether these are in the early stages or the researchers are attempting to work out some glitches or information was censored due to startling discoveries remains uncertain.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>*rubs the bridge of her nose*<br /> <br /> So, when we were writing the Chapter on Ceremonies and Regalia, we had to do some of the figuring out how and what, exactly, Ceremonies are in the world. You get the gist of it in the main book, but to go a little more into it, Ceremonies are the result of rituals repeatedly practiced around &quot;death&quot; in all of it's forms, so much that it picks up deathly resonance-variants performed by Krewes or those who explicitly practice around Avernian Gates accumulate that resonance faster but also weirder, which is why some ceremonies look like off-kilter versions of the familiar rituals. But, that said, it takes time for the living world's death aspect to get scarred that way, to develop that trauma response to a Ceremony.<br /> <br /> Between that and the much more straightforward rules in Mage, THe Contagion Player Guide, and (most importantly) Imperial Mysteries regarding the affectation and creation of supernatural powers, I'd say something this sort of schtick is absolutely the purview of Archmasters Only, at <i>best</i> as a 7 Dot Practice of Entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T12:06:59-08:00","id":1475850,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475844#post1475844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the most potent ones leverage the energies of death to create powerful effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly not how Ceremonies work.<br /> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This grants a target [Potency] dots of Ceremonies for the duration. </div> </div> </div>If it takes a Fate 5 spell to give a target dots in a Supernatural Merit, why on earth should it be within the scope of a Patterning spell to provide dots of a more expensive Trait representing specific knowledge?</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A few hushed whispers say that the Mysterium is working on ways to have them affect Supernal beings by adapting the rituals with Prime, but the details are very sparse. Some even say that a Fate variation is being researched to attempt to create Ceremonies to influence the Hedge. Whether these are in the early stages or the researchers are attempting to work out some glitches or information was censored due to startling discoveries remains uncertain. </div> </div> </div>Per the PGCC, Prime is already the Arcanum to use for studying Ceremonies, and Ceremonies function as Yantras for spells whose effects align with theirs. The spell as you've written it appears to be founded in an arbitrary symmetry that simply isn't there.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:28:00-08:00","id":1475910,"title":"","content":"Interesting, there are a lot more factors than what I had considered. Unfortunately I do not own the Contagion Chronicle, so the corelation between Prime, Ceremonies and yantras is unexpected.<br /> <br /> When based on Geist 2ed, the explanation on Ceremonies made me think they were bits of occult knowledge with a strong death resonance. So as a skill, acquiring them with a Patterning of Death or Mind sounded plausible, would that not be the case ? Fate provides another solution, but I wanted to explore other ways to do it. Would it still be impossible with those other two ?<br /> <br /> In regards to modifying them, since my current knowledge of them is from the Geist core book, it seemed like equivalents for other Twilight phases could be created by researching occult correspondences related to them. So its complex enough that normal research is not enough and only archmastery could cover it ? In such a case, would there be any reference book that expanded on how Ceremonies work ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T11:57:25-08:00","id":1475923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475910#post1475910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, there are a lot more factors than what I had considered. Unfortunately I do not own the Contagion Chronicle, so the corelation between Prime, Ceremonies and yantras is unexpected.<br /> <br /> When based on Geist 2ed, the explanation on Ceremonies made me think they were bits of occult knowledge with a strong death resonance. So as a skill, acquiring them with a Patterning of Death or Mind sounded plausible, would that not be the case ? Fate provides another solution, but I wanted to explore other ways to do it. Would it still be impossible with those other two ?<br /> <br /> In regards to modifying them, since my current knowledge of them is from the Geist core book, it seemed like equivalents for other Twilight phases could be created by researching occult correspondences related to them. So its complex enough that normal research is not enough and only archmastery could cover it ? In such a case, would there be any reference book that expanded on how Ceremonies work ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet. THe beginning of Chapter 2 in Memento Mori lightly touches on the stuff I talked about, but anyone wanting to read that as just poetic license has the room to.<br /> <br /> Still, Imperial Mysteries pretty well makes it clear that the creation of new forms of existing non-Supernal magic is pretty often the result of Archmastery as mages go, with the odd exceptions being. well. Odd Exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T12:16:59-08:00","id":1475924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475910#post1475910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When based on Geist 2ed, the explanation on Ceremonies made me think they were bits of occult knowledge with a strong death resonance. So as a skill, acquiring them with a Patterning of Death or Mind sounded plausible, would that not be the case ? Fate provides another solution, but I wanted to explore other ways to do it. Would it still be impossible with those other two ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think simply granting knowledge of how to perform existing Ceremonies should indeed be comparable to the Mind Patterning spell Gain Skill, since theoretically all you need is the right knowledge to perform them. (As opposed to creating entirely new Ceremonies, which presumably would involve archmaster Practices). <br /> <br /> While Ceremonies as presented in Geist are very death-themed, the actual metaphysics involved (especially considering the Contagion Player\u2019s Guide) don\u2019t seem to strictly tied to Death at all. Rather, they\u2019re a confluence of occult laws and symbolism, and thus fit more under the purview of Prime. However, since Supernal magic often cares more about the end result than the underlaying technobabble of other magic systems, it could be that, rather than Ceremonies as a whole falling under this or that Arcanum, an individual Ceremony is under the purview of whatever effect it actually has. Theoretically, \u201cCeremonies\u201d aren\u2019t limited to being death-themed, it\u2019s just that the ones Sin-Eaters and their Krews learn and use tend to be so because death and ghosts are what they spend most of their time dealing with. Hence, a lot of the Ceremonies in Sin-Eater will involve Death from a mage\u2019s perspective (since they have effects on ghosts, which fall under Death\u2019s purview), but aren\u2019t actually \u201cpowered\u201d by Death, and Death doesn\u2019t cover Ceremonies as a whole. (And, for what it\u2019s worth, the Player\u2019s Guide only says that Prime \u201cis the best Arcanum for studying Ceremonies\u201d, not manipulating their effects.)<br /> <br /> As an aside, I think there is a solid argument to be made for a Mind+Spirit Patterning spell granting knowledge of, and capacity to perform, Pack Rites from Werewolf, since all those seem to require is a combination of a connection with the Shadow (usually through a pack totem) and the necessary knowledge to invoke the laws and agreements already in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 03-06-2022, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T12:54:27-08:00","id":1475927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475910#post1475910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, there are a lot more factors than what I had considered. Unfortunately I do not own the Contagion Chronicle, so the corelation between Prime, Ceremonies and yantras is unexpected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf rites can likewise serve as Yantras for appropriate spells and grant their bonus in the same fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When based on Geist 2ed, the explanation on Ceremonies made me think they were bits of occult knowledge with a strong death resonance. So as a skill, acquiring them with a Patterning of Death or Mind sounded plausible, would that not be the case? </div> </div> </div>So here's the thing: In the mechanical context of Mage, a Ceremony is a Mystery. People can do them by accident or without realizing that's what they're doing, but what they're doing is making use of a particular weird thing about the way the world works. The Awakened have Mage Sight for the purposes of figuring out stuff like this normally.<br /> <br /> What this means for using spells to provide them is that either you shouldn't be able to provide Ceremonies to a character as a mechanical element on their character sheet (What happens when the Duration runs out? Why can't Mind be used in this fashion to fish for <i>any other type of specific true occult knowledge?</i>) or there's no <i>point</i> in providing it as a thing that's part of the character instead of conveying that information prosaically because performing the Ceremony is as simple as doing the steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T01:51:18-08:00","id":1475976,"title":"","content":"I'm not quite sure what Ceremonies are, but I think even if you don't need to be supernatural to use them the game generally presents things in terms of mages, within themselves, being only able to use powers that come from being Awakened. The whole thing where you lose Supernatural Merits and can't get them back.<br /> <br /> I would think the justification for this in character is a combination of the metaphysical connection to the Supernal not resting well with more messy forms of power, and the mental effects of Gnosis interfering a bit with comprehensive understanding in cases where something might be purely knowledge based; there are some intuitive connections or processes that elude you when you keep seeing the symbolic underpinnings.<br /> <br /> Besides, I think Werewolf Rites are more than just applications of knowledge, they're about how the Uratha are metaphysically entangled in the ecology of the Shadow, and have a lineage to give them some claim of authority to it. You don't have the levels of Arcana necessary to make yourself a descendant of Wolf and/or Luna.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think you could cast a spell to let mages act as participants in a Rite led by somebody else, and let werewolves use rite skills to aid in appropriate ritual spell casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T06:17:38-08:00","id":1475983,"title":"","content":"I think Dark Eras 2: Mysterious Frontiers establishes some decent standards for how Awakened magic might engage with the powers of other beings. That one is concerned with mages and engagement with the Wyrd, and has spells to allow them to make Supernal beings and ephemeral entities into valid sources of equivalents to Goblin Contracts, they get some facility for shaping the Hedge, and they can make somebody who wouldn't otherwise be into a valid participant in Wyrd backed oaths, although not able to initiate them (in that case, the spell ending with the oath unfulfilled means the subject can no longer count for performing their obligations, but is still under the jurisdiction to be punished for having essentially broken their word).<br /> <br /> I'm seeing things like being able to enable other beings to carve Gifts into werewolves or discerning sources for them to find Rites, rather than acquiring those powers for themselves. The mage core already has a spell to allow the Awakened to use other people's objects of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T08:18:33-08:00","id":1475985,"title":"","content":"My reasoning for being a mage being able to spoof Pack Rites is that they aren\u2019t unique to the Uratha, and you don\u2019t actually have connection to Luna or Father Wolf to perform them. They seem to be a thing anyone can do with the right connection to the Shadow. Being Wolf-Blooded doesn\u2019t itself allow it, except as a side-effect of certain Tells with a strong spiritual component to them. Further, Shadow Occultists can perform them without even being part of a pack. It\u2019s implied Claimed can as well. So at the very least, the metaphysical requirements seem less weighty than full template altering. Wolf Rites, on the other hand, do seem to require a relation to the Shadow unique to Uratha (or those oddball human packs with the blessing of Luna). <br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible I\u2019ve spent too much time trying to dissect the various ritual magic systems in this setting.<br /> <br /> Edit: though I admit I don\u2019t really like the precedent that Gain Skill sets for a mage being able to insert technical knowledge into someone\u2019s head without possessing that knowledge themselves, so I\u2019d be happy if someone can rationalize for me why Mind Patterning can grant dots in Science but not the knowledge component of ritual magics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 03-07-2022, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T15:06:30-08:00","id":1476002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475985#post1475985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: though I admit I don\u2019t really like the precedent that Gain Skill sets for a mage being able to insert technical knowledge into someone\u2019s head without possessing that knowledge themselves, so I\u2019d be happy if someone can rationalize for me why Mind Patterning can grant dots in Science but not the knowledge component of ritual magics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game reason is because Skill dots are an abstraction and specific concrete knowledge isn't. &quot;Someone who's competent at Science&quot; is different than &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474648-does-magic-require-explanation?p=1475951#post1475951\">Someone who knows this specific piece of information that I can't form an Imago for because I don't know it.</a>&quot; You know what the symbol of A Scientist looks like and have the tools to impose that symbolism over your own competencies, but if you don't know the way to make all the frogs in the pond at the center of town croak a chorus that makes it rain, you can't make yourself know it without lucking into that knowledge through natural or Fate-assisted legwork, and at that point it's no longer about adding a thing to your character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-07-2022, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T01:28:39-08:00","id":1476032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1475985#post1475985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I admit I don\u2019t really like the precedent that Gain Skill sets for a mage being able to insert technical knowledge into someone\u2019s head without possessing that knowledge themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>The precedent set by Gain Skill isn't channeling information into somebody's head telepathically, it's being able to transform minds to the level of things like, say, totally rewriting their personality.<br /> <br /> Mundane examples of reality are more accessible by magic across the board, whereas supernatural things, whether objects or information, tend to be more numinous in ways that require a base example. So it's also why Matter magic can't turn things into the alloys of perfected metals directly, it needs to have those metals to meld together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T07:34:39-08:00","id":1476046,"title":"","content":"Oh okay. So it\u2019s more that you\u2019re reshaping someone\u2019s mind to be optimized for Science, rather than imparting scientific knowledge. So when given five dots of Science, a subject doesn\u2019t suddenly know how a nuclear reactor works, but they\u2019d have a much better chance of figuring it out. By the same token, you can increase someone\u2019s capacity to understand general mystical principles (raising Occult), but without imparting explicit knowledge, like how to perform specific rituals (dots of Ceremonies, Rites, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T00:44:08-08:00","id":1476085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1476046#post1476046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh okay. So it\u2019s more that you\u2019re reshaping someone\u2019s mind to be optimized for Science, rather than imparting scientific knowledge. So when given five dots of Science, a subject doesn\u2019t suddenly know how a nuclear reactor works, but they\u2019d have a much better chance of figuring it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that's how Skills work. A foundational aptitude is an Attribute, a Skill constitutes actual knowledge acquired and practiced. It's already a bit undefined as to particular specialty, and you might not be up on everything even within a specialty (actual scientists still need to read journals and attend conferences to keep up), but you'll have something.<br /> <br /> The knowledge is not sourced, it appears there to align with the fact that you've altered the essence of reality to say that the subject has this particular Skill. If you use a Patterning of Matter to turn wood into steel, you don't ask where the iron came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same token, you can increase someone\u2019s capacity to understand general mystical principles (raising Occult), but without imparting explicit knowledge, like how to perform specific rituals (dots of Ceremonies, Rites, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about Ceremonies, but I do know that Werewolf Rites are not bound to being used by rolling the Occult Skill, so already they can comfortably be said to be more than an application of it. You can give a person a base of knowledge that would allow them to know a lot <i>about</i> werewolves and their magic, but actual supernatural power runs deeper.<br /> <br /> You said anyone with the right connection to the Shadow can use Rites, would it not make sense that mages lack that connection and cannot create it without being archmasters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T07:35:18-08:00","id":1476095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1476085#post1476085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said anyone with the right connection to the Shadow can use Rites, would it not make sense that mages lack that connection and cannot create it without being archmasters?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to perform Pack Rites seems to really be a side effect of a number of different conditions, most of which mages can at least approximate with Spirit. For example, it seems that most spirits have the intrinsic capacity to form the bond necessary to create Shadow Occultists (which is basically an otherwise normal human with access to spirit powers, including Pack Rites), hence I assume it would only take Patterning (or at most Making) to do something similar. At the very least, a mage should be able to coerce a spirit into forming the bond themselves. (I have been mainly picturing a mage granting rites to an otherwise mortal subject, whether or not Gnosis would interfere with the process if done on a mage is another question). Of course, this would only last as long as the spell. Permanently altering someone\u2019s spiritual makeup would naturally be the province of archmastery. <br /> <br /> My point was just that, of the number of different \u201cexclusive\u201d magic systems, it seems relatively easy to get access to Pack Rites. So if the goal is to temporarily hack into other ritual systems, Pack Rites sounded like a plausible option to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T15:58:45-08:00","id":1476123,"title":"","content":"With all that is being said, I altered the spell to use a Making of Fate instead. However, now I am very curious about Scriptorian's inquiry on whether granting Shadow Occultist abilities being viable. Its too bad there aren't Astral rites as well, I am curious what shape that would take.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T16:06:41-08:00","id":1476124,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s always the option of\u2026 just\u2026 having a spirit Ride/Possess/Claim the poor sucker, then chasing the spirit away, then persuading another (or the same) spirit to do the transgressive exchange that instills Shadow Occultism. All with judicious uses of common Spirit spells.<br /> <br /> Hey, no one said we had to do it in a single go, right?<br /> <br /> Edit;<br /> Even better \u2014 have your Familiar spirit as the Occultist\u2019s patron. Or the patron of several Occultists. You now have a powder keg of a henchman, or two, or dozen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-09-2022, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T16:33:00-08:00","id":1476127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1476123#post1476123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all that is being said, I altered the spell to use a Making of Fate instead. However, now I am very curious about Scriptorian's inquiry on whether granting Shadow Occultist abilities being viable. Its too bad there aren't Astral rites as well, I am curious what shape that would take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practitioners of Obcasus Rites are extremely niche, being a subset of a group outnumbered by mages. The Rites require consecrated spaces to perform and involve a fairly hefty amount of trappings in the form of props and participants, especially at higher tiers.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking, there's no Underworld rites, either \u2014 again, Ceremonies aren't intrinsically tied to the energies of death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1476085#post1476085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said anyone with the right connection to the Shadow can use Rites, would it not make sense that mages lack that connection and cannot create it without being archmasters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly this is plugging information from two different Night Horrors books into each other, but:<br /> <br /> The Fault of the Enraptured Thyrsus known as Spiral establishes that Awakened magic is capable of inducing spirits to Claim people, albeit this is framed in terms of Claimed coming from spirits possessing people for long enough (and Spiral doesn't have any special spell or Dread Power to enable this \u2014 she's got Bind Spirit as a Praxis and learned how to make herself Hive-Claimed in exchange for giving up her sympathetic name to &quot;something horrific from the deep Shadow&quot;). The same section also notes that few spirits can normally start that process (and, admittedly, when Possession normally only lasts a scene and Awakened magic allows it to last much longer, the distinction between Claim and indefinite Possession is academic in many cases), which would seem likely to indicate that in this case, it's a matter of knowing that form of Manifestation is possible and how it occurs.<br /> <br /> Shadow Occultists are made when a spirit can be persuaded to pour its Essence into a human who has been Ridden or Claimed to give them some of its own Influence and the capacity to pick up more. The process entails at least one breaking point and can incur several more down the line. As a traumatic and niche application of spiritual power, it's likewise probably not so much impossible to induce a spirit to perform as it is necessary to know about in the first place.<br /> <br /> This isn't quite like trying to create Sin-Eaters by inflating a ghost's Rank and giving it the Bargain (for which, as with many other supernatural agreements, very probably entails both parties forge the connection of their own free will) \u2014 it's likely more akin to how spirits can be persuaded to form totem bonds without any sort of rite, i.e. it's a weird thing spirits do that's beyond the scope of Mage's corebook to address as the extended look at spirit ecology Werewolf deals with, but it's not wholly beyond the reach of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> That said, while it's theoretically within the capabilities of Traveler Arcana to engineer the sort of connection necessary to be able to use Pack Rites without being a werewolf or Wolf-Blooded, bestowing Rites themselves is in an even weirder split-unavailability than Ceremonies \u2014 rites draw on otherworldy agreements that underpin the landscape of the Shadow, which means we run afoul of the aforementioned need for specific knowledge to be able to impart knowledge of a rite beyond the prosaic description of the necessary symbolism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-09-2022, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T10:16:05-07:00","id":1478699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1175514#post1175514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a spell I've been considering for a while. I'm not entirely certain about it, whether it should require a point of Mana, etc. But, this is what I have:<br /> <br /> <b>Hasten Symbolism (Time </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Expression, Occult<br /> <br /> The mage enhances the target's ability to conceptualize the symbols of magical power, condensing what would take multiple moments into a single, graceful movement. The next time the target casts a spell during this spell's Duration, the target may utilize an additional number of Yantras equal to this spell's Potency in the same reflexive action. This does not affect Yantras that normally require more than a reflexive action to employ (such as High Speech or Runes), nor does it increase the Gnosis-derived number of Yantras the target may access.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The target can use the High Speech Yantra as a reflexive action.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Add this spell's Potency to the target's Gnosis for the purpose of determining how long it takes to draw runes.<br /> <b>+1 Reach, +1 Mana:</b> The target benefits from this spell's effects on a number of spells equal to Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would it work for ritually cast spells or just quick casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T14:27:24-07:00","id":1478710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1478699#post1478699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it work for ritually cast spells or just quick casting?</div> </div> </div> </div>My intent was for it to apply to instant casting, since ritual spells take so long that except at the highest tiers of Gnosis, reflexive actions are a non-issue. I don't see any problems with letting it apply to rituals though, since it does nothing to reduce their overall casting time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:45:48-07:00","id":1478733,"title":"","content":"That is a very lucky find, I have been looking for that spell's reference for a while. I think the ability to allow the spell to act multiple times could just be the result of adding Potency, rather than requiring a Reach and a mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T07:27:59-07:00","id":1479076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Co-Temperus (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Mana Cost:</b> 1<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Larceny, Politics, Subterfuge<br /> By making the present as indeterminable as the future, this spell can allow the subject to participate in multiple \u2018potential presents\u2019 simultaneously. The subject splits into one additional version of themselves per Potency. This is not a true division of the subject, but instead is the subject existing in multiple timelines. They share a single Willpower and Mana pool, but are otherwise treated as separate. At the beginning of the subject\u2019s turn, each version of themselves may perform their actions as normal. However, apply the results of only one version of the subject on the world around them, and each version of the subject completely ignores what the others do (sometimes even occupying the same space). For instance, if one version of the subject opens a door and goes through it, all other versions of the subject still have to open the door and walk through it. If at the end of the turn the subject chooses to apply the changes of another version of themselves who did not open the door on the world, then the door would be closed at the end of the turn (having never been opened). Any supernatural powers that affect one or more versions of the subject affects all of them. When the spell ends or is canceled, only one version of the subject sticks around, and that version suffers all of the damage, conditions and tilts suffered by all other versions of themselves, but also gains all knowledge and experiences from the discarded versions of themselves.<br /> <b>Add Mind (\u2022\u2022): </b>The different versions of the subject may communicate telepathically.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The different versions of the subject are more insulated from each other. When one or more of them is affected by a supernatural power, then they may roll a Clash of Wills to keep all other versions from themselves from being equally affected.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The version of the subject that remains after the spell expires gains the worst damage from all versions of themselves, instead of all of it.<br /> <b>+3 Reach:</b> When the spell expires, the damage, conditions and tilts from the discarded versions of the subject is not applied to the subject.<br /> <b>Note:</b> A Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 equivalent of this spell exists, but relies on a duplication of the character\u2019s spatial presence instead of timelines. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If at the end of the turn the subject chooses to apply the changes of another version of themselves who did not open the door on the world, then the door would be closed at the end of the turn (having never been opened). </div> </div> </div>In this example, if the versions do not communicate with each other, how would one version know that in another version, the door was not opened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27342-werikscs","name":"werikscs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T09:59:12-07:00","id":1479135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werikscs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479076#post1479076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> In this example, if the versions do not communicate with each other, how would one version know that in another version, the door was not opened?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine they could talk via a phone if the caster is short on spell control. Some other options include using Oaths Fulfilled to let the other versions know, using a Unveiling of Forces to listen to the sound each make, creating an improvised radio system. Familiars can be used as intermediaries and scrying windows are always useful. But I feel you might be looking for something more along the line of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1441659#post1441659\">Converging Potentiality</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T10:03:42-07:00","id":1479345,"title":"","content":"How hard would it be to make yourself into a pseudo-Hive Souled? Life 5 with a Mind component to create the additional bodies that you're puppetting, plus One Mind Two Thoughts to make simultaneous actions between all bodies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:01:19-07:00","id":1479350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479345#post1479345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard would it be to make yourself into a pseudo-Hive Souled? Life 5 with a Mind component to create the additional bodies that you're puppeteering, plus One Mind Two Thoughts to make simultaneous actions between all bodies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That might work, another way could be if they utilize a Patterning of Life and Mind to transform the subject into a biomass manipulating virus with a shared Oneiros. The virus would have a severity of Potency and would rewrite the thought processes of the infected in order to match those of the original host. When the virus reproduces and infects someone else, the host gains one more body to act as an additional agent. The you could use a separate Making of Life to create a central processing unit biocomputer, which would draw information in, come to some conclusions and then feed it as surface thoughts to the Oneiros. Think of it as something similar to how the infected hive mind works in Prototype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:04:31-07:00","id":1479351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479350#post1479350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That might work, another way could be if they utilize a Patterning of Life and Mind to transform the subject into a biomass manipulating virus with a shared Oneiros. The virus would have a severity of Potency and would rewrite the thought processes of the infected in order to match those of the original host. When the virus reproduces and infects someone else, the host gains one more body to act as an additional agent. The you could use a separate Making of Life to create a central processing unit biocomputer, which would draw information in, come to some conclusions and then feed it as surface thoughts to the Oneiros. Think of it as something similar to how the infected hive mind works in Prototype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh jeez, I was just thinking of ways to lead a double life. Like, if you have a date to keep but need to do some legwork for the local Hierarch. You went right for the bioweapon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:38:02-07:00","id":1479355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479351#post1479351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh jeez, I was just thinking of ways to lead a double life. Like, if you have a date to keep but need to do some legwork for the local Hierarch. You went right for the bioweapon!</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you wanted to create an antagonist that could be eerily good at being in multiple places at once. But for leading a double life, I think your approach sounds pretty sensible. The key challenge is real time updates and multitasking. Because otherwise you could make, for example, a lifelike Golem and animate it with a Mind copy of the original, effectively an ushabti. The main issue would be that, at some point you would need to download the new memories and trust the choices they made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:42:38-07:00","id":1479356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479355#post1479355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you wanted to create an antagonist that could be eerily good at being in multiple places at once. But for leading a double life, I think your approach sounds pretty sensible. The key challenge is real time updates and multitasking. Because otherwise you could make, for example, a lifelike Golem and animate it with a Mind copy of the original, effectively an ushabti. The main issue would be that, at some point you would need to download the new memories and trust the choices they made.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a scaled down version of 1e's Ochema, so maybe something along those lines? Both are passively aware of what happens to one another, but the main body needs to concentrate to notice any emotional bleed from the duplicate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T11:53:47-07:00","id":1479358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1479356#post1479356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like a scaled down version of 1e's Ochema, so maybe something along those lines? Both are passively aware of what happens to one another, but the main body needs to concentrate to notice any emotional bleed from the duplicate?</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, you might want to look at the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1441659#post1441659\">Converging Potentiality</a> spell. Creating discount Ochema was the intention when designing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T18:44:42-07:00","id":1480231,"title":"","content":"<b>Nihilum AKA Nothing After Nothing Crawled Into The World (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Befouled)</b><br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Intimidation, Expression<br /> Withstood: Resolve<br /> Cost: 1 Mana <br /> <br /> <i>Your belief in the Supernal is distorted and distant, like a repressed memory of something unspeakable. You are overwhelmed by a creeping, uncanny sense that nothing is real. Polite and dripping voices infest your Oneiros, whispering insane delusions and empty epiphanies that sound perfectly True. Your Mage Sight becomes a cracked mirror that reflects anti-symbols reveling lethargically in your imprisonment-transcendence.<br /> <br /> Apathy is love, the future is remembered in prophecy that already happened, all roads lead nowhere and everywhere. You wake up in a cold sweat at 11:59 PM and time has stopped. Lingering nightmares are falling out of your broken soul and filling your bedroom. A long lost friend emerges from an empty corner and reassures you that everything will be wrong.</i><br /> <br /> This spell was devised by a Scelestus who wanted to enlighten other Mages about the liberating potential of the Abyss. He theorized that all of Awakened society is ultimately a gilded crib for frightened children who cannot bear to exist in an universe devoid of cosmically-ordained meaning and purpose. This spell forces the target to confront that existential fear by manifesting a reality in which their magic is hollowed out and filled with unreality. <br /> <br /> In other words, each point of Potency makes the target suffer a Paradox Condition [Mage 2ed Core 116], whose effects and methods of Resolution are designed by the spellcaster. Use the target's Wisdom to determine how long it takes for these Paradox Conditions to lapse on their own.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: Whenever someone attempts to Pattern Scour any Paradox Conditions caused by this spell, they must also lose Mana equal to the spell's Potency, or upgrade the Damage into 1 Resistant Aggravated. If the target dies as a result of this Resistant Aggravated Damage, their soul is used as an entrance into reality by an Abyssal Entity with a Rank up to the spellcaster's [Gnosis/2 Rounded Up]. This Abyssal Entity is chosen by the spellcaster when forming the Imago.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T09:34:23-07:00","id":1483879,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Void Prison (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 / Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Making</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Brawl, Intimidation, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A cherished belief of the Praetorians is that in order to build someone up into cannon fodder for the General, one first needs to break them down completely. Brainwashing spells have limited duration, and making a mind suitably malleable for conditioning can take weeks, this spell was designed to solve this issue quickly and efficiently.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The subject becomes trapped in a total sensory deprivation void, experiencing nothing but emptiness while being forced to remain conscious </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They cannot scream, sleep, speak, move, not even perceive darkness (since perceiving the absence of light is still perceiving something). This is accomplished by either fully shutting down the mind's ability to process the senses while trapping the body in temporal stasis, or trapping them in an empty pocket of space while only allowing them to retain their ability to perceive time, without being able to interact with it. Because of this, subjects do not age, nor do they require rest or sustenance. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is created for the subject according to the duration of the spell, making it appear to outside observers that the effect happens in a single turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every day spent within this void constitutes a breaking point. A especially cruel feature of this spell is that it loopholes the Lie. Having nothing around means there is nothing to Disbelieve and nothing that can be used by the Quiescence to rationalize it away. Because of this, Sleepers, Sleepwalker, Proximi and similar often emerge from it panicked, crying and screaming in despair.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In addition, the absence of sensory stimuli for long periods causes the mind to break down its thought processes in an attempt to mitigate stress, causing each breaking point to apply a Derangement rather than a Condition. Common ones include Nyctophobia (fear of the dark), Sciophobia (fear of shadows), Photophobia, Agoraphobia, Claustrophobia and Somniphobia.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The utilization of this spell is usually banned in Consilia by Bronze Laws and even sanctioned use is considered cruel and unusual punishment. Seers known for utilizing it are normally terminated after all their useful knowledge is extracted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach and a mana:</b> The spell can affect the minds of supernatural creatures, causing a breaking point in their equivalent morality system (rolling for their current level of Wisdom/Harmony/Clarity/etc).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Observation 1:</b> Inspired by Dr Bob's presentation of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bq8PQkZKF6w\" target=\"_blank\">SCP-2701</a>, one of the most low key and horrifying anomalies.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation 2:</b> For practical purposes, the different phobias act according to the generic Phobia derangement described on <i>World of Darkness </i>page 97, meaning characters must roll Resolve + Composure to even approach the object they fear. Each successful roll adds a -1 penalty to the next roll, up to a maximum of -5. Afterwards, the next consecutive success will require rolling for a breaking point (or equivalent). The character can opt to not roll in order to break the success streak. These are resolved when the character gains a point of Integrity. This secondary effect was created by adapting the Strained condition from page 318 of the core book.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-25-2022, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T16:37:40-07:00","id":1483929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1483879#post1483879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Void Prison (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 / Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of that Black Mirror episode &quot;White Christmas&quot;. So it's effectively the default Pocket Dimension with a Time sub-component to extend subjective perception of time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T16:56:31-07:00","id":1483931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1483929#post1483929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reminds me of that Black Mirror episode &quot;White Christmas&quot;. So it's effectively the default Pocket Dimension with a Time sub-component to extend subjective perception of time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It uses elements of each of them, creating the effect can be accomplished by using either Pocket Dimension with Time to allow the subject to only perceive the flow of time (plus your own thoughts) or, alternately, using Mind and Time to create a much more extreme version of an isolation tank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-15-2022, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T11:44:12-07:00","id":1484434,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporal Buffer (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Patterning</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Science</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes despite a mage's best efforts, avoiding a deadly threat is impossible. In such situations, buying a few moments allows one last hand to be played to reverse one's fate. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This rote was developed by the Mystagogue Dr Typhon, a specialist in bioengineering. When cast upon a subject, it delays the application of any negative changes by [Potency] turns after they were inflicted, whether they are unwilling temporal alterations, damage, Conditions or means of instant death. Utilizing this, Dr Typhon was able to subject his creations to multiple deadly situations, being able to collect more data from each failed experiment before they expired.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One curious property of this spell allows one to heal the damage buffered before it takes hold, either through magic or medicine. However, being able to quantify the damage normally requires an Unveiling of Time, Prime or Life. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When Dr Typhon's cruel experiments lead to his inevitable Rapture, he relied on this rote to stay alive. Normally he could use it to heal himself from any catastrophic wounds. Occasionally some unsavory employers or persistent Sentinels were able to overwhelm even his ability to heal, causing him to go back in time to try to avoid the scenario entirely. Because of this, he was considered one of the most resilient Rapt on record.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>The negative changes become more evident, manifesting as temporal echoes around the subject, who is able to instinctively feel the severity of the incoming damage. With conjunctional Fate 1 or Mind 1, these are only revealed whenever the subject (or a caster that retains spell control) wants them to be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sentinel's Ears (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Investigation, Occult, Survival</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When delving into unavoidable danger, only the most vigilant stand a chance at survival. This maxim was attributed to Cerberus, a Thunderbolt Guardian renowned for her successful hunt of Reapers. She attributed development of this rote as a fundamental pillar in her success.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This sharpens the Peripheral Mage Sight of the target, allowing them to detect supernatural abilities that are currently active, even if they were not activated in their presence. A werewolf, for example, will not be perceived for merely existing, but one under the influence of a Sacred Hunt will draw attention. Ambient spells or mages that walk around with various enchantments will stand out, but supernaturally concealed abilities will not be detected as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Furthermore, the subject has an idea of the general direction where the effect came from, although not the distance. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With conjunctional Space 1, the subject also knows the distance to the origin and/or center of the effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With conjunctional Fate 1 or Mind 1, they know the intent behind the effect. They would be aware, for example, that an ability was activated as bait to any mages in a crowd. But what the ability does or even who used it would require further investigation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>The mage's supernatural senses are fine tuned enough that they pick up even the most nuanced effects of phenomena, granting them the Keen Periphery merit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage gains an uncanny facility for bringing all their focus into actively seeking out supernaturally concealed secrets, granting them [Potency] dots of the Piercing Glance merit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Temporal Dispellation (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Arcana rating of the subject spell\u2019s caster or dot rating of the supernatural ability\u2019s user</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Recommended Rote Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Academics, Intimidation, Occult</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A spell created by the Libertine Altjira, who had accidentally fallen into the Hedge while navigating the inner realms towards the Dreamtime. The Hedge embodies stories and narratives, so he reasoned that just like all stories eventually end, so must its spells. By carefully choosing which supernatural effects to end and which to continue, he was able to prune the narrative much like one does a bonsai tree, directing its progress towards him finding a way out. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This ends any spells or supernatural abilities that it targets, unmaking the time they have left to exist and all changes they would have applied during that interval. In order to do this, the mage needs to be able to perceive the ability in some way, which is usually simple for Awakened magic or more explicit powers, such as a chess spirit animating a knight\u2019s suit of armor with its Influence. A popular method of achieving this for more subtle effects is by Unveiling the perception the user has of them using Mind magic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell cannot end an archmage's spells or abilities of Rank 6+ entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> A similar effect to <i>Temporal Dispelation</i> can be replicated by using a Making of Death to create an end to the spell or, alternatively, by using Death 2 and Prime 1 to decay the spell (although it only works on Awakened magic without conjunctional Arcana). </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-20-2022, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T20:40:54-07:00","id":1485006,"title":"","content":"<i>Void Prison</i> was updated to be closer to the inspiration. Before it wasn't implied that the subject cannot expire in containment, which is now clarified. It should work as a way to inflict a fate worse than death, which showcases the depth of insanity Seers can reach. The logic behind the spell was fleshed out as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T01:07:30-07:00","id":1485825,"title":"","content":"Maintenance spell, giving you a chance to save your hard-earned Enhanced Items before they're Dissonanced into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <b>Spackle</b> (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b>Potency<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Mana per Potency <br /> <b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Crafts, Occult<br /> <br /> Sleepers are detrimental to the health of spells - this can be a problem for vital things like Enhanced items. This spell exists as a stop-gap against the day the Abyss is finally closed, a way to press Mana into the Imago of a spell corroded by Dissonance. <br /> <br /> This spell repairs a spell affected by Dissonance, at a rate of 1 spell-factor step per point of Potency. This explicitly may not alter the repaired spell, only restore it to the state it was cast in.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> This spell can restore Dissonance-erroded Reach effects, at a rate of one Reach per two points of Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The effects of this spell are Lasting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-05-2022, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T21:19:32-07:00","id":1485956,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Backrooms of History (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Unmaking</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Recommended Rote Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The time will come when the mage faces a truly daunting challenge, where discretion and absolute precision are key. In those times, one\u2019s own history and connections can make one\u2019s opponents too guarded to defeat. When presented with these situations, the Guardians have learned to forego their place in history to go into the deepest type of cover possible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell erases the mage\u2019s presence on history for the duration. The subject will be unknown from all who meet them, no records, histories or evidence about their life will exist. Some mages choose to supplement this spell by granting themselves an Alternate Identity. Any rolls regarding maintaining said identity automatically succeed, since there exists no other information to disprove it. Any mundane attempts to investigate their past before this spell was cast automatically fail and any supernatural ones provoke a Clash of Wills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Alternatively, the caster can choose to have their actions been performed by someone else, allowing them to have a perfectly clean record.</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> Once the durations end, their history reasserts itself, appended with whatever actions they took while it was active. This leaves enemies baffled with how the mage was working with them or right under their noses, with no one reacting appropriately.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Observation: </span></span></b><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Constant Presence</i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> would probably be the way the mage could exclude certain targets, making it so cabalmates and other key contacts remembered them. Utilizing conjunctional Fate 2 could allow them to be affected by certain aspects, that way the full cabal can benefit from the spell without forgetting about each other.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Unerring Eye (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Perfecting</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Recommended Rote Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Brawl, Firearms, Weaponry</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When dealing with a deadly opponent or one that is surrounded by allies, being quick and precise can make the difference between success and being overwhelmed. A sniper that takes too long to shoot risks their position being discovered and an assassin that cannot disable their target quickly risks backup arriving. Arrows carrying operations deep within enemy lines created this rote to minimize risk.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It allows the subject to quickly take stock of the factors in combat and adjust their attacks, making them able to fully aim an attack in a single turn. In addition, whether in a shootout or in the chaos of close quarter combat, they become able to quickly adjust their attacks to account for minute changes in the target\u2019s movement, reducing all penalties for attacks aimed at specific body parts by [Potency].</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The subject\u2019s maximum Aim bonus is increased by [Potency]. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-07-2022, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T18:12:13-07:00","id":1489596,"title":"","content":"<b>Subliminal Conditioning (Mind 3)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Apprentice mages peruse the in-universe equivalent of the Awakening corebook and their eyes bulge at the possibilities of Psychic Domination. What power at such a meager price of entry! More experienced workers of Mind raise an eyebrow and smirk in their knowing of so much more sophisticated ways of manipulating a sentient being.<br /> <br /> This spell implants both a trigger and a response in the subconscious of its subject. The trigger may be a certain phrase, such as \u201cmonarchs and milkweeds,\u201d or a sight, feeling, condition, or anything else the subject can experience. The first time the subject perceives the trigger during the spell\u2019s Duration, they immediately perform the response, which must be a simple action that can be undertaken in one turn (or about a minute outside action scenes), such as lashing out physically against the nearest person or mailbox, speaking a certain phrase, freezing in place, doing a funny dance, etc. The response can also affect the subject\u2019s mood enough to increase or decrease their Impression level with another character by one step (or add/subtract [Potency] dice from one Social roll against the subject outside Social Maneuvering). The subject is aware that they are performing the action, though they may not understand why, and do so more as a reflex than as a fully conscious decision. As with Psychic Domination, the mage cannot implant responses that would be immediately dangerous to the subject if performed, and cannot force a mage to cast a spell this way. The spell has no effect on the body\u2019s autonomic responses.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can instill a more complex response that takes up to Potency minutes to perform.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject can be affected by the trigger a number of times equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Instead of an action, the mage can cause the subject to gain an emotional Condition when experiencing the trigger.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, +1 Mana: </b>The mage can program a response that would be directly harmful to the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Life 2:</b> The spell can also affect the subject\u2019s bodily autonomy, such as causing them to sweat or convulse. With a Reach, this can inflict an appropriate Tilt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T18:49:34-07:00","id":1489597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1489596#post1489596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Subliminal Conditioning (Mind 3)<br /> <br /> Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Resolve<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Persuasion, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Apprentice mages peruse the in-universe equivalent of the Awakening corebook and their eyes bulge at the possibilities of Psychic Domination. What power at such a meager price of entry! More experienced workers of Mind raise an eyebrow and smirk in their knowing of so much more sophisticated ways of manipulating a sentient being.<br /> <br /> This spell implants both a trigger and a response in the subconscious of its subject. The trigger may be a certain phrase, such as \u201cmonarchs and milkweeds,\u201d or a sight, feeling, condition, or anything else the subject can experience. The first time the subject perceives the trigger during the spell\u2019s Duration, they immediately perform the response, which must be a simple action that can be undertaken in one turn (or about a minute outside action scenes), such as lashing out physically against the nearest person or mailbox, speaking a certain phrase, freezing in place, doing a funny dance, etc. The response can also affect the subject\u2019s mood enough to increase or decrease their Impression level with another character by one step (or add/subtract [Potency] dice from one Social roll against the subject outside Social Maneuvering). The subject is aware that they are performing the action, though they may not understand why, and do so more as a reflex than as a fully conscious decision. As with Psychic Domination, the mage cannot implant responses that would be immediately dangerous to the subject if performed, and cannot force a mage to cast a spell this way. The spell has no effect on the body\u2019s autonomic responses.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The mage can instill a more complex response that takes up to Potency minutes to perform.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject can be affected by the trigger a number of times equal to Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Instead of an action, the mage can cause the subject to gain an emotional Condition when experiencing the trigger.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, +1 Mana: </b>The mage can program a response that would be directly harmful to the subject.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Life 2:</b> The spell can also affect the subject\u2019s bodily autonomy, such as causing them to sweat or convulse. With a Reach, this can inflict an appropriate Tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might fall into the complex commands of Psychic Domination, but with so many possible Reach options, this is a far cleaner format. Nothing like a manchurian agent, so many possibilities for a devious mage. Really reminds me of the Dai Li from Avatar and how the phrase &quot;The Earth King has invited you to Lake Laogai&quot; was used as a universal trigger for the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T20:23:59-07:00","id":1489601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1489597#post1489597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this might fall into the complex commands of Psychic Domination, but with so many possible Reach options, this is a far cleaner format.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the distinction between this and Psychic Domination is awareness in the victims - Domination leaves them aware of an outside force influencing them, whereas this is hidden until triggered.<br /> <br /> Seconding my appreciation of it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-13-2022, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T01:27:59-07:00","id":1490683,"title":"","content":"<b>Never Gonna Die (Death </b>\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice: Veiling<br /> <br /> Primary Spell Factor: Duration.<br /> <br /> Withstand: Resolve.</b><br /> <br /> This spell hides away a subjects sense of personal mortality, overriding all natural instincts to protect oneself from danger. They are incapable of being beaten down. Their defense each turn is penalized by spell potency. If they have the Common Sense Merit, it cannot be used to measure existential danger.<br /> The Subject is prone to take incautious actions that they would otherwise instinctively avoid in the absence of self-preservation, though they are not driven to take actions that self-preservation was not a factor in preventing. They are far less likely to drive the speed limit, look both ways at crossing, and stay cognizant of their surroundings walking home at night. They are far more likely to climb a 2 story brick building to impress a girl. <br /> <br /> <b>Add Fate</b> \u25cf: The subject finds themself presented with an opportunity each day to do something dangerously foolhardy.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Mind</b> \u25cf: The subject gains a new vice: Daredevil. They must spend one willpower each scene not to commit to a dangerous stunt that presents itself to them. With a reach, this can also add the Persistent Addicted Condition--Thrill Seeking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T10:07:46-07:00","id":1490723,"title":"","content":"Rereading Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell and got the idea for adapting a spell<br /> <br /> <b>\u01a8noi\u0248\u0254\u0258l\u0287\u0258\u042f (Matter </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice: Weaving</b><br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor: Duration</b><br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Occult, Larceny</b><br /> <br /> The mage alters the properties of a mirror or other reflective surface. While the spell is in effect, reflections in the mirror may be removed, and real objects may be put onto the reflective surface. Reflected objects have the physical shape of the object they reflect but no other properties; they have 0 durability and 1 structure, reflected Artifacts or Imbued Items have no spells or effects, reflected people have neither minds nor souls and can only be altered by Matter spells rather than Life etc.<br /> <br /> If a real object is put onto the mirror, its reflection comes off of the mirror. The space on the mirror is limited by what it reflects. It is not possible to move beyond the field of the reflective surface.<br /> <br /> When the spell ends, things may no longer move onto or off the mirror, but anything which has already done so remains where it is; real objects remain in the mirror, reflected objects outside the mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","user":"TakWrote","date":".  Edited for phrasing consistency. 08-19-2022, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T16:35:35-07:00","id":1490745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TakWrote</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1490723#post1490723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rereading Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell and got the idea for adapting a spell<br /> <br /> <b>\u01a8noi\u0248\u0254\u0258l\u0287\u0258\u042f (Matter </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice: Weaving</b><br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor: Duration</b><br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Occult, Larceny</b><br /> <br /> The mage alters the properties of a mirror or other reflective surface to permit things to pass through. While the spell is in effect, reflections in the mirror may be taken out, and real objects may be put into the reflective surface. Reflected objects have the physical shape of the object they reflect but no other properties; they have 0 durability and 1 structure, reflected Artifacts or Imbued Items have no spells or effects, reflected people have neither minds nor souls and can only be altered by Matter spells rather than Life etc. A reflected object which is removed from the field of view of the mirror it came from ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> If a real object is put into the mirror, its reflection comes out of the mirror. The space inside the mirror is limited by what it reflects. It is not possible to move beyond the field of view of the reflective surface.<br /> <br /> When the spell ends, things may no longer pass through the mirror, but anything which has already done so remains where it is; real objects remain in the mirror, reflected objects outside the mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div>This definitely can't be accomplished with Matter alone outside of the context of an Atypical Legacy Attainment or exploiting a particular Mystery, because messing with a &quot;space&quot; that only normally exists as function of how reflections work to make it actually physically permeable uses principles that don't map to messing with the material qualities of a thing alone \u2014 you'd need Space and/or some number of the Subtle Arcana for that. Other supernaturals get weird mirror powers because they're not building them from first principles (and maybe long practice) every time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T17:42:21-07:00","id":1490746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1490745#post1490745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This definitely can't be accomplished with Matter alone outside of the context of an Atypical Legacy Attainment or exploiting a particular Mystery, because messing with a &quot;space&quot; that only normally exists as function of how reflections work to make it actually physically permeable uses principles that don't map to messing with the material qualities of a thing alone \u2014 you'd need Space and/or some number of the Subtle Arcana for that. Other supernaturals get weird mirror powers because they're not building them from first principles (and maybe long practice) every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I struggled with it for a while on those grounds. I ultimately decided on Matter alone because I don't think the spell actually manipulates space any more than a spell like &quot;Ghost Gate&quot; does. It grants access to a &quot;space&quot;, but what the spell directly affects is the Matter of the reflective material and that &quot;space&quot; is more like a state of being than anything else. I think it depends a lot on how &quot;real&quot; a reflection is considered to be; if the reflection is a real property of Matter then this spell simply manipulates that in a very abstract way. It transmutes things from reflection to material and back again.<br /> <br /> If the reflection is illusory then the spell is actually creating a space and simply uses the mirror as an aesthetic; it's basically just &quot;Secret Room&quot;. Both a Space or a Matter approach could work, along very different lines.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've updated the original spell phrasing to make it clearer how I think it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26659,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","user":"TakWrote","date":".  Update on the original spell 08-19-2022, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26659-takwrote","name":"TakWrote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26659_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T15:44:57-07:00","id":1491048,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Would inverting Shared Sight still be an Unveiling practice? Might be Patterning, since that's what Apocalypse is.<br /> <br /> <b>Borrowed Goggles</b> </span><b>(</b><b>Prime</b>\u25cf)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Practice</b>: Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost</b>: 1 Mana</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Withstand</b>: Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Science, Larceny</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Rather than bestow their own understanding on others, the Mage can borrow expertise in a different Arcana. This spell allows the Mage to mimic the Ruling Mage Sights from the spell's target, allowing the caster to treat them as Ruling Mage Sights in addition to their own. Foreign Ruling Arcana use the originator\u2019s symbolism, which may be jarring for the recipient.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Fate/Spirit/Death/Mind</b> </span>\u25cf: <span style=\"color:#000000\">Can be used on other Supernaturals if the mage knows the relevant Arcana, with results up to the ST's</span> discretion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Totally useless spell:<br /> <br /> <b>Battle Tapes</b><br /> <b>(</b><b>Mind \u25cf\u25cf \u00b1 Prime \u25cf\u25cf</b>)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Expression, Craft<br /> <br /> This spell causes the subject to be constantly accompanied by a &quot;theme song&quot; appropriate to their situation at a given time. This is similar to Mage's Nimbus in that it doesn't have a direct impact on the world around it, but sentient creatures within range can subconsciously &quot;feel&quot; the music.<br /> <br /> The exact music playing is unpredictable; some individuals generate a new composition of instrumental music that shifts according to mood, others jump between facsimiles of existing songs. <br /> It also cannot be used as a &quot;danger sense&quot;, as the music reacts purely to the subject's perceptions of a situation.<br /> <br /> Edit Mark 2: Less useless spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Telekine Limbs (Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b>*Science, Medicine, Expression<br /> <br /> Twisting the principles behind Telekinesis, the Mage crafts a hollow force-simulacrum to replace a subject's lost limbs. Each application of this spell negates one Limb Wrack Tilt for its duration. This limb is functionally identical to their normal limb, but is only visible as a minor distortion of light. Attempts to inflict the Limb Wrack Tilt on a replaced limb fail. The limb may be used to block objects in much the same way a flesh-and-blood limb would, however any attack that would penetrate more than 50% of the way into a normal limb simply passes through unhindered. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The limb provides an equipment bonus equal to Potency on relevant tasks. This is limited by the applicability - only having one telekinesis-leg may present situations where the equipment bonus doesn't apply.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The limb gains a reactive sheath of light, causing it to be visually indistinguishable from flesh and blood limbs. Dissonance may still result from the lack of body heat, blood, or a hearbeat.<br /> <br /> <b>We All Lift Together (Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b>*Science, Medicine, Larceny<br /> <br /> This spell utilizes elements of Honing The Form and Degrading The Form. Rather than simply increase their own physique maiming another's, however, the Mage links several subjects together. Members of the link can, as a reflexive action, &quot;borrow&quot; up to Potency Physical Attributes from other participants. This cannot take subjects below 1 in a given Attribute, and the &quot;borrowed&quot; stats can be taken in any combination from other participants. By default, no loan of Attributes can take a subject above their Gnosis-derived maximum. <br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Subjects may exceed their Gnosis-derived limits when borrowing Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-25-2022, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:18:15-07:00","id":1491325,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Forge Talen (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Intimidating, Weaponry<br /> <br /> Mage is tearing out part of willing spirit\u2019s energy, fraying his Essence and coalescing part of his power into small trinket called Talen. This spell is usually used after negotiating with spirit in question, which agrees to cede part of itself in exchange for favors or services from the Shaman.<br /> <br /> Storyteller and player create the resulting Talen together; as general rule, power of Talen is roughly equal to single use of spirit\u2018s most powerful Influence. Storyteller may also use spirit\u2019s Numina or werewolf\u2019s Gifts for inspiration. Powers of the Talen should be linked with spirit thematically; you cannot create Talen which allows to cure wounds from spirit of pain. Player may also choose to just tear out the Essence of the spirit; Talen holds (Potency) of Essence with resonance of the spirit, which may be used with Channel Essence and alike spells.<br /> <br /> Talen exists and has semi-material form for the Duration of the spell; or until it is used or destroyed. After this, it dissolves, releasing bound spiritual energy, which returns to the original owner. This spell causes resistant lethal damage to the spirit equal to Potency of the spell. This damage is immediately healed when Talen ceases to exist. Talen has Strong sympathy to the spirit it was created from.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Spirit does not have to be willing; the spell becomes Withstood with spirit's Rank.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, 1 Mana:</b> The Duration of spell becomes Lasting, and talen persists until it is used or destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> Instead of creating new form for the Talen, shaman can immediately bind torn energy to the existing material item, which will become Talen. This item will not dissolved when it's used as Talen, but Talen is still one-use only.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> As above, but Imbued Item can be used instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> As above, but ritual space or chamber can be used instead<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Through the Eyes of Hunger (Spirit \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Empathy, Stealth<br /> <br /> <i>To rule spirits, one must understand them. And what better way to do this than to experience world as they do?</i><br /> <br /> For the Duration of the spell, mage feels world as spirit does: through the lens of hunger and need. Mage defines nature of the spirit and becomes able to feel Resonances, distinguish between Resonances which are &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature, and roughly understands how powerful Resonance for the purpose of using Channel Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Mage becomes able to sense sources of Resonances &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature from up to a mile away, like spirit does.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Mage can sense the presence of Resonances &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature from a large distance. The base range becomes (Potency)*2 miles<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>No Consequences (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Intimidation, Politics<br /> <br /> <i>One of the most fundamental truths from Primal Wild is that actions have consequences, felt long after deed is done. World remembers what was done, even if people have forgotten. But there is no truth which cannot be changed, if you are wise enough. You are above consequences.</i><br /> <br /> For the Duration of the spell, fundamental link between Flesh and Shadow is torn in the chosen area; no mundane actions in Flesh have spiritual reflections in the Shadow, and supernatural ones Clash against that spell. On the most base level this means that nothing is Resonant in the selected area, and no actions done in it produce Essence. No new spirits can arise from those actions; Rank 0 spirits will drift away from this area as soon as possible, being unable to feed on ambient Resonance. If this spell persists for long enough, it can produce Lasting effect, creating Barren; spiritually dead place, sucking the energy from those unlucky enough to enter it. This can be an Act of Hubris on Falling level, hurting the world on the fundamental level.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Area becomes practically uninhabitable for spirits, who cannot even stand this place. Every spirit must Clash to stay in the area or enter it; if he loses, he gains Spooked Condition and must exit it immediately by any means available.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 08-25-2022, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T18:31:19-07:00","id":1491385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1491325#post1491325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Forge Talen (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Intimidating, Weaponry<br /> <br /> Mage is tearing out part of willing spirit\u2019s energy, fraying his Essence and coalescing part of his power into small trinket called Talen. This spell is usually used after negotiating with spirit in question, which agrees to cede part of itself in exchange for favors or services from the Shaman.<br /> <br /> Storyteller and player create the resulting Talen together; as general rule, power of Talen is roughly equal to single use of spirit\u2018s most powerful Influence. Storyteller may also use spirit\u2019s Numina or werewolf\u2019s Gifts for inspiration. Powers of the Talen should be linked with spirit thematically; you cannot create Talen which allows to cure wounds from spirit of pain. Player may also choose to just tear out the Essence of the spirit; Talen holds (Potency) of Essence with resonance of the spirit, which may be used with Channel Essence and alike spells.<br /> <br /> Talen exists and has semi-material form for the Duration of the spell; or until it is used or destroyed. After this, it dissolves, releasing bound spiritual energy, which returns to the original owner. This spell causes resistant lethal damage to the spirit equal to Potency of the spell. This damage is immediately healed when Talen ceases to exist. Talen has Strong sympathy to the spirit it was created from.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Spirit does not have to be willing; the spell becomes Withstood with spirit's Rank.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach, 1 Mana:</b> The Duration of spell becomes Lasting, and talen persists until it is used or destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> Instead of creating new form for the Talen, shaman can immediately bind torn energy to the existing material item, which will become Talen. This item will not dissolved when it's used as Talen, but Talen is still one-use only.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> As above, but Imbued Item can be used instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> As above, but ritual space or chamber can be used instead<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Through the Eyes of Hunger (Spirit \u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Empathy, Stealth<br /> <br /> <i>To rule spirits, one must understand them. And what better way to do this than to experience world as they do?</i><br /> <br /> For the Duration of the spell, mage feels world as spirit does: through the lens of hunger and need. Mage defines nature of the spirit and becomes able to feel Resonances, distinguish between Resonances which are &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature, and roughly understands how powerful Resonance for the purpose of using Channel Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Mage becomes able to sense sources of Resonances &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature from up to a mile away, like spirit does.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> Mage can sense the presence of Resonances &quot;compatible&quot; with chosen nature from a large distance. The base range becomes (Potency)*2 miles<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>No Consequences (Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Intimidation, Politics<br /> <br /> <i>One of the most fundamental truths from Primal Wild is that actions have consequences, felt long after deed is done. World remembers what was done, even if people have forgotten. But there is no truth which cannot be changed, if you are wise enough. You are above consequences.</i><br /> <br /> For the Duration of the spell, fundamental link between Flesh and Shadow is torn in the chosen area; no mundane actions in Flesh have spiritual reflections in the Shadow, and supernatural ones Clash against that spell. On the most base level this means that nothing is Resonant in the selected area, and no actions done in it produce Essence. No new spirits can arise from those actions; Rank 0 spirits will drift away from this area as soon as possible, being unable to feed on ambient Resonance. If this spell persists for long enough, it can produce Lasting effect, creating Barren; spiritually dead place, sucking the energy from those unlucky enough to enter it. This can be an Act of Hubris on Falling level, hurting the world on the fundamental level.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Area becomes practically uninhabitable for spirits, who cannot even stand this place. Every spirit must Clash to stay in the area or enter it; if he loses, he gains Spooked Condition and must exit it immediately by any means available.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are some incredibly flavorful spells. I was wondering if <i>No Consequences</i> would force a Clash against uses of <i>Coaxing the Spirits</i> or if it would just fail because there is no ephemera to command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T04:59:18-07:00","id":1491465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1491385#post1491385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Those are some incredibly flavorful spells. I was wondering if <i>No Consequences</i> would force a Clash against uses of <i>Coaxing the Spirits</i> or if it would just fail because there is no ephemera to command.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the ephemera is here, but part of it with minimal volition is trying to get away as soon as possible. So it would probably depend on how long the spell is in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T19:08:23-07:00","id":1491546,"title":"","content":"<b>Shifting Context </b>(Space \u2022\u2022 + Mind \u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Resolve <br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Socialize, Persuasion <br /> <br /> The Mage changes the emotional context of one of the target's Sympathetic Connections, or more if resources are given to Scale. These emotional shifts cannot be something diametrically opposed to the original context, but the Mage could shift deep respect to unconditional love, or abject hatred to driving competitiveness. These changes will potentially affect the subject's First Impressions towards the connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-27-2022, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T21:07:28-07:00","id":1492066,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fencer's Capote (Fate/Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Perfecting</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Intimidation, Weaponry </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rote developed by the fencing master Zorro, as part of the Arrow's reaction against the Praetorian, seeking to oppose their cruel tactics by embodying the romantic ideals of a bold warrior.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When cast upon an item, it enchants it to invoke the concept of a powerful taunt, daring challenges to face the user mano a mano. Those that fail to Withstand the effect can only fight the user in close combat, not even considering using ranged options. This manifests in a number of ways, sometimes in recognizing a worthy challenger, other times because something made them reach the last straw on a very bad day or their mission requiring it. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most popular application is for users to enchant their swords, preferring to embody a daring swashbuckler. Some enchant a toreador's capote, favoring a combat style that incorporates some showmanship. There have been users that learned this rote and turned it on its head, enchanting trench coats and dusters, using the effect alongside magically enhanced speed and ranged weapons to kite opponents around, preferring the image of the guile hero.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Subjects feel their blood boil, detesting the holder even more, gaining the Bestial condition, lashing out at the them in sheer rage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach:</b> Subjects feel the item's movements taunt them and cannot have peace of mind until they defeat the user. Affected subjects also gain the Fixated condition, which can be resolved by defeating the user.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-01-2022, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T21:22:56-07:00","id":1492068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1492066#post1492066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fencer's Capote (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022 / Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>The \u201cGive Me That\u201d spell does something similar at Mind 3 Perfecting, so maybe Fate isn\u2019t really needed? Perhaps we could have a Add Fate \u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022 option instead, where circumstances arrange themselves so that no third party bumps into the contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Grammar 09-01-2022, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T21:33:40-07:00","id":1492071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1492068#post1492068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The \u201cGive Me That\u201d spell does something similar at Mind 3 Perfecting, so maybe Fate isn\u2019t really needed? Perhaps we could have a Add Fate \u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022 option instead, where circumstances arrange themselves so that no third party bumps into the contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I changed the formatting a bit, the idea is that it can be cast using either Arcanum, rather than both. One approach is building on the idea of <i>Give Me That</i>, the other option is to achieve the effect by utilizing Fate's domain of intent to alter it's context (from &quot;the holder can be fought&quot; to &quot;the holder can be fought in close combat&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-01-2022, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T14:00:40-07:00","id":1493130,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Little Eye (Forces \u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Unveiling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand: </b>N/A</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Empathy, Investigation, Survival</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell is extremely well know for it's ability to restore sight to those Mages without. It's other common usage is as a remote eye, absorbing and transmitting light and sending it back to to a mage. With the advent of video technology, this spell has begun to fade in popularity somewhat, but many still find it useful in other ways. This Spell when cast on a subject allows a mage to see as if they were perfectly sighted, and in the subjects position. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>+1 Reach: </b>The spell also transmits audio or tactile information. For an additional reach, it transmits both.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spell shares information between subjects, including or excluding subjects at the mage's </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">choosing. The Mage may exclude themselves from receiving information. This choice is at the time of casting of the spell, unless the Mage spends a additional reach to change the information flow at any time</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Trying my hand at a new spell, since I've been gone a while and I might be out of practice. It's fairly simple, which is most likely why no one has posted a version of it yet. (I think.)<br /> <br /> As a side bonus, what do y'all think of a Time Unveiling to see other's internal Time dilatation ie seeing other people's boredom, enjoyment or focus? I admit it's not my idea, I saw it on a mage the ascension discussion, but I don't think it ever made it's way into this forum, and it's very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 09-15-2022, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T15:04:34-07:00","id":1493135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1493130#post1493130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side bonus, what do y'all think of a Time Unveiling to see other's internal Time dilatation ie seeing other people's boredom, enjoyment or focus. I admit it's not my idea, I saw it on a mage the ascension discussion, but I don't think it ever made it's way into this forum, and it's very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I would probably allow it, but it also skirts pretty close to Mind territory without bringing a lot of Time with it. RAW, the purview of Time is &quot;Prophecy, change, postcognition, time travel, time contraction and dilation&quot;; I suppose you <i>could</i> argue for subjective perception of time being an acceptable contraction or dilation, but it feels like it would need a Mind rider, which defeats the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T09:03:10-07:00","id":1493247,"title":"","content":"Moving this here rather than flood AASQ with my potential pontificating. Does this seem reasonable, as a means to create <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XDQHlfYc7oc\" target=\"_blank\">holographic projections in distant locations</a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98tU3TUbTpo\" target=\"_blank\">trolling Pentacle-Apostate Seers?</a><br /> <br /> <b>Telepresence</b> (Forces \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf + Mind \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Science, Stealth<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's useful to be seen, but imprudent to truly be present. This spell is functionally identical to Psychic Projection, except that the Projection is visible on the material plane via a hologram-avatar. The subject also perceives the world normally, as opposed to the distorted view normally provided by Twilight.<br /> <br /> The subject's avatar is visually indistinguishable from the real thing, but cannot physically interact with objects. The appearance is determined at the time of casting and can be anything within the scope of Scale and imagination, but must be canceled and reactivated to be altered. Attempts to touch or directly interact with the avatar will likely result in Dissonance if done in the presence of Sleepers, as will drastically inhuman or implausable avatars.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> by spending a point of Mana during casting, the avatar is infused with a limited framework of telekinetic force. The subject can selectively interact with objects, but only has an effective Strength and Dexterity of 1. This has the side-benefit of reducing the chance of Dissonance, since the avatar can now perform simple niceties like shake hands. The subject can only engage in one interaction at a time, and must be aware of the interaction to exert this telekinetic field. Unexpected object will still pass through them, as will anything moving at combat speeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Space</b> \u25cf\u25cf: The avatar is spawned at a location dictated by whatever Sympathetic Connections are used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 09-18-2022, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-21T16:07:09-07:00","id":1495383,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Tranquil Vigil (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Perfecting </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Withstand:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stamina</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Recommended Rote Skills:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Empathy, Expression, Medicine</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A rote that eases the passing of those on death's door, ending their suffering quicker and peacefully. It can only be used on those who are suffering from aggravated damage, halving the time between bleedout for each level of Potency. The convalescent also gains the Palliated condition, which spares them of any pain or wound penalties, and they start feeling at peace with their approaching death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There exists a Stygian entity that wanders the Tellurian, called Someone To Watch Over Us. He only appears to those dying alone, offering them a cigarette before lighting his own. He then places his hand atop theirs, or holds their hand or places it on their shoulder, putting them at ease. He doesn't say a word, but stays with them until their time comes, then vanishes. This rote was discovered inscribed on a subject's cigarette and its mudras are the entity's gestures. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While its combat potential has been acknowledged, its very rarely used, as practitioners feel its a disservice to the Truth it represents.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+1 Reach:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The time between damage ticks is instead reduced by a quarter per Potency.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-21-2022, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T07:22:02-08:00","id":1496308,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Everyman's Luck (Fate \u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice:</b> Compelling</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Withstand:</b> Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Recommended Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Streetwise, Subterfuge</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A spell that brings fortune back into the neutral state that permeates everyday life, neither overly good or bad, just average.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The subject's dramatic failures on mundane rolls become normal failures and their exceptional successes transform into regular successes. Th\u00e9archs have used it to stop skilled orators from utterly captivating a crowd for the Seer's agenda. Guardians employ it to delay those pursuing dangerous research, preventing them from uncovering the breakthroughs that shortens the process. Arrows have utilized it to weaken enemy combatants, gunslingers becoming unable to shoot while </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">acrobatically </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">maneuvering around the battlefield.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+<b>2 Reach:</b> The spell also affects supernatural powers. This is sometimes employed by Arrows to ensure their enemies can't pierce their defenses with exceptionally well constructed Imagos and Mystagogues have been known to deploy it on rivals to delay summonings.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-06-2022, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T07:46:47-08:00","id":1496310,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Astral Pathway (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Empathy<br /> <br /> The Mage intertwines distant regions of the Astral Realms, allowing him to use symbolic proximity as a substitute for &quot;physical&quot; movement. For each dot of [Potency], the Mage can establish one relatively specific symbol, such as &quot;Cars&quot;, &quot;Anger&quot; or &quot;Dogs&quot;. if he comes across one of these symbols in the Astral, he can effectively teleport to the immediate vicinity of any of the established symbols as an Instant Action. This only allows the Mage to form pathways between Oneiroi, and there must be a significantly firm, clear or intuitive semiotic connection between the symbols used. The Mage can teleport towards a specific instance of a symbol whose existence he is aware of, but does not inherently know if the symbol still occupies the same coordinates in the Astral, or whether the spell will bring him closer to his goals.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The symbols can be broader, such as &quot;Vehicles&quot;, &quot;Emotions&quot; or &quot;Animals&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The semiotic connections can be more flexible, abstract or esoteric.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach or +2 Reach:</b> The Mage can travel through the Temenos and Anima Mundi, respectively.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Masked Significance (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Expression, Subterfuge, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The Mage hides the true meaning of the target's actions so that the latter appears to be doing something else. While Duration remains active, each dot of Potency can be used to make a roll of [Attribute + Skill] be interpreted by observers as a different combination of [Attribute + Skill]. This also applies to rolls based on [Attribute + Attribute], such as Strength + Stamina to lift or break objects. There must be a relatively significant proximity between the original meaning of the action and the meaning which the Mage wants others to see. For example: it is possible to make an attempt at seduction (Presence + Persuasion) be seen as a threat of violence (Presence + Intimidation), but the Mage cannot make observers think of it as attempted homicide with a gun (Dexterity + Firearms). Supernatural means of piercing this spell will trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can make an action appear to be something wildly different from what it actually is, as long as there is the barest symbolic connection between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-06-2022, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T16:49:01-08:00","id":1496340,"title":"","content":"I'm iffy about the Practice, and on how the Life/Death Reach works. Any suggestions?<br /> <br /> <b>Reduced to Atoms</b> (Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Academics, Brawl<br /> <br /> Why destroy when you can recycle? This spell is a favorite for those resource-conscious Mages who lack long-term attachments to their tools. It also has uses in drawing out impurities in base materials used for crafting, making it a common tool for craftsmen.<br /> <br /> The target of this spell is transformed into [Potency] categories of it\u2019s constituent makeup - a stainless steel knife can be transformed into a lump of chromium and a lump of iron, for example, or wine be filtered into water, ethanol, glycerol and polysaccharides. Milk and sugar can be unstirred from coffee. By default, this spell does not cause matter to change states, and as such it is prudent to prepare separate containers for liquid separation. Solids are transformed into rough spheres of the designated materials, while gasses simply disperse unless otherwise contained.<br /> <br /> If used on an animated entity such as a Golem, the spell provokes a Clash of Wills with the entity's creator.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Rendered matter can be shifted one step along the solid-liquid-gas gradient. This change is enforced for the Duration of the spell, after which point normal physics reassert themselves. For two Reach, they can shift two steps.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Solids can be transformed into simple shapes - cubes, spheres, icosahedrons, and the like. This is often referred to as \u201cdicing\u201d the original object.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death or Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf:</b> This spell can be used on corpses and living beings, respectively. If used on the living, it is Withstood by Stamina, and does [Potency] points of damage, in addition to drawing out the desired materials. Treat an animated corpse -such as those produced by Quicken Corpse or possessed by an ephemeral entity- as a Golem for the purposes of Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-06-2022, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T17:03:28-08:00","id":1496341,"title":"","content":"Hmm, yeah the Practice is really hard. I\u2019d actually say Fraying, if the component parts are kept the exactly the same as the ones used to make it. For alloys and dissolved solids, it should be fine, but I\u2019d say if a chemical reaction took place, then you would need a reach to separate into back into components. Or maybe not, it just feels easier to draw the salt out of sea water than the wood out of a hammer, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T17:10:33-08:00","id":1496346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496340#post1496340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm iffy about the Practice, and on how the Life/Death Reach works. Any suggestions?<br /> <br /> <b>Reduced to Atoms</b> (Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning (Should it be Unraveling?)<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Academics, Brawl<br /> <br /> Why destroy when you can recycle? This spell is a favorite for those resource-conscious Mages who lack long-term attachments to their tools. It also has uses in drawing out impurities in base materials used for crafting, making it a common tool for craftsmen.<br /> <br /> The target of this spell is transformed into [Potency] categories of it\u2019s constituent makeup - a stainless steel knife can be transformed into a lump of chromium and a lump of iron, for example, or wine be filtered into water, ethanol, glycerol and polysaccharides. Milk and sugar can be unstirred from coffee. By default, this spell does not cause matter to change states, and as such it is prudent to prepare separate containers for liquid separation. Solids are transformed into rough spheres of the designated materials, while gasses simply disperse unless otherwise contained.<br /> <br /> If used on an animated entity such as a Golem, the spell provokes a Clash of Wills with the entity's creator.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Rendered matter can be shifted one step along the solid-liquid-gas gradient. This change is enforced for the Duration of the spell, after which point normal physics reassert themselves. For two Reach, they can shift two steps.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> Solids can be transformed into simple shapes - cubes, spheres, icosahedrons, and the like. This is often referred to as \u201cdicing\u201d the original object.<br /> <br /> <b>Add Death or Life \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf:</b> This spell can be used on corpses and living beings, respectively. If used on the living, it is Withstood by Stamina, and does [Potency] points of damage, in addition to drawing out the desired materials. Treat an animated corpse -such as those produced by Quicken Corpse or possessed by an ephemeral entity- as a Golem for the purposes of Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its definitely an Unraveling, since its breaking down the phenomena into its constituent parts. The Life and Death Reaches should work similarly, but resisted by Stamina for the living. <br /> <br /> The first problem is that a human body will have, on average, to quote FMA:<br /> <br /> Water: 35 liters, Carbon: 20 kg, Ammonia: 4 liters, Lime:1.5 kg, Phosphrus: 800 g, salt: 250g, saltpeter:100g, Sulfer: 80g, Fluorine: 7.5 g, iron: 5.6 g, Silicon: 3g, and 15 other elements in small quantities..<br /> <br /> Which means that you might need to cast it multiple times to break it down to the granularity you are aiming for. On one hand, it means an imbued item with this spell will act like the recycler grenade from Prey, allowing for a useful tool to improvise materials on the field and a quick way to unblock passages.<br /> <br /> However, it can also be used to do horrific things, such as instantly dessicating a person by removing the water from the victim's body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T17:11:50-08:00","id":1496347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496341#post1496341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, yeah the Practice is really hard. I\u2019d actually say Fraying, if the component parts are kept the exactly the same as the ones used to make it. For alloys and dissolved solids, it should be fine, but I\u2019d say if a chemical reaction took place, then you would need a reach to separate into back into components. Or maybe not, it just feels easier to draw the salt out of sea water than the wood out of a hammer, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd almost say use Forces for the chemical reactions, although that's one of those bits where Matter and Forces blur for me.<br /> <br /> I'd actually find the sea water and the hammer to be about even. The hammer is composed of fairly distinct parts, with the head being a fairly durable material and the haft being a resilent but yeilding material. Sea water, in contrast, is water-impregnated-with-salt, which requires more visualization of how that's possible. Just my perception of the problem tho, as conceptually &quot;sea is salty water&quot; IS simpler than &quot;Tool is composed of these materials in this configuration&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496346#post1496346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its definitely an Unraveling, since its breaking down the phenomena into its constituent parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sort of is, but it's primarily shifting things from one state to another. Unraveling or Fraying seems to be the consensus (of two) so far, so it's definately a destructive practice by that metric...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496346#post1496346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Life and Death Reaches should work similarly, but resisted by Stamina for the living.<br /> <br /> The first problem is that a human body will have, on average, to quote FMA:<br /> <br /> Water: 35 liters, Carbon: 20 kg, Ammonia: 4 liters, Lime:1.5 kg, Phosphrus: 800 g, salt: 250g, saltpeter:100g, Sulfer: 80g, Fluorine: 7.5 g, iron: 5.6 g, Silicon: 3g, and 15 other elements in small quantities.<br /> <br /> Which means that you might need to cast it multiple times to break it down to the granularity you are aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I also intended it to be a symbolic transformation. You could, for example, disentagle bones or blood from flesh and organs. The Milk-and-sugar-from-coffee was meant to be an example of that, although it also serves as a nice &quot;piss off parables, I'm a Mage!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496346#post1496346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, it means an imbued item with this spell will act like the recycler grenade from Prey, allowing for a useful tool to improvise materials on the field and a quick way to unblock passages.</div> </div> </div> </div> I hadn't thought of making a grenade out of it, that's neat. Also a cool disintigration-ray Wand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1496346#post1496346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it can also be used to do horrific things, such as instantly dessicating a person by removing the water from the victim's body.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=i&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.penny-arcade.com%2Fcomic%2F2011%2F12%2F02%2Fthe-conflux-part-five&amp;psig=AOvVaw0DPW5_TzSTI-tk3VuZZn0M&amp;ust=1667872517316000&amp;source=images&amp;cd=vfe&amp;ved=0CA0QjRxqFwoTCLDA1rn7mvsCFQAAAAAdAAAAABAE\" target=\"_blank\">To saaaaaand.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 11-06-2022, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T19:51:58-08:00","id":1499111,"title":"","content":"Nerdsniper<br /> Prime 3 Fraying<br /> This spell scribes itself into the Pattern or Nimbus of a target and waits for some mage to inspect the target with Magesight, whereupon it acts as a basilisk spell and attacks the viewer. The more they opened up their mage sight to perceive it, the more it can ravage them: if the spell succeeds in dealing damage, add one more per arcana of mage sight they had active","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T07:43:25-08:00","id":1499520,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been researching how to effectively layer different types of spells for protection and the spells \u201cGrave Misfortune\u201d and \u201cAlter Conductivity\u201d have caught my eye due to how they mechanically work. Based on the aforementioned spells, I\u2019m wondering if the below is a valid spell effect per Creative Thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aetheric Alteration (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Fraying or Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina or N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The Mage enhances or diminishes the effects celestial magic from the Aether has upon the Subject, changing the manner in which the Subject is affected by fire. For each level of Potency, this spell causes the Subject to receive an additional point of fire damage or reduces fire damage taken by one.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can alter the effects of other forms of energy, such as electricity, heat, sound, or even light. Each additional form of energy is an extra Reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea is to have a Forces Shielding spell that protects the Subject from fire, granting immunity to mundane fire, while provoking a Clash of Wills against supernatural fire. Then, adding the above spell as a back-up layer for when the Clash of Wills fails and there is a need to reduce the incoming damage. <br /> <br /> The addition of a Fraying option was to simply reduce the need for an entirely separate spell that is mechanically very similar. A 1:1 damage to Potency ratio was chosen based on \u201cGrave Misfortune\u201d as even though this new spell has a more restrictive scope of damage sources, a 2:1 ratio seemed too strong balance wise (I believe the 2:1 ratio from \u201cAlter Conductivity\u201d is based on the Transform Energy chart and the fact that each level of electricity damage is a difference of two bashing damage).<br /> <br /> So, the overall question, is this a viable spell, or what needs to change to make it one? If it is viable, then I imagine it would also work for the other Arcanum and their purviews? For example, a Prime spell to increase or decrease Magic damage, or Spirit to increase or decrease the damage from Essence effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27725-immortalmage","name":"Immortalmage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T10:02:27-08:00","id":1499533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Immortalmage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1499520#post1499520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been researching how to effectively layer different types of spells for protection and the spells \u201cGrave Misfortune\u201d and \u201cAlter Conductivity\u201d have caught my eye due to how they mechanically work. Based on the aforementioned spells, I\u2019m wondering if the below is a valid spell effect per Creative Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aetheric Alteration (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Fraying or Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina or N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Science, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The Mage enhances or diminishes the effects celestial magic from the Aether has upon the Subject, changing the manner in which the Subject is affected by fire. For each level of Potency, this spell causes the Subject to receive an additional point of fire damage or reduces fire damage taken by one.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The Mage can alter the effects of other forms of energy, such as electricity, heat, sound, or even light. Each additional form of energy is an extra Reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea is to have a Forces Shielding spell that protects the Subject from fire, granting immunity to mundane fire, while provoking a Clash of Wills against supernatural fire. Then, adding the above spell as a back-up layer for when the Clash of Wills fails and there is a need to reduce the incoming damage.<br /> <br /> The addition of a Fraying option was to simply reduce the need for an entirely separate spell that is mechanically very similar. A 1:1 damage to Potency ratio was chosen based on \u201cGrave Misfortune\u201d as even though this new spell has a more restrictive scope of damage sources, a 2:1 ratio seemed too strong balance wise (I believe the 2:1 ratio from \u201cAlter Conductivity\u201d is based on the Transform Energy chart and the fact that each level of electricity damage is a difference of two bashing damage).<br /> <br /> So, the overall question, is this a viable spell, or what needs to change to make it one? If it is viable, then I imagine it would also work for the other Arcanum and their purviews? For example, a Prime spell to increase or decrease Magic damage, or Spirit to increase or decrease the damage from Essence effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>So first off the spell is Weaving, like Alter Conductivity. I\u2019d argue the spell is basically Alter Conductivity through Forces, except with Fire as it\u2019s base. Something I just noticed however, is that Alter Conductivity doesn\u2019t say whether or not the subject has to be non living material, which is how I assumed it worked up until now. With living subjects that are valid as the target, I\u2019d say the spell is valid. Otherwise, I\u2019d say you would need to target the energy instead.<br /> <br /> Edit:Clarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-13-2022, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T10:55:26-08:00","id":1499545,"title":"","content":"I think it can target the subject, since its essentially <i>Alter Combustability</i> . This could have a Reach effect to make them catch fire when in a place with Extreme Heat or spontaneously catch fire after Stamina turns of continuous physical activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T11:10:05-08:00","id":1499665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1499545#post1499545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it can target the subject, since its essentially <i>Alter Combustability</i> . This could have a Reach effect to make them catch fire when in a place with Extreme Heat or spontaneously catch fire after Stamina turns of continuous physical activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like that as a Reach effect, good idea. <br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27725-immortalmage","name":"Immortalmage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T05:11:34-07:00","id":1506301,"title":"","content":"Hypothetical spell - <u>As Beautiful As You Are On The Inside</u> - some Mind/Life combo that makes &quot;good&quot; people pretty and &quot;bad&quot; people ugly? Striking Looks is the simplest way to model the effect mechanics, but I can't quite think of how to easily convert &quot;spell analyzes target's personality and sorts them between binary categories based on the caster's moral biases&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T06:08:48-07:00","id":1506302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1506301#post1506301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hypothetical spell - <u>As Beautiful As You Are On The Inside</u> - some Mind/Life combo that makes &quot;good&quot; people pretty and &quot;bad&quot; people ugly? Striking Looks is the simplest way to model the effect mechanics, but I can't quite think of how to easily convert &quot;spell analyzes target's personality and sorts them between binary categories based on the caster's moral biases&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a finicky feat to attempt. For my own use, I\u2019d just make a Life 3 + Mind 1 spell that reads someone\u2019s Virtue and/or Vice and shapes their face, posture, etc accordingly, and call it a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T13:02:59-07:00","id":1506340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1506302#post1506302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite a finicky feat to attempt. For my own use, I\u2019d just make a Life 3 + Mind 1 spell that reads someone\u2019s Virtue and/or Vice and shapes their face, posture, etc accordingly, and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how Mutable Mask works, you could get it down to Life 2. Since I imagine it\u2019s just the appearance that matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T13:55:04-07:00","id":1507118,"title":"","content":"I'd like some feedback on the following:<br /> <br /> Shadow Binding (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) <br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> A blanket of shadow that envelopes the target. Treated as a grapple with Strength = Potency. Every turn the target can roll to break free with Strength + Athletics/Brawl vs. Potency + Death. If the target succeeds they break free. Otherwise they take 1 Bashing damage from the effort. They suffer the immobilized Tilt until they break free.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T15:44:49-07:00","id":1507124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1507118#post1507118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some feedback on the following:<br /> <br /> Shadow Binding (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> A blanket of shadow that envelopes the target. Treated as a grapple with Strength = Potency. Every turn the target can roll to break free with Strength + Athletics/Brawl vs. Potency + Death. If the target succeeds they break free. Otherwise they take 1 Bashing damage from the effort. They suffer the immobilized Tilt until they break free.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool idea. I'd maybe specify that there needs to be some deep shadow within the spell's area.<br /> <br /> I'd probably say breaking free should just be resisted by Potency rather than contested and the language should probably be 'As an instant action...'<br /> <br /> I'd also consider applying Blinded rather than dealing bashing damage. Or both with a Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T17:20:47-07:00","id":1507133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1507118#post1507118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some feedback on the following:<br /> <br /> Shadow Binding (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> <br /> A blanket of shadow that envelopes the target. Treated as a grapple with Strength = Potency. Every turn the target can roll to break free with Strength + Athletics/Brawl vs. Potency + Death. If the target succeeds they break free. Otherwise they take 1 Bashing damage from the effort. They suffer the immobilized Tilt until they break free.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest the spell conform a bit more to the regular grappling rules. The most recent print is in <b>Deviant</b>, so building off that...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shadowbind (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Brawl, Athletics, Crafts<br /> <br /> The mage conjures blankets and bands of shadow to envelop the target. This initiates a grapple; the caster chooses one grapple option, which the shadows constantly attempt to apply to the target for its Duration. The chosen option gets applied immediately as the grapple starts, as if having achieved an Exceptional Success in the Grab action. Use the caster's own Initiative, but for the Grappling action, apply the spell's Potency as successes.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The caster assigns one additional grapple option per extra Reach.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Access the &quot;Seal Yantra&quot; grapple option; if the grappled target is a mage, she cannot access any Yantras other than personas.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: When using the Disarm option, the disarmed weapon gets shunted off into Death-Twilight and destroyed as per Death 3 &quot;Ghost Gate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T17:34:02-07:00","id":1507135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1507133#post1507133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd suggest the spell conform a bit more to the regular grappling rules. The most recent print is in <b>Deviant</b>, so building off that...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shadowbind (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Brawl, Athletics, Crafts<br /> <br /> The mage conjures blankets and bands of shadow to envelop the target. This initiates a grapple; the caster chooses one grapple option, which the shadows constantly attempt to apply to the target for its Duration. The chosen option gets applied immediately as the grapple starts, as if having achieved an Exceptional Success in the Grab action. Use the caster's own Initiative, but for the Grappling action, apply the spell's Potency as successes.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The caster assigns one additional grapple option per extra Reach.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Access the &quot;Seal Yantra&quot; grapple option; if the grappled target is a mage, she cannot access any Yantras other than personas.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: When using the Disarm option, the disarmed weapon gets shunted off into Death-Twilight and destroyed as per Death 3 &quot;Ghost Gate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that last reach is <u>mean</u>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T11:04:26-07:00","id":1507298,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone. I've decided to settle on the following:<br /> <br /> Shadow Binding (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Brawl, Athletics, Crafts<br /> <br /> In an area with deep shadows, the mage conjures blankets and bands of shadow to envelop the target. This initiates a grapple; the caster chooses one grapple option, which the shadows constantly attempt to apply to the target for its Duration. The chosen option gets applied immediately as the grapple starts, as if having achieved an Exceptional Success in the Grab action. Use the caster's own Initiative, but for the Grappling action, apply the spell's Potency as successes.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The caster assigns one additional grapple option per extra Reach.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Access the &quot;Seal Yantra&quot; grapple option; if the grappled target is a mage, she cannot access any Yantras other than personas.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: When using the Disarm option, the disarmed weapon gets shunted off into Death-Twilight and destroyed as per Death 3 &quot;Ghost Gate.&quot;\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T12:53:26-07:00","id":1507309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1507298#post1507298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks everyone. I've decided to settle on the following:<br /> <br /> Shadow Binding (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Brawl, Athletics, Crafts<br /> <br /> In an area with deep shadows, the mage conjures blankets and bands of shadow to envelop the target. This initiates a grapple; the caster chooses one grapple option, which the shadows constantly attempt to apply to the target for its Duration. The chosen option gets applied immediately as the grapple starts, as if having achieved an Exceptional Success in the Grab action. Use the caster's own Initiative, but for the Grappling action, apply the spell's Potency as successes.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The caster assigns one additional grapple option per extra Reach.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: Access the &quot;Seal Yantra&quot; grapple option; if the grappled target is a mage, she cannot access any Yantras other than personas.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: When using the Disarm option, the disarmed weapon gets shunted off into Death-Twilight and destroyed as per Death 3 &quot;Ghost Gate.&quot;\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of the Lasombra's Obtenebration, I like that.<br /> <br /> The first Reach option is more deadly than dedicated damage spells. If you can Control Weapon and Damage each turn, that would lead to a massive damage spike. If it instead requires conditions to choose which maneuver to apply, it needs something to justify it being a &quot;smart spell&quot;. The third Reach option is terrifying in a very cool way, but it would need something to justify it knowing what a weapon is and to throw it into Twilight.<br /> <br /> The second Reach option might not cover every scenario where a yantra could be used. Lets say the mage seals someone from using their palm lines as a material yantra for a Fate buff, how is it doing that, by binding their hands with an Arm Wrack ? What if they want to use High Speech or say say a haiku, how is it sealing their mouths without also applying Mute ?<br /> <br /> With all that in mind, I recommend that the spell instead applies the Immobilized tilt, with the default binding of their arms and legs, with Potency acting as the shadow's grapple penalty (where Durability would normally be applied). Reach options could include the target being hog tied or Muted.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T17:22:55-07:00","id":1508944,"title":"","content":"Worthy mods for balance. I'll rewrite when I get the chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T20:25:20-07:00","id":1515820,"title":"","content":"So, I came up with this spell for a Legacy that I've been working on that I might post up latter, but I could use some help in refining this spell. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Motion Tracker </span></span>(Forces \u2022)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Knowing</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Survival, Empathy</span></span><br /> <br /> Forces mage sight is able to sense motion, but some mage have deemed it necessary to replicate and refine this feature into a proper spell, to better keep track of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage now knows the precise vector and strength of any motion in her sensory range. The mage can negate the cumulative dice penalty from multiple attackers up to potency, provided that the attackers are physical in nature (ghosts and spirits pay heed to a different set of paraphysical laws). Supernatural effects that augment stealth can challenge this spell with a clash of wills, though effects that rely on esoteric means such as shifting into twilight or adopting ephemeral qualities might defeat this spell entirely. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Death, Mind, or Spirit 1: Motion Tracker can now track ephemeral entities of the appropriate type while manifested or on twilight (Death for ghosts, Mind for Goetia, Spirit for Spirits)<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: the mage can now reflexively backtrack the trajectory of any thrown or fired object to its point of origin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach: The mage can now apply her Defense to firearms.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T15:24:31-07:00","id":1515968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lone Gunman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1515820#post1515820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I came up with this spell for a Legacy that I've been working on that I might post up latter, but I could use some help in refining this spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Motion Tracker </span></span>(Forces \u2022)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Knowing</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Survival, Empathy</span></span><br /> <br /> Forces mage sight is able to sense motion, but some mage have deemed it necessary to replicate and refine this feature into a proper spell, to better keep track of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mage now knows the precise vector and strength of any motion in her sensory range. The mage can negate the cumulative dice penalty from multiple attackers up to potency, provided that the attackers are physical in nature (ghosts and spirits pay heed to a different set of paraphysical laws). Supernatural effects that augment stealth can challenge this spell with a clash of wills, though effects that rely on esoteric means such as shifting into twilight or adopting ephemeral qualities might defeat this spell entirely. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Add Death, Mind, or Spirit 1: Motion Tracker can now track ephemeral entities of the appropriate type while manifested or on twilight (Death for ghosts, Mind for Goetia, Spirit for Spirits)<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: the mage can now reflexively backtrack the trajectory of any thrown or fired object to its point of origin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+2 Reach: The mage can now apply her Defense to firearms.</span></span><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be area of spell, not sensory range. Also, the +2 reach option to apply defense against firearms is, imo, too much for a 1-dot spell and doesn't really work: sure, you know the vector of the bullet once it enters sensory/area of spell, but you still can't actually react fast enough to do anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T04:31:51-07:00","id":1517152,"title":"","content":"The <b>Reaching</b> spell (Spirit 3) mimics the <u>Reaching</u> Manifestation with its base effect, and the <u>Gateway</u> Manifestation with its +1 Reach effect. <b>World Walker</b> (Spirit 4) mimics the <u>Gauntlet Breach</u> Manifestation with its base effect, and can do the <u>Materialize</u> Manifestation with its +1 Reach effect. <b>Twilit Body</b> (Spirit 4) can be framed as granting the <u>Twilight Form</u> Manifestation to non-ephemerals. <b><u>Familiar</u></b> (Spirit 4) is self-explanatory.<br /> <br /> Then what about other ephemeral Manifestations?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Discorporation (Spirit 4)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Patterning<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Stamina<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Stealth, Medicine, Occult<br /> <br /> The shaman transmutes the subject's body and all her immediate possessions into a thousand shards of visible ephemera, spread within a space up to the spell's Scale (Area). What shape the shards take depend on the caster's Nimbus and Shadow Name; a mage calling himself Stratos and accompanied by stormy skies could Discorporate into a rolling carpet of thick clouds and static electricity.<br /> The subject retains all her traits, but cannot take Physical actions other than moving, fleeing, and hiding. As she is made of ephemera in this state, only attacks and restraints that work on Spirit-Twilight can affect her.<br /> When the spell's Duration expires, the subject chooses where her body reforms along the space her Discorporated body is spread over.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The mage can cast this spell as a Reflexive action, but only with herself as the subject.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject can attempt to cross the Gauntlet with a Stamina + Occult roll, with an Equipment bonus up to the spell's Potency.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The subject's ephemeral mass is fully Materialized; use the <u>Swarms</u> rule as the sidebar in <b>Mage</b>.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The subject is healed when she reforms. Each level of Potency removes one lethal damage, two bashing damage, or one Physical Tilt.<br /> <b>Add Space \u2022\u2022</b>: The mage can transport the subject as he Discorporates to a location of her choosing, within her sensory range. This can be across the Gauntlet; the spell becomes Withstood by the lower of Stamina or Gauntlet Strength. Sympathetic Range can be applied.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gauntlet Projection (Spirit 3)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Larceny, Occult, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> The shaman alters the angles of the Gauntlet around her body, such that it projects a remote visual image of herself. The image can be placed at any three-dimensional point within the spell's Area. The mage can attempt to project the image across the Gauntlet, if she can perceive it. This makes the spell <b>Withstood</b> by Gauntlet Strength.<br /> The caster can manipulate the image's movements as an Instant Mental action; without this, the image mimics her own movements.<br /> The image rarely appears as the mage's exact form. It will reflect her Shadow Name and Dream Form, albeit within recognizable range.<br /> The spell expires prematurely if someone touches the image, making it disperse immediately. Even without touch, Perception rolls could discover that the something is wrong with the image.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The image expands to all five senses. Merely touching this image does not end the spell, as the touched image promptly rebuilds itself. An attack however will still prematurely end the spell, and the image will appear to die.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: The caster can radically change the image's appearance. Forming the image in shapes unfamiliar to the mage himself prompts a Wits + Expression roll; the mage's own Dream Form and the shape of his own Familiars (if any) are always considered familiar.<br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022</b>: The image is perceptible only to people meeting certain criteria, selected by the mage. It could be broad as &quot;Women&quot;, or narrow as &quot;Former widows who married newly&quot;.<br /> <b>Add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The image gains a semblance of life, registering as being alive to mundane observation and even Active Mage Sight (Life).<br /> <b>Add Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: Spend 1+ Mana points. The image may undertake a number of Physical actions equal to spent Mana.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Riding (Spirit 3)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor</b>: Duration<br /> <b>Withstand</b>: Composure<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills</b>: Drive, Intimidation, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The shaman sends out her spirit to 'ride' and fetter to a subject as many spirits do. Summarize the caster's Nimbus as one or two words; this spell can only target subjects that are Resonant with the caster's Nimbus as such. The subject gains a variant of the Urged Condition, with the caster in place of the ephemeral entity. The caster rolls whatever Attribute + Skill dice pool would be appropriate to her approach for reading thoughts or compelling actions, contested as usual, but with an Equipment bonus up to the spell's Potency.<br /> Should the mage target the subject with something that costs Essence (e.g. using a fetish, giving away Essence via the Channel Essence spell), she uses 1 point less.<br /> Reading thoughts or compelling actions require the subject to be within the caster's sensory range at the moment. Sympathetic Range can be applied.<br /> The spell expires prematurely if the subject somehow becomes not Resonant with the mage's Nimbus.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach</b>: If the mage has spirit Familiars, he may use their Influences instead of his Nimbus. At increased Scale, he can target each subject with a different Resonance (including his Nimbus).<br /> <b>+1 Reach and add Life \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: By successfully compelling an action, the mage can reshape parts of the subject's body in ways that best enable the compulsion (using the guidelines for the Many Faces and Transform Life spells). A changed feature reverts when the mage wills it, the subject succeeds on a Stamina + Composure roll, or when the spell ends.<br /> <b>Add Space \u2022\u2022\u2022</b>: The mage can use Strong or better sympathetic connections as the spell's vector, instead of Resonances. With <b>+1 Reach</b>, Medium connections are available too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  There was a redundant Reach effect that I intended to fold into the main effect 07-04-2023, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T20:23:21-07:00","id":1517191,"title":"","content":"Any suggestions for a spell to do an Obi Wan/Professor X style mental projection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 07-04-2023, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T20:50:29-07:00","id":1517193,"title":"","content":"<u>Co-Location</u> would be the most basic. Sympathetic Range <u>Hallucination</u> or a beefed up Sympathetic Range <u>Control Light/Sound</u> would also do<br /> <br /> Edit: also, <u>Psychic Projection</u>. Possibly with a Forces or Spirit conjunctive effect to make the projection visible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-04-2023, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:01:15-07:00","id":1517274,"title":"","content":"Hey all !<br /> <br /> For reasons of storage, I've had to create a new Google document holding <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1J0cRG3FoML35hqvMOrpHVfn6JfhegDThswwdyWth1a8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">a lot of the new spells created here</a>. It's far from up to date but a lot of them are here. I probably won't make it editable by everyone because it could result in quite the hefty load on my Drive, but that's always a start !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T07:49:05-07:00","id":1520818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1517274#post1517274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all !<br /> <br /> For reasons of storage, I've had to create a new Google document holding <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1J0cRG3FoML35hqvMOrpHVfn6JfhegDThswwdyWth1a8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">a lot of the new spells created here</a>. It's far from up to date but a lot of them are here. I probably won't make it editable by everyone because it could result in quite the hefty load on my Drive, but that's always a start !</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to allow suggested edits, i would be happy to add a few suggestions, also I noticed the Making and Unmaking sections for Death are together, but only Making spells follow.<br /> <br /> As it happens i wrote an Unmaking spell today<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Life without End (Death \u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7)<br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary factor: duration<br /> Suggested rotes: occult, medicine, survival<br /> <br /> Life naturally comes to an end, however with this spell the caster removes the ending from the subject.<br /> <br /> Though their body can still be injured and heal at the normal rate, their soul never leaves their body. Thus after taking what would normally be lethal damage the body continues to move under the owner's control, similar to a zombie controlled by their own ghost.<br /> <br /> However the subject has not died and will continue to suffer pain as long as their damaged body is still attached.<br /> <br /> Even catastrophic bodily damage can not kill them, however this may be a fate worse than death, as a body cremated and scattered to the wind is not particularly useful and would be very difficult to reassemble.<br /> \u200b</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added i dent to the spell description 08-17-2023, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T02:06:40-07:00","id":1520928,"title":"","content":"Resonant Focus <b>Prime</b> (\u00b7\u00b7)<br /> <br /> <b>Practice</b>: Ruling<br /> <b>Primary factor</b>: duration<br /> Suggested rote skills: Persuasion, Crafts, Survival<br /> <br /> The resonance of an activity naturally imprints on the world, by means of this spell the subject can reinforce and focus that resonance into their soul.<br /> <br /> When a subject under the effect of this spell perform a Legacy Oblation, the mana produced is infused with resonance appropriate to the Oblation (which is usable as a +1 persona yantra).<br /> <br /> Each act is limited to the spell's potency in resonace generated, so if the Oblation (or other action) would generate 3 mana, but the spell only has potency 1, you get 1 resonant mana and 2 normal mana, requiring another Oblation to generate more resonant mana.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 reach</b>: When a subject of this spell scoures their pattern for mana the mana they gain is infused with the resonance of the act (self-sacrifice for lethal damage, strength for reducing the attribute).<br /> <br /> <b>+2 reach</b>: the subject may build up resonance in their soul by performing resonant actions. This may be released by flaring their Nimbus\u2020<br /> <br /> \u2020i am not sure what this would do, apart from attracting spirits? Or producing a burst of essence?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  added some spell details and formatting 08-19-2023, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T09:08:47-07:00","id":1521511,"title":"","content":"What would be acceptable/logical Arcana combinations to recreate <u>Acceleration</u> without using Time? Mind+Forces or Mind+Life are my default - Mind to allow the subject to think at an accelerated speed, and Forces or Life to reinforce the body while optimizing synaptic responses and movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T10:23:50-07:00","id":1521515,"title":"","content":"Mind + Space? Nothing quite like moving \u201cfaster\u201d by reducing the distance you have to travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T11:30:09-07:00","id":1523313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1521511#post1521511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be acceptable/logical Arcana combinations to recreate <u>Acceleration</u> without using Time? Mind+Forces or Mind+Life are my default - Mind to allow the subject to think at an accelerated speed, and Forces or Life to reinforce the body while optimizing synaptic responses and movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use a Patterning of Life and Forces, become light and therefore move at the speed of light for a short burst. That could arguably be superior to <i>Acceleration.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T13:31:43-07:00","id":1523323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1523313#post1523313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could use a Patterning of Life and Forces, become light and therefore move at the speed of light for a short burst. That could arguably be superior to <i>Acceleration.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good way to move quickly, but I feel like default it's gonna be hard to interact with anything if you're made of light. I could see the spell compensating for decoherence by default, but consistently switching between tangible and intangible while the spell is ongoing seems a stretch for a non-Imperial spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T13:41:12-07:00","id":1523324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1523323#post1523323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a good way to move quickly, but I feel like default it's gonna be hard to interact with anything if you're made of light. I could see the spell compensating for decoherence by default, but consistently switching between tangible and intangible while the spell is ongoing seems a stretch for a non-Imperial spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably be duration primary, correct ? So the user can reflexively choose to Withstand it to turn the effect on or off. Another option is to make them into a being of light and kinetic energy, like the Codex from XCOM2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T14:06:50-07:00","id":1523326,"title":"","content":"I'm always leery of that reading of the Withstand rules. It's... internally consistent, mostly, it just feels <i>weird</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T11:16:22-07:00","id":1523564,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Crystal Furnace (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Practice: </b>Perfecting<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>N/A<br /> <b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Academics, Crafts, Science<br /> <br /> A rote developed by the entrepreneurial Nameless crafter Rinaldo, who provided aid to vampire hunters in exchange for their quarry's ashes. It provides the ideal conditions to crystallize carbon into diamonds. In addition, each level of Potency halves the time needed to create them.<br /> <br /> After extracting the carbon from the vampire ashes, Rinaldo was able to transform them into highly sought after yantras. The Thrice Great use them in their rituals involving Venus, a few Libertines employ experiments to create supernatural quantum computers. Some mages instead use this rote to transform the ashes of the fallen into memorial diamonds, as a final way to honor their contributions to the Diamond Orders.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The time is instead reduced to a quarter per Potency.</span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-04-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-31T13:27:01-08:00","id":1527663,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Gl\u00e1mr's Vigil (Space \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Practice: </b>Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>N/A<br /> <b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Expression, Intimidation, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> It is said that when Grettir slayed the dreaded Gl\u00e1mr, the revenant cursed him to be tormented with visions of his ghostly eyes in the dark, wearing at his sanity. Inspired by this tale, the Panoptes D\u00e9racin\u00e9 developed a rote to keep her adversaries in line by the mere fear of being watched.<br /> <br /> Subjects feel like there is a presence constantly watching them, just out of the edge of their vision or in the one corner they haven't checked. This afflicts them with the Paranoid condition.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The paranoia grows so strong that subjects tie certain objects to their mysterious watcher, such as windows, reflective surfaces, ringing telephones or closed doors. The mage can specify up to [Potency] Keys that grant the Shaken condition.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The spell can be fine tuned to only work when certain Key is present. The feeling might only trigger when they are in the presence of another member of their cabal, when inside small spaces, when outside of a settlement or even when the subject is alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T14:51:48-07:00","id":1539500,"title":"","content":"I made a bunch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Deja Fu (Time ooo)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Summon from the past circumstances that led to the last instance of bashing damage on your target. Potency must be equal to the amount of damage inflicted. The target experiences a stutter of time in which it relives the moment of infliction. The damage properties and circumstances remain the same, even if a bullet is spent or a blade is broken.<br /> +1 Reach: you may instead duplicate damage from any instance in the scene.<br /> <br /> Lightning Rod (Fate ooo)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> The target of the spell becomes rife with bad fortune; if a negative effect occurs in the vicinity of the target, it must preferentially include the target. Spilled drinks, clumsy right hooks, embarrassing faux pas all seem to befall the target instead of their intended recipients (if any).<br /> +2 Reach: The effect may influence supernatural powers with a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Proxy (Space ooo)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Balance an object larger than your silhouette on a spatial precipice, allowing you to reflexively (wits+resolve?) swap places with it a number of times equal to potency. If the structure of the object becomes destroyed, the spell falls apart as the balance is disrupted. This doesn\u2019t prevent you from being targeted by supernatural effect, but does allow skirting of aimed spells and firearms you are aware of.<br /> Add Forces: inertia and other forces can be transferred to the proxy.<br /> <br /> Godiva (Forces o)<br /> Practice: Compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Eases the friction between substances, causing simple fastenings that are under tension to become undone, such as knots, velcro and buttons. At potency 3 more complex fastenings like buckles and straps can be affected.<br /> <br /> Essence Sway (Spirit oo)<br /> Practice: Perfecting<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Channelling essence equal to potency into a target may illicit changes in its behaviour or nature. A stout wall may be weakened by the essence of decay, a frantic person may be calmed by tranquil essence, and a meek businessperson could be made to viciously close a deal with predatory essence. The amount of essence must overcome the target\u2019s resolve, composure or structure, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> Bi-Location (Space ooo)<br /> Practice: Fraying<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> You precariously straddle two different locations and are present in each physically. Taking actions simultaneously in each location is difficult and you take a -2 to any attempt unless under the effect of One Mind, Two Thoughts. As you are present in both locations you can take advantage of your surrounds, for example climbing stairs in one location to seemingly levitate in another, or submerging yourself in water in one location to walk through fire with less risk in another. Otherwise, each action you do is performed in both locations.<br /> <br /> +1 reach: Your movement can be asymmetrical in each location, allowing you to act in different directions. Facing yourself in the same room for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T20:47:26-08:00","id":1546018,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I'll ever get to play this character, but I came up with the idea of the Acanthus who seeks to help ghosts pass on to wherever they go after being stuck here. To facilitate this she has a praxis to give her information on the next steps they need to take on their journey.<br /> <br /> <i>A Path to Somewhere (Death \u2022 + Fate \u2022)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Practice: </b>Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Occult, Survival <br /> In order to pass on to whatever comes after their existence post death a ghost must resolve their anchors. This spell allows the mage to gain insight not only into what a ghost\u2019s anchors are, but also what the next step to resolving it might be.<br /> For each level of potency the mage learns one of a ghost's anchors and the next step that can be taken towards resolving that anchor. The anchors chosen are always the strongest anchor the ghost has, and then works down to their weakest.<br /> <i>+1 Reach</i> The mage may allocate potency into learning more about a single anchor, as opposed to learning about a new one. The mage gains insight into the next steps that should be taken towards resolving that anchor for each potency past the first allocated towards it<br /> <i>+1 Reach </i>The mage may learn about any anchor they wish, instead of the strongest working their way down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-17-2024, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T10:15:31-08:00","id":1546078,"title":"","content":"I really like this for a character who's interested in helping ghosts move on, I'd love to use it if I ever get to roll a Moros.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T12:02:11-08:00","id":1546079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hydrophiliak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1546078#post1546078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this for a character who's interested in helping ghosts move on, I'd love to use it if I ever get to roll a Moros.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The character I had in mind is an Acanthus who's whole thing is helping everyone move on after death, living and dead alike. Singer in Silence character. I hope to get to play a character with it at some point but I also have about 12 characters in mind so we'll see","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-27T14:25:15-08:00","id":1547285,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gearing up to play a Tamer of Blood and wanted to make a Praxis that worked for her, so here we are!<br /> <br /> <u>Known by Blood (Life \u2022)</u></span><br /> <br /> <b>Practice:</b> Knowing<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Science, Survival<br /> By understanding someone\u2019s blood you can understand them. This spell allows the mage to analyze blood to learn about the person the blood came from. The mage may ask a number of questions equal to the potency of this spell about the source of any blood she has, the answers gained through this spell give information about how the subject was when they lost the blood, not as they currently are. The following are example questions;<ul><li>What species is the subject?</li> <li>What sex is the subject?</li> <li>What is the total number of physical attribute dots the subject has?</li> <li>What illnesses is the subject suffering from, if any?</li> <li>What sort of diet does the subject have?</li> <li>Is the subject postpubescent or prepubescent?</li> <li>Was the subject under significant stress when the blood was separated from the body?</li> </ul><i>Add Space \u2022\u2022</i>: By using Sympathetic casting, the questions give information on the subject based on how they are now, not how they were when they lost the blood.<br /> <i>+1 Reach</i> The mage can determine if there are multiple sources of blood. If they have Space \u2022 they are able to tell which blood came from the same source.<br /> <i>+1 Reach</i> For the duration of the spell the mage recognizes the blood in people. They can determine if someone they see is the source of the blood, or if the person has had a blood transfusion, or similar procedures, from the original source of blood.<br /> <i>+1 Reach</i> The mage can ask for the specific number of dots in each physical attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-27-2024, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-10T11:22:26-08:00","id":1547665,"title":"","content":"<u><i>We\u2019ve Paid the Price</i> (Death \u2022\u2022)</u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> Those who sail along the rivers of the Underworld without a boatmen attract the attention of the Chthonians that live in the waters of the rivers, but, having paid a boatman for their services acts as a sort of shield against the Chthonians. While the reason for this is not known, this spell allows mages to trick the Chthonians into believing a boatman has been paid.<br /> For the duration of this spell, the vessel that serves as the subject of this spell appears to have a boatman that has been paid to provide safe passage along the rivers of the Underworld.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T17:21:41-07:00","id":1549172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1547665#post1547665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><i>We\u2019ve Paid the Price</i> (Death \u2022\u2022)</u><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Occult, Stealth, Subterfuge<br /> Those who sail along the rivers of the Underworld without a boatmen attract the attention of the Chthonians that live in the waters of the rivers, but, having paid a boatman for their services acts as a sort of shield against the Chthonians. While the reason for this is not known, this spell allows mages to trick the Chthonians into believing a boatman has been paid.<br /> For the duration of this spell, the vessel that serves as the subject of this spell appears to have a boatman that has been paid to provide safe passage along the rivers of the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps as a similar spell could have been conceived to fool Irkalla's Gates that their price was already paid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T10:26:09-07:00","id":1553376,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dead Man's Tales (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <br /> Not all deaths create a ghost, and sometimes a case has gone cold for so long that a specter might not even exist anymore. In those situations, a Guarding may choose to reanimate dead neurons, restoring vestiges of consciousness to a corpse. <br /> <br /> When used on a dead subject, it restores their body and reanimates their brain enough to answer any questions of the caster. It answers honestly and remember all it knew in life perfectly, but their answers will be colored by personal experience and biases. Because it is an echo of a mind, it cannot give an opinion it had not considered in life, cannot learn new information, make new theories or even remember anything that happened since their time of death. Many an Arrow warn of leaving bodies of dead comrades behind, all too aware of the danger of their knowledge falling in the wrong hands.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T18:01:58-07:00","id":1554133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1553376#post1553376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dead Man's Tales (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022, Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Medicine, Occult, Persuasion<br /> <br /> Not all deaths create a ghost, and sometimes a case has gone cold for so long that a specter might not even exist anymore. In those situations, a Guarding may choose to reanimate dead neurons, restoring vestiges of consciousness to a corpse.<br /> <br /> When used on a dead subject, it restores their body and reanimates their brain enough to answer any questions of the caster. It answers honestly and remember all it knew in life perfectly, but their answers will be colored by personal experience and biases. Because it is an echo of a mind, it cannot give an opinion it had not considered in life, cannot learn new information, make new theories or even remember anything that happened since their time of death. Many an Arrow warn of leaving bodies of dead comrades behind, all too aware of the danger of their knowledge falling in the wrong hands.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>that's sick, love it. Had an idea for a Mind/Death character and she'd be interested in this sort of magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T01:21:48-07:00","id":1554220,"title":"","content":"Could a space 3/mind 3 spell create a version of Ban that moves and change shape as one subject concentrates on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-07T07:38:07-07:00","id":1554222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1554220#post1554220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a space 3/mind 3 spell create a version of Ban that moves and change shape as one subject concentrates on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Redefining the boundaries of an unanchored area of effect in a non-subtractive way is mostly outside the scope of Traveler Arcana; generally speaking dynamic alterations to a subject require a spell that either makes the subject pliable or creates a force that you control as an instant action, with more involved stuff being multiple castings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T15:06:56-08:00","id":1557813,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Disassemble (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Practice: </b>Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Durability<br /> <b>Recommended Rote Skills: </b>Crafts, Intimidation, Science<br /> <br /> A rote developed by the Vidantus, as a way to provide less than lethal solutions for talons. The targeted object has all it's parts fall apart, landing quietly and harmlessly on the ground. A gun's components will be separated down to the smallest piece, a section of wall will break apart into lumps of bricks and cement, ropes, kevlar and tapestries will unravel into individual clumps of threads; armor will have it's plates fall off and even cars will be left unusable in moments. Talons have found it a great, if not particularly subtle aid for rapid infiltrations and sabotage.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-21-2026, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T09:10:28-08:00","id":1558471,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fall Control (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice: </b> Shielding </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Withstand: </b> N/A</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b> Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Stealth, Survival </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A field spell of the Adamantine Arrow, which allows that talons to safely drop from great heights when scouting or infiltrating. Some say it was developed to quickly and discretely escape medieval fortresses, others claim it was developed from Japanese mages for assassination work, others say it was created in WW1 to survive plane falls. Subjects under its effects suffer no fall damage, as well as add [Potency] to rolls to fall or grip the intended target. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+2 Reach and a point of mana:</b> The caster can use the spell reflexively, allowing them to potentially survive being thrown off high altitudes.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-20T08:03:46-07:00","id":1558950,"title":"","content":"How would you flesh out using Forces to allow a cell phone to have data connectivity without a SIM? Unlike Tune In I would actually like to use the cell phone partially just for the vibe but also because that should allow cell phone apps and hardware to handle interpreting the data and doing transmissions. Is this as simple as a very specific form of the Free Council Forces 2 password rote to handle handshaking with the network?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","user":"Madmarcus","date":". 03-20-2026, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T04:01:09-07:00","id":1559116,"title":"","content":"Ill try one let me know if i mess up:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Natural invisiblity (Life \u2022\u2022)</b> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice: </b>Veiling</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Withstand: </b> N/A</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Stealth, Survival </span><br /> This is a personal spell that veils the living caster from the eyes of others, making him invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 03-30-2026, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T19:31:35-07:00","id":1561149,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">An attempt to expand on the pool of Unveiling of Life spells</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Tell-Tale Eye (Life \u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Empathy, Socialize, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> A spell that expands a subject's capacity to perceive and interpret body language, picking up on minute details they otherwise wouldn't notice. It provides a bonus of [Potency] to any rolls to detect lies or read the emotional states of others. In addition, because the subject can perceive the subtle tells of fight or flight responses, they can react to them much faster, providing a bonus of [Potency] to Initiative. It is a favorite rote amongst the Guardians, who teach that while many mages may protect their minds, the body still talks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T11:57:37-07:00","id":1563603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1558471#post1558471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fall Control (Forces \u2022\u2022)</b> </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Practice: </b> Shielding </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Withstand: </b> N/A</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b> Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Stealth, Survival </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A field spell of the Adamantine Arrow, which allows that talons to safely drop from great heights when scouting or infiltrating. Some say it was developed to quickly and discretely escape medieval fortresses, others claim it was developed from Japanese mages for assassination work, others say it was created in WW1 to survive plane falls. Subjects under its effects suffer no fall damage, as well as add [Potency] to rolls to fall or grip the intended target. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>+2 Reach and a point of mana:</b> The caster can use the spell reflexively, allowing them to potentially survive being thrown off high altitudes.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So what exactly is this spell shielding you from? Not disagreeing with the idea of the spell, just not sure what you are actually &quot;shielding&quot;. I could see it being a Ruling spell? With the idea being that you are controlling how you fall? A whole &quot;falling with style&quot;/gliding logic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26144-eshangray","name":"eshangray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"